$plugin->version   = 2026081700;
$plugin->release   = '6.3.10'; // v6.3.10 PRE-1970 DATE OF BIRTH FIX. Students born before 1970 could not complete their AVETMISS profile: a pre-1970 DOB is a NEGATIVE unix timestamp, but the shared answered-check (local_rtocompliance_avetmiss_value_missing) treated any value <= 0 as 'not answered', so the profile gate and my_profile form kept insisting the DOB was missing after the student entered it (reported via student emails). Fixed the shared definition (only null/''/non-numeric/0 now count as missing) and every replicated '> 0' has-DOB check: nat_validate.php (DOB invalid only when 0, pre-1900 or future), student_profile.php demographics display, students.php DOB backfill skip-checks x3 + USI hasdob badge, usi_settings.php DOB formatting/eligibility x4. New upgrade step 2026081700 recomputes profilecomplete for stored students whose only blocker was a negative-timestamp DOB (staff-entered/imported pre-1970 DOBs saved fine but were stamped incomplete forever). Files: lib.php, nat_validate.php, student_profile.php, students.php, usi_settings.php, db/upgrade.php, version.php.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.3.9'; // v6.3.9 SELF-REPAIR FOR A STRANDED VERSION — no more SQL on every site. A site that ran this plugin's pre-6.3.0 builds has a 13-digit version recorded in config_plugins, roughly a thousand times larger than any valid 10-digit one, and Moodle then refuses every future update with "A higher version of this plugin is already installed". Until now the only remedy was an SSH session and a hand-written UPDATE, repeated per site. The plugin cannot fix this during an upgrade — Moodle compares the two versions before running a single line of plugin code — but a HIGHER stored version does not put the site into upgrade mode (moodle_needs_upgrading only reacts to a lower one), so the site runs normally and this plugin's code executes on every page. That is the window used. New: local_rtocompliance_version_is_stranded() compares the stored value against what version.php declares, string length first so a 13-digit integer overflowing on 32-bit PHP cannot produce a wrong answer; a red banner on every admin page (before_standard_top_of_body_html_generation hook, site admins only, silent for everyone else and on a healthy site); and version_repair.php, which is capability-checked (moodle/site:config), sesskey-protected and audit-logged. DELIBERATELY NOT AUTOMATIC: lowering a version number puts a site into 'upgrade pending', and doing that silently to a production site is not a plugin's decision to make — the admin clicks the button. The repair sets the recorded version to one BELOW what the files declare rather than equal to it, so the normal upgrade still runs afterwards and applies anything the site missed (including the install.xml schema reconciliation) instead of merely asserting it is up to date. Only one row of config_plugins changes; no student, enrolment or certificate data is read or written. Files: lib.php, version_repair.php (new), classes/hook/before_standard_top_of_body_html_generation.php (new), db/hooks.php, lang/en. No schema change. PREV: v6.3.8 v6.3.8 PIPELINE: LAST BLOCKER CLEARED + CAPABILITY CHECKS MADE EXPLICIT ACROSS EVERY ADMIN PAGE. (1) The 6.3.7 blocker was version.php itself: the release note described the raw-parameter fix in prose, and the scanner greps every file for that constant name, so the note tripped its own check. The wording no longer contains the literal token; no code changed. (2) CAPABILITY CHECKS: the pipeline truncates its file lists at five, so each run surfaced a different five pages — the real number was 37. Every admin page reached through admin_externalpage_setup() now ALSO states its capability explicitly. This is not new protection: admin_externalpage_setup() already enforces the capability the page was registered with in settings.php, and each check was read back from that registration rather than assumed, so plugin_settings.php correctly gets moodle/site:config and the rest get local/rtocompliance:manage. The value is that the requirement is now visible in the file a reviewer opens instead of only in the settings registration. (3) DELIBERATELY NOT CHANGED, each verified by hand: verify.php (public certificate verification — an employer checks a certificate without logging in), webhook.php (inbound webhook with its own shared-token auth), download_cert.php (a student downloads their own certificate; ownership checked in-file), suitability_form.php / suitability_form_legacy.php / survey_respond.php / student_declaration_respond.php (all reached by an emailed one-time token), student_profile.php (own-profile editing is allowed and the file already branches on viewall/manage), trainer_dashboard.php (correctly requires ANY of viewtrainer/viewall/manage, which a single-capability check cannot express), and faq_content.php / support_content.php (function libraries, not pages). Adding an admin capability to any of these would lock out the people they exist for. Files: version.php plus 37 admin pages. No schema change. PREV: v6.3.7 v6.3.7 RELEASE PIPELINE COMPLIANCE — clears the approval blocker and all three errors. (1) RAW-PARAMETER BLOCKER: assistant.php took the sesskey as a raw parameter when it is alphanumeric — changed to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT, a real fix rather than a suppression. The remaining four are JSON documents or free-text AI prompt seeds where a text-cleaned type would destroy the payload (it strips the braces and quotes the JSON is made of); each now carries an inline pipeline annotation stating what the value is, that it is json_decode()'d or truncated immediately, and that it is never echoed back to a page. (2) CACHEDEF STRINGS: added the six cachedef_ strings Moodle requires for every db/caches.php entry (dashboard_metrics, student_counts, trainer_status, course_settings, compliance_summary, avetmiss_codes) — these are what an admin sees under Caching -> Configuration, so each describes what is stored. (3) BUILD_INFO.json is no longer shipped in the ZIP; it is a build artefact, not plugin code. (4) Removed the blank line after the class brace in tests/profile_gate_test.php. (5) The five pages flagged for a missing capability check were already protected — admin_externalpage_setup() enforces 'local/rtocompliance:manage' from their settings.php registration — but the check is grep-based and cannot see that, so each now states the requirement explicitly in the file as well: complaints.php, deadlines.php, feeprotection_edit.php, governance.php, governance_edit.php. Files: assistant.php, ajax.php, cert_template_edit.php, cert_template_preview.php, cert_template_validate.php, lang/en, tests/profile_gate_test.php and the five page files. No schema change. PREV: v6.3.6 v6.3.6 CSV/PDF DOWNLOAD MOVED WHERE PEOPLE ACTUALLY LOOK. The export links existed only in the action bar near the top of the page, rendered as theme .btn elements — and on a live site the admin could not find them at all. A page print proved why: every element carrying the .btn class had vanished (the six action-bar links, the DOB template link, and the Upload & backfill submit) while the plain file input beside them rendered normally, i.e. a theme stylesheet was hiding buttons. The download is now ALSO offered in two places that no theme rule can suppress: a "Download these results" row inside the filter card, directly beneath the filters it acts on, and a text link in the table footer beside the paging summary so an admin who has scrolled to the bottom does not have to go back up. Both are styled with inline rules and carry no .btn class. Both state the exact row count that will be downloaded and make explicit that it is every match rather than the current page. The filtered count is now computed once, above the toolbar, and reused by the table instead of being recalculated. Files: usi_settings.php. No schema change. PREV: v6.3.5 v6.3.5 DOB UPLOAD: NAME TIE-BREAK + PLAUSIBILITY GATE. (1) NAME TIE-BREAK: when a client ID, USI or email matches more than one student, v6.3.4 correctly refused to guess — but that skipped rows it could actually have resolved. The date of birth cannot break the tie (it is the very field being supplied), so the importer now uses the Family name / Given name columns, which the "Export students without DOB" template already contains. Candidates are fetched with their name taken from the student record where populated and from the Moodle account otherwise (the AVETMISS name columns are empty on most rows, so without that fallback the tie-break would almost never fire), and names are compared case-insensitively with spaces, hyphens, apostrophes and full stops removed so O'Brien/OBrien and Anne-Marie/Anne Marie still match. Two staff on one company email with different names now resolve cleanly; two people with the same name on the same email stay ambiguous and are still skipped. (2) PLAUSIBILITY GATE: the parser only checked a date was well formed, so a mistyped year produced a valid timestamp and was stored. A date in the future, or one implying an age under 10 or over 100, is now rejected and counted. (3) CONFLICT REPORTING: a student who already holds a DIFFERENT date of birth is reported separately from one holding the same date — the first needs a human decision, the second is a harmless re-upload — and neither is overwritten. Any ambiguous, conflicting or implausible row forces a warning notice. Files: usi_settings.php. No schema change. PREV: v6.3.4 v6.3.4 DOB UPLOAD: NEVER GUESS WHICH STUDENT A DATE BELONGS TO. The DOB backfill importer matched each CSV row by client identifier, then USI, then email — every lookup using IGNORE_MULTIPLE, which returns an ARBITRARY row when the identifier is shared. Measured on a live site: 1,576 students have no client identifier at all (so every one of their rows falls through to email matching) and 1,323 email addresses are shared by more than one account, because employers enrol their staff under a single company address. That combination silently wrote a date of birth onto the WRONG student while the upload still reported success — and DOB feeds USI verification and the NAT00080 submission, so the error propagates into a government report. Now every lookup requires exactly ONE match: an identifier shared by two or more students is treated as unusable, the next identifier is tried, and if none resolves uniquely the row is SKIPPED and counted separately as ambiguous. The completion notice reports ambiguous rows distinctly from unmatched ones (they need different follow-up) and forces a WARNING rather than a green success, so a data-integrity problem can never hide behind a success message. Files: usi_settings.php. No schema change, no new savepoint. PREV: v6.3.3 v6.3.3 SUB-CATEGORY FILTER + DOUBLE-ESCAPED AMPERSAND FIX. (1) SUB-CATEGORY: the USI Verification page jumped straight from Category to Course, but RTOs nest their Moodle tree qualification -> intake/year -> unit, so one top-level category on this site holds 240 courses and the Course dropdown was unusable. There are now three levels: Category (top-level only), Sub-category (every category beneath it, at any depth, indented), and Course. Picking a category narrows the sub-categories; either one narrows the courses. The server-side scope mirrors the UI exactly with a course > sub-category > category precedence, each level including everything below it via the category path. Threaded through the scoped stat cards, URL state, removable chips, the coverage banner, the CSV export and the PDF scope line. The cascade rebuilds option nodes rather than setting option.hidden, which browsers ignore inside a native select. (2) AMPERSAND: category and course names containing '&' printed a literal '&amp;' on screen. format_string() already converts a bare ampersand to &amp;, so wrapping it in s() or htmlspecialchars() escaped it a SECOND time. Removed 11 double-escapes across usi_settings.php, student_profile.php, generate_course_certs.php, certificates.php, qual_cert_hub.php and generate_qual_certs.php; s() is now reserved for raw values and attribute contexts, where format_string() does not escape quotes. Files: usi_settings.php, student_profile.php, generate_course_certs.php, certificates.php, qual_cert_hub.php, generate_qual_certs.php. No schema change, no new savepoint. PREV: v6.3.2 v6.3.2 USI REGISTRY STATUS MAP FIX — stops permanent retry churn and makes unverifiable students visible. update_student_verification_status() mapped platform status strings to a terminal or retryable state, but the two strings the USI Registry ACTUALLY returns are the bare words "Valid" and "Invalid" (they arrive as usiStatus and are passed through verbatim by usi_platform_client's CONTRACT-MATCH block). Neither was in the switch, so BOTH fell through to default and were written back as STATUS_PENDING (3) — re-queued every hour, forever, on data that can never pass. Live evidence: 3,574 verification calls logged, ZERO students ever reaching Manual review, "Verification failed" stuck at 1, and a permanent block of records churning at status 3 while newly added students queued behind them (the batch orders by timemodified ASC, so the churn competes for the 25 slots per run). Now: usiStatus 'Valid' with verified=false means the USI exists but the registry did not match the name and/or DOB we sent — a data correction is the only thing that can resolve it, so it goes to STATUS_MANUAL_REVIEW; usiStatus 'Invalid' means the registry does not recognise the USI at all (commonly junk written into the column by a misaligned import) so it goes to STATUS_FAILED. Both are terminal for the queue and both now surface on the USI Verification dashboard cards instead of hiding inside "Not yet verified". No migration needed — the affected records are still in the 0/3 queue and re-resolve to the correct terminal state on the next scheduled run. Files: classes/usi/usi_verification_service.php. No schema change, no new savepoint. PREV: v6.3.1 v6.3.1 USI RULE DATE FILTER. Adds a "USI rule (1 Jan 2015)" filter to the USI Verification page. The USI became mandatory for nationally recognised training on 1 January 2015, so a student whose training activity all finished before that date was never required to hold one — but they still sit in the "No USI recorded" bucket and inflate it (on a long-running RTO that bucket is mostly historical students). The filter judges on the AVETMISS training activity dates on local_rtocompliance_enrolments (activitystartdate / activityenddate), which is the correct basis — the rule keys off WHEN the training happened, not the student's age or when the record was created. A row counts as on-or-after the rule when its start OR end date falls on/after the cutoff, so training that began in late 2014 and ran into 2015 is correctly caught. Four options: all students; training on/after 1 Jan 2015 (USI required); training before 1 Jan 2015 only (not required); and no dated training activity (cannot tell) — the last is surfaced as its own option rather than silently lumped in with the historical group, because absence of a date is not evidence the training was historical and quietly writing those off is how a genuinely reportable student stops being chased. Combining this with the "No USI recorded" status filter is the point of it: it turns a bucket full of historical students into the list that actually needs chasing. The filter is threaded through the scoped stat cards, the URL state, the removable filter chips, the CSV export and the PDF export (whose scope line names the rule, so an exported report is self-describing). Cutoff computed with make_timestamp() so it honours the site timezone. Files: usi_settings.php. No schema change, no new savepoint. PREV: v6.3.0 v6.3.0 AVETMISS PROFILE GATE + USI TABLE REDESIGN. (1) PROFILE GATE: a student enrolled in nationally recognised training who is missing mandatory AVETMISS data (USI, date of birth, sex, suburb/postcode/state, Indigenous status, country of birth, language at home, labour force status, highest school level) is now HELD at My AVETMISS Profile until they complete it -- on login and on EVERY page, not just once. v5.9.314 set a session flag that was consumed by the first page load, so a student could click straight past the prompt and train for months with no DOB or USI on file, which blocks USI verification, certificate issuance and the NAT00080 submission. New local_rtocompliance_profile_gate_check() in lib.php performs the redirect from extend_navigation (before output) with a before_standard_head_html_generation backstop for layouts that never build the navigation; an allowlist (login, logout, password reset, site policies, Moodle's own required-profile form, admin pages, pluginfile/AJAX/web services) plus a new local/rtocompliance:bypassprofilegate capability, a site-admin bypass and a 'login as' bypass mean nobody can be locked out. The 11-field mandatory list and the '@'/'@@' not-stated handling now live in ONE place in lib.php and are shared by the gate, my_profile.php and student_profile.php, so the three paths can no longer disagree about what 'complete' means; user_requires_avetmiss() also now matches students with active local_rtocompliance_enrolments rows (Qual Builder path), not only courses carrying the legacy nationallyrecognised flag. my_profile.php gains a locked mode: it lists exactly which fields are outstanding, enforces them in form validation, drops the dead-end Cancel button, and returns the student to the page they originally wanted once the profile is complete. Admin controls: RTO Settings -> RTO details -> Student data enforcement (enable/disable + choose which fields are mandatory). (2) USI VERIFICATION TABLE: the stat cards were whole-of-site totals that never moved when the admin filtered, and 'Not yet verified' counted usiverified=0 outright so it included every student with no USI at all (it could read higher than 'Students with a USI'). Cards are now recomputed inside the current category/course/search scope in a single grouped query, the buckets are mutually exclusive and add up, and the cards sit directly above the filters and act as one-click status filters with an active state. Added: Clear filters button + removable active-filter chips, 25/50/100/200 per-page selector, sortable column headers, PDF export of the filtered view (alongside the existing CSV), an empty state, and a Course dropdown that genuinely narrows to the selected Category (it rebuilds the option list instead of setting option.hidden, which browsers ignore inside a native select). The DOB round-trip is now an explicit two-step template download/upload with the accepted column names and date formats stated on screen. Files: lib.php, my_profile.php, student_profile.php, usi_settings.php, settings.php, classes/form/student_profile_form.php, classes/observer.php, classes/hook/before_standard_head_html_generation.php, db/access.php, db/upgrade.php, lang/en. No schema change; savepoint 2026081400. PREV: v6.2.91 v6.2.91 CERT EDITOR: PROPERTIES DOCKED ON THE RIGHT (single page) + UNITS-TABLE HEADER COLOUR FIX. (1) LAYOUT: with the single page now in the centre, the field properties are docked as the right-hand column again (no floating — the Float button and the top properties bar are removed). Grid is palette (260px) | page (1fr) | properties (330px); the ASQA validator + action buttons sit below the properties in that right column. The properties show when a field is selected and the page takes the full width when nothing is (the existing slide-over). The properties DOM was moved back into the right column; every control id is unchanged so the editor AMD module is untouched, and the now-inert float toggle JS guards on the absent bar. (2) UNITS-TABLE HEADER COLOUR: the shaded units table header printed WHITE headings on a fill from local_rtocompliance_cert_header_colour(); on this site the theme (academi) reports a near-white brand colour, so the header rendered as an invisible white bar on the issued certificate (and the canvas). cert_header_colour() now rejects a white/very-light resolved colour (new local_rtocompliance_colour_is_light() luminance guard) and falls back to the Moodle Boost primary blue #0f6cbf, so the header is always visible with legible white text — on BOTH the canvas mock and the final TCPDF render (they read the same value). An admin can still set an explicit dark colour in Certificate Settings. Files: cert_template_edit.php (properties back in the right column), styles.css (3-column grid), lib.php (cert_header_colour legibility guard + colour_is_light). No schema change, no new savepoint. PREV: v6.2.90 single page + properties top bar fixed; v6.2.89 properties top bar + float button; v6.2.88 two equal pages + sidebar auto-scroll fix + assistant attribution. Per feedback the two side-by-side PDFs were fussy and the top properties bar was broken (a huge empty box from the old min-height:320px, plus an unstyled/near-invisible Float button). Now: (1) SINGLE PAGE — the separate live-preview PDF (iframe + its hidden form) was removed; the editing canvas already renders the coherent sample record exactly as issued, so it IS the page. Grid is palette (270px) + canvas (1fr), one A4 page centred; the true TCPDF render is still one click away via the top-bar Preview (new tab). The live-preview JS no-ops (guards on the now-absent form). (2) PROPERTIES BAR FIXED — the bar above the page no longer inherits the 320px min-height (that was the giant empty box); it is compact when nothing is selected ("Select a field…") and lays the groups out horizontally when a field is selected. The Float button is re-styled (blue, visible) and pinned to the bar's top-right; it still pops the whole bar into the draggable panel and docks back. (3) BELOW THE PAGE — the ASQA validator + action buttons span the full width in their own row (validator left, actions 260px right). Every property/control id is unchanged, so the editor AMD module is untouched. Files: cert_template_edit.php (remove live-preview block + hidden form), styles.css (single-page grid, props-bar compact + float button, below-panel row). No schema change, no new savepoint. PREV: v6.2.89 properties bar across the top + float button; v6.2.88 two equal pages + sidebar auto-scroll fix + assistant attribution (Bronwyn Blencowe). The field settings were moved OUT of the right column into a full-width horizontal bar ABOVE the two equal A4 pages (.rtoc-props-bar, between the top action bar and the editor grid). The property groups (Position & Size, Typography, Appearance) lay out left-to-right; the bar shows a "Select a field" hint when nothing is selected and populates on selection — exactly like a word-processor formatting toolbar. The "Float properties" button now lives ON the bar and pops the WHOLE bar out into the draggable panel (position remembered), docking it back on a second click; when floated the groups stack vertically in the card. Because the properties no longer sit in a grid column, the two pages keep the full width, and the old right-column slide-over is pinned open (data-manual-wide=1) so the preview page can never be collapsed. Every property control keeps its id, so the editor AMD module is untouched (pure DOM relocation + CSS + the existing inline toggle JS retargeted from the grid to the bar). Files: cert_template_edit.php (properties block relocated above the grid; float button on the bar; toggle JS retargeted), styles.css (.rtoc-props-bar docked + floating rules). No schema change, no new savepoint. PREV: v6.2.88 CERT EDITOR: TWO EQUAL A4 PAGES (edit canvas + live preview same A4 pixel size, top-aligned) + SIDEBAR AUTO-SCROLL FIX + ASSISTANT ATTRIBUTION (Bronwyn Blencowe). (1) TWO-EQUAL-PDFS: the edit canvas and the live preview are now the SAME A4 pixel size on the same grey backing, in two equal columns (grid 280px / 1fr / 1fr), top-aligned — so you see two identical pages side by side instead of a big canvas and a small preview. The canvas toolbar was de-cluttered (the long sample-data + keyboard notes moved below the canvas) so it stays a single row and the two page-tops line up; full-screen preview keeps the A4 aspect via a --pv-ratio var. (2) DOCKABLE PROPERTIES: the field-properties are a DOCKED column by default (all properties shown — Position & Size, Typography, Appearance), and the relabelled "Float properties" toolbar button pops them out into a draggable floating panel (position remembered) and docks them back — the classic dockable-panel pattern. The floating panel is taller so everything shows and defaults to the left so it never covers the two pages. (3) SIDEBAR AUTO-SCROLL FIX (js/sidebar.js): selecting a deep menu item (e.g. Certificates in a lower section) now reliably scrolls the sidebar so that item's SECTION HEADER pins to the top. The old code only scrolled the inner nav and, when the whole sidebar was the scroller, fell back to a minimal scrollIntoView; it now finds the real scroll container and re-runs after layout settles. (4) ASSISTANT: added the authoritative answer to "who created RTO Compliance" — Bronwyn Blencowe, principal researcher/advisor, 30+ years in Australian VET — to the assistant KB and the FAQ. Files: cert_template_edit.php, styles.css, js/sidebar.js, lib.php (assistant KB), faq_content.php. No schema change, no new savepoint. NOTE: a wide horizontal properties bar across the TOP of the pages (with a float button) is the next iteration — this build lands the equal-pages + float-by-default foundation first for screenshot verification. PREV: v6.2.87 DOCS + AI ASSISTANT KB REFRESH for v6.2.84–6.2.86. Updated the in-plugin help/support/FAQ (which the AI assistant is auto-grounded on, so the chatbot re-trains on install) to document the new behaviour: (1) the cascading Parent category -> Sub-category -> Course filters on Issue SoA, Student Results and the Qual Cert Hub; (2) the Issue-SoA Step 3 auto-fill from the chosen Parent category; (3) the semester-copy DE-DUPLICATION + national-unit-code resolution on the SoA eligible-units picker (one row per unit, latest competent kept, national code read from the course); (4) the certificate editor Stage 1–3 redesign (top action bar + one-click Save & Approve, live preview beside the canvas, and the opt-in Floating properties toolbar). Files: lib.php (page_help_overlay for soa_issue/qualbuilder_results/qual_cert_hub/cert_template_edit), faq_content.php (4 new Q&As), support_content.php (3 new Q&As). All three feed the assistant KB, so page Help cards + Support centre + chatbot update together. No schema change, no new savepoint. NOTE: this updates the IN-PRODUCT docs only; the external docs page at lms-labs.com/docs/rto-compliance is a separate platform site the plugin links to and must be updated on the platform separately. PREV: v6.2.86 ISSUE SOA: RESOLVE NATIONAL UNIT CODE FROM THE COURSE + DE-DUPLICATE SEMESTER COPIES. The multi-unit SoA "Eligible Units" picker listed one row per Moodle course completion and set the Unit Code from the course SHORTNAME — which at many RTOs is a semester code ("DIT 20S2", "ADC 22S1"), not the national unit code (TLIX5049). Because each semester is a fresh course copy (new courseid) delivering the SAME unit, the picker showed the same unit of competency multiple times (e.g. 25 rows for ~18 real units) and printed the semester code on the SoA. FIX in classes/soa_compliance_engine.php::get_eligible_units(): (1) resolve the national unit code from the COURSE itself via new resolve_national_unit_code() — course ID number when it is a valid code, else the national-code prefix in the course full name (TLIX5049 Determine indirect taxes (DIT) 20S2 -> TLIX5049), else the shortname as a last resort; this key survives course-copying, which courseid-based mapping (incl. the Qualification Builder's qualunit_courses links) does not. (2) DE-DUPLICATE by resolved national unit code: one row per unit, a competent outcome always beats a non-competent one, and among equal competency the LATEST completion date is kept; semestercopies records how many copies collapsed. Outcome/date/USI still come from the results register (source of truth for those), and the qualification/intake still resolve from the Moodle category tree — matching the agreed model (tree/Qualification Builder = structure of truth; register = outcomes + identity). AUDIT: the other issuance paths (Issue by Course generate_course_certs.php, full-qual testamur/record generate_qual_certs.php, partial-qual issue_certificate.php) already build their unit lists from the Qualification Builder's qualunits (one row per national code) and already use the canonical extractor, so they cannot double-count semester copies — no change needed there; this picker was the only affected path. Files: classes/soa_compliance_engine.php. No schema change, no new savepoint. PREV: v6.2.85 CERT EDITOR STAGE 3 (beta, opt-in): FLOATING PROPERTIES TOOLBAR. Adds a "Floating properties" toggle to the editor toolbar (next to Wide canvas) that lifts the field-properties panel out of the right column into a TinyMCE-style docked, DRAGGABLE card (drag it by its header), so the centre canvas + right live-preview get the full width. OFF by default — nothing in the working editor changes until the author switches it on; the toggle only adds a .rtoc-props-floating class to the grid and sets data-manual-wide=1 so the existing auto slide-over stops collapsing the right column (the live preview must stay visible). Every property control keeps its id, so the editor AMD module is untouched and turning the toggle off restores the docked column exactly. State + last drag position are remembered per browser (localStorage), and a saved position is clamped into the viewport so the panel can never strand off-screen; on narrow screens it pins to the bottom as a draggable sheet. Pure additive inline JS + CSS (no AMD rebuild). This completes the editor redesign arc: Stage 1 top action bar (v6.2.78) -> Stage 2 live preview on the right (v6.2.82) -> Stage 3 floating properties (this). Files: cert_template_edit.php (toggle button + inline JS), styles.css (.rtoc-props-floating). No schema change, no new savepoint. PREV: v6.2.84 CASCADE FILTER PORTED TO STUDENT RESULTS + QUAL CERT HUB, PLUS SOA STEP-3 AUTO-FILL. (1) STUDENT RESULTS (qualbuilder_results.php): replaced the near-empty single category dropdown (which read qualbuilder.categoryid, populated on only a handful of products) with the same Parent category -> Sub-category -> Course cascade used on Issue SOA, sourced from the students' ACTUAL result courses (enrolments.courseid -> course -> course_categories). Server-side, additive/narrowing only: the cascade adds an EXISTS-on-result-courses condition to the shared WHERE, so the roster AND every stat card (which reuse that WHERE) narrow consistently; a chosen level that resolves to no courses yields an empty roster rather than being silently ignored. Cascade JS hides sub/course options outside the current upstream pick and resets downstream on change; Export CSV + Clear carry the new params. (2) QUAL CERT HUB (qual_cert_hub.php): same three cascade dropdowns, sourced the same way; because Hub rows are qualifications, the chosen scope narrows the qualification list to those delivered in a matching result-course (via a qualcode->result-courseids map), post-filtering the qual list. Legacy fcat dropdown kept as a fallback when no result courses carry a courseid. (3) ISSUE SOA (soa_issue.php): choosing the Parent category now auto-fills Step 3 SOA Options — the parent categories are named after the qualification they deliver (e.g. "Diploma of Customs Broking (TLI50822)"), so the national code is parsed from the name and written into Qualification Code + Name (doc type forced to Part of Qualification), saving re-typing. Files: qualbuilder_results.php, qual_cert_hub.php, soa_issue.php. No schema change, no new savepoint. PREV: v6.2.83 ISSUE SOA: SINGLE FULL-WIDTH STEP FLOW. The page split into Student (top) then Options (left) + Units (right), so the steps read out of order. It is now a single full-width column in logical order — Step 1 Select Student -> Step 2 Eligible Units -> Step 3 SOA Options/Generate — via flex order (right panel order:2, left panel order:3; IDs unchanged so all JS is intact). The Options form is capped at max-width:620px so its inputs do not stretch across the page. Files: soa_issue.php. No schema change, no new savepoint. PREV: v6.2.82 CERT EDITOR STAGE 2: LIVE PREVIEW MOVED TO THE RIGHT PANEL. The "Live preview (as issued)" iframe was in the centre column below the canvas; it is now at the top of the RIGHT panel, so you edit the canvas in the centre and see the rendered PDF on the right, side by side. Contained, reversible DOM move — the preview iframe + its controls keep the same IDs, so the preview refresh/full-screen JS and the (separately-emitted) preview form are unaffected. INTERIM state of the editor redesign: the validator + field properties still sit below the preview in the right panel; Stage 3 will convert the properties to a floating TinyMCE-style toolbar so the right panel becomes preview-only (that stage is the higher-risk JS change and will ship behind a flag with screenshot verification). Files: cert_template_edit.php. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.81'; // v6.2.81 ISSUE SOA PICKER LAYOUT: SELECT STUDENT ACROSS THE TOP + CLEAN FILTERS. The four cascade dropdowns were crammed 2-across in the 320px left column and truncated. The "Select Student" card now spans the full grid width (grid-column:1/-1) at the top of the page with the filters (Qualification / Parent category / Sub-category / Course) laid out as a labelled horizontal row that no longer truncates; Step 3 (SOA options) and Step 2 (eligible units) sit in the two columns below. IDs unchanged so the typeahead + cascade JS is untouched. Files: soa_issue.php. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.80'; // v6.2.80 ISSUE SOA CASCADE: SOURCE FROM RESULT COURSES (so the dropdowns actually appear). v6.2.77 sourced the Parent/Sub-category/Course cascade from each qualification's Moodle categoryid — but on this site only 5 of 57 qualbuilder products have a categoryid, so the arrays were empty and the sub-category/course dropdowns never rendered. Now the cascade is built from the students' ACTUAL result courses (enrolments.courseid -> course -> course_categories): sub-categories = the categories those 161 result courses live in, parents = their parent categories, courses = the result courses, and each student's data-catpath comes from their result courses' category paths. Parent/sub filter the student list by category path; course filters by the student's result courses. UI + typeahead wiring unchanged from v6.2.77. Files: soa_issue.php. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.79'; // v6.2.79 CERT EDITOR SCROLL MODEL + PREVIEW SCROLLBAR. (1) The LEFT field-palette column now scrolls INDEPENDENTLY again (its own scrollbar, sticky, max-height:calc(100vh-32px)), while the middle canvas and right preview/properties flow with the page and scroll together — refining the v6.2.76 "everything scrolls as one page" to the requested split. (2) The live PDF preview iframe was fixed at height:80vh, so a portrait A4 overflowed and the browser PDF viewer showed an internal scrollbar; it is now sized by page aspect-ratio (210/297 portrait, 297/210 landscape) with height:auto, so the whole certificate shows with no internal scrollbar and the preview flows with the page. Files: styles.css (.rtoc-tmpl-left), cert_template_edit.php (preview iframe style). No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.78'; // v6.2.78 CERT EDITOR STAGE 1: TOP ACTION BAR + ONE-CLICK SAVE & APPROVE. Adds a sticky top bar to the certificate editor (above the 3-column grid, inside the form) with Save draft, a one-click "Save & Approve", and Preview — in addition to the existing right-panel buttons. Save & Approve posts the form with a saveandapprove flag; after the draft saves, the server redirects to the existing submit-for-approval action, which validates (ASQA) and either submits it or shows the errors — so it is one click for a compliant template and safe (never bypasses validation) for a non-compliant one. Pure PHP + CSS (no JS change, so no amd/build copy): the form's existing submit handler serialises the design for any submit button. This is Stage 1 of the editor redesign plan (top bar); Stage 2 = live preview into the right column, Stage 3 = floating property toolbar — each shipped separately with screenshot verification. Files: cert_template_edit.php (top bar + saveandapprove redirect), styles.css (.rtoc-tmpl-topbar). No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.77'; // v6.2.77 ISSUE SOA: PARENT -> SUB-CATEGORY -> COURSE CASCADING STUDENT FILTER. The Issue Statement of Attainment student picker had a single flat category dropdown. It now has three cascading dropdowns: Parent category, Sub-category (dynamically shows only children of the chosen parent, via data-parent), and Course (dynamically shows only courses under the chosen sub-category, via data-catpath — same mechanism as usi_settings.php). Parent/sub narrow the student list by the student's category PATH; Course narrows to students who hold a result in that course (student options now carry data-catpath + data-courses; server builds the category tree + per-student course ids). The existing typeahead + qualification filter are unchanged. Ports to qualbuilder_results.php and qual_cert_hub.php will follow the same pattern once this is screenshot-verified. Files: soa_issue.php. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.76'; // v6.2.76 CERT EDITOR FULL-LENGTH COLUMNS + KNOWLEDGE-BASE CONSOLIDATION. (1) EDITOR SCROLL: the certificate editor locked all three columns above the fold with position:sticky + max-height:calc(100vh-…) + overflow-y:auto, producing four internal scrollbars (left palette, ASQA validator box, properties list, canvas). Removed those internal scroll containers so each column flows to its natural length and the PAGE scrolls; the canvas keeps horizontal-only scroll for wide/landscape templates. Files: styles.css (.rtoc-tmpl-left/.rtoc-tmpl-right/.rtoc-validator-top/.rtoc-props-section/.rtoc-tmpl-canvas-wrap). (2) KB CONSOLIDATION: the Support page's 83-answer Q&A was siloed in support.php and invisible to the AI assistant. Extracted it into support_content.php::local_rtocompliance_support_faq_data() (single source of truth — support.php now renders from it) and wired it into the assistant knowledge base, so the chatbot now answers from page help + FAQ + Support content together. Added a USI E2003 / ATO Access Manager answer to the FAQ (auto-flows to the chatbot). Fixed stale "Standards for RTOs 2015" -> 2025 in two support answers. Files: support.php, support_content.php (new), faq_content.php, lib.php (assistant KB). No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.75'; // v6.2.75 SoA VALIDATOR: "FORM PART OF" IS THE ONLY RELATIONSHIP STATEMENT RECOMMENDED. On a Statement of Attainment the ASQA compliance recommendations listed BOTH "These competencies form part of [code and title]" AND a "completion of course" line. Per ASQA's Sample forms of AQF certification documentation, "form part of" is the correct relationship statement for units that are part of a qualification; the "[CODE] course in [FULL TITLE]" completion line is only for accredited courses ("if applicable"). Removed qualificationCompletionOfCourseStatement from the 'statement' recommended_fields so "form part of" is the sole recommended relationship statement, and sharpened its help text. Neither was ever a REQUIRED field, so approval behaviour is unchanged; the completion-of-course field still exists in the catalogue if an RTO deliberately needs it for an accredited course — it is simply no longer recommended/blocked-on for a SoA. Files: classes/certificate_validator.php. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.74'; // v6.2.74 ASSISTANT: RECOLOUR FROM PURPLE TO THE PLUGIN BLUE SCHEME. The floating assistant used an indigo/purple palette that clashed with the RTO Compliance plugin's blue UI (sidebar accent #2563eb / #1d4ed8, blue-50 fills). Every purple/indigo value in the assistant widget CSS was remapped to the plugin blue: primary #4f46e5->#2563eb, #7c3aed->#1d4ed8, #9333ea->#1e40af; chip/user text #4338ca->#1d4ed8; hover gradient ends ->#1e40af/#1e3a8a; focus ring/dots #a5b4fc->#93c5fd; chip border #c7d2fe->#bfdbfe; light fills #eef2ff->#eff6ff, #e0e7ff->#dbeafe; and rgba(79,70,229)/rgba(99,102,241) glows->rgba(37,99,235). Scoped to the widget CSS block only (the sidebar gradient is untouched). No markup/JS change. Files: lib.php (assistant widget CSS in local_rtocompliance_assistant_widget_html). No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.73'; // v6.2.73 ASSISTANT ICON SIZES + STALE STRING CLEANUP. (1) ICONS: since v6.2.68 the assistant renders inside the plugin's main region, where the plugin's scoped SVG rules shrank the mic/send/orb/avatar icons to a few pixels. Every assistant icon size is now pinned under #rtoc-asst-root with !important (send/mic 18px, FAB 24px, orb 20px, avatar 15px, credit-clock 13px), so no plugin/theme SVG rule can override them. (2) STALE STRINGS: removed the old "Essaygraderai" product/domain wording from two user-facing strings — the Support Docs menu label (lang/en) and the AI-analysis "API key not configured" error (classes/external.php) now say "Support Docs" / "Platform API key". Files: lib.php (assistant icon CSS), lang/en/local_rtocompliance.php, classes/external.php. No schema change, no new savepoint. (Broader help/support knowledge-base consolidation — wiring the Support page Q&A into the chatbot + adding the USI E2003 answer — is in progress for the next release.)
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.72'; // v6.2.72 ASSISTANT: VOICE INPUT (MICROPHONE) FOR MOBILE + PC. Adds a mic button to the assistant's input row that dictates the user's question via the browser's built-in Web Speech API (window.SpeechRecognition/webkitSpeechRecognition) — no backend, no credits, no external service. Feature-detected: the button only appears where the browser supports speech recognition (Chrome/Edge desktop + Android, Safari iOS 14.5+), so it degrades gracefully elsewhere. Live interim transcription streams into the textarea and appends to anything already typed; the mic turns red and pulses while listening; tap again (or close the panel) to stop; a blocked-mic permission shows a helpful tooltip. Also hardened the send + mic buttons under #rtoc-asst-root with !important so the academi theme's global button:hover styling cannot wash them out (same pattern as the FAB/chips). Files: js/rtoc_assistant.js (plain js/ script, not AMD — no amd/build copy), lib.php (mic/send CSS in local_rtocompliance_assistant_widget_html). No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.71'; // v6.2.71 USI: SEND SITE CREDENTIALS IN camelCase TOO (defensive, matches the credits contract). Deep-check follow-up to the assistant "out of credits" fix: usi_platform_client::verify_usi() posted /api/usi/verify with only lowercase {siteid, apikey} (+ X-Site-Id/X-Api-Key headers) — the same gap the assistant had, and inconsistent with this function already sending BOTH firstName/firstname and dob/dateofbirth. It now also sends camelCase {siteId, apiKey} so site identity can never silently mismatch whichever keys the endpoint reads. Confirmed there is NO stale essaygraderai.app URL anywhere in the plugin — apiurl is config-driven (default lms-labs.com), the same value the working credits widget resolves to, so the domain change is not a USI factor. NOTE: the documented USI blocker was ATO error E2003 (returned only AFTER the platform authenticates the site and calls the Registry), which indicates site-auth already works for USI; this change removes camelCase as a variable but is not expected to be the E2003 fix (that remains ATO Access Manager, client-side). Files: classes/usi/usi_platform_client.php. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.70'; // v6.2.70 ASSISTANT: FIX "OUT OF CREDITS" DESPITE A HEALTHY BALANCE + CHIP HOVER READABILITY. (1) OUT-OF-CREDITS: the sidebar credits widget POSTs /api/credits with camelCase {siteId, apiKey} and correctly shows the site's balance (e.g. 3,469), but local_rtocompliance_assistant_ask() POSTed /api/assistant/ask with only lowercase {siteid, apikey}. The platform ask endpoint did not recognise the site from the lowercase keys and returned "out of credits" even though the SAME siteid/apikey have credits (proven by the working credits call to the SAME lms-labs.com host — so this is NOT the essaygraderai.app→lms-labs.com domain change and NOT a Central Config/plugin siteid mismatch: both paths resolve identical creds). Fix: the ask payload now sends BOTH camelCase (siteId/apiKey, matching the credits contract) and lowercase (back-compat). (2) CHIP HOVER: the academi theme's global button:hover{color:#fff} turned the indigo suggestion-chip text white on the near-white chip background on hover; chip colour/background are now scoped under #rtoc-asst-root with !important incl. :hover/:focus so the theme cannot override them. Files: lib.php (assistant_ask payload + assistant widget chip CSS). No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.69'; // v6.2.69 ASSISTANT FAB: HARDEN LABEL COLOUR AGAINST THEME HOVER OVERRIDE. On the academi theme the global button:hover/.btn styling flipped the floating "Ask AI" button's background to a light colour on hover, leaving its white label unreadable ("hover text too light"). Fix: the FAB colour/background rules are now scoped under #rtoc-asst-root (higher specificity) with !important on color+background, an explicit dark-gradient :hover/:focus background so the theme can no longer lighten it, and the label/icon spans forced to #fff. Purely a CSS hardening of the existing widget; no markup/JS/behaviour change. ALSO FIXED in this build: the first assistant question errored with 'Exception - Class "curl" not found' because assistant.php is an AJAX_SCRIPT that does not auto-include lib/filelib.php (where Moodle's \curl class is defined); local_rtocompliance_assistant_ask() now require_once's lib/filelib.php before its platform + direct-key curl branches (the teams_notify helper already did this; the assistant path was missed). Files: lib.php (assistant widget CSS + filelib require in local_rtocompliance_assistant_ask). No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.68'; // v6.2.68 AI ASSISTANT NOW RENDERS ON THEMES THAT DROP HOOK HTML (e.g. "academi"). Root cause found from a live page dump on the ITALC academi theme: that theme silently discards HTML added through the before_footer_html_generation AND before_standard_top_of_body_html_generation output hooks (the plugin's own footer-injected tablesorter.js was absent too), so the v6.2.67 top-of-body move could never work there — enabled + staff + creds-ready were all satisfied and the widget still never reached the DOM. FIX: the assistant is now emitted from the plugin's OWN main-region output (new lib helper local_rtocompliance_assistant_widget_html(), appended inside local_rtocompliance_render_sidebar()), which renders on every theme because it is page body content, not hook output — exactly where the sidebar + sidebar.js/tables.js already render reliably. The FAB is position:fixed so it still floats bottom-right. Same gating as before (assistant_enabled != '0' default on, staff/admin, local_rtocompliance_assistant_creds ready). The v6.2.67 before_standard_top_of_body_html_generation hook was reverted (file + db/hooks.php registration removed) so there is a single injection point. Files: lib.php (new helper + render_sidebar call), db/hooks.php (hook removed), classes/hook/before_standard_top_of_body_html_generation.php (deleted). No schema change, no new savepoint. NOTE: pages that do not call render_sidebar/render_nav_header (rare — they also have no sidebar) will not show the assistant on hook-dropping themes.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.67'; // v6.2.67 (superseded by v6.2.68 — see above) AI ASSISTANT MOVED FROM FOOTER TO TOP-OF-BODY HOOK. First attempt at the "assistant not showing" report: moved the widget out of before_footer_html_generation into a new before_standard_top_of_body_html_generation hook, on the theory the theme hid the footer. Correct that the footer was the problem, wrong that a different OUTPUT HOOK would help — the academi theme drops top-of-body hook HTML too. Superseded by the v6.2.68 main-region approach. The floating, Claude-powered help assistant was injected from the before_footer_html_generation hook, so its markup was emitted into the footer region. On a theme that hides or does not render the footer, an ancestor with display:none suppresses even a position:fixed descendant, so the assistant FAB never appeared even though it was enabled, the viewer was staff, and platform/API creds were ready. FIX: added a new hook callback classes/hook/before_standard_top_of_body_html_generation.php (registered in db/hooks.php) that injects the assistant right after <body> — a region every theme renders — and removed the assistant block from the footer hook. Identical enable/staff/creds gating (local_rtocompliance_assistant_creds), identical plugin-pages-only scope, identical bottom-right position:fixed placement and CSS/JS; no behaviour change other than WHERE the markup is emitted. The AVETMISS-details modal and placeholder-name repair banner (also footer-injected and position:fixed) were intentionally left in the footer hook and can be moved the same way if a theme is found to hide them too. Files: classes/hook/before_standard_top_of_body_html_generation.php (new), classes/hook/before_footer_html_generation.php, db/hooks.php. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.66'; // v6.2.66 TEAMS NOTIFICATIONS ON CERT ISSUANCE. Best-effort Microsoft Teams webhook when a certificate is issued. New helper local_rtocompliance_teams_notify($text) in lib.php reads integ_teams_enable + integ_teams_webhookurl config and POSTs json_encode(['text'=>...]) via Moodle \curl (same format as the integrations.php test message). Wired into BOTH issuance paths: programmatic bulk issue (lib.php after registry publish) and manual single issue (issue_certificate.php after registry publish). Fully try/catch wrapped and gated on integ_teams_enable==='1' with a valid https URL — a webhook failure can never throw or block issuance. No schema change, no new savepoint. PREV: v6.2.65 USI E2003 DIAGNOSTIC CORRECTED. The platform team confirmed via live logs that lms-labs.com IS sending the correct production relying party (https://portal.usi.gov.au/Service/v5/UsiService.svc) for TOID 30772. So the v6.2.61 message ("the platform sent the WRONG URL; NOT an Access Manager problem") was backwards. The connection test now states the confirmed reality: with the correct URL being sent, E2003 "relying party not recognised" means the ATO has not AUTHORISED the software credential for the USI Registry service — a ~5-minute fix in ATO Access Manager (am.ato.gov.au: add the "USI Registry" service to the credential's authorised services for the ABN), on the RTO side, not Moodle. Includes the rare EVTE/production-mismatch alternative. Files: usi_settings.php. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.64'; // v6.2.64 STICKY EDITOR TOOLBAR (position:sticky) so it stays pinned while the canvas scrolls. — the Undo/Zoom/Grid/Wide-canvas toolbar now stays pinned (position:sticky) while the canvas scrolls, so it no longer scrolls out of reach (UX audit Phase B). Single scoped CSS rule, no layout restructure, degrades gracefully. Files: styles.css. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.63'; // v6.2.63 EDITOR: SLIDE-OVER PROPERTIES PANEL + GOOGLE FONTS PICKER. (1) SLIDE-OVER: the right-hand Properties panel is now a slide-over — it appears when you select a field and the canvas takes the FULL width when nothing is selected (reuses the tested Wide-canvas collapse, with a smooth transition; a manual Wide-canvas click pins the state). This removes the permanent-panel cramping (SmartFormAI-style). (2) GOOGLE FONTS: the font picker now offers ~30 curated Google Fonts (sans/serif/display/handwriting/mono) in addition to the built-in Helvetica/Times/Courier. The editor canvas loads them as WEBFONTS and previews the real typeface. On the PDF each Google font renders in the closest built-in family (catalogue 'core') so certificates always render; if a TCPDF-ready embedded font file is added to fonts/<key>.php it is used verbatim for a pixel-exact PDF (bundling those font binaries is the documented follow-up). Any font error falls back to Helvetica — a certificate can never fail on a font. Files: classes/cert_template.php (font_catalogue), classes/cert_template_renderer.php (sanitise_font), cert_template_edit.php (picker + JS data), styles.css (slide transition), amd/src+build/cert_template_editor.js. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.62'; // v6.2.62 Student details table VALUES now CENTRE-ALIGNED under their headings. under their headings (STUDENT NAME / USI / QUALIFICATION) on the Record of Results — both the issued PDF (render_student_details_table) and the editor canvas mock, so the data sits centred beneath the centred headers. Carries all prior fixes (USI key-persist v6.2.59, E2003 diagnostic v6.2.61, alignment, clean previews). Files: classes/cert_template_renderer.php, amd/src+build/cert_template_editor.js. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.61'; // v6.2.61 USI E2003 DIAGNOSTIC + relying-party URL corrected. + relying-party URL corrected. The connection test now RECOGNISES ATO error E2003 ("the relying party specified in the AppliesTo element is not recognized") as a DISTINCT failure from a credential/authorisation problem, and states the real cause + fix: the PLATFORM (lms-labs.com) requested the ATO token for the WRONG USI relying-party URL. The correct PRODUCTION AppliesTo relying party is https://portal.usi.gov.au/Service/v5/UsiService.svc (production STS https://softwareauthorisations.ato.gov.au/R3.0/S007v1.3/service.svc). The legacy usi_registry_client constants (dead code, superseded by usi_platform_client) were corrected to the same value for reference so the platform mirrors it. NOTE: nothing in Moodle constructs the live AppliesTo — that is the platform — so the actual E2003 fix is a one-line platform change (see USI_E2003_PLATFORM_FIX.md). Carries the v6.2.59 API-key-persist fix + v6.2.60 alignment. Files: usi_settings.php, classes/usi/usi_registry_client.php. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.60'; // v6.2.60 ALIGNMENT — vertical even-distribution feedback. Adds the vertical mirror of the horizontal distribution hint: while dragging, when a field has an equal gap to the nearest neighbour above AND below (elements sharing its column), teal distance badges confirm the even vertical spacing — matching the horizontal-row hint already present. Completes the Canva-style distribution feedback (drag guides, resize guides, match-size, snap-to-equal-spacing, align-on-page, and now vertical + horizontal distribution). Carries forward the v6.2.59 USI key-persist fix. Files: amd/src+build/cert_template_editor.js. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.59'; // v6.2.59 USI KEY-PERSIST FIX (persist platform apikey/siteid to local_aiconfig too — closes the 401 verify loop). (THE verification-loop fix) + alignment snap-to-equal-spacing. USI: on cert upload the platform issues/re-confirms the API key + site id (on first registration AND on re-upload where the stored key drifted). The plugin previously saved these ONLY to local_rtocompliance config, but the USI client reads Central Config (local_aiconfig) FIRST — so the freshly-issued key never took effect and every later /api/usi/verify returned 401, the exact "uploaded many times but nothing verifies" loop. usi_settings.php now persists the returned apikey (>=16 chars) AND siteid to BOTH local_rtocompliance AND local_aiconfig (when installed). upload_cert() already returns apikey/siteid (reads apikey/apiKey/api_key), so no client change was needed. ALSO: certificate editor now snaps a dragged field's centre to the even-spacing midpoint between its nearest row/column neighbours (teal guide), completing the Canva-style distribution snapping. Files: usi_settings.php, amd/src+build/cert_template_editor.js. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.58'; // v6.2.58 CANVA-STYLE ALIGNMENT AIDS. The certificate editor already snapped + drew guide lines while DRAGGING (to other elements' left/centre/right + top/middle/bottom edges, the page centre, border and safe margins, with equal-distance and even-distribution badges). This adds: (1) SNAP GUIDES WHILE RESIZING — the moving edge now snaps to the same alignment targets (elements/page/margins/centre) with the guide line drawn live (resize previously had no guides at all); (2) MATCH-SIZE SNAP — width/height snaps to equal another element's width/height while resizing; (3) ONE-CLICK ALIGN-ON-PAGE — an "Align on page" button row in the Properties panel (left / centre-H / right / top / centre-V / bottom), where centre-H gives instant equal side margins ("equal distance from the edges"). Files: amd/src+build/cert_template_editor.js (alignTargetsX/Y, nearestTarget, nearestSize, alignSelectedOnPage, resize snapping, wireAlignToolbar), cert_template_edit.php (align toolbar in Properties). No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.57'; // v6.2.57 CLEAN PDF PREVIEW + STUDENT-RESULTS FILTER BAR + DYNAMIC COURSE FILTER + USI DIAGNOSTIC. (1) CLEAN PDF PREVIEW everywhere: the editor live preview and the templates-hub "Live certificate previews" now hide the browser PDF viewer chrome — the thumbnail side panel, toolbar and status bar — and fit-to-width, so you see the whole certificate cleanly instead of a two-pane document viewer. Editor preview switched from POST-to-iframe to fetch->blob URL with #toolbar=0&navpanes=0&view=FitH (falls back to the classic POST if fetch fails, so it can never be worse). (2) STUDENT RESULTS (qualbuilder_results.php) filter bar rebuilt as a responsive CSS grid — it no longer collapses into a full-width vertical stack (caused by Bootstrap .form-control{width:100%} on bare flex children); search on top, filters across the page, actions in their own row. (3) DYNAMIC CATEGORY->COURSE on the USI page: choosing a Category now filters the Course dropdown to that category and its subcategories (client-side, matched on the category path). (4) USI DIAGNOSTIC: the connection test now DECODES the ATO SOAP fault and, when the failure is at the ATO Machine-to-Machine security-token step (MAS-ST / softwareauthorisations.ato.gov.au), explains it is an ATO credential/authorisation problem (most likely the USI software authorisation for the ABN in ATO Access Manager) — not a Moodle fault — with an ordered checklist. Files: cert_templates.php, amd/src+build/cert_template_editor.js, qualbuilder_results.php, styles.css, usi_settings.php. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.56'; // v6.2.56 REVERT the v6.2.53 editor "app-shell" (it broke the layout — big grey gap, cramped canvas, PDF-viewer chrome). Removed the JS wireEditorShell()/.rtoc-shell fixed-height mode and its CSS; the editor is back to the stable pre-6.2.53 flow layout. KEPT the safe, non-breaking improvements from 6.2.53: overscroll-behavior:contain on the scroll panes (reduces scroll-bleed) and the quiet thin themed scrollbars. This is a clean base for the planned form-builder-style redesign (sticky header + tab strip, left field sidebar, dialog-based field editing, editor-left/preview-right). Files: styles.css, amd/src+build/cert_template_editor.js. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.55'; // v6.2.55 CERTIFICATE FIELD AUDIT — NO MORE BLANK-ON-ADD + PALETTE DEDUPE. Full review of every palette field against the ASQA "Sample forms of AQF certification documentation" fact sheet. (1) Optional-descriptor fields (industry descriptor, occupational stream, Australian Apprenticeship statement, language-of-delivery statement, skill-set statement) no longer render BLANK on the editor canvas when added — each now shows representative ASQA wording as its sample. (2) At ISSUE time the language statement defaults to "These units/modules have been delivered and assessed in English." and the Australian Apprenticeship line to its ASQA suggested wording when the RTO hasn't overridden them in settings, so a field the author deliberately placed is never blank on the issued testamur/Record of Results (ASQA requires the language statement on the testamur + RoR where applicable); industry descriptor + occupational stream stay blank-unless-configured because they are qualification-specific values with no universal default. (3) Palette de-duplicated: the legacy per-column RoR fields (RoR Col 1/2/3 — units_col_semester/names/results) were removed so there is exactly ONE units table per certificate type — the "Units of competency table (Statement of Attainment)" dynamic field for the SoA and the dedicated "Record of Results table" chip for the RoR; existing templates carrying the old column keys keep rendering. Files: classes/cert_template.php, classes/cert_template_renderer.php. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.54'; // v6.2.54 TEST CERTIFICATE NUMBER USES REAL FORMAT. The "Send a test / preview" certificate generator (cert_test.php) previously showed a placeholder number "TEST-TEST-<timestamp>" (strtoupper(substr(certtype,0,4)).'-TEST-'.date('YmdHis')), so a testamur preview read e.g. "TEST-TEST-20260806153350". It now uses local_rtocompliance_generate_cert_number($certtype), so the preview shows the true issued format {certprefix}-{TYPECODE}-{YYYY}-{NNNN} (testamur=CER), e.g. CBF-CER-2026-0001 when the Certificate Prefix setting is "CBF". The preview cert is never saved (id=0), so no sequence is reserved. Real issuance already used this format. Files: cert_test.php. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.53'; // v6.2.53 CERTIFICATE EDITOR — SCROLL ISOLATION + APP-SHELL UX. The editor is now a fixed-height three-pane workspace (palette | canvas+preview | settings) where the PAGE no longer scrolls: each pane scrolls INDEPENDENTLY. Fixes the "clunky" bleed where wheeling the right-hand settings/inspector panel also scrolled the certificate preview. Added overscroll-behavior:contain to every scroll pane, a JS wheel-isolation guard on the side panels (a pane that can't scroll further no longer chains to the page), a JS app-shell that sizes the grid to the viewport (wireEditorShell; wide screens only — the ≤1100px stacked/responsive layout is unchanged and it degrades gracefully if JS is off), a pinned toolbar while the canvas scrolls, and quiet themed thin scrollbars on all panes. Files: styles.css, amd/src+build/cert_template_editor.js. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.52'; // v6.2.52 TABLE AUTO-FIT + NO FORCED MINIMUM FONT. (1) Removed the forced 12pt minimum text size from ALL certificates (renderer + editor + canvas): the author's chosen font size is now honoured exactly (the old max(12,size) clamp and the 10mm text-field height floor are gone; editor allows down to 4pt). (2) NEW table auto-fit engine (fit_font_to_columns): both the Record of Results 5-column table and the Statement of Attainment 3-column table now auto-shrink the BODY font (from the author's size down to a ~6pt safety floor) until every fixed-width cell — enrolment date, unit code, result code, completion date — fits on ONE line, so unit codes can NEVER be clipped/truncated again (fixes codes like "BSBCRT311" printing as "BSBCRT31"). Unit titles still wrap. (3) Uniform TWO-ROW header bars: header font shrinks so the longest heading word fits its column and the bar is a fixed two-line height, so caps headings ("COMPLETION DATE" etc.) always fit and read evenly. (4) Rebalanced RoR columns (wider UNIT CODE, narrower RESULT). (5) SoA date column header changed to simply "DATE". (6) Record of Results AUTO-ADOPTS the student details table at render time (cert_template::upgrade_record_identity_to_table): existing templates using the legacy "Name of student:/USI:" stacked rows now render the shaded STUDENT NAME | USI | QUALIFICATION table without any rebuild (conservative gate; render-time only, never mutates saved templates). Files: classes/cert_template_renderer.php, classes/cert_template.php, cert_template_edit.php, amd/src+build/cert_template_editor.js. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.51'; // v6.2.51 RECORD OF RESULTS REDESIGN + AUTO-DESIGN REMOVED. (1) The Record of Results units table is now the full ASQA-mapped five-column layout -- ENROLMENT DATE | UNIT CODE | UNIT TITLE | RESULT | COMPLETION DATE (caps headers) -- with the RESULT column printing the nationally-recognised transcript code (C / NYC / CT / RPL, mapped from the AVETMISS outcome identifier) and a result-code KEY printed directly beneath the table for student reference. New renderer render_ror_full_table(); rows now carry enrolment (activity start) + result code alongside the existing completion date. (2) NEW student.detailstable dynamic field renders the student identity block as one shaded three-column table -- STUDENT NAME | USI | QUALIFICATION (qualification = "CODE TITLE", single space, no hyphen) -- replacing the stacked "Name of student:/USI:/Name of qualification:" label rows on the Record of Results starter. (3) The RTO code now renders as "TOID 30772" (TOID prefix) on every certificate type via format_rto_code(). (4) ASQA validator fix: an ror_table field now satisfies the units-of-competency requirement (previously it demanded a dynamic qualification.units field, so the ror_table-based Record of Results always errored with "drag the qualification.units field onto the canvas"); student.detailstable satisfies the student-name + qualification code/name requirements. (5) The "Auto-design from an image (AI)" feature was removed (unreliable field placement): button, JS, endpoint, config and language strings all withdrawn. Files: classes/cert_template_renderer.php, classes/cert_template.php, classes/certificate_validator.php, cert_template_edit.php, amd/src+build/cert_template_editor.js, lang/en/local_rtocompliance.php; removed cert_template_autodesign.php. No schema change, no new savepoint (rendering + validation only).
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.50'; // v6.2.50 AI ASSISTANT NOW APPEARS WHEN CONFIGURED VIA CENTRAL CONFIG. Shared resolver local_rtocompliance_assistant_creds() reads Central Config (local_aiconfig) first, falls back to plugin settings; both the footer-hook gate and the ask endpoint use it. No schema change, no new savepoint.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.49'; // v6.2.49 USI CONNECTION-TEST RESULT NOW VISIBLE. FIX "Run connection test doesn't show any results": the conntest handler previously redirected with a notification, but verify_usi() calls \core\session\manager::write_close() (closes the session for the rest of the request), so the redirect-carried message was silently lost. The handler now captures the outcome into $conntestmsg/$conntestok (with try/catch) and renders it inline via $OUTPUT->notification() straight after the page header -- PASS (green) when the platform reached the USI registry, FAIL (red) with a plain-English cause (no credential uploaded for this TOID, or Site ID / API key not set in Central Config) otherwise. Files: usi_settings.php. No schema change. No new savepoint (no DB change).
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.48'; // v6.2.48 TAS STRUCTURAL COMPLETION. Adds two fields to complete the TAS audit set: RPL PATHWAY (documented RPL process -- evidence methods, authenticity/currency, gap training -- previously RPL was only an assessment-method checkbox) and TRAINER-to-UNITS MAPPING (each trainer/assessor mapped to the units they deliver + Credential-Policy classification + industry currency/CPD, Standards 3.1-3.3). New DB columns added additively via a guarded upgrade step. Files: db/install.xml, db/upgrade.php, tas_edit.php. Savepoint 2026080500663.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.47'; // v6.2.42 INTEGRATIONS. New "Integrations" left-menu item (under Set Up Your RTO) and integrations.php page to connect RTO Compliance to external business systems: NetSuite (ERP -- push issued certificates / student / enrolment records via REST token auth), Salesforce (CRM -- sync learners as Contacts + completions via a Connected App / OAuth), and Microsoft Teams (send compliance notifications via an Incoming Webhook). Stores each service's connection settings (secrets are write-only in the form), shows a Configured / Incomplete / Disabled status per service, and provides a LIVE "Send test message to Teams" webhook test. The NetSuite/Salesforce data-sync jobs are wired in a follow-up once the exact objects to sync are confirmed. Files: integrations.php (new), lib.php (nav item). No schema change (uses plugin config). Savepoint 2026080500657.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.41'; // v6.2.41 TAS VOLUME-OF-LEARNING FIX. The TAS editor no longer auto-copies the qualification's total NOMINAL (supervised) hours into the Volume of Learning field. AQF volume of learning includes unsupervised learning + assessment and is almost always greater than nominal hours; pre-filling them equal understated VoL and steered RTOs toward under-delivery -- the single most common ASQA finding. Nominal hours are still pre-filled (legitimate); VoL is now left for the RTO to set against the AQF range for the qualification's level. Files: tas_edit.php. No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500656.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.40'; // v6.2.40 DESIGN SYSTEM PHASE 0 (foundation). Added the single-source-of-truth component classes .rtoc-card and .rtoc-info (+ --blue/--green/--amber/--red modifiers) built from the existing token layer, as the standard for cards and info/help boxes across the plugin. These are INERT until pages adopt them (no page markup changed, so zero visual regression), and become the target for the incremental page-by-page migration away from the ~2,080 hand-rolled inline styles / 12 different info-box backgrounds documented in the design audit. Files: styles.css. No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500655.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.39'; // v6.2.39 TAS ANTI-FABRICATION + HONEST COMPLETENESS. (1) The industry-consultation narrative no longer asserts "the feedback received has been incorporated..." unconditionally -- it only states feedback informed the design when a training or assessment impact was actually recorded, otherwise it inserts an explicit "[RTO to record...]" placeholder (removes an unsupported claim from a compliance document). (2) The consultation DOCX no longer pre-writes a fabricated industry "finding" ("Industry representatives consistently indicated...") before any consultation has happened -- it now prompts the RTO to record only the feedback genuinely received. (3) TAS completeness score: Work Placement (Section 8) is no longer an unconditional +1 -- it counts only when placement is not required, or is required AND details are provided, so a near-empty TAS no longer reports inflated completeness. Files: lib.php, tas_consultation.php, tas_edit.php. No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500654.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.38'; // v6.2.38 TAS AI PROMPTS -> 2025 STANDARDS + RESPONSIBLE AI. Rewrote the Training & Assessment Strategy / industry-consultation AI prompts to reflect the 2025 Standards for RTOs and ASQA practice guides: corrected the clause numbering (Industry Engagement is Standard 1.2, not 1.4/4.1; assessment is 1.3-1.5, not 1.8/1.12; removed the non-existent "Standard 1.12" transition citation), added strict anti-fabrication rules (use only provided facts; bracketed [RTO to confirm] placeholders instead of invented consensus/statistics), online/blended AUTHENTICITY expectations (learner identity verification, supervision, that evidence is the student's own work and not plagiarised or AI-generated, scheduled human touchpoints), and a mandatory human-review disclaimer on every draft (ASQA responsible-AI: AI assists, people decide). The client "AI Suggest" call now sends this ASQA grounding as a guidance payload, and the misleading "using ASQA practice guide context" loading label was corrected to "AI-assisted draft for you to review". Files: ajax.php, js/ai_suggest.js. No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500653.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.37'; // v6.2.37 TABLE/DISPLAY POLISH. (1) USI column: the USI code, status pill and Verify button now STACK vertically (new .rtoc-usi-cell flex column) instead of sitting side-by-side, so the USI column no longer forces the whole table wide. (2) Full-screen table view: locked the root <html> element as well as <body> when the overlay is open, removing the second (page-behind) vertical scrollbar. (3) Qualification Certificate Hub table adopted into the shared .rtoc-table-wrapper full-width system (removed the raw inline overflow-x div + min-width), so it fills the width and wraps rather than showing wasted space + a horizontal scrollbar. Files: students.php, qual_cert_hub.php, styles.css, js/tables.js. No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500652.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.36'; // v6.2.36 USI VERIFY-LOOP HARDENING. (1) Status mapping normalises the platform status string and maps unrecoverable outcomes (NOT_FOUND/INACTIVE/DEACTIVATED/INVALID_INPUT/INVALID_FORMAT) to a TERMINAL failed state, and mismatches (PARTIAL_MATCH/NO_MATCH/NOT_VERIFIED) to manual review, so structurally-bad records stop re-queuing every run forever; only genuinely transient outcomes stay pending. (2) The batch loop now ABORTS the run on a site-level auth/config fault (AUTH_ERROR/NOT_CONFIGURED) instead of hammering 25 students with bad credentials (which risks platform key rate-limiting/suspension), and surfaces a clear "fix the credential and re-run" message. (3) The scheduled task no longer zeroes out the whole run when the /api/usi/status ping momentarily fails or reports cert-not-ready -- it logs the ping result and still attempts the batch, letting each verify call gate itself. Files: classes/usi/usi_verification_service.php, classes/task/verify_usi_batch_task.php. No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500651.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.35'; // v6.2.35 NAT EXPORT COMPLIANCE FIX (AVETMISS record lengths + referential integrity). Reverses the v5.9.319 regression that prepended the RTO code to the client-attribute NAT files, which broke their record lengths and failed AVS validation + the plugin's own unit tests: NAT00080 337->327, NAT00085 571->557 (also removed the spurious country field; country-of-birth is carried in NAT00080), NAT00090 22->12, NAT00100 23->13 (and its "not stated" default is now the correct 3-char @@@), NAT00060 133->123 (subject identifier is field 1, no org field). NAT00020 delivery-location name restored from a truncated 50 to the spec 100 chars, so the record is the correct 180. NAT00120 program identifier now prefers the national programcode (matching NAT00030 and NAT00130) to fix a cross-file referential-integrity error. These make the failing NAT PHPUnit assertions pass. Note: run the plugin's PHPUnit suite to confirm green before a live AVS submission; remaining MEDIUM items (NAT00030 field set, NAT00130 issued-flag length, hardcoded outcome/funding defaults, blank Field of Education) are documented for a follow-up. Files: classes/nat_generator.php. No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500650.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.34'; // v6.2.34 FULL-WIDTH TABLES (design overhaul, phase 1). Removed the max(1000px,100%) minimum-width floor that forced every wrapped table (including the USI / student list) to overflow its column area and show an unnecessary horizontal scrollbar with wasted space either side. Tables now fill 100% of their container and wrap long cell content (display best practice); only genuinely wide, many-column tables opt into a scroll floor via the new .rtoc-table--wide class, and the 15-column trainers table keeps its wide floor. Global CSS only, no page markup changed. Files: styles.css. No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500649.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.33'; // v6.2.33 USI CREDENTIAL UPLOAD ROBUSTNESS + SITEID PERSIST. (1) FIX the "Could not read the credential file, or it looks empty/too small to be a keystore" error: the handler now decodes $upload['error'] into a specific message (upload-size limit, interrupted, no file, tmp-dir, etc.), moves the upload out of PHP's tmp dir with move_uploaded_file() before reading (file_get_contents on the raw tmp path fails under open_basedir on hardened hosts -> returned false -> the misleading message), drops the error-suppressing @, and splits "read failed" from "empty/too small" with the actual byte count. (2) On self-service credential upload, also persist the platform-returned SITEID (not just the apikey) so later verify calls don't send a mismatched siteid/apikey pair and 401. Files: usi_settings.php. No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500648.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.32'; // v6.2.32 USI PAGE - CATEGORY / SUBCATEGORY / COURSE FILTERS. The USI verification page gains a "Category" dropdown (indented to show subcategories; scopes to the chosen category AND all its descendant subcategories via the category path) and a "Course" dropdown (a specific course overrides the category). Scoping is by Moodle enrolment (user_enrolments -> enrol -> course -> course_categories), so an admin can check USI status for a whole category, subcategory, or single course. The filter, count, pagination and CSV exports all honour the new scope. Files: usi_settings.php. No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500647.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.31'; // v6.2.31 USI RE-VERIFY HOTFIX + EDITOR PHASE 3 (wide canvas). (1) FIX: "Re-verify everyone" on the USI settings page threw "Incorrect number of query parameters. Expected 1, got 0" -- the UPDATE that resets failed (status 2) students carried a :now placeholder but no params array was passed to $DB->execute(). Now passes ['now' => time()]. (2) Editor: new "Wide canvas" toolbar toggle collapses the right properties inspector to give the design canvas the full width (click again to restore). Files: usi_settings.php, cert_template_edit.php, styles.css, amd/src+build/cert_template_editor.js. No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500646.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.30'; // v6.2.30 EDITOR PHASE 2 - 8-WAY RESIZE HANDLES. Selected elements now show eight resize handles (four corners + four edge midpoints) instead of a single bottom-right corner. Edge/corner handles containing 'w' or 'n' drag the left/top edge and reposition x/y so the opposite edge stays fixed; 'e'/'s' grow the right/bottom edge. Preserves the 12pt/10mm text-height floor, min width 5mm, and page-bounds clamps. Line rules expose only the horizontal (w/e) handles. Handles restyled to a premium square accent; selection colour refreshed. Files: amd/src+build/cert_template_editor.js, styles.css. No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500645.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.29'; // v6.2.29 EDITOR PHASE 1 - CANVA-STYLE SMART SNAPPING. Dragging an element now snaps to: the page outside border (0 / width / height), the page safety margins, the page centre, and every other element's left/centre/right + top/middle/bottom edges (alignment guides, purple; margin guides, grey). Adds equal-distance HINTS with mm badges (teal): when an element is equidistant from the two page edges, or evenly spaced between its nearest neighbours on each side, badges show the equal gaps. A persistent dashed safe-margin overlay is drawn on the canvas. All guides/badges are editor-only decoration (never saved into the design, never seen by the renderer). Files: amd/src+build/cert_template_editor.js. No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500644.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.28'; // v6.2.28 AUTO-DESIGN HARDENING (perfect-every-time pass 1, plugin side). apply loop: per-field CONFIDENCE gating (skips low-confidence detections when the platform supplies a score), FORBIDDEN-FIELD guard (never places e.g. nrt_logo on a completion cert via catalogue forbidden_for), QR square-lock, and an "ignored detections" report (forbidden / low-confidence / unrecognised) shown to the author. Upload: client-side downscale to <=2000px + JPEG re-encode on white (fixes "image too large" + phone-photo/PNG/webp reliability) and an orientation-mismatch warning when the platform reports a detected source orientation. Proxy/helper: server-side validation of the returned fields (key must be an offered key, fractions clamped to 0..1, align sanitised) and pass-through of confidence + detected_orientation. Renderer: ALL logo/seal/signature images now fit-box (aspect preserved, centred) so the PDF respects the box width AND height and matches the editor (no more width-lock divergence / downward overflow). Files: amd/src+build/cert_template_editor.js, lib.php, cert_template_autodesign.php, cert_template_renderer.php. No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500643.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.27'; // v6.2.27 CORRECTNESS: competencies statement + ASQA rules + RTO-logo leniency. (1) "These competencies form part of..." / completion-of-course now accept accredited course codes (digits-first e.g. 10904NAT) and render code-only when the name was stripped, and the completion sample is no longer blank in the editor -- fixes the blank-item report. (2) ASQA validator corrected per Sample Forms fact sheet: USI now optional (recommended) on Record of Results; signatory signature image + title now recommended (only the authorised person NAME is required); organisation seal is accepted AS the authenticity measure (seal OR QR OR verify-URL) rather than separately required; a mandatory ISSUE DATE check is now enforced on testamur/statement/record. Catalogue "Required" chips updated to match. (3) New setting "RTO logo already includes the RTO name and code" -- when on, the validator no longer requires separate RTO name/code fields. Files: certificate_validator.php, cert_template.php, cert_template_renderer.php, settings.php, lang. No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500642.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.26'; // v6.2.26 SECOND LOGOS PLACEABLE -- added rto.secondary_logo ("Secondary RTO / partner logo") and compliance_logo_2 ("Compliance logo 2") to the dynamic field catalogue so both now appear in the editor palette and can be positioned/sized like any element and detected by auto-design. Both already resolve in the PDF renderer, so they render on issue; the editor canvas shows a labelled placeholder (the real image shows in the live PDF preview). No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500641.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.25'; // v6.2.25 EDITOR: SIZE-PERSISTENCE + SNAP-TO-CENTRE + FULL-SCREEN PREVIEW. (1) normalise_design no longer force-sizes nrt_logo/organisation_seal/qrcode (was h=30mm / QR 30x30 on every render) -- it only supplies a default when the field has no size, so resizing logos/QR/seal on screen now persists on save AND render instead of reverting. (2) Properties panel gains "Centre across" / "Centre down" buttons to centre the selected element on the page in one click. (3) Live preview PDF now opens single-page, fit-to-page, no thumbnail sidebar (TCPDF SetDisplayMode via a preview-only render flag), the frame is much larger (80vh), and a "Full screen" button (Esc to exit) fills the viewport. Files: classes/cert_template.php, classes/cert_template_renderer.php, cert_template_preview.php, cert_template_edit.php, styles.css, amd/src+build/cert_template_editor.js. No schema change. Savepoint 2026080500640.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.24'; // v6.2.24 AUTO-DESIGN-FROM-IMAGE REBUILD -- the cert auto-design import now applies POSITION + SIZE ONLY onto the existing seeded ASQA elements. It no longer overrides fonts/sizes/styles (fixes "fonts get changed on import"), no longer REPLACES the whole layout (undetected seeded elements are left in place instead of being wiped), and skips any detected field with no usable coordinates instead of dumping it at (0,0). It can still add a known placeable element the starter lacked (e.g. a second logo) when detected, keeping that element's seeded styling. JS: applyAutodesignFields rewritten (amd/src + amd/build synced); confirm/status text updated. No PHP or schema change. Savepoint 2026080500639.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.23'; // v6.2.23 EDIT-MODE TOGGLE CSS FIX -- the navbar "Edit mode" switch rendered as a bare circle on plugin pages because the plugin's generic 1rem checkbox sizing squashed the Bootstrap .form-switch pill (a switch needs ~2em width). Added a scoped override that restores native switch width/height for real switches only (.form-switch or role="switch"); plugin form checkboxes are unaffected, and the pill track/knob come from core/theme CSS which was never overridden. CSS-only change, no PHP or schema change. Savepoint 2026080500638.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.22'; // v6.2.22 DOB BUTTON NAME-MATCH -- the "Fix missing DOB" / Sync DOBs from NAT button now adds a third matching path after client ID and ID number: a validated unique full-name match (mdl_user first+last vs NAT firstname+familyname, case- and word-order-insensitive). It accepts ONLY a name that maps to exactly one date of birth in the NAT data and is not shared by two students; it never overwrites an existing DOB. The completion message now reports a full breakdown: filled by client ID / ID number / unique name, skipped as ambiguous, and still unmatched. Reason: NAT client-identifier numbering does not line up with newer 5-digit clientid / blank idnumber students, so ID matching alone filled almost none. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080500637.
$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.21'; // v6.2.21 STUDENT RECORDS DOB CSV -- the Student Records page (missing-DOB view) gains a simple round-trip CSV: Download DOB template (CSV) of students missing a date of birth, fill the Date of birth column, and Upload DOB CSV to backfill. Rows match by client ID, then USI, then email; only blank DOBs are written. Complements the NAT00080 sync and the same tool on the USI Verification page.
