$plugin->release_prev = '6.2.15'; // v6.2.15 LIVE PREVIEW NOW MATCHES THE ISSUED CERTIFICATE (background image + org seal). The live preview used sample_payload(), which deliberately ignored the per-cert-type applies-to config and painted the system background image (and org seal) on EVERY cert type. So the Statement of Attainment / Record of Results / Completion previews showed the testamur-only decorative background even though the ISSUED certificate correctly omits it. Fixed: sample_payload() now honours cert_background_cert_types and org_seal_cert_types, exactly like real issuance — the background only appears on the cert types it is configured for (e.g. testamur). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400630. — prior v6.2.14 BIGGER PROPERTIES PANEL in the certificate editor. Selecting a field and reaching common controls (Alignment/centre, X/Y/W/H, Z-order) meant scrolling inside a tiny box, because the ASQA validator 'Recommendations' box at the top of the right column had no height limit and hogged the space. Fixes: (1) the validator box is now capped at ~190px and scrolls on its own, so the field Properties section gets the large majority of the column height; (2) the Properties section has a 320px minimum height and grows to fill the freed space; (3) the right column is widened from 320px to 400px so the property controls fit without wrapping or a horizontal scrollbar. So the property controls now fit with little or no scrolling. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400629. — prior v6.2.13 AUTO-DESIGN REPLACES (not adds) the layout. When you auto-design a template from an uploaded certificate image, the detected fields now REPLACE the current template layout instead of being added on top of it — previously every element was duplicated (two logos, two titles, two units tables, two signatures). The detected fields are built first and only replace the layout when at least one field is found, so a failed/empty detection never wipes the template; Undo restores the previous layout and nothing is saved until Save draft. Detected text fields also keep the 10mm minimum height so 12pt text does not clip. (Location/size precision is a separate platform-side vision improvement.) No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400628. — prior v6.2.12 THREE FIXES. (1) AUTO-DESIGN CURL CRASH: uploading an image to the AI auto-design feature failed with 'Class "curl" not found' — the AJAX endpoint (cert_template_autodesign.php) runs as AJAX_SCRIPT, which does NOT auto-load Moodle's lib/filelib.php where the \curl class lives. Now filelib.php is required in both the endpoint and the helper before \curl is used. (2) BACKGROUND IMAGE LEAKING ONTO NON-TESTAMUR CERTS: the system-wide certificate background image was appearing on the Statement of Attainment / Record of Results / Certificate of Completion live previews and PDFs, not just the testamur. Root cause: the per-cert-type applies-to check returned 'apply to ALL cert types' whenever its setting was empty — but a Moodle configmulticheckbox default (testamur only for the background, testamur+statement for the org seal) is only written to the DB when the settings page is SAVED. So an uploaded-but-unsaved setting behaved as the OPPOSITE of its intended default. The empty-config fallback now matches the settings-form defaults, so the background stays on the testamur (and the org seal on testamur+statement) until the RTO explicitly changes it. (3) EDITOR BUTTON HOVER CONTRAST: the certificate editor renders outside .rtoc-main-content, so the v6.2.11 outline-button hover fix did not reach it — 'Auto-design from an image (AI)' and 'Preview' showed white text on a white hover background. Added a matching guaranteed-contrast hover block scoped to the editor grid (.rtoc-tmpl-grid) plus the auto-design button by id. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400627. — prior v6.2.11 UI POLISH: certificate-template button hover contrast + minimum field height. (1) The Actions-column outline buttons on the Certificate Templates page (Edit, Preview, Make non-active, Archive, Duplicate, Reset to ASQA starter, Delete) had poor contrast on hover — the base '.btn color !important' rule and partial hover rules left dark text on a coloured/tinted hover background, and the Moodle theme could win the text colour. Added one definitive, high-specificity, last-in-cascade hover block (with !important) for every outline variant (primary/secondary/warning/danger/success/info, plus focus, and <a>/<button>/<input>): on hover each fills with its solid brand colour and switches to a guaranteed-contrast text colour (white, or near-black on amber), so the theme can no longer override it. (2) MINIMUM FIELD HEIGHT: because certificate text uses a 12pt minimum font, a field box shorter than ~10mm clips the bottom of the text. Text-bearing fields (text + dynamic) now enforce a 10mm minimum height everywhere — the editor Height box snaps values below 10mm up, the resize handle can no longer drag them shorter than 10mm, the canvas shows the floored height, and the issued PDF floors the text field's max-height at 10mm so even legacy templates with a too-short box no longer clip. Lines, boxes and images are exempt. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400626. — prior v6.2.10 BRANDING: replaced all remaining 'AI Grader' / 'Essay Grader AI' references with LMS-Labs.com. User-facing help text (Platform API Settings remote-configuration + webhook-key descriptions, AI usage report) now says 'LMS-Labs.com support' / 'LMS-Labs.com admin portal'; every file's @copyright header now reads 'LMS Labs'; stale certificate-verify URL comments updated from essaygradeai.app to lms-labs.com. Historical changelog entries left intact as a version record. No functional, schema or UI-logic changes. Savepoint 2026080400625. — prior v6.2.9 RECORD-OF-RESULTS compliance + AVETMISS export terminology. (1) ROR RESULTS COLUMN: the certificate units table can now show the assessment RESULT (Competent / Not Yet Competent) in its third column instead of a completion date. Per the ASQA 'Sample forms of AQF certification documentation', a Record of Results must show results — previously the styled table showed only a completion date, and a separate legacy header row (Semester/Year | Units/modules enrolled | Results) was rendered ABOVE it, producing a confusing double header. Both default Record of Results templates (portrait + landscape) now use a single styled table with its own header (Unit Code | Unit Title | Results) via a new field option col3mode='result'; the duplicate legacy header row is removed. Statements of Attainment keep the completion date (col3mode default 'date'), and every existing template is unchanged. A 'Third column shows' selector (Completion date / Results) is added to the editor properties so authors can switch existing Record of Results templates to the Results column. Renderer, editor canvas and live preview all honour the setting. (2) AVETMISS TERMINOLOGY on the Student Roster CSV: state and sex now use official AVETMISS labels — the not-stated fills (@@, @, blank) and legacy '99' render as 'Not stated' instead of leaking raw codes; sex '@' reads 'Not stated', 'X' reads 'Other'; state 09 reads 'Other Australian territory'. (3) The AI certificate auto-design endpoint is now live on the platform, so the v6.2.7 'Auto-design from an image (AI)' button works end to end. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400624. — prior v6.2.8 USI-VERIFIED ACCURACY (compliance-critical) + certificate header theme colour. (1) A read-only SQL cross-check of the Student Roster CSV export against the live database found the export was OVERSTATING USI verification: the 'USI Verified' column used a truthy test on the usiverified field, so status 3 (verification PENDING/stuck) printed as 'Yes'. In the DB only status 1 (STATUS_VERIFIED, confirmed against usi.gov.au) is truly verified — statuses 0/2/3/4 are not. The export therefore reported hundreds of students as verified when the true verified count was zero. Fixed by centralising the rule in one helper, local_rtocompliance_usi_is_verified() (verified == status 1 only), and routing EVERY 'is verified' decision through it — the roster CSV, the USI-health CSV, the students/roster badges, the certificate list USI-verified badges, the public verification page, and — critically — the certificate-issuance gates (programmatic issue in lib.php, reissue, email, bulk actions, Statement-of-Attainment AJAX, and the certificate validator). Pending/failed/manual-review USIs are now correctly treated as NOT verified everywhere, so AQF certs are no longer issued or reported as if the USI were verified when it is not. Explicit SQL comparisons (= 1, IN (0,3)) were already correct and are unchanged. NOTE: because no USI currently reaches status 1 on this site (the verification pipeline is returning pending), testamur/SoA issuance will now correctly block on 'USI not verified' until verification completes — fix the USI machine-credential/verification batch so students reach status 1. (2) CERT-HEADER-THEME-COLOUR: the shaded header bar on certificate tables (Record of Results, Statement of Attainment units table) now defaults to the site's Moodle theme primary/brand colour, resolved live via a shared helper and applied consistently across the editor canvas, the live preview and the issued PDF. New Certificate Settings toggle 'Use site theme colour for certificate table headers' (on by default); untick to use a custom colour. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400623. — prior v6.2.7 AI CERTIFICATE AUTO-DESIGN. New '✨ Auto-design from an image (AI)' button in the certificate template editor: upload a photo or scan of an existing certificate and the platform vision AI detects where each element sits (logo, RTO name, student name, signature, units table, dates, mandatory statements) and drops those fields onto the canvas roughly where they appear, for the author to nudge and Save. Flow: the editor posts the image to a new server-side proxy (cert_template_autodesign.php, capability + sesskey protected, keeps the API key server-side) which forwards it to the platform's /api/certtemplate/autodesign endpoint; detected boxes come back as page fractions and are mapped to mm and built via the existing field-starter logic (so each field keeps its correct kind and the 12pt minimum). Uses ~10 AI credits per run (platform-enforced); existing canvas fields are kept and detected fields are added on top. Requires the platform vision endpoint (built separately on the platform). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400622. — prior v6.2.6 CERTIFICATE EDITOR ROOT-CAUSE FIX + orientation filter. (1) ROOT CAUSE of Save/branding/preview all failing: the hidden live-preview form was NESTED inside the main editor form. HTML forbids nested forms, so the browser closed the main form ~250 lines early — orphaning the Save button and, worse, leaving a SECOND input named 'designjson' (empty) inside the main form that overrode the real one, so every save posted an empty payload and showed 'the layout data did not reach the server'. The preview form is now a sibling, not nested. This single fix restores Save draft, org seal / logo / NRT / signature uploads (which only post on a working save), AND the live preview (its form element was never created while nested). Prior 'malformed payload' fixes treated the symptom, not this. (2) MIN FONT 12 now enforced in the EDITOR too — the properties box floors at 12pt, the on-canvas text is clamped to 12, and a typed value below 12 snaps to 12, matching the PDF's existing 12pt floor (they previously disagreed, so 12 looked unenforced). (3) The dead 'Show sample data' checkbox (a no-op since v5.9.442) is replaced with an honest label — the canvas always shows sample data. (4) ASQA ACCURACY: the validator recommendation no longer says 'completed in pursuit of' (not ASQA wording) — corrected to ASQA's sample 'These competencies form part of [code and title of qualification]'. (5) NEW Certificate Settings option 'Certificate orientations you use' (portrait / landscape / both). The Certificate Templates page now lists only templates in the ticked orientation(s) and shows the preview in that orientation, decluttering the page; hidden templates are counted and never deleted. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400621. — prior v6.2.5 PLUGIN-WIDE PILL & TOOLTIP SWEEP + security hardening. (1) Added simply-written, first-time-user hover tooltips to every status pill, badge and stat tile across the whole plugin (Compliance Health, Students, Qual Builder, Qual Builder Results, Certificate Hub, Certificates, Trainers, Validation, Deadlines, National Validation, NAT Export, AI Usage, Reconcile, Data Import, Complaints, RPL, Transitions, Governance, Risk, Third Party, TAS) so a new user learns what each coloured pill and number means just by hovering — roughly 230 new tooltips. (2) Defence-in-depth: added an explicit manage-capability check to five admin pages (AI Usage report, Appeal edit, Audit, Audit log, Complaint edit) on top of their existing admin-page protection. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400620. — prior v6.2.4 Release-pipeline fix: removed a literal function-with-no-space substring from the changelog text in version.php that the style scanner flagged (it was inside a sentence describing an earlier fix, not actual code). No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400619. — prior v6.2.3 HELP PILLS now link to the lms-labs.com ASQA guide mirror. The practice-guide pill on each help card now opens the guide from a stable, self-owned mirror (https://lms-labs.com/guides/<slug>.pdf) instead of asqa.gov.au, so links never break when ASQA restructures its site. The platform re-fetches each official guide from ASQA monthly; until a guide is fetched the mirror returns a short notice pointing back to the ASQA page, so a pill is never a hard dead link. State Funding still points to the NCVER RTO Hub. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400618. — prior v6.2.2 SIMPLE-LANGUAGE HELP OVERHAUL COMPLETE + sticky bar + pill tooltips + bigger cards. (1) Rewrote the 'How to use it' steps (89 pages) and 'Key Features' (86 pages) into plain, numbered, day-1 English — every step names the exact button/field and acronyms are explained in everyday words. Together with v6.2.1 this means all four help-card tabs (What / Why / How / Key Features) are now first-time-user friendly on every page. (2) The top bar (Dashboard / page name / FAQ / Help) is now sticky so it stays visible as you scroll. (3) Added plain-English hover tooltips to the Course Map status pills (Total, Confirmed, Unconfirmed, QB-linked, Auto-detected, Manual) so a new user learns what each number means. (4) Increased the text size in the explainer cards across the plugin and enlarged the Course Map 'What is this?' card for readability. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400617. — prior v6.2.1 SIMPLE-LANGUAGE HELP OVERHAUL (What it is / Why it matters) + release-pipeline fixes. Rewrote the 'What it is' and 'Why it matters' help-card text on all 97 pages/tabs into plain, day-1 English a brand-new user understands on first read — every acronym is explained in everyday words (USI = the student ID number, AVETMISS = the national VET data standard, RPL = credit for prior skills, SoA = Statement of Attainment, TAS = training and assessment strategy, NAT files = the national report files) and each is one short sentence. Also fixed three release-pipeline errors: added @copyright and @license doc tags to faq.php and faq_content.php, and corrected a missing space after the function keyword in locations.php. (The 'How to use it' steps and 'Key Features' are being simplified in the next pass.) No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400616. — prior v6.2.0 NEW FAQ PAGE + plugin-wide tooltips/explainer cards. (1) Added a beautiful FAQ page (faq.php): 100 plain-English questions across 20 topics (Getting started, Qualifications, Course mapping, Students, USI, AVETMISS import/export, Certificates, Templates, SoA, Credits, Results, RPL, Trainers, TAS, Validation, Complaints, Governance, State funding, AI assistant), rendered as a pure-CSS accordion (no JavaScript, CSP-safe) with jump-to-topic chips and a Go-to-page link on every answer. Added to the left menu and registered as an admin page. A FAQ link now appears top-right of EVERY plugin page, and prominent FAQ call-to-action cards were added to the Support and How It Works pages. The AI assistant is automatically trained on all 100 FAQ answers (same shared content), so it gives the same simple answers and can point users to the FAQ. (2) Plugin-wide clarity sweep: added hover tooltips to table column headers and meaningful action buttons across ~40 pages, and added 'what this shows' explainer cards above data tables on pages that lacked them. (3) Fixed the cut-off 'Filter by qualification code' box on the Course Map. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400615. — prior v6.1.4 QUAL CERT HUB variant column + explainer card, and State Funding reference link. (1) The Qualification Certificate Hub table now has a dedicated VARIANT column showing each product's version/intake (e.g. a semester like 2026 S1 or an archived year) next to the qualification, so products sharing a code but differing by variant are distinguishable at a glance. (2) Added a 'What each column means' information card above the hub table explaining Enrolled/Complete/Issued/Pending/Queue (and the 5-credit cost), so the funnel — especially the autocert 'Queue' column — is clear. (3) The State Funding help pill is now a working link to the NCVER RTO Hub (AVETMISS reporting home), and the help-pill tooltip wording is generic (ASQA practice guide, or NCVER for AVETMISS). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400614. — prior v6.1.3 PLUGIN-WIDE WIDTH FIX + My Documents card styling. (1) Extended the CSS that absorbs inline fixed-pixel page-width caps to cover every large cap (1000-1500px), so ~15 pages that capped content width (Compliance Health, Compliance Map, ASQA Standards Map, NAT Validate, Qualification Builder edit/auto-create/recover, Reconcile, SoA, Trainer currency/vocational competency, Support and others) now fill the available width and expand when the left sidebar is collapsed, instead of leaving empty space on the right. (2) My Documents & Certificates: the 'Issued Certificates' and 'Uploaded Documents' sections used the dark navy rtoc-clause-banner (white title, no body styling), so the muted empty-state text was unreadable on dark; they are now standard white content cards matching the plugin design, and every column header and action button on the page has a hover tooltip. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400613. — prior v6.1.2 FIX: USI Verification Status page (usi_settings.php) errored when opened from the admin tree / left menu. It is registered as an admin external page but was doing manual require_login()/set_pagelayout('admin') instead of admin_externalpage_setup(); it now calls admin_externalpage_setup('local_rtocompliance_usi_pertenant') as required, loads filelib (so the \curl class is always available), and wraps the platform status call in a guard so a network/platform issue shows a graceful 'status unavailable' message instead of taking the page down. Confirmed with the platform that the USI endpoints (/api/usi/status, /api/usi/verify) are unchanged and current, so no re-wiring was needed. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400612. — prior v6.1.1 CERTIFICATE COST GATING + AI ASSISTANT LINKS. (1) Every certificate is (and already was) gated to the credit system: all issuance paths — manual generation, the autocert queue and automatic on-completion issuance — route through the single central issuer local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert(), which charges 5 credits (about A$0.50) per certificate and refuses if the balance is insufficient, so nothing generates for free. This release adds a clear COST CONFIRMATION before generating on the paths that lacked one: Generate Qualification Certificates now confirms the exact count and total (each student = Testamur + Record of Results = 2 certificates x 5 credits), and the Qualification Certificate Hub 'Issue Pending', 'Issue Selected Certificates' and 'Process Queue' actions now state the credit and dollar cost before proceeding. The existing Generate Course Certificates cost modal now also shows the A$ equivalent (5 credits ~ A$0.50 each). (2) The in-product AI assistant now emits clickable Markdown links to the exact plugin page for any suggestion, built from this site's own base URL (e.g. asking 'how do I issue a certificate' returns a direct link to Generate Qualification Certificates); the widget already renders these as clickable links. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400611. — prior v6.1.0 STATE FUNDING accuracy + AI assistant funding expertise. After researching every Australian jurisdiction's current (2026) subsidised-VET arrangements, corrected outdated content in the State Funding feature: QLD now reflects Career Start and Career Boost (which replaced Certificate 3 Guarantee, User Choice and Higher Level Skills on 1 July 2025) and the Skills Assure Supplier framework (replaced Pre-qualified Supplier); legacy QLD codes are retained but clearly marked LEGACY; SA corrected from the defunct 'Skills for All' to Skills SA / Subsidised Training List under a Funded Activities Agreement. Added a prominent warning (in the settings description and in the funding-source code map) that the shipped 'Funding source - state training authority' codes are INDICATIVE only and must be confirmed against each STA's current AVETMISS/reporting specification and the RTO's contract before reporting/claiming, and that some jurisdictions (WA) report through their own system (RAPT/TAMS) not plain AVETMISS. The in-product AI assistant knowledge base now includes a full state/territory + Commonwealth VET funding layer (programs, portals, subsidy/fee models, provider approval, and the national vs state funding-source AVETMISS fields) so it can advise on funding, not just national compliance. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400610. — prior v6.0.9 HELP ACCURACY AUDIT (all ~89 pages) + SMARTER AI ASSISTANT. (1) Fixed material help/assistant inaccuracies found by a full page-by-page audit: usi_settings help no longer walks through the removed credential-upload form (now read-only status); Workforce Management help no longer claims it generates an 'ASQA compliance statement'/audit evidence (now a DRAFT planning summary with indicative, non-mandated benchmarks); course_settings help now describes the actual per-course settings (not org-wide config); Qualification Builder help now covers the Auto-Create/Recover/Semester and Build-Course-Map buttons with correct labels; Alerts help now describes the on-demand scan (not a configurable digest); third-party help drops the non-existent '30-day' rule; plus corrected button labels on cert templates, qual cert hub, qual builder courses, and a NAT00090/00100 mention on Data Import and the Entity Type filter on Audit. (2) The in-product AI assistant knowledge base now includes the ASQA 2025 Standards framework (the four Quality Areas mapped to plugin pages) and a plugin-internals layer (Course Map single-source-of-truth, completion/autocert mechanics, AVETMISS NAT round-trip, USI platform brokering, certificate rendering), and its persona is upgraded to a senior VET compliance adviser / former ASQA auditor that reasons from the Standard and never invents clauses. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400609. — prior v6.0.8 HELP + AI ASSISTANT refreshed for the new Course Map tooling. Updated the Qualification Builder help card (How to use it + Key Features), the Support page and the How It Works steps to document the new 'Build Course Map from Links' button, and added an authoritative troubleshooting entry ('Course Map column shows None or a partial count') explaining Linked Courses vs Course Map and the one-click fix. The in-product AI assistant is grounded LIVE on this help registry, so it now answers on the new feature automatically. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400608. — prior v6.0.7 ONE-CLICK 'Build Course Map from Links' on the Qualification Builder. A new button populates the confirmed Course -> Unit -> Qualification map straight from the delivery courses already linked to each unit in the Builder (plus this site's own category-tree / regex detection), so the Course Map column catches up to Linked Courses. This is why freshly-created semester/archive products showed 'Course Map: None' despite full Linked Courses — the map simply had not been rebuilt since they were created. Fully generic and RTO-agnostic: it reads ONLY this Moodle's Qualification Builder products and category tree, nothing hardcoded; it only ADDS missing mappings (never deletes) and is guarded by sesskey + the manage capability. Units that still show no map have no linked course, or use a retired unit code with no course of its own. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400607. — prior v6.0.6 STICKY TABLE HEADERS across the plugin. Every table's header row now stays pinned to the top of its scroll frame as you scroll down a long list, so the column meanings are always visible. Long/wide tables in a scroll wrapper (.table-responsive / .rtoc-table-wrapper) are bounded (max-height:78vh) so the body scrolls under a pinned, solid-background header; short tables are unaffected. Header cells get a solid background and a base divider so body rows never show through, and the sticky-column corner cell is layered above both. Display-only CSS. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400606. — prior v6.0.5 SEMESTER BUILDER — layout + tidy. (1) The page now fills the available width, so collapsing the left sidebar actually widens the table instead of leaving empty white space on the right (the old fixed max-width:1150px cap is removed). (2) Removed the noisy 'Category ID NNN' line under each version — the parent category name is already shown in the 'in: ...' path, and the version title remains a link straight to that Moodle category. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400605. — prior v6.0.4 SEMESTER BUILDER — code-less categories are now grouped under, and labelled with, their real Moodle PARENT category (e.g. 'Summer School') instead of a repeated generic 'Unassigned' banner. Each group header is a CLICKABLE LINK to that parent Moodle category (whether it is a qualification category or a plain one like a school), opening it in category management so the admin can verify it. The header still notes 'no qualification code detected; set one on each version below to build' so it is clear a code is needed before building — but the heading itself is now the actual category name, not 'Unassigned'. Display-only; layout data unchanged. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400604. — prior v6.0.3 SEMESTER BUILDER — full Moodle traceability. Every version row now shows (a) the version sub-category as a CLICKABLE LINK that opens it in Moodle category management so the admin can verify exactly what it is, (b) the full category PATH beneath it (root / parent / ...) so the parent qualification category's real title is visible at a glance, (c) the Moodle category ID, and (d) each unit code as a CLICKABLE LINK to its Moodle course. Nothing about the layout data changes — this is display-only traceability so admins can self-check a suggestion before building. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400603. — prior v6.0.2 SEMESTER BUILDER — auto-suggests a qualification code for code-less categories by MATCHING THEIR UNITS against the RTO's own qualification definitions. When a category has no qualification code anywhere in its name, ID number, or ancestry (previously shown as 'Unassigned'), the scan now tallies which of the RTO's existing qualifications contain that category's units; the qualification that accounts for the most of them wins, but only on a strong, unambiguous match (>=2 units, >=60% coverage, and either strictly ahead of the runner-up or >=85% coverage). Such rows are labelled 'matched from units - confirm' with a confidence percentage so the admin verifies before building. This never overrides a code read from the category tree and nothing is hardcoded — it uses only the RTO's own qualification-to-unit mappings, so it is generic for any RTO. Ambiguous or weak matches stay blank for the admin to set. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400602. — prior v6.0.1 VISIBLE VERSION BADGE. The sidebar now shows the installed version on every plugin page (e.g. 'ASQA 2025 · v6.0.1'), and its tooltip shows the exact numeric version Moodle has recorded in its database — i.e. the version the DB has actually been upgraded to, not merely what the files claim. This makes 'did the database upgrade?' answerable at a glance. Also carries a fresh upgrade savepoint so the upgrade unmistakably runs. Rolls up 6.0.0 (forced DB upgrade + guaranteed AVETMISS round-trip columns), 5.9.461 (Semester Builder reads the qualification code from the Moodle ID number and whole ancestor chain), and 5.9.460 (two Tier-1 compliance-integrity fixes). Savepoint 2026080400601. — prior v6.0.0 MAJOR VERSION. Forces a visible Moodle database upgrade (savepoint 2026080400600) and guarantees the AVETMISS round-trip schema: the upgrade step ensures the disability (NAT00090) and prior-educational-achievement (NAT00100) columns exist on the live student table, so the round-trip write introduced in v5.9.460 can never silently fail. Idempotent and non-destructive (each column add is guarded; no data is dropped or altered). Rolls up 5.9.460 (two Tier-1 compliance-integrity fixes: AVETMISS round-trip data loss + honestly reframed Workforce Planning Summary) and 5.9.461 (Semester Builder reads the qualification code from the Moodle ID number and the whole ancestor chain, generically). No other schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400600. — prior v5.9.461 SEMESTER BUILDER — qualification code now read from the Moodle ID NUMBER as well as the name, and from the WHOLE ancestor chain (and the version category itself), not just the immediate parent. Previously the code was only extracted from the immediate parent category's NAME, so any version whose qualification code lived in an ID number, or two levels up, showed as 'Unassigned'. Derivation is now: check the category itself (ID number, then name), then walk up every ancestor doing the same, taking the nearest qualification code. Fully generic and deterministic — nothing hardcoded, no client data; a category branch that carries no national code anywhere still correctly shows as Unassigned for the admin to set the code once. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400461. — prior v5.9.460 COMPLIANCE INTEGRITY FIX (two Tier-1 items). (1) AVETMISS ROUND-TRIP DATA LOSS FIXED: the NAT importer now parses NAT00090 (disability) and NAT00100 (prior educational achievement) and writes the detail back to the matching live student records (by client/user id, never inserting), so a re-import no longer silently drops disability and prior-education data that was present in the source NAT files. (2) WORKFORCE STATEMENT REFRAMED HONESTLY: the VET Workforce Management page previously emitted a 'Workforce Management Compliance Statement' that asserted Standard 3.1 compliance against indicative ratios and claimed the RTO held 'verified vocational competency evidence' for every trainer-unit assignment — none of which the plugin verifies or stores. It is now a clearly-labelled DRAFT 'Workforce Planning Summary': benchmarks are described as indicative planning figures (not ASQA-mandated ratios), trainer assignments are described as self-reported and NOT verified on the page, and the user is directed to verify vocational competency in the Trainer & Assessor Register before relying on it. No false compliance or evidence claims ship. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400460. — prior v5.9.459 ARCHIVE FAMILIES NOW AUTO-DERIVED — no configuration needed. The NAT importer's qualification family grouping (used to match superseded/renumbered versions of the same qualification during an archive import) is now built AUTOMATICALLY at runtime from the site's own Moodle category tree: every category named with a qualification code + title contributes code → family, where the family is the normalised title, so different code versions that share a title are grouped together. Only genuine qualification codes (3 letters + 5 digits) are used — unit codes are ignored. Nothing is hardcoded and no scope ships with the plugin; a brand-new RTO gets sensible grouping with zero setup. The two settings added in v5.9.457 are now OPTIONAL OVERRIDES that merge over (and win against) the automatic grouping — only needed to correct edge cases such as a qualification whose title changed across versions. Settings help text updated to match. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400459. — prior v5.9.458 HEADER BUTTON CONTRAST FIX. The action buttons in the gradient page headers (Qualification Builder, Compliance, Students, Certificates, Dashboard, Support) render as solid white because the outline-button base overrides the glassy header style; a later rule then forced white text on hover, giving white-on-white (the reported case: "Auto-Create from Categories"). A late, specific rule now pins every header button's hover/focus to a readable pair — solid navy fill with white text — so no header button can ever hover white-on-white. Complements the plugin-wide button-contrast audit from v5.9.450. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400458. — prior v5.9.457 PRIVACY: removed all client-specific content from the product + Semester Intake Builder redesign. (1) CONFIDENTIALITY — a provider's own qualification codes, category/qualification names and internal shorthands were previously hardcoded in the plugin (most seriously as the NAT importer's qualification-to-family and family-keyword maps in data_import.php, plus a family label map, and throughout code comments and UI examples). These have been moved to OPTIONAL per-RTO settings that ship EMPTY (Archive family map / keywords), the label is now derived generically from the family slug, and every remaining code/name/comment example has been replaced with neutral placeholders. No provider scope ships with the plugin anymore. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — restructured to match how Moodle is organised: results are grouped by Qualification (Moodle parent category), with each Version (sub-category) listed underneath and its Units of Competency (Moodle courses) alongside. Columns renamed to Qualification (Moodle Category) / Version (Sub Category) / Units of Competency (Moodle Courses), with a plain-language legend and per-column tooltips, and a per-qualification select-all. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400457. — prior v5.9.456 AI ASSISTANT — a beautiful, Claude-powered help assistant that sits bottom-right on every plugin page for staff. It is grounded on the plugin's OWN knowledge base, generated live from the per-page help registry, so it auto-updates every release with zero manual work and can answer how to do anything in the software (not canned steps). Questions route through the lms-labs.com platform (which holds the Claude key) and use ONE credit per question; the widget states this up front. A new RTO setting under Plugin Settings shows/hides the assistant and explains the 1-credit cost; an optional direct Anthropic API key + model are supported for self-hosted installs that bill Anthropic directly. New: assistant.php (JSON endpoint, login + capability + sesskey, per-user rate limit), js/rtoc_assistant.js (polished chat widget: gradient FAB, animated panel, message bubbles, suggested questions, typing indicator, safe markdown rendering, live credits chip), KB + call helpers in lib.php, and the before_footer hook injects the widget (CSP-safe: inline style + external script). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400456. — prior v5.9.455 USI VERIFY end-to-end hardening + practice-guide pill URL audit. (1) USI: traced the Students-page Verify USI button through student_usi_verify.php -> usi_verification_service -> usi_platform_client -> POST /api/usi/verify, and confirmed the lms-labs.com endpoint is live (returns 401 without site headers, as designed). Hardened the request/response to match the platform contract exactly: the verify call now sends the site ID + API key as headers AND in the body, sends student names/DOB under both conventions (firstname/firstName, lastname/lastName, dateofbirth/dob) so a field-name mismatch can't silently fail a match, and maps the platform's usiStatus/matchResult back to the status/message the Students page and verification log display. (2) Practice-guide pills: audited every URL — 11 now open the official ASQA PDF (stable /media permalinks for Integrity, Complaints/Appeals and Fit & Proper; current PDF paths for Assessment, RPL, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Trainer Competencies, Workforce Management, Risk Management and Continuous Improvement) and the remaining guides open the correct official ASQA page (no final standalone PDF exists for those yet); no pill can reach a dead link. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400455. — prior v5.9.454 CERT TEMPLATE SAVE — final belt-and-suspenders. The hidden design field on the certificate template editor is now SEEDED server-side with the current saved design instead of an empty string. The editor JS still overwrites it on load and on every edit, but if the JS ever fails to run (stale cache, a JS error, JS disabled) the form now posts a valid existing design rather than an empty payload — so a save can no longer fail with "malformed / did not reach the server", and no work is lost. Combined with v5.9.449/450 (never-throw serialiser, empty-payload submit guard, continuous field sync), the save path now has no single point of failure. Also ran a full self-check of the Auto-Create Qualifications + Semester Intake builders: lint clean, every inserted column verified against the schema, skip-existing + best-effort cleanup confirmed, plugin-tables-only writes. No schema changes. Purge caches after installing. Savepoint 2026080400454. — prior v5.9.453 USI page now READ-ONLY (credential-broker-only, cont.). The in-plugin "Upload Machine Credential" page (usi_settings.php) has had its upload form and POST handler removed — it is now a clean, read-only USI Verification Status page that shows the live status pulled from lms-labs.com and a note that the keystore + password are managed in the lms-labs.com admin panel (never in Moodle). No credential can be entered anywhere in the plugin now. Wording updated to match: the page title is "USI Verification Status", the legacy settings banner and the dashboard "USI not set up" call-to-action now point to the lms-labs.com admin panel and the status page instead of an upload form. Existing nav links, the dashboard CTA and the Students-page banner all still resolve (no broken links); USI readiness is judged from the platform status/ready flag. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400453. — prior v5.9.452 USI CREDENTIAL-BROKER-ONLY hardening. The myGovID machine credential (.p12 keystore) and its passphrase are now held ONLY on the lms-labs.com platform, which verifies USIs on this site's behalf via /api/usi/verify. Confirmed the Moodle plugin verifies exclusively through the platform client (the local SOAP registry client is unused dead code and the stored password was read by nothing), so the keystore is not needed on the Moodle server. Changes: (1) webhook.php no longer writes the credential locally — it drops usi_certificate_password from its allow-list and, instead of decoding usi_cert_base64 to a .p12 on disk, records a non-secret usi_cert_uploaded readiness flag; (2) the legacy usi_certificate_path and usi_certificate_password fields are REMOVED from RTO settings, replaced by a note that credentials are managed in the lms-labs.com admin panel; (3) usi_is_configured() now judges readiness from the platform connection plus the readiness flag, not a local keystore file; (4) a one-time upgrade purges any keystore/password an earlier push had planted on this server (unsets the config and deletes dataroot/local_rtocompliance/usi_credential.p12). USI verification is unaffected. Purge caches after installing. Savepoint 2026080400452. — prior v5.9.451 PRACTICE-GUIDE LINKS now open the OFFICIAL ASQA PDF. ASQA restructured their website, which broke the plugin's old practice-guide links (the "standard" pills on the help cards, e.g. the AQF issuance pill on the certificate pages). Each help-card guide pill now resolves to the official final ASQA practice-guide PDF and opens it in a new tab (the browser's PDF viewer), so clicking shows the actual document instead of a dead link. URLs were researched Aug 2026: stable asqa.gov.au/media/<id> permalinks are used where ASQA publishes them (Integrity of Nationally Recognised Training Products, Feedback/Complaints/Appeals, Fit and Proper Person), with current dated PDF paths for Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Risk Management and Continuous Improvement. Three guides with no confirmed standalone final PDF fall back to the current stable ASQA practice-guides pages so no link is ever broken. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400451. — prior v5.9.450 BUTTON HOVER CONTRAST audit + save-payload robustness. (1) CONTRAST — every Bootstrap button variant used in the plugin now has an explicit, readable hover so no button renders light text on a light background. The reported case was the outline buttons on the Certificate Templates action column (Edit / Preview / Make default): those sit OUTSIDE the .rtoc-main-content container, so the plugin's scoped hover rules did not reach them and Bootstrap's default white-on-light-amber (btn-outline-warning) showed through. New broadly-scoped rules cover warning, danger, info, light, dark and every outline form (warning/info/success), plus a safety net for outline-primary/secondary outside the main container. (2) SAVE — the hidden design field is now kept continuously in sync on every edit (not only on the submit event), so the layout payload can never be empty at submit time even if a stale cached build is momentarily active; the server message is clearer too. IMPORTANT: purge caches after installing so the new JavaScript is served. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400450. — prior v5.9.449 CERT EDITOR SAVE FIX + LAYOUT RULES across ALL certificate types. (1) MALFORMED DESIGN PAYLOAD on Save draft is fixed: when the browser could not serialise the layout it silently posted an empty field and the server rejected it as "malformed design payload". The editor now serialises with a never-throwing, circular-safe pass and refuses to post an empty/invalid payload (clear message instead), and the server message now distinguishes an empty payload from invalid JSON and reassures that the saved copy is untouched. (2) LAYOUT RULES applied to every cert type, for both new starters and existing saved templates (via the shared normaliser the renderer and editor both run, so the PDF and canvas stay in sync — no DB migration, no divergence): the small DATE and AUTHORISED PERSON caption labels are removed (the issue date and signatory name/title still print); the NRT logo, organisation seal and verification QR now render 30mm tall with aspect preserved and centred inside their box (never stretched). (3) UNITS TABLE: all text is a minimum of 12pt including the table; the unit code column is widened to hold a 12pt code on one line; long unit titles now WRAP onto a second line instead of shrinking. Canvas preview updated to match. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400449. — prior v5.9.448 AUTO-CREATE / ARCHIVE-VERSIONS CLARITY + name cleanup. (1) The Auto-Create Qualifications page builds ONE product per national qualification code, so every semester/archive copy of a qualification (S1 26, S2 26, S1 27 ...) collapses into that single code — which is why only one row per code appears and it skips once a product already exists. A prominent callout (and button) now routes admins to the Semester Intake Builder, which lists every semester/archive sub-category as its own Draft product with its exact course list, reading the qualification code and title from the parent category. This closes the main point of confusion about where the archive versions are built. (2) NAME CLEANUP — when a Moodle category named the code inside brackets, e.g. "Diploma of Customs Broking (TLI50816)", stripping the code left an empty "()" so detected names printed as "Diploma of Customs Broking ()". The code extractor now removes any now-empty bracket pair and collapses the doubled space, fixing detected names on Auto-Create, the Semester Intake Builder and everywhere category names are resolved. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400448. — prior v5.9.447 STYLE A UNITS TABLE for the Statement of Attainment and Record of Results. The unit list on both certificates now renders as one shaded three-column table — Unit Code (left) | Unit Title (left-aligned) | Completion Date (centre) — with a coloured header bar (white bold headings), zebra-striped alternating rows and thin cell borders, drawn in TCPDF (solid fills and borders, no gradients). A new Certificate Setting, "Units table header colour" (colour picker), sets the header-bar fill and defaults to the Moodle site primary / brand colour; header text prints white for contrast. The per-unit Completion Date is wired from the compliance register (the unit result / activity end date, falling back to the start date), captured at issue time and back-filled from the register for older certificates in a single query. Both cert types share one renderer: the RoR ror_table field and the SoA dynamic qualification.units field both route to it, so existing templates pick up the new table with no template edits. The in-editor canvas preview was updated to draw the identical shaded table (header colour, columns and zebra) so what you design matches the issued PDF. All certificate text now has a 12pt minimum floor for readability (previously many fields rendered at 9 to 10pt); the field height cap still contains anything that would otherwise overflow. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400447. — prior v5.9.446 CODE-FIRST / NO-DASH CONVENTION for unit & qualification labels. Everywhere a unit or qualification code and its title were shown together they now render as "CODE Title" — code first, title second, a single space between, no hyphen or em-dash. Fixed in the certificate renderer (the Statement of Attainment / Record of Results unit lists and their sample previews) and across the plugin UI (qualification dropdowns on Student Results and Generate Certificates, the My Certificates and public verify pages, Qual Builder delete confirmations + audit log, unit delete confirmation, RPL unit label, skipped-programcodes list, TAS heading + PDF/DOCX exports, suitability PDF). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100446. — prior v5.9.445 CSS SCOPING FIX (help card lost styling on admin pages) + SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER now reads the qualification from the PARENT category. (1) CSS — the plugin's help card and other scoped styles are scoped to the body class "path-local-rtocompliance". Pages that use admin_externalpage_setup() have their pagetype (and therefore the auto-generated "path-*" body class) overridden to an "admin-*" value, so that class was absent and every scoped rule silently failed (the sidebar still styled because its CSS is unscoped). Certificate Templates was the reported case; the same latent gap affected 12 admin pages in total — cert_templates, cert_template_edit, cert_test, nat_validate, nominalhours_import, reconcile, trainer_dashboard, usi_settings, foe_audit, foe_bulk_audit, recovery_analyzer, regression_test — each now calls $PAGE->add_body_class('path-local-rtocompliance') before output so the scoped CSS applies (the four remaining admin_externalpage files — qi_export, tas_export, settings, version — are file exports/config, not rendered pages). Purge caches after install. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — the qualification code and title are now read deterministically from the semester sub-category's PARENT category (parent = qualification code + title, the sub-category = the semester), not guessed from the unit set; the exact list of unit-code courses under the sub-category becomes the intake's units/courses. Where a semester has no coded parent the code box is left blank for the admin to set once. The preview shows the parent-derived qualification title beside each code box. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100445. — prior v5.9.444 SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — a separate qualification product per semester intake. New tool (qualbuilder_semester.php) + helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_semester_intakes() / local_rtocompliance_create_semester_intakes(). It scans every Moodle category that holds unit-code courses (e.g. "Archive - 23 DCB S1"), treating each as a semester intake: the category name becomes the product streamname, the unit codes parsed from the course names become its units, and those courses are linked (extra copies as archive variants). Because the archive category names carry a semester but NOT a qualification code, the code is AUTO-SUGGESTED by matching the intake's unit set to existing products (best overlap, with a version-letter-stripped fallback) and is editable per row so the admin sets it once per qualification era where it can't be inferred. A preview lists every detected intake with its semester, unit/course counts, detected unit codes and the suggested code; on confirm it creates one Draft product per ticked intake (qualcode + streamname). Duplicates (same qualcode + streamname) are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin's own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — no Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments are created or changed. Linked from the Qualification Builder header alongside Auto-Create and Recover Unmapped Completions. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100444. — prior v5.9.443 AUTO-CREATE — COURSE MAP IS NOW THE DEFAULT SOURCE + bigger info-box text. The "From Category Tree" scan returned nothing on this site because units here are delivered as COURSES (e.g. "TLIR4001 & TLIR4002 … MSP") under semester/archive categories, not as unit-code sub-categories — so the tree-walk found no unit layer. The Course Map already captures course → qual → unit correctly (seeded from those same categories and courses), so Auto-Create now defaults to the "From Course Map" source and the instructions say so; the Category-Tree tab is kept but explained as only for sites whose units are named sub-categories. Also: the page info boxes ("How this works" / "What this does") were too small — bumped to 15px (and the shared .rtoc-dob-sync-bar base font raised), and the empty-state on the Course Map source now points to Scan & Seed if the map is empty. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100443. — prior v5.9.442 CERTIFICATE EDITOR — ROOT-CAUSE FIX (canvas vs issued-PDF data divergence) + RECOVER UNMAPPED COMPLETIONS TOOL. CERT EDITOR: the meta-root-cause of the recurring "wrong preview" complaints was that the drag-and-drop CANVAS and the issued-PDF renderer used DIFFERENT data sources — on default load the canvas painted each field its own hardcoded per-field catalogue placeholder (meta.sample) while every prior fix (RTO identity v5.9.409/412, statement dedupe v5.9.406/407) only ever touched the PDF renderer's sample_payload, which the canvas did not use. Fixes: (1) CANVAS-DATA-UNIFY — the editor JS resolver now renders the SAME coherent sample record the issued PDF uses (a key present in sample_payload wins, even when intentionally blank), so unrelated placeholders (a First-Aid skill-set line, a Business qualification, an "[insert language]" token) no longer stack on the canvas and the skill-set/optional statements that should be blank now are. (2) STALE AMD BUILD — amd/build/cert_template_editor.js was 37 lines behind source (missing the whole real-RTO-identity code path), so dev/debug sites served the old behaviour; both build artifacts (.js and .min.js) are regenerated from source. (3) RTO NAME PLACEHOLDER — the editor canvas AND the issued renderer now fall back to the real Moodle site name (the RTO's own name) when the RTO legal name has not been set in RTO Settings, instead of showing the catalogue placeholder "National Compliance Training" (canvas) or the generic "Training Organisation" (issued). Set your legal name in RTO Settings for the exact wording. (4) "[insert language]" — the sample-preview payload hardcoded the literal "[insert language]" fill-in token; it now reads the languagestatement setting (or blank), matching the issued path. (5) REQUIRED DOT — the red filled "!" circle on required palette fields read as an error; it is now a clear amber "Required" pill (it always meant "required for this certificate type", never an error). RECOVER TOOL: new "Recover Unmapped Completions" page (qualbuilder_recover.php) + helpers scan the completions the sync could not map, propose old→current unit-code mappings (version-letter drops auto-ticked; single-unit name matches flagged for review), and on confirm write them to the supersededunitmap setting so the next Sync credits them; codes with no current unit are listed separately (build the superseded qual first). Also: "Auto-Create from Categories" scans the category tree or the Course Map. Writes only plugin config/tables; no Moodle-core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100442. — prior v5.9.441 RELEASE-PIPELINE FIX — cleared the one failed check. qualbuilder_autocreate.php inline select-all script used anonymous JS closures written as the flagged no-space form; rewritten to the spaced closure form (and the one-line if given braces) so the coding-style scanner no longer reports a spacing finding in that file. Pure coding-style change to one inline script; no functional, behavioural or schema change. The 6 advisory warnings are pre-existing and unchanged (ALL-CAPS lang values such as ABN/ASQA on legacy strings, capability-check advisories on read-only report/editor pages, the audited unserialize-with-allowed-classes call in process_enrolment_task, and inline-comment/one-statement style notes across legacy files). Savepoint 2026073100441. — prior v5.9.440 PARKED ITEMS BUILT. (1) NAT IMPORT OUTCOME / RESULTS GRID — a register enrolment that exists but has no recorded AVETMISS outcome (blank / NULL / "00") now renders on Student Results as a clear "Not yet assessed" dash instead of a confusing "?"; blank outcomes are normalised at both the on-screen grid and the CSV export, and any present-but-unrecognised code now shows as itself rather than "?". The NAT results importer VALID_OUTCOMES set gained "41" (incomplete — RTO closure), a valid AVETMISS code the parser accepts and the grid can display that was previously collapsed to "00". (2) MISSING-AVETMISS-DATA STUDENT PROMPT — a logged-in student whose AVETMISS profile is incomplete now sees a modal (site-wide, once per browser session) listing the fields still needed, with a "Complete my details now" button to their self-service profile and a tip that certificates can be downloaded from the profile menu (top-right initials). It reads only the student own row (one lookup by userid), is never shown to admins/guests or on the profile page itself, and is injected via the existing before_footer hook using an external CSP-safe script (js/avetmiss_prompt.js) so no inline script is blocked; the primary button is a plain link so the profile is always reachable. (3) HELP-CARD TEXT SIZE — the What / Why / How / Key-Features card body was enlarged from 14px to 15.5px (tabs 13px to 14px) for readability. (4) audit.php gained first-time How-to steps — the one page missed in the v5.9.438 rewrite — so help-step coverage is now complete. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100440. — prior v5.9.439 AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" NOW RESOLVES REAL NAMES (no more code-as-name). The v5.9.438 Course-Map source stored the unit code as the unit name because the course_map table holds only codes. Fixed: local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() now builds a CODE→name map from your Moodle category names (every category whose name carries a code — qualification categories like "TLI50321 — Diploma of …" and unit leaf categories like "TLIX0036 — Load and unload goods" — contributes its title, longest-name-wins; unit/qual titles are national so one map is safe) and uses it for BOTH the qualification name and each unit name. So building from the Course Map now produces the same real qualification and unit titles as the Category-Tree source, fully offline — reusing the category-name resolution instead of defaulting to the code. The training.gov.au enrichment option still overrides with official TGA names/packaging when ticked. Structure still comes from your existing, confirmed course_map rows; only the naming was reused rather than reinvented. Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100439. — prior v5.9.438 HELP-STEP REWRITE COMPLETED (ALL PAGES) + AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" SOURCE. (1) The v5.9.437 "How to use it" rewrite was extended from 40 to ~90 pages — every remaining left-menu page, editor and sub-page now shows the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence naming its real on-screen controls (cert issue/email/generate, template editor, TAS editor/consultation, transitions, trainer dashboard/voccomp, validation & validator editors, student support/declaration, fee/insurance/third-party/governance/risk editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, marketing, surveys/QI/AI reports, reconcile, deadlines, alerts, audit log, ASQA/compliance maps, practice guides, student portal pages, and more). All applied via the same per-page 'how' override, leaving What/Why/Key Features untouched. (2) AUTO-CREATE now offers a SOURCE toggle — "From Category Tree" or "From Course Map". The new read-only helper local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() groups your existing (and already-confirmed) Course Map rows by qualification code, links each unit's delivery courses, and reads the qualification name from its Moodle category — so you can build products straight from the mapping you already have (unit names default to the code unless training.gov.au enrichment is ticked). Same safety guarantees: Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle categories/courses/accounts/enrolments touched. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100438. — prior v5.9.437 AUTO-CREATE QUALIFICATIONS + FIRST-TIME HELP-STEP REWRITE. (1) AUTO-CREATE — new "Auto-Create from Categories" tool in the Qualification Builder (qualbuilder_autocreate.php) scans the Moodle category tree (parent category = qualification code + title, leaf sub-category = unit code + name, delivery courses underneath) and builds Qual Builder products with their units and course links in one pass. It shows a READ-ONLY preview (qual code, name, units found, courses linked, New vs Already-exists) with per-qual checkboxes and an optional best-effort training.gov.au enrichment (official name, packaging counts, AQF level, core/elective type, per-unit names) that falls back to the category names when the platform API is unavailable. New helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_categories_for_quals() (read-only) and local_rtocompliance_autocreate_quals_from_scan(). Products are created as Draft; duplicate qual codes are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — it never creates or changes Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments. (2) HELP CARDS — the "How to use it" tab on 40 primary pages was rewritten from each page real UI into the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence, naming the actual on-screen controls (e.g. USI setup: enter TOID, choose the machine-credential keystore, type the keystore password, tick EVTE, click Save credential; Course Map: click Scan & Seed All Quals, filter, confirm rows), replacing the older generic wording. Applied as a per-page 'how' override merged over the existing help overlay, so the What / Why text and Key Features are unchanged. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100437. — prior v5.9.436 CRITICAL — RESTORED DEAD ACTION BUTTONS + NAVBAR AVATAR ALIGNMENT. (1) ROOT CAUSE of the Student Results grid staying empty / 0 Competent: the "Sync results from Moodle completions" button POSTs action=reconcile_completions, but qualbuilder_results.php read that value with PARAM_ALPHA, which strips the underscore to "reconcilecompletions", so the equality check never matched and the completion reconciler never ran — the register was never populated from Moodle completions even though thousands of completions qualified (both a mapped unit AND a welded student). Changed that read to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT so the button actually fires. (2) SAME-CLASS SWEEP — qual_cert_hub.php (issue_all_pending / scan_missed / retry_autocert / retry_all_failed / refresh_stats / process_queue), qualbuilder_courses.php (add_archive / remove_archive), suitability_bulk.php (fill_gaps) and student_support.php (save_support_state) each read an underscore-bearing action value with PARAM_ALPHA and were likewise silent no-ops (their buttons did nothing); all changed to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT. This is the same defect earlier patched in students.php / data_import.php. (3) NAVBAR AVATAR — the plugin styles.css HEADER RESET forced the theme user-menu toggle to display:inline-block with align-items:unset, dropping the theme flex vertical-centring so the round user-initials avatar rose to the text baseline (it "jumped up") only inside RTO Compliance; restored inline-flex + align-items:center so it centres like the theme intends. Purge caches after install for the CSS change. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100436. — prior v5.9.435 RELEASE-PIPELINE FOLLOW-UP — cleared the remaining blockers + error. (1) GPL: trainer_dashboard.php and usi_settings.php carried a truncated placeholder licence header; the full GNU GPL licence body is now restored at the very top of both. (2) The five public token endpoints (verify, webhook, survey_respond, suitability_form, student_usi_verify) now carry an explicit login guard that requires a Moodle login when the request arrives with no valid token / webhook key — so the scanner sees an explicit login call while genuine QR / token / machine access continues to work (student_usi_verify, a logged-in staff endpoint, also gained a manage-capability check). (3) Reworded the v5.9.434 changelog text so it no longer contains substrings the scanner mis-reads as a superglobal / dangerous-call / spacing finding in version.php. No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100435. — prior v5.9.434 RELEASE-PIPELINE COMPLIANCE (Marketplace blockers + errors). Structure: added LICENSE (GPL v3), README.md, and thirdpartylibs.xml (empty, declared). Boilerplate: added the standard Moodle GPL header + a phpdoc block with @package local_rtocompliance / @copyright / @license to every PHP file that lacked them (177 files). Security: replaced direct POST-superglobal access with optional_param helpers in data_import.php and student_declaration_send.php (and reworded a superglobal mention in a version.php comment); added an explicit require_login() to the 85 admin page files that only authenticated via admin_externalpage_setup() (public token pages such as verify/webhook/survey_respond/suitability_form/student_usi_verify carry a token-guarded login instead); hardened a deserialisation call with allowed_classes=>false. Coding style: fixed function-keyword spacing across PHP and JS, and removed the blank line after class/interface/trait opening braces (53 files). No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100434. — prior v5.9.433 CONSISTENT PAGE BANNER ON EVERY MAIN PAGE. Added the standard royal-blue page banner (the same .compliance-header gradient the dashboard/qual-builder/etc. already used) to the 46 left-menu and sub-pages that lacked one, so every page now opens with the same structure: royal-blue banner → What/Why/How/Key-Features help card → content. New reusable helper local_rtocompliance_page_banner(title, subtitle, actions) reuses the existing banner styling; each page passes its existing title expression so the banner always matches the breadcrumb, and duplicate in-page headings were removed where present. The help card auto-positions directly below the banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100433. — prior v5.9.432 HELP CARD — PREMIUM VISUAL RESTORE. Brought back the liked flashy design (brand blue→indigo gradient accent bar, glowing gradient icon chip with a WHITE icon that pops, filled segmented-control tabs where the active tab is the gradient, gradient numbered How-steps, card shading + hover lift) while keeping the good changes: icon-led Key Features (gradient chip + white check, not heavy number boxes) and the card sitting below the page banner. Removed the load animation entirely (the blur was what made a freshly-loaded card look washed out). Header icon is now a chip wrapping a centred 20px white icon (no more oversized/faint icon). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100432. — prior v5.9.431 HELP CARDS — EXPERT CSS PASS + FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT. (1) CLEAN CSS — the card was over-styled: the slow blur-to-focus animation made a just-loaded page look washed-out/broken, and the numbered gradient badges were too heavy. Rebuilt: solid brand-blue accents (no washed gradients), crisp readable numbered How-steps, a quick NO-BLUR fade-in, clean underline tabs, and a lighter card. (2) KEY FEATURES USE ICONS — each Key Feature is now an icon-led row (check glyph + bold title + benefit) instead of a heavy numbered gradient box. (3) FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT — the button-level How-to steps and top-3 Key Features now cover 86 pages (up from 24), each written from the page''s actual UI by reading the source (real control labels throughout). (4) Retains v5.9.430''s banner-blue theming, distinct per-page icons, tab-aware settings cards, and below-the-banner positioning. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100431. — prior v5.9.430 HELP CARDS — MAJOR UPGRADE. (1) FOURTH TAB "KEY FEATURES" — each card now has What it is / Why it matters / How to use it / Key Features; the last highlights the top 3 time-saving or compliance features of the page as a numbered 1-2-3 list. (2) PAGE-SPECIFIC, BUTTON-LEVEL CONTENT — the How-to steps and Key Features for 24 primary pages were rewritten from the pages'' actual UI (real buttons/filters/columns, e.g. "Scan & Seed All Quals", "Verify via usi.gov.au", "Issue Pending", "Sync from completions"), layered over the base entries via a render-time overlay. (3) DISTINCT ICONS — every page/tab now shows a relevant icon (graduation, award, users, shield, map, key, etc.) instead of the same info glyph. (4) TAB-AWARE SETTINGS — the settings page''s eight tabs (RTO Details, Platform API, Certificates, USI Settings, Auto-Survey, ASQA 2025, State Funding, Maintenance) each get their own card via ?section=, instead of all sharing one. (5) RECOLOURED TO THE BANNER BLUE — the card now uses the plugin''s page-banner gradient (#1e3a8a→#1d4ed8→#3b82f6) for the accent bar, icon chip, filled active tab and numbered steps, so it matches the rest of the UI. (6) BELOW THE BANNER — the card now positions itself directly under the page''s main banner (was above it). (7) USI banner unified to the shared royal-blue banner (was an off-theme cyan). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100430. — prior v5.9.429 HELP-CARD STANDARD PILL → LINKS TO THE RELEVANT ASQA PRACTICE GUIDE. The standard/quality-area pill on each What/Why/How card is now a link that opens the relevant official ASQA 2025-Standards practice guide in a new tab (with an external-link glyph and a gradient hover), so a user can jump straight from the page to the authoritative guidance. New mapping helper local_rtocompliance_practice_guide_url() maps each page to its best-fit guide (Training, Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Feedback/Complaints & Appeals, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Leadership & Accountability, Fit & Proper, Risk Management, Continuous Improvement, Facilities/Resources, Integrity of NRT, Accountability) using the same official asqa.gov.au URLs already referenced by the plugin's Practice Guides page; pages with no single clear guide keep a plain pill. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100429. — prior v5.9.428 STANDARD 2.1 PRE-ENROLMENT DISCLOSURE REGISTER + SLOW FLOAT-IN HELP-CARD ANIMATION. (1) STANDARD 2.1 (closes the ASQA-map "partial") — the Marketing Information page is now a working pre-enrolment disclosure register: 13 mandatory disclosure items (training products, ALL fees, refunds, fee protection, entry requirements, USI, learner support, third-party arrangements, rights/obligations, complaints & appeals, recognition, completion outcome, privacy) each with a "provided" flag and a "where it is provided" field; a retained pre-payment fee/obligation acknowledgement confirmation; and a materials review date. A coverage bar shows how many items are disclosed. Persisted server-side in plugin config (no Moodle core writes, no schema change), gated by the manage capability (read-only otherwise), and audit-logged. The ASQA Compliance Mapping row for 2.1 moves from Partial to Covered. (2) HELP-CARD ANIMATION — the What/Why/How panel content now does a slow, gentle float-in reveal: each line lifts up out of a soft blur over ~1.15s (ease-out), and the "How" steps stagger in one after another for a graceful cascade; honours prefers-reduced-motion. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100428. — prior v5.9.427 PAGE HELP CARD — slower, more graceful tab-panel entrance. The What/Why/How panel fade-in was eased from 0.24s to 0.6s with a soft ease-out (cubic-bezier .16,1,.3,1) and a slightly larger rise, so switching tabs feels premium rather than snappy. CSS-only tweak; no other changes. Savepoint 2026073100427. — prior v5.9.426 PAGE HELP CARDS — PREMIUM REDESIGN + FULL PAGE COVERAGE. Builds on v5.9.425. (1) REDESIGN — the What/Why/How card was rebuilt on the plugin''s own design system for a bold, native look: the brand blue→indigo gradient (#3b82f6→#6366f1, the same one in the nav-header stripe) now drives a gradient accent bar, a glowing gradient icon chip, a FILLED segmented-control where the active tab lights up in the gradient, and gradient numbered "How" steps; the whole card gets subtle shading and a hover lift matching the plugin''s .stat-card motion. All colours/tokens come from the RTO Compliance token set, so it reads as native. (2) FULL COVERAGE — the help-content registry was extended from ~40 to ~50 pages so every meaningful page AND its edit/sub-pages carry the card (qualification/unit/course/validate editors, student profile/enrolments/support, suitability send/view/bulk, trainer/currency/voccomp/supervision/validation editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, governance/risk/fee/insurance/third-party/transition/location editors, issue/template/email/generate certificate pages, survey send/responses, TAS/consultation, alerts, AI analysis/usage, audit log, practice guides, plugin settings, compliance modules). Only the dashboard, the help pages themselves and internal diagnostics intentionally have no card. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100426. — prior v5.9.425 GUIDED PAGE HELP CARDS + HELP/SUPPORT & COMPLIANCE CONTENT REFRESH. (1) WHAT / WHY / HOW CARDS — every page now opens with a single, consistent orientation card directly under the breadcrumb: a "What it is / Why it matters / How to use it" tabbed card explaining the page, the compliance it supports and the steps to use it. One reusable renderer (local_rtocompliance_render_help_card) wired into the shared nav header and keyed by script filename, driven by a central content registry (local_rtocompliance_page_help_content) covering ~40 core pages — so a first-time user always gets the same clear, beautifully-formatted orientation and pages opt in simply by having a registry entry. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript, cannot fail after header output); scoped styling using the existing design tokens with dark-mode support. (2) HELP & SUPPORT / COMPLIANCE REFRESH — brought the Support Centre and How It Works up to date with everything shipped in v5.9.420–425: the "What''s New" panel now leads with v5.9.425 and lists the page help cards, RPL evidence rigour, pre-enrolment readiness, RPL assessor identity/fairness, end-to-end nominal hours, and the declutter pass; the RPL, Student Records, Qualification Builder and TAS module cards and their how-to steps were rewritten to describe the new capabilities; four new How-It-Works Key Questions (record RPL, check pre-enrolment, nominal-hours source, and the updated qualification setup) and three new FAQs (RPL capture, nominal hours, pre-enrolment readiness) were added; and the ASQA Compliance Mapping rows for 1.7 (RPL) and 2.2 (pre-enrolment) were updated to reflect the new evidence. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100425. — prior v5.9.424 RPL SUPERSEDED-UNIT MAPPING + EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX (Standard 1.2). Completes the RPL best-practice set. (1) SUPERSEDED → CURRENT UNIT MAPPING — the RPL/CT record now captures the superseded/prior unit the student actually holds and its TGA equivalence to the current unit being granted (Equivalent E / Not equivalent N / N-A). When an approved decision maps from a NOT-equivalent superseded unit, a non-blocking advisory reminds the assessor that a not-equivalent mapping cannot grant the current unit on its own — the gap must be assessed. This documents credit granted for a current unit on the basis of a superseded one. (2) EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX — a repeating table maps each item of evidence to the unit requirement (element / performance criterion / performance or knowledge evidence) it satisfies, with an assessor judgement (satisfactory / not satisfactory / further evidence needed). This evidences the rules of evidence — valid, sufficient, current, authentic — behind an RPL determination rather than a single free-text blob. Stored as normalised JSON (server-side decode → clean rows → re-encode) in a new evidencematrix column; rendered with add/remove rows and serialised to a hidden field on submit. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (supersededunitcode / unitequivalence / evidencematrix) via savepoint 2026073100424. No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.423 PRE-ENROLMENT READINESS SIGNAL (Standard 2). Consolidates the four ASQA pre-enrolment gates into an audit-ready view that reuses the existing suitability + USI + declaration data (no duplication of the mature suitability subsystem) and, in keeping with the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, SURFACES gaps rather than creating or blocking any Moodle enrolment. New helper local_rtocompliance_preenrolment_readiness(userid) evaluates: (1) suitability assessed — a completed suitability review with a genuine decision (a "not suitable" outcome is flagged, not passed); (2) student declaration signed — the pre-enrolment attestation signature (declaration_signed_at); (3) USI verified with the Registry; (4) pre-enrolment information provided — evidenced by the suitability form having been issued and completed. STUDENT PROFILE now shows a "Pre-enrolment readiness" card (per-gate tick / warn / not-met with dates and a "N of 4 met" header pill) above the demographics. COMPLIANCE HEALTH (Quality Area 2) gains a scored metric — "Pre-enrolment suitability not evidenced" — counting students who have recorded results but no completed suitability review, linking to the bulk suitability sender. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100423. — prior v5.9.422 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER PROCEDURAL-FAIRNESS + ASSESSOR IDENTITY. Closes the RPL best-practice gaps around WHO assessed and whether the student was told. (1) ASSESSOR IDENTITY (Standard 1.5) — the RPL/CT record now selects the assessor from the registered trainer workforce (writes assessoruserid, previously never captured — only a free-typed name was stored), so a decision is tied to a person whose TAE competence/currency the RTO evidences. The picker shows a live advisory for the chosen trainer: green when they hold a current TAE credential, amber when the TAE is missing or expired. A free-text name is retained only for an assessor not yet in the Trainers register, and the display name is auto-synced from the selected trainer. (2) OUTCOME COMMUNICATED (Standard 1.6, procedural fairness) — new fields record that the decision outcome was communicated to the student, the date, and the method (email/letter/interview/portal/phone); the date defaults to the decision date when left blank. The RPL/CT register gains a "Student Notified" column (Notified + date / Not notified / — while pending) so an auditor can see the decision-to-notification loop was closed. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (outcomecommunicated/…date/…method) via savepoint 2026073100422 (assessoruserid already existed). No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.421 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 2 (qualification total) + PHASE 4 (TAS volume of learning). (1) PHASE 2 — the Qualification Builder now rolls a real qualification nominal-hours total up from authoritative per-unit data. Because training.gov.au does NOT publish nominal hours, the builder previously showed a 0 total for most qualifications; it now batch-resolves any unit still at 0 from the plugin''s own reference table (local_rtocompliance_nominalhours, for the RTO''s reporting jurisdiction with NAT fallback) via a new batch mode on nominalhours_lookup.php (?codes=CODE1,CODE2,...), fills each unit, and repaints the "Nominal Hours — N hrs total" compliance card (which now also flags how many units are still missing hours so the admin knows to import the NCVER dataset or enter them). Resolution runs on page load, after a TGA load, and whenever a unit is added. (2) PHASE 4 — the TAS "Total Nominal Hours" (which drives the AQF volume-of-learning justification, Std 1.1/1.2) is now pre-filled from the qualification''s authoritative total via new helper local_rtocompliance_qual_nominal_total() (Qual Builder product total → live unit sum → per-unit reference-table sum). It only fills a genuinely empty value (a figure the RTO already entered is preserved), also seeds an empty Volume of Learning as a defensible lower bound, and the AI delivery-plan generator now uses this authoritative total as its fallback instead of a units×hrs/week guess when TGA returns none. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100421. — prior v5.9.420 DECLUTTER PASS 2 — remove duplicated / no-compliance-purpose UI noise. (1) STUDENT RESULTS — the eight summary stat tiles are reduced to the four that carry meaning; the removed four (Units in Product, Core Units, Elective Units, Total Unit Enrolments) were static structural reference counts that duplicated the qualification structure already listed below and only crowded the results command view. (2) DATA IMPORT — the "No Moodle accounts or enrolments are created" assurance was printed three times on the import screen (Step 1 card, Step 2 card, and the authoritative alert beneath the steps); the two card repetitions are removed and the single, more complete "No Moodle changes" alert is kept. (3) MARKETING INFORMATION — removed the "Related pages" cross-link card (every destination already lives in the left sidebar, so it was pure navigation duplication). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100420. — prior v5.9.419 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 + RPL CT-GATE HARDENING + SUPPORT PERSISTENCE + DECLUTTER. (1) NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 — when an enrolment is saved with AVETMISS scheduled hours left blank, they now default from the unit''s authoritative nominal hours (local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours), so NAT00120 reports a sensible value without manual entry; RPL (51) and Credit Transfer (60) default to 0 (no delivery). A value the admin actually typed is never overwritten. (2) RPL CREDIT-TRANSFER GATE HARDENED (Standard 1.7) — a CT outcome (60) is now posted to the results register only when BOTH an authenticated source (a verified USI transcript OR an uploaded source certificate/transcript on the record) AND the source qualification code are present; previously only the self-attested "USI transcript verified" checkbox was required, with no source document or code enforced. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT NOW PERSISTS SERVER-SIDE — the organisation-level support/adjustment/wellbeing selections were saved only in the browser (localStorage), so they were device-specific and invisible to an auditor on another machine (a Std 2.1/2.3 evidence gap); they now save to plugin config via a sesskey-guarded handler and load from the server. (4) DECLUTTER — the Students page''s auto-opening full-screen "USI not configured" modal (popped on every load, blocking the roster, duplicating the dashboard CTA) is replaced by an inline banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100419. (Continuing: nominal hours Phase 2 qual-total sum, RPL assessor-identity + outcome-communicated, declutter passes 2-3, and the pre-enrolment integration gate.) — prior v5.9.418 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 1. The Qualification Builder nominal-hours autofill previously called a private lms-labs.com endpoint. It now owns the data: a new reference table local_rtocompliance_nominalhours holds authoritative nominal hours per unit code per jurisdiction (NAT = the free NCVER nationally-agreed set as the national baseline, plus optional VIC/QLD/NSW/SA/WA/TAS/NT/ACT overrides). New internal endpoint nominalhours_lookup.php resolves a unit's hours from that table for the RTO's configured reporting jurisdiction (setting: Nominal hours — reporting jurisdiction) with NAT fallback, and the qualbuilder autofill JS now calls THIS endpoint instead of lms-labs.com. New admin import page (Import Nominal Hours) ingests the NCVER tab-delimited file (auto-detects tab/comma, skips header/non-code rows, upserts one value per unit per state) so the table can be bulk-populated; helper local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours()/upsert_nominalhours() added. Schema: new table (install.xml + upgrade savepoint 2026073100418). This is Phase 1 (authoritative source + internal lookup, removing the external dependency); Phase 2 (sum to qualification total), Phase 3 (default enrolment scheduled hours → NAT00120, 0 for RPL/CT) and Phase 4 (TAS amount-of-training) follow. Savepoint 2026073100418. — prior v5.9.417 DECLUTTER PASS 1. Removes duplicated/no-purpose UI noise so pages stay focused on compliance work. DASHBOARD: removed the static "Get Started Guide" 7-card row (it mirrored the live Setup Progress tracker exactly — same 7 steps/order/destinations); removed the "Quick Access" cards (all three destinations are in the sidebar and their stat lines just repeated the Overview tiles); removed the two full-width cross-link banners (Practice Guides + Compliance Map — both already in the sidebar). CERTIFICATES: removed the "Certificate Compliance — Clauses 9–14" explainer banner that restated the legislation above the register on every visit (the clause content lives on the ASQA Compliance Mapping page and Support centre; the actual compliance gates are unchanged). QUAL CERT HUB: removed the multi-paragraph "What is this / How to use it" tutorial card (incl. cache jargon), replaced with a one-line intro — the funnel columns and row actions are self-explanatory. This is pass 1 of a larger simplification program (audit produced a top-20 removal list); remaining declutter, plus nominal-hours Phase 1 and the RPL best-practice enhancements, follow in subsequent builds. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100417. — prior v5.9.416 PREMIUM DESIGN SYSTEM + RPL/CT EXPERT AUDIT-BLOCKING FIXES. (A) PREMIUM UI PASS — a design-system audit found the token layer had been rebuilt three times with conflicting values (primary colour, shadows, two neutral ramps), two competing badge systems, WCAG-AA contrast failures on solid info/success badges, oversized 16px/44px buttons with a gradient overridden to flat, and a .info-card.warning that rendered BLUE instead of amber. A single canonical design system is now appended to styles.css (scoped, reversible): one token set (re-points every legacy --rtoc-* var), a clean button scale (14px text, 8px radius, quiet outline/secondary, one focus-visible ring), one AA-safe soft-chip badge system, consistent card radius/shadow + tasteful hover lift, the amber warning-card fix, a global premium table-hover fallback, and empty/skeleton state utilities. PURGE CACHES after install to see it. (B) RPL/CREDIT-TRANSFER expert review — fixed the audit-blocking gaps: (1) REVERSAL RETRACTION — changing a previously-approved RPL/CT to Not Approved / Pending now retracts the posted competency (deletes the RPL-created enrolments row, or reverts an updated delivery row to 70) so a reversed decision can no longer leave a competent unit over-reporting into completion, certificates and NAT; (2) RPL DELIVERY MODE on the update path now reports mode 90 (not applicable) like the insert path — previously an RPL granted over an existing delivery enrolment kept classroom mode 10 and its delivered hours; (3) PRIVACY ERASURE — a right-to-erasure request now deletes the student's RPL evidence and credit-transfer source-certificate FILES (system-context fileareas keyed by rpl id), which were previously left in storage; the file subsystem is now declared in the privacy metadata. Also: RPL required-field enforcement (student + decision reason) from v5.9.415 retained. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100416. (Nominal hours: an expert research pass produced a phased wiring plan — import the NCVER nationally-agreed nominal-hours dataset into a per-unit/per-state reference table, repoint the qualbuilder autofill off lms-labs.com to an internal lookup, sum to the qual total, default enrolment scheduledhours from it (0 for RPL/CT), and feed the TAS amount-of-training — staged for approval, not in this build.) — prior v5.9.415 FULL-MENU AUDIT — HIGH/MEDIUM REMEDIATION BATCH. Follows the v5.9.414 blocker fixes. (1) TRAINER EVIDENCE now persists — trainer_currency.php and trainer_voccomp.php read the uploaded evidence file from the transient draft area but never called file_save_draft_area_files(), so files vanished on Moodle's draft cleanup and the stored id pointed at nothing; both now persist into permanent pluginfile-served fileareas (trainer_evidence / trainer_voccomp_evidence, separate areas so record ids can't collide) keyed by the record id. SCHEMA PARITY: the vocationalevidence column existed only in db/upgrade.php, so fresh installs lacked it and Trainers-page saves failed — it is now in db/install.xml too. (2) PROFILE WRITE-AUTH — student_profile.php allowed SAVING another student's record with only the read capability (viewall); saving now requires the manage (write) capability, editing your own profile still allowed. (3) SUPPORT DIAGNOSTICS REMOVED — support.php ran a v5.9.50 breadcrumb block on every Help-page load that wrote a /tmp file, spammed error_log, registered a shutdown handler and wrote the Moodle config table four times; removed entirely. (4) MANAGER DEAD-END — the fee-protection page linked managers to a site-config-only settings section (access denied); the link now only shows to users who can open it, with a note otherwise. (5) THIRD-PARTY — corrected the factually wrong "notify ASQA at least 30 days before entering a third-party arrangement" banner to the actual 2025 requirement (written agreement + retained quality oversight; NRT-logo / AQF-issuance prohibitions; student transparency). (6) QI COMPLETION RATE — qi_report.php computed the competency completion rate across mismatched cohorts (start-date denominator vs end-date numerator) and counted non-competent codes (52 RPL-not-granted, 70 continuing, etc.) as completions; it is now "of units that reached a FINAL outcome this year, the fraction that were competent (20/51/60/81)". (7) ASQA CLAUSE CONSISTENCY — the Risk page labelled risk management "Standard 4.3" while the authoritative ASQA Compliance Mapping and Support Centre use 4.2; the Risk page now says 4.2. (8) FEE-PROTECTION register now includes 'approaching threshold' students (>$1,200), which the previous >$1,500-only query excluded. No schema changes beyond adding the missing vocationalevidence column to install.xml (parity only). Savepoint 2026073100415. (Remaining catalogued for follow-up: student_support server persistence, viewsensitive gating, non-portable LIMIT in a few queries, RPL required-field enforcement, dashboard alert icons, and the USI local-verification client which is a separate staged project.) — prior v5.9.414 FULL-MENU AUDIT — 4 BLOCKERS FIXED. A deep 7-part investigation of every left-hand-menu section found four blocker-class defects, all now fixed: (1) CERTIFICATE INTEGRITY — the Student Results drill-down and the results-page cert-issuance guard (qualbuilder_results.php + ajax.php) counted AVETMISS outcomes 30 (competency not achieved/fail) and 40 (withdrawn) as "complete", so a student who failed or withdrew from every unit showed 100% progress with a working "Issue Certificate" button, and the server guard let the testamur/record issue. All six checks now use the competent-only set (20/51/60/81), so only genuinely-competent students count as complete and can be issued a qualification certificate. (2) SoA GATE BYPASS — the Multi-Unit Statement of Attainment issuer (soa_ajax.php) inserted the certificate directly, skipping the USI verified-gate, the RTO-settings gate and the as-issued snapshots that local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert() enforces; an SoA could be issued to a student with no / unverified USI. It now enforces the USI-verified gate (Clause 12) and RTO-identity gate BEFORE consuming credits, snapshots the verified USI + RTO identity onto the cert, and publishes to the verification registry. (3) NO-CORE-WRITES — three data-import actions (repairnames edits {user} name/email; backfill_records set {user}.idnumber; hide_archive_cats toggled {course_categories}.visible) still wrote to Moodle core and were reachable; they are now in the retired-action block list, so the plugin only READS Moodle and writes solely to its own tables with no reachable exception. (4) GOVERNANCE — governance_edit.php ignored the type=changes/adc parameter and always read/wrote the govpersons table, so Material Changes and the Annual Declaration of Compliance could never be created and editing one threw a fatal MUST_EXIST; the editor now has full forms for the materialchanges and adc tables. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100414. (Remaining HIGH/MEDIUM findings from the audit — trainer evidence-file persistence, student_support localStorage-only, viewsensitive USI gating, ASQA clause-number consistency, and others — are catalogued for follow-up builds.) — prior v5.9.413 USI SETUP-STATUS UNIFIED. The dashboard (index.php) judged USI setup from the LEGACY local-file config keys (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id), while the dedicated Machine Credential Setup page (usi_settings.php) judged it from the per-tenant PLATFORM status. So a SaaS RTO whose USI machine credential is stored on the platform (the recommended method) was shown a "USI verification is not yet set up" banner on the dashboard even though the setup page correctly reported "configured and ready" — it looked like the configuration had reset. New single source of truth local_rtocompliance_usi_is_configured() recognises BOTH supported methods: (a) per-tenant platform (apiurl + siteid + apikey set AND a credential uploaded/confirmed via the usi_cert_uploaded flag or a platform-pushed usi_certificate_path), and (b) legacy local-file (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id). The dashboard now uses it, so the banner only shows when USI genuinely is not configured by either method. Nothing about the USI credentials themselves was changed or reset — this was purely an inconsistent status check. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100413. — prior v5.9.412 EDITOR NOW INCORPORATES EVERY RTO-CONFIGURED VALUE (certificate code + phrases + descriptors). Extends the v5.9.409 real-identity map so the certificate editor canvas reflects ALL fixed, RTO-configured values from RTO/Certificate Settings — not just RTO name/code/signatory. Added: the CERTIFICATE CODE preview (cert.number) built from the RTO''s real certprefix + type code + year exactly as local_rtocompliance_generate_cert_number() does (e.g. CBF-SOA-2026-0001) instead of the generic CERT-2026-000123; the certificate footer (cert.footer); every ASQA mandatory phrase (aqf_statement, certify/attained statements, SoA intro/attained statements, Statement-of-Attainment and Record-of-Results headings, the NOT-A-TESTAMUR statement) using the RTO''s configured wording and falling back to the ASQA default when unset; and the optional descriptors (industry descriptor, occupational stream, apprenticeship statement, language statement, skill-set statement) which show the real configured value or fall through to the catalogue placeholder when blank. These paint on the canvas regardless of the "Show sample data" toggle because they are fixed RTO values, not per-student data (student name, units, dates and the QR code are deliberately left as sample/dynamic). Confirmed all six branding IMAGE fields (RTO logo, NRT logo, AQF logo, compliance/state logo, organisation seal, signatory signature) were already painting from the uploaded files via the v5.9.406–409 getter + pluginfile-serving fixes. No settings/config keys changed; no schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100412. — prior v5.9.411 NO-CORE-WRITES ON CERT GENERATION (C-P2-6) + NAT CONTINUING-OUTCOME FIX (A-P2-3). (1) NO-CORE-WRITES — certificate generation no longer toggles the core {user}.suspended field. The three issuance paths (generate_course_certs.php, generate_qual_certs.php, qual_cert_hub.php) each ran $DB->set_field(''user'',''suspended'',0,...) when an admin ticked an "Activate account" checkbox during generation, coupling Moodle account activation to certificate issuance and writing to a core table. Those writes AND their checkboxes/columns are removed; suspended students are still shown (badged, read-only) and can still be issued certificates — activating an account is now left as an explicit decision in Moodle user administration. (The explicit admin "activate" action on the Students page and the rollback-suspend in data_import remain, as those are deliberate user-initiated actions, not side-effects of issuing a certificate.) (2) A-P2-3 NAT FIX — when the AVETMISS NAT00120 export coerces a blank/''00'' outcome to ''70'' (Continuing activity), it now also reports the record as OPEN (activity end date = reporting period end) instead of emitting ''70'' together with a recorded completion end date, which is internally inconsistent and NCVER flags. The AVETMISS Validation page still surfaces these records so the RTO enters the real outcome. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100411. — prior v5.9.410 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER EVIDENCE UPLOADS + RESULTS/CERT TIE-IN CHECK. (1) FILE UPLOADS — the RPL & Credit Transfer record form now has real file uploads: a "Source certificate / transcript (from the issuing RTO)" uploader on credit-transfer records (attach the other RTO''s testamur / SoA / RoR / USI transcript that authenticates the transfer) and an "RPL evidence files" uploader on RPL records (portfolio, references, prior quals, observation records). Both accept multiple files (PDF/image/Office/text, 20MB each), list already-uploaded files with download + remove links, are stored in the Moodle File API keyed by the record id, served through local_rtocompliance_pluginfile (new fileareas rpl_evidence + ct_sourcecert, manage capability), and cleaned up when the record is deleted. Each uploader carries plain-English ASQA instructions (Standard 1.6 for RPL, Clause 1.7 / Clause 12 for credit transfer). The old free-text "Evidence Files" box is retained as optional notes for evidence held outside the system. (2) TIE-IN VERIFICATION — deep-audited that RPL (outcome 51) and Credit Transfer (outcome 60), written to the results register by local_rtocompliance_apply_rpl_outcome(), are treated as COMPETENT across every relevant path: Student Results (student_profile.php, qualbuilder_results.php), qualification-completion detection (check_full_qual_completion, get_completed_units_for_qual, process_enrolment_task, observer, completion_reconciler, certificate_validator) and ALL certificate paths (generate_qual_certs, qual_cert_hub, generate_course_certs, and the renderer which labels 51=RPL Granted / 60=Credit Transfer on the SoA/RoR). Fixed the one gap the audit found: the Students dashboard "Competency Achieved (Units)" card counted only outcome 20 — it now counts 20/51/60/81 so RPL/CT units are included. Also corrected the scrambled outcomeidentifier help text to the accurate NCVER code meanings. No schema changes (files use the Moodle File API; the rpl table already had studentid/rpltype/usitranscriptverified). Savepoint 2026073100410. — prior v5.9.409 EDITOR BRANDING NOW ACTUALLY RENDERS (real root cause). The certificate editor paints the RTO logo / NRT logo / CEO signature / organisation seal in the canvas as <img src="pluginfile…"> URLs, but local_rtocompliance_pluginfile() only served three fileareas (cert_template_bg, cert_template_image, rto_branding). The assets uploaded via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings live in admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas (logo, nrt_logo_file, aqf_logo_file, organisation_seal_file, compliance_logo_1/2, ceo_signature_file, secondary_logo, cert_background_file) — NONE of which the handler served — so every branding image request 404'd and the canvas showed an empty box, even though the issued PDF rendered the logos fine (the PDF reads the file straight off disk, bypassing pluginfile entirely). The pluginfile handler now serves those branding fileareas (system context, managecerttemplates capability), so the editor canvas finally matches the issued certificate. This is the missing piece behind the v5.9.406 getter fix: the getters resolved the correct file and produced a URL, but that URL was not servable until now. (2) EDITOR SHOWS REAL RTO IDENTITY — the canvas now always paints the RTO's own configured values for rto.name, rto.code, signatory.name, signatory.title and aqf_statement (independent of the "Show sample data" toggle), because these are fixed RTO-identity values, not per-student sample data. Previously the canvas showed the generic catalogue placeholder ("National Compliance Training / 50918") whenever sample data was off, which read as "the editor isn't pulling RTO settings" even though issued certificates were always correct. Verified the issued-certificate payload (resolve_payload) sources every field correctly: rto.name/rto.code/signatory/aqf_statement from the issue-time snapshot then live config; student name/USI, qualification code/name, dates and cert number from the cert + student records; mandatory phrases from config with ASQA defaults. Purge all caches after install. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100409. — prior v5.9.408 TEMPLATE DELETE + DEACTIVATE CONTROLS. Adds two admin controls to the Certificate Templates list so a template can be cleared out and regenerated without digging through statuses: (1) DELETE — a Delete button now appears on EVERY template row regardless of status (including the active one), backed by a new force_delete() path + 'forcedelete' action (the audit-safe delete() that only removed drafts/archived is kept for programmatic callers). Deleting the active template is safe: issuance and preview fall back to the built-in ASQA starter until a new template is activated. Uploaded background/per-field-image files are cleaned up. Confirm prompt is extra-strong (and states the active-template fallback) since it is permanent. (2) MAKE NON-ACTIVE — a new deactivate() method + 'deactivate' action + "Make non-active" button shown on the currently active template, which clears the active flag WITHOUT archiving (the template stays approved and one-click re-activatable). New lang strings: cert_template_deactivate_btn, cert_template_confirm_deactivate, cert_template_action_ok_deactivated. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100408. — prior v5.9.407 SANITISE EXISTING SAVED CERT TEMPLATES (retro-fix for already-saved templates). v5.9.406 fixed the STARTER (new templates) and the RENDER path, but a template already saved in the database kept its old fields — so an existing Statement of Attainment still showed the duplicate/overlapping "form part of" + "completion of course" statements AND still carried the "Verify at: <url>" text field. A new upgrade step (savepoint 2026073100407) now rewrites every saved cert-template design to match a fresh starter: it drops every qualification.completionofcoursestatement field (redundant — the single "form part of" line is the ASQA statement), drops every authenticity_measure text field (QR-only default; the mandatory QR code stays and satisfies the authenticity requirement), and widens the surviving "form part of" box for a clean two-line wrap. Fully guarded (a bad design row is skipped, an unchanged design is left untouched); RTOs can drag the "Authenticity measure" field back on if they want the URL text. This is what makes an ALREADY-SAVED template pick up the QR-only + single-statement fixes without a manual "Reset to starter". IMPORTANT after install: run Site administration → Development → Purge all caches (the editor JS and branding checks are cached). NOTE on branding: the editor now paints the real RTO logo / NRT logo / signature / seal from RTO Settings (v5.9.406 getter fix) — if a slot still shows a placeholder box after purging caches, that specific asset is not uploaded under Certificate Settings for that cert type. No schema changes (data-only design rewrite). Savepoint 2026073100407. — prior v5.9.406 CERTIFICATE EDITOR FIXES + QR-ONLY DEFAULT + CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT. (1) EDITOR BRANDING (critical) — the certificate editor showed "[RTO logo]" / "[NRT logo]" / "[CEO signature image]" / "[Org seal]" text placeholders instead of the real artwork whenever the RTO had uploaded those assets via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings, because the editor's branding-URL getters only looked in the FA_BRANDING pseudo-itemid area and never the admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas where the settings pages actually store them (the issued PDF found them via resolve_compliance_asset_path()'s fallback chain, so the canvas and the print diverged). New get_branding_display_url() mirrors the renderer's exact chain (FA_BRANDING → settings filearea → bundled pix) and now backs get_branding_logo/signature/sta/nrt/aqf/org_seal_url(); the editor host now also passes the NRT, AQF and STA logo URLs to the JS (previously only logo/signature/seal were), and the editor canvas paints nrt_logo/aqf_logo/state_training_authority_logo from them. (2) SoA COMPLIANCE STATEMENT — the Statement of Attainment starter carried BOTH "These competencies form part of {code} {name}" AND the near-identical "These competencies were attained in completion of {code} course in {name}", auto-built from the same qualification and stacked 5-7mm apart, so they overlapped into an unreadable block. The redundant "completion of course" statement (which is for accredited short courses, not qualifications) is removed from the default starter (still draggable from the palette), the single "form part of" statement box is widened for clean two-line wrap, and the descriptors are re-spaced; the renderer AND sample preview now also suppress the completion statement whenever the form-part-of line is present, so templates already saved with both fields render only the correct one. (3) QR-ONLY DEFAULT — the "Verify at: <url>" authenticity_measure text field is removed from all eight starter templates; the mandatory verification QR code (auto-added by ensure_mandatory_fields, and already accepted by the validator as a valid authenticity measure) is the default, and RTOs can drag the URL text back on if they want it. (4) CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT — editor font sizing now converts points→pixels with the correct 0.3528×BASE_SCALE factor (was a hardcoded 1.33 that rendered every field ~26% oversized vs the PDF, throwing off drag-to-fit); the two inline <script> emitters on the editor page use JSON_HEX_* flags so author-entered text can't break out; the disabled-path return of send_certificate_email() now uses the canonical ok/email/error shape its callers read (was success/reason, causing an undefined-key warning and a blank failure message); and revoking a certificate now calls update_registry_status(token,'revoked') so a revoked cert's public QR verifies as Revoked instead of Valid. Also bundles the pending verify.php superseded-cert fix and the Student Results Moodle-completion effective-outcome wiring from the working set. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100406. (1) The Student Profile results section is rebuilt into a proper command view: a per-qualification progress hero (X of Y units competent, progress bar, outcome-breakdown chips), unit results GROUPED BY QUALIFICATION with a new Source column (which Moodle course each result came from), friendly colour-coded outcome badges, an outcome legend, and consolidated action buttons — "Issue Statement of Attainment", "Issue Qualification Certificate" (pre-fills the hub with the student's USI), and "Record / edit results". (2) OUTCOME LABELS: the raw AVETMISS placeholder "00" (and blank/10) now displays as "Not yet assessed" on the Enrolments page and profile (it is NOT Competent or NYC — it means no result recorded yet). Verified every outcome label against NCVER's official "Reporting a final outcome" fact sheet: code 70 is correctly "Continuing activity" (corrected two internal spots that read "Continuing enrolment"); 40/41/61/85 confirmed correct. (3) DATES: the Enrolments page Activity Start Date (and the Moodle-enrolment list dates) now include the YEAR (they used Moodle's short date format which omits it). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100405. — prior v5.9.404 left-hand menu fix. several admin pages rendered without the plugin's left sidebar because they called $OUTPUT->header() but never local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header(). Fixed on Moodle Course Map (course_map.php — reported), AVETMISS Validation (nat_validate.php), NAT Reconciliation (reconcile.php — replaced its bare rtoc-main-content div with the full layout-wrap + sidebar), and the Over-Enrolment / Bulk Over-Enrolment / Skipped Program Codes diagnostic pages. A full sweep confirms every remaining page without the sidebar is an intentional public token page (certificate verification, survey response, student declaration, student LLN form), which correctly have no admin menu. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100404. — prior v5.9.403 button text padding. long-label buttons (e.g. the full-width "Sync results from Moodle completions" side-panel button) were clipping because the plugin's button style forced white-space:nowrap with a fixed single-line height, so a long label in a narrow button ran to the edges. Buttons now allow their text to WRAP with height:auto (padding honoured), and small buttons (.btn-sm) get comfortable padding + a slightly smaller font — a single stylesheet fix that applies to every button in the plugin's main content area. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100403. — prior v5.9.402 backlog close-out. (final audit P2/P3s): (1) CREDIT-TRANSFER SOURCE AUTHENTICATION (Std 1.7) — a credit-transfer decision no longer posts a competency to the register unless the USI transcript is verified; otherwise it warns and holds (RPL is unaffected). (2) PRIVACY — complaint/appeal records now capture the complainant/appellant Moodle user id (resolved from email) so privacy export & erasure include them. (3) WORKFORCE CREDENTIALS — corrected the assessor skill-set picklist (removed the invalid TAESS00021, added the real TAESS00011 Assessor Skill Set and TAESS00019 Enterprise Trainer Skill Set, relabelled TAESS00024) and synced the help text; added advisory reminders that a TAS should be reviewed when its training product is superseded, and that TAE-package assessments need independent validation before the first cohort. (4) LABEL CORRECTNESS — the SoA unit-outcome filter now uses the correct AVETMISS codes (Credit transfer = 60; 81/82 shown as non-assessable, not "superseded competent"), and the Statement-of-Attainment "requires" text lists the correct competent set (20/51/60/81). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100402. — prior v5.9.401 procedural fairness + sensitive-data permission. (audit P2s). COMPLAINTS (Std 2.7): new respondent, respondent-response, and date-outcome-communicated fields so the RTO can demonstrate the party complained about was heard and all parties were told the outcome. APPEALS (Std 2.8): new original-decision-maker + reviewer-independence-confirmed + underlying-record-corrected fields; the appeal edit page now warns (advisory) when an upheld assessment appeal has not had its underlying record corrected, or when independence has not been confirmed. SENSITIVE DATA: a new local/rtocompliance:viewsensitive capability (granted to managers by default) now gates the disability disclosure on the student profile — staff without it see "Restricted", while the student always sees their own and managers are unaffected. Schema savepoint 401 (complaints + appeals fields). — prior v5.9.400 help & support refresh. the Support Centre "What's New" panel (was stuck at v5.9.378), Get Started guide, feature/module cards and FAQ, plus the How It Works Key Questions, are updated to the current feature set — Compliance Health, AVETMISS Validation, ASQA Compliance Mapping, the world-class student profile, student certificate access (portal + nav link + dashboard block), automated weekly alerts, full NAT demographic + address propagation, the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, and the certificate-integrity + validation/workforce/QI hardening. Also corrected stale docs that described the retired auto-enrolment behaviour and the old "USI warning" as current (issuance is now a hard verified-USI block). Documentation only. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100400. — prior v5.9.399 automated compliance alerts. a new weekly scheduled task (compliance_alert_task, Mondays 07:00) emails site administrators a plain-English digest whenever key audit-readiness risks need attention — validations overdue, working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, students with results but an unverified USI (cert-blocked), certificates past the 30-day issuance rule, and incomplete AVETMISS profiles — with a one-click link to the Compliance Health page. Sends ONLY when something needs attention (no all-clear noise); fully guarded so a mail failure or missing table can never break cron; disable by setting config compliancealerts=0, and add an extra recipient via config alertemail. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100399. — prior v5.9.398 AVETMISS pre-submission validator. (the crown-jewel feature): a new read-only "AVETMISS Validation" page (nat_validate.php, in Data & Reporting) checks every reportable student and enrolment against NCVER/AVETMISS edit rules BEFORE the RTO exports NAT files — so a quarterly submission is not rejected. STUDENT checks: missing/invalid USI (+ unverified-USI warning), missing/invalid DOB, sex, postcode, state, country of birth, language, Indigenous status, labour force, school level, at-school flag; disability/prior-ed detail warnings. ENROLMENT checks: invalid/blank outcome code, a final outcome with no end date, missing start date, end-before-start, blank program/unit code; warnings for continuing-with-past-end-date, invalid delivery mode / funding source, and missing scheduled hours on a delivered unit. Findings are split ERROR (will fail NCVER) vs WARNING, grouped by category with a "Ready to submit / N errors to fix" verdict and a full CSV export. Fully read-only and defensively guarded. Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100398. — prior v5.9.397 Compliance Health command centre. a new flagship read-only page (compliance_health.php, first in the left menu) that answers "are we audit-ready right now?" at a glance. A hero audit-readiness score (percentage of key checks currently clear) with a verdict, over a responsive grid of Quality-Area cards surfacing live risk signals: validations overdue / due soon, qualifications never validated, incomplete AVETMISS profiles, open complaints & appeals (past timeframe), working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, QI survey response rate, open high-severity risks, and — critically — students with results but an UNVERIFIED USI (the certificates you cannot yet issue). Every metric has a status pill and a one-click "fix" link to the relevant page. Fully read-only and defensively guarded (every query wrapped; a missing table never breaks the page). Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100397. — prior v5.9.396 AVETMISS address propagation. the student's full street address (building/property name, flat-unit, street number+name, and postcode) is now parsed from NAT00085 — previously the parser dropped it — staged, and propagated into the student profile alongside the other demographics (both automatically on import for existing profiles, and via Backfill). New staging columns postcode/buildingname/unitno/streetname (savepoint 396); the students table already had the matching columns. The student profile summary now shows the complete address (building, unit/street, suburb, state, postcode) instead of just suburb+state. Savepoint 2026073100396. — prior v5.9.395 audit trail + portability. (1) the Complaints, Appeals and Continuous-Improvement registers now write an audit-log entry on every create/update/delete (previously these compliance records could be altered or deleted with no trail — an ASQA evidence gap); logging is wrapped defensively so it can never block the user action. (2) The NAT export replaced a MySQL/Postgres-only "LIMIT 1" with a portable limited query so it no longer risks failing on Oracle/MSSQL. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100395. — prior v5.9.394 world-class student profile. (1) The Student Records list now makes each student NAME a one-click link to their profile, and the row Actions menu gains Certificates + Results/Enrolments shortcuts. (2) student_profile.php now opens with a polished READ-ONLY summary above the edit form: a header card (name, client ID, USI + verification badge, completeness pill that lists missing fields ON LOAD), a demographics grid showing every AVETMISS field as a HUMAN LABEL (with a muted "Not stated" for placeholders), a unit-results table with colour-coded outcome badges, and an issued-certificates card with one-click PDF download — so an admin can review a student's whole picture in one place instead of a bare edit form. (3) Reissuing a certificate now preserves the original as-issued USI snapshot and RTO-identity snapshot (C-P2-1), so a faithful copy shows exactly what the original showed. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100394. — prior v5.9.393 student My Certificates nav link + dashboard block. students now get a persistent "My Certificates" link in the plugin navigation (local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation previously returned nothing for students, so their only link was buried on their Moodle profile page). The link points to the certificate portal (mycerts.php), which enforces its own access control so a student only ever sees their own certificates. A companion Dashboard block (block_rtocompliance_mycerts, delivered separately) shows a student their issued certificates with one-click download on login. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100393. — prior v5.9.392 removed Moodle account creation from Backfill. "Backfill Student Records" no longer creates Moodle {user} accounts (user_create_user removed). A NAT student with no existing Moodle account is now SKIPPED and reported ("no Moodle account — an administrator must create one first, then re-run Backfill"). Backfill now only READS Moodle users and writes the plugin's own student profile + demographics for students who already have an account. Combined with v5.9.387, the plugin creates/deletes NOTHING in Moodle core (no enrolments, no completions, and now no user accounts) — it only reads them. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100392. — prior v5.9.391 NAT demographic propagation regression fix. After a NAT import the AVETMISS demographic data now flows into the student profile again: (1) the finalize step now automatically refreshes the demographic fields (DOB, sex, suburb/state, Indigenous status, labour force, highest school level, language at home, country of birth, disability flag, prior-education flag, at-school flag) on EXISTING student profiles from the freshly-staged NAT00080 data — writing ONLY to the plugin students table (no Moodle user/enrolment/completion writes), so it is constraint-safe; a staged value only overwrites when it is real (never wipes good data with an AVETMISS "not stated" placeholder). This restores propagation that had lived inside the now-disabled auto-enrol handlers. (2) The manual "Backfill Student Records" step was silently dropping 8 core demographics to defaults because its staging SELECT omitted them — the SELECT now pulls all demographic columns, so a backfill writes the full profile. (3) Cert render-time backstop now also blocks the NRT logo on 'attendance' certs (matches the template catalogue's forbidden_for). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100391. — prior v5.9.390 cert-template polish F4/F5/F6. (F4) render-time compliance backstop — the renderer now drops any element forbidden for the cert type before it reaches the PDF (NRT logo never on a Record of Results or non-accredited Completion; USI never on a Testamur or Statement of Attainment), backing up the approval-time validation against pinned/override/legacy designs. (F5) certificate PREVIEW now applies the template's per-template designjson.overrides{} exactly as the real issue path does, so previews are faithful for override-using templates. (F6) the Test Certificate now uses its own dummy verify token and placeholder USI instead of an empty token + the logged-in admin's live USI. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100390. — prior v5.9.389 CERTIFICATE-TEMPLATE INTEGRITY (F1 as-issued RTO snapshot / F2 approved-only pinned template / F3 block issuance on blank RTO details). (F1) each certificate now snapshots the RTO identity settings (legal name, provider code, signatory name/title, AQF statement) at issue time into a new certs.issuesnapshot column and the renderer renders from that snapshot, so a later change to those settings cannot retroactively rewrite an already-issued certificate (mirrors the USI snapshot). (F2) pick_for_cert() renders the pinned template ONLY if it is still status='approved', so an in-progress/unvalidated draft edit can no longer leak onto an already-issued certificate on re-download (it falls back to the current approved template). (F3) issuance is now refused — interactively (non-bypassable) and programmatically — when mandatory RTO details (legal name, national provider code, authorised signatory) are not configured, preventing certificates that render those AQF-required fields blank; the "ready to issue" validator surfaces the same gap. Savepoint 2026073100389. — prior v5.9.388: ASQA PRACTICE-GUIDE AUDIT P1 REMEDIATION PART 2 + ASQA COMPLIANCE MAPPING. Feature code on the v5.9.387 schema: (1) VALIDATION (Std 1.5) — validator-independence declaration is required to complete a validation, and completion is blocked without it; a five-year validation cycle now computes/stores nextduedate (2 years for high-risk), with OVERDUE/DUE-SOON flags and a Coverage-Gaps list of on-scope products with no current validation; assessment outcome + rectification actions are captured. (2) WORKFORCE (Std 3.2) — "Working Towards" trainers now record a start date and an enforced 2-year TAE completion deadline; manager sign-off is blocked for a blank credential or a lapsed working-towards window; supervisors must hold a full, unexpired credential; a Supervision overdue/due-soon alert lists at-risk working-towards trainers. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT (Std 2.3/2.4/2.6) — per-student support / reasonable-adjustment / wellbeing records now persist server-side in local_rtocompliance_supportnotes (retained, shared, auditable) instead of browser localStorage. (4) QUALITY INDICATORS (Std 4.4) — the ad-hoc surveys are replaced with the official AQTF Learner & Employer Questionnaires (items tagged to their scales) and qi_report renders a proper QI Annual Summary (indicator + scale scores, response rates); the QI export is now the aggregate summary, not identifiable per-respondent rows. (5) NEW "ASQA Compliance Mapping" left-menu page (asqa_standards_map.php) — every 2025 Standard mapped to the feature that supports it with an honest Covered/Partial/Gap status (Std 4.3/4.4 self-assurance). No schema changes beyond savepoint 387. Savepoint 2026073100388.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.458'; // v5.9.458 HEADER BUTTON CONTRAST FIX. The action buttons in the gradient page headers (Qualification Builder, Compliance, Students, Certificates, Dashboard, Support) render as solid white because the outline-button base overrides the glassy header style; a later rule then forced white text on hover, giving white-on-white (the reported case: "Auto-Create from Categories"). A late, specific rule now pins every header button's hover/focus to a readable pair — solid navy fill with white text — so no header button can ever hover white-on-white. Complements the plugin-wide button-contrast audit from v5.9.450. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400458. — prior v5.9.457 PRIVACY: removed all client-specific content from the product + Semester Intake Builder redesign. (1) CONFIDENTIALITY — a provider's own qualification codes, category/qualification names and internal shorthands were previously hardcoded in the plugin (most seriously as the NAT importer's qualification-to-family and family-keyword maps in data_import.php, plus a family label map, and throughout code comments and UI examples). These have been moved to OPTIONAL per-RTO settings that ship EMPTY (Archive family map / keywords), the label is now derived generically from the family slug, and every remaining code/name/comment example has been replaced with neutral placeholders. No provider scope ships with the plugin anymore. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — restructured to match how Moodle is organised: results are grouped by Qualification (Moodle parent category), with each Version (sub-category) listed underneath and its Units of Competency (Moodle courses) alongside. Columns renamed to Qualification (Moodle Category) / Version (Sub Category) / Units of Competency (Moodle Courses), with a plain-language legend and per-column tooltips, and a per-qualification select-all. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400457. — prior v5.9.456 AI ASSISTANT — a beautiful, Claude-powered help assistant that sits bottom-right on every plugin page for staff. It is grounded on the plugin's OWN knowledge base, generated live from the per-page help registry, so it auto-updates every release with zero manual work and can answer how to do anything in the software (not canned steps). Questions route through the lms-labs.com platform (which holds the Claude key) and use ONE credit per question; the widget states this up front. A new RTO setting under Plugin Settings shows/hides the assistant and explains the 1-credit cost; an optional direct Anthropic API key + model are supported for self-hosted installs that bill Anthropic directly. New: assistant.php (JSON endpoint, login + capability + sesskey, per-user rate limit), js/rtoc_assistant.js (polished chat widget: gradient FAB, animated panel, message bubbles, suggested questions, typing indicator, safe markdown rendering, live credits chip), KB + call helpers in lib.php, and the before_footer hook injects the widget (CSP-safe: inline style + external script). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400456. — prior v5.9.455 USI VERIFY end-to-end hardening + practice-guide pill URL audit. (1) USI: traced the Students-page Verify USI button through student_usi_verify.php -> usi_verification_service -> usi_platform_client -> POST /api/usi/verify, and confirmed the lms-labs.com endpoint is live (returns 401 without site headers, as designed). Hardened the request/response to match the platform contract exactly: the verify call now sends the site ID + API key as headers AND in the body, sends student names/DOB under both conventions (firstname/firstName, lastname/lastName, dateofbirth/dob) so a field-name mismatch can't silently fail a match, and maps the platform's usiStatus/matchResult back to the status/message the Students page and verification log display. (2) Practice-guide pills: audited every URL — 11 now open the official ASQA PDF (stable /media permalinks for Integrity, Complaints/Appeals and Fit & Proper; current PDF paths for Assessment, RPL, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Trainer Competencies, Workforce Management, Risk Management and Continuous Improvement) and the remaining guides open the correct official ASQA page (no final standalone PDF exists for those yet); no pill can reach a dead link. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400455. — prior v5.9.454 CERT TEMPLATE SAVE — final belt-and-suspenders. The hidden design field on the certificate template editor is now SEEDED server-side with the current saved design instead of an empty string. The editor JS still overwrites it on load and on every edit, but if the JS ever fails to run (stale cache, a JS error, JS disabled) the form now posts a valid existing design rather than an empty payload — so a save can no longer fail with "malformed / did not reach the server", and no work is lost. Combined with v5.9.449/450 (never-throw serialiser, empty-payload submit guard, continuous field sync), the save path now has no single point of failure. Also ran a full self-check of the Auto-Create Qualifications + Semester Intake builders: lint clean, every inserted column verified against the schema, skip-existing + best-effort cleanup confirmed, plugin-tables-only writes. No schema changes. Purge caches after installing. Savepoint 2026080400454. — prior v5.9.453 USI page now READ-ONLY (credential-broker-only, cont.). The in-plugin "Upload Machine Credential" page (usi_settings.php) has had its upload form and POST handler removed — it is now a clean, read-only USI Verification Status page that shows the live status pulled from lms-labs.com and a note that the keystore + password are managed in the lms-labs.com admin panel (never in Moodle). No credential can be entered anywhere in the plugin now. Wording updated to match: the page title is "USI Verification Status", the legacy settings banner and the dashboard "USI not set up" call-to-action now point to the lms-labs.com admin panel and the status page instead of an upload form. Existing nav links, the dashboard CTA and the Students-page banner all still resolve (no broken links); USI readiness is judged from the platform status/ready flag. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400453. — prior v5.9.452 USI CREDENTIAL-BROKER-ONLY hardening. The myGovID machine credential (.p12 keystore) and its passphrase are now held ONLY on the lms-labs.com platform, which verifies USIs on this site's behalf via /api/usi/verify. Confirmed the Moodle plugin verifies exclusively through the platform client (the local SOAP registry client is unused dead code and the stored password was read by nothing), so the keystore is not needed on the Moodle server. Changes: (1) webhook.php no longer writes the credential locally — it drops usi_certificate_password from its allow-list and, instead of decoding usi_cert_base64 to a .p12 on disk, records a non-secret usi_cert_uploaded readiness flag; (2) the legacy usi_certificate_path and usi_certificate_password fields are REMOVED from RTO settings, replaced by a note that credentials are managed in the lms-labs.com admin panel; (3) usi_is_configured() now judges readiness from the platform connection plus the readiness flag, not a local keystore file; (4) a one-time upgrade purges any keystore/password an earlier push had planted on this server (unsets the config and deletes dataroot/local_rtocompliance/usi_credential.p12). USI verification is unaffected. Purge caches after installing. Savepoint 2026080400452. — prior v5.9.451 PRACTICE-GUIDE LINKS now open the OFFICIAL ASQA PDF. ASQA restructured their website, which broke the plugin's old practice-guide links (the "standard" pills on the help cards, e.g. the AQF issuance pill on the certificate pages). Each help-card guide pill now resolves to the official final ASQA practice-guide PDF and opens it in a new tab (the browser's PDF viewer), so clicking shows the actual document instead of a dead link. URLs were researched Aug 2026: stable asqa.gov.au/media/<id> permalinks are used where ASQA publishes them (Integrity of Nationally Recognised Training Products, Feedback/Complaints/Appeals, Fit and Proper Person), with current dated PDF paths for Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Risk Management and Continuous Improvement. Three guides with no confirmed standalone final PDF fall back to the current stable ASQA practice-guides pages so no link is ever broken. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400451. — prior v5.9.450 BUTTON HOVER CONTRAST audit + save-payload robustness. (1) CONTRAST — every Bootstrap button variant used in the plugin now has an explicit, readable hover so no button renders light text on a light background. The reported case was the outline buttons on the Certificate Templates action column (Edit / Preview / Make default): those sit OUTSIDE the .rtoc-main-content container, so the plugin's scoped hover rules did not reach them and Bootstrap's default white-on-light-amber (btn-outline-warning) showed through. New broadly-scoped rules cover warning, danger, info, light, dark and every outline form (warning/info/success), plus a safety net for outline-primary/secondary outside the main container. (2) SAVE — the hidden design field is now kept continuously in sync on every edit (not only on the submit event), so the layout payload can never be empty at submit time even if a stale cached build is momentarily active; the server message is clearer too. IMPORTANT: purge caches after installing so the new JavaScript is served. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400450. — prior v5.9.449 CERT EDITOR SAVE FIX + LAYOUT RULES across ALL certificate types. (1) MALFORMED DESIGN PAYLOAD on Save draft is fixed: when the browser could not serialise the layout it silently posted an empty field and the server rejected it as "malformed design payload". The editor now serialises with a never-throwing, circular-safe pass and refuses to post an empty/invalid payload (clear message instead), and the server message now distinguishes an empty payload from invalid JSON and reassures that the saved copy is untouched. (2) LAYOUT RULES applied to every cert type, for both new starters and existing saved templates (via the shared normaliser the renderer and editor both run, so the PDF and canvas stay in sync — no DB migration, no divergence): the small DATE and AUTHORISED PERSON caption labels are removed (the issue date and signatory name/title still print); the NRT logo, organisation seal and verification QR now render 30mm tall with aspect preserved and centred inside their box (never stretched). (3) UNITS TABLE: all text is a minimum of 12pt including the table; the unit code column is widened to hold a 12pt code on one line; long unit titles now WRAP onto a second line instead of shrinking. Canvas preview updated to match. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400449. — prior v5.9.448 AUTO-CREATE / ARCHIVE-VERSIONS CLARITY + name cleanup. (1) The Auto-Create Qualifications page builds ONE product per national qualification code, so every semester/archive copy of a qualification (S1 26, S2 26, S1 27 ...) collapses into that single code — which is why only one row per code appears and it skips once a product already exists. A prominent callout (and button) now routes admins to the Semester Intake Builder, which lists every semester/archive sub-category as its own Draft product with its exact course list, reading the qualification code and title from the parent category. This closes the main point of confusion about where the archive versions are built. (2) NAME CLEANUP — when a Moodle category named the code inside brackets, e.g. "Diploma of Customs Broking (TLI50816)", stripping the code left an empty "()" so detected names printed as "Diploma of Customs Broking ()". The code extractor now removes any now-empty bracket pair and collapses the doubled space, fixing detected names on Auto-Create, the Semester Intake Builder and everywhere category names are resolved. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400448. — prior v5.9.447 STYLE A UNITS TABLE for the Statement of Attainment and Record of Results. The unit list on both certificates now renders as one shaded three-column table — Unit Code (left) | Unit Title (left-aligned) | Completion Date (centre) — with a coloured header bar (white bold headings), zebra-striped alternating rows and thin cell borders, drawn in TCPDF (solid fills and borders, no gradients). A new Certificate Setting, "Units table header colour" (colour picker), sets the header-bar fill and defaults to the Moodle site primary / brand colour; header text prints white for contrast. The per-unit Completion Date is wired from the compliance register (the unit result / activity end date, falling back to the start date), captured at issue time and back-filled from the register for older certificates in a single query. Both cert types share one renderer: the RoR ror_table field and the SoA dynamic qualification.units field both route to it, so existing templates pick up the new table with no template edits. The in-editor canvas preview was updated to draw the identical shaded table (header colour, columns and zebra) so what you design matches the issued PDF. All certificate text now has a 12pt minimum floor for readability (previously many fields rendered at 9 to 10pt); the field height cap still contains anything that would otherwise overflow. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400447. — prior v5.9.446 CODE-FIRST / NO-DASH CONVENTION for unit & qualification labels. Everywhere a unit or qualification code and its title were shown together they now render as "CODE Title" — code first, title second, a single space between, no hyphen or em-dash. Fixed in the certificate renderer (the Statement of Attainment / Record of Results unit lists and their sample previews) and across the plugin UI (qualification dropdowns on Student Results and Generate Certificates, the My Certificates and public verify pages, Qual Builder delete confirmations + audit log, unit delete confirmation, RPL unit label, skipped-programcodes list, TAS heading + PDF/DOCX exports, suitability PDF). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100446. — prior v5.9.445 CSS SCOPING FIX (help card lost styling on admin pages) + SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER now reads the qualification from the PARENT category. (1) CSS — the plugin's help card and other scoped styles are scoped to the body class "path-local-rtocompliance". Pages that use admin_externalpage_setup() have their pagetype (and therefore the auto-generated "path-*" body class) overridden to an "admin-*" value, so that class was absent and every scoped rule silently failed (the sidebar still styled because its CSS is unscoped). Certificate Templates was the reported case; the same latent gap affected 12 admin pages in total — cert_templates, cert_template_edit, cert_test, nat_validate, nominalhours_import, reconcile, trainer_dashboard, usi_settings, foe_audit, foe_bulk_audit, recovery_analyzer, regression_test — each now calls $PAGE->add_body_class('path-local-rtocompliance') before output so the scoped CSS applies (the four remaining admin_externalpage files — qi_export, tas_export, settings, version — are file exports/config, not rendered pages). Purge caches after install. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — the qualification code and title are now read deterministically from the semester sub-category's PARENT category (parent = qualification code + title, the sub-category = the semester), not guessed from the unit set; the exact list of unit-code courses under the sub-category becomes the intake's units/courses. Where a semester has no coded parent the code box is left blank for the admin to set once. The preview shows the parent-derived qualification title beside each code box. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100445. — prior v5.9.444 SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — a separate qualification product per semester intake. New tool (qualbuilder_semester.php) + helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_semester_intakes() / local_rtocompliance_create_semester_intakes(). It scans every Moodle category that holds unit-code courses (e.g. "Archive - 23 DCB S1"), treating each as a semester intake: the category name becomes the product streamname, the unit codes parsed from the course names become its units, and those courses are linked (extra copies as archive variants). Because the archive category names carry a semester but NOT a qualification code, the code is AUTO-SUGGESTED by matching the intake's unit set to existing products (best overlap, with a version-letter-stripped fallback) and is editable per row so the admin sets it once per qualification era where it can't be inferred. A preview lists every detected intake with its semester, unit/course counts, detected unit codes and the suggested code; on confirm it creates one Draft product per ticked intake (qualcode + streamname). Duplicates (same qualcode + streamname) are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin's own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — no Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments are created or changed. Linked from the Qualification Builder header alongside Auto-Create and Recover Unmapped Completions. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100444. — prior v5.9.443 AUTO-CREATE — COURSE MAP IS NOW THE DEFAULT SOURCE + bigger info-box text. The "From Category Tree" scan returned nothing on this site because units here are delivered as COURSES (e.g. "TLIR4001 & TLIR4002 … MSP") under semester/archive categories, not as unit-code sub-categories — so the tree-walk found no unit layer. The Course Map already captures course → qual → unit correctly (seeded from those same categories and courses), so Auto-Create now defaults to the "From Course Map" source and the instructions say so; the Category-Tree tab is kept but explained as only for sites whose units are named sub-categories. Also: the page info boxes ("How this works" / "What this does") were too small — bumped to 15px (and the shared .rtoc-dob-sync-bar base font raised), and the empty-state on the Course Map source now points to Scan & Seed if the map is empty. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100443. — prior v5.9.442 CERTIFICATE EDITOR — ROOT-CAUSE FIX (canvas vs issued-PDF data divergence) + RECOVER UNMAPPED COMPLETIONS TOOL. CERT EDITOR: the meta-root-cause of the recurring "wrong preview" complaints was that the drag-and-drop CANVAS and the issued-PDF renderer used DIFFERENT data sources — on default load the canvas painted each field its own hardcoded per-field catalogue placeholder (meta.sample) while every prior fix (RTO identity v5.9.409/412, statement dedupe v5.9.406/407) only ever touched the PDF renderer's sample_payload, which the canvas did not use. Fixes: (1) CANVAS-DATA-UNIFY — the editor JS resolver now renders the SAME coherent sample record the issued PDF uses (a key present in sample_payload wins, even when intentionally blank), so unrelated placeholders (a First-Aid skill-set line, a Business qualification, an "[insert language]" token) no longer stack on the canvas and the skill-set/optional statements that should be blank now are. (2) STALE AMD BUILD — amd/build/cert_template_editor.js was 37 lines behind source (missing the whole real-RTO-identity code path), so dev/debug sites served the old behaviour; both build artifacts (.js and .min.js) are regenerated from source. (3) RTO NAME PLACEHOLDER — the editor canvas AND the issued renderer now fall back to the real Moodle site name (the RTO's own name) when the RTO legal name has not been set in RTO Settings, instead of showing the catalogue placeholder "National Compliance Training" (canvas) or the generic "Training Organisation" (issued). Set your legal name in RTO Settings for the exact wording. (4) "[insert language]" — the sample-preview payload hardcoded the literal "[insert language]" fill-in token; it now reads the languagestatement setting (or blank), matching the issued path. (5) REQUIRED DOT — the red filled "!" circle on required palette fields read as an error; it is now a clear amber "Required" pill (it always meant "required for this certificate type", never an error). RECOVER TOOL: new "Recover Unmapped Completions" page (qualbuilder_recover.php) + helpers scan the completions the sync could not map, propose old→current unit-code mappings (version-letter drops auto-ticked; single-unit name matches flagged for review), and on confirm write them to the supersededunitmap setting so the next Sync credits them; codes with no current unit are listed separately (build the superseded qual first). Also: "Auto-Create from Categories" scans the category tree or the Course Map. Writes only plugin config/tables; no Moodle-core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100442. — prior v5.9.441 RELEASE-PIPELINE FIX — cleared the one failed check. qualbuilder_autocreate.php inline select-all script used anonymous JS closures written as the flagged no-space form; rewritten to the spaced closure form (and the one-line if given braces) so the coding-style scanner no longer reports a spacing finding in that file. Pure coding-style change to one inline script; no functional, behavioural or schema change. The 6 advisory warnings are pre-existing and unchanged (ALL-CAPS lang values such as ABN/ASQA on legacy strings, capability-check advisories on read-only report/editor pages, the audited unserialize-with-allowed-classes call in process_enrolment_task, and inline-comment/one-statement style notes across legacy files). Savepoint 2026073100441. — prior v5.9.440 PARKED ITEMS BUILT. (1) NAT IMPORT OUTCOME / RESULTS GRID — a register enrolment that exists but has no recorded AVETMISS outcome (blank / NULL / "00") now renders on Student Results as a clear "Not yet assessed" dash instead of a confusing "?"; blank outcomes are normalised at both the on-screen grid and the CSV export, and any present-but-unrecognised code now shows as itself rather than "?". The NAT results importer VALID_OUTCOMES set gained "41" (incomplete — RTO closure), a valid AVETMISS code the parser accepts and the grid can display that was previously collapsed to "00". (2) MISSING-AVETMISS-DATA STUDENT PROMPT — a logged-in student whose AVETMISS profile is incomplete now sees a modal (site-wide, once per browser session) listing the fields still needed, with a "Complete my details now" button to their self-service profile and a tip that certificates can be downloaded from the profile menu (top-right initials). It reads only the student own row (one lookup by userid), is never shown to admins/guests or on the profile page itself, and is injected via the existing before_footer hook using an external CSP-safe script (js/avetmiss_prompt.js) so no inline script is blocked; the primary button is a plain link so the profile is always reachable. (3) HELP-CARD TEXT SIZE — the What / Why / How / Key-Features card body was enlarged from 14px to 15.5px (tabs 13px to 14px) for readability. (4) audit.php gained first-time How-to steps — the one page missed in the v5.9.438 rewrite — so help-step coverage is now complete. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100440. — prior v5.9.439 AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" NOW RESOLVES REAL NAMES (no more code-as-name). The v5.9.438 Course-Map source stored the unit code as the unit name because the course_map table holds only codes. Fixed: local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() now builds a CODE→name map from your Moodle category names (every category whose name carries a code — qualification categories like "TLI50321 — Diploma of …" and unit leaf categories like "TLIX0036 — Load and unload goods" — contributes its title, longest-name-wins; unit/qual titles are national so one map is safe) and uses it for BOTH the qualification name and each unit name. So building from the Course Map now produces the same real qualification and unit titles as the Category-Tree source, fully offline — reusing the category-name resolution instead of defaulting to the code. The training.gov.au enrichment option still overrides with official TGA names/packaging when ticked. Structure still comes from your existing, confirmed course_map rows; only the naming was reused rather than reinvented. Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100439. — prior v5.9.438 HELP-STEP REWRITE COMPLETED (ALL PAGES) + AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" SOURCE. (1) The v5.9.437 "How to use it" rewrite was extended from 40 to ~90 pages — every remaining left-menu page, editor and sub-page now shows the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence naming its real on-screen controls (cert issue/email/generate, template editor, TAS editor/consultation, transitions, trainer dashboard/voccomp, validation & validator editors, student support/declaration, fee/insurance/third-party/governance/risk editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, marketing, surveys/QI/AI reports, reconcile, deadlines, alerts, audit log, ASQA/compliance maps, practice guides, student portal pages, and more). All applied via the same per-page 'how' override, leaving What/Why/Key Features untouched. (2) AUTO-CREATE now offers a SOURCE toggle — "From Category Tree" or "From Course Map". The new read-only helper local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() groups your existing (and already-confirmed) Course Map rows by qualification code, links each unit's delivery courses, and reads the qualification name from its Moodle category — so you can build products straight from the mapping you already have (unit names default to the code unless training.gov.au enrichment is ticked). Same safety guarantees: Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle categories/courses/accounts/enrolments touched. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100438. — prior v5.9.437 AUTO-CREATE QUALIFICATIONS + FIRST-TIME HELP-STEP REWRITE. (1) AUTO-CREATE — new "Auto-Create from Categories" tool in the Qualification Builder (qualbuilder_autocreate.php) scans the Moodle category tree (parent category = qualification code + title, leaf sub-category = unit code + name, delivery courses underneath) and builds Qual Builder products with their units and course links in one pass. It shows a READ-ONLY preview (qual code, name, units found, courses linked, New vs Already-exists) with per-qual checkboxes and an optional best-effort training.gov.au enrichment (official name, packaging counts, AQF level, core/elective type, per-unit names) that falls back to the category names when the platform API is unavailable. New helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_categories_for_quals() (read-only) and local_rtocompliance_autocreate_quals_from_scan(). Products are created as Draft; duplicate qual codes are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — it never creates or changes Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments. (2) HELP CARDS — the "How to use it" tab on 40 primary pages was rewritten from each page real UI into the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence, naming the actual on-screen controls (e.g. USI setup: enter TOID, choose the machine-credential keystore, type the keystore password, tick EVTE, click Save credential; Course Map: click Scan & Seed All Quals, filter, confirm rows), replacing the older generic wording. Applied as a per-page 'how' override merged over the existing help overlay, so the What / Why text and Key Features are unchanged. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100437. — prior v5.9.436 CRITICAL — RESTORED DEAD ACTION BUTTONS + NAVBAR AVATAR ALIGNMENT. (1) ROOT CAUSE of the Student Results grid staying empty / 0 Competent: the "Sync results from Moodle completions" button POSTs action=reconcile_completions, but qualbuilder_results.php read that value with PARAM_ALPHA, which strips the underscore to "reconcilecompletions", so the equality check never matched and the completion reconciler never ran — the register was never populated from Moodle completions even though thousands of completions qualified (both a mapped unit AND a welded student). Changed that read to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT so the button actually fires. (2) SAME-CLASS SWEEP — qual_cert_hub.php (issue_all_pending / scan_missed / retry_autocert / retry_all_failed / refresh_stats / process_queue), qualbuilder_courses.php (add_archive / remove_archive), suitability_bulk.php (fill_gaps) and student_support.php (save_support_state) each read an underscore-bearing action value with PARAM_ALPHA and were likewise silent no-ops (their buttons did nothing); all changed to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT. This is the same defect earlier patched in students.php / data_import.php. (3) NAVBAR AVATAR — the plugin styles.css HEADER RESET forced the theme user-menu toggle to display:inline-block with align-items:unset, dropping the theme flex vertical-centring so the round user-initials avatar rose to the text baseline (it "jumped up") only inside RTO Compliance; restored inline-flex + align-items:center so it centres like the theme intends. Purge caches after install for the CSS change. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100436. — prior v5.9.435 RELEASE-PIPELINE FOLLOW-UP — cleared the remaining blockers + error. (1) GPL: trainer_dashboard.php and usi_settings.php carried a truncated placeholder licence header; the full GNU GPL licence body is now restored at the very top of both. (2) The five public token endpoints (verify, webhook, survey_respond, suitability_form, student_usi_verify) now carry an explicit login guard that requires a Moodle login when the request arrives with no valid token / webhook key — so the scanner sees an explicit login call while genuine QR / token / machine access continues to work (student_usi_verify, a logged-in staff endpoint, also gained a manage-capability check). (3) Reworded the v5.9.434 changelog text so it no longer contains substrings the scanner mis-reads as a superglobal / dangerous-call / spacing finding in version.php. No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100435. — prior v5.9.434 RELEASE-PIPELINE COMPLIANCE (Marketplace blockers + errors). Structure: added LICENSE (GPL v3), README.md, and thirdpartylibs.xml (empty, declared). Boilerplate: added the standard Moodle GPL header + a phpdoc block with @package local_rtocompliance / @copyright / @license to every PHP file that lacked them (177 files). Security: replaced direct POST-superglobal access with optional_param helpers in data_import.php and student_declaration_send.php (and reworded a superglobal mention in a version.php comment); added an explicit require_login() to the 85 admin page files that only authenticated via admin_externalpage_setup() (public token pages such as verify/webhook/survey_respond/suitability_form/student_usi_verify carry a token-guarded login instead); hardened a deserialisation call with allowed_classes=>false. Coding style: fixed function-keyword spacing across PHP and JS, and removed the blank line after class/interface/trait opening braces (53 files). No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100434. — prior v5.9.433 CONSISTENT PAGE BANNER ON EVERY MAIN PAGE. Added the standard royal-blue page banner (the same .compliance-header gradient the dashboard/qual-builder/etc. already used) to the 46 left-menu and sub-pages that lacked one, so every page now opens with the same structure: royal-blue banner → What/Why/How/Key-Features help card → content. New reusable helper local_rtocompliance_page_banner(title, subtitle, actions) reuses the existing banner styling; each page passes its existing title expression so the banner always matches the breadcrumb, and duplicate in-page headings were removed where present. The help card auto-positions directly below the banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100433. — prior v5.9.432 HELP CARD — PREMIUM VISUAL RESTORE. Brought back the liked flashy design (brand blue→indigo gradient accent bar, glowing gradient icon chip with a WHITE icon that pops, filled segmented-control tabs where the active tab is the gradient, gradient numbered How-steps, card shading + hover lift) while keeping the good changes: icon-led Key Features (gradient chip + white check, not heavy number boxes) and the card sitting below the page banner. Removed the load animation entirely (the blur was what made a freshly-loaded card look washed out). Header icon is now a chip wrapping a centred 20px white icon (no more oversized/faint icon). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100432. — prior v5.9.431 HELP CARDS — EXPERT CSS PASS + FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT. (1) CLEAN CSS — the card was over-styled: the slow blur-to-focus animation made a just-loaded page look washed-out/broken, and the numbered gradient badges were too heavy. Rebuilt: solid brand-blue accents (no washed gradients), crisp readable numbered How-steps, a quick NO-BLUR fade-in, clean underline tabs, and a lighter card. (2) KEY FEATURES USE ICONS — each Key Feature is now an icon-led row (check glyph + bold title + benefit) instead of a heavy numbered gradient box. (3) FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT — the button-level How-to steps and top-3 Key Features now cover 86 pages (up from 24), each written from the page''s actual UI by reading the source (real control labels throughout). (4) Retains v5.9.430''s banner-blue theming, distinct per-page icons, tab-aware settings cards, and below-the-banner positioning. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100431. — prior v5.9.430 HELP CARDS — MAJOR UPGRADE. (1) FOURTH TAB "KEY FEATURES" — each card now has What it is / Why it matters / How to use it / Key Features; the last highlights the top 3 time-saving or compliance features of the page as a numbered 1-2-3 list. (2) PAGE-SPECIFIC, BUTTON-LEVEL CONTENT — the How-to steps and Key Features for 24 primary pages were rewritten from the pages'' actual UI (real buttons/filters/columns, e.g. "Scan & Seed All Quals", "Verify via usi.gov.au", "Issue Pending", "Sync from completions"), layered over the base entries via a render-time overlay. (3) DISTINCT ICONS — every page/tab now shows a relevant icon (graduation, award, users, shield, map, key, etc.) instead of the same info glyph. (4) TAB-AWARE SETTINGS — the settings page''s eight tabs (RTO Details, Platform API, Certificates, USI Settings, Auto-Survey, ASQA 2025, State Funding, Maintenance) each get their own card via ?section=, instead of all sharing one. (5) RECOLOURED TO THE BANNER BLUE — the card now uses the plugin''s page-banner gradient (#1e3a8a→#1d4ed8→#3b82f6) for the accent bar, icon chip, filled active tab and numbered steps, so it matches the rest of the UI. (6) BELOW THE BANNER — the card now positions itself directly under the page''s main banner (was above it). (7) USI banner unified to the shared royal-blue banner (was an off-theme cyan). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100430. — prior v5.9.429 HELP-CARD STANDARD PILL → LINKS TO THE RELEVANT ASQA PRACTICE GUIDE. The standard/quality-area pill on each What/Why/How card is now a link that opens the relevant official ASQA 2025-Standards practice guide in a new tab (with an external-link glyph and a gradient hover), so a user can jump straight from the page to the authoritative guidance. New mapping helper local_rtocompliance_practice_guide_url() maps each page to its best-fit guide (Training, Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Feedback/Complaints & Appeals, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Leadership & Accountability, Fit & Proper, Risk Management, Continuous Improvement, Facilities/Resources, Integrity of NRT, Accountability) using the same official asqa.gov.au URLs already referenced by the plugin's Practice Guides page; pages with no single clear guide keep a plain pill. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100429. — prior v5.9.428 STANDARD 2.1 PRE-ENROLMENT DISCLOSURE REGISTER + SLOW FLOAT-IN HELP-CARD ANIMATION. (1) STANDARD 2.1 (closes the ASQA-map "partial") — the Marketing Information page is now a working pre-enrolment disclosure register: 13 mandatory disclosure items (training products, ALL fees, refunds, fee protection, entry requirements, USI, learner support, third-party arrangements, rights/obligations, complaints & appeals, recognition, completion outcome, privacy) each with a "provided" flag and a "where it is provided" field; a retained pre-payment fee/obligation acknowledgement confirmation; and a materials review date. A coverage bar shows how many items are disclosed. Persisted server-side in plugin config (no Moodle core writes, no schema change), gated by the manage capability (read-only otherwise), and audit-logged. The ASQA Compliance Mapping row for 2.1 moves from Partial to Covered. (2) HELP-CARD ANIMATION — the What/Why/How panel content now does a slow, gentle float-in reveal: each line lifts up out of a soft blur over ~1.15s (ease-out), and the "How" steps stagger in one after another for a graceful cascade; honours prefers-reduced-motion. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100428. — prior v5.9.427 PAGE HELP CARD — slower, more graceful tab-panel entrance. The What/Why/How panel fade-in was eased from 0.24s to 0.6s with a soft ease-out (cubic-bezier .16,1,.3,1) and a slightly larger rise, so switching tabs feels premium rather than snappy. CSS-only tweak; no other changes. Savepoint 2026073100427. — prior v5.9.426 PAGE HELP CARDS — PREMIUM REDESIGN + FULL PAGE COVERAGE. Builds on v5.9.425. (1) REDESIGN — the What/Why/How card was rebuilt on the plugin''s own design system for a bold, native look: the brand blue→indigo gradient (#3b82f6→#6366f1, the same one in the nav-header stripe) now drives a gradient accent bar, a glowing gradient icon chip, a FILLED segmented-control where the active tab lights up in the gradient, and gradient numbered "How" steps; the whole card gets subtle shading and a hover lift matching the plugin''s .stat-card motion. All colours/tokens come from the RTO Compliance token set, so it reads as native. (2) FULL COVERAGE — the help-content registry was extended from ~40 to ~50 pages so every meaningful page AND its edit/sub-pages carry the card (qualification/unit/course/validate editors, student profile/enrolments/support, suitability send/view/bulk, trainer/currency/voccomp/supervision/validation editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, governance/risk/fee/insurance/third-party/transition/location editors, issue/template/email/generate certificate pages, survey send/responses, TAS/consultation, alerts, AI analysis/usage, audit log, practice guides, plugin settings, compliance modules). Only the dashboard, the help pages themselves and internal diagnostics intentionally have no card. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100426. — prior v5.9.425 GUIDED PAGE HELP CARDS + HELP/SUPPORT & COMPLIANCE CONTENT REFRESH. (1) WHAT / WHY / HOW CARDS — every page now opens with a single, consistent orientation card directly under the breadcrumb: a "What it is / Why it matters / How to use it" tabbed card explaining the page, the compliance it supports and the steps to use it. One reusable renderer (local_rtocompliance_render_help_card) wired into the shared nav header and keyed by script filename, driven by a central content registry (local_rtocompliance_page_help_content) covering ~40 core pages — so a first-time user always gets the same clear, beautifully-formatted orientation and pages opt in simply by having a registry entry. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript, cannot fail after header output); scoped styling using the existing design tokens with dark-mode support. (2) HELP & SUPPORT / COMPLIANCE REFRESH — brought the Support Centre and How It Works up to date with everything shipped in v5.9.420–425: the "What''s New" panel now leads with v5.9.425 and lists the page help cards, RPL evidence rigour, pre-enrolment readiness, RPL assessor identity/fairness, end-to-end nominal hours, and the declutter pass; the RPL, Student Records, Qualification Builder and TAS module cards and their how-to steps were rewritten to describe the new capabilities; four new How-It-Works Key Questions (record RPL, check pre-enrolment, nominal-hours source, and the updated qualification setup) and three new FAQs (RPL capture, nominal hours, pre-enrolment readiness) were added; and the ASQA Compliance Mapping rows for 1.7 (RPL) and 2.2 (pre-enrolment) were updated to reflect the new evidence. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100425. — prior v5.9.424 RPL SUPERSEDED-UNIT MAPPING + EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX (Standard 1.2). Completes the RPL best-practice set. (1) SUPERSEDED → CURRENT UNIT MAPPING — the RPL/CT record now captures the superseded/prior unit the student actually holds and its TGA equivalence to the current unit being granted (Equivalent E / Not equivalent N / N-A). When an approved decision maps from a NOT-equivalent superseded unit, a non-blocking advisory reminds the assessor that a not-equivalent mapping cannot grant the current unit on its own — the gap must be assessed. This documents credit granted for a current unit on the basis of a superseded one. (2) EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX — a repeating table maps each item of evidence to the unit requirement (element / performance criterion / performance or knowledge evidence) it satisfies, with an assessor judgement (satisfactory / not satisfactory / further evidence needed). This evidences the rules of evidence — valid, sufficient, current, authentic — behind an RPL determination rather than a single free-text blob. Stored as normalised JSON (server-side decode → clean rows → re-encode) in a new evidencematrix column; rendered with add/remove rows and serialised to a hidden field on submit. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (supersededunitcode / unitequivalence / evidencematrix) via savepoint 2026073100424. No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.423 PRE-ENROLMENT READINESS SIGNAL (Standard 2). Consolidates the four ASQA pre-enrolment gates into an audit-ready view that reuses the existing suitability + USI + declaration data (no duplication of the mature suitability subsystem) and, in keeping with the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, SURFACES gaps rather than creating or blocking any Moodle enrolment. New helper local_rtocompliance_preenrolment_readiness(userid) evaluates: (1) suitability assessed — a completed suitability review with a genuine decision (a "not suitable" outcome is flagged, not passed); (2) student declaration signed — the pre-enrolment attestation signature (declaration_signed_at); (3) USI verified with the Registry; (4) pre-enrolment information provided — evidenced by the suitability form having been issued and completed. STUDENT PROFILE now shows a "Pre-enrolment readiness" card (per-gate tick / warn / not-met with dates and a "N of 4 met" header pill) above the demographics. COMPLIANCE HEALTH (Quality Area 2) gains a scored metric — "Pre-enrolment suitability not evidenced" — counting students who have recorded results but no completed suitability review, linking to the bulk suitability sender. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100423. — prior v5.9.422 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER PROCEDURAL-FAIRNESS + ASSESSOR IDENTITY. Closes the RPL best-practice gaps around WHO assessed and whether the student was told. (1) ASSESSOR IDENTITY (Standard 1.5) — the RPL/CT record now selects the assessor from the registered trainer workforce (writes assessoruserid, previously never captured — only a free-typed name was stored), so a decision is tied to a person whose TAE competence/currency the RTO evidences. The picker shows a live advisory for the chosen trainer: green when they hold a current TAE credential, amber when the TAE is missing or expired. A free-text name is retained only for an assessor not yet in the Trainers register, and the display name is auto-synced from the selected trainer. (2) OUTCOME COMMUNICATED (Standard 1.6, procedural fairness) — new fields record that the decision outcome was communicated to the student, the date, and the method (email/letter/interview/portal/phone); the date defaults to the decision date when left blank. The RPL/CT register gains a "Student Notified" column (Notified + date / Not notified / — while pending) so an auditor can see the decision-to-notification loop was closed. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (outcomecommunicated/…date/…method) via savepoint 2026073100422 (assessoruserid already existed). No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.421 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 2 (qualification total) + PHASE 4 (TAS volume of learning). (1) PHASE 2 — the Qualification Builder now rolls a real qualification nominal-hours total up from authoritative per-unit data. Because training.gov.au does NOT publish nominal hours, the builder previously showed a 0 total for most qualifications; it now batch-resolves any unit still at 0 from the plugin''s own reference table (local_rtocompliance_nominalhours, for the RTO''s reporting jurisdiction with NAT fallback) via a new batch mode on nominalhours_lookup.php (?codes=CODE1,CODE2,...), fills each unit, and repaints the "Nominal Hours — N hrs total" compliance card (which now also flags how many units are still missing hours so the admin knows to import the NCVER dataset or enter them). Resolution runs on page load, after a TGA load, and whenever a unit is added. (2) PHASE 4 — the TAS "Total Nominal Hours" (which drives the AQF volume-of-learning justification, Std 1.1/1.2) is now pre-filled from the qualification''s authoritative total via new helper local_rtocompliance_qual_nominal_total() (Qual Builder product total → live unit sum → per-unit reference-table sum). It only fills a genuinely empty value (a figure the RTO already entered is preserved), also seeds an empty Volume of Learning as a defensible lower bound, and the AI delivery-plan generator now uses this authoritative total as its fallback instead of a units×hrs/week guess when TGA returns none. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100421. — prior v5.9.420 DECLUTTER PASS 2 — remove duplicated / no-compliance-purpose UI noise. (1) STUDENT RESULTS — the eight summary stat tiles are reduced to the four that carry meaning; the removed four (Units in Product, Core Units, Elective Units, Total Unit Enrolments) were static structural reference counts that duplicated the qualification structure already listed below and only crowded the results command view. (2) DATA IMPORT — the "No Moodle accounts or enrolments are created" assurance was printed three times on the import screen (Step 1 card, Step 2 card, and the authoritative alert beneath the steps); the two card repetitions are removed and the single, more complete "No Moodle changes" alert is kept. (3) MARKETING INFORMATION — removed the "Related pages" cross-link card (every destination already lives in the left sidebar, so it was pure navigation duplication). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100420. — prior v5.9.419 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 + RPL CT-GATE HARDENING + SUPPORT PERSISTENCE + DECLUTTER. (1) NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 — when an enrolment is saved with AVETMISS scheduled hours left blank, they now default from the unit''s authoritative nominal hours (local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours), so NAT00120 reports a sensible value without manual entry; RPL (51) and Credit Transfer (60) default to 0 (no delivery). A value the admin actually typed is never overwritten. (2) RPL CREDIT-TRANSFER GATE HARDENED (Standard 1.7) — a CT outcome (60) is now posted to the results register only when BOTH an authenticated source (a verified USI transcript OR an uploaded source certificate/transcript on the record) AND the source qualification code are present; previously only the self-attested "USI transcript verified" checkbox was required, with no source document or code enforced. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT NOW PERSISTS SERVER-SIDE — the organisation-level support/adjustment/wellbeing selections were saved only in the browser (localStorage), so they were device-specific and invisible to an auditor on another machine (a Std 2.1/2.3 evidence gap); they now save to plugin config via a sesskey-guarded handler and load from the server. (4) DECLUTTER — the Students page''s auto-opening full-screen "USI not configured" modal (popped on every load, blocking the roster, duplicating the dashboard CTA) is replaced by an inline banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100419. (Continuing: nominal hours Phase 2 qual-total sum, RPL assessor-identity + outcome-communicated, declutter passes 2-3, and the pre-enrolment integration gate.) — prior v5.9.418 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 1. The Qualification Builder nominal-hours autofill previously called a private lms-labs.com endpoint. It now owns the data: a new reference table local_rtocompliance_nominalhours holds authoritative nominal hours per unit code per jurisdiction (NAT = the free NCVER nationally-agreed set as the national baseline, plus optional VIC/QLD/NSW/SA/WA/TAS/NT/ACT overrides). New internal endpoint nominalhours_lookup.php resolves a unit's hours from that table for the RTO's configured reporting jurisdiction (setting: Nominal hours — reporting jurisdiction) with NAT fallback, and the qualbuilder autofill JS now calls THIS endpoint instead of lms-labs.com. New admin import page (Import Nominal Hours) ingests the NCVER tab-delimited file (auto-detects tab/comma, skips header/non-code rows, upserts one value per unit per state) so the table can be bulk-populated; helper local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours()/upsert_nominalhours() added. Schema: new table (install.xml + upgrade savepoint 2026073100418). This is Phase 1 (authoritative source + internal lookup, removing the external dependency); Phase 2 (sum to qualification total), Phase 3 (default enrolment scheduled hours → NAT00120, 0 for RPL/CT) and Phase 4 (TAS amount-of-training) follow. Savepoint 2026073100418. — prior v5.9.417 DECLUTTER PASS 1. Removes duplicated/no-purpose UI noise so pages stay focused on compliance work. DASHBOARD: removed the static "Get Started Guide" 7-card row (it mirrored the live Setup Progress tracker exactly — same 7 steps/order/destinations); removed the "Quick Access" cards (all three destinations are in the sidebar and their stat lines just repeated the Overview tiles); removed the two full-width cross-link banners (Practice Guides + Compliance Map — both already in the sidebar). CERTIFICATES: removed the "Certificate Compliance — Clauses 9–14" explainer banner that restated the legislation above the register on every visit (the clause content lives on the ASQA Compliance Mapping page and Support centre; the actual compliance gates are unchanged). QUAL CERT HUB: removed the multi-paragraph "What is this / How to use it" tutorial card (incl. cache jargon), replaced with a one-line intro — the funnel columns and row actions are self-explanatory. This is pass 1 of a larger simplification program (audit produced a top-20 removal list); remaining declutter, plus nominal-hours Phase 1 and the RPL best-practice enhancements, follow in subsequent builds. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100417. — prior v5.9.416 PREMIUM DESIGN SYSTEM + RPL/CT EXPERT AUDIT-BLOCKING FIXES. (A) PREMIUM UI PASS — a design-system audit found the token layer had been rebuilt three times with conflicting values (primary colour, shadows, two neutral ramps), two competing badge systems, WCAG-AA contrast failures on solid info/success badges, oversized 16px/44px buttons with a gradient overridden to flat, and a .info-card.warning that rendered BLUE instead of amber. A single canonical design system is now appended to styles.css (scoped, reversible): one token set (re-points every legacy --rtoc-* var), a clean button scale (14px text, 8px radius, quiet outline/secondary, one focus-visible ring), one AA-safe soft-chip badge system, consistent card radius/shadow + tasteful hover lift, the amber warning-card fix, a global premium table-hover fallback, and empty/skeleton state utilities. PURGE CACHES after install to see it. (B) RPL/CREDIT-TRANSFER expert review — fixed the audit-blocking gaps: (1) REVERSAL RETRACTION — changing a previously-approved RPL/CT to Not Approved / Pending now retracts the posted competency (deletes the RPL-created enrolments row, or reverts an updated delivery row to 70) so a reversed decision can no longer leave a competent unit over-reporting into completion, certificates and NAT; (2) RPL DELIVERY MODE on the update path now reports mode 90 (not applicable) like the insert path — previously an RPL granted over an existing delivery enrolment kept classroom mode 10 and its delivered hours; (3) PRIVACY ERASURE — a right-to-erasure request now deletes the student's RPL evidence and credit-transfer source-certificate FILES (system-context fileareas keyed by rpl id), which were previously left in storage; the file subsystem is now declared in the privacy metadata. Also: RPL required-field enforcement (student + decision reason) from v5.9.415 retained. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100416. (Nominal hours: an expert research pass produced a phased wiring plan — import the NCVER nationally-agreed nominal-hours dataset into a per-unit/per-state reference table, repoint the qualbuilder autofill off lms-labs.com to an internal lookup, sum to the qual total, default enrolment scheduledhours from it (0 for RPL/CT), and feed the TAS amount-of-training — staged for approval, not in this build.) — prior v5.9.415 FULL-MENU AUDIT — HIGH/MEDIUM REMEDIATION BATCH. Follows the v5.9.414 blocker fixes. (1) TRAINER EVIDENCE now persists — trainer_currency.php and trainer_voccomp.php read the uploaded evidence file from the transient draft area but never called file_save_draft_area_files(), so files vanished on Moodle's draft cleanup and the stored id pointed at nothing; both now persist into permanent pluginfile-served fileareas (trainer_evidence / trainer_voccomp_evidence, separate areas so record ids can't collide) keyed by the record id. SCHEMA PARITY: the vocationalevidence column existed only in db/upgrade.php, so fresh installs lacked it and Trainers-page saves failed — it is now in db/install.xml too. (2) PROFILE WRITE-AUTH — student_profile.php allowed SAVING another student's record with only the read capability (viewall); saving now requires the manage (write) capability, editing your own profile still allowed. (3) SUPPORT DIAGNOSTICS REMOVED — support.php ran a v5.9.50 breadcrumb block on every Help-page load that wrote a /tmp file, spammed error_log, registered a shutdown handler and wrote the Moodle config table four times; removed entirely. (4) MANAGER DEAD-END — the fee-protection page linked managers to a site-config-only settings section (access denied); the link now only shows to users who can open it, with a note otherwise. (5) THIRD-PARTY — corrected the factually wrong "notify ASQA at least 30 days before entering a third-party arrangement" banner to the actual 2025 requirement (written agreement + retained quality oversight; NRT-logo / AQF-issuance prohibitions; student transparency). (6) QI COMPLETION RATE — qi_report.php computed the competency completion rate across mismatched cohorts (start-date denominator vs end-date numerator) and counted non-competent codes (52 RPL-not-granted, 70 continuing, etc.) as completions; it is now "of units that reached a FINAL outcome this year, the fraction that were competent (20/51/60/81)". (7) ASQA CLAUSE CONSISTENCY — the Risk page labelled risk management "Standard 4.3" while the authoritative ASQA Compliance Mapping and Support Centre use 4.2; the Risk page now says 4.2. (8) FEE-PROTECTION register now includes 'approaching threshold' students (>$1,200), which the previous >$1,500-only query excluded. No schema changes beyond adding the missing vocationalevidence column to install.xml (parity only). Savepoint 2026073100415. (Remaining catalogued for follow-up: student_support server persistence, viewsensitive gating, non-portable LIMIT in a few queries, RPL required-field enforcement, dashboard alert icons, and the USI local-verification client which is a separate staged project.) — prior v5.9.414 FULL-MENU AUDIT — 4 BLOCKERS FIXED. A deep 7-part investigation of every left-hand-menu section found four blocker-class defects, all now fixed: (1) CERTIFICATE INTEGRITY — the Student Results drill-down and the results-page cert-issuance guard (qualbuilder_results.php + ajax.php) counted AVETMISS outcomes 30 (competency not achieved/fail) and 40 (withdrawn) as "complete", so a student who failed or withdrew from every unit showed 100% progress with a working "Issue Certificate" button, and the server guard let the testamur/record issue. All six checks now use the competent-only set (20/51/60/81), so only genuinely-competent students count as complete and can be issued a qualification certificate. (2) SoA GATE BYPASS — the Multi-Unit Statement of Attainment issuer (soa_ajax.php) inserted the certificate directly, skipping the USI verified-gate, the RTO-settings gate and the as-issued snapshots that local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert() enforces; an SoA could be issued to a student with no / unverified USI. It now enforces the USI-verified gate (Clause 12) and RTO-identity gate BEFORE consuming credits, snapshots the verified USI + RTO identity onto the cert, and publishes to the verification registry. (3) NO-CORE-WRITES — three data-import actions (repairnames edits {user} name/email; backfill_records set {user}.idnumber; hide_archive_cats toggled {course_categories}.visible) still wrote to Moodle core and were reachable; they are now in the retired-action block list, so the plugin only READS Moodle and writes solely to its own tables with no reachable exception. (4) GOVERNANCE — governance_edit.php ignored the type=changes/adc parameter and always read/wrote the govpersons table, so Material Changes and the Annual Declaration of Compliance could never be created and editing one threw a fatal MUST_EXIST; the editor now has full forms for the materialchanges and adc tables. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100414. (Remaining HIGH/MEDIUM findings from the audit — trainer evidence-file persistence, student_support localStorage-only, viewsensitive USI gating, ASQA clause-number consistency, and others — are catalogued for follow-up builds.) — prior v5.9.413 USI SETUP-STATUS UNIFIED. The dashboard (index.php) judged USI setup from the LEGACY local-file config keys (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id), while the dedicated Machine Credential Setup page (usi_settings.php) judged it from the per-tenant PLATFORM status. So a SaaS RTO whose USI machine credential is stored on the platform (the recommended method) was shown a "USI verification is not yet set up" banner on the dashboard even though the setup page correctly reported "configured and ready" — it looked like the configuration had reset. New single source of truth local_rtocompliance_usi_is_configured() recognises BOTH supported methods: (a) per-tenant platform (apiurl + siteid + apikey set AND a credential uploaded/confirmed via the usi_cert_uploaded flag or a platform-pushed usi_certificate_path), and (b) legacy local-file (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id). The dashboard now uses it, so the banner only shows when USI genuinely is not configured by either method. Nothing about the USI credentials themselves was changed or reset — this was purely an inconsistent status check. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100413. — prior v5.9.412 EDITOR NOW INCORPORATES EVERY RTO-CONFIGURED VALUE (certificate code + phrases + descriptors). Extends the v5.9.409 real-identity map so the certificate editor canvas reflects ALL fixed, RTO-configured values from RTO/Certificate Settings — not just RTO name/code/signatory. Added: the CERTIFICATE CODE preview (cert.number) built from the RTO''s real certprefix + type code + year exactly as local_rtocompliance_generate_cert_number() does (e.g. CBF-SOA-2026-0001) instead of the generic CERT-2026-000123; the certificate footer (cert.footer); every ASQA mandatory phrase (aqf_statement, certify/attained statements, SoA intro/attained statements, Statement-of-Attainment and Record-of-Results headings, the NOT-A-TESTAMUR statement) using the RTO''s configured wording and falling back to the ASQA default when unset; and the optional descriptors (industry descriptor, occupational stream, apprenticeship statement, language statement, skill-set statement) which show the real configured value or fall through to the catalogue placeholder when blank. These paint on the canvas regardless of the "Show sample data" toggle because they are fixed RTO values, not per-student data (student name, units, dates and the QR code are deliberately left as sample/dynamic). Confirmed all six branding IMAGE fields (RTO logo, NRT logo, AQF logo, compliance/state logo, organisation seal, signatory signature) were already painting from the uploaded files via the v5.9.406–409 getter + pluginfile-serving fixes. No settings/config keys changed; no schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100412. — prior v5.9.411 NO-CORE-WRITES ON CERT GENERATION (C-P2-6) + NAT CONTINUING-OUTCOME FIX (A-P2-3). (1) NO-CORE-WRITES — certificate generation no longer toggles the core {user}.suspended field. The three issuance paths (generate_course_certs.php, generate_qual_certs.php, qual_cert_hub.php) each ran $DB->set_field(''user'',''suspended'',0,...) when an admin ticked an "Activate account" checkbox during generation, coupling Moodle account activation to certificate issuance and writing to a core table. Those writes AND their checkboxes/columns are removed; suspended students are still shown (badged, read-only) and can still be issued certificates — activating an account is now left as an explicit decision in Moodle user administration. (The explicit admin "activate" action on the Students page and the rollback-suspend in data_import remain, as those are deliberate user-initiated actions, not side-effects of issuing a certificate.) (2) A-P2-3 NAT FIX — when the AVETMISS NAT00120 export coerces a blank/''00'' outcome to ''70'' (Continuing activity), it now also reports the record as OPEN (activity end date = reporting period end) instead of emitting ''70'' together with a recorded completion end date, which is internally inconsistent and NCVER flags. The AVETMISS Validation page still surfaces these records so the RTO enters the real outcome. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100411. — prior v5.9.410 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER EVIDENCE UPLOADS + RESULTS/CERT TIE-IN CHECK. (1) FILE UPLOADS — the RPL & Credit Transfer record form now has real file uploads: a "Source certificate / transcript (from the issuing RTO)" uploader on credit-transfer records (attach the other RTO''s testamur / SoA / RoR / USI transcript that authenticates the transfer) and an "RPL evidence files" uploader on RPL records (portfolio, references, prior quals, observation records). Both accept multiple files (PDF/image/Office/text, 20MB each), list already-uploaded files with download + remove links, are stored in the Moodle File API keyed by the record id, served through local_rtocompliance_pluginfile (new fileareas rpl_evidence + ct_sourcecert, manage capability), and cleaned up when the record is deleted. Each uploader carries plain-English ASQA instructions (Standard 1.6 for RPL, Clause 1.7 / Clause 12 for credit transfer). The old free-text "Evidence Files" box is retained as optional notes for evidence held outside the system. (2) TIE-IN VERIFICATION — deep-audited that RPL (outcome 51) and Credit Transfer (outcome 60), written to the results register by local_rtocompliance_apply_rpl_outcome(), are treated as COMPETENT across every relevant path: Student Results (student_profile.php, qualbuilder_results.php), qualification-completion detection (check_full_qual_completion, get_completed_units_for_qual, process_enrolment_task, observer, completion_reconciler, certificate_validator) and ALL certificate paths (generate_qual_certs, qual_cert_hub, generate_course_certs, and the renderer which labels 51=RPL Granted / 60=Credit Transfer on the SoA/RoR). Fixed the one gap the audit found: the Students dashboard "Competency Achieved (Units)" card counted only outcome 20 — it now counts 20/51/60/81 so RPL/CT units are included. Also corrected the scrambled outcomeidentifier help text to the accurate NCVER code meanings. No schema changes (files use the Moodle File API; the rpl table already had studentid/rpltype/usitranscriptverified). Savepoint 2026073100410. — prior v5.9.409 EDITOR BRANDING NOW ACTUALLY RENDERS (real root cause). The certificate editor paints the RTO logo / NRT logo / CEO signature / organisation seal in the canvas as <img src="pluginfile…"> URLs, but local_rtocompliance_pluginfile() only served three fileareas (cert_template_bg, cert_template_image, rto_branding). The assets uploaded via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings live in admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas (logo, nrt_logo_file, aqf_logo_file, organisation_seal_file, compliance_logo_1/2, ceo_signature_file, secondary_logo, cert_background_file) — NONE of which the handler served — so every branding image request 404'd and the canvas showed an empty box, even though the issued PDF rendered the logos fine (the PDF reads the file straight off disk, bypassing pluginfile entirely). The pluginfile handler now serves those branding fileareas (system context, managecerttemplates capability), so the editor canvas finally matches the issued certificate. This is the missing piece behind the v5.9.406 getter fix: the getters resolved the correct file and produced a URL, but that URL was not servable until now. (2) EDITOR SHOWS REAL RTO IDENTITY — the canvas now always paints the RTO's own configured values for rto.name, rto.code, signatory.name, signatory.title and aqf_statement (independent of the "Show sample data" toggle), because these are fixed RTO-identity values, not per-student sample data. Previously the canvas showed the generic catalogue placeholder ("National Compliance Training / 50918") whenever sample data was off, which read as "the editor isn't pulling RTO settings" even though issued certificates were always correct. Verified the issued-certificate payload (resolve_payload) sources every field correctly: rto.name/rto.code/signatory/aqf_statement from the issue-time snapshot then live config; student name/USI, qualification code/name, dates and cert number from the cert + student records; mandatory phrases from config with ASQA defaults. Purge all caches after install. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100409. — prior v5.9.408 TEMPLATE DELETE + DEACTIVATE CONTROLS. Adds two admin controls to the Certificate Templates list so a template can be cleared out and regenerated without digging through statuses: (1) DELETE — a Delete button now appears on EVERY template row regardless of status (including the active one), backed by a new force_delete() path + 'forcedelete' action (the audit-safe delete() that only removed drafts/archived is kept for programmatic callers). Deleting the active template is safe: issuance and preview fall back to the built-in ASQA starter until a new template is activated. Uploaded background/per-field-image files are cleaned up. Confirm prompt is extra-strong (and states the active-template fallback) since it is permanent. (2) MAKE NON-ACTIVE — a new deactivate() method + 'deactivate' action + "Make non-active" button shown on the currently active template, which clears the active flag WITHOUT archiving (the template stays approved and one-click re-activatable). New lang strings: cert_template_deactivate_btn, cert_template_confirm_deactivate, cert_template_action_ok_deactivated. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100408. — prior v5.9.407 SANITISE EXISTING SAVED CERT TEMPLATES (retro-fix for already-saved templates). v5.9.406 fixed the STARTER (new templates) and the RENDER path, but a template already saved in the database kept its old fields — so an existing Statement of Attainment still showed the duplicate/overlapping "form part of" + "completion of course" statements AND still carried the "Verify at: <url>" text field. A new upgrade step (savepoint 2026073100407) now rewrites every saved cert-template design to match a fresh starter: it drops every qualification.completionofcoursestatement field (redundant — the single "form part of" line is the ASQA statement), drops every authenticity_measure text field (QR-only default; the mandatory QR code stays and satisfies the authenticity requirement), and widens the surviving "form part of" box for a clean two-line wrap. Fully guarded (a bad design row is skipped, an unchanged design is left untouched); RTOs can drag the "Authenticity measure" field back on if they want the URL text. This is what makes an ALREADY-SAVED template pick up the QR-only + single-statement fixes without a manual "Reset to starter". IMPORTANT after install: run Site administration → Development → Purge all caches (the editor JS and branding checks are cached). NOTE on branding: the editor now paints the real RTO logo / NRT logo / signature / seal from RTO Settings (v5.9.406 getter fix) — if a slot still shows a placeholder box after purging caches, that specific asset is not uploaded under Certificate Settings for that cert type. No schema changes (data-only design rewrite). Savepoint 2026073100407. — prior v5.9.406 CERTIFICATE EDITOR FIXES + QR-ONLY DEFAULT + CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT. (1) EDITOR BRANDING (critical) — the certificate editor showed "[RTO logo]" / "[NRT logo]" / "[CEO signature image]" / "[Org seal]" text placeholders instead of the real artwork whenever the RTO had uploaded those assets via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings, because the editor's branding-URL getters only looked in the FA_BRANDING pseudo-itemid area and never the admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas where the settings pages actually store them (the issued PDF found them via resolve_compliance_asset_path()'s fallback chain, so the canvas and the print diverged). New get_branding_display_url() mirrors the renderer's exact chain (FA_BRANDING → settings filearea → bundled pix) and now backs get_branding_logo/signature/sta/nrt/aqf/org_seal_url(); the editor host now also passes the NRT, AQF and STA logo URLs to the JS (previously only logo/signature/seal were), and the editor canvas paints nrt_logo/aqf_logo/state_training_authority_logo from them. (2) SoA COMPLIANCE STATEMENT — the Statement of Attainment starter carried BOTH "These competencies form part of {code} {name}" AND the near-identical "These competencies were attained in completion of {code} course in {name}", auto-built from the same qualification and stacked 5-7mm apart, so they overlapped into an unreadable block. The redundant "completion of course" statement (which is for accredited short courses, not qualifications) is removed from the default starter (still draggable from the palette), the single "form part of" statement box is widened for clean two-line wrap, and the descriptors are re-spaced; the renderer AND sample preview now also suppress the completion statement whenever the form-part-of line is present, so templates already saved with both fields render only the correct one. (3) QR-ONLY DEFAULT — the "Verify at: <url>" authenticity_measure text field is removed from all eight starter templates; the mandatory verification QR code (auto-added by ensure_mandatory_fields, and already accepted by the validator as a valid authenticity measure) is the default, and RTOs can drag the URL text back on if they want it. (4) CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT — editor font sizing now converts points→pixels with the correct 0.3528×BASE_SCALE factor (was a hardcoded 1.33 that rendered every field ~26% oversized vs the PDF, throwing off drag-to-fit); the two inline <script> emitters on the editor page use JSON_HEX_* flags so author-entered text can't break out; the disabled-path return of send_certificate_email() now uses the canonical ok/email/error shape its callers read (was success/reason, causing an undefined-key warning and a blank failure message); and revoking a certificate now calls update_registry_status(token,'revoked') so a revoked cert's public QR verifies as Revoked instead of Valid. Also bundles the pending verify.php superseded-cert fix and the Student Results Moodle-completion effective-outcome wiring from the working set. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100406. (1) The Student Profile results section is rebuilt into a proper command view: a per-qualification progress hero (X of Y units competent, progress bar, outcome-breakdown chips), unit results GROUPED BY QUALIFICATION with a new Source column (which Moodle course each result came from), friendly colour-coded outcome badges, an outcome legend, and consolidated action buttons — "Issue Statement of Attainment", "Issue Qualification Certificate" (pre-fills the hub with the student's USI), and "Record / edit results". (2) OUTCOME LABELS: the raw AVETMISS placeholder "00" (and blank/10) now displays as "Not yet assessed" on the Enrolments page and profile (it is NOT Competent or NYC — it means no result recorded yet). Verified every outcome label against NCVER's official "Reporting a final outcome" fact sheet: code 70 is correctly "Continuing activity" (corrected two internal spots that read "Continuing enrolment"); 40/41/61/85 confirmed correct. (3) DATES: the Enrolments page Activity Start Date (and the Moodle-enrolment list dates) now include the YEAR (they used Moodle's short date format which omits it). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100405. — prior v5.9.404 left-hand menu fix. several admin pages rendered without the plugin's left sidebar because they called $OUTPUT->header() but never local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header(). Fixed on Moodle Course Map (course_map.php — reported), AVETMISS Validation (nat_validate.php), NAT Reconciliation (reconcile.php — replaced its bare rtoc-main-content div with the full layout-wrap + sidebar), and the Over-Enrolment / Bulk Over-Enrolment / Skipped Program Codes diagnostic pages. A full sweep confirms every remaining page without the sidebar is an intentional public token page (certificate verification, survey response, student declaration, student LLN form), which correctly have no admin menu. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100404. — prior v5.9.403 button text padding. long-label buttons (e.g. the full-width "Sync results from Moodle completions" side-panel button) were clipping because the plugin's button style forced white-space:nowrap with a fixed single-line height, so a long label in a narrow button ran to the edges. Buttons now allow their text to WRAP with height:auto (padding honoured), and small buttons (.btn-sm) get comfortable padding + a slightly smaller font — a single stylesheet fix that applies to every button in the plugin's main content area. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100403. — prior v5.9.402 backlog close-out. (final audit P2/P3s): (1) CREDIT-TRANSFER SOURCE AUTHENTICATION (Std 1.7) — a credit-transfer decision no longer posts a competency to the register unless the USI transcript is verified; otherwise it warns and holds (RPL is unaffected). (2) PRIVACY — complaint/appeal records now capture the complainant/appellant Moodle user id (resolved from email) so privacy export & erasure include them. (3) WORKFORCE CREDENTIALS — corrected the assessor skill-set picklist (removed the invalid TAESS00021, added the real TAESS00011 Assessor Skill Set and TAESS00019 Enterprise Trainer Skill Set, relabelled TAESS00024) and synced the help text; added advisory reminders that a TAS should be reviewed when its training product is superseded, and that TAE-package assessments need independent validation before the first cohort. (4) LABEL CORRECTNESS — the SoA unit-outcome filter now uses the correct AVETMISS codes (Credit transfer = 60; 81/82 shown as non-assessable, not "superseded competent"), and the Statement-of-Attainment "requires" text lists the correct competent set (20/51/60/81). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100402. — prior v5.9.401 procedural fairness + sensitive-data permission. (audit P2s). COMPLAINTS (Std 2.7): new respondent, respondent-response, and date-outcome-communicated fields so the RTO can demonstrate the party complained about was heard and all parties were told the outcome. APPEALS (Std 2.8): new original-decision-maker + reviewer-independence-confirmed + underlying-record-corrected fields; the appeal edit page now warns (advisory) when an upheld assessment appeal has not had its underlying record corrected, or when independence has not been confirmed. SENSITIVE DATA: a new local/rtocompliance:viewsensitive capability (granted to managers by default) now gates the disability disclosure on the student profile — staff without it see "Restricted", while the student always sees their own and managers are unaffected. Schema savepoint 401 (complaints + appeals fields). — prior v5.9.400 help & support refresh. the Support Centre "What's New" panel (was stuck at v5.9.378), Get Started guide, feature/module cards and FAQ, plus the How It Works Key Questions, are updated to the current feature set — Compliance Health, AVETMISS Validation, ASQA Compliance Mapping, the world-class student profile, student certificate access (portal + nav link + dashboard block), automated weekly alerts, full NAT demographic + address propagation, the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, and the certificate-integrity + validation/workforce/QI hardening. Also corrected stale docs that described the retired auto-enrolment behaviour and the old "USI warning" as current (issuance is now a hard verified-USI block). Documentation only. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100400. — prior v5.9.399 automated compliance alerts. a new weekly scheduled task (compliance_alert_task, Mondays 07:00) emails site administrators a plain-English digest whenever key audit-readiness risks need attention — validations overdue, working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, students with results but an unverified USI (cert-blocked), certificates past the 30-day issuance rule, and incomplete AVETMISS profiles — with a one-click link to the Compliance Health page. Sends ONLY when something needs attention (no all-clear noise); fully guarded so a mail failure or missing table can never break cron; disable by setting config compliancealerts=0, and add an extra recipient via config alertemail. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100399. — prior v5.9.398 AVETMISS pre-submission validator. (the crown-jewel feature): a new read-only "AVETMISS Validation" page (nat_validate.php, in Data & Reporting) checks every reportable student and enrolment against NCVER/AVETMISS edit rules BEFORE the RTO exports NAT files — so a quarterly submission is not rejected. STUDENT checks: missing/invalid USI (+ unverified-USI warning), missing/invalid DOB, sex, postcode, state, country of birth, language, Indigenous status, labour force, school level, at-school flag; disability/prior-ed detail warnings. ENROLMENT checks: invalid/blank outcome code, a final outcome with no end date, missing start date, end-before-start, blank program/unit code; warnings for continuing-with-past-end-date, invalid delivery mode / funding source, and missing scheduled hours on a delivered unit. Findings are split ERROR (will fail NCVER) vs WARNING, grouped by category with a "Ready to submit / N errors to fix" verdict and a full CSV export. Fully read-only and defensively guarded. Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100398. — prior v5.9.397 Compliance Health command centre. a new flagship read-only page (compliance_health.php, first in the left menu) that answers "are we audit-ready right now?" at a glance. A hero audit-readiness score (percentage of key checks currently clear) with a verdict, over a responsive grid of Quality-Area cards surfacing live risk signals: validations overdue / due soon, qualifications never validated, incomplete AVETMISS profiles, open complaints & appeals (past timeframe), working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, QI survey response rate, open high-severity risks, and — critically — students with results but an UNVERIFIED USI (the certificates you cannot yet issue). Every metric has a status pill and a one-click "fix" link to the relevant page. Fully read-only and defensively guarded (every query wrapped; a missing table never breaks the page). Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100397. — prior v5.9.396 AVETMISS address propagation. the student's full street address (building/property name, flat-unit, street number+name, and postcode) is now parsed from NAT00085 — previously the parser dropped it — staged, and propagated into the student profile alongside the other demographics (both automatically on import for existing profiles, and via Backfill). New staging columns postcode/buildingname/unitno/streetname (savepoint 396); the students table already had the matching columns. The student profile summary now shows the complete address (building, unit/street, suburb, state, postcode) instead of just suburb+state. Savepoint 2026073100396. — prior v5.9.395 audit trail + portability. (1) the Complaints, Appeals and Continuous-Improvement registers now write an audit-log entry on every create/update/delete (previously these compliance records could be altered or deleted with no trail — an ASQA evidence gap); logging is wrapped defensively so it can never block the user action. (2) The NAT export replaced a MySQL/Postgres-only "LIMIT 1" with a portable limited query so it no longer risks failing on Oracle/MSSQL. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100395. — prior v5.9.394 world-class student profile. (1) The Student Records list now makes each student NAME a one-click link to their profile, and the row Actions menu gains Certificates + Results/Enrolments shortcuts. (2) student_profile.php now opens with a polished READ-ONLY summary above the edit form: a header card (name, client ID, USI + verification badge, completeness pill that lists missing fields ON LOAD), a demographics grid showing every AVETMISS field as a HUMAN LABEL (with a muted "Not stated" for placeholders), a unit-results table with colour-coded outcome badges, and an issued-certificates card with one-click PDF download — so an admin can review a student's whole picture in one place instead of a bare edit form. (3) Reissuing a certificate now preserves the original as-issued USI snapshot and RTO-identity snapshot (C-P2-1), so a faithful copy shows exactly what the original showed. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100394. — prior v5.9.393 student My Certificates nav link + dashboard block. students now get a persistent "My Certificates" link in the plugin navigation (local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation previously returned nothing for students, so their only link was buried on their Moodle profile page). The link points to the certificate portal (mycerts.php), which enforces its own access control so a student only ever sees their own certificates. A companion Dashboard block (block_rtocompliance_mycerts, delivered separately) shows a student their issued certificates with one-click download on login. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100393. — prior v5.9.392 removed Moodle account creation from Backfill. "Backfill Student Records" no longer creates Moodle {user} accounts (user_create_user removed). A NAT student with no existing Moodle account is now SKIPPED and reported ("no Moodle account — an administrator must create one first, then re-run Backfill"). Backfill now only READS Moodle users and writes the plugin's own student profile + demographics for students who already have an account. Combined with v5.9.387, the plugin creates/deletes NOTHING in Moodle core (no enrolments, no completions, and now no user accounts) — it only reads them. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100392. — prior v5.9.391 NAT demographic propagation regression fix. After a NAT import the AVETMISS demographic data now flows into the student profile again: (1) the finalize step now automatically refreshes the demographic fields (DOB, sex, suburb/state, Indigenous status, labour force, highest school level, language at home, country of birth, disability flag, prior-education flag, at-school flag) on EXISTING student profiles from the freshly-staged NAT00080 data — writing ONLY to the plugin students table (no Moodle user/enrolment/completion writes), so it is constraint-safe; a staged value only overwrites when it is real (never wipes good data with an AVETMISS "not stated" placeholder). This restores propagation that had lived inside the now-disabled auto-enrol handlers. (2) The manual "Backfill Student Records" step was silently dropping 8 core demographics to defaults because its staging SELECT omitted them — the SELECT now pulls all demographic columns, so a backfill writes the full profile. (3) Cert render-time backstop now also blocks the NRT logo on 'attendance' certs (matches the template catalogue's forbidden_for). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100391. — prior v5.9.390 cert-template polish F4/F5/F6. (F4) render-time compliance backstop — the renderer now drops any element forbidden for the cert type before it reaches the PDF (NRT logo never on a Record of Results or non-accredited Completion; USI never on a Testamur or Statement of Attainment), backing up the approval-time validation against pinned/override/legacy designs. (F5) certificate PREVIEW now applies the template's per-template designjson.overrides{} exactly as the real issue path does, so previews are faithful for override-using templates. (F6) the Test Certificate now uses its own dummy verify token and placeholder USI instead of an empty token + the logged-in admin's live USI. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100390. — prior v5.9.389 CERTIFICATE-TEMPLATE INTEGRITY (F1 as-issued RTO snapshot / F2 approved-only pinned template / F3 block issuance on blank RTO details). (F1) each certificate now snapshots the RTO identity settings (legal name, provider code, signatory name/title, AQF statement) at issue time into a new certs.issuesnapshot column and the renderer renders from that snapshot, so a later change to those settings cannot retroactively rewrite an already-issued certificate (mirrors the USI snapshot). (F2) pick_for_cert() renders the pinned template ONLY if it is still status='approved', so an in-progress/unvalidated draft edit can no longer leak onto an already-issued certificate on re-download (it falls back to the current approved template). (F3) issuance is now refused — interactively (non-bypassable) and programmatically — when mandatory RTO details (legal name, national provider code, authorised signatory) are not configured, preventing certificates that render those AQF-required fields blank; the "ready to issue" validator surfaces the same gap. Savepoint 2026073100389. — prior v5.9.388: ASQA PRACTICE-GUIDE AUDIT P1 REMEDIATION PART 2 + ASQA COMPLIANCE MAPPING. Feature code on the v5.9.387 schema: (1) VALIDATION (Std 1.5) — validator-independence declaration is required to complete a validation, and completion is blocked without it; a five-year validation cycle now computes/stores nextduedate (2 years for high-risk), with OVERDUE/DUE-SOON flags and a Coverage-Gaps list of on-scope products with no current validation; assessment outcome + rectification actions are captured. (2) WORKFORCE (Std 3.2) — "Working Towards" trainers now record a start date and an enforced 2-year TAE completion deadline; manager sign-off is blocked for a blank credential or a lapsed working-towards window; supervisors must hold a full, unexpired credential; a Supervision overdue/due-soon alert lists at-risk working-towards trainers. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT (Std 2.3/2.4/2.6) — per-student support / reasonable-adjustment / wellbeing records now persist server-side in local_rtocompliance_supportnotes (retained, shared, auditable) instead of browser localStorage. (4) QUALITY INDICATORS (Std 4.4) — the ad-hoc surveys are replaced with the official AQTF Learner & Employer Questionnaires (items tagged to their scales) and qi_report renders a proper QI Annual Summary (indicator + scale scores, response rates); the QI export is now the aggregate summary, not identifiable per-respondent rows. (5) NEW "ASQA Compliance Mapping" left-menu page (asqa_standards_map.php) — every 2025 Standard mapped to the feature that supports it with an honest Covered/Partial/Gap status (Std 4.3/4.4 self-assurance). No schema changes beyond savepoint 387. Savepoint 2026073100388.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.457'; // v5.9.457 PRIVACY: removed all client-specific content from the product + Semester Intake Builder redesign. (1) CONFIDENTIALITY — a provider's own qualification codes, category/qualification names and internal shorthands were previously hardcoded in the plugin (most seriously as the NAT importer's qualification-to-family and family-keyword maps in data_import.php, plus a family label map, and throughout code comments and UI examples). These have been moved to OPTIONAL per-RTO settings that ship EMPTY (Archive family map / keywords), the label is now derived generically from the family slug, and every remaining code/name/comment example has been replaced with neutral placeholders. No provider scope ships with the plugin anymore. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — restructured to match how Moodle is organised: results are grouped by Qualification (Moodle parent category), with each Version (sub-category) listed underneath and its Units of Competency (Moodle courses) alongside. Columns renamed to Qualification (Moodle Category) / Version (Sub Category) / Units of Competency (Moodle Courses), with a plain-language legend and per-column tooltips, and a per-qualification select-all. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400457. — prior v5.9.456 AI ASSISTANT — a beautiful, Claude-powered help assistant that sits bottom-right on every plugin page for staff. It is grounded on the plugin's OWN knowledge base, generated live from the per-page help registry, so it auto-updates every release with zero manual work and can answer how to do anything in the software (not canned steps). Questions route through the lms-labs.com platform (which holds the Claude key) and use ONE credit per question; the widget states this up front. A new RTO setting under Plugin Settings shows/hides the assistant and explains the 1-credit cost; an optional direct Anthropic API key + model are supported for self-hosted installs that bill Anthropic directly. New: assistant.php (JSON endpoint, login + capability + sesskey, per-user rate limit), js/rtoc_assistant.js (polished chat widget: gradient FAB, animated panel, message bubbles, suggested questions, typing indicator, safe markdown rendering, live credits chip), KB + call helpers in lib.php, and the before_footer hook injects the widget (CSP-safe: inline style + external script). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400456. — prior v5.9.455 USI VERIFY end-to-end hardening + practice-guide pill URL audit. (1) USI: traced the Students-page Verify USI button through student_usi_verify.php -> usi_verification_service -> usi_platform_client -> POST /api/usi/verify, and confirmed the lms-labs.com endpoint is live (returns 401 without site headers, as designed). Hardened the request/response to match the platform contract exactly: the verify call now sends the site ID + API key as headers AND in the body, sends student names/DOB under both conventions (firstname/firstName, lastname/lastName, dateofbirth/dob) so a field-name mismatch can't silently fail a match, and maps the platform's usiStatus/matchResult back to the status/message the Students page and verification log display. (2) Practice-guide pills: audited every URL — 11 now open the official ASQA PDF (stable /media permalinks for Integrity, Complaints/Appeals and Fit & Proper; current PDF paths for Assessment, RPL, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Trainer Competencies, Workforce Management, Risk Management and Continuous Improvement) and the remaining guides open the correct official ASQA page (no final standalone PDF exists for those yet); no pill can reach a dead link. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400455. — prior v5.9.454 CERT TEMPLATE SAVE — final belt-and-suspenders. The hidden design field on the certificate template editor is now SEEDED server-side with the current saved design instead of an empty string. The editor JS still overwrites it on load and on every edit, but if the JS ever fails to run (stale cache, a JS error, JS disabled) the form now posts a valid existing design rather than an empty payload — so a save can no longer fail with "malformed / did not reach the server", and no work is lost. Combined with v5.9.449/450 (never-throw serialiser, empty-payload submit guard, continuous field sync), the save path now has no single point of failure. Also ran a full self-check of the Auto-Create Qualifications + Semester Intake builders: lint clean, every inserted column verified against the schema, skip-existing + best-effort cleanup confirmed, plugin-tables-only writes. No schema changes. Purge caches after installing. Savepoint 2026080400454. — prior v5.9.453 USI page now READ-ONLY (credential-broker-only, cont.). The in-plugin "Upload Machine Credential" page (usi_settings.php) has had its upload form and POST handler removed — it is now a clean, read-only USI Verification Status page that shows the live status pulled from lms-labs.com and a note that the keystore + password are managed in the lms-labs.com admin panel (never in Moodle). No credential can be entered anywhere in the plugin now. Wording updated to match: the page title is "USI Verification Status", the legacy settings banner and the dashboard "USI not set up" call-to-action now point to the lms-labs.com admin panel and the status page instead of an upload form. Existing nav links, the dashboard CTA and the Students-page banner all still resolve (no broken links); USI readiness is judged from the platform status/ready flag. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400453. — prior v5.9.452 USI CREDENTIAL-BROKER-ONLY hardening. The myGovID machine credential (.p12 keystore) and its passphrase are now held ONLY on the lms-labs.com platform, which verifies USIs on this site's behalf via /api/usi/verify. Confirmed the Moodle plugin verifies exclusively through the platform client (the local SOAP registry client is unused dead code and the stored password was read by nothing), so the keystore is not needed on the Moodle server. Changes: (1) webhook.php no longer writes the credential locally — it drops usi_certificate_password from its allow-list and, instead of decoding usi_cert_base64 to a .p12 on disk, records a non-secret usi_cert_uploaded readiness flag; (2) the legacy usi_certificate_path and usi_certificate_password fields are REMOVED from RTO settings, replaced by a note that credentials are managed in the lms-labs.com admin panel; (3) usi_is_configured() now judges readiness from the platform connection plus the readiness flag, not a local keystore file; (4) a one-time upgrade purges any keystore/password an earlier push had planted on this server (unsets the config and deletes dataroot/local_rtocompliance/usi_credential.p12). USI verification is unaffected. Purge caches after installing. Savepoint 2026080400452. — prior v5.9.451 PRACTICE-GUIDE LINKS now open the OFFICIAL ASQA PDF. ASQA restructured their website, which broke the plugin's old practice-guide links (the "standard" pills on the help cards, e.g. the AQF issuance pill on the certificate pages). Each help-card guide pill now resolves to the official final ASQA practice-guide PDF and opens it in a new tab (the browser's PDF viewer), so clicking shows the actual document instead of a dead link. URLs were researched Aug 2026: stable asqa.gov.au/media/<id> permalinks are used where ASQA publishes them (Integrity of Nationally Recognised Training Products, Feedback/Complaints/Appeals, Fit and Proper Person), with current dated PDF paths for Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Risk Management and Continuous Improvement. Three guides with no confirmed standalone final PDF fall back to the current stable ASQA practice-guides pages so no link is ever broken. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400451. — prior v5.9.450 BUTTON HOVER CONTRAST audit + save-payload robustness. (1) CONTRAST — every Bootstrap button variant used in the plugin now has an explicit, readable hover so no button renders light text on a light background. The reported case was the outline buttons on the Certificate Templates action column (Edit / Preview / Make default): those sit OUTSIDE the .rtoc-main-content container, so the plugin's scoped hover rules did not reach them and Bootstrap's default white-on-light-amber (btn-outline-warning) showed through. New broadly-scoped rules cover warning, danger, info, light, dark and every outline form (warning/info/success), plus a safety net for outline-primary/secondary outside the main container. (2) SAVE — the hidden design field is now kept continuously in sync on every edit (not only on the submit event), so the layout payload can never be empty at submit time even if a stale cached build is momentarily active; the server message is clearer too. IMPORTANT: purge caches after installing so the new JavaScript is served. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400450. — prior v5.9.449 CERT EDITOR SAVE FIX + LAYOUT RULES across ALL certificate types. (1) MALFORMED DESIGN PAYLOAD on Save draft is fixed: when the browser could not serialise the layout it silently posted an empty field and the server rejected it as "malformed design payload". The editor now serialises with a never-throwing, circular-safe pass and refuses to post an empty/invalid payload (clear message instead), and the server message now distinguishes an empty payload from invalid JSON and reassures that the saved copy is untouched. (2) LAYOUT RULES applied to every cert type, for both new starters and existing saved templates (via the shared normaliser the renderer and editor both run, so the PDF and canvas stay in sync — no DB migration, no divergence): the small DATE and AUTHORISED PERSON caption labels are removed (the issue date and signatory name/title still print); the NRT logo, organisation seal and verification QR now render 30mm tall with aspect preserved and centred inside their box (never stretched). (3) UNITS TABLE: all text is a minimum of 12pt including the table; the unit code column is widened to hold a 12pt code on one line; long unit titles now WRAP onto a second line instead of shrinking. Canvas preview updated to match. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400449. — prior v5.9.448 AUTO-CREATE / ARCHIVE-VERSIONS CLARITY + name cleanup. (1) The Auto-Create Qualifications page builds ONE product per national qualification code, so every semester/archive copy of a qualification (S1 26, S2 26, S1 27 ...) collapses into that single code — which is why only one row per code appears and it skips once a product already exists. A prominent callout (and button) now routes admins to the Semester Intake Builder, which lists every semester/archive sub-category as its own Draft product with its exact course list, reading the qualification code and title from the parent category. This closes the main point of confusion about where the archive versions are built. (2) NAME CLEANUP — when a Moodle category named the code inside brackets, e.g. "Diploma of Customs Broking (TLI50816)", stripping the code left an empty "()" so detected names printed as "Diploma of Customs Broking ()". The code extractor now removes any now-empty bracket pair and collapses the doubled space, fixing detected names on Auto-Create, the Semester Intake Builder and everywhere category names are resolved. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400448. — prior v5.9.447 STYLE A UNITS TABLE for the Statement of Attainment and Record of Results. The unit list on both certificates now renders as one shaded three-column table — Unit Code (left) | Unit Title (left-aligned) | Completion Date (centre) — with a coloured header bar (white bold headings), zebra-striped alternating rows and thin cell borders, drawn in TCPDF (solid fills and borders, no gradients). A new Certificate Setting, "Units table header colour" (colour picker), sets the header-bar fill and defaults to the Moodle site primary / brand colour; header text prints white for contrast. The per-unit Completion Date is wired from the compliance register (the unit result / activity end date, falling back to the start date), captured at issue time and back-filled from the register for older certificates in a single query. Both cert types share one renderer: the RoR ror_table field and the SoA dynamic qualification.units field both route to it, so existing templates pick up the new table with no template edits. The in-editor canvas preview was updated to draw the identical shaded table (header colour, columns and zebra) so what you design matches the issued PDF. All certificate text now has a 12pt minimum floor for readability (previously many fields rendered at 9 to 10pt); the field height cap still contains anything that would otherwise overflow. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400447. — prior v5.9.446 CODE-FIRST / NO-DASH CONVENTION for unit & qualification labels. Everywhere a unit or qualification code and its title were shown together they now render as "CODE Title" — code first, title second, a single space between, no hyphen or em-dash. Fixed in the certificate renderer (the Statement of Attainment / Record of Results unit lists and their sample previews) and across the plugin UI (qualification dropdowns on Student Results and Generate Certificates, the My Certificates and public verify pages, Qual Builder delete confirmations + audit log, unit delete confirmation, RPL unit label, skipped-programcodes list, TAS heading + PDF/DOCX exports, suitability PDF). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100446. — prior v5.9.445 CSS SCOPING FIX (help card lost styling on admin pages) + SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER now reads the qualification from the PARENT category. (1) CSS — the plugin's help card and other scoped styles are scoped to the body class "path-local-rtocompliance". Pages that use admin_externalpage_setup() have their pagetype (and therefore the auto-generated "path-*" body class) overridden to an "admin-*" value, so that class was absent and every scoped rule silently failed (the sidebar still styled because its CSS is unscoped). Certificate Templates was the reported case; the same latent gap affected 12 admin pages in total — cert_templates, cert_template_edit, cert_test, nat_validate, nominalhours_import, reconcile, trainer_dashboard, usi_settings, foe_audit, foe_bulk_audit, recovery_analyzer, regression_test — each now calls $PAGE->add_body_class('path-local-rtocompliance') before output so the scoped CSS applies (the four remaining admin_externalpage files — qi_export, tas_export, settings, version — are file exports/config, not rendered pages). Purge caches after install. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — the qualification code and title are now read deterministically from the semester sub-category's PARENT category (parent = qualification code + title, the sub-category = the semester), not guessed from the unit set; the exact list of unit-code courses under the sub-category becomes the intake's units/courses. Where a semester has no coded parent the code box is left blank for the admin to set once. The preview shows the parent-derived qualification title beside each code box. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100445. — prior v5.9.444 SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — a separate qualification product per semester intake. New tool (qualbuilder_semester.php) + helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_semester_intakes() / local_rtocompliance_create_semester_intakes(). It scans every Moodle category that holds unit-code courses (e.g. "Archive - 23 DCB S1"), treating each as a semester intake: the category name becomes the product streamname, the unit codes parsed from the course names become its units, and those courses are linked (extra copies as archive variants). Because the archive category names carry a semester but NOT a qualification code, the code is AUTO-SUGGESTED by matching the intake's unit set to existing products (best overlap, with a version-letter-stripped fallback) and is editable per row so the admin sets it once per qualification era where it can't be inferred. A preview lists every detected intake with its semester, unit/course counts, detected unit codes and the suggested code; on confirm it creates one Draft product per ticked intake (qualcode + streamname). Duplicates (same qualcode + streamname) are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin's own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — no Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments are created or changed. Linked from the Qualification Builder header alongside Auto-Create and Recover Unmapped Completions. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100444. — prior v5.9.443 AUTO-CREATE — COURSE MAP IS NOW THE DEFAULT SOURCE + bigger info-box text. The "From Category Tree" scan returned nothing on this site because units here are delivered as COURSES (e.g. "TLIR4001 & TLIR4002 … MSP") under semester/archive categories, not as unit-code sub-categories — so the tree-walk found no unit layer. The Course Map already captures course → qual → unit correctly (seeded from those same categories and courses), so Auto-Create now defaults to the "From Course Map" source and the instructions say so; the Category-Tree tab is kept but explained as only for sites whose units are named sub-categories. Also: the page info boxes ("How this works" / "What this does") were too small — bumped to 15px (and the shared .rtoc-dob-sync-bar base font raised), and the empty-state on the Course Map source now points to Scan & Seed if the map is empty. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100443. — prior v5.9.442 CERTIFICATE EDITOR — ROOT-CAUSE FIX (canvas vs issued-PDF data divergence) + RECOVER UNMAPPED COMPLETIONS TOOL. CERT EDITOR: the meta-root-cause of the recurring "wrong preview" complaints was that the drag-and-drop CANVAS and the issued-PDF renderer used DIFFERENT data sources — on default load the canvas painted each field its own hardcoded per-field catalogue placeholder (meta.sample) while every prior fix (RTO identity v5.9.409/412, statement dedupe v5.9.406/407) only ever touched the PDF renderer's sample_payload, which the canvas did not use. Fixes: (1) CANVAS-DATA-UNIFY — the editor JS resolver now renders the SAME coherent sample record the issued PDF uses (a key present in sample_payload wins, even when intentionally blank), so unrelated placeholders (a First-Aid skill-set line, a Business qualification, an "[insert language]" token) no longer stack on the canvas and the skill-set/optional statements that should be blank now are. (2) STALE AMD BUILD — amd/build/cert_template_editor.js was 37 lines behind source (missing the whole real-RTO-identity code path), so dev/debug sites served the old behaviour; both build artifacts (.js and .min.js) are regenerated from source. (3) RTO NAME PLACEHOLDER — the editor canvas AND the issued renderer now fall back to the real Moodle site name (the RTO's own name) when the RTO legal name has not been set in RTO Settings, instead of showing the catalogue placeholder "National Compliance Training" (canvas) or the generic "Training Organisation" (issued). Set your legal name in RTO Settings for the exact wording. (4) "[insert language]" — the sample-preview payload hardcoded the literal "[insert language]" fill-in token; it now reads the languagestatement setting (or blank), matching the issued path. (5) REQUIRED DOT — the red filled "!" circle on required palette fields read as an error; it is now a clear amber "Required" pill (it always meant "required for this certificate type", never an error). RECOVER TOOL: new "Recover Unmapped Completions" page (qualbuilder_recover.php) + helpers scan the completions the sync could not map, propose old→current unit-code mappings (version-letter drops auto-ticked; single-unit name matches flagged for review), and on confirm write them to the supersededunitmap setting so the next Sync credits them; codes with no current unit are listed separately (build the superseded qual first). Also: "Auto-Create from Categories" scans the category tree or the Course Map. Writes only plugin config/tables; no Moodle-core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100442. — prior v5.9.441 RELEASE-PIPELINE FIX — cleared the one failed check. qualbuilder_autocreate.php inline select-all script used anonymous JS closures written as the flagged no-space form; rewritten to the spaced closure form (and the one-line if given braces) so the coding-style scanner no longer reports a spacing finding in that file. Pure coding-style change to one inline script; no functional, behavioural or schema change. The 6 advisory warnings are pre-existing and unchanged (ALL-CAPS lang values such as ABN/ASQA on legacy strings, capability-check advisories on read-only report/editor pages, the audited unserialize-with-allowed-classes call in process_enrolment_task, and inline-comment/one-statement style notes across legacy files). Savepoint 2026073100441. — prior v5.9.440 PARKED ITEMS BUILT. (1) NAT IMPORT OUTCOME / RESULTS GRID — a register enrolment that exists but has no recorded AVETMISS outcome (blank / NULL / "00") now renders on Student Results as a clear "Not yet assessed" dash instead of a confusing "?"; blank outcomes are normalised at both the on-screen grid and the CSV export, and any present-but-unrecognised code now shows as itself rather than "?". The NAT results importer VALID_OUTCOMES set gained "41" (incomplete — RTO closure), a valid AVETMISS code the parser accepts and the grid can display that was previously collapsed to "00". (2) MISSING-AVETMISS-DATA STUDENT PROMPT — a logged-in student whose AVETMISS profile is incomplete now sees a modal (site-wide, once per browser session) listing the fields still needed, with a "Complete my details now" button to their self-service profile and a tip that certificates can be downloaded from the profile menu (top-right initials). It reads only the student own row (one lookup by userid), is never shown to admins/guests or on the profile page itself, and is injected via the existing before_footer hook using an external CSP-safe script (js/avetmiss_prompt.js) so no inline script is blocked; the primary button is a plain link so the profile is always reachable. (3) HELP-CARD TEXT SIZE — the What / Why / How / Key-Features card body was enlarged from 14px to 15.5px (tabs 13px to 14px) for readability. (4) audit.php gained first-time How-to steps — the one page missed in the v5.9.438 rewrite — so help-step coverage is now complete. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100440. — prior v5.9.439 AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" NOW RESOLVES REAL NAMES (no more code-as-name). The v5.9.438 Course-Map source stored the unit code as the unit name because the course_map table holds only codes. Fixed: local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() now builds a CODE→name map from your Moodle category names (every category whose name carries a code — qualification categories like "TLI50321 — Diploma of …" and unit leaf categories like "TLIX0036 — Load and unload goods" — contributes its title, longest-name-wins; unit/qual titles are national so one map is safe) and uses it for BOTH the qualification name and each unit name. So building from the Course Map now produces the same real qualification and unit titles as the Category-Tree source, fully offline — reusing the category-name resolution instead of defaulting to the code. The training.gov.au enrichment option still overrides with official TGA names/packaging when ticked. Structure still comes from your existing, confirmed course_map rows; only the naming was reused rather than reinvented. Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100439. — prior v5.9.438 HELP-STEP REWRITE COMPLETED (ALL PAGES) + AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" SOURCE. (1) The v5.9.437 "How to use it" rewrite was extended from 40 to ~90 pages — every remaining left-menu page, editor and sub-page now shows the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence naming its real on-screen controls (cert issue/email/generate, template editor, TAS editor/consultation, transitions, trainer dashboard/voccomp, validation & validator editors, student support/declaration, fee/insurance/third-party/governance/risk editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, marketing, surveys/QI/AI reports, reconcile, deadlines, alerts, audit log, ASQA/compliance maps, practice guides, student portal pages, and more). All applied via the same per-page 'how' override, leaving What/Why/Key Features untouched. (2) AUTO-CREATE now offers a SOURCE toggle — "From Category Tree" or "From Course Map". The new read-only helper local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() groups your existing (and already-confirmed) Course Map rows by qualification code, links each unit's delivery courses, and reads the qualification name from its Moodle category — so you can build products straight from the mapping you already have (unit names default to the code unless training.gov.au enrichment is ticked). Same safety guarantees: Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle categories/courses/accounts/enrolments touched. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100438. — prior v5.9.437 AUTO-CREATE QUALIFICATIONS + FIRST-TIME HELP-STEP REWRITE. (1) AUTO-CREATE — new "Auto-Create from Categories" tool in the Qualification Builder (qualbuilder_autocreate.php) scans the Moodle category tree (parent category = qualification code + title, leaf sub-category = unit code + name, delivery courses underneath) and builds Qual Builder products with their units and course links in one pass. It shows a READ-ONLY preview (qual code, name, units found, courses linked, New vs Already-exists) with per-qual checkboxes and an optional best-effort training.gov.au enrichment (official name, packaging counts, AQF level, core/elective type, per-unit names) that falls back to the category names when the platform API is unavailable. New helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_categories_for_quals() (read-only) and local_rtocompliance_autocreate_quals_from_scan(). Products are created as Draft; duplicate qual codes are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — it never creates or changes Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments. (2) HELP CARDS — the "How to use it" tab on 40 primary pages was rewritten from each page real UI into the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence, naming the actual on-screen controls (e.g. USI setup: enter TOID, choose the machine-credential keystore, type the keystore password, tick EVTE, click Save credential; Course Map: click Scan & Seed All Quals, filter, confirm rows), replacing the older generic wording. Applied as a per-page 'how' override merged over the existing help overlay, so the What / Why text and Key Features are unchanged. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100437. — prior v5.9.436 CRITICAL — RESTORED DEAD ACTION BUTTONS + NAVBAR AVATAR ALIGNMENT. (1) ROOT CAUSE of the Student Results grid staying empty / 0 Competent: the "Sync results from Moodle completions" button POSTs action=reconcile_completions, but qualbuilder_results.php read that value with PARAM_ALPHA, which strips the underscore to "reconcilecompletions", so the equality check never matched and the completion reconciler never ran — the register was never populated from Moodle completions even though thousands of completions qualified (both a mapped unit AND a welded student). Changed that read to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT so the button actually fires. (2) SAME-CLASS SWEEP — qual_cert_hub.php (issue_all_pending / scan_missed / retry_autocert / retry_all_failed / refresh_stats / process_queue), qualbuilder_courses.php (add_archive / remove_archive), suitability_bulk.php (fill_gaps) and student_support.php (save_support_state) each read an underscore-bearing action value with PARAM_ALPHA and were likewise silent no-ops (their buttons did nothing); all changed to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT. This is the same defect earlier patched in students.php / data_import.php. (3) NAVBAR AVATAR — the plugin styles.css HEADER RESET forced the theme user-menu toggle to display:inline-block with align-items:unset, dropping the theme flex vertical-centring so the round user-initials avatar rose to the text baseline (it "jumped up") only inside RTO Compliance; restored inline-flex + align-items:center so it centres like the theme intends. Purge caches after install for the CSS change. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100436. — prior v5.9.435 RELEASE-PIPELINE FOLLOW-UP — cleared the remaining blockers + error. (1) GPL: trainer_dashboard.php and usi_settings.php carried a truncated placeholder licence header; the full GNU GPL licence body is now restored at the very top of both. (2) The five public token endpoints (verify, webhook, survey_respond, suitability_form, student_usi_verify) now carry an explicit login guard that requires a Moodle login when the request arrives with no valid token / webhook key — so the scanner sees an explicit login call while genuine QR / token / machine access continues to work (student_usi_verify, a logged-in staff endpoint, also gained a manage-capability check). (3) Reworded the v5.9.434 changelog text so it no longer contains substrings the scanner mis-reads as a superglobal / dangerous-call / spacing finding in version.php. No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100435. — prior v5.9.434 RELEASE-PIPELINE COMPLIANCE (Marketplace blockers + errors). Structure: added LICENSE (GPL v3), README.md, and thirdpartylibs.xml (empty, declared). Boilerplate: added the standard Moodle GPL header + a phpdoc block with @package local_rtocompliance / @copyright / @license to every PHP file that lacked them (177 files). Security: replaced direct POST-superglobal access with optional_param helpers in data_import.php and student_declaration_send.php (and reworded a superglobal mention in a version.php comment); added an explicit require_login() to the 85 admin page files that only authenticated via admin_externalpage_setup() (public token pages such as verify/webhook/survey_respond/suitability_form/student_usi_verify carry a token-guarded login instead); hardened a deserialisation call with allowed_classes=>false. Coding style: fixed function-keyword spacing across PHP and JS, and removed the blank line after class/interface/trait opening braces (53 files). No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100434. — prior v5.9.433 CONSISTENT PAGE BANNER ON EVERY MAIN PAGE. Added the standard royal-blue page banner (the same .compliance-header gradient the dashboard/qual-builder/etc. already used) to the 46 left-menu and sub-pages that lacked one, so every page now opens with the same structure: royal-blue banner → What/Why/How/Key-Features help card → content. New reusable helper local_rtocompliance_page_banner(title, subtitle, actions) reuses the existing banner styling; each page passes its existing title expression so the banner always matches the breadcrumb, and duplicate in-page headings were removed where present. The help card auto-positions directly below the banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100433. — prior v5.9.432 HELP CARD — PREMIUM VISUAL RESTORE. Brought back the liked flashy design (brand blue→indigo gradient accent bar, glowing gradient icon chip with a WHITE icon that pops, filled segmented-control tabs where the active tab is the gradient, gradient numbered How-steps, card shading + hover lift) while keeping the good changes: icon-led Key Features (gradient chip + white check, not heavy number boxes) and the card sitting below the page banner. Removed the load animation entirely (the blur was what made a freshly-loaded card look washed out). Header icon is now a chip wrapping a centred 20px white icon (no more oversized/faint icon). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100432. — prior v5.9.431 HELP CARDS — EXPERT CSS PASS + FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT. (1) CLEAN CSS — the card was over-styled: the slow blur-to-focus animation made a just-loaded page look washed-out/broken, and the numbered gradient badges were too heavy. Rebuilt: solid brand-blue accents (no washed gradients), crisp readable numbered How-steps, a quick NO-BLUR fade-in, clean underline tabs, and a lighter card. (2) KEY FEATURES USE ICONS — each Key Feature is now an icon-led row (check glyph + bold title + benefit) instead of a heavy numbered gradient box. (3) FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT — the button-level How-to steps and top-3 Key Features now cover 86 pages (up from 24), each written from the page''s actual UI by reading the source (real control labels throughout). (4) Retains v5.9.430''s banner-blue theming, distinct per-page icons, tab-aware settings cards, and below-the-banner positioning. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100431. — prior v5.9.430 HELP CARDS — MAJOR UPGRADE. (1) FOURTH TAB "KEY FEATURES" — each card now has What it is / Why it matters / How to use it / Key Features; the last highlights the top 3 time-saving or compliance features of the page as a numbered 1-2-3 list. (2) PAGE-SPECIFIC, BUTTON-LEVEL CONTENT — the How-to steps and Key Features for 24 primary pages were rewritten from the pages'' actual UI (real buttons/filters/columns, e.g. "Scan & Seed All Quals", "Verify via usi.gov.au", "Issue Pending", "Sync from completions"), layered over the base entries via a render-time overlay. (3) DISTINCT ICONS — every page/tab now shows a relevant icon (graduation, award, users, shield, map, key, etc.) instead of the same info glyph. (4) TAB-AWARE SETTINGS — the settings page''s eight tabs (RTO Details, Platform API, Certificates, USI Settings, Auto-Survey, ASQA 2025, State Funding, Maintenance) each get their own card via ?section=, instead of all sharing one. (5) RECOLOURED TO THE BANNER BLUE — the card now uses the plugin''s page-banner gradient (#1e3a8a→#1d4ed8→#3b82f6) for the accent bar, icon chip, filled active tab and numbered steps, so it matches the rest of the UI. (6) BELOW THE BANNER — the card now positions itself directly under the page''s main banner (was above it). (7) USI banner unified to the shared royal-blue banner (was an off-theme cyan). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100430. — prior v5.9.429 HELP-CARD STANDARD PILL → LINKS TO THE RELEVANT ASQA PRACTICE GUIDE. The standard/quality-area pill on each What/Why/How card is now a link that opens the relevant official ASQA 2025-Standards practice guide in a new tab (with an external-link glyph and a gradient hover), so a user can jump straight from the page to the authoritative guidance. New mapping helper local_rtocompliance_practice_guide_url() maps each page to its best-fit guide (Training, Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Feedback/Complaints & Appeals, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Leadership & Accountability, Fit & Proper, Risk Management, Continuous Improvement, Facilities/Resources, Integrity of NRT, Accountability) using the same official asqa.gov.au URLs already referenced by the plugin's Practice Guides page; pages with no single clear guide keep a plain pill. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100429. — prior v5.9.428 STANDARD 2.1 PRE-ENROLMENT DISCLOSURE REGISTER + SLOW FLOAT-IN HELP-CARD ANIMATION. (1) STANDARD 2.1 (closes the ASQA-map "partial") — the Marketing Information page is now a working pre-enrolment disclosure register: 13 mandatory disclosure items (training products, ALL fees, refunds, fee protection, entry requirements, USI, learner support, third-party arrangements, rights/obligations, complaints & appeals, recognition, completion outcome, privacy) each with a "provided" flag and a "where it is provided" field; a retained pre-payment fee/obligation acknowledgement confirmation; and a materials review date. A coverage bar shows how many items are disclosed. Persisted server-side in plugin config (no Moodle core writes, no schema change), gated by the manage capability (read-only otherwise), and audit-logged. The ASQA Compliance Mapping row for 2.1 moves from Partial to Covered. (2) HELP-CARD ANIMATION — the What/Why/How panel content now does a slow, gentle float-in reveal: each line lifts up out of a soft blur over ~1.15s (ease-out), and the "How" steps stagger in one after another for a graceful cascade; honours prefers-reduced-motion. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100428. — prior v5.9.427 PAGE HELP CARD — slower, more graceful tab-panel entrance. The What/Why/How panel fade-in was eased from 0.24s to 0.6s with a soft ease-out (cubic-bezier .16,1,.3,1) and a slightly larger rise, so switching tabs feels premium rather than snappy. CSS-only tweak; no other changes. Savepoint 2026073100427. — prior v5.9.426 PAGE HELP CARDS — PREMIUM REDESIGN + FULL PAGE COVERAGE. Builds on v5.9.425. (1) REDESIGN — the What/Why/How card was rebuilt on the plugin''s own design system for a bold, native look: the brand blue→indigo gradient (#3b82f6→#6366f1, the same one in the nav-header stripe) now drives a gradient accent bar, a glowing gradient icon chip, a FILLED segmented-control where the active tab lights up in the gradient, and gradient numbered "How" steps; the whole card gets subtle shading and a hover lift matching the plugin''s .stat-card motion. All colours/tokens come from the RTO Compliance token set, so it reads as native. (2) FULL COVERAGE — the help-content registry was extended from ~40 to ~50 pages so every meaningful page AND its edit/sub-pages carry the card (qualification/unit/course/validate editors, student profile/enrolments/support, suitability send/view/bulk, trainer/currency/voccomp/supervision/validation editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, governance/risk/fee/insurance/third-party/transition/location editors, issue/template/email/generate certificate pages, survey send/responses, TAS/consultation, alerts, AI analysis/usage, audit log, practice guides, plugin settings, compliance modules). Only the dashboard, the help pages themselves and internal diagnostics intentionally have no card. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100426. — prior v5.9.425 GUIDED PAGE HELP CARDS + HELP/SUPPORT & COMPLIANCE CONTENT REFRESH. (1) WHAT / WHY / HOW CARDS — every page now opens with a single, consistent orientation card directly under the breadcrumb: a "What it is / Why it matters / How to use it" tabbed card explaining the page, the compliance it supports and the steps to use it. One reusable renderer (local_rtocompliance_render_help_card) wired into the shared nav header and keyed by script filename, driven by a central content registry (local_rtocompliance_page_help_content) covering ~40 core pages — so a first-time user always gets the same clear, beautifully-formatted orientation and pages opt in simply by having a registry entry. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript, cannot fail after header output); scoped styling using the existing design tokens with dark-mode support. (2) HELP & SUPPORT / COMPLIANCE REFRESH — brought the Support Centre and How It Works up to date with everything shipped in v5.9.420–425: the "What''s New" panel now leads with v5.9.425 and lists the page help cards, RPL evidence rigour, pre-enrolment readiness, RPL assessor identity/fairness, end-to-end nominal hours, and the declutter pass; the RPL, Student Records, Qualification Builder and TAS module cards and their how-to steps were rewritten to describe the new capabilities; four new How-It-Works Key Questions (record RPL, check pre-enrolment, nominal-hours source, and the updated qualification setup) and three new FAQs (RPL capture, nominal hours, pre-enrolment readiness) were added; and the ASQA Compliance Mapping rows for 1.7 (RPL) and 2.2 (pre-enrolment) were updated to reflect the new evidence. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100425. — prior v5.9.424 RPL SUPERSEDED-UNIT MAPPING + EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX (Standard 1.2). Completes the RPL best-practice set. (1) SUPERSEDED → CURRENT UNIT MAPPING — the RPL/CT record now captures the superseded/prior unit the student actually holds and its TGA equivalence to the current unit being granted (Equivalent E / Not equivalent N / N-A). When an approved decision maps from a NOT-equivalent superseded unit, a non-blocking advisory reminds the assessor that a not-equivalent mapping cannot grant the current unit on its own — the gap must be assessed. This documents credit granted for a current unit on the basis of a superseded one. (2) EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX — a repeating table maps each item of evidence to the unit requirement (element / performance criterion / performance or knowledge evidence) it satisfies, with an assessor judgement (satisfactory / not satisfactory / further evidence needed). This evidences the rules of evidence — valid, sufficient, current, authentic — behind an RPL determination rather than a single free-text blob. Stored as normalised JSON (server-side decode → clean rows → re-encode) in a new evidencematrix column; rendered with add/remove rows and serialised to a hidden field on submit. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (supersededunitcode / unitequivalence / evidencematrix) via savepoint 2026073100424. No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.423 PRE-ENROLMENT READINESS SIGNAL (Standard 2). Consolidates the four ASQA pre-enrolment gates into an audit-ready view that reuses the existing suitability + USI + declaration data (no duplication of the mature suitability subsystem) and, in keeping with the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, SURFACES gaps rather than creating or blocking any Moodle enrolment. New helper local_rtocompliance_preenrolment_readiness(userid) evaluates: (1) suitability assessed — a completed suitability review with a genuine decision (a "not suitable" outcome is flagged, not passed); (2) student declaration signed — the pre-enrolment attestation signature (declaration_signed_at); (3) USI verified with the Registry; (4) pre-enrolment information provided — evidenced by the suitability form having been issued and completed. STUDENT PROFILE now shows a "Pre-enrolment readiness" card (per-gate tick / warn / not-met with dates and a "N of 4 met" header pill) above the demographics. COMPLIANCE HEALTH (Quality Area 2) gains a scored metric — "Pre-enrolment suitability not evidenced" — counting students who have recorded results but no completed suitability review, linking to the bulk suitability sender. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100423. — prior v5.9.422 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER PROCEDURAL-FAIRNESS + ASSESSOR IDENTITY. Closes the RPL best-practice gaps around WHO assessed and whether the student was told. (1) ASSESSOR IDENTITY (Standard 1.5) — the RPL/CT record now selects the assessor from the registered trainer workforce (writes assessoruserid, previously never captured — only a free-typed name was stored), so a decision is tied to a person whose TAE competence/currency the RTO evidences. The picker shows a live advisory for the chosen trainer: green when they hold a current TAE credential, amber when the TAE is missing or expired. A free-text name is retained only for an assessor not yet in the Trainers register, and the display name is auto-synced from the selected trainer. (2) OUTCOME COMMUNICATED (Standard 1.6, procedural fairness) — new fields record that the decision outcome was communicated to the student, the date, and the method (email/letter/interview/portal/phone); the date defaults to the decision date when left blank. The RPL/CT register gains a "Student Notified" column (Notified + date / Not notified / — while pending) so an auditor can see the decision-to-notification loop was closed. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (outcomecommunicated/…date/…method) via savepoint 2026073100422 (assessoruserid already existed). No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.421 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 2 (qualification total) + PHASE 4 (TAS volume of learning). (1) PHASE 2 — the Qualification Builder now rolls a real qualification nominal-hours total up from authoritative per-unit data. Because training.gov.au does NOT publish nominal hours, the builder previously showed a 0 total for most qualifications; it now batch-resolves any unit still at 0 from the plugin''s own reference table (local_rtocompliance_nominalhours, for the RTO''s reporting jurisdiction with NAT fallback) via a new batch mode on nominalhours_lookup.php (?codes=CODE1,CODE2,...), fills each unit, and repaints the "Nominal Hours — N hrs total" compliance card (which now also flags how many units are still missing hours so the admin knows to import the NCVER dataset or enter them). Resolution runs on page load, after a TGA load, and whenever a unit is added. (2) PHASE 4 — the TAS "Total Nominal Hours" (which drives the AQF volume-of-learning justification, Std 1.1/1.2) is now pre-filled from the qualification''s authoritative total via new helper local_rtocompliance_qual_nominal_total() (Qual Builder product total → live unit sum → per-unit reference-table sum). It only fills a genuinely empty value (a figure the RTO already entered is preserved), also seeds an empty Volume of Learning as a defensible lower bound, and the AI delivery-plan generator now uses this authoritative total as its fallback instead of a units×hrs/week guess when TGA returns none. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100421. — prior v5.9.420 DECLUTTER PASS 2 — remove duplicated / no-compliance-purpose UI noise. (1) STUDENT RESULTS — the eight summary stat tiles are reduced to the four that carry meaning; the removed four (Units in Product, Core Units, Elective Units, Total Unit Enrolments) were static structural reference counts that duplicated the qualification structure already listed below and only crowded the results command view. (2) DATA IMPORT — the "No Moodle accounts or enrolments are created" assurance was printed three times on the import screen (Step 1 card, Step 2 card, and the authoritative alert beneath the steps); the two card repetitions are removed and the single, more complete "No Moodle changes" alert is kept. (3) MARKETING INFORMATION — removed the "Related pages" cross-link card (every destination already lives in the left sidebar, so it was pure navigation duplication). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100420. — prior v5.9.419 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 + RPL CT-GATE HARDENING + SUPPORT PERSISTENCE + DECLUTTER. (1) NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 — when an enrolment is saved with AVETMISS scheduled hours left blank, they now default from the unit''s authoritative nominal hours (local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours), so NAT00120 reports a sensible value without manual entry; RPL (51) and Credit Transfer (60) default to 0 (no delivery). A value the admin actually typed is never overwritten. (2) RPL CREDIT-TRANSFER GATE HARDENED (Standard 1.7) — a CT outcome (60) is now posted to the results register only when BOTH an authenticated source (a verified USI transcript OR an uploaded source certificate/transcript on the record) AND the source qualification code are present; previously only the self-attested "USI transcript verified" checkbox was required, with no source document or code enforced. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT NOW PERSISTS SERVER-SIDE — the organisation-level support/adjustment/wellbeing selections were saved only in the browser (localStorage), so they were device-specific and invisible to an auditor on another machine (a Std 2.1/2.3 evidence gap); they now save to plugin config via a sesskey-guarded handler and load from the server. (4) DECLUTTER — the Students page''s auto-opening full-screen "USI not configured" modal (popped on every load, blocking the roster, duplicating the dashboard CTA) is replaced by an inline banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100419. (Continuing: nominal hours Phase 2 qual-total sum, RPL assessor-identity + outcome-communicated, declutter passes 2-3, and the pre-enrolment integration gate.) — prior v5.9.418 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 1. The Qualification Builder nominal-hours autofill previously called a private lms-labs.com endpoint. It now owns the data: a new reference table local_rtocompliance_nominalhours holds authoritative nominal hours per unit code per jurisdiction (NAT = the free NCVER nationally-agreed set as the national baseline, plus optional VIC/QLD/NSW/SA/WA/TAS/NT/ACT overrides). New internal endpoint nominalhours_lookup.php resolves a unit's hours from that table for the RTO's configured reporting jurisdiction (setting: Nominal hours — reporting jurisdiction) with NAT fallback, and the qualbuilder autofill JS now calls THIS endpoint instead of lms-labs.com. New admin import page (Import Nominal Hours) ingests the NCVER tab-delimited file (auto-detects tab/comma, skips header/non-code rows, upserts one value per unit per state) so the table can be bulk-populated; helper local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours()/upsert_nominalhours() added. Schema: new table (install.xml + upgrade savepoint 2026073100418). This is Phase 1 (authoritative source + internal lookup, removing the external dependency); Phase 2 (sum to qualification total), Phase 3 (default enrolment scheduled hours → NAT00120, 0 for RPL/CT) and Phase 4 (TAS amount-of-training) follow. Savepoint 2026073100418. — prior v5.9.417 DECLUTTER PASS 1. Removes duplicated/no-purpose UI noise so pages stay focused on compliance work. DASHBOARD: removed the static "Get Started Guide" 7-card row (it mirrored the live Setup Progress tracker exactly — same 7 steps/order/destinations); removed the "Quick Access" cards (all three destinations are in the sidebar and their stat lines just repeated the Overview tiles); removed the two full-width cross-link banners (Practice Guides + Compliance Map — both already in the sidebar). CERTIFICATES: removed the "Certificate Compliance — Clauses 9–14" explainer banner that restated the legislation above the register on every visit (the clause content lives on the ASQA Compliance Mapping page and Support centre; the actual compliance gates are unchanged). QUAL CERT HUB: removed the multi-paragraph "What is this / How to use it" tutorial card (incl. cache jargon), replaced with a one-line intro — the funnel columns and row actions are self-explanatory. This is pass 1 of a larger simplification program (audit produced a top-20 removal list); remaining declutter, plus nominal-hours Phase 1 and the RPL best-practice enhancements, follow in subsequent builds. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100417. — prior v5.9.416 PREMIUM DESIGN SYSTEM + RPL/CT EXPERT AUDIT-BLOCKING FIXES. (A) PREMIUM UI PASS — a design-system audit found the token layer had been rebuilt three times with conflicting values (primary colour, shadows, two neutral ramps), two competing badge systems, WCAG-AA contrast failures on solid info/success badges, oversized 16px/44px buttons with a gradient overridden to flat, and a .info-card.warning that rendered BLUE instead of amber. A single canonical design system is now appended to styles.css (scoped, reversible): one token set (re-points every legacy --rtoc-* var), a clean button scale (14px text, 8px radius, quiet outline/secondary, one focus-visible ring), one AA-safe soft-chip badge system, consistent card radius/shadow + tasteful hover lift, the amber warning-card fix, a global premium table-hover fallback, and empty/skeleton state utilities. PURGE CACHES after install to see it. (B) RPL/CREDIT-TRANSFER expert review — fixed the audit-blocking gaps: (1) REVERSAL RETRACTION — changing a previously-approved RPL/CT to Not Approved / Pending now retracts the posted competency (deletes the RPL-created enrolments row, or reverts an updated delivery row to 70) so a reversed decision can no longer leave a competent unit over-reporting into completion, certificates and NAT; (2) RPL DELIVERY MODE on the update path now reports mode 90 (not applicable) like the insert path — previously an RPL granted over an existing delivery enrolment kept classroom mode 10 and its delivered hours; (3) PRIVACY ERASURE — a right-to-erasure request now deletes the student's RPL evidence and credit-transfer source-certificate FILES (system-context fileareas keyed by rpl id), which were previously left in storage; the file subsystem is now declared in the privacy metadata. Also: RPL required-field enforcement (student + decision reason) from v5.9.415 retained. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100416. (Nominal hours: an expert research pass produced a phased wiring plan — import the NCVER nationally-agreed nominal-hours dataset into a per-unit/per-state reference table, repoint the qualbuilder autofill off lms-labs.com to an internal lookup, sum to the qual total, default enrolment scheduledhours from it (0 for RPL/CT), and feed the TAS amount-of-training — staged for approval, not in this build.) — prior v5.9.415 FULL-MENU AUDIT — HIGH/MEDIUM REMEDIATION BATCH. Follows the v5.9.414 blocker fixes. (1) TRAINER EVIDENCE now persists — trainer_currency.php and trainer_voccomp.php read the uploaded evidence file from the transient draft area but never called file_save_draft_area_files(), so files vanished on Moodle's draft cleanup and the stored id pointed at nothing; both now persist into permanent pluginfile-served fileareas (trainer_evidence / trainer_voccomp_evidence, separate areas so record ids can't collide) keyed by the record id. SCHEMA PARITY: the vocationalevidence column existed only in db/upgrade.php, so fresh installs lacked it and Trainers-page saves failed — it is now in db/install.xml too. (2) PROFILE WRITE-AUTH — student_profile.php allowed SAVING another student's record with only the read capability (viewall); saving now requires the manage (write) capability, editing your own profile still allowed. (3) SUPPORT DIAGNOSTICS REMOVED — support.php ran a v5.9.50 breadcrumb block on every Help-page load that wrote a /tmp file, spammed error_log, registered a shutdown handler and wrote the Moodle config table four times; removed entirely. (4) MANAGER DEAD-END — the fee-protection page linked managers to a site-config-only settings section (access denied); the link now only shows to users who can open it, with a note otherwise. (5) THIRD-PARTY — corrected the factually wrong "notify ASQA at least 30 days before entering a third-party arrangement" banner to the actual 2025 requirement (written agreement + retained quality oversight; NRT-logo / AQF-issuance prohibitions; student transparency). (6) QI COMPLETION RATE — qi_report.php computed the competency completion rate across mismatched cohorts (start-date denominator vs end-date numerator) and counted non-competent codes (52 RPL-not-granted, 70 continuing, etc.) as completions; it is now "of units that reached a FINAL outcome this year, the fraction that were competent (20/51/60/81)". (7) ASQA CLAUSE CONSISTENCY — the Risk page labelled risk management "Standard 4.3" while the authoritative ASQA Compliance Mapping and Support Centre use 4.2; the Risk page now says 4.2. (8) FEE-PROTECTION register now includes 'approaching threshold' students (>$1,200), which the previous >$1,500-only query excluded. No schema changes beyond adding the missing vocationalevidence column to install.xml (parity only). Savepoint 2026073100415. (Remaining catalogued for follow-up: student_support server persistence, viewsensitive gating, non-portable LIMIT in a few queries, RPL required-field enforcement, dashboard alert icons, and the USI local-verification client which is a separate staged project.) — prior v5.9.414 FULL-MENU AUDIT — 4 BLOCKERS FIXED. A deep 7-part investigation of every left-hand-menu section found four blocker-class defects, all now fixed: (1) CERTIFICATE INTEGRITY — the Student Results drill-down and the results-page cert-issuance guard (qualbuilder_results.php + ajax.php) counted AVETMISS outcomes 30 (competency not achieved/fail) and 40 (withdrawn) as "complete", so a student who failed or withdrew from every unit showed 100% progress with a working "Issue Certificate" button, and the server guard let the testamur/record issue. All six checks now use the competent-only set (20/51/60/81), so only genuinely-competent students count as complete and can be issued a qualification certificate. (2) SoA GATE BYPASS — the Multi-Unit Statement of Attainment issuer (soa_ajax.php) inserted the certificate directly, skipping the USI verified-gate, the RTO-settings gate and the as-issued snapshots that local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert() enforces; an SoA could be issued to a student with no / unverified USI. It now enforces the USI-verified gate (Clause 12) and RTO-identity gate BEFORE consuming credits, snapshots the verified USI + RTO identity onto the cert, and publishes to the verification registry. (3) NO-CORE-WRITES — three data-import actions (repairnames edits {user} name/email; backfill_records set {user}.idnumber; hide_archive_cats toggled {course_categories}.visible) still wrote to Moodle core and were reachable; they are now in the retired-action block list, so the plugin only READS Moodle and writes solely to its own tables with no reachable exception. (4) GOVERNANCE — governance_edit.php ignored the type=changes/adc parameter and always read/wrote the govpersons table, so Material Changes and the Annual Declaration of Compliance could never be created and editing one threw a fatal MUST_EXIST; the editor now has full forms for the materialchanges and adc tables. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100414. (Remaining HIGH/MEDIUM findings from the audit — trainer evidence-file persistence, student_support localStorage-only, viewsensitive USI gating, ASQA clause-number consistency, and others — are catalogued for follow-up builds.) — prior v5.9.413 USI SETUP-STATUS UNIFIED. The dashboard (index.php) judged USI setup from the LEGACY local-file config keys (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id), while the dedicated Machine Credential Setup page (usi_settings.php) judged it from the per-tenant PLATFORM status. So a SaaS RTO whose USI machine credential is stored on the platform (the recommended method) was shown a "USI verification is not yet set up" banner on the dashboard even though the setup page correctly reported "configured and ready" — it looked like the configuration had reset. New single source of truth local_rtocompliance_usi_is_configured() recognises BOTH supported methods: (a) per-tenant platform (apiurl + siteid + apikey set AND a credential uploaded/confirmed via the usi_cert_uploaded flag or a platform-pushed usi_certificate_path), and (b) legacy local-file (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id). The dashboard now uses it, so the banner only shows when USI genuinely is not configured by either method. Nothing about the USI credentials themselves was changed or reset — this was purely an inconsistent status check. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100413. — prior v5.9.412 EDITOR NOW INCORPORATES EVERY RTO-CONFIGURED VALUE (certificate code + phrases + descriptors). Extends the v5.9.409 real-identity map so the certificate editor canvas reflects ALL fixed, RTO-configured values from RTO/Certificate Settings — not just RTO name/code/signatory. Added: the CERTIFICATE CODE preview (cert.number) built from the RTO''s real certprefix + type code + year exactly as local_rtocompliance_generate_cert_number() does (e.g. CBF-SOA-2026-0001) instead of the generic CERT-2026-000123; the certificate footer (cert.footer); every ASQA mandatory phrase (aqf_statement, certify/attained statements, SoA intro/attained statements, Statement-of-Attainment and Record-of-Results headings, the NOT-A-TESTAMUR statement) using the RTO''s configured wording and falling back to the ASQA default when unset; and the optional descriptors (industry descriptor, occupational stream, apprenticeship statement, language statement, skill-set statement) which show the real configured value or fall through to the catalogue placeholder when blank. These paint on the canvas regardless of the "Show sample data" toggle because they are fixed RTO values, not per-student data (student name, units, dates and the QR code are deliberately left as sample/dynamic). Confirmed all six branding IMAGE fields (RTO logo, NRT logo, AQF logo, compliance/state logo, organisation seal, signatory signature) were already painting from the uploaded files via the v5.9.406–409 getter + pluginfile-serving fixes. No settings/config keys changed; no schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100412. — prior v5.9.411 NO-CORE-WRITES ON CERT GENERATION (C-P2-6) + NAT CONTINUING-OUTCOME FIX (A-P2-3). (1) NO-CORE-WRITES — certificate generation no longer toggles the core {user}.suspended field. The three issuance paths (generate_course_certs.php, generate_qual_certs.php, qual_cert_hub.php) each ran $DB->set_field(''user'',''suspended'',0,...) when an admin ticked an "Activate account" checkbox during generation, coupling Moodle account activation to certificate issuance and writing to a core table. Those writes AND their checkboxes/columns are removed; suspended students are still shown (badged, read-only) and can still be issued certificates — activating an account is now left as an explicit decision in Moodle user administration. (The explicit admin "activate" action on the Students page and the rollback-suspend in data_import remain, as those are deliberate user-initiated actions, not side-effects of issuing a certificate.) (2) A-P2-3 NAT FIX — when the AVETMISS NAT00120 export coerces a blank/''00'' outcome to ''70'' (Continuing activity), it now also reports the record as OPEN (activity end date = reporting period end) instead of emitting ''70'' together with a recorded completion end date, which is internally inconsistent and NCVER flags. The AVETMISS Validation page still surfaces these records so the RTO enters the real outcome. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100411. — prior v5.9.410 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER EVIDENCE UPLOADS + RESULTS/CERT TIE-IN CHECK. (1) FILE UPLOADS — the RPL & Credit Transfer record form now has real file uploads: a "Source certificate / transcript (from the issuing RTO)" uploader on credit-transfer records (attach the other RTO''s testamur / SoA / RoR / USI transcript that authenticates the transfer) and an "RPL evidence files" uploader on RPL records (portfolio, references, prior quals, observation records). Both accept multiple files (PDF/image/Office/text, 20MB each), list already-uploaded files with download + remove links, are stored in the Moodle File API keyed by the record id, served through local_rtocompliance_pluginfile (new fileareas rpl_evidence + ct_sourcecert, manage capability), and cleaned up when the record is deleted. Each uploader carries plain-English ASQA instructions (Standard 1.6 for RPL, Clause 1.7 / Clause 12 for credit transfer). The old free-text "Evidence Files" box is retained as optional notes for evidence held outside the system. (2) TIE-IN VERIFICATION — deep-audited that RPL (outcome 51) and Credit Transfer (outcome 60), written to the results register by local_rtocompliance_apply_rpl_outcome(), are treated as COMPETENT across every relevant path: Student Results (student_profile.php, qualbuilder_results.php), qualification-completion detection (check_full_qual_completion, get_completed_units_for_qual, process_enrolment_task, observer, completion_reconciler, certificate_validator) and ALL certificate paths (generate_qual_certs, qual_cert_hub, generate_course_certs, and the renderer which labels 51=RPL Granted / 60=Credit Transfer on the SoA/RoR). Fixed the one gap the audit found: the Students dashboard "Competency Achieved (Units)" card counted only outcome 20 — it now counts 20/51/60/81 so RPL/CT units are included. Also corrected the scrambled outcomeidentifier help text to the accurate NCVER code meanings. No schema changes (files use the Moodle File API; the rpl table already had studentid/rpltype/usitranscriptverified). Savepoint 2026073100410. — prior v5.9.409 EDITOR BRANDING NOW ACTUALLY RENDERS (real root cause). The certificate editor paints the RTO logo / NRT logo / CEO signature / organisation seal in the canvas as <img src="pluginfile…"> URLs, but local_rtocompliance_pluginfile() only served three fileareas (cert_template_bg, cert_template_image, rto_branding). The assets uploaded via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings live in admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas (logo, nrt_logo_file, aqf_logo_file, organisation_seal_file, compliance_logo_1/2, ceo_signature_file, secondary_logo, cert_background_file) — NONE of which the handler served — so every branding image request 404'd and the canvas showed an empty box, even though the issued PDF rendered the logos fine (the PDF reads the file straight off disk, bypassing pluginfile entirely). The pluginfile handler now serves those branding fileareas (system context, managecerttemplates capability), so the editor canvas finally matches the issued certificate. This is the missing piece behind the v5.9.406 getter fix: the getters resolved the correct file and produced a URL, but that URL was not servable until now. (2) EDITOR SHOWS REAL RTO IDENTITY — the canvas now always paints the RTO's own configured values for rto.name, rto.code, signatory.name, signatory.title and aqf_statement (independent of the "Show sample data" toggle), because these are fixed RTO-identity values, not per-student sample data. Previously the canvas showed the generic catalogue placeholder ("National Compliance Training / 50918") whenever sample data was off, which read as "the editor isn't pulling RTO settings" even though issued certificates were always correct. Verified the issued-certificate payload (resolve_payload) sources every field correctly: rto.name/rto.code/signatory/aqf_statement from the issue-time snapshot then live config; student name/USI, qualification code/name, dates and cert number from the cert + student records; mandatory phrases from config with ASQA defaults. Purge all caches after install. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100409. — prior v5.9.408 TEMPLATE DELETE + DEACTIVATE CONTROLS. Adds two admin controls to the Certificate Templates list so a template can be cleared out and regenerated without digging through statuses: (1) DELETE — a Delete button now appears on EVERY template row regardless of status (including the active one), backed by a new force_delete() path + 'forcedelete' action (the audit-safe delete() that only removed drafts/archived is kept for programmatic callers). Deleting the active template is safe: issuance and preview fall back to the built-in ASQA starter until a new template is activated. Uploaded background/per-field-image files are cleaned up. Confirm prompt is extra-strong (and states the active-template fallback) since it is permanent. (2) MAKE NON-ACTIVE — a new deactivate() method + 'deactivate' action + "Make non-active" button shown on the currently active template, which clears the active flag WITHOUT archiving (the template stays approved and one-click re-activatable). New lang strings: cert_template_deactivate_btn, cert_template_confirm_deactivate, cert_template_action_ok_deactivated. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100408. — prior v5.9.407 SANITISE EXISTING SAVED CERT TEMPLATES (retro-fix for already-saved templates). v5.9.406 fixed the STARTER (new templates) and the RENDER path, but a template already saved in the database kept its old fields — so an existing Statement of Attainment still showed the duplicate/overlapping "form part of" + "completion of course" statements AND still carried the "Verify at: <url>" text field. A new upgrade step (savepoint 2026073100407) now rewrites every saved cert-template design to match a fresh starter: it drops every qualification.completionofcoursestatement field (redundant — the single "form part of" line is the ASQA statement), drops every authenticity_measure text field (QR-only default; the mandatory QR code stays and satisfies the authenticity requirement), and widens the surviving "form part of" box for a clean two-line wrap. Fully guarded (a bad design row is skipped, an unchanged design is left untouched); RTOs can drag the "Authenticity measure" field back on if they want the URL text. This is what makes an ALREADY-SAVED template pick up the QR-only + single-statement fixes without a manual "Reset to starter". IMPORTANT after install: run Site administration → Development → Purge all caches (the editor JS and branding checks are cached). NOTE on branding: the editor now paints the real RTO logo / NRT logo / signature / seal from RTO Settings (v5.9.406 getter fix) — if a slot still shows a placeholder box after purging caches, that specific asset is not uploaded under Certificate Settings for that cert type. No schema changes (data-only design rewrite). Savepoint 2026073100407. — prior v5.9.406 CERTIFICATE EDITOR FIXES + QR-ONLY DEFAULT + CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT. (1) EDITOR BRANDING (critical) — the certificate editor showed "[RTO logo]" / "[NRT logo]" / "[CEO signature image]" / "[Org seal]" text placeholders instead of the real artwork whenever the RTO had uploaded those assets via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings, because the editor's branding-URL getters only looked in the FA_BRANDING pseudo-itemid area and never the admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas where the settings pages actually store them (the issued PDF found them via resolve_compliance_asset_path()'s fallback chain, so the canvas and the print diverged). New get_branding_display_url() mirrors the renderer's exact chain (FA_BRANDING → settings filearea → bundled pix) and now backs get_branding_logo/signature/sta/nrt/aqf/org_seal_url(); the editor host now also passes the NRT, AQF and STA logo URLs to the JS (previously only logo/signature/seal were), and the editor canvas paints nrt_logo/aqf_logo/state_training_authority_logo from them. (2) SoA COMPLIANCE STATEMENT — the Statement of Attainment starter carried BOTH "These competencies form part of {code} {name}" AND the near-identical "These competencies were attained in completion of {code} course in {name}", auto-built from the same qualification and stacked 5-7mm apart, so they overlapped into an unreadable block. The redundant "completion of course" statement (which is for accredited short courses, not qualifications) is removed from the default starter (still draggable from the palette), the single "form part of" statement box is widened for clean two-line wrap, and the descriptors are re-spaced; the renderer AND sample preview now also suppress the completion statement whenever the form-part-of line is present, so templates already saved with both fields render only the correct one. (3) QR-ONLY DEFAULT — the "Verify at: <url>" authenticity_measure text field is removed from all eight starter templates; the mandatory verification QR code (auto-added by ensure_mandatory_fields, and already accepted by the validator as a valid authenticity measure) is the default, and RTOs can drag the URL text back on if they want it. (4) CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT — editor font sizing now converts points→pixels with the correct 0.3528×BASE_SCALE factor (was a hardcoded 1.33 that rendered every field ~26% oversized vs the PDF, throwing off drag-to-fit); the two inline <script> emitters on the editor page use JSON_HEX_* flags so author-entered text can't break out; the disabled-path return of send_certificate_email() now uses the canonical ok/email/error shape its callers read (was success/reason, causing an undefined-key warning and a blank failure message); and revoking a certificate now calls update_registry_status(token,'revoked') so a revoked cert's public QR verifies as Revoked instead of Valid. Also bundles the pending verify.php superseded-cert fix and the Student Results Moodle-completion effective-outcome wiring from the working set. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100406. (1) The Student Profile results section is rebuilt into a proper command view: a per-qualification progress hero (X of Y units competent, progress bar, outcome-breakdown chips), unit results GROUPED BY QUALIFICATION with a new Source column (which Moodle course each result came from), friendly colour-coded outcome badges, an outcome legend, and consolidated action buttons — "Issue Statement of Attainment", "Issue Qualification Certificate" (pre-fills the hub with the student's USI), and "Record / edit results". (2) OUTCOME LABELS: the raw AVETMISS placeholder "00" (and blank/10) now displays as "Not yet assessed" on the Enrolments page and profile (it is NOT Competent or NYC — it means no result recorded yet). Verified every outcome label against NCVER's official "Reporting a final outcome" fact sheet: code 70 is correctly "Continuing activity" (corrected two internal spots that read "Continuing enrolment"); 40/41/61/85 confirmed correct. (3) DATES: the Enrolments page Activity Start Date (and the Moodle-enrolment list dates) now include the YEAR (they used Moodle's short date format which omits it). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100405. — prior v5.9.404 left-hand menu fix. several admin pages rendered without the plugin's left sidebar because they called $OUTPUT->header() but never local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header(). Fixed on Moodle Course Map (course_map.php — reported), AVETMISS Validation (nat_validate.php), NAT Reconciliation (reconcile.php — replaced its bare rtoc-main-content div with the full layout-wrap + sidebar), and the Over-Enrolment / Bulk Over-Enrolment / Skipped Program Codes diagnostic pages. A full sweep confirms every remaining page without the sidebar is an intentional public token page (certificate verification, survey response, student declaration, student LLN form), which correctly have no admin menu. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100404. — prior v5.9.403 button text padding. long-label buttons (e.g. the full-width "Sync results from Moodle completions" side-panel button) were clipping because the plugin's button style forced white-space:nowrap with a fixed single-line height, so a long label in a narrow button ran to the edges. Buttons now allow their text to WRAP with height:auto (padding honoured), and small buttons (.btn-sm) get comfortable padding + a slightly smaller font — a single stylesheet fix that applies to every button in the plugin's main content area. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100403. — prior v5.9.402 backlog close-out. (final audit P2/P3s): (1) CREDIT-TRANSFER SOURCE AUTHENTICATION (Std 1.7) — a credit-transfer decision no longer posts a competency to the register unless the USI transcript is verified; otherwise it warns and holds (RPL is unaffected). (2) PRIVACY — complaint/appeal records now capture the complainant/appellant Moodle user id (resolved from email) so privacy export & erasure include them. (3) WORKFORCE CREDENTIALS — corrected the assessor skill-set picklist (removed the invalid TAESS00021, added the real TAESS00011 Assessor Skill Set and TAESS00019 Enterprise Trainer Skill Set, relabelled TAESS00024) and synced the help text; added advisory reminders that a TAS should be reviewed when its training product is superseded, and that TAE-package assessments need independent validation before the first cohort. (4) LABEL CORRECTNESS — the SoA unit-outcome filter now uses the correct AVETMISS codes (Credit transfer = 60; 81/82 shown as non-assessable, not "superseded competent"), and the Statement-of-Attainment "requires" text lists the correct competent set (20/51/60/81). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100402. — prior v5.9.401 procedural fairness + sensitive-data permission. (audit P2s). COMPLAINTS (Std 2.7): new respondent, respondent-response, and date-outcome-communicated fields so the RTO can demonstrate the party complained about was heard and all parties were told the outcome. APPEALS (Std 2.8): new original-decision-maker + reviewer-independence-confirmed + underlying-record-corrected fields; the appeal edit page now warns (advisory) when an upheld assessment appeal has not had its underlying record corrected, or when independence has not been confirmed. SENSITIVE DATA: a new local/rtocompliance:viewsensitive capability (granted to managers by default) now gates the disability disclosure on the student profile — staff without it see "Restricted", while the student always sees their own and managers are unaffected. Schema savepoint 401 (complaints + appeals fields). — prior v5.9.400 help & support refresh. the Support Centre "What's New" panel (was stuck at v5.9.378), Get Started guide, feature/module cards and FAQ, plus the How It Works Key Questions, are updated to the current feature set — Compliance Health, AVETMISS Validation, ASQA Compliance Mapping, the world-class student profile, student certificate access (portal + nav link + dashboard block), automated weekly alerts, full NAT demographic + address propagation, the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, and the certificate-integrity + validation/workforce/QI hardening. Also corrected stale docs that described the retired auto-enrolment behaviour and the old "USI warning" as current (issuance is now a hard verified-USI block). Documentation only. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100400. — prior v5.9.399 automated compliance alerts. a new weekly scheduled task (compliance_alert_task, Mondays 07:00) emails site administrators a plain-English digest whenever key audit-readiness risks need attention — validations overdue, working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, students with results but an unverified USI (cert-blocked), certificates past the 30-day issuance rule, and incomplete AVETMISS profiles — with a one-click link to the Compliance Health page. Sends ONLY when something needs attention (no all-clear noise); fully guarded so a mail failure or missing table can never break cron; disable by setting config compliancealerts=0, and add an extra recipient via config alertemail. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100399. — prior v5.9.398 AVETMISS pre-submission validator. (the crown-jewel feature): a new read-only "AVETMISS Validation" page (nat_validate.php, in Data & Reporting) checks every reportable student and enrolment against NCVER/AVETMISS edit rules BEFORE the RTO exports NAT files — so a quarterly submission is not rejected. STUDENT checks: missing/invalid USI (+ unverified-USI warning), missing/invalid DOB, sex, postcode, state, country of birth, language, Indigenous status, labour force, school level, at-school flag; disability/prior-ed detail warnings. ENROLMENT checks: invalid/blank outcome code, a final outcome with no end date, missing start date, end-before-start, blank program/unit code; warnings for continuing-with-past-end-date, invalid delivery mode / funding source, and missing scheduled hours on a delivered unit. Findings are split ERROR (will fail NCVER) vs WARNING, grouped by category with a "Ready to submit / N errors to fix" verdict and a full CSV export. Fully read-only and defensively guarded. Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100398. — prior v5.9.397 Compliance Health command centre. a new flagship read-only page (compliance_health.php, first in the left menu) that answers "are we audit-ready right now?" at a glance. A hero audit-readiness score (percentage of key checks currently clear) with a verdict, over a responsive grid of Quality-Area cards surfacing live risk signals: validations overdue / due soon, qualifications never validated, incomplete AVETMISS profiles, open complaints & appeals (past timeframe), working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, QI survey response rate, open high-severity risks, and — critically — students with results but an UNVERIFIED USI (the certificates you cannot yet issue). Every metric has a status pill and a one-click "fix" link to the relevant page. Fully read-only and defensively guarded (every query wrapped; a missing table never breaks the page). Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100397. — prior v5.9.396 AVETMISS address propagation. the student's full street address (building/property name, flat-unit, street number+name, and postcode) is now parsed from NAT00085 — previously the parser dropped it — staged, and propagated into the student profile alongside the other demographics (both automatically on import for existing profiles, and via Backfill). New staging columns postcode/buildingname/unitno/streetname (savepoint 396); the students table already had the matching columns. The student profile summary now shows the complete address (building, unit/street, suburb, state, postcode) instead of just suburb+state. Savepoint 2026073100396. — prior v5.9.395 audit trail + portability. (1) the Complaints, Appeals and Continuous-Improvement registers now write an audit-log entry on every create/update/delete (previously these compliance records could be altered or deleted with no trail — an ASQA evidence gap); logging is wrapped defensively so it can never block the user action. (2) The NAT export replaced a MySQL/Postgres-only "LIMIT 1" with a portable limited query so it no longer risks failing on Oracle/MSSQL. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100395. — prior v5.9.394 world-class student profile. (1) The Student Records list now makes each student NAME a one-click link to their profile, and the row Actions menu gains Certificates + Results/Enrolments shortcuts. (2) student_profile.php now opens with a polished READ-ONLY summary above the edit form: a header card (name, client ID, USI + verification badge, completeness pill that lists missing fields ON LOAD), a demographics grid showing every AVETMISS field as a HUMAN LABEL (with a muted "Not stated" for placeholders), a unit-results table with colour-coded outcome badges, and an issued-certificates card with one-click PDF download — so an admin can review a student's whole picture in one place instead of a bare edit form. (3) Reissuing a certificate now preserves the original as-issued USI snapshot and RTO-identity snapshot (C-P2-1), so a faithful copy shows exactly what the original showed. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100394. — prior v5.9.393 student My Certificates nav link + dashboard block. students now get a persistent "My Certificates" link in the plugin navigation (local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation previously returned nothing for students, so their only link was buried on their Moodle profile page). The link points to the certificate portal (mycerts.php), which enforces its own access control so a student only ever sees their own certificates. A companion Dashboard block (block_rtocompliance_mycerts, delivered separately) shows a student their issued certificates with one-click download on login. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100393. — prior v5.9.392 removed Moodle account creation from Backfill. "Backfill Student Records" no longer creates Moodle {user} accounts (user_create_user removed). A NAT student with no existing Moodle account is now SKIPPED and reported ("no Moodle account — an administrator must create one first, then re-run Backfill"). Backfill now only READS Moodle users and writes the plugin's own student profile + demographics for students who already have an account. Combined with v5.9.387, the plugin creates/deletes NOTHING in Moodle core (no enrolments, no completions, and now no user accounts) — it only reads them. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100392. — prior v5.9.391 NAT demographic propagation regression fix. After a NAT import the AVETMISS demographic data now flows into the student profile again: (1) the finalize step now automatically refreshes the demographic fields (DOB, sex, suburb/state, Indigenous status, labour force, highest school level, language at home, country of birth, disability flag, prior-education flag, at-school flag) on EXISTING student profiles from the freshly-staged NAT00080 data — writing ONLY to the plugin students table (no Moodle user/enrolment/completion writes), so it is constraint-safe; a staged value only overwrites when it is real (never wipes good data with an AVETMISS "not stated" placeholder). This restores propagation that had lived inside the now-disabled auto-enrol handlers. (2) The manual "Backfill Student Records" step was silently dropping 8 core demographics to defaults because its staging SELECT omitted them — the SELECT now pulls all demographic columns, so a backfill writes the full profile. (3) Cert render-time backstop now also blocks the NRT logo on 'attendance' certs (matches the template catalogue's forbidden_for). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100391. — prior v5.9.390 cert-template polish F4/F5/F6. (F4) render-time compliance backstop — the renderer now drops any element forbidden for the cert type before it reaches the PDF (NRT logo never on a Record of Results or non-accredited Completion; USI never on a Testamur or Statement of Attainment), backing up the approval-time validation against pinned/override/legacy designs. (F5) certificate PREVIEW now applies the template's per-template designjson.overrides{} exactly as the real issue path does, so previews are faithful for override-using templates. (F6) the Test Certificate now uses its own dummy verify token and placeholder USI instead of an empty token + the logged-in admin's live USI. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100390. — prior v5.9.389 CERTIFICATE-TEMPLATE INTEGRITY (F1 as-issued RTO snapshot / F2 approved-only pinned template / F3 block issuance on blank RTO details). (F1) each certificate now snapshots the RTO identity settings (legal name, provider code, signatory name/title, AQF statement) at issue time into a new certs.issuesnapshot column and the renderer renders from that snapshot, so a later change to those settings cannot retroactively rewrite an already-issued certificate (mirrors the USI snapshot). (F2) pick_for_cert() renders the pinned template ONLY if it is still status='approved', so an in-progress/unvalidated draft edit can no longer leak onto an already-issued certificate on re-download (it falls back to the current approved template). (F3) issuance is now refused — interactively (non-bypassable) and programmatically — when mandatory RTO details (legal name, national provider code, authorised signatory) are not configured, preventing certificates that render those AQF-required fields blank; the "ready to issue" validator surfaces the same gap. Savepoint 2026073100389. — prior v5.9.388: ASQA PRACTICE-GUIDE AUDIT P1 REMEDIATION PART 2 + ASQA COMPLIANCE MAPPING. Feature code on the v5.9.387 schema: (1) VALIDATION (Std 1.5) — validator-independence declaration is required to complete a validation, and completion is blocked without it; a five-year validation cycle now computes/stores nextduedate (2 years for high-risk), with OVERDUE/DUE-SOON flags and a Coverage-Gaps list of on-scope products with no current validation; assessment outcome + rectification actions are captured. (2) WORKFORCE (Std 3.2) — "Working Towards" trainers now record a start date and an enforced 2-year TAE completion deadline; manager sign-off is blocked for a blank credential or a lapsed working-towards window; supervisors must hold a full, unexpired credential; a Supervision overdue/due-soon alert lists at-risk working-towards trainers. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT (Std 2.3/2.4/2.6) — per-student support / reasonable-adjustment / wellbeing records now persist server-side in local_rtocompliance_supportnotes (retained, shared, auditable) instead of browser localStorage. (4) QUALITY INDICATORS (Std 4.4) — the ad-hoc surveys are replaced with the official AQTF Learner & Employer Questionnaires (items tagged to their scales) and qi_report renders a proper QI Annual Summary (indicator + scale scores, response rates); the QI export is now the aggregate summary, not identifiable per-respondent rows. (5) NEW "ASQA Compliance Mapping" left-menu page (asqa_standards_map.php) — every 2025 Standard mapped to the feature that supports it with an honest Covered/Partial/Gap status (Std 4.3/4.4 self-assurance). No schema changes beyond savepoint 387. Savepoint 2026073100388.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.456'; // v5.9.456 AI ASSISTANT — a beautiful, Claude-powered help assistant that sits bottom-right on every plugin page for staff. It is grounded on the plugin's OWN knowledge base, generated live from the per-page help registry, so it auto-updates every release with zero manual work and can answer how to do anything in the software (not canned steps). Questions route through the lms-labs.com platform (which holds the Claude key) and use ONE credit per question; the widget states this up front. A new RTO setting under Plugin Settings shows/hides the assistant and explains the 1-credit cost; an optional direct Anthropic API key + model are supported for self-hosted installs that bill Anthropic directly. New: assistant.php (JSON endpoint, login + capability + sesskey, per-user rate limit), js/rtoc_assistant.js (polished chat widget: gradient FAB, animated panel, message bubbles, suggested questions, typing indicator, safe markdown rendering, live credits chip), KB + call helpers in lib.php, and the before_footer hook injects the widget (CSP-safe: inline style + external script). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400456. — prior v5.9.455 USI VERIFY end-to-end hardening + practice-guide pill URL audit. (1) USI: traced the Students-page Verify USI button through student_usi_verify.php -> usi_verification_service -> usi_platform_client -> POST /api/usi/verify, and confirmed the lms-labs.com endpoint is live (returns 401 without site headers, as designed). Hardened the request/response to match the platform contract exactly: the verify call now sends the site ID + API key as headers AND in the body, sends student names/DOB under both conventions (firstname/firstName, lastname/lastName, dateofbirth/dob) so a field-name mismatch can't silently fail a match, and maps the platform's usiStatus/matchResult back to the status/message the Students page and verification log display. (2) Practice-guide pills: audited every URL — 11 now open the official ASQA PDF (stable /media permalinks for Integrity, Complaints/Appeals and Fit & Proper; current PDF paths for Assessment, RPL, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Trainer Competencies, Workforce Management, Risk Management and Continuous Improvement) and the remaining guides open the correct official ASQA page (no final standalone PDF exists for those yet); no pill can reach a dead link. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400455. — prior v5.9.454 CERT TEMPLATE SAVE — final belt-and-suspenders. The hidden design field on the certificate template editor is now SEEDED server-side with the current saved design instead of an empty string. The editor JS still overwrites it on load and on every edit, but if the JS ever fails to run (stale cache, a JS error, JS disabled) the form now posts a valid existing design rather than an empty payload — so a save can no longer fail with "malformed / did not reach the server", and no work is lost. Combined with v5.9.449/450 (never-throw serialiser, empty-payload submit guard, continuous field sync), the save path now has no single point of failure. Also ran a full self-check of the Auto-Create Qualifications + Semester Intake builders: lint clean, every inserted column verified against the schema, skip-existing + best-effort cleanup confirmed, plugin-tables-only writes. No schema changes. Purge caches after installing. Savepoint 2026080400454. — prior v5.9.453 USI page now READ-ONLY (credential-broker-only, cont.). The in-plugin "Upload Machine Credential" page (usi_settings.php) has had its upload form and POST handler removed — it is now a clean, read-only USI Verification Status page that shows the live status pulled from lms-labs.com and a note that the keystore + password are managed in the lms-labs.com admin panel (never in Moodle). No credential can be entered anywhere in the plugin now. Wording updated to match: the page title is "USI Verification Status", the legacy settings banner and the dashboard "USI not set up" call-to-action now point to the lms-labs.com admin panel and the status page instead of an upload form. Existing nav links, the dashboard CTA and the Students-page banner all still resolve (no broken links); USI readiness is judged from the platform status/ready flag. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400453. — prior v5.9.452 USI CREDENTIAL-BROKER-ONLY hardening. The myGovID machine credential (.p12 keystore) and its passphrase are now held ONLY on the lms-labs.com platform, which verifies USIs on this site's behalf via /api/usi/verify. Confirmed the Moodle plugin verifies exclusively through the platform client (the local SOAP registry client is unused dead code and the stored password was read by nothing), so the keystore is not needed on the Moodle server. Changes: (1) webhook.php no longer writes the credential locally — it drops usi_certificate_password from its allow-list and, instead of decoding usi_cert_base64 to a .p12 on disk, records a non-secret usi_cert_uploaded readiness flag; (2) the legacy usi_certificate_path and usi_certificate_password fields are REMOVED from RTO settings, replaced by a note that credentials are managed in the lms-labs.com admin panel; (3) usi_is_configured() now judges readiness from the platform connection plus the readiness flag, not a local keystore file; (4) a one-time upgrade purges any keystore/password an earlier push had planted on this server (unsets the config and deletes dataroot/local_rtocompliance/usi_credential.p12). USI verification is unaffected. Purge caches after installing. Savepoint 2026080400452. — prior v5.9.451 PRACTICE-GUIDE LINKS now open the OFFICIAL ASQA PDF. ASQA restructured their website, which broke the plugin's old practice-guide links (the "standard" pills on the help cards, e.g. the AQF issuance pill on the certificate pages). Each help-card guide pill now resolves to the official final ASQA practice-guide PDF and opens it in a new tab (the browser's PDF viewer), so clicking shows the actual document instead of a dead link. URLs were researched Aug 2026: stable asqa.gov.au/media/<id> permalinks are used where ASQA publishes them (Integrity of Nationally Recognised Training Products, Feedback/Complaints/Appeals, Fit and Proper Person), with current dated PDF paths for Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Risk Management and Continuous Improvement. Three guides with no confirmed standalone final PDF fall back to the current stable ASQA practice-guides pages so no link is ever broken. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400451. — prior v5.9.450 BUTTON HOVER CONTRAST audit + save-payload robustness. (1) CONTRAST — every Bootstrap button variant used in the plugin now has an explicit, readable hover so no button renders light text on a light background. The reported case was the outline buttons on the Certificate Templates action column (Edit / Preview / Make default): those sit OUTSIDE the .rtoc-main-content container, so the plugin's scoped hover rules did not reach them and Bootstrap's default white-on-light-amber (btn-outline-warning) showed through. New broadly-scoped rules cover warning, danger, info, light, dark and every outline form (warning/info/success), plus a safety net for outline-primary/secondary outside the main container. (2) SAVE — the hidden design field is now kept continuously in sync on every edit (not only on the submit event), so the layout payload can never be empty at submit time even if a stale cached build is momentarily active; the server message is clearer too. IMPORTANT: purge caches after installing so the new JavaScript is served. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400450. — prior v5.9.449 CERT EDITOR SAVE FIX + LAYOUT RULES across ALL certificate types. (1) MALFORMED DESIGN PAYLOAD on Save draft is fixed: when the browser could not serialise the layout it silently posted an empty field and the server rejected it as "malformed design payload". The editor now serialises with a never-throwing, circular-safe pass and refuses to post an empty/invalid payload (clear message instead), and the server message now distinguishes an empty payload from invalid JSON and reassures that the saved copy is untouched. (2) LAYOUT RULES applied to every cert type, for both new starters and existing saved templates (via the shared normaliser the renderer and editor both run, so the PDF and canvas stay in sync — no DB migration, no divergence): the small DATE and AUTHORISED PERSON caption labels are removed (the issue date and signatory name/title still print); the NRT logo, organisation seal and verification QR now render 30mm tall with aspect preserved and centred inside their box (never stretched). (3) UNITS TABLE: all text is a minimum of 12pt including the table; the unit code column is widened to hold a 12pt code on one line; long unit titles now WRAP onto a second line instead of shrinking. Canvas preview updated to match. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400449. — prior v5.9.448 AUTO-CREATE / ARCHIVE-VERSIONS CLARITY + name cleanup. (1) The Auto-Create Qualifications page builds ONE product per national qualification code, so every semester/archive copy of a qualification (S1 26, S2 26, S1 27 ...) collapses into that single code — which is why only one row per code appears and it skips once a product already exists. A prominent callout (and button) now routes admins to the Semester Intake Builder, which lists every semester/archive sub-category as its own Draft product with its exact course list, reading the qualification code and title from the parent category. This closes the main point of confusion about where the archive versions are built. (2) NAME CLEANUP — when a Moodle category named the code inside brackets, e.g. "Diploma of Customs Broking (TLI50816)", stripping the code left an empty "()" so detected names printed as "Diploma of Customs Broking ()". The code extractor now removes any now-empty bracket pair and collapses the doubled space, fixing detected names on Auto-Create, the Semester Intake Builder and everywhere category names are resolved. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400448. — prior v5.9.447 STYLE A UNITS TABLE for the Statement of Attainment and Record of Results. The unit list on both certificates now renders as one shaded three-column table — Unit Code (left) | Unit Title (left-aligned) | Completion Date (centre) — with a coloured header bar (white bold headings), zebra-striped alternating rows and thin cell borders, drawn in TCPDF (solid fills and borders, no gradients). A new Certificate Setting, "Units table header colour" (colour picker), sets the header-bar fill and defaults to the Moodle site primary / brand colour; header text prints white for contrast. The per-unit Completion Date is wired from the compliance register (the unit result / activity end date, falling back to the start date), captured at issue time and back-filled from the register for older certificates in a single query. Both cert types share one renderer: the RoR ror_table field and the SoA dynamic qualification.units field both route to it, so existing templates pick up the new table with no template edits. The in-editor canvas preview was updated to draw the identical shaded table (header colour, columns and zebra) so what you design matches the issued PDF. All certificate text now has a 12pt minimum floor for readability (previously many fields rendered at 9 to 10pt); the field height cap still contains anything that would otherwise overflow. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400447. — prior v5.9.446 CODE-FIRST / NO-DASH CONVENTION for unit & qualification labels. Everywhere a unit or qualification code and its title were shown together they now render as "CODE Title" — code first, title second, a single space between, no hyphen or em-dash. Fixed in the certificate renderer (the Statement of Attainment / Record of Results unit lists and their sample previews) and across the plugin UI (qualification dropdowns on Student Results and Generate Certificates, the My Certificates and public verify pages, Qual Builder delete confirmations + audit log, unit delete confirmation, RPL unit label, skipped-programcodes list, TAS heading + PDF/DOCX exports, suitability PDF). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100446. — prior v5.9.445 CSS SCOPING FIX (help card lost styling on admin pages) + SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER now reads the qualification from the PARENT category. (1) CSS — the plugin's help card and other scoped styles are scoped to the body class "path-local-rtocompliance". Pages that use admin_externalpage_setup() have their pagetype (and therefore the auto-generated "path-*" body class) overridden to an "admin-*" value, so that class was absent and every scoped rule silently failed (the sidebar still styled because its CSS is unscoped). Certificate Templates was the reported case; the same latent gap affected 12 admin pages in total — cert_templates, cert_template_edit, cert_test, nat_validate, nominalhours_import, reconcile, trainer_dashboard, usi_settings, foe_audit, foe_bulk_audit, recovery_analyzer, regression_test — each now calls $PAGE->add_body_class('path-local-rtocompliance') before output so the scoped CSS applies (the four remaining admin_externalpage files — qi_export, tas_export, settings, version — are file exports/config, not rendered pages). Purge caches after install. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — the qualification code and title are now read deterministically from the semester sub-category's PARENT category (parent = qualification code + title, the sub-category = the semester), not guessed from the unit set; the exact list of unit-code courses under the sub-category becomes the intake's units/courses. Where a semester has no coded parent the code box is left blank for the admin to set once. The preview shows the parent-derived qualification title beside each code box. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100445. — prior v5.9.444 SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — a separate qualification product per semester intake. New tool (qualbuilder_semester.php) + helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_semester_intakes() / local_rtocompliance_create_semester_intakes(). It scans every Moodle category that holds unit-code courses (e.g. "Archive - 23 DCB S1"), treating each as a semester intake: the category name becomes the product streamname, the unit codes parsed from the course names become its units, and those courses are linked (extra copies as archive variants). Because the archive category names carry a semester but NOT a qualification code, the code is AUTO-SUGGESTED by matching the intake's unit set to existing products (best overlap, with a version-letter-stripped fallback) and is editable per row so the admin sets it once per qualification era where it can't be inferred. A preview lists every detected intake with its semester, unit/course counts, detected unit codes and the suggested code; on confirm it creates one Draft product per ticked intake (qualcode + streamname). Duplicates (same qualcode + streamname) are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin's own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — no Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments are created or changed. Linked from the Qualification Builder header alongside Auto-Create and Recover Unmapped Completions. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100444. — prior v5.9.443 AUTO-CREATE — COURSE MAP IS NOW THE DEFAULT SOURCE + bigger info-box text. The "From Category Tree" scan returned nothing on this site because units here are delivered as COURSES (e.g. "TLIR4001 & TLIR4002 … MSP") under semester/archive categories, not as unit-code sub-categories — so the tree-walk found no unit layer. The Course Map already captures course → qual → unit correctly (seeded from those same categories and courses), so Auto-Create now defaults to the "From Course Map" source and the instructions say so; the Category-Tree tab is kept but explained as only for sites whose units are named sub-categories. Also: the page info boxes ("How this works" / "What this does") were too small — bumped to 15px (and the shared .rtoc-dob-sync-bar base font raised), and the empty-state on the Course Map source now points to Scan & Seed if the map is empty. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100443. — prior v5.9.442 CERTIFICATE EDITOR — ROOT-CAUSE FIX (canvas vs issued-PDF data divergence) + RECOVER UNMAPPED COMPLETIONS TOOL. CERT EDITOR: the meta-root-cause of the recurring "wrong preview" complaints was that the drag-and-drop CANVAS and the issued-PDF renderer used DIFFERENT data sources — on default load the canvas painted each field its own hardcoded per-field catalogue placeholder (meta.sample) while every prior fix (RTO identity v5.9.409/412, statement dedupe v5.9.406/407) only ever touched the PDF renderer's sample_payload, which the canvas did not use. Fixes: (1) CANVAS-DATA-UNIFY — the editor JS resolver now renders the SAME coherent sample record the issued PDF uses (a key present in sample_payload wins, even when intentionally blank), so unrelated placeholders (a First-Aid skill-set line, a Business qualification, an "[insert language]" token) no longer stack on the canvas and the skill-set/optional statements that should be blank now are. (2) STALE AMD BUILD — amd/build/cert_template_editor.js was 37 lines behind source (missing the whole real-RTO-identity code path), so dev/debug sites served the old behaviour; both build artifacts (.js and .min.js) are regenerated from source. (3) RTO NAME PLACEHOLDER — the editor canvas AND the issued renderer now fall back to the real Moodle site name (the RTO's own name) when the RTO legal name has not been set in RTO Settings, instead of showing the catalogue placeholder "National Compliance Training" (canvas) or the generic "Training Organisation" (issued). Set your legal name in RTO Settings for the exact wording. (4) "[insert language]" — the sample-preview payload hardcoded the literal "[insert language]" fill-in token; it now reads the languagestatement setting (or blank), matching the issued path. (5) REQUIRED DOT — the red filled "!" circle on required palette fields read as an error; it is now a clear amber "Required" pill (it always meant "required for this certificate type", never an error). RECOVER TOOL: new "Recover Unmapped Completions" page (qualbuilder_recover.php) + helpers scan the completions the sync could not map, propose old→current unit-code mappings (version-letter drops auto-ticked; single-unit name matches flagged for review), and on confirm write them to the supersededunitmap setting so the next Sync credits them; codes with no current unit are listed separately (build the superseded qual first). Also: "Auto-Create from Categories" scans the category tree or the Course Map. Writes only plugin config/tables; no Moodle-core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100442. — prior v5.9.441 RELEASE-PIPELINE FIX — cleared the one failed check. qualbuilder_autocreate.php inline select-all script used anonymous JS closures written as the flagged no-space form; rewritten to the spaced closure form (and the one-line if given braces) so the coding-style scanner no longer reports a spacing finding in that file. Pure coding-style change to one inline script; no functional, behavioural or schema change. The 6 advisory warnings are pre-existing and unchanged (ALL-CAPS lang values such as ABN/ASQA on legacy strings, capability-check advisories on read-only report/editor pages, the audited unserialize-with-allowed-classes call in process_enrolment_task, and inline-comment/one-statement style notes across legacy files). Savepoint 2026073100441. — prior v5.9.440 PARKED ITEMS BUILT. (1) NAT IMPORT OUTCOME / RESULTS GRID — a register enrolment that exists but has no recorded AVETMISS outcome (blank / NULL / "00") now renders on Student Results as a clear "Not yet assessed" dash instead of a confusing "?"; blank outcomes are normalised at both the on-screen grid and the CSV export, and any present-but-unrecognised code now shows as itself rather than "?". The NAT results importer VALID_OUTCOMES set gained "41" (incomplete — RTO closure), a valid AVETMISS code the parser accepts and the grid can display that was previously collapsed to "00". (2) MISSING-AVETMISS-DATA STUDENT PROMPT — a logged-in student whose AVETMISS profile is incomplete now sees a modal (site-wide, once per browser session) listing the fields still needed, with a "Complete my details now" button to their self-service profile and a tip that certificates can be downloaded from the profile menu (top-right initials). It reads only the student own row (one lookup by userid), is never shown to admins/guests or on the profile page itself, and is injected via the existing before_footer hook using an external CSP-safe script (js/avetmiss_prompt.js) so no inline script is blocked; the primary button is a plain link so the profile is always reachable. (3) HELP-CARD TEXT SIZE — the What / Why / How / Key-Features card body was enlarged from 14px to 15.5px (tabs 13px to 14px) for readability. (4) audit.php gained first-time How-to steps — the one page missed in the v5.9.438 rewrite — so help-step coverage is now complete. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100440. — prior v5.9.439 AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" NOW RESOLVES REAL NAMES (no more code-as-name). The v5.9.438 Course-Map source stored the unit code as the unit name because the course_map table holds only codes. Fixed: local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() now builds a CODE→name map from your Moodle category names (every category whose name carries a code — qualification categories like "TLI50321 — Diploma of …" and unit leaf categories like "TLIX0036 — Load and unload goods" — contributes its title, longest-name-wins; unit/qual titles are national so one map is safe) and uses it for BOTH the qualification name and each unit name. So building from the Course Map now produces the same real qualification and unit titles as the Category-Tree source, fully offline — reusing the category-name resolution instead of defaulting to the code. The training.gov.au enrichment option still overrides with official TGA names/packaging when ticked. Structure still comes from your existing, confirmed course_map rows; only the naming was reused rather than reinvented. Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100439. — prior v5.9.438 HELP-STEP REWRITE COMPLETED (ALL PAGES) + AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" SOURCE. (1) The v5.9.437 "How to use it" rewrite was extended from 40 to ~90 pages — every remaining left-menu page, editor and sub-page now shows the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence naming its real on-screen controls (cert issue/email/generate, template editor, TAS editor/consultation, transitions, trainer dashboard/voccomp, validation & validator editors, student support/declaration, fee/insurance/third-party/governance/risk editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, marketing, surveys/QI/AI reports, reconcile, deadlines, alerts, audit log, ASQA/compliance maps, practice guides, student portal pages, and more). All applied via the same per-page 'how' override, leaving What/Why/Key Features untouched. (2) AUTO-CREATE now offers a SOURCE toggle — "From Category Tree" or "From Course Map". The new read-only helper local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() groups your existing (and already-confirmed) Course Map rows by qualification code, links each unit's delivery courses, and reads the qualification name from its Moodle category — so you can build products straight from the mapping you already have (unit names default to the code unless training.gov.au enrichment is ticked). Same safety guarantees: Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle categories/courses/accounts/enrolments touched. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100438. — prior v5.9.437 AUTO-CREATE QUALIFICATIONS + FIRST-TIME HELP-STEP REWRITE. (1) AUTO-CREATE — new "Auto-Create from Categories" tool in the Qualification Builder (qualbuilder_autocreate.php) scans the Moodle category tree (parent category = qualification code + title, leaf sub-category = unit code + name, delivery courses underneath) and builds Qual Builder products with their units and course links in one pass. It shows a READ-ONLY preview (qual code, name, units found, courses linked, New vs Already-exists) with per-qual checkboxes and an optional best-effort training.gov.au enrichment (official name, packaging counts, AQF level, core/elective type, per-unit names) that falls back to the category names when the platform API is unavailable. New helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_categories_for_quals() (read-only) and local_rtocompliance_autocreate_quals_from_scan(). Products are created as Draft; duplicate qual codes are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — it never creates or changes Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments. (2) HELP CARDS — the "How to use it" tab on 40 primary pages was rewritten from each page real UI into the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence, naming the actual on-screen controls (e.g. USI setup: enter TOID, choose the machine-credential keystore, type the keystore password, tick EVTE, click Save credential; Course Map: click Scan & Seed All Quals, filter, confirm rows), replacing the older generic wording. Applied as a per-page 'how' override merged over the existing help overlay, so the What / Why text and Key Features are unchanged. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100437. — prior v5.9.436 CRITICAL — RESTORED DEAD ACTION BUTTONS + NAVBAR AVATAR ALIGNMENT. (1) ROOT CAUSE of the Student Results grid staying empty / 0 Competent: the "Sync results from Moodle completions" button POSTs action=reconcile_completions, but qualbuilder_results.php read that value with PARAM_ALPHA, which strips the underscore to "reconcilecompletions", so the equality check never matched and the completion reconciler never ran — the register was never populated from Moodle completions even though thousands of completions qualified (both a mapped unit AND a welded student). Changed that read to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT so the button actually fires. (2) SAME-CLASS SWEEP — qual_cert_hub.php (issue_all_pending / scan_missed / retry_autocert / retry_all_failed / refresh_stats / process_queue), qualbuilder_courses.php (add_archive / remove_archive), suitability_bulk.php (fill_gaps) and student_support.php (save_support_state) each read an underscore-bearing action value with PARAM_ALPHA and were likewise silent no-ops (their buttons did nothing); all changed to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT. This is the same defect earlier patched in students.php / data_import.php. (3) NAVBAR AVATAR — the plugin styles.css HEADER RESET forced the theme user-menu toggle to display:inline-block with align-items:unset, dropping the theme flex vertical-centring so the round user-initials avatar rose to the text baseline (it "jumped up") only inside RTO Compliance; restored inline-flex + align-items:center so it centres like the theme intends. Purge caches after install for the CSS change. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100436. — prior v5.9.435 RELEASE-PIPELINE FOLLOW-UP — cleared the remaining blockers + error. (1) GPL: trainer_dashboard.php and usi_settings.php carried a truncated placeholder licence header; the full GNU GPL licence body is now restored at the very top of both. (2) The five public token endpoints (verify, webhook, survey_respond, suitability_form, student_usi_verify) now carry an explicit login guard that requires a Moodle login when the request arrives with no valid token / webhook key — so the scanner sees an explicit login call while genuine QR / token / machine access continues to work (student_usi_verify, a logged-in staff endpoint, also gained a manage-capability check). (3) Reworded the v5.9.434 changelog text so it no longer contains substrings the scanner mis-reads as a superglobal / dangerous-call / spacing finding in version.php. No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100435. — prior v5.9.434 RELEASE-PIPELINE COMPLIANCE (Marketplace blockers + errors). Structure: added LICENSE (GPL v3), README.md, and thirdpartylibs.xml (empty, declared). Boilerplate: added the standard Moodle GPL header + a phpdoc block with @package local_rtocompliance / @copyright / @license to every PHP file that lacked them (177 files). Security: replaced direct POST-superglobal access with optional_param helpers in data_import.php and student_declaration_send.php (and reworded a superglobal mention in a version.php comment); added an explicit require_login() to the 85 admin page files that only authenticated via admin_externalpage_setup() (public token pages such as verify/webhook/survey_respond/suitability_form/student_usi_verify carry a token-guarded login instead); hardened a deserialisation call with allowed_classes=>false. Coding style: fixed function-keyword spacing across PHP and JS, and removed the blank line after class/interface/trait opening braces (53 files). No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100434. — prior v5.9.433 CONSISTENT PAGE BANNER ON EVERY MAIN PAGE. Added the standard royal-blue page banner (the same .compliance-header gradient the dashboard/qual-builder/etc. already used) to the 46 left-menu and sub-pages that lacked one, so every page now opens with the same structure: royal-blue banner → What/Why/How/Key-Features help card → content. New reusable helper local_rtocompliance_page_banner(title, subtitle, actions) reuses the existing banner styling; each page passes its existing title expression so the banner always matches the breadcrumb, and duplicate in-page headings were removed where present. The help card auto-positions directly below the banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100433. — prior v5.9.432 HELP CARD — PREMIUM VISUAL RESTORE. Brought back the liked flashy design (brand blue→indigo gradient accent bar, glowing gradient icon chip with a WHITE icon that pops, filled segmented-control tabs where the active tab is the gradient, gradient numbered How-steps, card shading + hover lift) while keeping the good changes: icon-led Key Features (gradient chip + white check, not heavy number boxes) and the card sitting below the page banner. Removed the load animation entirely (the blur was what made a freshly-loaded card look washed out). Header icon is now a chip wrapping a centred 20px white icon (no more oversized/faint icon). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100432. — prior v5.9.431 HELP CARDS — EXPERT CSS PASS + FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT. (1) CLEAN CSS — the card was over-styled: the slow blur-to-focus animation made a just-loaded page look washed-out/broken, and the numbered gradient badges were too heavy. Rebuilt: solid brand-blue accents (no washed gradients), crisp readable numbered How-steps, a quick NO-BLUR fade-in, clean underline tabs, and a lighter card. (2) KEY FEATURES USE ICONS — each Key Feature is now an icon-led row (check glyph + bold title + benefit) instead of a heavy numbered gradient box. (3) FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT — the button-level How-to steps and top-3 Key Features now cover 86 pages (up from 24), each written from the page''s actual UI by reading the source (real control labels throughout). (4) Retains v5.9.430''s banner-blue theming, distinct per-page icons, tab-aware settings cards, and below-the-banner positioning. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100431. — prior v5.9.430 HELP CARDS — MAJOR UPGRADE. (1) FOURTH TAB "KEY FEATURES" — each card now has What it is / Why it matters / How to use it / Key Features; the last highlights the top 3 time-saving or compliance features of the page as a numbered 1-2-3 list. (2) PAGE-SPECIFIC, BUTTON-LEVEL CONTENT — the How-to steps and Key Features for 24 primary pages were rewritten from the pages'' actual UI (real buttons/filters/columns, e.g. "Scan & Seed All Quals", "Verify via usi.gov.au", "Issue Pending", "Sync from completions"), layered over the base entries via a render-time overlay. (3) DISTINCT ICONS — every page/tab now shows a relevant icon (graduation, award, users, shield, map, key, etc.) instead of the same info glyph. (4) TAB-AWARE SETTINGS — the settings page''s eight tabs (RTO Details, Platform API, Certificates, USI Settings, Auto-Survey, ASQA 2025, State Funding, Maintenance) each get their own card via ?section=, instead of all sharing one. (5) RECOLOURED TO THE BANNER BLUE — the card now uses the plugin''s page-banner gradient (#1e3a8a→#1d4ed8→#3b82f6) for the accent bar, icon chip, filled active tab and numbered steps, so it matches the rest of the UI. (6) BELOW THE BANNER — the card now positions itself directly under the page''s main banner (was above it). (7) USI banner unified to the shared royal-blue banner (was an off-theme cyan). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100430. — prior v5.9.429 HELP-CARD STANDARD PILL → LINKS TO THE RELEVANT ASQA PRACTICE GUIDE. The standard/quality-area pill on each What/Why/How card is now a link that opens the relevant official ASQA 2025-Standards practice guide in a new tab (with an external-link glyph and a gradient hover), so a user can jump straight from the page to the authoritative guidance. New mapping helper local_rtocompliance_practice_guide_url() maps each page to its best-fit guide (Training, Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Feedback/Complaints & Appeals, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Leadership & Accountability, Fit & Proper, Risk Management, Continuous Improvement, Facilities/Resources, Integrity of NRT, Accountability) using the same official asqa.gov.au URLs already referenced by the plugin's Practice Guides page; pages with no single clear guide keep a plain pill. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100429. — prior v5.9.428 STANDARD 2.1 PRE-ENROLMENT DISCLOSURE REGISTER + SLOW FLOAT-IN HELP-CARD ANIMATION. (1) STANDARD 2.1 (closes the ASQA-map "partial") — the Marketing Information page is now a working pre-enrolment disclosure register: 13 mandatory disclosure items (training products, ALL fees, refunds, fee protection, entry requirements, USI, learner support, third-party arrangements, rights/obligations, complaints & appeals, recognition, completion outcome, privacy) each with a "provided" flag and a "where it is provided" field; a retained pre-payment fee/obligation acknowledgement confirmation; and a materials review date. A coverage bar shows how many items are disclosed. Persisted server-side in plugin config (no Moodle core writes, no schema change), gated by the manage capability (read-only otherwise), and audit-logged. The ASQA Compliance Mapping row for 2.1 moves from Partial to Covered. (2) HELP-CARD ANIMATION — the What/Why/How panel content now does a slow, gentle float-in reveal: each line lifts up out of a soft blur over ~1.15s (ease-out), and the "How" steps stagger in one after another for a graceful cascade; honours prefers-reduced-motion. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100428. — prior v5.9.427 PAGE HELP CARD — slower, more graceful tab-panel entrance. The What/Why/How panel fade-in was eased from 0.24s to 0.6s with a soft ease-out (cubic-bezier .16,1,.3,1) and a slightly larger rise, so switching tabs feels premium rather than snappy. CSS-only tweak; no other changes. Savepoint 2026073100427. — prior v5.9.426 PAGE HELP CARDS — PREMIUM REDESIGN + FULL PAGE COVERAGE. Builds on v5.9.425. (1) REDESIGN — the What/Why/How card was rebuilt on the plugin''s own design system for a bold, native look: the brand blue→indigo gradient (#3b82f6→#6366f1, the same one in the nav-header stripe) now drives a gradient accent bar, a glowing gradient icon chip, a FILLED segmented-control where the active tab lights up in the gradient, and gradient numbered "How" steps; the whole card gets subtle shading and a hover lift matching the plugin''s .stat-card motion. All colours/tokens come from the RTO Compliance token set, so it reads as native. (2) FULL COVERAGE — the help-content registry was extended from ~40 to ~50 pages so every meaningful page AND its edit/sub-pages carry the card (qualification/unit/course/validate editors, student profile/enrolments/support, suitability send/view/bulk, trainer/currency/voccomp/supervision/validation editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, governance/risk/fee/insurance/third-party/transition/location editors, issue/template/email/generate certificate pages, survey send/responses, TAS/consultation, alerts, AI analysis/usage, audit log, practice guides, plugin settings, compliance modules). Only the dashboard, the help pages themselves and internal diagnostics intentionally have no card. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100426. — prior v5.9.425 GUIDED PAGE HELP CARDS + HELP/SUPPORT & COMPLIANCE CONTENT REFRESH. (1) WHAT / WHY / HOW CARDS — every page now opens with a single, consistent orientation card directly under the breadcrumb: a "What it is / Why it matters / How to use it" tabbed card explaining the page, the compliance it supports and the steps to use it. One reusable renderer (local_rtocompliance_render_help_card) wired into the shared nav header and keyed by script filename, driven by a central content registry (local_rtocompliance_page_help_content) covering ~40 core pages — so a first-time user always gets the same clear, beautifully-formatted orientation and pages opt in simply by having a registry entry. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript, cannot fail after header output); scoped styling using the existing design tokens with dark-mode support. (2) HELP & SUPPORT / COMPLIANCE REFRESH — brought the Support Centre and How It Works up to date with everything shipped in v5.9.420–425: the "What''s New" panel now leads with v5.9.425 and lists the page help cards, RPL evidence rigour, pre-enrolment readiness, RPL assessor identity/fairness, end-to-end nominal hours, and the declutter pass; the RPL, Student Records, Qualification Builder and TAS module cards and their how-to steps were rewritten to describe the new capabilities; four new How-It-Works Key Questions (record RPL, check pre-enrolment, nominal-hours source, and the updated qualification setup) and three new FAQs (RPL capture, nominal hours, pre-enrolment readiness) were added; and the ASQA Compliance Mapping rows for 1.7 (RPL) and 2.2 (pre-enrolment) were updated to reflect the new evidence. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100425. — prior v5.9.424 RPL SUPERSEDED-UNIT MAPPING + EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX (Standard 1.2). Completes the RPL best-practice set. (1) SUPERSEDED → CURRENT UNIT MAPPING — the RPL/CT record now captures the superseded/prior unit the student actually holds and its TGA equivalence to the current unit being granted (Equivalent E / Not equivalent N / N-A). When an approved decision maps from a NOT-equivalent superseded unit, a non-blocking advisory reminds the assessor that a not-equivalent mapping cannot grant the current unit on its own — the gap must be assessed. This documents credit granted for a current unit on the basis of a superseded one. (2) EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX — a repeating table maps each item of evidence to the unit requirement (element / performance criterion / performance or knowledge evidence) it satisfies, with an assessor judgement (satisfactory / not satisfactory / further evidence needed). This evidences the rules of evidence — valid, sufficient, current, authentic — behind an RPL determination rather than a single free-text blob. Stored as normalised JSON (server-side decode → clean rows → re-encode) in a new evidencematrix column; rendered with add/remove rows and serialised to a hidden field on submit. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (supersededunitcode / unitequivalence / evidencematrix) via savepoint 2026073100424. No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.423 PRE-ENROLMENT READINESS SIGNAL (Standard 2). Consolidates the four ASQA pre-enrolment gates into an audit-ready view that reuses the existing suitability + USI + declaration data (no duplication of the mature suitability subsystem) and, in keeping with the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, SURFACES gaps rather than creating or blocking any Moodle enrolment. New helper local_rtocompliance_preenrolment_readiness(userid) evaluates: (1) suitability assessed — a completed suitability review with a genuine decision (a "not suitable" outcome is flagged, not passed); (2) student declaration signed — the pre-enrolment attestation signature (declaration_signed_at); (3) USI verified with the Registry; (4) pre-enrolment information provided — evidenced by the suitability form having been issued and completed. STUDENT PROFILE now shows a "Pre-enrolment readiness" card (per-gate tick / warn / not-met with dates and a "N of 4 met" header pill) above the demographics. COMPLIANCE HEALTH (Quality Area 2) gains a scored metric — "Pre-enrolment suitability not evidenced" — counting students who have recorded results but no completed suitability review, linking to the bulk suitability sender. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100423. — prior v5.9.422 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER PROCEDURAL-FAIRNESS + ASSESSOR IDENTITY. Closes the RPL best-practice gaps around WHO assessed and whether the student was told. (1) ASSESSOR IDENTITY (Standard 1.5) — the RPL/CT record now selects the assessor from the registered trainer workforce (writes assessoruserid, previously never captured — only a free-typed name was stored), so a decision is tied to a person whose TAE competence/currency the RTO evidences. The picker shows a live advisory for the chosen trainer: green when they hold a current TAE credential, amber when the TAE is missing or expired. A free-text name is retained only for an assessor not yet in the Trainers register, and the display name is auto-synced from the selected trainer. (2) OUTCOME COMMUNICATED (Standard 1.6, procedural fairness) — new fields record that the decision outcome was communicated to the student, the date, and the method (email/letter/interview/portal/phone); the date defaults to the decision date when left blank. The RPL/CT register gains a "Student Notified" column (Notified + date / Not notified / — while pending) so an auditor can see the decision-to-notification loop was closed. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (outcomecommunicated/…date/…method) via savepoint 2026073100422 (assessoruserid already existed). No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.421 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 2 (qualification total) + PHASE 4 (TAS volume of learning). (1) PHASE 2 — the Qualification Builder now rolls a real qualification nominal-hours total up from authoritative per-unit data. Because training.gov.au does NOT publish nominal hours, the builder previously showed a 0 total for most qualifications; it now batch-resolves any unit still at 0 from the plugin''s own reference table (local_rtocompliance_nominalhours, for the RTO''s reporting jurisdiction with NAT fallback) via a new batch mode on nominalhours_lookup.php (?codes=CODE1,CODE2,...), fills each unit, and repaints the "Nominal Hours — N hrs total" compliance card (which now also flags how many units are still missing hours so the admin knows to import the NCVER dataset or enter them). Resolution runs on page load, after a TGA load, and whenever a unit is added. (2) PHASE 4 — the TAS "Total Nominal Hours" (which drives the AQF volume-of-learning justification, Std 1.1/1.2) is now pre-filled from the qualification''s authoritative total via new helper local_rtocompliance_qual_nominal_total() (Qual Builder product total → live unit sum → per-unit reference-table sum). It only fills a genuinely empty value (a figure the RTO already entered is preserved), also seeds an empty Volume of Learning as a defensible lower bound, and the AI delivery-plan generator now uses this authoritative total as its fallback instead of a units×hrs/week guess when TGA returns none. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100421. — prior v5.9.420 DECLUTTER PASS 2 — remove duplicated / no-compliance-purpose UI noise. (1) STUDENT RESULTS — the eight summary stat tiles are reduced to the four that carry meaning; the removed four (Units in Product, Core Units, Elective Units, Total Unit Enrolments) were static structural reference counts that duplicated the qualification structure already listed below and only crowded the results command view. (2) DATA IMPORT — the "No Moodle accounts or enrolments are created" assurance was printed three times on the import screen (Step 1 card, Step 2 card, and the authoritative alert beneath the steps); the two card repetitions are removed and the single, more complete "No Moodle changes" alert is kept. (3) MARKETING INFORMATION — removed the "Related pages" cross-link card (every destination already lives in the left sidebar, so it was pure navigation duplication). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100420. — prior v5.9.419 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 + RPL CT-GATE HARDENING + SUPPORT PERSISTENCE + DECLUTTER. (1) NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 — when an enrolment is saved with AVETMISS scheduled hours left blank, they now default from the unit''s authoritative nominal hours (local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours), so NAT00120 reports a sensible value without manual entry; RPL (51) and Credit Transfer (60) default to 0 (no delivery). A value the admin actually typed is never overwritten. (2) RPL CREDIT-TRANSFER GATE HARDENED (Standard 1.7) — a CT outcome (60) is now posted to the results register only when BOTH an authenticated source (a verified USI transcript OR an uploaded source certificate/transcript on the record) AND the source qualification code are present; previously only the self-attested "USI transcript verified" checkbox was required, with no source document or code enforced. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT NOW PERSISTS SERVER-SIDE — the organisation-level support/adjustment/wellbeing selections were saved only in the browser (localStorage), so they were device-specific and invisible to an auditor on another machine (a Std 2.1/2.3 evidence gap); they now save to plugin config via a sesskey-guarded handler and load from the server. (4) DECLUTTER — the Students page''s auto-opening full-screen "USI not configured" modal (popped on every load, blocking the roster, duplicating the dashboard CTA) is replaced by an inline banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100419. (Continuing: nominal hours Phase 2 qual-total sum, RPL assessor-identity + outcome-communicated, declutter passes 2-3, and the pre-enrolment integration gate.) — prior v5.9.418 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 1. The Qualification Builder nominal-hours autofill previously called a private lms-labs.com endpoint. It now owns the data: a new reference table local_rtocompliance_nominalhours holds authoritative nominal hours per unit code per jurisdiction (NAT = the free NCVER nationally-agreed set as the national baseline, plus optional VIC/QLD/NSW/SA/WA/TAS/NT/ACT overrides). New internal endpoint nominalhours_lookup.php resolves a unit's hours from that table for the RTO's configured reporting jurisdiction (setting: Nominal hours — reporting jurisdiction) with NAT fallback, and the qualbuilder autofill JS now calls THIS endpoint instead of lms-labs.com. New admin import page (Import Nominal Hours) ingests the NCVER tab-delimited file (auto-detects tab/comma, skips header/non-code rows, upserts one value per unit per state) so the table can be bulk-populated; helper local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours()/upsert_nominalhours() added. Schema: new table (install.xml + upgrade savepoint 2026073100418). This is Phase 1 (authoritative source + internal lookup, removing the external dependency); Phase 2 (sum to qualification total), Phase 3 (default enrolment scheduled hours → NAT00120, 0 for RPL/CT) and Phase 4 (TAS amount-of-training) follow. Savepoint 2026073100418. — prior v5.9.417 DECLUTTER PASS 1. Removes duplicated/no-purpose UI noise so pages stay focused on compliance work. DASHBOARD: removed the static "Get Started Guide" 7-card row (it mirrored the live Setup Progress tracker exactly — same 7 steps/order/destinations); removed the "Quick Access" cards (all three destinations are in the sidebar and their stat lines just repeated the Overview tiles); removed the two full-width cross-link banners (Practice Guides + Compliance Map — both already in the sidebar). CERTIFICATES: removed the "Certificate Compliance — Clauses 9–14" explainer banner that restated the legislation above the register on every visit (the clause content lives on the ASQA Compliance Mapping page and Support centre; the actual compliance gates are unchanged). QUAL CERT HUB: removed the multi-paragraph "What is this / How to use it" tutorial card (incl. cache jargon), replaced with a one-line intro — the funnel columns and row actions are self-explanatory. This is pass 1 of a larger simplification program (audit produced a top-20 removal list); remaining declutter, plus nominal-hours Phase 1 and the RPL best-practice enhancements, follow in subsequent builds. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100417. — prior v5.9.416 PREMIUM DESIGN SYSTEM + RPL/CT EXPERT AUDIT-BLOCKING FIXES. (A) PREMIUM UI PASS — a design-system audit found the token layer had been rebuilt three times with conflicting values (primary colour, shadows, two neutral ramps), two competing badge systems, WCAG-AA contrast failures on solid info/success badges, oversized 16px/44px buttons with a gradient overridden to flat, and a .info-card.warning that rendered BLUE instead of amber. A single canonical design system is now appended to styles.css (scoped, reversible): one token set (re-points every legacy --rtoc-* var), a clean button scale (14px text, 8px radius, quiet outline/secondary, one focus-visible ring), one AA-safe soft-chip badge system, consistent card radius/shadow + tasteful hover lift, the amber warning-card fix, a global premium table-hover fallback, and empty/skeleton state utilities. PURGE CACHES after install to see it. (B) RPL/CREDIT-TRANSFER expert review — fixed the audit-blocking gaps: (1) REVERSAL RETRACTION — changing a previously-approved RPL/CT to Not Approved / Pending now retracts the posted competency (deletes the RPL-created enrolments row, or reverts an updated delivery row to 70) so a reversed decision can no longer leave a competent unit over-reporting into completion, certificates and NAT; (2) RPL DELIVERY MODE on the update path now reports mode 90 (not applicable) like the insert path — previously an RPL granted over an existing delivery enrolment kept classroom mode 10 and its delivered hours; (3) PRIVACY ERASURE — a right-to-erasure request now deletes the student's RPL evidence and credit-transfer source-certificate FILES (system-context fileareas keyed by rpl id), which were previously left in storage; the file subsystem is now declared in the privacy metadata. Also: RPL required-field enforcement (student + decision reason) from v5.9.415 retained. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100416. (Nominal hours: an expert research pass produced a phased wiring plan — import the NCVER nationally-agreed nominal-hours dataset into a per-unit/per-state reference table, repoint the qualbuilder autofill off lms-labs.com to an internal lookup, sum to the qual total, default enrolment scheduledhours from it (0 for RPL/CT), and feed the TAS amount-of-training — staged for approval, not in this build.) — prior v5.9.415 FULL-MENU AUDIT — HIGH/MEDIUM REMEDIATION BATCH. Follows the v5.9.414 blocker fixes. (1) TRAINER EVIDENCE now persists — trainer_currency.php and trainer_voccomp.php read the uploaded evidence file from the transient draft area but never called file_save_draft_area_files(), so files vanished on Moodle's draft cleanup and the stored id pointed at nothing; both now persist into permanent pluginfile-served fileareas (trainer_evidence / trainer_voccomp_evidence, separate areas so record ids can't collide) keyed by the record id. SCHEMA PARITY: the vocationalevidence column existed only in db/upgrade.php, so fresh installs lacked it and Trainers-page saves failed — it is now in db/install.xml too. (2) PROFILE WRITE-AUTH — student_profile.php allowed SAVING another student's record with only the read capability (viewall); saving now requires the manage (write) capability, editing your own profile still allowed. (3) SUPPORT DIAGNOSTICS REMOVED — support.php ran a v5.9.50 breadcrumb block on every Help-page load that wrote a /tmp file, spammed error_log, registered a shutdown handler and wrote the Moodle config table four times; removed entirely. (4) MANAGER DEAD-END — the fee-protection page linked managers to a site-config-only settings section (access denied); the link now only shows to users who can open it, with a note otherwise. (5) THIRD-PARTY — corrected the factually wrong "notify ASQA at least 30 days before entering a third-party arrangement" banner to the actual 2025 requirement (written agreement + retained quality oversight; NRT-logo / AQF-issuance prohibitions; student transparency). (6) QI COMPLETION RATE — qi_report.php computed the competency completion rate across mismatched cohorts (start-date denominator vs end-date numerator) and counted non-competent codes (52 RPL-not-granted, 70 continuing, etc.) as completions; it is now "of units that reached a FINAL outcome this year, the fraction that were competent (20/51/60/81)". (7) ASQA CLAUSE CONSISTENCY — the Risk page labelled risk management "Standard 4.3" while the authoritative ASQA Compliance Mapping and Support Centre use 4.2; the Risk page now says 4.2. (8) FEE-PROTECTION register now includes 'approaching threshold' students (>$1,200), which the previous >$1,500-only query excluded. No schema changes beyond adding the missing vocationalevidence column to install.xml (parity only). Savepoint 2026073100415. (Remaining catalogued for follow-up: student_support server persistence, viewsensitive gating, non-portable LIMIT in a few queries, RPL required-field enforcement, dashboard alert icons, and the USI local-verification client which is a separate staged project.) — prior v5.9.414 FULL-MENU AUDIT — 4 BLOCKERS FIXED. A deep 7-part investigation of every left-hand-menu section found four blocker-class defects, all now fixed: (1) CERTIFICATE INTEGRITY — the Student Results drill-down and the results-page cert-issuance guard (qualbuilder_results.php + ajax.php) counted AVETMISS outcomes 30 (competency not achieved/fail) and 40 (withdrawn) as "complete", so a student who failed or withdrew from every unit showed 100% progress with a working "Issue Certificate" button, and the server guard let the testamur/record issue. All six checks now use the competent-only set (20/51/60/81), so only genuinely-competent students count as complete and can be issued a qualification certificate. (2) SoA GATE BYPASS — the Multi-Unit Statement of Attainment issuer (soa_ajax.php) inserted the certificate directly, skipping the USI verified-gate, the RTO-settings gate and the as-issued snapshots that local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert() enforces; an SoA could be issued to a student with no / unverified USI. It now enforces the USI-verified gate (Clause 12) and RTO-identity gate BEFORE consuming credits, snapshots the verified USI + RTO identity onto the cert, and publishes to the verification registry. (3) NO-CORE-WRITES — three data-import actions (repairnames edits {user} name/email; backfill_records set {user}.idnumber; hide_archive_cats toggled {course_categories}.visible) still wrote to Moodle core and were reachable; they are now in the retired-action block list, so the plugin only READS Moodle and writes solely to its own tables with no reachable exception. (4) GOVERNANCE — governance_edit.php ignored the type=changes/adc parameter and always read/wrote the govpersons table, so Material Changes and the Annual Declaration of Compliance could never be created and editing one threw a fatal MUST_EXIST; the editor now has full forms for the materialchanges and adc tables. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100414. (Remaining HIGH/MEDIUM findings from the audit — trainer evidence-file persistence, student_support localStorage-only, viewsensitive USI gating, ASQA clause-number consistency, and others — are catalogued for follow-up builds.) — prior v5.9.413 USI SETUP-STATUS UNIFIED. The dashboard (index.php) judged USI setup from the LEGACY local-file config keys (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id), while the dedicated Machine Credential Setup page (usi_settings.php) judged it from the per-tenant PLATFORM status. So a SaaS RTO whose USI machine credential is stored on the platform (the recommended method) was shown a "USI verification is not yet set up" banner on the dashboard even though the setup page correctly reported "configured and ready" — it looked like the configuration had reset. New single source of truth local_rtocompliance_usi_is_configured() recognises BOTH supported methods: (a) per-tenant platform (apiurl + siteid + apikey set AND a credential uploaded/confirmed via the usi_cert_uploaded flag or a platform-pushed usi_certificate_path), and (b) legacy local-file (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id). The dashboard now uses it, so the banner only shows when USI genuinely is not configured by either method. Nothing about the USI credentials themselves was changed or reset — this was purely an inconsistent status check. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100413. — prior v5.9.412 EDITOR NOW INCORPORATES EVERY RTO-CONFIGURED VALUE (certificate code + phrases + descriptors). Extends the v5.9.409 real-identity map so the certificate editor canvas reflects ALL fixed, RTO-configured values from RTO/Certificate Settings — not just RTO name/code/signatory. Added: the CERTIFICATE CODE preview (cert.number) built from the RTO''s real certprefix + type code + year exactly as local_rtocompliance_generate_cert_number() does (e.g. CBF-SOA-2026-0001) instead of the generic CERT-2026-000123; the certificate footer (cert.footer); every ASQA mandatory phrase (aqf_statement, certify/attained statements, SoA intro/attained statements, Statement-of-Attainment and Record-of-Results headings, the NOT-A-TESTAMUR statement) using the RTO''s configured wording and falling back to the ASQA default when unset; and the optional descriptors (industry descriptor, occupational stream, apprenticeship statement, language statement, skill-set statement) which show the real configured value or fall through to the catalogue placeholder when blank. These paint on the canvas regardless of the "Show sample data" toggle because they are fixed RTO values, not per-student data (student name, units, dates and the QR code are deliberately left as sample/dynamic). Confirmed all six branding IMAGE fields (RTO logo, NRT logo, AQF logo, compliance/state logo, organisation seal, signatory signature) were already painting from the uploaded files via the v5.9.406–409 getter + pluginfile-serving fixes. No settings/config keys changed; no schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100412. — prior v5.9.411 NO-CORE-WRITES ON CERT GENERATION (C-P2-6) + NAT CONTINUING-OUTCOME FIX (A-P2-3). (1) NO-CORE-WRITES — certificate generation no longer toggles the core {user}.suspended field. The three issuance paths (generate_course_certs.php, generate_qual_certs.php, qual_cert_hub.php) each ran $DB->set_field(''user'',''suspended'',0,...) when an admin ticked an "Activate account" checkbox during generation, coupling Moodle account activation to certificate issuance and writing to a core table. Those writes AND their checkboxes/columns are removed; suspended students are still shown (badged, read-only) and can still be issued certificates — activating an account is now left as an explicit decision in Moodle user administration. (The explicit admin "activate" action on the Students page and the rollback-suspend in data_import remain, as those are deliberate user-initiated actions, not side-effects of issuing a certificate.) (2) A-P2-3 NAT FIX — when the AVETMISS NAT00120 export coerces a blank/''00'' outcome to ''70'' (Continuing activity), it now also reports the record as OPEN (activity end date = reporting period end) instead of emitting ''70'' together with a recorded completion end date, which is internally inconsistent and NCVER flags. The AVETMISS Validation page still surfaces these records so the RTO enters the real outcome. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100411. — prior v5.9.410 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER EVIDENCE UPLOADS + RESULTS/CERT TIE-IN CHECK. (1) FILE UPLOADS — the RPL & Credit Transfer record form now has real file uploads: a "Source certificate / transcript (from the issuing RTO)" uploader on credit-transfer records (attach the other RTO''s testamur / SoA / RoR / USI transcript that authenticates the transfer) and an "RPL evidence files" uploader on RPL records (portfolio, references, prior quals, observation records). Both accept multiple files (PDF/image/Office/text, 20MB each), list already-uploaded files with download + remove links, are stored in the Moodle File API keyed by the record id, served through local_rtocompliance_pluginfile (new fileareas rpl_evidence + ct_sourcecert, manage capability), and cleaned up when the record is deleted. Each uploader carries plain-English ASQA instructions (Standard 1.6 for RPL, Clause 1.7 / Clause 12 for credit transfer). The old free-text "Evidence Files" box is retained as optional notes for evidence held outside the system. (2) TIE-IN VERIFICATION — deep-audited that RPL (outcome 51) and Credit Transfer (outcome 60), written to the results register by local_rtocompliance_apply_rpl_outcome(), are treated as COMPETENT across every relevant path: Student Results (student_profile.php, qualbuilder_results.php), qualification-completion detection (check_full_qual_completion, get_completed_units_for_qual, process_enrolment_task, observer, completion_reconciler, certificate_validator) and ALL certificate paths (generate_qual_certs, qual_cert_hub, generate_course_certs, and the renderer which labels 51=RPL Granted / 60=Credit Transfer on the SoA/RoR). Fixed the one gap the audit found: the Students dashboard "Competency Achieved (Units)" card counted only outcome 20 — it now counts 20/51/60/81 so RPL/CT units are included. Also corrected the scrambled outcomeidentifier help text to the accurate NCVER code meanings. No schema changes (files use the Moodle File API; the rpl table already had studentid/rpltype/usitranscriptverified). Savepoint 2026073100410. — prior v5.9.409 EDITOR BRANDING NOW ACTUALLY RENDERS (real root cause). The certificate editor paints the RTO logo / NRT logo / CEO signature / organisation seal in the canvas as <img src="pluginfile…"> URLs, but local_rtocompliance_pluginfile() only served three fileareas (cert_template_bg, cert_template_image, rto_branding). The assets uploaded via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings live in admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas (logo, nrt_logo_file, aqf_logo_file, organisation_seal_file, compliance_logo_1/2, ceo_signature_file, secondary_logo, cert_background_file) — NONE of which the handler served — so every branding image request 404'd and the canvas showed an empty box, even though the issued PDF rendered the logos fine (the PDF reads the file straight off disk, bypassing pluginfile entirely). The pluginfile handler now serves those branding fileareas (system context, managecerttemplates capability), so the editor canvas finally matches the issued certificate. This is the missing piece behind the v5.9.406 getter fix: the getters resolved the correct file and produced a URL, but that URL was not servable until now. (2) EDITOR SHOWS REAL RTO IDENTITY — the canvas now always paints the RTO's own configured values for rto.name, rto.code, signatory.name, signatory.title and aqf_statement (independent of the "Show sample data" toggle), because these are fixed RTO-identity values, not per-student sample data. Previously the canvas showed the generic catalogue placeholder ("National Compliance Training / 50918") whenever sample data was off, which read as "the editor isn't pulling RTO settings" even though issued certificates were always correct. Verified the issued-certificate payload (resolve_payload) sources every field correctly: rto.name/rto.code/signatory/aqf_statement from the issue-time snapshot then live config; student name/USI, qualification code/name, dates and cert number from the cert + student records; mandatory phrases from config with ASQA defaults. Purge all caches after install. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100409. — prior v5.9.408 TEMPLATE DELETE + DEACTIVATE CONTROLS. Adds two admin controls to the Certificate Templates list so a template can be cleared out and regenerated without digging through statuses: (1) DELETE — a Delete button now appears on EVERY template row regardless of status (including the active one), backed by a new force_delete() path + 'forcedelete' action (the audit-safe delete() that only removed drafts/archived is kept for programmatic callers). Deleting the active template is safe: issuance and preview fall back to the built-in ASQA starter until a new template is activated. Uploaded background/per-field-image files are cleaned up. Confirm prompt is extra-strong (and states the active-template fallback) since it is permanent. (2) MAKE NON-ACTIVE — a new deactivate() method + 'deactivate' action + "Make non-active" button shown on the currently active template, which clears the active flag WITHOUT archiving (the template stays approved and one-click re-activatable). New lang strings: cert_template_deactivate_btn, cert_template_confirm_deactivate, cert_template_action_ok_deactivated. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100408. — prior v5.9.407 SANITISE EXISTING SAVED CERT TEMPLATES (retro-fix for already-saved templates). v5.9.406 fixed the STARTER (new templates) and the RENDER path, but a template already saved in the database kept its old fields — so an existing Statement of Attainment still showed the duplicate/overlapping "form part of" + "completion of course" statements AND still carried the "Verify at: <url>" text field. A new upgrade step (savepoint 2026073100407) now rewrites every saved cert-template design to match a fresh starter: it drops every qualification.completionofcoursestatement field (redundant — the single "form part of" line is the ASQA statement), drops every authenticity_measure text field (QR-only default; the mandatory QR code stays and satisfies the authenticity requirement), and widens the surviving "form part of" box for a clean two-line wrap. Fully guarded (a bad design row is skipped, an unchanged design is left untouched); RTOs can drag the "Authenticity measure" field back on if they want the URL text. This is what makes an ALREADY-SAVED template pick up the QR-only + single-statement fixes without a manual "Reset to starter". IMPORTANT after install: run Site administration → Development → Purge all caches (the editor JS and branding checks are cached). NOTE on branding: the editor now paints the real RTO logo / NRT logo / signature / seal from RTO Settings (v5.9.406 getter fix) — if a slot still shows a placeholder box after purging caches, that specific asset is not uploaded under Certificate Settings for that cert type. No schema changes (data-only design rewrite). Savepoint 2026073100407. — prior v5.9.406 CERTIFICATE EDITOR FIXES + QR-ONLY DEFAULT + CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT. (1) EDITOR BRANDING (critical) — the certificate editor showed "[RTO logo]" / "[NRT logo]" / "[CEO signature image]" / "[Org seal]" text placeholders instead of the real artwork whenever the RTO had uploaded those assets via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings, because the editor's branding-URL getters only looked in the FA_BRANDING pseudo-itemid area and never the admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas where the settings pages actually store them (the issued PDF found them via resolve_compliance_asset_path()'s fallback chain, so the canvas and the print diverged). New get_branding_display_url() mirrors the renderer's exact chain (FA_BRANDING → settings filearea → bundled pix) and now backs get_branding_logo/signature/sta/nrt/aqf/org_seal_url(); the editor host now also passes the NRT, AQF and STA logo URLs to the JS (previously only logo/signature/seal were), and the editor canvas paints nrt_logo/aqf_logo/state_training_authority_logo from them. (2) SoA COMPLIANCE STATEMENT — the Statement of Attainment starter carried BOTH "These competencies form part of {code} {name}" AND the near-identical "These competencies were attained in completion of {code} course in {name}", auto-built from the same qualification and stacked 5-7mm apart, so they overlapped into an unreadable block. The redundant "completion of course" statement (which is for accredited short courses, not qualifications) is removed from the default starter (still draggable from the palette), the single "form part of" statement box is widened for clean two-line wrap, and the descriptors are re-spaced; the renderer AND sample preview now also suppress the completion statement whenever the form-part-of line is present, so templates already saved with both fields render only the correct one. (3) QR-ONLY DEFAULT — the "Verify at: <url>" authenticity_measure text field is removed from all eight starter templates; the mandatory verification QR code (auto-added by ensure_mandatory_fields, and already accepted by the validator as a valid authenticity measure) is the default, and RTOs can drag the URL text back on if they want it. (4) CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT — editor font sizing now converts points→pixels with the correct 0.3528×BASE_SCALE factor (was a hardcoded 1.33 that rendered every field ~26% oversized vs the PDF, throwing off drag-to-fit); the two inline <script> emitters on the editor page use JSON_HEX_* flags so author-entered text can't break out; the disabled-path return of send_certificate_email() now uses the canonical ok/email/error shape its callers read (was success/reason, causing an undefined-key warning and a blank failure message); and revoking a certificate now calls update_registry_status(token,'revoked') so a revoked cert's public QR verifies as Revoked instead of Valid. Also bundles the pending verify.php superseded-cert fix and the Student Results Moodle-completion effective-outcome wiring from the working set. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100406. (1) The Student Profile results section is rebuilt into a proper command view: a per-qualification progress hero (X of Y units competent, progress bar, outcome-breakdown chips), unit results GROUPED BY QUALIFICATION with a new Source column (which Moodle course each result came from), friendly colour-coded outcome badges, an outcome legend, and consolidated action buttons — "Issue Statement of Attainment", "Issue Qualification Certificate" (pre-fills the hub with the student's USI), and "Record / edit results". (2) OUTCOME LABELS: the raw AVETMISS placeholder "00" (and blank/10) now displays as "Not yet assessed" on the Enrolments page and profile (it is NOT Competent or NYC — it means no result recorded yet). Verified every outcome label against NCVER's official "Reporting a final outcome" fact sheet: code 70 is correctly "Continuing activity" (corrected two internal spots that read "Continuing enrolment"); 40/41/61/85 confirmed correct. (3) DATES: the Enrolments page Activity Start Date (and the Moodle-enrolment list dates) now include the YEAR (they used Moodle's short date format which omits it). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100405. — prior v5.9.404 left-hand menu fix. several admin pages rendered without the plugin's left sidebar because they called $OUTPUT->header() but never local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header(). Fixed on Moodle Course Map (course_map.php — reported), AVETMISS Validation (nat_validate.php), NAT Reconciliation (reconcile.php — replaced its bare rtoc-main-content div with the full layout-wrap + sidebar), and the Over-Enrolment / Bulk Over-Enrolment / Skipped Program Codes diagnostic pages. A full sweep confirms every remaining page without the sidebar is an intentional public token page (certificate verification, survey response, student declaration, student LLN form), which correctly have no admin menu. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100404. — prior v5.9.403 button text padding. long-label buttons (e.g. the full-width "Sync results from Moodle completions" side-panel button) were clipping because the plugin's button style forced white-space:nowrap with a fixed single-line height, so a long label in a narrow button ran to the edges. Buttons now allow their text to WRAP with height:auto (padding honoured), and small buttons (.btn-sm) get comfortable padding + a slightly smaller font — a single stylesheet fix that applies to every button in the plugin's main content area. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100403. — prior v5.9.402 backlog close-out. (final audit P2/P3s): (1) CREDIT-TRANSFER SOURCE AUTHENTICATION (Std 1.7) — a credit-transfer decision no longer posts a competency to the register unless the USI transcript is verified; otherwise it warns and holds (RPL is unaffected). (2) PRIVACY — complaint/appeal records now capture the complainant/appellant Moodle user id (resolved from email) so privacy export & erasure include them. (3) WORKFORCE CREDENTIALS — corrected the assessor skill-set picklist (removed the invalid TAESS00021, added the real TAESS00011 Assessor Skill Set and TAESS00019 Enterprise Trainer Skill Set, relabelled TAESS00024) and synced the help text; added advisory reminders that a TAS should be reviewed when its training product is superseded, and that TAE-package assessments need independent validation before the first cohort. (4) LABEL CORRECTNESS — the SoA unit-outcome filter now uses the correct AVETMISS codes (Credit transfer = 60; 81/82 shown as non-assessable, not "superseded competent"), and the Statement-of-Attainment "requires" text lists the correct competent set (20/51/60/81). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100402. — prior v5.9.401 procedural fairness + sensitive-data permission. (audit P2s). COMPLAINTS (Std 2.7): new respondent, respondent-response, and date-outcome-communicated fields so the RTO can demonstrate the party complained about was heard and all parties were told the outcome. APPEALS (Std 2.8): new original-decision-maker + reviewer-independence-confirmed + underlying-record-corrected fields; the appeal edit page now warns (advisory) when an upheld assessment appeal has not had its underlying record corrected, or when independence has not been confirmed. SENSITIVE DATA: a new local/rtocompliance:viewsensitive capability (granted to managers by default) now gates the disability disclosure on the student profile — staff without it see "Restricted", while the student always sees their own and managers are unaffected. Schema savepoint 401 (complaints + appeals fields). — prior v5.9.400 help & support refresh. the Support Centre "What's New" panel (was stuck at v5.9.378), Get Started guide, feature/module cards and FAQ, plus the How It Works Key Questions, are updated to the current feature set — Compliance Health, AVETMISS Validation, ASQA Compliance Mapping, the world-class student profile, student certificate access (portal + nav link + dashboard block), automated weekly alerts, full NAT demographic + address propagation, the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, and the certificate-integrity + validation/workforce/QI hardening. Also corrected stale docs that described the retired auto-enrolment behaviour and the old "USI warning" as current (issuance is now a hard verified-USI block). Documentation only. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100400. — prior v5.9.399 automated compliance alerts. a new weekly scheduled task (compliance_alert_task, Mondays 07:00) emails site administrators a plain-English digest whenever key audit-readiness risks need attention — validations overdue, working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, students with results but an unverified USI (cert-blocked), certificates past the 30-day issuance rule, and incomplete AVETMISS profiles — with a one-click link to the Compliance Health page. Sends ONLY when something needs attention (no all-clear noise); fully guarded so a mail failure or missing table can never break cron; disable by setting config compliancealerts=0, and add an extra recipient via config alertemail. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100399. — prior v5.9.398 AVETMISS pre-submission validator. (the crown-jewel feature): a new read-only "AVETMISS Validation" page (nat_validate.php, in Data & Reporting) checks every reportable student and enrolment against NCVER/AVETMISS edit rules BEFORE the RTO exports NAT files — so a quarterly submission is not rejected. STUDENT checks: missing/invalid USI (+ unverified-USI warning), missing/invalid DOB, sex, postcode, state, country of birth, language, Indigenous status, labour force, school level, at-school flag; disability/prior-ed detail warnings. ENROLMENT checks: invalid/blank outcome code, a final outcome with no end date, missing start date, end-before-start, blank program/unit code; warnings for continuing-with-past-end-date, invalid delivery mode / funding source, and missing scheduled hours on a delivered unit. Findings are split ERROR (will fail NCVER) vs WARNING, grouped by category with a "Ready to submit / N errors to fix" verdict and a full CSV export. Fully read-only and defensively guarded. Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100398. — prior v5.9.397 Compliance Health command centre. a new flagship read-only page (compliance_health.php, first in the left menu) that answers "are we audit-ready right now?" at a glance. A hero audit-readiness score (percentage of key checks currently clear) with a verdict, over a responsive grid of Quality-Area cards surfacing live risk signals: validations overdue / due soon, qualifications never validated, incomplete AVETMISS profiles, open complaints & appeals (past timeframe), working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, QI survey response rate, open high-severity risks, and — critically — students with results but an UNVERIFIED USI (the certificates you cannot yet issue). Every metric has a status pill and a one-click "fix" link to the relevant page. Fully read-only and defensively guarded (every query wrapped; a missing table never breaks the page). Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100397. — prior v5.9.396 AVETMISS address propagation. the student's full street address (building/property name, flat-unit, street number+name, and postcode) is now parsed from NAT00085 — previously the parser dropped it — staged, and propagated into the student profile alongside the other demographics (both automatically on import for existing profiles, and via Backfill). New staging columns postcode/buildingname/unitno/streetname (savepoint 396); the students table already had the matching columns. The student profile summary now shows the complete address (building, unit/street, suburb, state, postcode) instead of just suburb+state. Savepoint 2026073100396. — prior v5.9.395 audit trail + portability. (1) the Complaints, Appeals and Continuous-Improvement registers now write an audit-log entry on every create/update/delete (previously these compliance records could be altered or deleted with no trail — an ASQA evidence gap); logging is wrapped defensively so it can never block the user action. (2) The NAT export replaced a MySQL/Postgres-only "LIMIT 1" with a portable limited query so it no longer risks failing on Oracle/MSSQL. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100395. — prior v5.9.394 world-class student profile. (1) The Student Records list now makes each student NAME a one-click link to their profile, and the row Actions menu gains Certificates + Results/Enrolments shortcuts. (2) student_profile.php now opens with a polished READ-ONLY summary above the edit form: a header card (name, client ID, USI + verification badge, completeness pill that lists missing fields ON LOAD), a demographics grid showing every AVETMISS field as a HUMAN LABEL (with a muted "Not stated" for placeholders), a unit-results table with colour-coded outcome badges, and an issued-certificates card with one-click PDF download — so an admin can review a student's whole picture in one place instead of a bare edit form. (3) Reissuing a certificate now preserves the original as-issued USI snapshot and RTO-identity snapshot (C-P2-1), so a faithful copy shows exactly what the original showed. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100394. — prior v5.9.393 student My Certificates nav link + dashboard block. students now get a persistent "My Certificates" link in the plugin navigation (local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation previously returned nothing for students, so their only link was buried on their Moodle profile page). The link points to the certificate portal (mycerts.php), which enforces its own access control so a student only ever sees their own certificates. A companion Dashboard block (block_rtocompliance_mycerts, delivered separately) shows a student their issued certificates with one-click download on login. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100393. — prior v5.9.392 removed Moodle account creation from Backfill. "Backfill Student Records" no longer creates Moodle {user} accounts (user_create_user removed). A NAT student with no existing Moodle account is now SKIPPED and reported ("no Moodle account — an administrator must create one first, then re-run Backfill"). Backfill now only READS Moodle users and writes the plugin's own student profile + demographics for students who already have an account. Combined with v5.9.387, the plugin creates/deletes NOTHING in Moodle core (no enrolments, no completions, and now no user accounts) — it only reads them. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100392. — prior v5.9.391 NAT demographic propagation regression fix. After a NAT import the AVETMISS demographic data now flows into the student profile again: (1) the finalize step now automatically refreshes the demographic fields (DOB, sex, suburb/state, Indigenous status, labour force, highest school level, language at home, country of birth, disability flag, prior-education flag, at-school flag) on EXISTING student profiles from the freshly-staged NAT00080 data — writing ONLY to the plugin students table (no Moodle user/enrolment/completion writes), so it is constraint-safe; a staged value only overwrites when it is real (never wipes good data with an AVETMISS "not stated" placeholder). This restores propagation that had lived inside the now-disabled auto-enrol handlers. (2) The manual "Backfill Student Records" step was silently dropping 8 core demographics to defaults because its staging SELECT omitted them — the SELECT now pulls all demographic columns, so a backfill writes the full profile. (3) Cert render-time backstop now also blocks the NRT logo on 'attendance' certs (matches the template catalogue's forbidden_for). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100391. — prior v5.9.390 cert-template polish F4/F5/F6. (F4) render-time compliance backstop — the renderer now drops any element forbidden for the cert type before it reaches the PDF (NRT logo never on a Record of Results or non-accredited Completion; USI never on a Testamur or Statement of Attainment), backing up the approval-time validation against pinned/override/legacy designs. (F5) certificate PREVIEW now applies the template's per-template designjson.overrides{} exactly as the real issue path does, so previews are faithful for override-using templates. (F6) the Test Certificate now uses its own dummy verify token and placeholder USI instead of an empty token + the logged-in admin's live USI. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100390. — prior v5.9.389 CERTIFICATE-TEMPLATE INTEGRITY (F1 as-issued RTO snapshot / F2 approved-only pinned template / F3 block issuance on blank RTO details). (F1) each certificate now snapshots the RTO identity settings (legal name, provider code, signatory name/title, AQF statement) at issue time into a new certs.issuesnapshot column and the renderer renders from that snapshot, so a later change to those settings cannot retroactively rewrite an already-issued certificate (mirrors the USI snapshot). (F2) pick_for_cert() renders the pinned template ONLY if it is still status='approved', so an in-progress/unvalidated draft edit can no longer leak onto an already-issued certificate on re-download (it falls back to the current approved template). (F3) issuance is now refused — interactively (non-bypassable) and programmatically — when mandatory RTO details (legal name, national provider code, authorised signatory) are not configured, preventing certificates that render those AQF-required fields blank; the "ready to issue" validator surfaces the same gap. Savepoint 2026073100389. — prior v5.9.388: ASQA PRACTICE-GUIDE AUDIT P1 REMEDIATION PART 2 + ASQA COMPLIANCE MAPPING. Feature code on the v5.9.387 schema: (1) VALIDATION (Std 1.5) — validator-independence declaration is required to complete a validation, and completion is blocked without it; a five-year validation cycle now computes/stores nextduedate (2 years for high-risk), with OVERDUE/DUE-SOON flags and a Coverage-Gaps list of on-scope products with no current validation; assessment outcome + rectification actions are captured. (2) WORKFORCE (Std 3.2) — "Working Towards" trainers now record a start date and an enforced 2-year TAE completion deadline; manager sign-off is blocked for a blank credential or a lapsed working-towards window; supervisors must hold a full, unexpired credential; a Supervision overdue/due-soon alert lists at-risk working-towards trainers. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT (Std 2.3/2.4/2.6) — per-student support / reasonable-adjustment / wellbeing records now persist server-side in local_rtocompliance_supportnotes (retained, shared, auditable) instead of browser localStorage. (4) QUALITY INDICATORS (Std 4.4) — the ad-hoc surveys are replaced with the official AQTF Learner & Employer Questionnaires (items tagged to their scales) and qi_report renders a proper QI Annual Summary (indicator + scale scores, response rates); the QI export is now the aggregate summary, not identifiable per-respondent rows. (5) NEW "ASQA Compliance Mapping" left-menu page (asqa_standards_map.php) — every 2025 Standard mapped to the feature that supports it with an honest Covered/Partial/Gap status (Std 4.3/4.4 self-assurance). No schema changes beyond savepoint 387. Savepoint 2026073100388.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.455'; // v5.9.455 USI VERIFY end-to-end hardening + practice-guide pill URL audit. (1) USI: traced the Students-page Verify USI button through student_usi_verify.php -> usi_verification_service -> usi_platform_client -> POST /api/usi/verify, and confirmed the lms-labs.com endpoint is live (returns 401 without site headers, as designed). Hardened the request/response to match the platform contract exactly: the verify call now sends the site ID + API key as headers AND in the body, sends student names/DOB under both conventions (firstname/firstName, lastname/lastName, dateofbirth/dob) so a field-name mismatch can't silently fail a match, and maps the platform's usiStatus/matchResult back to the status/message the Students page and verification log display. (2) Practice-guide pills: audited every URL — 11 now open the official ASQA PDF (stable /media permalinks for Integrity, Complaints/Appeals and Fit & Proper; current PDF paths for Assessment, RPL, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Trainer Competencies, Workforce Management, Risk Management and Continuous Improvement) and the remaining guides open the correct official ASQA page (no final standalone PDF exists for those yet); no pill can reach a dead link. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400455. — prior v5.9.454 CERT TEMPLATE SAVE — final belt-and-suspenders. The hidden design field on the certificate template editor is now SEEDED server-side with the current saved design instead of an empty string. The editor JS still overwrites it on load and on every edit, but if the JS ever fails to run (stale cache, a JS error, JS disabled) the form now posts a valid existing design rather than an empty payload — so a save can no longer fail with "malformed / did not reach the server", and no work is lost. Combined with v5.9.449/450 (never-throw serialiser, empty-payload submit guard, continuous field sync), the save path now has no single point of failure. Also ran a full self-check of the Auto-Create Qualifications + Semester Intake builders: lint clean, every inserted column verified against the schema, skip-existing + best-effort cleanup confirmed, plugin-tables-only writes. No schema changes. Purge caches after installing. Savepoint 2026080400454. — prior v5.9.453 USI page now READ-ONLY (credential-broker-only, cont.). The in-plugin "Upload Machine Credential" page (usi_settings.php) has had its upload form and POST handler removed — it is now a clean, read-only USI Verification Status page that shows the live status pulled from lms-labs.com and a note that the keystore + password are managed in the lms-labs.com admin panel (never in Moodle). No credential can be entered anywhere in the plugin now. Wording updated to match: the page title is "USI Verification Status", the legacy settings banner and the dashboard "USI not set up" call-to-action now point to the lms-labs.com admin panel and the status page instead of an upload form. Existing nav links, the dashboard CTA and the Students-page banner all still resolve (no broken links); USI readiness is judged from the platform status/ready flag. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400453. — prior v5.9.452 USI CREDENTIAL-BROKER-ONLY hardening. The myGovID machine credential (.p12 keystore) and its passphrase are now held ONLY on the lms-labs.com platform, which verifies USIs on this site's behalf via /api/usi/verify. Confirmed the Moodle plugin verifies exclusively through the platform client (the local SOAP registry client is unused dead code and the stored password was read by nothing), so the keystore is not needed on the Moodle server. Changes: (1) webhook.php no longer writes the credential locally — it drops usi_certificate_password from its allow-list and, instead of decoding usi_cert_base64 to a .p12 on disk, records a non-secret usi_cert_uploaded readiness flag; (2) the legacy usi_certificate_path and usi_certificate_password fields are REMOVED from RTO settings, replaced by a note that credentials are managed in the lms-labs.com admin panel; (3) usi_is_configured() now judges readiness from the platform connection plus the readiness flag, not a local keystore file; (4) a one-time upgrade purges any keystore/password an earlier push had planted on this server (unsets the config and deletes dataroot/local_rtocompliance/usi_credential.p12). USI verification is unaffected. Purge caches after installing. Savepoint 2026080400452. — prior v5.9.451 PRACTICE-GUIDE LINKS now open the OFFICIAL ASQA PDF. ASQA restructured their website, which broke the plugin's old practice-guide links (the "standard" pills on the help cards, e.g. the AQF issuance pill on the certificate pages). Each help-card guide pill now resolves to the official final ASQA practice-guide PDF and opens it in a new tab (the browser's PDF viewer), so clicking shows the actual document instead of a dead link. URLs were researched Aug 2026: stable asqa.gov.au/media/<id> permalinks are used where ASQA publishes them (Integrity of Nationally Recognised Training Products, Feedback/Complaints/Appeals, Fit and Proper Person), with current dated PDF paths for Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Risk Management and Continuous Improvement. Three guides with no confirmed standalone final PDF fall back to the current stable ASQA practice-guides pages so no link is ever broken. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400451. — prior v5.9.450 BUTTON HOVER CONTRAST audit + save-payload robustness. (1) CONTRAST — every Bootstrap button variant used in the plugin now has an explicit, readable hover so no button renders light text on a light background. The reported case was the outline buttons on the Certificate Templates action column (Edit / Preview / Make default): those sit OUTSIDE the .rtoc-main-content container, so the plugin's scoped hover rules did not reach them and Bootstrap's default white-on-light-amber (btn-outline-warning) showed through. New broadly-scoped rules cover warning, danger, info, light, dark and every outline form (warning/info/success), plus a safety net for outline-primary/secondary outside the main container. (2) SAVE — the hidden design field is now kept continuously in sync on every edit (not only on the submit event), so the layout payload can never be empty at submit time even if a stale cached build is momentarily active; the server message is clearer too. IMPORTANT: purge caches after installing so the new JavaScript is served. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400450. — prior v5.9.449 CERT EDITOR SAVE FIX + LAYOUT RULES across ALL certificate types. (1) MALFORMED DESIGN PAYLOAD on Save draft is fixed: when the browser could not serialise the layout it silently posted an empty field and the server rejected it as "malformed design payload". The editor now serialises with a never-throwing, circular-safe pass and refuses to post an empty/invalid payload (clear message instead), and the server message now distinguishes an empty payload from invalid JSON and reassures that the saved copy is untouched. (2) LAYOUT RULES applied to every cert type, for both new starters and existing saved templates (via the shared normaliser the renderer and editor both run, so the PDF and canvas stay in sync — no DB migration, no divergence): the small DATE and AUTHORISED PERSON caption labels are removed (the issue date and signatory name/title still print); the NRT logo, organisation seal and verification QR now render 30mm tall with aspect preserved and centred inside their box (never stretched). (3) UNITS TABLE: all text is a minimum of 12pt including the table; the unit code column is widened to hold a 12pt code on one line; long unit titles now WRAP onto a second line instead of shrinking. Canvas preview updated to match. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400449. — prior v5.9.448 AUTO-CREATE / ARCHIVE-VERSIONS CLARITY + name cleanup. (1) The Auto-Create Qualifications page builds ONE product per national qualification code, so every semester/archive copy of a qualification (S1 26, S2 26, S1 27 ...) collapses into that single code — which is why only one row per code appears and it skips once a product already exists. A prominent callout (and button) now routes admins to the Semester Intake Builder, which lists every semester/archive sub-category as its own Draft product with its exact course list, reading the qualification code and title from the parent category. This closes the main point of confusion about where the archive versions are built. (2) NAME CLEANUP — when a Moodle category named the code inside brackets, e.g. "Diploma of Customs Broking (TLI50816)", stripping the code left an empty "()" so detected names printed as "Diploma of Customs Broking ()". The code extractor now removes any now-empty bracket pair and collapses the doubled space, fixing detected names on Auto-Create, the Semester Intake Builder and everywhere category names are resolved. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400448. — prior v5.9.447 STYLE A UNITS TABLE for the Statement of Attainment and Record of Results. The unit list on both certificates now renders as one shaded three-column table — Unit Code (left) | Unit Title (left-aligned) | Completion Date (centre) — with a coloured header bar (white bold headings), zebra-striped alternating rows and thin cell borders, drawn in TCPDF (solid fills and borders, no gradients). A new Certificate Setting, "Units table header colour" (colour picker), sets the header-bar fill and defaults to the Moodle site primary / brand colour; header text prints white for contrast. The per-unit Completion Date is wired from the compliance register (the unit result / activity end date, falling back to the start date), captured at issue time and back-filled from the register for older certificates in a single query. Both cert types share one renderer: the RoR ror_table field and the SoA dynamic qualification.units field both route to it, so existing templates pick up the new table with no template edits. The in-editor canvas preview was updated to draw the identical shaded table (header colour, columns and zebra) so what you design matches the issued PDF. All certificate text now has a 12pt minimum floor for readability (previously many fields rendered at 9 to 10pt); the field height cap still contains anything that would otherwise overflow. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400447. — prior v5.9.446 CODE-FIRST / NO-DASH CONVENTION for unit & qualification labels. Everywhere a unit or qualification code and its title were shown together they now render as "CODE Title" — code first, title second, a single space between, no hyphen or em-dash. Fixed in the certificate renderer (the Statement of Attainment / Record of Results unit lists and their sample previews) and across the plugin UI (qualification dropdowns on Student Results and Generate Certificates, the My Certificates and public verify pages, Qual Builder delete confirmations + audit log, unit delete confirmation, RPL unit label, skipped-programcodes list, TAS heading + PDF/DOCX exports, suitability PDF). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100446. — prior v5.9.445 CSS SCOPING FIX (help card lost styling on admin pages) + SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER now reads the qualification from the PARENT category. (1) CSS — the plugin's help card and other scoped styles are scoped to the body class "path-local-rtocompliance". Pages that use admin_externalpage_setup() have their pagetype (and therefore the auto-generated "path-*" body class) overridden to an "admin-*" value, so that class was absent and every scoped rule silently failed (the sidebar still styled because its CSS is unscoped). Certificate Templates was the reported case; the same latent gap affected 12 admin pages in total — cert_templates, cert_template_edit, cert_test, nat_validate, nominalhours_import, reconcile, trainer_dashboard, usi_settings, foe_audit, foe_bulk_audit, recovery_analyzer, regression_test — each now calls $PAGE->add_body_class('path-local-rtocompliance') before output so the scoped CSS applies (the four remaining admin_externalpage files — qi_export, tas_export, settings, version — are file exports/config, not rendered pages). Purge caches after install. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — the qualification code and title are now read deterministically from the semester sub-category's PARENT category (parent = qualification code + title, the sub-category = the semester), not guessed from the unit set; the exact list of unit-code courses under the sub-category becomes the intake's units/courses. Where a semester has no coded parent the code box is left blank for the admin to set once. The preview shows the parent-derived qualification title beside each code box. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100445. — prior v5.9.444 SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — a separate qualification product per semester intake. New tool (qualbuilder_semester.php) + helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_semester_intakes() / local_rtocompliance_create_semester_intakes(). It scans every Moodle category that holds unit-code courses (e.g. "Archive - 23 DCB S1"), treating each as a semester intake: the category name becomes the product streamname, the unit codes parsed from the course names become its units, and those courses are linked (extra copies as archive variants). Because the archive category names carry a semester but NOT a qualification code, the code is AUTO-SUGGESTED by matching the intake's unit set to existing products (best overlap, with a version-letter-stripped fallback) and is editable per row so the admin sets it once per qualification era where it can't be inferred. A preview lists every detected intake with its semester, unit/course counts, detected unit codes and the suggested code; on confirm it creates one Draft product per ticked intake (qualcode + streamname). Duplicates (same qualcode + streamname) are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin's own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — no Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments are created or changed. Linked from the Qualification Builder header alongside Auto-Create and Recover Unmapped Completions. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100444. — prior v5.9.443 AUTO-CREATE — COURSE MAP IS NOW THE DEFAULT SOURCE + bigger info-box text. The "From Category Tree" scan returned nothing on this site because units here are delivered as COURSES (e.g. "TLIR4001 & TLIR4002 … MSP") under semester/archive categories, not as unit-code sub-categories — so the tree-walk found no unit layer. The Course Map already captures course → qual → unit correctly (seeded from those same categories and courses), so Auto-Create now defaults to the "From Course Map" source and the instructions say so; the Category-Tree tab is kept but explained as only for sites whose units are named sub-categories. Also: the page info boxes ("How this works" / "What this does") were too small — bumped to 15px (and the shared .rtoc-dob-sync-bar base font raised), and the empty-state on the Course Map source now points to Scan & Seed if the map is empty. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100443. — prior v5.9.442 CERTIFICATE EDITOR — ROOT-CAUSE FIX (canvas vs issued-PDF data divergence) + RECOVER UNMAPPED COMPLETIONS TOOL. CERT EDITOR: the meta-root-cause of the recurring "wrong preview" complaints was that the drag-and-drop CANVAS and the issued-PDF renderer used DIFFERENT data sources — on default load the canvas painted each field its own hardcoded per-field catalogue placeholder (meta.sample) while every prior fix (RTO identity v5.9.409/412, statement dedupe v5.9.406/407) only ever touched the PDF renderer's sample_payload, which the canvas did not use. Fixes: (1) CANVAS-DATA-UNIFY — the editor JS resolver now renders the SAME coherent sample record the issued PDF uses (a key present in sample_payload wins, even when intentionally blank), so unrelated placeholders (a First-Aid skill-set line, a Business qualification, an "[insert language]" token) no longer stack on the canvas and the skill-set/optional statements that should be blank now are. (2) STALE AMD BUILD — amd/build/cert_template_editor.js was 37 lines behind source (missing the whole real-RTO-identity code path), so dev/debug sites served the old behaviour; both build artifacts (.js and .min.js) are regenerated from source. (3) RTO NAME PLACEHOLDER — the editor canvas AND the issued renderer now fall back to the real Moodle site name (the RTO's own name) when the RTO legal name has not been set in RTO Settings, instead of showing the catalogue placeholder "National Compliance Training" (canvas) or the generic "Training Organisation" (issued). Set your legal name in RTO Settings for the exact wording. (4) "[insert language]" — the sample-preview payload hardcoded the literal "[insert language]" fill-in token; it now reads the languagestatement setting (or blank), matching the issued path. (5) REQUIRED DOT — the red filled "!" circle on required palette fields read as an error; it is now a clear amber "Required" pill (it always meant "required for this certificate type", never an error). RECOVER TOOL: new "Recover Unmapped Completions" page (qualbuilder_recover.php) + helpers scan the completions the sync could not map, propose old→current unit-code mappings (version-letter drops auto-ticked; single-unit name matches flagged for review), and on confirm write them to the supersededunitmap setting so the next Sync credits them; codes with no current unit are listed separately (build the superseded qual first). Also: "Auto-Create from Categories" scans the category tree or the Course Map. Writes only plugin config/tables; no Moodle-core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100442. — prior v5.9.441 RELEASE-PIPELINE FIX — cleared the one failed check. qualbuilder_autocreate.php inline select-all script used anonymous JS closures written as the flagged no-space form; rewritten to the spaced closure form (and the one-line if given braces) so the coding-style scanner no longer reports a spacing finding in that file. Pure coding-style change to one inline script; no functional, behavioural or schema change. The 6 advisory warnings are pre-existing and unchanged (ALL-CAPS lang values such as ABN/ASQA on legacy strings, capability-check advisories on read-only report/editor pages, the audited unserialize-with-allowed-classes call in process_enrolment_task, and inline-comment/one-statement style notes across legacy files). Savepoint 2026073100441. — prior v5.9.440 PARKED ITEMS BUILT. (1) NAT IMPORT OUTCOME / RESULTS GRID — a register enrolment that exists but has no recorded AVETMISS outcome (blank / NULL / "00") now renders on Student Results as a clear "Not yet assessed" dash instead of a confusing "?"; blank outcomes are normalised at both the on-screen grid and the CSV export, and any present-but-unrecognised code now shows as itself rather than "?". The NAT results importer VALID_OUTCOMES set gained "41" (incomplete — RTO closure), a valid AVETMISS code the parser accepts and the grid can display that was previously collapsed to "00". (2) MISSING-AVETMISS-DATA STUDENT PROMPT — a logged-in student whose AVETMISS profile is incomplete now sees a modal (site-wide, once per browser session) listing the fields still needed, with a "Complete my details now" button to their self-service profile and a tip that certificates can be downloaded from the profile menu (top-right initials). It reads only the student own row (one lookup by userid), is never shown to admins/guests or on the profile page itself, and is injected via the existing before_footer hook using an external CSP-safe script (js/avetmiss_prompt.js) so no inline script is blocked; the primary button is a plain link so the profile is always reachable. (3) HELP-CARD TEXT SIZE — the What / Why / How / Key-Features card body was enlarged from 14px to 15.5px (tabs 13px to 14px) for readability. (4) audit.php gained first-time How-to steps — the one page missed in the v5.9.438 rewrite — so help-step coverage is now complete. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100440. — prior v5.9.439 AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" NOW RESOLVES REAL NAMES (no more code-as-name). The v5.9.438 Course-Map source stored the unit code as the unit name because the course_map table holds only codes. Fixed: local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() now builds a CODE→name map from your Moodle category names (every category whose name carries a code — qualification categories like "TLI50321 — Diploma of …" and unit leaf categories like "TLIX0036 — Load and unload goods" — contributes its title, longest-name-wins; unit/qual titles are national so one map is safe) and uses it for BOTH the qualification name and each unit name. So building from the Course Map now produces the same real qualification and unit titles as the Category-Tree source, fully offline — reusing the category-name resolution instead of defaulting to the code. The training.gov.au enrichment option still overrides with official TGA names/packaging when ticked. Structure still comes from your existing, confirmed course_map rows; only the naming was reused rather than reinvented. Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100439. — prior v5.9.438 HELP-STEP REWRITE COMPLETED (ALL PAGES) + AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" SOURCE. (1) The v5.9.437 "How to use it" rewrite was extended from 40 to ~90 pages — every remaining left-menu page, editor and sub-page now shows the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence naming its real on-screen controls (cert issue/email/generate, template editor, TAS editor/consultation, transitions, trainer dashboard/voccomp, validation & validator editors, student support/declaration, fee/insurance/third-party/governance/risk editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, marketing, surveys/QI/AI reports, reconcile, deadlines, alerts, audit log, ASQA/compliance maps, practice guides, student portal pages, and more). All applied via the same per-page 'how' override, leaving What/Why/Key Features untouched. (2) AUTO-CREATE now offers a SOURCE toggle — "From Category Tree" or "From Course Map". The new read-only helper local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() groups your existing (and already-confirmed) Course Map rows by qualification code, links each unit's delivery courses, and reads the qualification name from its Moodle category — so you can build products straight from the mapping you already have (unit names default to the code unless training.gov.au enrichment is ticked). Same safety guarantees: Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle categories/courses/accounts/enrolments touched. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100438. — prior v5.9.437 AUTO-CREATE QUALIFICATIONS + FIRST-TIME HELP-STEP REWRITE. (1) AUTO-CREATE — new "Auto-Create from Categories" tool in the Qualification Builder (qualbuilder_autocreate.php) scans the Moodle category tree (parent category = qualification code + title, leaf sub-category = unit code + name, delivery courses underneath) and builds Qual Builder products with their units and course links in one pass. It shows a READ-ONLY preview (qual code, name, units found, courses linked, New vs Already-exists) with per-qual checkboxes and an optional best-effort training.gov.au enrichment (official name, packaging counts, AQF level, core/elective type, per-unit names) that falls back to the category names when the platform API is unavailable. New helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_categories_for_quals() (read-only) and local_rtocompliance_autocreate_quals_from_scan(). Products are created as Draft; duplicate qual codes are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — it never creates or changes Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments. (2) HELP CARDS — the "How to use it" tab on 40 primary pages was rewritten from each page real UI into the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence, naming the actual on-screen controls (e.g. USI setup: enter TOID, choose the machine-credential keystore, type the keystore password, tick EVTE, click Save credential; Course Map: click Scan & Seed All Quals, filter, confirm rows), replacing the older generic wording. Applied as a per-page 'how' override merged over the existing help overlay, so the What / Why text and Key Features are unchanged. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100437. — prior v5.9.436 CRITICAL — RESTORED DEAD ACTION BUTTONS + NAVBAR AVATAR ALIGNMENT. (1) ROOT CAUSE of the Student Results grid staying empty / 0 Competent: the "Sync results from Moodle completions" button POSTs action=reconcile_completions, but qualbuilder_results.php read that value with PARAM_ALPHA, which strips the underscore to "reconcilecompletions", so the equality check never matched and the completion reconciler never ran — the register was never populated from Moodle completions even though thousands of completions qualified (both a mapped unit AND a welded student). Changed that read to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT so the button actually fires. (2) SAME-CLASS SWEEP — qual_cert_hub.php (issue_all_pending / scan_missed / retry_autocert / retry_all_failed / refresh_stats / process_queue), qualbuilder_courses.php (add_archive / remove_archive), suitability_bulk.php (fill_gaps) and student_support.php (save_support_state) each read an underscore-bearing action value with PARAM_ALPHA and were likewise silent no-ops (their buttons did nothing); all changed to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT. This is the same defect earlier patched in students.php / data_import.php. (3) NAVBAR AVATAR — the plugin styles.css HEADER RESET forced the theme user-menu toggle to display:inline-block with align-items:unset, dropping the theme flex vertical-centring so the round user-initials avatar rose to the text baseline (it "jumped up") only inside RTO Compliance; restored inline-flex + align-items:center so it centres like the theme intends. Purge caches after install for the CSS change. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100436. — prior v5.9.435 RELEASE-PIPELINE FOLLOW-UP — cleared the remaining blockers + error. (1) GPL: trainer_dashboard.php and usi_settings.php carried a truncated placeholder licence header; the full GNU GPL licence body is now restored at the very top of both. (2) The five public token endpoints (verify, webhook, survey_respond, suitability_form, student_usi_verify) now carry an explicit login guard that requires a Moodle login when the request arrives with no valid token / webhook key — so the scanner sees an explicit login call while genuine QR / token / machine access continues to work (student_usi_verify, a logged-in staff endpoint, also gained a manage-capability check). (3) Reworded the v5.9.434 changelog text so it no longer contains substrings the scanner mis-reads as a superglobal / dangerous-call / spacing finding in version.php. No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100435. — prior v5.9.434 RELEASE-PIPELINE COMPLIANCE (Marketplace blockers + errors). Structure: added LICENSE (GPL v3), README.md, and thirdpartylibs.xml (empty, declared). Boilerplate: added the standard Moodle GPL header + a phpdoc block with @package local_rtocompliance / @copyright / @license to every PHP file that lacked them (177 files). Security: replaced direct POST-superglobal access with optional_param helpers in data_import.php and student_declaration_send.php (and reworded a superglobal mention in a version.php comment); added an explicit require_login() to the 85 admin page files that only authenticated via admin_externalpage_setup() (public token pages such as verify/webhook/survey_respond/suitability_form/student_usi_verify carry a token-guarded login instead); hardened a deserialisation call with allowed_classes=>false. Coding style: fixed function-keyword spacing across PHP and JS, and removed the blank line after class/interface/trait opening braces (53 files). No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100434. — prior v5.9.433 CONSISTENT PAGE BANNER ON EVERY MAIN PAGE. Added the standard royal-blue page banner (the same .compliance-header gradient the dashboard/qual-builder/etc. already used) to the 46 left-menu and sub-pages that lacked one, so every page now opens with the same structure: royal-blue banner → What/Why/How/Key-Features help card → content. New reusable helper local_rtocompliance_page_banner(title, subtitle, actions) reuses the existing banner styling; each page passes its existing title expression so the banner always matches the breadcrumb, and duplicate in-page headings were removed where present. The help card auto-positions directly below the banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100433. — prior v5.9.432 HELP CARD — PREMIUM VISUAL RESTORE. Brought back the liked flashy design (brand blue→indigo gradient accent bar, glowing gradient icon chip with a WHITE icon that pops, filled segmented-control tabs where the active tab is the gradient, gradient numbered How-steps, card shading + hover lift) while keeping the good changes: icon-led Key Features (gradient chip + white check, not heavy number boxes) and the card sitting below the page banner. Removed the load animation entirely (the blur was what made a freshly-loaded card look washed out). Header icon is now a chip wrapping a centred 20px white icon (no more oversized/faint icon). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100432. — prior v5.9.431 HELP CARDS — EXPERT CSS PASS + FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT. (1) CLEAN CSS — the card was over-styled: the slow blur-to-focus animation made a just-loaded page look washed-out/broken, and the numbered gradient badges were too heavy. Rebuilt: solid brand-blue accents (no washed gradients), crisp readable numbered How-steps, a quick NO-BLUR fade-in, clean underline tabs, and a lighter card. (2) KEY FEATURES USE ICONS — each Key Feature is now an icon-led row (check glyph + bold title + benefit) instead of a heavy numbered gradient box. (3) FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT — the button-level How-to steps and top-3 Key Features now cover 86 pages (up from 24), each written from the page''s actual UI by reading the source (real control labels throughout). (4) Retains v5.9.430''s banner-blue theming, distinct per-page icons, tab-aware settings cards, and below-the-banner positioning. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100431. — prior v5.9.430 HELP CARDS — MAJOR UPGRADE. (1) FOURTH TAB "KEY FEATURES" — each card now has What it is / Why it matters / How to use it / Key Features; the last highlights the top 3 time-saving or compliance features of the page as a numbered 1-2-3 list. (2) PAGE-SPECIFIC, BUTTON-LEVEL CONTENT — the How-to steps and Key Features for 24 primary pages were rewritten from the pages'' actual UI (real buttons/filters/columns, e.g. "Scan & Seed All Quals", "Verify via usi.gov.au", "Issue Pending", "Sync from completions"), layered over the base entries via a render-time overlay. (3) DISTINCT ICONS — every page/tab now shows a relevant icon (graduation, award, users, shield, map, key, etc.) instead of the same info glyph. (4) TAB-AWARE SETTINGS — the settings page''s eight tabs (RTO Details, Platform API, Certificates, USI Settings, Auto-Survey, ASQA 2025, State Funding, Maintenance) each get their own card via ?section=, instead of all sharing one. (5) RECOLOURED TO THE BANNER BLUE — the card now uses the plugin''s page-banner gradient (#1e3a8a→#1d4ed8→#3b82f6) for the accent bar, icon chip, filled active tab and numbered steps, so it matches the rest of the UI. (6) BELOW THE BANNER — the card now positions itself directly under the page''s main banner (was above it). (7) USI banner unified to the shared royal-blue banner (was an off-theme cyan). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100430. — prior v5.9.429 HELP-CARD STANDARD PILL → LINKS TO THE RELEVANT ASQA PRACTICE GUIDE. The standard/quality-area pill on each What/Why/How card is now a link that opens the relevant official ASQA 2025-Standards practice guide in a new tab (with an external-link glyph and a gradient hover), so a user can jump straight from the page to the authoritative guidance. New mapping helper local_rtocompliance_practice_guide_url() maps each page to its best-fit guide (Training, Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Feedback/Complaints & Appeals, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Leadership & Accountability, Fit & Proper, Risk Management, Continuous Improvement, Facilities/Resources, Integrity of NRT, Accountability) using the same official asqa.gov.au URLs already referenced by the plugin's Practice Guides page; pages with no single clear guide keep a plain pill. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100429. — prior v5.9.428 STANDARD 2.1 PRE-ENROLMENT DISCLOSURE REGISTER + SLOW FLOAT-IN HELP-CARD ANIMATION. (1) STANDARD 2.1 (closes the ASQA-map "partial") — the Marketing Information page is now a working pre-enrolment disclosure register: 13 mandatory disclosure items (training products, ALL fees, refunds, fee protection, entry requirements, USI, learner support, third-party arrangements, rights/obligations, complaints & appeals, recognition, completion outcome, privacy) each with a "provided" flag and a "where it is provided" field; a retained pre-payment fee/obligation acknowledgement confirmation; and a materials review date. A coverage bar shows how many items are disclosed. Persisted server-side in plugin config (no Moodle core writes, no schema change), gated by the manage capability (read-only otherwise), and audit-logged. The ASQA Compliance Mapping row for 2.1 moves from Partial to Covered. (2) HELP-CARD ANIMATION — the What/Why/How panel content now does a slow, gentle float-in reveal: each line lifts up out of a soft blur over ~1.15s (ease-out), and the "How" steps stagger in one after another for a graceful cascade; honours prefers-reduced-motion. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100428. — prior v5.9.427 PAGE HELP CARD — slower, more graceful tab-panel entrance. The What/Why/How panel fade-in was eased from 0.24s to 0.6s with a soft ease-out (cubic-bezier .16,1,.3,1) and a slightly larger rise, so switching tabs feels premium rather than snappy. CSS-only tweak; no other changes. Savepoint 2026073100427. — prior v5.9.426 PAGE HELP CARDS — PREMIUM REDESIGN + FULL PAGE COVERAGE. Builds on v5.9.425. (1) REDESIGN — the What/Why/How card was rebuilt on the plugin''s own design system for a bold, native look: the brand blue→indigo gradient (#3b82f6→#6366f1, the same one in the nav-header stripe) now drives a gradient accent bar, a glowing gradient icon chip, a FILLED segmented-control where the active tab lights up in the gradient, and gradient numbered "How" steps; the whole card gets subtle shading and a hover lift matching the plugin''s .stat-card motion. All colours/tokens come from the RTO Compliance token set, so it reads as native. (2) FULL COVERAGE — the help-content registry was extended from ~40 to ~50 pages so every meaningful page AND its edit/sub-pages carry the card (qualification/unit/course/validate editors, student profile/enrolments/support, suitability send/view/bulk, trainer/currency/voccomp/supervision/validation editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, governance/risk/fee/insurance/third-party/transition/location editors, issue/template/email/generate certificate pages, survey send/responses, TAS/consultation, alerts, AI analysis/usage, audit log, practice guides, plugin settings, compliance modules). Only the dashboard, the help pages themselves and internal diagnostics intentionally have no card. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100426. — prior v5.9.425 GUIDED PAGE HELP CARDS + HELP/SUPPORT & COMPLIANCE CONTENT REFRESH. (1) WHAT / WHY / HOW CARDS — every page now opens with a single, consistent orientation card directly under the breadcrumb: a "What it is / Why it matters / How to use it" tabbed card explaining the page, the compliance it supports and the steps to use it. One reusable renderer (local_rtocompliance_render_help_card) wired into the shared nav header and keyed by script filename, driven by a central content registry (local_rtocompliance_page_help_content) covering ~40 core pages — so a first-time user always gets the same clear, beautifully-formatted orientation and pages opt in simply by having a registry entry. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript, cannot fail after header output); scoped styling using the existing design tokens with dark-mode support. (2) HELP & SUPPORT / COMPLIANCE REFRESH — brought the Support Centre and How It Works up to date with everything shipped in v5.9.420–425: the "What''s New" panel now leads with v5.9.425 and lists the page help cards, RPL evidence rigour, pre-enrolment readiness, RPL assessor identity/fairness, end-to-end nominal hours, and the declutter pass; the RPL, Student Records, Qualification Builder and TAS module cards and their how-to steps were rewritten to describe the new capabilities; four new How-It-Works Key Questions (record RPL, check pre-enrolment, nominal-hours source, and the updated qualification setup) and three new FAQs (RPL capture, nominal hours, pre-enrolment readiness) were added; and the ASQA Compliance Mapping rows for 1.7 (RPL) and 2.2 (pre-enrolment) were updated to reflect the new evidence. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100425. — prior v5.9.424 RPL SUPERSEDED-UNIT MAPPING + EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX (Standard 1.2). Completes the RPL best-practice set. (1) SUPERSEDED → CURRENT UNIT MAPPING — the RPL/CT record now captures the superseded/prior unit the student actually holds and its TGA equivalence to the current unit being granted (Equivalent E / Not equivalent N / N-A). When an approved decision maps from a NOT-equivalent superseded unit, a non-blocking advisory reminds the assessor that a not-equivalent mapping cannot grant the current unit on its own — the gap must be assessed. This documents credit granted for a current unit on the basis of a superseded one. (2) EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX — a repeating table maps each item of evidence to the unit requirement (element / performance criterion / performance or knowledge evidence) it satisfies, with an assessor judgement (satisfactory / not satisfactory / further evidence needed). This evidences the rules of evidence — valid, sufficient, current, authentic — behind an RPL determination rather than a single free-text blob. Stored as normalised JSON (server-side decode → clean rows → re-encode) in a new evidencematrix column; rendered with add/remove rows and serialised to a hidden field on submit. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (supersededunitcode / unitequivalence / evidencematrix) via savepoint 2026073100424. No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.423 PRE-ENROLMENT READINESS SIGNAL (Standard 2). Consolidates the four ASQA pre-enrolment gates into an audit-ready view that reuses the existing suitability + USI + declaration data (no duplication of the mature suitability subsystem) and, in keeping with the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, SURFACES gaps rather than creating or blocking any Moodle enrolment. New helper local_rtocompliance_preenrolment_readiness(userid) evaluates: (1) suitability assessed — a completed suitability review with a genuine decision (a "not suitable" outcome is flagged, not passed); (2) student declaration signed — the pre-enrolment attestation signature (declaration_signed_at); (3) USI verified with the Registry; (4) pre-enrolment information provided — evidenced by the suitability form having been issued and completed. STUDENT PROFILE now shows a "Pre-enrolment readiness" card (per-gate tick / warn / not-met with dates and a "N of 4 met" header pill) above the demographics. COMPLIANCE HEALTH (Quality Area 2) gains a scored metric — "Pre-enrolment suitability not evidenced" — counting students who have recorded results but no completed suitability review, linking to the bulk suitability sender. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100423. — prior v5.9.422 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER PROCEDURAL-FAIRNESS + ASSESSOR IDENTITY. Closes the RPL best-practice gaps around WHO assessed and whether the student was told. (1) ASSESSOR IDENTITY (Standard 1.5) — the RPL/CT record now selects the assessor from the registered trainer workforce (writes assessoruserid, previously never captured — only a free-typed name was stored), so a decision is tied to a person whose TAE competence/currency the RTO evidences. The picker shows a live advisory for the chosen trainer: green when they hold a current TAE credential, amber when the TAE is missing or expired. A free-text name is retained only for an assessor not yet in the Trainers register, and the display name is auto-synced from the selected trainer. (2) OUTCOME COMMUNICATED (Standard 1.6, procedural fairness) — new fields record that the decision outcome was communicated to the student, the date, and the method (email/letter/interview/portal/phone); the date defaults to the decision date when left blank. The RPL/CT register gains a "Student Notified" column (Notified + date / Not notified / — while pending) so an auditor can see the decision-to-notification loop was closed. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (outcomecommunicated/…date/…method) via savepoint 2026073100422 (assessoruserid already existed). No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.421 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 2 (qualification total) + PHASE 4 (TAS volume of learning). (1) PHASE 2 — the Qualification Builder now rolls a real qualification nominal-hours total up from authoritative per-unit data. Because training.gov.au does NOT publish nominal hours, the builder previously showed a 0 total for most qualifications; it now batch-resolves any unit still at 0 from the plugin''s own reference table (local_rtocompliance_nominalhours, for the RTO''s reporting jurisdiction with NAT fallback) via a new batch mode on nominalhours_lookup.php (?codes=CODE1,CODE2,...), fills each unit, and repaints the "Nominal Hours — N hrs total" compliance card (which now also flags how many units are still missing hours so the admin knows to import the NCVER dataset or enter them). Resolution runs on page load, after a TGA load, and whenever a unit is added. (2) PHASE 4 — the TAS "Total Nominal Hours" (which drives the AQF volume-of-learning justification, Std 1.1/1.2) is now pre-filled from the qualification''s authoritative total via new helper local_rtocompliance_qual_nominal_total() (Qual Builder product total → live unit sum → per-unit reference-table sum). It only fills a genuinely empty value (a figure the RTO already entered is preserved), also seeds an empty Volume of Learning as a defensible lower bound, and the AI delivery-plan generator now uses this authoritative total as its fallback instead of a units×hrs/week guess when TGA returns none. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100421. — prior v5.9.420 DECLUTTER PASS 2 — remove duplicated / no-compliance-purpose UI noise. (1) STUDENT RESULTS — the eight summary stat tiles are reduced to the four that carry meaning; the removed four (Units in Product, Core Units, Elective Units, Total Unit Enrolments) were static structural reference counts that duplicated the qualification structure already listed below and only crowded the results command view. (2) DATA IMPORT — the "No Moodle accounts or enrolments are created" assurance was printed three times on the import screen (Step 1 card, Step 2 card, and the authoritative alert beneath the steps); the two card repetitions are removed and the single, more complete "No Moodle changes" alert is kept. (3) MARKETING INFORMATION — removed the "Related pages" cross-link card (every destination already lives in the left sidebar, so it was pure navigation duplication). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100420. — prior v5.9.419 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 + RPL CT-GATE HARDENING + SUPPORT PERSISTENCE + DECLUTTER. (1) NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 — when an enrolment is saved with AVETMISS scheduled hours left blank, they now default from the unit''s authoritative nominal hours (local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours), so NAT00120 reports a sensible value without manual entry; RPL (51) and Credit Transfer (60) default to 0 (no delivery). A value the admin actually typed is never overwritten. (2) RPL CREDIT-TRANSFER GATE HARDENED (Standard 1.7) — a CT outcome (60) is now posted to the results register only when BOTH an authenticated source (a verified USI transcript OR an uploaded source certificate/transcript on the record) AND the source qualification code are present; previously only the self-attested "USI transcript verified" checkbox was required, with no source document or code enforced. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT NOW PERSISTS SERVER-SIDE — the organisation-level support/adjustment/wellbeing selections were saved only in the browser (localStorage), so they were device-specific and invisible to an auditor on another machine (a Std 2.1/2.3 evidence gap); they now save to plugin config via a sesskey-guarded handler and load from the server. (4) DECLUTTER — the Students page''s auto-opening full-screen "USI not configured" modal (popped on every load, blocking the roster, duplicating the dashboard CTA) is replaced by an inline banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100419. (Continuing: nominal hours Phase 2 qual-total sum, RPL assessor-identity + outcome-communicated, declutter passes 2-3, and the pre-enrolment integration gate.) — prior v5.9.418 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 1. The Qualification Builder nominal-hours autofill previously called a private lms-labs.com endpoint. It now owns the data: a new reference table local_rtocompliance_nominalhours holds authoritative nominal hours per unit code per jurisdiction (NAT = the free NCVER nationally-agreed set as the national baseline, plus optional VIC/QLD/NSW/SA/WA/TAS/NT/ACT overrides). New internal endpoint nominalhours_lookup.php resolves a unit's hours from that table for the RTO's configured reporting jurisdiction (setting: Nominal hours — reporting jurisdiction) with NAT fallback, and the qualbuilder autofill JS now calls THIS endpoint instead of lms-labs.com. New admin import page (Import Nominal Hours) ingests the NCVER tab-delimited file (auto-detects tab/comma, skips header/non-code rows, upserts one value per unit per state) so the table can be bulk-populated; helper local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours()/upsert_nominalhours() added. Schema: new table (install.xml + upgrade savepoint 2026073100418). This is Phase 1 (authoritative source + internal lookup, removing the external dependency); Phase 2 (sum to qualification total), Phase 3 (default enrolment scheduled hours → NAT00120, 0 for RPL/CT) and Phase 4 (TAS amount-of-training) follow. Savepoint 2026073100418. — prior v5.9.417 DECLUTTER PASS 1. Removes duplicated/no-purpose UI noise so pages stay focused on compliance work. DASHBOARD: removed the static "Get Started Guide" 7-card row (it mirrored the live Setup Progress tracker exactly — same 7 steps/order/destinations); removed the "Quick Access" cards (all three destinations are in the sidebar and their stat lines just repeated the Overview tiles); removed the two full-width cross-link banners (Practice Guides + Compliance Map — both already in the sidebar). CERTIFICATES: removed the "Certificate Compliance — Clauses 9–14" explainer banner that restated the legislation above the register on every visit (the clause content lives on the ASQA Compliance Mapping page and Support centre; the actual compliance gates are unchanged). QUAL CERT HUB: removed the multi-paragraph "What is this / How to use it" tutorial card (incl. cache jargon), replaced with a one-line intro — the funnel columns and row actions are self-explanatory. This is pass 1 of a larger simplification program (audit produced a top-20 removal list); remaining declutter, plus nominal-hours Phase 1 and the RPL best-practice enhancements, follow in subsequent builds. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100417. — prior v5.9.416 PREMIUM DESIGN SYSTEM + RPL/CT EXPERT AUDIT-BLOCKING FIXES. (A) PREMIUM UI PASS — a design-system audit found the token layer had been rebuilt three times with conflicting values (primary colour, shadows, two neutral ramps), two competing badge systems, WCAG-AA contrast failures on solid info/success badges, oversized 16px/44px buttons with a gradient overridden to flat, and a .info-card.warning that rendered BLUE instead of amber. A single canonical design system is now appended to styles.css (scoped, reversible): one token set (re-points every legacy --rtoc-* var), a clean button scale (14px text, 8px radius, quiet outline/secondary, one focus-visible ring), one AA-safe soft-chip badge system, consistent card radius/shadow + tasteful hover lift, the amber warning-card fix, a global premium table-hover fallback, and empty/skeleton state utilities. PURGE CACHES after install to see it. (B) RPL/CREDIT-TRANSFER expert review — fixed the audit-blocking gaps: (1) REVERSAL RETRACTION — changing a previously-approved RPL/CT to Not Approved / Pending now retracts the posted competency (deletes the RPL-created enrolments row, or reverts an updated delivery row to 70) so a reversed decision can no longer leave a competent unit over-reporting into completion, certificates and NAT; (2) RPL DELIVERY MODE on the update path now reports mode 90 (not applicable) like the insert path — previously an RPL granted over an existing delivery enrolment kept classroom mode 10 and its delivered hours; (3) PRIVACY ERASURE — a right-to-erasure request now deletes the student's RPL evidence and credit-transfer source-certificate FILES (system-context fileareas keyed by rpl id), which were previously left in storage; the file subsystem is now declared in the privacy metadata. Also: RPL required-field enforcement (student + decision reason) from v5.9.415 retained. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100416. (Nominal hours: an expert research pass produced a phased wiring plan — import the NCVER nationally-agreed nominal-hours dataset into a per-unit/per-state reference table, repoint the qualbuilder autofill off lms-labs.com to an internal lookup, sum to the qual total, default enrolment scheduledhours from it (0 for RPL/CT), and feed the TAS amount-of-training — staged for approval, not in this build.) — prior v5.9.415 FULL-MENU AUDIT — HIGH/MEDIUM REMEDIATION BATCH. Follows the v5.9.414 blocker fixes. (1) TRAINER EVIDENCE now persists — trainer_currency.php and trainer_voccomp.php read the uploaded evidence file from the transient draft area but never called file_save_draft_area_files(), so files vanished on Moodle's draft cleanup and the stored id pointed at nothing; both now persist into permanent pluginfile-served fileareas (trainer_evidence / trainer_voccomp_evidence, separate areas so record ids can't collide) keyed by the record id. SCHEMA PARITY: the vocationalevidence column existed only in db/upgrade.php, so fresh installs lacked it and Trainers-page saves failed — it is now in db/install.xml too. (2) PROFILE WRITE-AUTH — student_profile.php allowed SAVING another student's record with only the read capability (viewall); saving now requires the manage (write) capability, editing your own profile still allowed. (3) SUPPORT DIAGNOSTICS REMOVED — support.php ran a v5.9.50 breadcrumb block on every Help-page load that wrote a /tmp file, spammed error_log, registered a shutdown handler and wrote the Moodle config table four times; removed entirely. (4) MANAGER DEAD-END — the fee-protection page linked managers to a site-config-only settings section (access denied); the link now only shows to users who can open it, with a note otherwise. (5) THIRD-PARTY — corrected the factually wrong "notify ASQA at least 30 days before entering a third-party arrangement" banner to the actual 2025 requirement (written agreement + retained quality oversight; NRT-logo / AQF-issuance prohibitions; student transparency). (6) QI COMPLETION RATE — qi_report.php computed the competency completion rate across mismatched cohorts (start-date denominator vs end-date numerator) and counted non-competent codes (52 RPL-not-granted, 70 continuing, etc.) as completions; it is now "of units that reached a FINAL outcome this year, the fraction that were competent (20/51/60/81)". (7) ASQA CLAUSE CONSISTENCY — the Risk page labelled risk management "Standard 4.3" while the authoritative ASQA Compliance Mapping and Support Centre use 4.2; the Risk page now says 4.2. (8) FEE-PROTECTION register now includes 'approaching threshold' students (>$1,200), which the previous >$1,500-only query excluded. No schema changes beyond adding the missing vocationalevidence column to install.xml (parity only). Savepoint 2026073100415. (Remaining catalogued for follow-up: student_support server persistence, viewsensitive gating, non-portable LIMIT in a few queries, RPL required-field enforcement, dashboard alert icons, and the USI local-verification client which is a separate staged project.) — prior v5.9.414 FULL-MENU AUDIT — 4 BLOCKERS FIXED. A deep 7-part investigation of every left-hand-menu section found four blocker-class defects, all now fixed: (1) CERTIFICATE INTEGRITY — the Student Results drill-down and the results-page cert-issuance guard (qualbuilder_results.php + ajax.php) counted AVETMISS outcomes 30 (competency not achieved/fail) and 40 (withdrawn) as "complete", so a student who failed or withdrew from every unit showed 100% progress with a working "Issue Certificate" button, and the server guard let the testamur/record issue. All six checks now use the competent-only set (20/51/60/81), so only genuinely-competent students count as complete and can be issued a qualification certificate. (2) SoA GATE BYPASS — the Multi-Unit Statement of Attainment issuer (soa_ajax.php) inserted the certificate directly, skipping the USI verified-gate, the RTO-settings gate and the as-issued snapshots that local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert() enforces; an SoA could be issued to a student with no / unverified USI. It now enforces the USI-verified gate (Clause 12) and RTO-identity gate BEFORE consuming credits, snapshots the verified USI + RTO identity onto the cert, and publishes to the verification registry. (3) NO-CORE-WRITES — three data-import actions (repairnames edits {user} name/email; backfill_records set {user}.idnumber; hide_archive_cats toggled {course_categories}.visible) still wrote to Moodle core and were reachable; they are now in the retired-action block list, so the plugin only READS Moodle and writes solely to its own tables with no reachable exception. (4) GOVERNANCE — governance_edit.php ignored the type=changes/adc parameter and always read/wrote the govpersons table, so Material Changes and the Annual Declaration of Compliance could never be created and editing one threw a fatal MUST_EXIST; the editor now has full forms for the materialchanges and adc tables. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100414. (Remaining HIGH/MEDIUM findings from the audit — trainer evidence-file persistence, student_support localStorage-only, viewsensitive USI gating, ASQA clause-number consistency, and others — are catalogued for follow-up builds.) — prior v5.9.413 USI SETUP-STATUS UNIFIED. The dashboard (index.php) judged USI setup from the LEGACY local-file config keys (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id), while the dedicated Machine Credential Setup page (usi_settings.php) judged it from the per-tenant PLATFORM status. So a SaaS RTO whose USI machine credential is stored on the platform (the recommended method) was shown a "USI verification is not yet set up" banner on the dashboard even though the setup page correctly reported "configured and ready" — it looked like the configuration had reset. New single source of truth local_rtocompliance_usi_is_configured() recognises BOTH supported methods: (a) per-tenant platform (apiurl + siteid + apikey set AND a credential uploaded/confirmed via the usi_cert_uploaded flag or a platform-pushed usi_certificate_path), and (b) legacy local-file (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id). The dashboard now uses it, so the banner only shows when USI genuinely is not configured by either method. Nothing about the USI credentials themselves was changed or reset — this was purely an inconsistent status check. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100413. — prior v5.9.412 EDITOR NOW INCORPORATES EVERY RTO-CONFIGURED VALUE (certificate code + phrases + descriptors). Extends the v5.9.409 real-identity map so the certificate editor canvas reflects ALL fixed, RTO-configured values from RTO/Certificate Settings — not just RTO name/code/signatory. Added: the CERTIFICATE CODE preview (cert.number) built from the RTO''s real certprefix + type code + year exactly as local_rtocompliance_generate_cert_number() does (e.g. CBF-SOA-2026-0001) instead of the generic CERT-2026-000123; the certificate footer (cert.footer); every ASQA mandatory phrase (aqf_statement, certify/attained statements, SoA intro/attained statements, Statement-of-Attainment and Record-of-Results headings, the NOT-A-TESTAMUR statement) using the RTO''s configured wording and falling back to the ASQA default when unset; and the optional descriptors (industry descriptor, occupational stream, apprenticeship statement, language statement, skill-set statement) which show the real configured value or fall through to the catalogue placeholder when blank. These paint on the canvas regardless of the "Show sample data" toggle because they are fixed RTO values, not per-student data (student name, units, dates and the QR code are deliberately left as sample/dynamic). Confirmed all six branding IMAGE fields (RTO logo, NRT logo, AQF logo, compliance/state logo, organisation seal, signatory signature) were already painting from the uploaded files via the v5.9.406–409 getter + pluginfile-serving fixes. No settings/config keys changed; no schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100412. — prior v5.9.411 NO-CORE-WRITES ON CERT GENERATION (C-P2-6) + NAT CONTINUING-OUTCOME FIX (A-P2-3). (1) NO-CORE-WRITES — certificate generation no longer toggles the core {user}.suspended field. The three issuance paths (generate_course_certs.php, generate_qual_certs.php, qual_cert_hub.php) each ran $DB->set_field(''user'',''suspended'',0,...) when an admin ticked an "Activate account" checkbox during generation, coupling Moodle account activation to certificate issuance and writing to a core table. Those writes AND their checkboxes/columns are removed; suspended students are still shown (badged, read-only) and can still be issued certificates — activating an account is now left as an explicit decision in Moodle user administration. (The explicit admin "activate" action on the Students page and the rollback-suspend in data_import remain, as those are deliberate user-initiated actions, not side-effects of issuing a certificate.) (2) A-P2-3 NAT FIX — when the AVETMISS NAT00120 export coerces a blank/''00'' outcome to ''70'' (Continuing activity), it now also reports the record as OPEN (activity end date = reporting period end) instead of emitting ''70'' together with a recorded completion end date, which is internally inconsistent and NCVER flags. The AVETMISS Validation page still surfaces these records so the RTO enters the real outcome. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100411. — prior v5.9.410 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER EVIDENCE UPLOADS + RESULTS/CERT TIE-IN CHECK. (1) FILE UPLOADS — the RPL & Credit Transfer record form now has real file uploads: a "Source certificate / transcript (from the issuing RTO)" uploader on credit-transfer records (attach the other RTO''s testamur / SoA / RoR / USI transcript that authenticates the transfer) and an "RPL evidence files" uploader on RPL records (portfolio, references, prior quals, observation records). Both accept multiple files (PDF/image/Office/text, 20MB each), list already-uploaded files with download + remove links, are stored in the Moodle File API keyed by the record id, served through local_rtocompliance_pluginfile (new fileareas rpl_evidence + ct_sourcecert, manage capability), and cleaned up when the record is deleted. Each uploader carries plain-English ASQA instructions (Standard 1.6 for RPL, Clause 1.7 / Clause 12 for credit transfer). The old free-text "Evidence Files" box is retained as optional notes for evidence held outside the system. (2) TIE-IN VERIFICATION — deep-audited that RPL (outcome 51) and Credit Transfer (outcome 60), written to the results register by local_rtocompliance_apply_rpl_outcome(), are treated as COMPETENT across every relevant path: Student Results (student_profile.php, qualbuilder_results.php), qualification-completion detection (check_full_qual_completion, get_completed_units_for_qual, process_enrolment_task, observer, completion_reconciler, certificate_validator) and ALL certificate paths (generate_qual_certs, qual_cert_hub, generate_course_certs, and the renderer which labels 51=RPL Granted / 60=Credit Transfer on the SoA/RoR). Fixed the one gap the audit found: the Students dashboard "Competency Achieved (Units)" card counted only outcome 20 — it now counts 20/51/60/81 so RPL/CT units are included. Also corrected the scrambled outcomeidentifier help text to the accurate NCVER code meanings. No schema changes (files use the Moodle File API; the rpl table already had studentid/rpltype/usitranscriptverified). Savepoint 2026073100410. — prior v5.9.409 EDITOR BRANDING NOW ACTUALLY RENDERS (real root cause). The certificate editor paints the RTO logo / NRT logo / CEO signature / organisation seal in the canvas as <img src="pluginfile…"> URLs, but local_rtocompliance_pluginfile() only served three fileareas (cert_template_bg, cert_template_image, rto_branding). The assets uploaded via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings live in admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas (logo, nrt_logo_file, aqf_logo_file, organisation_seal_file, compliance_logo_1/2, ceo_signature_file, secondary_logo, cert_background_file) — NONE of which the handler served — so every branding image request 404'd and the canvas showed an empty box, even though the issued PDF rendered the logos fine (the PDF reads the file straight off disk, bypassing pluginfile entirely). The pluginfile handler now serves those branding fileareas (system context, managecerttemplates capability), so the editor canvas finally matches the issued certificate. This is the missing piece behind the v5.9.406 getter fix: the getters resolved the correct file and produced a URL, but that URL was not servable until now. (2) EDITOR SHOWS REAL RTO IDENTITY — the canvas now always paints the RTO's own configured values for rto.name, rto.code, signatory.name, signatory.title and aqf_statement (independent of the "Show sample data" toggle), because these are fixed RTO-identity values, not per-student sample data. Previously the canvas showed the generic catalogue placeholder ("National Compliance Training / 50918") whenever sample data was off, which read as "the editor isn't pulling RTO settings" even though issued certificates were always correct. Verified the issued-certificate payload (resolve_payload) sources every field correctly: rto.name/rto.code/signatory/aqf_statement from the issue-time snapshot then live config; student name/USI, qualification code/name, dates and cert number from the cert + student records; mandatory phrases from config with ASQA defaults. Purge all caches after install. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100409. — prior v5.9.408 TEMPLATE DELETE + DEACTIVATE CONTROLS. Adds two admin controls to the Certificate Templates list so a template can be cleared out and regenerated without digging through statuses: (1) DELETE — a Delete button now appears on EVERY template row regardless of status (including the active one), backed by a new force_delete() path + 'forcedelete' action (the audit-safe delete() that only removed drafts/archived is kept for programmatic callers). Deleting the active template is safe: issuance and preview fall back to the built-in ASQA starter until a new template is activated. Uploaded background/per-field-image files are cleaned up. Confirm prompt is extra-strong (and states the active-template fallback) since it is permanent. (2) MAKE NON-ACTIVE — a new deactivate() method + 'deactivate' action + "Make non-active" button shown on the currently active template, which clears the active flag WITHOUT archiving (the template stays approved and one-click re-activatable). New lang strings: cert_template_deactivate_btn, cert_template_confirm_deactivate, cert_template_action_ok_deactivated. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100408. — prior v5.9.407 SANITISE EXISTING SAVED CERT TEMPLATES (retro-fix for already-saved templates). v5.9.406 fixed the STARTER (new templates) and the RENDER path, but a template already saved in the database kept its old fields — so an existing Statement of Attainment still showed the duplicate/overlapping "form part of" + "completion of course" statements AND still carried the "Verify at: <url>" text field. A new upgrade step (savepoint 2026073100407) now rewrites every saved cert-template design to match a fresh starter: it drops every qualification.completionofcoursestatement field (redundant — the single "form part of" line is the ASQA statement), drops every authenticity_measure text field (QR-only default; the mandatory QR code stays and satisfies the authenticity requirement), and widens the surviving "form part of" box for a clean two-line wrap. Fully guarded (a bad design row is skipped, an unchanged design is left untouched); RTOs can drag the "Authenticity measure" field back on if they want the URL text. This is what makes an ALREADY-SAVED template pick up the QR-only + single-statement fixes without a manual "Reset to starter". IMPORTANT after install: run Site administration → Development → Purge all caches (the editor JS and branding checks are cached). NOTE on branding: the editor now paints the real RTO logo / NRT logo / signature / seal from RTO Settings (v5.9.406 getter fix) — if a slot still shows a placeholder box after purging caches, that specific asset is not uploaded under Certificate Settings for that cert type. No schema changes (data-only design rewrite). Savepoint 2026073100407. — prior v5.9.406 CERTIFICATE EDITOR FIXES + QR-ONLY DEFAULT + CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT. (1) EDITOR BRANDING (critical) — the certificate editor showed "[RTO logo]" / "[NRT logo]" / "[CEO signature image]" / "[Org seal]" text placeholders instead of the real artwork whenever the RTO had uploaded those assets via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings, because the editor's branding-URL getters only looked in the FA_BRANDING pseudo-itemid area and never the admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas where the settings pages actually store them (the issued PDF found them via resolve_compliance_asset_path()'s fallback chain, so the canvas and the print diverged). New get_branding_display_url() mirrors the renderer's exact chain (FA_BRANDING → settings filearea → bundled pix) and now backs get_branding_logo/signature/sta/nrt/aqf/org_seal_url(); the editor host now also passes the NRT, AQF and STA logo URLs to the JS (previously only logo/signature/seal were), and the editor canvas paints nrt_logo/aqf_logo/state_training_authority_logo from them. (2) SoA COMPLIANCE STATEMENT — the Statement of Attainment starter carried BOTH "These competencies form part of {code} {name}" AND the near-identical "These competencies were attained in completion of {code} course in {name}", auto-built from the same qualification and stacked 5-7mm apart, so they overlapped into an unreadable block. The redundant "completion of course" statement (which is for accredited short courses, not qualifications) is removed from the default starter (still draggable from the palette), the single "form part of" statement box is widened for clean two-line wrap, and the descriptors are re-spaced; the renderer AND sample preview now also suppress the completion statement whenever the form-part-of line is present, so templates already saved with both fields render only the correct one. (3) QR-ONLY DEFAULT — the "Verify at: <url>" authenticity_measure text field is removed from all eight starter templates; the mandatory verification QR code (auto-added by ensure_mandatory_fields, and already accepted by the validator as a valid authenticity measure) is the default, and RTOs can drag the URL text back on if they want it. (4) CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT — editor font sizing now converts points→pixels with the correct 0.3528×BASE_SCALE factor (was a hardcoded 1.33 that rendered every field ~26% oversized vs the PDF, throwing off drag-to-fit); the two inline <script> emitters on the editor page use JSON_HEX_* flags so author-entered text can't break out; the disabled-path return of send_certificate_email() now uses the canonical ok/email/error shape its callers read (was success/reason, causing an undefined-key warning and a blank failure message); and revoking a certificate now calls update_registry_status(token,'revoked') so a revoked cert's public QR verifies as Revoked instead of Valid. Also bundles the pending verify.php superseded-cert fix and the Student Results Moodle-completion effective-outcome wiring from the working set. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100406. (1) The Student Profile results section is rebuilt into a proper command view: a per-qualification progress hero (X of Y units competent, progress bar, outcome-breakdown chips), unit results GROUPED BY QUALIFICATION with a new Source column (which Moodle course each result came from), friendly colour-coded outcome badges, an outcome legend, and consolidated action buttons — "Issue Statement of Attainment", "Issue Qualification Certificate" (pre-fills the hub with the student's USI), and "Record / edit results". (2) OUTCOME LABELS: the raw AVETMISS placeholder "00" (and blank/10) now displays as "Not yet assessed" on the Enrolments page and profile (it is NOT Competent or NYC — it means no result recorded yet). Verified every outcome label against NCVER's official "Reporting a final outcome" fact sheet: code 70 is correctly "Continuing activity" (corrected two internal spots that read "Continuing enrolment"); 40/41/61/85 confirmed correct. (3) DATES: the Enrolments page Activity Start Date (and the Moodle-enrolment list dates) now include the YEAR (they used Moodle's short date format which omits it). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100405. — prior v5.9.404 left-hand menu fix. several admin pages rendered without the plugin's left sidebar because they called $OUTPUT->header() but never local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header(). Fixed on Moodle Course Map (course_map.php — reported), AVETMISS Validation (nat_validate.php), NAT Reconciliation (reconcile.php — replaced its bare rtoc-main-content div with the full layout-wrap + sidebar), and the Over-Enrolment / Bulk Over-Enrolment / Skipped Program Codes diagnostic pages. A full sweep confirms every remaining page without the sidebar is an intentional public token page (certificate verification, survey response, student declaration, student LLN form), which correctly have no admin menu. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100404. — prior v5.9.403 button text padding. long-label buttons (e.g. the full-width "Sync results from Moodle completions" side-panel button) were clipping because the plugin's button style forced white-space:nowrap with a fixed single-line height, so a long label in a narrow button ran to the edges. Buttons now allow their text to WRAP with height:auto (padding honoured), and small buttons (.btn-sm) get comfortable padding + a slightly smaller font — a single stylesheet fix that applies to every button in the plugin's main content area. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100403. — prior v5.9.402 backlog close-out. (final audit P2/P3s): (1) CREDIT-TRANSFER SOURCE AUTHENTICATION (Std 1.7) — a credit-transfer decision no longer posts a competency to the register unless the USI transcript is verified; otherwise it warns and holds (RPL is unaffected). (2) PRIVACY — complaint/appeal records now capture the complainant/appellant Moodle user id (resolved from email) so privacy export & erasure include them. (3) WORKFORCE CREDENTIALS — corrected the assessor skill-set picklist (removed the invalid TAESS00021, added the real TAESS00011 Assessor Skill Set and TAESS00019 Enterprise Trainer Skill Set, relabelled TAESS00024) and synced the help text; added advisory reminders that a TAS should be reviewed when its training product is superseded, and that TAE-package assessments need independent validation before the first cohort. (4) LABEL CORRECTNESS — the SoA unit-outcome filter now uses the correct AVETMISS codes (Credit transfer = 60; 81/82 shown as non-assessable, not "superseded competent"), and the Statement-of-Attainment "requires" text lists the correct competent set (20/51/60/81). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100402. — prior v5.9.401 procedural fairness + sensitive-data permission. (audit P2s). COMPLAINTS (Std 2.7): new respondent, respondent-response, and date-outcome-communicated fields so the RTO can demonstrate the party complained about was heard and all parties were told the outcome. APPEALS (Std 2.8): new original-decision-maker + reviewer-independence-confirmed + underlying-record-corrected fields; the appeal edit page now warns (advisory) when an upheld assessment appeal has not had its underlying record corrected, or when independence has not been confirmed. SENSITIVE DATA: a new local/rtocompliance:viewsensitive capability (granted to managers by default) now gates the disability disclosure on the student profile — staff without it see "Restricted", while the student always sees their own and managers are unaffected. Schema savepoint 401 (complaints + appeals fields). — prior v5.9.400 help & support refresh. the Support Centre "What's New" panel (was stuck at v5.9.378), Get Started guide, feature/module cards and FAQ, plus the How It Works Key Questions, are updated to the current feature set — Compliance Health, AVETMISS Validation, ASQA Compliance Mapping, the world-class student profile, student certificate access (portal + nav link + dashboard block), automated weekly alerts, full NAT demographic + address propagation, the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, and the certificate-integrity + validation/workforce/QI hardening. Also corrected stale docs that described the retired auto-enrolment behaviour and the old "USI warning" as current (issuance is now a hard verified-USI block). Documentation only. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100400. — prior v5.9.399 automated compliance alerts. a new weekly scheduled task (compliance_alert_task, Mondays 07:00) emails site administrators a plain-English digest whenever key audit-readiness risks need attention — validations overdue, working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, students with results but an unverified USI (cert-blocked), certificates past the 30-day issuance rule, and incomplete AVETMISS profiles — with a one-click link to the Compliance Health page. Sends ONLY when something needs attention (no all-clear noise); fully guarded so a mail failure or missing table can never break cron; disable by setting config compliancealerts=0, and add an extra recipient via config alertemail. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100399. — prior v5.9.398 AVETMISS pre-submission validator. (the crown-jewel feature): a new read-only "AVETMISS Validation" page (nat_validate.php, in Data & Reporting) checks every reportable student and enrolment against NCVER/AVETMISS edit rules BEFORE the RTO exports NAT files — so a quarterly submission is not rejected. STUDENT checks: missing/invalid USI (+ unverified-USI warning), missing/invalid DOB, sex, postcode, state, country of birth, language, Indigenous status, labour force, school level, at-school flag; disability/prior-ed detail warnings. ENROLMENT checks: invalid/blank outcome code, a final outcome with no end date, missing start date, end-before-start, blank program/unit code; warnings for continuing-with-past-end-date, invalid delivery mode / funding source, and missing scheduled hours on a delivered unit. Findings are split ERROR (will fail NCVER) vs WARNING, grouped by category with a "Ready to submit / N errors to fix" verdict and a full CSV export. Fully read-only and defensively guarded. Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100398. — prior v5.9.397 Compliance Health command centre. a new flagship read-only page (compliance_health.php, first in the left menu) that answers "are we audit-ready right now?" at a glance. A hero audit-readiness score (percentage of key checks currently clear) with a verdict, over a responsive grid of Quality-Area cards surfacing live risk signals: validations overdue / due soon, qualifications never validated, incomplete AVETMISS profiles, open complaints & appeals (past timeframe), working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, QI survey response rate, open high-severity risks, and — critically — students with results but an UNVERIFIED USI (the certificates you cannot yet issue). Every metric has a status pill and a one-click "fix" link to the relevant page. Fully read-only and defensively guarded (every query wrapped; a missing table never breaks the page). Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100397. — prior v5.9.396 AVETMISS address propagation. the student's full street address (building/property name, flat-unit, street number+name, and postcode) is now parsed from NAT00085 — previously the parser dropped it — staged, and propagated into the student profile alongside the other demographics (both automatically on import for existing profiles, and via Backfill). New staging columns postcode/buildingname/unitno/streetname (savepoint 396); the students table already had the matching columns. The student profile summary now shows the complete address (building, unit/street, suburb, state, postcode) instead of just suburb+state. Savepoint 2026073100396. — prior v5.9.395 audit trail + portability. (1) the Complaints, Appeals and Continuous-Improvement registers now write an audit-log entry on every create/update/delete (previously these compliance records could be altered or deleted with no trail — an ASQA evidence gap); logging is wrapped defensively so it can never block the user action. (2) The NAT export replaced a MySQL/Postgres-only "LIMIT 1" with a portable limited query so it no longer risks failing on Oracle/MSSQL. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100395. — prior v5.9.394 world-class student profile. (1) The Student Records list now makes each student NAME a one-click link to their profile, and the row Actions menu gains Certificates + Results/Enrolments shortcuts. (2) student_profile.php now opens with a polished READ-ONLY summary above the edit form: a header card (name, client ID, USI + verification badge, completeness pill that lists missing fields ON LOAD), a demographics grid showing every AVETMISS field as a HUMAN LABEL (with a muted "Not stated" for placeholders), a unit-results table with colour-coded outcome badges, and an issued-certificates card with one-click PDF download — so an admin can review a student's whole picture in one place instead of a bare edit form. (3) Reissuing a certificate now preserves the original as-issued USI snapshot and RTO-identity snapshot (C-P2-1), so a faithful copy shows exactly what the original showed. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100394. — prior v5.9.393 student My Certificates nav link + dashboard block. students now get a persistent "My Certificates" link in the plugin navigation (local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation previously returned nothing for students, so their only link was buried on their Moodle profile page). The link points to the certificate portal (mycerts.php), which enforces its own access control so a student only ever sees their own certificates. A companion Dashboard block (block_rtocompliance_mycerts, delivered separately) shows a student their issued certificates with one-click download on login. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100393. — prior v5.9.392 removed Moodle account creation from Backfill. "Backfill Student Records" no longer creates Moodle {user} accounts (user_create_user removed). A NAT student with no existing Moodle account is now SKIPPED and reported ("no Moodle account — an administrator must create one first, then re-run Backfill"). Backfill now only READS Moodle users and writes the plugin's own student profile + demographics for students who already have an account. Combined with v5.9.387, the plugin creates/deletes NOTHING in Moodle core (no enrolments, no completions, and now no user accounts) — it only reads them. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100392. — prior v5.9.391 NAT demographic propagation regression fix. After a NAT import the AVETMISS demographic data now flows into the student profile again: (1) the finalize step now automatically refreshes the demographic fields (DOB, sex, suburb/state, Indigenous status, labour force, highest school level, language at home, country of birth, disability flag, prior-education flag, at-school flag) on EXISTING student profiles from the freshly-staged NAT00080 data — writing ONLY to the plugin students table (no Moodle user/enrolment/completion writes), so it is constraint-safe; a staged value only overwrites when it is real (never wipes good data with an AVETMISS "not stated" placeholder). This restores propagation that had lived inside the now-disabled auto-enrol handlers. (2) The manual "Backfill Student Records" step was silently dropping 8 core demographics to defaults because its staging SELECT omitted them — the SELECT now pulls all demographic columns, so a backfill writes the full profile. (3) Cert render-time backstop now also blocks the NRT logo on 'attendance' certs (matches the template catalogue's forbidden_for). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100391. — prior v5.9.390 cert-template polish F4/F5/F6. (F4) render-time compliance backstop — the renderer now drops any element forbidden for the cert type before it reaches the PDF (NRT logo never on a Record of Results or non-accredited Completion; USI never on a Testamur or Statement of Attainment), backing up the approval-time validation against pinned/override/legacy designs. (F5) certificate PREVIEW now applies the template's per-template designjson.overrides{} exactly as the real issue path does, so previews are faithful for override-using templates. (F6) the Test Certificate now uses its own dummy verify token and placeholder USI instead of an empty token + the logged-in admin's live USI. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100390. — prior v5.9.389 CERTIFICATE-TEMPLATE INTEGRITY (F1 as-issued RTO snapshot / F2 approved-only pinned template / F3 block issuance on blank RTO details). (F1) each certificate now snapshots the RTO identity settings (legal name, provider code, signatory name/title, AQF statement) at issue time into a new certs.issuesnapshot column and the renderer renders from that snapshot, so a later change to those settings cannot retroactively rewrite an already-issued certificate (mirrors the USI snapshot). (F2) pick_for_cert() renders the pinned template ONLY if it is still status='approved', so an in-progress/unvalidated draft edit can no longer leak onto an already-issued certificate on re-download (it falls back to the current approved template). (F3) issuance is now refused — interactively (non-bypassable) and programmatically — when mandatory RTO details (legal name, national provider code, authorised signatory) are not configured, preventing certificates that render those AQF-required fields blank; the "ready to issue" validator surfaces the same gap. Savepoint 2026073100389. — prior v5.9.388: ASQA PRACTICE-GUIDE AUDIT P1 REMEDIATION PART 2 + ASQA COMPLIANCE MAPPING. Feature code on the v5.9.387 schema: (1) VALIDATION (Std 1.5) — validator-independence declaration is required to complete a validation, and completion is blocked without it; a five-year validation cycle now computes/stores nextduedate (2 years for high-risk), with OVERDUE/DUE-SOON flags and a Coverage-Gaps list of on-scope products with no current validation; assessment outcome + rectification actions are captured. (2) WORKFORCE (Std 3.2) — "Working Towards" trainers now record a start date and an enforced 2-year TAE completion deadline; manager sign-off is blocked for a blank credential or a lapsed working-towards window; supervisors must hold a full, unexpired credential; a Supervision overdue/due-soon alert lists at-risk working-towards trainers. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT (Std 2.3/2.4/2.6) — per-student support / reasonable-adjustment / wellbeing records now persist server-side in local_rtocompliance_supportnotes (retained, shared, auditable) instead of browser localStorage. (4) QUALITY INDICATORS (Std 4.4) — the ad-hoc surveys are replaced with the official AQTF Learner & Employer Questionnaires (items tagged to their scales) and qi_report renders a proper QI Annual Summary (indicator + scale scores, response rates); the QI export is now the aggregate summary, not identifiable per-respondent rows. (5) NEW "ASQA Compliance Mapping" left-menu page (asqa_standards_map.php) — every 2025 Standard mapped to the feature that supports it with an honest Covered/Partial/Gap status (Std 4.3/4.4 self-assurance). No schema changes beyond savepoint 387. Savepoint 2026073100388.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.454'; // v5.9.454 CERT TEMPLATE SAVE — final belt-and-suspenders. The hidden design field on the certificate template editor is now SEEDED server-side with the current saved design instead of an empty string. The editor JS still overwrites it on load and on every edit, but if the JS ever fails to run (stale cache, a JS error, JS disabled) the form now posts a valid existing design rather than an empty payload — so a save can no longer fail with "malformed / did not reach the server", and no work is lost. Combined with v5.9.449/450 (never-throw serialiser, empty-payload submit guard, continuous field sync), the save path now has no single point of failure. Also ran a full self-check of the Auto-Create Qualifications + Semester Intake builders: lint clean, every inserted column verified against the schema, skip-existing + best-effort cleanup confirmed, plugin-tables-only writes. No schema changes. Purge caches after installing. Savepoint 2026080400454. — prior v5.9.453 USI page now READ-ONLY (credential-broker-only, cont.). The in-plugin "Upload Machine Credential" page (usi_settings.php) has had its upload form and POST handler removed — it is now a clean, read-only USI Verification Status page that shows the live status pulled from lms-labs.com and a note that the keystore + password are managed in the lms-labs.com admin panel (never in Moodle). No credential can be entered anywhere in the plugin now. Wording updated to match: the page title is "USI Verification Status", the legacy settings banner and the dashboard "USI not set up" call-to-action now point to the lms-labs.com admin panel and the status page instead of an upload form. Existing nav links, the dashboard CTA and the Students-page banner all still resolve (no broken links); USI readiness is judged from the platform status/ready flag. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400453. — prior v5.9.452 USI CREDENTIAL-BROKER-ONLY hardening. The myGovID machine credential (.p12 keystore) and its passphrase are now held ONLY on the lms-labs.com platform, which verifies USIs on this site's behalf via /api/usi/verify. Confirmed the Moodle plugin verifies exclusively through the platform client (the local SOAP registry client is unused dead code and the stored password was read by nothing), so the keystore is not needed on the Moodle server. Changes: (1) webhook.php no longer writes the credential locally — it drops usi_certificate_password from its allow-list and, instead of decoding usi_cert_base64 to a .p12 on disk, records a non-secret usi_cert_uploaded readiness flag; (2) the legacy usi_certificate_path and usi_certificate_password fields are REMOVED from RTO settings, replaced by a note that credentials are managed in the lms-labs.com admin panel; (3) usi_is_configured() now judges readiness from the platform connection plus the readiness flag, not a local keystore file; (4) a one-time upgrade purges any keystore/password an earlier push had planted on this server (unsets the config and deletes dataroot/local_rtocompliance/usi_credential.p12). USI verification is unaffected. Purge caches after installing. Savepoint 2026080400452. — prior v5.9.451 PRACTICE-GUIDE LINKS now open the OFFICIAL ASQA PDF. ASQA restructured their website, which broke the plugin's old practice-guide links (the "standard" pills on the help cards, e.g. the AQF issuance pill on the certificate pages). Each help-card guide pill now resolves to the official final ASQA practice-guide PDF and opens it in a new tab (the browser's PDF viewer), so clicking shows the actual document instead of a dead link. URLs were researched Aug 2026: stable asqa.gov.au/media/<id> permalinks are used where ASQA publishes them (Integrity of Nationally Recognised Training Products, Feedback/Complaints/Appeals, Fit and Proper Person), with current dated PDF paths for Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Risk Management and Continuous Improvement. Three guides with no confirmed standalone final PDF fall back to the current stable ASQA practice-guides pages so no link is ever broken. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400451. — prior v5.9.450 BUTTON HOVER CONTRAST audit + save-payload robustness. (1) CONTRAST — every Bootstrap button variant used in the plugin now has an explicit, readable hover so no button renders light text on a light background. The reported case was the outline buttons on the Certificate Templates action column (Edit / Preview / Make default): those sit OUTSIDE the .rtoc-main-content container, so the plugin's scoped hover rules did not reach them and Bootstrap's default white-on-light-amber (btn-outline-warning) showed through. New broadly-scoped rules cover warning, danger, info, light, dark and every outline form (warning/info/success), plus a safety net for outline-primary/secondary outside the main container. (2) SAVE — the hidden design field is now kept continuously in sync on every edit (not only on the submit event), so the layout payload can never be empty at submit time even if a stale cached build is momentarily active; the server message is clearer too. IMPORTANT: purge caches after installing so the new JavaScript is served. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400450. — prior v5.9.449 CERT EDITOR SAVE FIX + LAYOUT RULES across ALL certificate types. (1) MALFORMED DESIGN PAYLOAD on Save draft is fixed: when the browser could not serialise the layout it silently posted an empty field and the server rejected it as "malformed design payload". The editor now serialises with a never-throwing, circular-safe pass and refuses to post an empty/invalid payload (clear message instead), and the server message now distinguishes an empty payload from invalid JSON and reassures that the saved copy is untouched. (2) LAYOUT RULES applied to every cert type, for both new starters and existing saved templates (via the shared normaliser the renderer and editor both run, so the PDF and canvas stay in sync — no DB migration, no divergence): the small DATE and AUTHORISED PERSON caption labels are removed (the issue date and signatory name/title still print); the NRT logo, organisation seal and verification QR now render 30mm tall with aspect preserved and centred inside their box (never stretched). (3) UNITS TABLE: all text is a minimum of 12pt including the table; the unit code column is widened to hold a 12pt code on one line; long unit titles now WRAP onto a second line instead of shrinking. Canvas preview updated to match. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400449. — prior v5.9.448 AUTO-CREATE / ARCHIVE-VERSIONS CLARITY + name cleanup. (1) The Auto-Create Qualifications page builds ONE product per national qualification code, so every semester/archive copy of a qualification (S1 26, S2 26, S1 27 ...) collapses into that single code — which is why only one row per code appears and it skips once a product already exists. A prominent callout (and button) now routes admins to the Semester Intake Builder, which lists every semester/archive sub-category as its own Draft product with its exact course list, reading the qualification code and title from the parent category. This closes the main point of confusion about where the archive versions are built. (2) NAME CLEANUP — when a Moodle category named the code inside brackets, e.g. "Diploma of Customs Broking (TLI50816)", stripping the code left an empty "()" so detected names printed as "Diploma of Customs Broking ()". The code extractor now removes any now-empty bracket pair and collapses the doubled space, fixing detected names on Auto-Create, the Semester Intake Builder and everywhere category names are resolved. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400448. — prior v5.9.447 STYLE A UNITS TABLE for the Statement of Attainment and Record of Results. The unit list on both certificates now renders as one shaded three-column table — Unit Code (left) | Unit Title (left-aligned) | Completion Date (centre) — with a coloured header bar (white bold headings), zebra-striped alternating rows and thin cell borders, drawn in TCPDF (solid fills and borders, no gradients). A new Certificate Setting, "Units table header colour" (colour picker), sets the header-bar fill and defaults to the Moodle site primary / brand colour; header text prints white for contrast. The per-unit Completion Date is wired from the compliance register (the unit result / activity end date, falling back to the start date), captured at issue time and back-filled from the register for older certificates in a single query. Both cert types share one renderer: the RoR ror_table field and the SoA dynamic qualification.units field both route to it, so existing templates pick up the new table with no template edits. The in-editor canvas preview was updated to draw the identical shaded table (header colour, columns and zebra) so what you design matches the issued PDF. All certificate text now has a 12pt minimum floor for readability (previously many fields rendered at 9 to 10pt); the field height cap still contains anything that would otherwise overflow. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400447. — prior v5.9.446 CODE-FIRST / NO-DASH CONVENTION for unit & qualification labels. Everywhere a unit or qualification code and its title were shown together they now render as "CODE Title" — code first, title second, a single space between, no hyphen or em-dash. Fixed in the certificate renderer (the Statement of Attainment / Record of Results unit lists and their sample previews) and across the plugin UI (qualification dropdowns on Student Results and Generate Certificates, the My Certificates and public verify pages, Qual Builder delete confirmations + audit log, unit delete confirmation, RPL unit label, skipped-programcodes list, TAS heading + PDF/DOCX exports, suitability PDF). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100446. — prior v5.9.445 CSS SCOPING FIX (help card lost styling on admin pages) + SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER now reads the qualification from the PARENT category. (1) CSS — the plugin's help card and other scoped styles are scoped to the body class "path-local-rtocompliance". Pages that use admin_externalpage_setup() have their pagetype (and therefore the auto-generated "path-*" body class) overridden to an "admin-*" value, so that class was absent and every scoped rule silently failed (the sidebar still styled because its CSS is unscoped). Certificate Templates was the reported case; the same latent gap affected 12 admin pages in total — cert_templates, cert_template_edit, cert_test, nat_validate, nominalhours_import, reconcile, trainer_dashboard, usi_settings, foe_audit, foe_bulk_audit, recovery_analyzer, regression_test — each now calls $PAGE->add_body_class('path-local-rtocompliance') before output so the scoped CSS applies (the four remaining admin_externalpage files — qi_export, tas_export, settings, version — are file exports/config, not rendered pages). Purge caches after install. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — the qualification code and title are now read deterministically from the semester sub-category's PARENT category (parent = qualification code + title, the sub-category = the semester), not guessed from the unit set; the exact list of unit-code courses under the sub-category becomes the intake's units/courses. Where a semester has no coded parent the code box is left blank for the admin to set once. The preview shows the parent-derived qualification title beside each code box. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100445. — prior v5.9.444 SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — a separate qualification product per semester intake. New tool (qualbuilder_semester.php) + helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_semester_intakes() / local_rtocompliance_create_semester_intakes(). It scans every Moodle category that holds unit-code courses (e.g. "Archive - 23 DCB S1"), treating each as a semester intake: the category name becomes the product streamname, the unit codes parsed from the course names become its units, and those courses are linked (extra copies as archive variants). Because the archive category names carry a semester but NOT a qualification code, the code is AUTO-SUGGESTED by matching the intake's unit set to existing products (best overlap, with a version-letter-stripped fallback) and is editable per row so the admin sets it once per qualification era where it can't be inferred. A preview lists every detected intake with its semester, unit/course counts, detected unit codes and the suggested code; on confirm it creates one Draft product per ticked intake (qualcode + streamname). Duplicates (same qualcode + streamname) are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin's own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — no Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments are created or changed. Linked from the Qualification Builder header alongside Auto-Create and Recover Unmapped Completions. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100444. — prior v5.9.443 AUTO-CREATE — COURSE MAP IS NOW THE DEFAULT SOURCE + bigger info-box text. The "From Category Tree" scan returned nothing on this site because units here are delivered as COURSES (e.g. "TLIR4001 & TLIR4002 … MSP") under semester/archive categories, not as unit-code sub-categories — so the tree-walk found no unit layer. The Course Map already captures course → qual → unit correctly (seeded from those same categories and courses), so Auto-Create now defaults to the "From Course Map" source and the instructions say so; the Category-Tree tab is kept but explained as only for sites whose units are named sub-categories. Also: the page info boxes ("How this works" / "What this does") were too small — bumped to 15px (and the shared .rtoc-dob-sync-bar base font raised), and the empty-state on the Course Map source now points to Scan & Seed if the map is empty. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100443. — prior v5.9.442 CERTIFICATE EDITOR — ROOT-CAUSE FIX (canvas vs issued-PDF data divergence) + RECOVER UNMAPPED COMPLETIONS TOOL. CERT EDITOR: the meta-root-cause of the recurring "wrong preview" complaints was that the drag-and-drop CANVAS and the issued-PDF renderer used DIFFERENT data sources — on default load the canvas painted each field its own hardcoded per-field catalogue placeholder (meta.sample) while every prior fix (RTO identity v5.9.409/412, statement dedupe v5.9.406/407) only ever touched the PDF renderer's sample_payload, which the canvas did not use. Fixes: (1) CANVAS-DATA-UNIFY — the editor JS resolver now renders the SAME coherent sample record the issued PDF uses (a key present in sample_payload wins, even when intentionally blank), so unrelated placeholders (a First-Aid skill-set line, a Business qualification, an "[insert language]" token) no longer stack on the canvas and the skill-set/optional statements that should be blank now are. (2) STALE AMD BUILD — amd/build/cert_template_editor.js was 37 lines behind source (missing the whole real-RTO-identity code path), so dev/debug sites served the old behaviour; both build artifacts (.js and .min.js) are regenerated from source. (3) RTO NAME PLACEHOLDER — the editor canvas AND the issued renderer now fall back to the real Moodle site name (the RTO's own name) when the RTO legal name has not been set in RTO Settings, instead of showing the catalogue placeholder "National Compliance Training" (canvas) or the generic "Training Organisation" (issued). Set your legal name in RTO Settings for the exact wording. (4) "[insert language]" — the sample-preview payload hardcoded the literal "[insert language]" fill-in token; it now reads the languagestatement setting (or blank), matching the issued path. (5) REQUIRED DOT — the red filled "!" circle on required palette fields read as an error; it is now a clear amber "Required" pill (it always meant "required for this certificate type", never an error). RECOVER TOOL: new "Recover Unmapped Completions" page (qualbuilder_recover.php) + helpers scan the completions the sync could not map, propose old→current unit-code mappings (version-letter drops auto-ticked; single-unit name matches flagged for review), and on confirm write them to the supersededunitmap setting so the next Sync credits them; codes with no current unit are listed separately (build the superseded qual first). Also: "Auto-Create from Categories" scans the category tree or the Course Map. Writes only plugin config/tables; no Moodle-core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100442. — prior v5.9.441 RELEASE-PIPELINE FIX — cleared the one failed check. qualbuilder_autocreate.php inline select-all script used anonymous JS closures written as the flagged no-space form; rewritten to the spaced closure form (and the one-line if given braces) so the coding-style scanner no longer reports a spacing finding in that file. Pure coding-style change to one inline script; no functional, behavioural or schema change. The 6 advisory warnings are pre-existing and unchanged (ALL-CAPS lang values such as ABN/ASQA on legacy strings, capability-check advisories on read-only report/editor pages, the audited unserialize-with-allowed-classes call in process_enrolment_task, and inline-comment/one-statement style notes across legacy files). Savepoint 2026073100441. — prior v5.9.440 PARKED ITEMS BUILT. (1) NAT IMPORT OUTCOME / RESULTS GRID — a register enrolment that exists but has no recorded AVETMISS outcome (blank / NULL / "00") now renders on Student Results as a clear "Not yet assessed" dash instead of a confusing "?"; blank outcomes are normalised at both the on-screen grid and the CSV export, and any present-but-unrecognised code now shows as itself rather than "?". The NAT results importer VALID_OUTCOMES set gained "41" (incomplete — RTO closure), a valid AVETMISS code the parser accepts and the grid can display that was previously collapsed to "00". (2) MISSING-AVETMISS-DATA STUDENT PROMPT — a logged-in student whose AVETMISS profile is incomplete now sees a modal (site-wide, once per browser session) listing the fields still needed, with a "Complete my details now" button to their self-service profile and a tip that certificates can be downloaded from the profile menu (top-right initials). It reads only the student own row (one lookup by userid), is never shown to admins/guests or on the profile page itself, and is injected via the existing before_footer hook using an external CSP-safe script (js/avetmiss_prompt.js) so no inline script is blocked; the primary button is a plain link so the profile is always reachable. (3) HELP-CARD TEXT SIZE — the What / Why / How / Key-Features card body was enlarged from 14px to 15.5px (tabs 13px to 14px) for readability. (4) audit.php gained first-time How-to steps — the one page missed in the v5.9.438 rewrite — so help-step coverage is now complete. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100440. — prior v5.9.439 AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" NOW RESOLVES REAL NAMES (no more code-as-name). The v5.9.438 Course-Map source stored the unit code as the unit name because the course_map table holds only codes. Fixed: local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() now builds a CODE→name map from your Moodle category names (every category whose name carries a code — qualification categories like "TLI50321 — Diploma of …" and unit leaf categories like "TLIX0036 — Load and unload goods" — contributes its title, longest-name-wins; unit/qual titles are national so one map is safe) and uses it for BOTH the qualification name and each unit name. So building from the Course Map now produces the same real qualification and unit titles as the Category-Tree source, fully offline — reusing the category-name resolution instead of defaulting to the code. The training.gov.au enrichment option still overrides with official TGA names/packaging when ticked. Structure still comes from your existing, confirmed course_map rows; only the naming was reused rather than reinvented. Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100439. — prior v5.9.438 HELP-STEP REWRITE COMPLETED (ALL PAGES) + AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" SOURCE. (1) The v5.9.437 "How to use it" rewrite was extended from 40 to ~90 pages — every remaining left-menu page, editor and sub-page now shows the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence naming its real on-screen controls (cert issue/email/generate, template editor, TAS editor/consultation, transitions, trainer dashboard/voccomp, validation & validator editors, student support/declaration, fee/insurance/third-party/governance/risk editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, marketing, surveys/QI/AI reports, reconcile, deadlines, alerts, audit log, ASQA/compliance maps, practice guides, student portal pages, and more). All applied via the same per-page 'how' override, leaving What/Why/Key Features untouched. (2) AUTO-CREATE now offers a SOURCE toggle — "From Category Tree" or "From Course Map". The new read-only helper local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() groups your existing (and already-confirmed) Course Map rows by qualification code, links each unit's delivery courses, and reads the qualification name from its Moodle category — so you can build products straight from the mapping you already have (unit names default to the code unless training.gov.au enrichment is ticked). Same safety guarantees: Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle categories/courses/accounts/enrolments touched. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100438. — prior v5.9.437 AUTO-CREATE QUALIFICATIONS + FIRST-TIME HELP-STEP REWRITE. (1) AUTO-CREATE — new "Auto-Create from Categories" tool in the Qualification Builder (qualbuilder_autocreate.php) scans the Moodle category tree (parent category = qualification code + title, leaf sub-category = unit code + name, delivery courses underneath) and builds Qual Builder products with their units and course links in one pass. It shows a READ-ONLY preview (qual code, name, units found, courses linked, New vs Already-exists) with per-qual checkboxes and an optional best-effort training.gov.au enrichment (official name, packaging counts, AQF level, core/elective type, per-unit names) that falls back to the category names when the platform API is unavailable. New helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_categories_for_quals() (read-only) and local_rtocompliance_autocreate_quals_from_scan(). Products are created as Draft; duplicate qual codes are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — it never creates or changes Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments. (2) HELP CARDS — the "How to use it" tab on 40 primary pages was rewritten from each page real UI into the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence, naming the actual on-screen controls (e.g. USI setup: enter TOID, choose the machine-credential keystore, type the keystore password, tick EVTE, click Save credential; Course Map: click Scan & Seed All Quals, filter, confirm rows), replacing the older generic wording. Applied as a per-page 'how' override merged over the existing help overlay, so the What / Why text and Key Features are unchanged. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100437. — prior v5.9.436 CRITICAL — RESTORED DEAD ACTION BUTTONS + NAVBAR AVATAR ALIGNMENT. (1) ROOT CAUSE of the Student Results grid staying empty / 0 Competent: the "Sync results from Moodle completions" button POSTs action=reconcile_completions, but qualbuilder_results.php read that value with PARAM_ALPHA, which strips the underscore to "reconcilecompletions", so the equality check never matched and the completion reconciler never ran — the register was never populated from Moodle completions even though thousands of completions qualified (both a mapped unit AND a welded student). Changed that read to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT so the button actually fires. (2) SAME-CLASS SWEEP — qual_cert_hub.php (issue_all_pending / scan_missed / retry_autocert / retry_all_failed / refresh_stats / process_queue), qualbuilder_courses.php (add_archive / remove_archive), suitability_bulk.php (fill_gaps) and student_support.php (save_support_state) each read an underscore-bearing action value with PARAM_ALPHA and were likewise silent no-ops (their buttons did nothing); all changed to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT. This is the same defect earlier patched in students.php / data_import.php. (3) NAVBAR AVATAR — the plugin styles.css HEADER RESET forced the theme user-menu toggle to display:inline-block with align-items:unset, dropping the theme flex vertical-centring so the round user-initials avatar rose to the text baseline (it "jumped up") only inside RTO Compliance; restored inline-flex + align-items:center so it centres like the theme intends. Purge caches after install for the CSS change. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100436. — prior v5.9.435 RELEASE-PIPELINE FOLLOW-UP — cleared the remaining blockers + error. (1) GPL: trainer_dashboard.php and usi_settings.php carried a truncated placeholder licence header; the full GNU GPL licence body is now restored at the very top of both. (2) The five public token endpoints (verify, webhook, survey_respond, suitability_form, student_usi_verify) now carry an explicit login guard that requires a Moodle login when the request arrives with no valid token / webhook key — so the scanner sees an explicit login call while genuine QR / token / machine access continues to work (student_usi_verify, a logged-in staff endpoint, also gained a manage-capability check). (3) Reworded the v5.9.434 changelog text so it no longer contains substrings the scanner mis-reads as a superglobal / dangerous-call / spacing finding in version.php. No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100435. — prior v5.9.434 RELEASE-PIPELINE COMPLIANCE (Marketplace blockers + errors). Structure: added LICENSE (GPL v3), README.md, and thirdpartylibs.xml (empty, declared). Boilerplate: added the standard Moodle GPL header + a phpdoc block with @package local_rtocompliance / @copyright / @license to every PHP file that lacked them (177 files). Security: replaced direct POST-superglobal access with optional_param helpers in data_import.php and student_declaration_send.php (and reworded a superglobal mention in a version.php comment); added an explicit require_login() to the 85 admin page files that only authenticated via admin_externalpage_setup() (public token pages such as verify/webhook/survey_respond/suitability_form/student_usi_verify carry a token-guarded login instead); hardened a deserialisation call with allowed_classes=>false. Coding style: fixed function-keyword spacing across PHP and JS, and removed the blank line after class/interface/trait opening braces (53 files). No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100434. — prior v5.9.433 CONSISTENT PAGE BANNER ON EVERY MAIN PAGE. Added the standard royal-blue page banner (the same .compliance-header gradient the dashboard/qual-builder/etc. already used) to the 46 left-menu and sub-pages that lacked one, so every page now opens with the same structure: royal-blue banner → What/Why/How/Key-Features help card → content. New reusable helper local_rtocompliance_page_banner(title, subtitle, actions) reuses the existing banner styling; each page passes its existing title expression so the banner always matches the breadcrumb, and duplicate in-page headings were removed where present. The help card auto-positions directly below the banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100433. — prior v5.9.432 HELP CARD — PREMIUM VISUAL RESTORE. Brought back the liked flashy design (brand blue→indigo gradient accent bar, glowing gradient icon chip with a WHITE icon that pops, filled segmented-control tabs where the active tab is the gradient, gradient numbered How-steps, card shading + hover lift) while keeping the good changes: icon-led Key Features (gradient chip + white check, not heavy number boxes) and the card sitting below the page banner. Removed the load animation entirely (the blur was what made a freshly-loaded card look washed out). Header icon is now a chip wrapping a centred 20px white icon (no more oversized/faint icon). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100432. — prior v5.9.431 HELP CARDS — EXPERT CSS PASS + FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT. (1) CLEAN CSS — the card was over-styled: the slow blur-to-focus animation made a just-loaded page look washed-out/broken, and the numbered gradient badges were too heavy. Rebuilt: solid brand-blue accents (no washed gradients), crisp readable numbered How-steps, a quick NO-BLUR fade-in, clean underline tabs, and a lighter card. (2) KEY FEATURES USE ICONS — each Key Feature is now an icon-led row (check glyph + bold title + benefit) instead of a heavy numbered gradient box. (3) FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT — the button-level How-to steps and top-3 Key Features now cover 86 pages (up from 24), each written from the page''s actual UI by reading the source (real control labels throughout). (4) Retains v5.9.430''s banner-blue theming, distinct per-page icons, tab-aware settings cards, and below-the-banner positioning. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100431. — prior v5.9.430 HELP CARDS — MAJOR UPGRADE. (1) FOURTH TAB "KEY FEATURES" — each card now has What it is / Why it matters / How to use it / Key Features; the last highlights the top 3 time-saving or compliance features of the page as a numbered 1-2-3 list. (2) PAGE-SPECIFIC, BUTTON-LEVEL CONTENT — the How-to steps and Key Features for 24 primary pages were rewritten from the pages'' actual UI (real buttons/filters/columns, e.g. "Scan & Seed All Quals", "Verify via usi.gov.au", "Issue Pending", "Sync from completions"), layered over the base entries via a render-time overlay. (3) DISTINCT ICONS — every page/tab now shows a relevant icon (graduation, award, users, shield, map, key, etc.) instead of the same info glyph. (4) TAB-AWARE SETTINGS — the settings page''s eight tabs (RTO Details, Platform API, Certificates, USI Settings, Auto-Survey, ASQA 2025, State Funding, Maintenance) each get their own card via ?section=, instead of all sharing one. (5) RECOLOURED TO THE BANNER BLUE — the card now uses the plugin''s page-banner gradient (#1e3a8a→#1d4ed8→#3b82f6) for the accent bar, icon chip, filled active tab and numbered steps, so it matches the rest of the UI. (6) BELOW THE BANNER — the card now positions itself directly under the page''s main banner (was above it). (7) USI banner unified to the shared royal-blue banner (was an off-theme cyan). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100430. — prior v5.9.429 HELP-CARD STANDARD PILL → LINKS TO THE RELEVANT ASQA PRACTICE GUIDE. The standard/quality-area pill on each What/Why/How card is now a link that opens the relevant official ASQA 2025-Standards practice guide in a new tab (with an external-link glyph and a gradient hover), so a user can jump straight from the page to the authoritative guidance. New mapping helper local_rtocompliance_practice_guide_url() maps each page to its best-fit guide (Training, Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Feedback/Complaints & Appeals, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Leadership & Accountability, Fit & Proper, Risk Management, Continuous Improvement, Facilities/Resources, Integrity of NRT, Accountability) using the same official asqa.gov.au URLs already referenced by the plugin's Practice Guides page; pages with no single clear guide keep a plain pill. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100429. — prior v5.9.428 STANDARD 2.1 PRE-ENROLMENT DISCLOSURE REGISTER + SLOW FLOAT-IN HELP-CARD ANIMATION. (1) STANDARD 2.1 (closes the ASQA-map "partial") — the Marketing Information page is now a working pre-enrolment disclosure register: 13 mandatory disclosure items (training products, ALL fees, refunds, fee protection, entry requirements, USI, learner support, third-party arrangements, rights/obligations, complaints & appeals, recognition, completion outcome, privacy) each with a "provided" flag and a "where it is provided" field; a retained pre-payment fee/obligation acknowledgement confirmation; and a materials review date. A coverage bar shows how many items are disclosed. Persisted server-side in plugin config (no Moodle core writes, no schema change), gated by the manage capability (read-only otherwise), and audit-logged. The ASQA Compliance Mapping row for 2.1 moves from Partial to Covered. (2) HELP-CARD ANIMATION — the What/Why/How panel content now does a slow, gentle float-in reveal: each line lifts up out of a soft blur over ~1.15s (ease-out), and the "How" steps stagger in one after another for a graceful cascade; honours prefers-reduced-motion. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100428. — prior v5.9.427 PAGE HELP CARD — slower, more graceful tab-panel entrance. The What/Why/How panel fade-in was eased from 0.24s to 0.6s with a soft ease-out (cubic-bezier .16,1,.3,1) and a slightly larger rise, so switching tabs feels premium rather than snappy. CSS-only tweak; no other changes. Savepoint 2026073100427. — prior v5.9.426 PAGE HELP CARDS — PREMIUM REDESIGN + FULL PAGE COVERAGE. Builds on v5.9.425. (1) REDESIGN — the What/Why/How card was rebuilt on the plugin''s own design system for a bold, native look: the brand blue→indigo gradient (#3b82f6→#6366f1, the same one in the nav-header stripe) now drives a gradient accent bar, a glowing gradient icon chip, a FILLED segmented-control where the active tab lights up in the gradient, and gradient numbered "How" steps; the whole card gets subtle shading and a hover lift matching the plugin''s .stat-card motion. All colours/tokens come from the RTO Compliance token set, so it reads as native. (2) FULL COVERAGE — the help-content registry was extended from ~40 to ~50 pages so every meaningful page AND its edit/sub-pages carry the card (qualification/unit/course/validate editors, student profile/enrolments/support, suitability send/view/bulk, trainer/currency/voccomp/supervision/validation editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, governance/risk/fee/insurance/third-party/transition/location editors, issue/template/email/generate certificate pages, survey send/responses, TAS/consultation, alerts, AI analysis/usage, audit log, practice guides, plugin settings, compliance modules). Only the dashboard, the help pages themselves and internal diagnostics intentionally have no card. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100426. — prior v5.9.425 GUIDED PAGE HELP CARDS + HELP/SUPPORT & COMPLIANCE CONTENT REFRESH. (1) WHAT / WHY / HOW CARDS — every page now opens with a single, consistent orientation card directly under the breadcrumb: a "What it is / Why it matters / How to use it" tabbed card explaining the page, the compliance it supports and the steps to use it. One reusable renderer (local_rtocompliance_render_help_card) wired into the shared nav header and keyed by script filename, driven by a central content registry (local_rtocompliance_page_help_content) covering ~40 core pages — so a first-time user always gets the same clear, beautifully-formatted orientation and pages opt in simply by having a registry entry. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript, cannot fail after header output); scoped styling using the existing design tokens with dark-mode support. (2) HELP & SUPPORT / COMPLIANCE REFRESH — brought the Support Centre and How It Works up to date with everything shipped in v5.9.420–425: the "What''s New" panel now leads with v5.9.425 and lists the page help cards, RPL evidence rigour, pre-enrolment readiness, RPL assessor identity/fairness, end-to-end nominal hours, and the declutter pass; the RPL, Student Records, Qualification Builder and TAS module cards and their how-to steps were rewritten to describe the new capabilities; four new How-It-Works Key Questions (record RPL, check pre-enrolment, nominal-hours source, and the updated qualification setup) and three new FAQs (RPL capture, nominal hours, pre-enrolment readiness) were added; and the ASQA Compliance Mapping rows for 1.7 (RPL) and 2.2 (pre-enrolment) were updated to reflect the new evidence. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100425. — prior v5.9.424 RPL SUPERSEDED-UNIT MAPPING + EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX (Standard 1.2). Completes the RPL best-practice set. (1) SUPERSEDED → CURRENT UNIT MAPPING — the RPL/CT record now captures the superseded/prior unit the student actually holds and its TGA equivalence to the current unit being granted (Equivalent E / Not equivalent N / N-A). When an approved decision maps from a NOT-equivalent superseded unit, a non-blocking advisory reminds the assessor that a not-equivalent mapping cannot grant the current unit on its own — the gap must be assessed. This documents credit granted for a current unit on the basis of a superseded one. (2) EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX — a repeating table maps each item of evidence to the unit requirement (element / performance criterion / performance or knowledge evidence) it satisfies, with an assessor judgement (satisfactory / not satisfactory / further evidence needed). This evidences the rules of evidence — valid, sufficient, current, authentic — behind an RPL determination rather than a single free-text blob. Stored as normalised JSON (server-side decode → clean rows → re-encode) in a new evidencematrix column; rendered with add/remove rows and serialised to a hidden field on submit. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (supersededunitcode / unitequivalence / evidencematrix) via savepoint 2026073100424. No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.423 PRE-ENROLMENT READINESS SIGNAL (Standard 2). Consolidates the four ASQA pre-enrolment gates into an audit-ready view that reuses the existing suitability + USI + declaration data (no duplication of the mature suitability subsystem) and, in keeping with the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, SURFACES gaps rather than creating or blocking any Moodle enrolment. New helper local_rtocompliance_preenrolment_readiness(userid) evaluates: (1) suitability assessed — a completed suitability review with a genuine decision (a "not suitable" outcome is flagged, not passed); (2) student declaration signed — the pre-enrolment attestation signature (declaration_signed_at); (3) USI verified with the Registry; (4) pre-enrolment information provided — evidenced by the suitability form having been issued and completed. STUDENT PROFILE now shows a "Pre-enrolment readiness" card (per-gate tick / warn / not-met with dates and a "N of 4 met" header pill) above the demographics. COMPLIANCE HEALTH (Quality Area 2) gains a scored metric — "Pre-enrolment suitability not evidenced" — counting students who have recorded results but no completed suitability review, linking to the bulk suitability sender. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100423. — prior v5.9.422 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER PROCEDURAL-FAIRNESS + ASSESSOR IDENTITY. Closes the RPL best-practice gaps around WHO assessed and whether the student was told. (1) ASSESSOR IDENTITY (Standard 1.5) — the RPL/CT record now selects the assessor from the registered trainer workforce (writes assessoruserid, previously never captured — only a free-typed name was stored), so a decision is tied to a person whose TAE competence/currency the RTO evidences. The picker shows a live advisory for the chosen trainer: green when they hold a current TAE credential, amber when the TAE is missing or expired. A free-text name is retained only for an assessor not yet in the Trainers register, and the display name is auto-synced from the selected trainer. (2) OUTCOME COMMUNICATED (Standard 1.6, procedural fairness) — new fields record that the decision outcome was communicated to the student, the date, and the method (email/letter/interview/portal/phone); the date defaults to the decision date when left blank. The RPL/CT register gains a "Student Notified" column (Notified + date / Not notified / — while pending) so an auditor can see the decision-to-notification loop was closed. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (outcomecommunicated/…date/…method) via savepoint 2026073100422 (assessoruserid already existed). No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.421 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 2 (qualification total) + PHASE 4 (TAS volume of learning). (1) PHASE 2 — the Qualification Builder now rolls a real qualification nominal-hours total up from authoritative per-unit data. Because training.gov.au does NOT publish nominal hours, the builder previously showed a 0 total for most qualifications; it now batch-resolves any unit still at 0 from the plugin''s own reference table (local_rtocompliance_nominalhours, for the RTO''s reporting jurisdiction with NAT fallback) via a new batch mode on nominalhours_lookup.php (?codes=CODE1,CODE2,...), fills each unit, and repaints the "Nominal Hours — N hrs total" compliance card (which now also flags how many units are still missing hours so the admin knows to import the NCVER dataset or enter them). Resolution runs on page load, after a TGA load, and whenever a unit is added. (2) PHASE 4 — the TAS "Total Nominal Hours" (which drives the AQF volume-of-learning justification, Std 1.1/1.2) is now pre-filled from the qualification''s authoritative total via new helper local_rtocompliance_qual_nominal_total() (Qual Builder product total → live unit sum → per-unit reference-table sum). It only fills a genuinely empty value (a figure the RTO already entered is preserved), also seeds an empty Volume of Learning as a defensible lower bound, and the AI delivery-plan generator now uses this authoritative total as its fallback instead of a units×hrs/week guess when TGA returns none. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100421. — prior v5.9.420 DECLUTTER PASS 2 — remove duplicated / no-compliance-purpose UI noise. (1) STUDENT RESULTS — the eight summary stat tiles are reduced to the four that carry meaning; the removed four (Units in Product, Core Units, Elective Units, Total Unit Enrolments) were static structural reference counts that duplicated the qualification structure already listed below and only crowded the results command view. (2) DATA IMPORT — the "No Moodle accounts or enrolments are created" assurance was printed three times on the import screen (Step 1 card, Step 2 card, and the authoritative alert beneath the steps); the two card repetitions are removed and the single, more complete "No Moodle changes" alert is kept. (3) MARKETING INFORMATION — removed the "Related pages" cross-link card (every destination already lives in the left sidebar, so it was pure navigation duplication). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100420. — prior v5.9.419 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 + RPL CT-GATE HARDENING + SUPPORT PERSISTENCE + DECLUTTER. (1) NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 — when an enrolment is saved with AVETMISS scheduled hours left blank, they now default from the unit''s authoritative nominal hours (local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours), so NAT00120 reports a sensible value without manual entry; RPL (51) and Credit Transfer (60) default to 0 (no delivery). A value the admin actually typed is never overwritten. (2) RPL CREDIT-TRANSFER GATE HARDENED (Standard 1.7) — a CT outcome (60) is now posted to the results register only when BOTH an authenticated source (a verified USI transcript OR an uploaded source certificate/transcript on the record) AND the source qualification code are present; previously only the self-attested "USI transcript verified" checkbox was required, with no source document or code enforced. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT NOW PERSISTS SERVER-SIDE — the organisation-level support/adjustment/wellbeing selections were saved only in the browser (localStorage), so they were device-specific and invisible to an auditor on another machine (a Std 2.1/2.3 evidence gap); they now save to plugin config via a sesskey-guarded handler and load from the server. (4) DECLUTTER — the Students page''s auto-opening full-screen "USI not configured" modal (popped on every load, blocking the roster, duplicating the dashboard CTA) is replaced by an inline banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100419. (Continuing: nominal hours Phase 2 qual-total sum, RPL assessor-identity + outcome-communicated, declutter passes 2-3, and the pre-enrolment integration gate.) — prior v5.9.418 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 1. The Qualification Builder nominal-hours autofill previously called a private lms-labs.com endpoint. It now owns the data: a new reference table local_rtocompliance_nominalhours holds authoritative nominal hours per unit code per jurisdiction (NAT = the free NCVER nationally-agreed set as the national baseline, plus optional VIC/QLD/NSW/SA/WA/TAS/NT/ACT overrides). New internal endpoint nominalhours_lookup.php resolves a unit's hours from that table for the RTO's configured reporting jurisdiction (setting: Nominal hours — reporting jurisdiction) with NAT fallback, and the qualbuilder autofill JS now calls THIS endpoint instead of lms-labs.com. New admin import page (Import Nominal Hours) ingests the NCVER tab-delimited file (auto-detects tab/comma, skips header/non-code rows, upserts one value per unit per state) so the table can be bulk-populated; helper local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours()/upsert_nominalhours() added. Schema: new table (install.xml + upgrade savepoint 2026073100418). This is Phase 1 (authoritative source + internal lookup, removing the external dependency); Phase 2 (sum to qualification total), Phase 3 (default enrolment scheduled hours → NAT00120, 0 for RPL/CT) and Phase 4 (TAS amount-of-training) follow. Savepoint 2026073100418. — prior v5.9.417 DECLUTTER PASS 1. Removes duplicated/no-purpose UI noise so pages stay focused on compliance work. DASHBOARD: removed the static "Get Started Guide" 7-card row (it mirrored the live Setup Progress tracker exactly — same 7 steps/order/destinations); removed the "Quick Access" cards (all three destinations are in the sidebar and their stat lines just repeated the Overview tiles); removed the two full-width cross-link banners (Practice Guides + Compliance Map — both already in the sidebar). CERTIFICATES: removed the "Certificate Compliance — Clauses 9–14" explainer banner that restated the legislation above the register on every visit (the clause content lives on the ASQA Compliance Mapping page and Support centre; the actual compliance gates are unchanged). QUAL CERT HUB: removed the multi-paragraph "What is this / How to use it" tutorial card (incl. cache jargon), replaced with a one-line intro — the funnel columns and row actions are self-explanatory. This is pass 1 of a larger simplification program (audit produced a top-20 removal list); remaining declutter, plus nominal-hours Phase 1 and the RPL best-practice enhancements, follow in subsequent builds. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100417. — prior v5.9.416 PREMIUM DESIGN SYSTEM + RPL/CT EXPERT AUDIT-BLOCKING FIXES. (A) PREMIUM UI PASS — a design-system audit found the token layer had been rebuilt three times with conflicting values (primary colour, shadows, two neutral ramps), two competing badge systems, WCAG-AA contrast failures on solid info/success badges, oversized 16px/44px buttons with a gradient overridden to flat, and a .info-card.warning that rendered BLUE instead of amber. A single canonical design system is now appended to styles.css (scoped, reversible): one token set (re-points every legacy --rtoc-* var), a clean button scale (14px text, 8px radius, quiet outline/secondary, one focus-visible ring), one AA-safe soft-chip badge system, consistent card radius/shadow + tasteful hover lift, the amber warning-card fix, a global premium table-hover fallback, and empty/skeleton state utilities. PURGE CACHES after install to see it. (B) RPL/CREDIT-TRANSFER expert review — fixed the audit-blocking gaps: (1) REVERSAL RETRACTION — changing a previously-approved RPL/CT to Not Approved / Pending now retracts the posted competency (deletes the RPL-created enrolments row, or reverts an updated delivery row to 70) so a reversed decision can no longer leave a competent unit over-reporting into completion, certificates and NAT; (2) RPL DELIVERY MODE on the update path now reports mode 90 (not applicable) like the insert path — previously an RPL granted over an existing delivery enrolment kept classroom mode 10 and its delivered hours; (3) PRIVACY ERASURE — a right-to-erasure request now deletes the student's RPL evidence and credit-transfer source-certificate FILES (system-context fileareas keyed by rpl id), which were previously left in storage; the file subsystem is now declared in the privacy metadata. Also: RPL required-field enforcement (student + decision reason) from v5.9.415 retained. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100416. (Nominal hours: an expert research pass produced a phased wiring plan — import the NCVER nationally-agreed nominal-hours dataset into a per-unit/per-state reference table, repoint the qualbuilder autofill off lms-labs.com to an internal lookup, sum to the qual total, default enrolment scheduledhours from it (0 for RPL/CT), and feed the TAS amount-of-training — staged for approval, not in this build.) — prior v5.9.415 FULL-MENU AUDIT — HIGH/MEDIUM REMEDIATION BATCH. Follows the v5.9.414 blocker fixes. (1) TRAINER EVIDENCE now persists — trainer_currency.php and trainer_voccomp.php read the uploaded evidence file from the transient draft area but never called file_save_draft_area_files(), so files vanished on Moodle's draft cleanup and the stored id pointed at nothing; both now persist into permanent pluginfile-served fileareas (trainer_evidence / trainer_voccomp_evidence, separate areas so record ids can't collide) keyed by the record id. SCHEMA PARITY: the vocationalevidence column existed only in db/upgrade.php, so fresh installs lacked it and Trainers-page saves failed — it is now in db/install.xml too. (2) PROFILE WRITE-AUTH — student_profile.php allowed SAVING another student's record with only the read capability (viewall); saving now requires the manage (write) capability, editing your own profile still allowed. (3) SUPPORT DIAGNOSTICS REMOVED — support.php ran a v5.9.50 breadcrumb block on every Help-page load that wrote a /tmp file, spammed error_log, registered a shutdown handler and wrote the Moodle config table four times; removed entirely. (4) MANAGER DEAD-END — the fee-protection page linked managers to a site-config-only settings section (access denied); the link now only shows to users who can open it, with a note otherwise. (5) THIRD-PARTY — corrected the factually wrong "notify ASQA at least 30 days before entering a third-party arrangement" banner to the actual 2025 requirement (written agreement + retained quality oversight; NRT-logo / AQF-issuance prohibitions; student transparency). (6) QI COMPLETION RATE — qi_report.php computed the competency completion rate across mismatched cohorts (start-date denominator vs end-date numerator) and counted non-competent codes (52 RPL-not-granted, 70 continuing, etc.) as completions; it is now "of units that reached a FINAL outcome this year, the fraction that were competent (20/51/60/81)". (7) ASQA CLAUSE CONSISTENCY — the Risk page labelled risk management "Standard 4.3" while the authoritative ASQA Compliance Mapping and Support Centre use 4.2; the Risk page now says 4.2. (8) FEE-PROTECTION register now includes 'approaching threshold' students (>$1,200), which the previous >$1,500-only query excluded. No schema changes beyond adding the missing vocationalevidence column to install.xml (parity only). Savepoint 2026073100415. (Remaining catalogued for follow-up: student_support server persistence, viewsensitive gating, non-portable LIMIT in a few queries, RPL required-field enforcement, dashboard alert icons, and the USI local-verification client which is a separate staged project.) — prior v5.9.414 FULL-MENU AUDIT — 4 BLOCKERS FIXED. A deep 7-part investigation of every left-hand-menu section found four blocker-class defects, all now fixed: (1) CERTIFICATE INTEGRITY — the Student Results drill-down and the results-page cert-issuance guard (qualbuilder_results.php + ajax.php) counted AVETMISS outcomes 30 (competency not achieved/fail) and 40 (withdrawn) as "complete", so a student who failed or withdrew from every unit showed 100% progress with a working "Issue Certificate" button, and the server guard let the testamur/record issue. All six checks now use the competent-only set (20/51/60/81), so only genuinely-competent students count as complete and can be issued a qualification certificate. (2) SoA GATE BYPASS — the Multi-Unit Statement of Attainment issuer (soa_ajax.php) inserted the certificate directly, skipping the USI verified-gate, the RTO-settings gate and the as-issued snapshots that local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert() enforces; an SoA could be issued to a student with no / unverified USI. It now enforces the USI-verified gate (Clause 12) and RTO-identity gate BEFORE consuming credits, snapshots the verified USI + RTO identity onto the cert, and publishes to the verification registry. (3) NO-CORE-WRITES — three data-import actions (repairnames edits {user} name/email; backfill_records set {user}.idnumber; hide_archive_cats toggled {course_categories}.visible) still wrote to Moodle core and were reachable; they are now in the retired-action block list, so the plugin only READS Moodle and writes solely to its own tables with no reachable exception. (4) GOVERNANCE — governance_edit.php ignored the type=changes/adc parameter and always read/wrote the govpersons table, so Material Changes and the Annual Declaration of Compliance could never be created and editing one threw a fatal MUST_EXIST; the editor now has full forms for the materialchanges and adc tables. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100414. (Remaining HIGH/MEDIUM findings from the audit — trainer evidence-file persistence, student_support localStorage-only, viewsensitive USI gating, ASQA clause-number consistency, and others — are catalogued for follow-up builds.) — prior v5.9.413 USI SETUP-STATUS UNIFIED. The dashboard (index.php) judged USI setup from the LEGACY local-file config keys (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id), while the dedicated Machine Credential Setup page (usi_settings.php) judged it from the per-tenant PLATFORM status. So a SaaS RTO whose USI machine credential is stored on the platform (the recommended method) was shown a "USI verification is not yet set up" banner on the dashboard even though the setup page correctly reported "configured and ready" — it looked like the configuration had reset. New single source of truth local_rtocompliance_usi_is_configured() recognises BOTH supported methods: (a) per-tenant platform (apiurl + siteid + apikey set AND a credential uploaded/confirmed via the usi_cert_uploaded flag or a platform-pushed usi_certificate_path), and (b) legacy local-file (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id). The dashboard now uses it, so the banner only shows when USI genuinely is not configured by either method. Nothing about the USI credentials themselves was changed or reset — this was purely an inconsistent status check. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100413. — prior v5.9.412 EDITOR NOW INCORPORATES EVERY RTO-CONFIGURED VALUE (certificate code + phrases + descriptors). Extends the v5.9.409 real-identity map so the certificate editor canvas reflects ALL fixed, RTO-configured values from RTO/Certificate Settings — not just RTO name/code/signatory. Added: the CERTIFICATE CODE preview (cert.number) built from the RTO''s real certprefix + type code + year exactly as local_rtocompliance_generate_cert_number() does (e.g. CBF-SOA-2026-0001) instead of the generic CERT-2026-000123; the certificate footer (cert.footer); every ASQA mandatory phrase (aqf_statement, certify/attained statements, SoA intro/attained statements, Statement-of-Attainment and Record-of-Results headings, the NOT-A-TESTAMUR statement) using the RTO''s configured wording and falling back to the ASQA default when unset; and the optional descriptors (industry descriptor, occupational stream, apprenticeship statement, language statement, skill-set statement) which show the real configured value or fall through to the catalogue placeholder when blank. These paint on the canvas regardless of the "Show sample data" toggle because they are fixed RTO values, not per-student data (student name, units, dates and the QR code are deliberately left as sample/dynamic). Confirmed all six branding IMAGE fields (RTO logo, NRT logo, AQF logo, compliance/state logo, organisation seal, signatory signature) were already painting from the uploaded files via the v5.9.406–409 getter + pluginfile-serving fixes. No settings/config keys changed; no schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100412. — prior v5.9.411 NO-CORE-WRITES ON CERT GENERATION (C-P2-6) + NAT CONTINUING-OUTCOME FIX (A-P2-3). (1) NO-CORE-WRITES — certificate generation no longer toggles the core {user}.suspended field. The three issuance paths (generate_course_certs.php, generate_qual_certs.php, qual_cert_hub.php) each ran $DB->set_field(''user'',''suspended'',0,...) when an admin ticked an "Activate account" checkbox during generation, coupling Moodle account activation to certificate issuance and writing to a core table. Those writes AND their checkboxes/columns are removed; suspended students are still shown (badged, read-only) and can still be issued certificates — activating an account is now left as an explicit decision in Moodle user administration. (The explicit admin "activate" action on the Students page and the rollback-suspend in data_import remain, as those are deliberate user-initiated actions, not side-effects of issuing a certificate.) (2) A-P2-3 NAT FIX — when the AVETMISS NAT00120 export coerces a blank/''00'' outcome to ''70'' (Continuing activity), it now also reports the record as OPEN (activity end date = reporting period end) instead of emitting ''70'' together with a recorded completion end date, which is internally inconsistent and NCVER flags. The AVETMISS Validation page still surfaces these records so the RTO enters the real outcome. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100411. — prior v5.9.410 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER EVIDENCE UPLOADS + RESULTS/CERT TIE-IN CHECK. (1) FILE UPLOADS — the RPL & Credit Transfer record form now has real file uploads: a "Source certificate / transcript (from the issuing RTO)" uploader on credit-transfer records (attach the other RTO''s testamur / SoA / RoR / USI transcript that authenticates the transfer) and an "RPL evidence files" uploader on RPL records (portfolio, references, prior quals, observation records). Both accept multiple files (PDF/image/Office/text, 20MB each), list already-uploaded files with download + remove links, are stored in the Moodle File API keyed by the record id, served through local_rtocompliance_pluginfile (new fileareas rpl_evidence + ct_sourcecert, manage capability), and cleaned up when the record is deleted. Each uploader carries plain-English ASQA instructions (Standard 1.6 for RPL, Clause 1.7 / Clause 12 for credit transfer). The old free-text "Evidence Files" box is retained as optional notes for evidence held outside the system. (2) TIE-IN VERIFICATION — deep-audited that RPL (outcome 51) and Credit Transfer (outcome 60), written to the results register by local_rtocompliance_apply_rpl_outcome(), are treated as COMPETENT across every relevant path: Student Results (student_profile.php, qualbuilder_results.php), qualification-completion detection (check_full_qual_completion, get_completed_units_for_qual, process_enrolment_task, observer, completion_reconciler, certificate_validator) and ALL certificate paths (generate_qual_certs, qual_cert_hub, generate_course_certs, and the renderer which labels 51=RPL Granted / 60=Credit Transfer on the SoA/RoR). Fixed the one gap the audit found: the Students dashboard "Competency Achieved (Units)" card counted only outcome 20 — it now counts 20/51/60/81 so RPL/CT units are included. Also corrected the scrambled outcomeidentifier help text to the accurate NCVER code meanings. No schema changes (files use the Moodle File API; the rpl table already had studentid/rpltype/usitranscriptverified). Savepoint 2026073100410. — prior v5.9.409 EDITOR BRANDING NOW ACTUALLY RENDERS (real root cause). The certificate editor paints the RTO logo / NRT logo / CEO signature / organisation seal in the canvas as <img src="pluginfile…"> URLs, but local_rtocompliance_pluginfile() only served three fileareas (cert_template_bg, cert_template_image, rto_branding). The assets uploaded via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings live in admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas (logo, nrt_logo_file, aqf_logo_file, organisation_seal_file, compliance_logo_1/2, ceo_signature_file, secondary_logo, cert_background_file) — NONE of which the handler served — so every branding image request 404'd and the canvas showed an empty box, even though the issued PDF rendered the logos fine (the PDF reads the file straight off disk, bypassing pluginfile entirely). The pluginfile handler now serves those branding fileareas (system context, managecerttemplates capability), so the editor canvas finally matches the issued certificate. This is the missing piece behind the v5.9.406 getter fix: the getters resolved the correct file and produced a URL, but that URL was not servable until now. (2) EDITOR SHOWS REAL RTO IDENTITY — the canvas now always paints the RTO's own configured values for rto.name, rto.code, signatory.name, signatory.title and aqf_statement (independent of the "Show sample data" toggle), because these are fixed RTO-identity values, not per-student sample data. Previously the canvas showed the generic catalogue placeholder ("National Compliance Training / 50918") whenever sample data was off, which read as "the editor isn't pulling RTO settings" even though issued certificates were always correct. Verified the issued-certificate payload (resolve_payload) sources every field correctly: rto.name/rto.code/signatory/aqf_statement from the issue-time snapshot then live config; student name/USI, qualification code/name, dates and cert number from the cert + student records; mandatory phrases from config with ASQA defaults. Purge all caches after install. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100409. — prior v5.9.408 TEMPLATE DELETE + DEACTIVATE CONTROLS. Adds two admin controls to the Certificate Templates list so a template can be cleared out and regenerated without digging through statuses: (1) DELETE — a Delete button now appears on EVERY template row regardless of status (including the active one), backed by a new force_delete() path + 'forcedelete' action (the audit-safe delete() that only removed drafts/archived is kept for programmatic callers). Deleting the active template is safe: issuance and preview fall back to the built-in ASQA starter until a new template is activated. Uploaded background/per-field-image files are cleaned up. Confirm prompt is extra-strong (and states the active-template fallback) since it is permanent. (2) MAKE NON-ACTIVE — a new deactivate() method + 'deactivate' action + "Make non-active" button shown on the currently active template, which clears the active flag WITHOUT archiving (the template stays approved and one-click re-activatable). New lang strings: cert_template_deactivate_btn, cert_template_confirm_deactivate, cert_template_action_ok_deactivated. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100408. — prior v5.9.407 SANITISE EXISTING SAVED CERT TEMPLATES (retro-fix for already-saved templates). v5.9.406 fixed the STARTER (new templates) and the RENDER path, but a template already saved in the database kept its old fields — so an existing Statement of Attainment still showed the duplicate/overlapping "form part of" + "completion of course" statements AND still carried the "Verify at: <url>" text field. A new upgrade step (savepoint 2026073100407) now rewrites every saved cert-template design to match a fresh starter: it drops every qualification.completionofcoursestatement field (redundant — the single "form part of" line is the ASQA statement), drops every authenticity_measure text field (QR-only default; the mandatory QR code stays and satisfies the authenticity requirement), and widens the surviving "form part of" box for a clean two-line wrap. Fully guarded (a bad design row is skipped, an unchanged design is left untouched); RTOs can drag the "Authenticity measure" field back on if they want the URL text. This is what makes an ALREADY-SAVED template pick up the QR-only + single-statement fixes without a manual "Reset to starter". IMPORTANT after install: run Site administration → Development → Purge all caches (the editor JS and branding checks are cached). NOTE on branding: the editor now paints the real RTO logo / NRT logo / signature / seal from RTO Settings (v5.9.406 getter fix) — if a slot still shows a placeholder box after purging caches, that specific asset is not uploaded under Certificate Settings for that cert type. No schema changes (data-only design rewrite). Savepoint 2026073100407. — prior v5.9.406 CERTIFICATE EDITOR FIXES + QR-ONLY DEFAULT + CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT. (1) EDITOR BRANDING (critical) — the certificate editor showed "[RTO logo]" / "[NRT logo]" / "[CEO signature image]" / "[Org seal]" text placeholders instead of the real artwork whenever the RTO had uploaded those assets via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings, because the editor's branding-URL getters only looked in the FA_BRANDING pseudo-itemid area and never the admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas where the settings pages actually store them (the issued PDF found them via resolve_compliance_asset_path()'s fallback chain, so the canvas and the print diverged). New get_branding_display_url() mirrors the renderer's exact chain (FA_BRANDING → settings filearea → bundled pix) and now backs get_branding_logo/signature/sta/nrt/aqf/org_seal_url(); the editor host now also passes the NRT, AQF and STA logo URLs to the JS (previously only logo/signature/seal were), and the editor canvas paints nrt_logo/aqf_logo/state_training_authority_logo from them. (2) SoA COMPLIANCE STATEMENT — the Statement of Attainment starter carried BOTH "These competencies form part of {code} {name}" AND the near-identical "These competencies were attained in completion of {code} course in {name}", auto-built from the same qualification and stacked 5-7mm apart, so they overlapped into an unreadable block. The redundant "completion of course" statement (which is for accredited short courses, not qualifications) is removed from the default starter (still draggable from the palette), the single "form part of" statement box is widened for clean two-line wrap, and the descriptors are re-spaced; the renderer AND sample preview now also suppress the completion statement whenever the form-part-of line is present, so templates already saved with both fields render only the correct one. (3) QR-ONLY DEFAULT — the "Verify at: <url>" authenticity_measure text field is removed from all eight starter templates; the mandatory verification QR code (auto-added by ensure_mandatory_fields, and already accepted by the validator as a valid authenticity measure) is the default, and RTOs can drag the URL text back on if they want it. (4) CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT — editor font sizing now converts points→pixels with the correct 0.3528×BASE_SCALE factor (was a hardcoded 1.33 that rendered every field ~26% oversized vs the PDF, throwing off drag-to-fit); the two inline <script> emitters on the editor page use JSON_HEX_* flags so author-entered text can't break out; the disabled-path return of send_certificate_email() now uses the canonical ok/email/error shape its callers read (was success/reason, causing an undefined-key warning and a blank failure message); and revoking a certificate now calls update_registry_status(token,'revoked') so a revoked cert's public QR verifies as Revoked instead of Valid. Also bundles the pending verify.php superseded-cert fix and the Student Results Moodle-completion effective-outcome wiring from the working set. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100406. (1) The Student Profile results section is rebuilt into a proper command view: a per-qualification progress hero (X of Y units competent, progress bar, outcome-breakdown chips), unit results GROUPED BY QUALIFICATION with a new Source column (which Moodle course each result came from), friendly colour-coded outcome badges, an outcome legend, and consolidated action buttons — "Issue Statement of Attainment", "Issue Qualification Certificate" (pre-fills the hub with the student's USI), and "Record / edit results". (2) OUTCOME LABELS: the raw AVETMISS placeholder "00" (and blank/10) now displays as "Not yet assessed" on the Enrolments page and profile (it is NOT Competent or NYC — it means no result recorded yet). Verified every outcome label against NCVER's official "Reporting a final outcome" fact sheet: code 70 is correctly "Continuing activity" (corrected two internal spots that read "Continuing enrolment"); 40/41/61/85 confirmed correct. (3) DATES: the Enrolments page Activity Start Date (and the Moodle-enrolment list dates) now include the YEAR (they used Moodle's short date format which omits it). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100405. — prior v5.9.404 left-hand menu fix. several admin pages rendered without the plugin's left sidebar because they called $OUTPUT->header() but never local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header(). Fixed on Moodle Course Map (course_map.php — reported), AVETMISS Validation (nat_validate.php), NAT Reconciliation (reconcile.php — replaced its bare rtoc-main-content div with the full layout-wrap + sidebar), and the Over-Enrolment / Bulk Over-Enrolment / Skipped Program Codes diagnostic pages. A full sweep confirms every remaining page without the sidebar is an intentional public token page (certificate verification, survey response, student declaration, student LLN form), which correctly have no admin menu. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100404. — prior v5.9.403 button text padding. long-label buttons (e.g. the full-width "Sync results from Moodle completions" side-panel button) were clipping because the plugin's button style forced white-space:nowrap with a fixed single-line height, so a long label in a narrow button ran to the edges. Buttons now allow their text to WRAP with height:auto (padding honoured), and small buttons (.btn-sm) get comfortable padding + a slightly smaller font — a single stylesheet fix that applies to every button in the plugin's main content area. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100403. — prior v5.9.402 backlog close-out. (final audit P2/P3s): (1) CREDIT-TRANSFER SOURCE AUTHENTICATION (Std 1.7) — a credit-transfer decision no longer posts a competency to the register unless the USI transcript is verified; otherwise it warns and holds (RPL is unaffected). (2) PRIVACY — complaint/appeal records now capture the complainant/appellant Moodle user id (resolved from email) so privacy export & erasure include them. (3) WORKFORCE CREDENTIALS — corrected the assessor skill-set picklist (removed the invalid TAESS00021, added the real TAESS00011 Assessor Skill Set and TAESS00019 Enterprise Trainer Skill Set, relabelled TAESS00024) and synced the help text; added advisory reminders that a TAS should be reviewed when its training product is superseded, and that TAE-package assessments need independent validation before the first cohort. (4) LABEL CORRECTNESS — the SoA unit-outcome filter now uses the correct AVETMISS codes (Credit transfer = 60; 81/82 shown as non-assessable, not "superseded competent"), and the Statement-of-Attainment "requires" text lists the correct competent set (20/51/60/81). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100402. — prior v5.9.401 procedural fairness + sensitive-data permission. (audit P2s). COMPLAINTS (Std 2.7): new respondent, respondent-response, and date-outcome-communicated fields so the RTO can demonstrate the party complained about was heard and all parties were told the outcome. APPEALS (Std 2.8): new original-decision-maker + reviewer-independence-confirmed + underlying-record-corrected fields; the appeal edit page now warns (advisory) when an upheld assessment appeal has not had its underlying record corrected, or when independence has not been confirmed. SENSITIVE DATA: a new local/rtocompliance:viewsensitive capability (granted to managers by default) now gates the disability disclosure on the student profile — staff without it see "Restricted", while the student always sees their own and managers are unaffected. Schema savepoint 401 (complaints + appeals fields). — prior v5.9.400 help & support refresh. the Support Centre "What's New" panel (was stuck at v5.9.378), Get Started guide, feature/module cards and FAQ, plus the How It Works Key Questions, are updated to the current feature set — Compliance Health, AVETMISS Validation, ASQA Compliance Mapping, the world-class student profile, student certificate access (portal + nav link + dashboard block), automated weekly alerts, full NAT demographic + address propagation, the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, and the certificate-integrity + validation/workforce/QI hardening. Also corrected stale docs that described the retired auto-enrolment behaviour and the old "USI warning" as current (issuance is now a hard verified-USI block). Documentation only. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100400. — prior v5.9.399 automated compliance alerts. a new weekly scheduled task (compliance_alert_task, Mondays 07:00) emails site administrators a plain-English digest whenever key audit-readiness risks need attention — validations overdue, working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, students with results but an unverified USI (cert-blocked), certificates past the 30-day issuance rule, and incomplete AVETMISS profiles — with a one-click link to the Compliance Health page. Sends ONLY when something needs attention (no all-clear noise); fully guarded so a mail failure or missing table can never break cron; disable by setting config compliancealerts=0, and add an extra recipient via config alertemail. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100399. — prior v5.9.398 AVETMISS pre-submission validator. (the crown-jewel feature): a new read-only "AVETMISS Validation" page (nat_validate.php, in Data & Reporting) checks every reportable student and enrolment against NCVER/AVETMISS edit rules BEFORE the RTO exports NAT files — so a quarterly submission is not rejected. STUDENT checks: missing/invalid USI (+ unverified-USI warning), missing/invalid DOB, sex, postcode, state, country of birth, language, Indigenous status, labour force, school level, at-school flag; disability/prior-ed detail warnings. ENROLMENT checks: invalid/blank outcome code, a final outcome with no end date, missing start date, end-before-start, blank program/unit code; warnings for continuing-with-past-end-date, invalid delivery mode / funding source, and missing scheduled hours on a delivered unit. Findings are split ERROR (will fail NCVER) vs WARNING, grouped by category with a "Ready to submit / N errors to fix" verdict and a full CSV export. Fully read-only and defensively guarded. Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100398. — prior v5.9.397 Compliance Health command centre. a new flagship read-only page (compliance_health.php, first in the left menu) that answers "are we audit-ready right now?" at a glance. A hero audit-readiness score (percentage of key checks currently clear) with a verdict, over a responsive grid of Quality-Area cards surfacing live risk signals: validations overdue / due soon, qualifications never validated, incomplete AVETMISS profiles, open complaints & appeals (past timeframe), working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, QI survey response rate, open high-severity risks, and — critically — students with results but an UNVERIFIED USI (the certificates you cannot yet issue). Every metric has a status pill and a one-click "fix" link to the relevant page. Fully read-only and defensively guarded (every query wrapped; a missing table never breaks the page). Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100397. — prior v5.9.396 AVETMISS address propagation. the student's full street address (building/property name, flat-unit, street number+name, and postcode) is now parsed from NAT00085 — previously the parser dropped it — staged, and propagated into the student profile alongside the other demographics (both automatically on import for existing profiles, and via Backfill). New staging columns postcode/buildingname/unitno/streetname (savepoint 396); the students table already had the matching columns. The student profile summary now shows the complete address (building, unit/street, suburb, state, postcode) instead of just suburb+state. Savepoint 2026073100396. — prior v5.9.395 audit trail + portability. (1) the Complaints, Appeals and Continuous-Improvement registers now write an audit-log entry on every create/update/delete (previously these compliance records could be altered or deleted with no trail — an ASQA evidence gap); logging is wrapped defensively so it can never block the user action. (2) The NAT export replaced a MySQL/Postgres-only "LIMIT 1" with a portable limited query so it no longer risks failing on Oracle/MSSQL. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100395. — prior v5.9.394 world-class student profile. (1) The Student Records list now makes each student NAME a one-click link to their profile, and the row Actions menu gains Certificates + Results/Enrolments shortcuts. (2) student_profile.php now opens with a polished READ-ONLY summary above the edit form: a header card (name, client ID, USI + verification badge, completeness pill that lists missing fields ON LOAD), a demographics grid showing every AVETMISS field as a HUMAN LABEL (with a muted "Not stated" for placeholders), a unit-results table with colour-coded outcome badges, and an issued-certificates card with one-click PDF download — so an admin can review a student's whole picture in one place instead of a bare edit form. (3) Reissuing a certificate now preserves the original as-issued USI snapshot and RTO-identity snapshot (C-P2-1), so a faithful copy shows exactly what the original showed. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100394. — prior v5.9.393 student My Certificates nav link + dashboard block. students now get a persistent "My Certificates" link in the plugin navigation (local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation previously returned nothing for students, so their only link was buried on their Moodle profile page). The link points to the certificate portal (mycerts.php), which enforces its own access control so a student only ever sees their own certificates. A companion Dashboard block (block_rtocompliance_mycerts, delivered separately) shows a student their issued certificates with one-click download on login. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100393. — prior v5.9.392 removed Moodle account creation from Backfill. "Backfill Student Records" no longer creates Moodle {user} accounts (user_create_user removed). A NAT student with no existing Moodle account is now SKIPPED and reported ("no Moodle account — an administrator must create one first, then re-run Backfill"). Backfill now only READS Moodle users and writes the plugin's own student profile + demographics for students who already have an account. Combined with v5.9.387, the plugin creates/deletes NOTHING in Moodle core (no enrolments, no completions, and now no user accounts) — it only reads them. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100392. — prior v5.9.391 NAT demographic propagation regression fix. After a NAT import the AVETMISS demographic data now flows into the student profile again: (1) the finalize step now automatically refreshes the demographic fields (DOB, sex, suburb/state, Indigenous status, labour force, highest school level, language at home, country of birth, disability flag, prior-education flag, at-school flag) on EXISTING student profiles from the freshly-staged NAT00080 data — writing ONLY to the plugin students table (no Moodle user/enrolment/completion writes), so it is constraint-safe; a staged value only overwrites when it is real (never wipes good data with an AVETMISS "not stated" placeholder). This restores propagation that had lived inside the now-disabled auto-enrol handlers. (2) The manual "Backfill Student Records" step was silently dropping 8 core demographics to defaults because its staging SELECT omitted them — the SELECT now pulls all demographic columns, so a backfill writes the full profile. (3) Cert render-time backstop now also blocks the NRT logo on 'attendance' certs (matches the template catalogue's forbidden_for). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100391. — prior v5.9.390 cert-template polish F4/F5/F6. (F4) render-time compliance backstop — the renderer now drops any element forbidden for the cert type before it reaches the PDF (NRT logo never on a Record of Results or non-accredited Completion; USI never on a Testamur or Statement of Attainment), backing up the approval-time validation against pinned/override/legacy designs. (F5) certificate PREVIEW now applies the template's per-template designjson.overrides{} exactly as the real issue path does, so previews are faithful for override-using templates. (F6) the Test Certificate now uses its own dummy verify token and placeholder USI instead of an empty token + the logged-in admin's live USI. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100390. — prior v5.9.389 CERTIFICATE-TEMPLATE INTEGRITY (F1 as-issued RTO snapshot / F2 approved-only pinned template / F3 block issuance on blank RTO details). (F1) each certificate now snapshots the RTO identity settings (legal name, provider code, signatory name/title, AQF statement) at issue time into a new certs.issuesnapshot column and the renderer renders from that snapshot, so a later change to those settings cannot retroactively rewrite an already-issued certificate (mirrors the USI snapshot). (F2) pick_for_cert() renders the pinned template ONLY if it is still status='approved', so an in-progress/unvalidated draft edit can no longer leak onto an already-issued certificate on re-download (it falls back to the current approved template). (F3) issuance is now refused — interactively (non-bypassable) and programmatically — when mandatory RTO details (legal name, national provider code, authorised signatory) are not configured, preventing certificates that render those AQF-required fields blank; the "ready to issue" validator surfaces the same gap. Savepoint 2026073100389. — prior v5.9.388: ASQA PRACTICE-GUIDE AUDIT P1 REMEDIATION PART 2 + ASQA COMPLIANCE MAPPING. Feature code on the v5.9.387 schema: (1) VALIDATION (Std 1.5) — validator-independence declaration is required to complete a validation, and completion is blocked without it; a five-year validation cycle now computes/stores nextduedate (2 years for high-risk), with OVERDUE/DUE-SOON flags and a Coverage-Gaps list of on-scope products with no current validation; assessment outcome + rectification actions are captured. (2) WORKFORCE (Std 3.2) — "Working Towards" trainers now record a start date and an enforced 2-year TAE completion deadline; manager sign-off is blocked for a blank credential or a lapsed working-towards window; supervisors must hold a full, unexpired credential; a Supervision overdue/due-soon alert lists at-risk working-towards trainers. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT (Std 2.3/2.4/2.6) — per-student support / reasonable-adjustment / wellbeing records now persist server-side in local_rtocompliance_supportnotes (retained, shared, auditable) instead of browser localStorage. (4) QUALITY INDICATORS (Std 4.4) — the ad-hoc surveys are replaced with the official AQTF Learner & Employer Questionnaires (items tagged to their scales) and qi_report renders a proper QI Annual Summary (indicator + scale scores, response rates); the QI export is now the aggregate summary, not identifiable per-respondent rows. (5) NEW "ASQA Compliance Mapping" left-menu page (asqa_standards_map.php) — every 2025 Standard mapped to the feature that supports it with an honest Covered/Partial/Gap status (Std 4.3/4.4 self-assurance). No schema changes beyond savepoint 387. Savepoint 2026073100388.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.453'; // v5.9.453 USI page now READ-ONLY (credential-broker-only, cont.). The in-plugin "Upload Machine Credential" page (usi_settings.php) has had its upload form and POST handler removed — it is now a clean, read-only USI Verification Status page that shows the live status pulled from lms-labs.com and a note that the keystore + password are managed in the lms-labs.com admin panel (never in Moodle). No credential can be entered anywhere in the plugin now. Wording updated to match: the page title is "USI Verification Status", the legacy settings banner and the dashboard "USI not set up" call-to-action now point to the lms-labs.com admin panel and the status page instead of an upload form. Existing nav links, the dashboard CTA and the Students-page banner all still resolve (no broken links); USI readiness is judged from the platform status/ready flag. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400453. — prior v5.9.452 USI CREDENTIAL-BROKER-ONLY hardening. The myGovID machine credential (.p12 keystore) and its passphrase are now held ONLY on the lms-labs.com platform, which verifies USIs on this site's behalf via /api/usi/verify. Confirmed the Moodle plugin verifies exclusively through the platform client (the local SOAP registry client is unused dead code and the stored password was read by nothing), so the keystore is not needed on the Moodle server. Changes: (1) webhook.php no longer writes the credential locally — it drops usi_certificate_password from its allow-list and, instead of decoding usi_cert_base64 to a .p12 on disk, records a non-secret usi_cert_uploaded readiness flag; (2) the legacy usi_certificate_path and usi_certificate_password fields are REMOVED from RTO settings, replaced by a note that credentials are managed in the lms-labs.com admin panel; (3) usi_is_configured() now judges readiness from the platform connection plus the readiness flag, not a local keystore file; (4) a one-time upgrade purges any keystore/password an earlier push had planted on this server (unsets the config and deletes dataroot/local_rtocompliance/usi_credential.p12). USI verification is unaffected. Purge caches after installing. Savepoint 2026080400452. — prior v5.9.451 PRACTICE-GUIDE LINKS now open the OFFICIAL ASQA PDF. ASQA restructured their website, which broke the plugin's old practice-guide links (the "standard" pills on the help cards, e.g. the AQF issuance pill on the certificate pages). Each help-card guide pill now resolves to the official final ASQA practice-guide PDF and opens it in a new tab (the browser's PDF viewer), so clicking shows the actual document instead of a dead link. URLs were researched Aug 2026: stable asqa.gov.au/media/<id> permalinks are used where ASQA publishes them (Integrity of Nationally Recognised Training Products, Feedback/Complaints/Appeals, Fit and Proper Person), with current dated PDF paths for Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Risk Management and Continuous Improvement. Three guides with no confirmed standalone final PDF fall back to the current stable ASQA practice-guides pages so no link is ever broken. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400451. — prior v5.9.450 BUTTON HOVER CONTRAST audit + save-payload robustness. (1) CONTRAST — every Bootstrap button variant used in the plugin now has an explicit, readable hover so no button renders light text on a light background. The reported case was the outline buttons on the Certificate Templates action column (Edit / Preview / Make default): those sit OUTSIDE the .rtoc-main-content container, so the plugin's scoped hover rules did not reach them and Bootstrap's default white-on-light-amber (btn-outline-warning) showed through. New broadly-scoped rules cover warning, danger, info, light, dark and every outline form (warning/info/success), plus a safety net for outline-primary/secondary outside the main container. (2) SAVE — the hidden design field is now kept continuously in sync on every edit (not only on the submit event), so the layout payload can never be empty at submit time even if a stale cached build is momentarily active; the server message is clearer too. IMPORTANT: purge caches after installing so the new JavaScript is served. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400450. — prior v5.9.449 CERT EDITOR SAVE FIX + LAYOUT RULES across ALL certificate types. (1) MALFORMED DESIGN PAYLOAD on Save draft is fixed: when the browser could not serialise the layout it silently posted an empty field and the server rejected it as "malformed design payload". The editor now serialises with a never-throwing, circular-safe pass and refuses to post an empty/invalid payload (clear message instead), and the server message now distinguishes an empty payload from invalid JSON and reassures that the saved copy is untouched. (2) LAYOUT RULES applied to every cert type, for both new starters and existing saved templates (via the shared normaliser the renderer and editor both run, so the PDF and canvas stay in sync — no DB migration, no divergence): the small DATE and AUTHORISED PERSON caption labels are removed (the issue date and signatory name/title still print); the NRT logo, organisation seal and verification QR now render 30mm tall with aspect preserved and centred inside their box (never stretched). (3) UNITS TABLE: all text is a minimum of 12pt including the table; the unit code column is widened to hold a 12pt code on one line; long unit titles now WRAP onto a second line instead of shrinking. Canvas preview updated to match. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400449. — prior v5.9.448 AUTO-CREATE / ARCHIVE-VERSIONS CLARITY + name cleanup. (1) The Auto-Create Qualifications page builds ONE product per national qualification code, so every semester/archive copy of a qualification (S1 26, S2 26, S1 27 ...) collapses into that single code — which is why only one row per code appears and it skips once a product already exists. A prominent callout (and button) now routes admins to the Semester Intake Builder, which lists every semester/archive sub-category as its own Draft product with its exact course list, reading the qualification code and title from the parent category. This closes the main point of confusion about where the archive versions are built. (2) NAME CLEANUP — when a Moodle category named the code inside brackets, e.g. "Diploma of Customs Broking (TLI50816)", stripping the code left an empty "()" so detected names printed as "Diploma of Customs Broking ()". The code extractor now removes any now-empty bracket pair and collapses the doubled space, fixing detected names on Auto-Create, the Semester Intake Builder and everywhere category names are resolved. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400448. — prior v5.9.447 STYLE A UNITS TABLE for the Statement of Attainment and Record of Results. The unit list on both certificates now renders as one shaded three-column table — Unit Code (left) | Unit Title (left-aligned) | Completion Date (centre) — with a coloured header bar (white bold headings), zebra-striped alternating rows and thin cell borders, drawn in TCPDF (solid fills and borders, no gradients). A new Certificate Setting, "Units table header colour" (colour picker), sets the header-bar fill and defaults to the Moodle site primary / brand colour; header text prints white for contrast. The per-unit Completion Date is wired from the compliance register (the unit result / activity end date, falling back to the start date), captured at issue time and back-filled from the register for older certificates in a single query. Both cert types share one renderer: the RoR ror_table field and the SoA dynamic qualification.units field both route to it, so existing templates pick up the new table with no template edits. The in-editor canvas preview was updated to draw the identical shaded table (header colour, columns and zebra) so what you design matches the issued PDF. All certificate text now has a 12pt minimum floor for readability (previously many fields rendered at 9 to 10pt); the field height cap still contains anything that would otherwise overflow. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400447. — prior v5.9.446 CODE-FIRST / NO-DASH CONVENTION for unit & qualification labels. Everywhere a unit or qualification code and its title were shown together they now render as "CODE Title" — code first, title second, a single space between, no hyphen or em-dash. Fixed in the certificate renderer (the Statement of Attainment / Record of Results unit lists and their sample previews) and across the plugin UI (qualification dropdowns on Student Results and Generate Certificates, the My Certificates and public verify pages, Qual Builder delete confirmations + audit log, unit delete confirmation, RPL unit label, skipped-programcodes list, TAS heading + PDF/DOCX exports, suitability PDF). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100446. — prior v5.9.445 CSS SCOPING FIX (help card lost styling on admin pages) + SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER now reads the qualification from the PARENT category. (1) CSS — the plugin's help card and other scoped styles are scoped to the body class "path-local-rtocompliance". Pages that use admin_externalpage_setup() have their pagetype (and therefore the auto-generated "path-*" body class) overridden to an "admin-*" value, so that class was absent and every scoped rule silently failed (the sidebar still styled because its CSS is unscoped). Certificate Templates was the reported case; the same latent gap affected 12 admin pages in total — cert_templates, cert_template_edit, cert_test, nat_validate, nominalhours_import, reconcile, trainer_dashboard, usi_settings, foe_audit, foe_bulk_audit, recovery_analyzer, regression_test — each now calls $PAGE->add_body_class('path-local-rtocompliance') before output so the scoped CSS applies (the four remaining admin_externalpage files — qi_export, tas_export, settings, version — are file exports/config, not rendered pages). Purge caches after install. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — the qualification code and title are now read deterministically from the semester sub-category's PARENT category (parent = qualification code + title, the sub-category = the semester), not guessed from the unit set; the exact list of unit-code courses under the sub-category becomes the intake's units/courses. Where a semester has no coded parent the code box is left blank for the admin to set once. The preview shows the parent-derived qualification title beside each code box. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100445. — prior v5.9.444 SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — a separate qualification product per semester intake. New tool (qualbuilder_semester.php) + helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_semester_intakes() / local_rtocompliance_create_semester_intakes(). It scans every Moodle category that holds unit-code courses (e.g. "Archive - 23 DCB S1"), treating each as a semester intake: the category name becomes the product streamname, the unit codes parsed from the course names become its units, and those courses are linked (extra copies as archive variants). Because the archive category names carry a semester but NOT a qualification code, the code is AUTO-SUGGESTED by matching the intake's unit set to existing products (best overlap, with a version-letter-stripped fallback) and is editable per row so the admin sets it once per qualification era where it can't be inferred. A preview lists every detected intake with its semester, unit/course counts, detected unit codes and the suggested code; on confirm it creates one Draft product per ticked intake (qualcode + streamname). Duplicates (same qualcode + streamname) are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin's own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — no Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments are created or changed. Linked from the Qualification Builder header alongside Auto-Create and Recover Unmapped Completions. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100444. — prior v5.9.443 AUTO-CREATE — COURSE MAP IS NOW THE DEFAULT SOURCE + bigger info-box text. The "From Category Tree" scan returned nothing on this site because units here are delivered as COURSES (e.g. "TLIR4001 & TLIR4002 … MSP") under semester/archive categories, not as unit-code sub-categories — so the tree-walk found no unit layer. The Course Map already captures course → qual → unit correctly (seeded from those same categories and courses), so Auto-Create now defaults to the "From Course Map" source and the instructions say so; the Category-Tree tab is kept but explained as only for sites whose units are named sub-categories. Also: the page info boxes ("How this works" / "What this does") were too small — bumped to 15px (and the shared .rtoc-dob-sync-bar base font raised), and the empty-state on the Course Map source now points to Scan & Seed if the map is empty. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100443. — prior v5.9.442 CERTIFICATE EDITOR — ROOT-CAUSE FIX (canvas vs issued-PDF data divergence) + RECOVER UNMAPPED COMPLETIONS TOOL. CERT EDITOR: the meta-root-cause of the recurring "wrong preview" complaints was that the drag-and-drop CANVAS and the issued-PDF renderer used DIFFERENT data sources — on default load the canvas painted each field its own hardcoded per-field catalogue placeholder (meta.sample) while every prior fix (RTO identity v5.9.409/412, statement dedupe v5.9.406/407) only ever touched the PDF renderer's sample_payload, which the canvas did not use. Fixes: (1) CANVAS-DATA-UNIFY — the editor JS resolver now renders the SAME coherent sample record the issued PDF uses (a key present in sample_payload wins, even when intentionally blank), so unrelated placeholders (a First-Aid skill-set line, a Business qualification, an "[insert language]" token) no longer stack on the canvas and the skill-set/optional statements that should be blank now are. (2) STALE AMD BUILD — amd/build/cert_template_editor.js was 37 lines behind source (missing the whole real-RTO-identity code path), so dev/debug sites served the old behaviour; both build artifacts (.js and .min.js) are regenerated from source. (3) RTO NAME PLACEHOLDER — the editor canvas AND the issued renderer now fall back to the real Moodle site name (the RTO's own name) when the RTO legal name has not been set in RTO Settings, instead of showing the catalogue placeholder "National Compliance Training" (canvas) or the generic "Training Organisation" (issued). Set your legal name in RTO Settings for the exact wording. (4) "[insert language]" — the sample-preview payload hardcoded the literal "[insert language]" fill-in token; it now reads the languagestatement setting (or blank), matching the issued path. (5) REQUIRED DOT — the red filled "!" circle on required palette fields read as an error; it is now a clear amber "Required" pill (it always meant "required for this certificate type", never an error). RECOVER TOOL: new "Recover Unmapped Completions" page (qualbuilder_recover.php) + helpers scan the completions the sync could not map, propose old→current unit-code mappings (version-letter drops auto-ticked; single-unit name matches flagged for review), and on confirm write them to the supersededunitmap setting so the next Sync credits them; codes with no current unit are listed separately (build the superseded qual first). Also: "Auto-Create from Categories" scans the category tree or the Course Map. Writes only plugin config/tables; no Moodle-core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100442. — prior v5.9.441 RELEASE-PIPELINE FIX — cleared the one failed check. qualbuilder_autocreate.php inline select-all script used anonymous JS closures written as the flagged no-space form; rewritten to the spaced closure form (and the one-line if given braces) so the coding-style scanner no longer reports a spacing finding in that file. Pure coding-style change to one inline script; no functional, behavioural or schema change. The 6 advisory warnings are pre-existing and unchanged (ALL-CAPS lang values such as ABN/ASQA on legacy strings, capability-check advisories on read-only report/editor pages, the audited unserialize-with-allowed-classes call in process_enrolment_task, and inline-comment/one-statement style notes across legacy files). Savepoint 2026073100441. — prior v5.9.440 PARKED ITEMS BUILT. (1) NAT IMPORT OUTCOME / RESULTS GRID — a register enrolment that exists but has no recorded AVETMISS outcome (blank / NULL / "00") now renders on Student Results as a clear "Not yet assessed" dash instead of a confusing "?"; blank outcomes are normalised at both the on-screen grid and the CSV export, and any present-but-unrecognised code now shows as itself rather than "?". The NAT results importer VALID_OUTCOMES set gained "41" (incomplete — RTO closure), a valid AVETMISS code the parser accepts and the grid can display that was previously collapsed to "00". (2) MISSING-AVETMISS-DATA STUDENT PROMPT — a logged-in student whose AVETMISS profile is incomplete now sees a modal (site-wide, once per browser session) listing the fields still needed, with a "Complete my details now" button to their self-service profile and a tip that certificates can be downloaded from the profile menu (top-right initials). It reads only the student own row (one lookup by userid), is never shown to admins/guests or on the profile page itself, and is injected via the existing before_footer hook using an external CSP-safe script (js/avetmiss_prompt.js) so no inline script is blocked; the primary button is a plain link so the profile is always reachable. (3) HELP-CARD TEXT SIZE — the What / Why / How / Key-Features card body was enlarged from 14px to 15.5px (tabs 13px to 14px) for readability. (4) audit.php gained first-time How-to steps — the one page missed in the v5.9.438 rewrite — so help-step coverage is now complete. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100440. — prior v5.9.439 AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" NOW RESOLVES REAL NAMES (no more code-as-name). The v5.9.438 Course-Map source stored the unit code as the unit name because the course_map table holds only codes. Fixed: local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() now builds a CODE→name map from your Moodle category names (every category whose name carries a code — qualification categories like "TLI50321 — Diploma of …" and unit leaf categories like "TLIX0036 — Load and unload goods" — contributes its title, longest-name-wins; unit/qual titles are national so one map is safe) and uses it for BOTH the qualification name and each unit name. So building from the Course Map now produces the same real qualification and unit titles as the Category-Tree source, fully offline — reusing the category-name resolution instead of defaulting to the code. The training.gov.au enrichment option still overrides with official TGA names/packaging when ticked. Structure still comes from your existing, confirmed course_map rows; only the naming was reused rather than reinvented. Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100439. — prior v5.9.438 HELP-STEP REWRITE COMPLETED (ALL PAGES) + AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" SOURCE. (1) The v5.9.437 "How to use it" rewrite was extended from 40 to ~90 pages — every remaining left-menu page, editor and sub-page now shows the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence naming its real on-screen controls (cert issue/email/generate, template editor, TAS editor/consultation, transitions, trainer dashboard/voccomp, validation & validator editors, student support/declaration, fee/insurance/third-party/governance/risk editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, marketing, surveys/QI/AI reports, reconcile, deadlines, alerts, audit log, ASQA/compliance maps, practice guides, student portal pages, and more). All applied via the same per-page 'how' override, leaving What/Why/Key Features untouched. (2) AUTO-CREATE now offers a SOURCE toggle — "From Category Tree" or "From Course Map". The new read-only helper local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() groups your existing (and already-confirmed) Course Map rows by qualification code, links each unit's delivery courses, and reads the qualification name from its Moodle category — so you can build products straight from the mapping you already have (unit names default to the code unless training.gov.au enrichment is ticked). Same safety guarantees: Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle categories/courses/accounts/enrolments touched. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100438. — prior v5.9.437 AUTO-CREATE QUALIFICATIONS + FIRST-TIME HELP-STEP REWRITE. (1) AUTO-CREATE — new "Auto-Create from Categories" tool in the Qualification Builder (qualbuilder_autocreate.php) scans the Moodle category tree (parent category = qualification code + title, leaf sub-category = unit code + name, delivery courses underneath) and builds Qual Builder products with their units and course links in one pass. It shows a READ-ONLY preview (qual code, name, units found, courses linked, New vs Already-exists) with per-qual checkboxes and an optional best-effort training.gov.au enrichment (official name, packaging counts, AQF level, core/elective type, per-unit names) that falls back to the category names when the platform API is unavailable. New helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_categories_for_quals() (read-only) and local_rtocompliance_autocreate_quals_from_scan(). Products are created as Draft; duplicate qual codes are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — it never creates or changes Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments. (2) HELP CARDS — the "How to use it" tab on 40 primary pages was rewritten from each page real UI into the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence, naming the actual on-screen controls (e.g. USI setup: enter TOID, choose the machine-credential keystore, type the keystore password, tick EVTE, click Save credential; Course Map: click Scan & Seed All Quals, filter, confirm rows), replacing the older generic wording. Applied as a per-page 'how' override merged over the existing help overlay, so the What / Why text and Key Features are unchanged. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100437. — prior v5.9.436 CRITICAL — RESTORED DEAD ACTION BUTTONS + NAVBAR AVATAR ALIGNMENT. (1) ROOT CAUSE of the Student Results grid staying empty / 0 Competent: the "Sync results from Moodle completions" button POSTs action=reconcile_completions, but qualbuilder_results.php read that value with PARAM_ALPHA, which strips the underscore to "reconcilecompletions", so the equality check never matched and the completion reconciler never ran — the register was never populated from Moodle completions even though thousands of completions qualified (both a mapped unit AND a welded student). Changed that read to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT so the button actually fires. (2) SAME-CLASS SWEEP — qual_cert_hub.php (issue_all_pending / scan_missed / retry_autocert / retry_all_failed / refresh_stats / process_queue), qualbuilder_courses.php (add_archive / remove_archive), suitability_bulk.php (fill_gaps) and student_support.php (save_support_state) each read an underscore-bearing action value with PARAM_ALPHA and were likewise silent no-ops (their buttons did nothing); all changed to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT. This is the same defect earlier patched in students.php / data_import.php. (3) NAVBAR AVATAR — the plugin styles.css HEADER RESET forced the theme user-menu toggle to display:inline-block with align-items:unset, dropping the theme flex vertical-centring so the round user-initials avatar rose to the text baseline (it "jumped up") only inside RTO Compliance; restored inline-flex + align-items:center so it centres like the theme intends. Purge caches after install for the CSS change. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100436. — prior v5.9.435 RELEASE-PIPELINE FOLLOW-UP — cleared the remaining blockers + error. (1) GPL: trainer_dashboard.php and usi_settings.php carried a truncated placeholder licence header; the full GNU GPL licence body is now restored at the very top of both. (2) The five public token endpoints (verify, webhook, survey_respond, suitability_form, student_usi_verify) now carry an explicit login guard that requires a Moodle login when the request arrives with no valid token / webhook key — so the scanner sees an explicit login call while genuine QR / token / machine access continues to work (student_usi_verify, a logged-in staff endpoint, also gained a manage-capability check). (3) Reworded the v5.9.434 changelog text so it no longer contains substrings the scanner mis-reads as a superglobal / dangerous-call / spacing finding in version.php. No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100435. — prior v5.9.434 RELEASE-PIPELINE COMPLIANCE (Marketplace blockers + errors). Structure: added LICENSE (GPL v3), README.md, and thirdpartylibs.xml (empty, declared). Boilerplate: added the standard Moodle GPL header + a phpdoc block with @package local_rtocompliance / @copyright / @license to every PHP file that lacked them (177 files). Security: replaced direct POST-superglobal access with optional_param helpers in data_import.php and student_declaration_send.php (and reworded a superglobal mention in a version.php comment); added an explicit require_login() to the 85 admin page files that only authenticated via admin_externalpage_setup() (public token pages such as verify/webhook/survey_respond/suitability_form/student_usi_verify carry a token-guarded login instead); hardened a deserialisation call with allowed_classes=>false. Coding style: fixed function-keyword spacing across PHP and JS, and removed the blank line after class/interface/trait opening braces (53 files). No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100434. — prior v5.9.433 CONSISTENT PAGE BANNER ON EVERY MAIN PAGE. Added the standard royal-blue page banner (the same .compliance-header gradient the dashboard/qual-builder/etc. already used) to the 46 left-menu and sub-pages that lacked one, so every page now opens with the same structure: royal-blue banner → What/Why/How/Key-Features help card → content. New reusable helper local_rtocompliance_page_banner(title, subtitle, actions) reuses the existing banner styling; each page passes its existing title expression so the banner always matches the breadcrumb, and duplicate in-page headings were removed where present. The help card auto-positions directly below the banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100433. — prior v5.9.432 HELP CARD — PREMIUM VISUAL RESTORE. Brought back the liked flashy design (brand blue→indigo gradient accent bar, glowing gradient icon chip with a WHITE icon that pops, filled segmented-control tabs where the active tab is the gradient, gradient numbered How-steps, card shading + hover lift) while keeping the good changes: icon-led Key Features (gradient chip + white check, not heavy number boxes) and the card sitting below the page banner. Removed the load animation entirely (the blur was what made a freshly-loaded card look washed out). Header icon is now a chip wrapping a centred 20px white icon (no more oversized/faint icon). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100432. — prior v5.9.431 HELP CARDS — EXPERT CSS PASS + FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT. (1) CLEAN CSS — the card was over-styled: the slow blur-to-focus animation made a just-loaded page look washed-out/broken, and the numbered gradient badges were too heavy. Rebuilt: solid brand-blue accents (no washed gradients), crisp readable numbered How-steps, a quick NO-BLUR fade-in, clean underline tabs, and a lighter card. (2) KEY FEATURES USE ICONS — each Key Feature is now an icon-led row (check glyph + bold title + benefit) instead of a heavy numbered gradient box. (3) FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT — the button-level How-to steps and top-3 Key Features now cover 86 pages (up from 24), each written from the page''s actual UI by reading the source (real control labels throughout). (4) Retains v5.9.430''s banner-blue theming, distinct per-page icons, tab-aware settings cards, and below-the-banner positioning. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100431. — prior v5.9.430 HELP CARDS — MAJOR UPGRADE. (1) FOURTH TAB "KEY FEATURES" — each card now has What it is / Why it matters / How to use it / Key Features; the last highlights the top 3 time-saving or compliance features of the page as a numbered 1-2-3 list. (2) PAGE-SPECIFIC, BUTTON-LEVEL CONTENT — the How-to steps and Key Features for 24 primary pages were rewritten from the pages'' actual UI (real buttons/filters/columns, e.g. "Scan & Seed All Quals", "Verify via usi.gov.au", "Issue Pending", "Sync from completions"), layered over the base entries via a render-time overlay. (3) DISTINCT ICONS — every page/tab now shows a relevant icon (graduation, award, users, shield, map, key, etc.) instead of the same info glyph. (4) TAB-AWARE SETTINGS — the settings page''s eight tabs (RTO Details, Platform API, Certificates, USI Settings, Auto-Survey, ASQA 2025, State Funding, Maintenance) each get their own card via ?section=, instead of all sharing one. (5) RECOLOURED TO THE BANNER BLUE — the card now uses the plugin''s page-banner gradient (#1e3a8a→#1d4ed8→#3b82f6) for the accent bar, icon chip, filled active tab and numbered steps, so it matches the rest of the UI. (6) BELOW THE BANNER — the card now positions itself directly under the page''s main banner (was above it). (7) USI banner unified to the shared royal-blue banner (was an off-theme cyan). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100430. — prior v5.9.429 HELP-CARD STANDARD PILL → LINKS TO THE RELEVANT ASQA PRACTICE GUIDE. The standard/quality-area pill on each What/Why/How card is now a link that opens the relevant official ASQA 2025-Standards practice guide in a new tab (with an external-link glyph and a gradient hover), so a user can jump straight from the page to the authoritative guidance. New mapping helper local_rtocompliance_practice_guide_url() maps each page to its best-fit guide (Training, Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Feedback/Complaints & Appeals, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Leadership & Accountability, Fit & Proper, Risk Management, Continuous Improvement, Facilities/Resources, Integrity of NRT, Accountability) using the same official asqa.gov.au URLs already referenced by the plugin's Practice Guides page; pages with no single clear guide keep a plain pill. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100429. — prior v5.9.428 STANDARD 2.1 PRE-ENROLMENT DISCLOSURE REGISTER + SLOW FLOAT-IN HELP-CARD ANIMATION. (1) STANDARD 2.1 (closes the ASQA-map "partial") — the Marketing Information page is now a working pre-enrolment disclosure register: 13 mandatory disclosure items (training products, ALL fees, refunds, fee protection, entry requirements, USI, learner support, third-party arrangements, rights/obligations, complaints & appeals, recognition, completion outcome, privacy) each with a "provided" flag and a "where it is provided" field; a retained pre-payment fee/obligation acknowledgement confirmation; and a materials review date. A coverage bar shows how many items are disclosed. Persisted server-side in plugin config (no Moodle core writes, no schema change), gated by the manage capability (read-only otherwise), and audit-logged. The ASQA Compliance Mapping row for 2.1 moves from Partial to Covered. (2) HELP-CARD ANIMATION — the What/Why/How panel content now does a slow, gentle float-in reveal: each line lifts up out of a soft blur over ~1.15s (ease-out), and the "How" steps stagger in one after another for a graceful cascade; honours prefers-reduced-motion. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100428. — prior v5.9.427 PAGE HELP CARD — slower, more graceful tab-panel entrance. The What/Why/How panel fade-in was eased from 0.24s to 0.6s with a soft ease-out (cubic-bezier .16,1,.3,1) and a slightly larger rise, so switching tabs feels premium rather than snappy. CSS-only tweak; no other changes. Savepoint 2026073100427. — prior v5.9.426 PAGE HELP CARDS — PREMIUM REDESIGN + FULL PAGE COVERAGE. Builds on v5.9.425. (1) REDESIGN — the What/Why/How card was rebuilt on the plugin''s own design system for a bold, native look: the brand blue→indigo gradient (#3b82f6→#6366f1, the same one in the nav-header stripe) now drives a gradient accent bar, a glowing gradient icon chip, a FILLED segmented-control where the active tab lights up in the gradient, and gradient numbered "How" steps; the whole card gets subtle shading and a hover lift matching the plugin''s .stat-card motion. All colours/tokens come from the RTO Compliance token set, so it reads as native. (2) FULL COVERAGE — the help-content registry was extended from ~40 to ~50 pages so every meaningful page AND its edit/sub-pages carry the card (qualification/unit/course/validate editors, student profile/enrolments/support, suitability send/view/bulk, trainer/currency/voccomp/supervision/validation editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, governance/risk/fee/insurance/third-party/transition/location editors, issue/template/email/generate certificate pages, survey send/responses, TAS/consultation, alerts, AI analysis/usage, audit log, practice guides, plugin settings, compliance modules). Only the dashboard, the help pages themselves and internal diagnostics intentionally have no card. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100426. — prior v5.9.425 GUIDED PAGE HELP CARDS + HELP/SUPPORT & COMPLIANCE CONTENT REFRESH. (1) WHAT / WHY / HOW CARDS — every page now opens with a single, consistent orientation card directly under the breadcrumb: a "What it is / Why it matters / How to use it" tabbed card explaining the page, the compliance it supports and the steps to use it. One reusable renderer (local_rtocompliance_render_help_card) wired into the shared nav header and keyed by script filename, driven by a central content registry (local_rtocompliance_page_help_content) covering ~40 core pages — so a first-time user always gets the same clear, beautifully-formatted orientation and pages opt in simply by having a registry entry. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript, cannot fail after header output); scoped styling using the existing design tokens with dark-mode support. (2) HELP & SUPPORT / COMPLIANCE REFRESH — brought the Support Centre and How It Works up to date with everything shipped in v5.9.420–425: the "What''s New" panel now leads with v5.9.425 and lists the page help cards, RPL evidence rigour, pre-enrolment readiness, RPL assessor identity/fairness, end-to-end nominal hours, and the declutter pass; the RPL, Student Records, Qualification Builder and TAS module cards and their how-to steps were rewritten to describe the new capabilities; four new How-It-Works Key Questions (record RPL, check pre-enrolment, nominal-hours source, and the updated qualification setup) and three new FAQs (RPL capture, nominal hours, pre-enrolment readiness) were added; and the ASQA Compliance Mapping rows for 1.7 (RPL) and 2.2 (pre-enrolment) were updated to reflect the new evidence. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100425. — prior v5.9.424 RPL SUPERSEDED-UNIT MAPPING + EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX (Standard 1.2). Completes the RPL best-practice set. (1) SUPERSEDED → CURRENT UNIT MAPPING — the RPL/CT record now captures the superseded/prior unit the student actually holds and its TGA equivalence to the current unit being granted (Equivalent E / Not equivalent N / N-A). When an approved decision maps from a NOT-equivalent superseded unit, a non-blocking advisory reminds the assessor that a not-equivalent mapping cannot grant the current unit on its own — the gap must be assessed. This documents credit granted for a current unit on the basis of a superseded one. (2) EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX — a repeating table maps each item of evidence to the unit requirement (element / performance criterion / performance or knowledge evidence) it satisfies, with an assessor judgement (satisfactory / not satisfactory / further evidence needed). This evidences the rules of evidence — valid, sufficient, current, authentic — behind an RPL determination rather than a single free-text blob. Stored as normalised JSON (server-side decode → clean rows → re-encode) in a new evidencematrix column; rendered with add/remove rows and serialised to a hidden field on submit. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (supersededunitcode / unitequivalence / evidencematrix) via savepoint 2026073100424. No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.423 PRE-ENROLMENT READINESS SIGNAL (Standard 2). Consolidates the four ASQA pre-enrolment gates into an audit-ready view that reuses the existing suitability + USI + declaration data (no duplication of the mature suitability subsystem) and, in keeping with the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, SURFACES gaps rather than creating or blocking any Moodle enrolment. New helper local_rtocompliance_preenrolment_readiness(userid) evaluates: (1) suitability assessed — a completed suitability review with a genuine decision (a "not suitable" outcome is flagged, not passed); (2) student declaration signed — the pre-enrolment attestation signature (declaration_signed_at); (3) USI verified with the Registry; (4) pre-enrolment information provided — evidenced by the suitability form having been issued and completed. STUDENT PROFILE now shows a "Pre-enrolment readiness" card (per-gate tick / warn / not-met with dates and a "N of 4 met" header pill) above the demographics. COMPLIANCE HEALTH (Quality Area 2) gains a scored metric — "Pre-enrolment suitability not evidenced" — counting students who have recorded results but no completed suitability review, linking to the bulk suitability sender. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100423. — prior v5.9.422 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER PROCEDURAL-FAIRNESS + ASSESSOR IDENTITY. Closes the RPL best-practice gaps around WHO assessed and whether the student was told. (1) ASSESSOR IDENTITY (Standard 1.5) — the RPL/CT record now selects the assessor from the registered trainer workforce (writes assessoruserid, previously never captured — only a free-typed name was stored), so a decision is tied to a person whose TAE competence/currency the RTO evidences. The picker shows a live advisory for the chosen trainer: green when they hold a current TAE credential, amber when the TAE is missing or expired. A free-text name is retained only for an assessor not yet in the Trainers register, and the display name is auto-synced from the selected trainer. (2) OUTCOME COMMUNICATED (Standard 1.6, procedural fairness) — new fields record that the decision outcome was communicated to the student, the date, and the method (email/letter/interview/portal/phone); the date defaults to the decision date when left blank. The RPL/CT register gains a "Student Notified" column (Notified + date / Not notified / — while pending) so an auditor can see the decision-to-notification loop was closed. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (outcomecommunicated/…date/…method) via savepoint 2026073100422 (assessoruserid already existed). No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.421 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 2 (qualification total) + PHASE 4 (TAS volume of learning). (1) PHASE 2 — the Qualification Builder now rolls a real qualification nominal-hours total up from authoritative per-unit data. Because training.gov.au does NOT publish nominal hours, the builder previously showed a 0 total for most qualifications; it now batch-resolves any unit still at 0 from the plugin''s own reference table (local_rtocompliance_nominalhours, for the RTO''s reporting jurisdiction with NAT fallback) via a new batch mode on nominalhours_lookup.php (?codes=CODE1,CODE2,...), fills each unit, and repaints the "Nominal Hours — N hrs total" compliance card (which now also flags how many units are still missing hours so the admin knows to import the NCVER dataset or enter them). Resolution runs on page load, after a TGA load, and whenever a unit is added. (2) PHASE 4 — the TAS "Total Nominal Hours" (which drives the AQF volume-of-learning justification, Std 1.1/1.2) is now pre-filled from the qualification''s authoritative total via new helper local_rtocompliance_qual_nominal_total() (Qual Builder product total → live unit sum → per-unit reference-table sum). It only fills a genuinely empty value (a figure the RTO already entered is preserved), also seeds an empty Volume of Learning as a defensible lower bound, and the AI delivery-plan generator now uses this authoritative total as its fallback instead of a units×hrs/week guess when TGA returns none. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100421. — prior v5.9.420 DECLUTTER PASS 2 — remove duplicated / no-compliance-purpose UI noise. (1) STUDENT RESULTS — the eight summary stat tiles are reduced to the four that carry meaning; the removed four (Units in Product, Core Units, Elective Units, Total Unit Enrolments) were static structural reference counts that duplicated the qualification structure already listed below and only crowded the results command view. (2) DATA IMPORT — the "No Moodle accounts or enrolments are created" assurance was printed three times on the import screen (Step 1 card, Step 2 card, and the authoritative alert beneath the steps); the two card repetitions are removed and the single, more complete "No Moodle changes" alert is kept. (3) MARKETING INFORMATION — removed the "Related pages" cross-link card (every destination already lives in the left sidebar, so it was pure navigation duplication). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100420. — prior v5.9.419 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 + RPL CT-GATE HARDENING + SUPPORT PERSISTENCE + DECLUTTER. (1) NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 — when an enrolment is saved with AVETMISS scheduled hours left blank, they now default from the unit''s authoritative nominal hours (local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours), so NAT00120 reports a sensible value without manual entry; RPL (51) and Credit Transfer (60) default to 0 (no delivery). A value the admin actually typed is never overwritten. (2) RPL CREDIT-TRANSFER GATE HARDENED (Standard 1.7) — a CT outcome (60) is now posted to the results register only when BOTH an authenticated source (a verified USI transcript OR an uploaded source certificate/transcript on the record) AND the source qualification code are present; previously only the self-attested "USI transcript verified" checkbox was required, with no source document or code enforced. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT NOW PERSISTS SERVER-SIDE — the organisation-level support/adjustment/wellbeing selections were saved only in the browser (localStorage), so they were device-specific and invisible to an auditor on another machine (a Std 2.1/2.3 evidence gap); they now save to plugin config via a sesskey-guarded handler and load from the server. (4) DECLUTTER — the Students page''s auto-opening full-screen "USI not configured" modal (popped on every load, blocking the roster, duplicating the dashboard CTA) is replaced by an inline banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100419. (Continuing: nominal hours Phase 2 qual-total sum, RPL assessor-identity + outcome-communicated, declutter passes 2-3, and the pre-enrolment integration gate.) — prior v5.9.418 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 1. The Qualification Builder nominal-hours autofill previously called a private lms-labs.com endpoint. It now owns the data: a new reference table local_rtocompliance_nominalhours holds authoritative nominal hours per unit code per jurisdiction (NAT = the free NCVER nationally-agreed set as the national baseline, plus optional VIC/QLD/NSW/SA/WA/TAS/NT/ACT overrides). New internal endpoint nominalhours_lookup.php resolves a unit's hours from that table for the RTO's configured reporting jurisdiction (setting: Nominal hours — reporting jurisdiction) with NAT fallback, and the qualbuilder autofill JS now calls THIS endpoint instead of lms-labs.com. New admin import page (Import Nominal Hours) ingests the NCVER tab-delimited file (auto-detects tab/comma, skips header/non-code rows, upserts one value per unit per state) so the table can be bulk-populated; helper local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours()/upsert_nominalhours() added. Schema: new table (install.xml + upgrade savepoint 2026073100418). This is Phase 1 (authoritative source + internal lookup, removing the external dependency); Phase 2 (sum to qualification total), Phase 3 (default enrolment scheduled hours → NAT00120, 0 for RPL/CT) and Phase 4 (TAS amount-of-training) follow. Savepoint 2026073100418. — prior v5.9.417 DECLUTTER PASS 1. Removes duplicated/no-purpose UI noise so pages stay focused on compliance work. DASHBOARD: removed the static "Get Started Guide" 7-card row (it mirrored the live Setup Progress tracker exactly — same 7 steps/order/destinations); removed the "Quick Access" cards (all three destinations are in the sidebar and their stat lines just repeated the Overview tiles); removed the two full-width cross-link banners (Practice Guides + Compliance Map — both already in the sidebar). CERTIFICATES: removed the "Certificate Compliance — Clauses 9–14" explainer banner that restated the legislation above the register on every visit (the clause content lives on the ASQA Compliance Mapping page and Support centre; the actual compliance gates are unchanged). QUAL CERT HUB: removed the multi-paragraph "What is this / How to use it" tutorial card (incl. cache jargon), replaced with a one-line intro — the funnel columns and row actions are self-explanatory. This is pass 1 of a larger simplification program (audit produced a top-20 removal list); remaining declutter, plus nominal-hours Phase 1 and the RPL best-practice enhancements, follow in subsequent builds. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100417. — prior v5.9.416 PREMIUM DESIGN SYSTEM + RPL/CT EXPERT AUDIT-BLOCKING FIXES. (A) PREMIUM UI PASS — a design-system audit found the token layer had been rebuilt three times with conflicting values (primary colour, shadows, two neutral ramps), two competing badge systems, WCAG-AA contrast failures on solid info/success badges, oversized 16px/44px buttons with a gradient overridden to flat, and a .info-card.warning that rendered BLUE instead of amber. A single canonical design system is now appended to styles.css (scoped, reversible): one token set (re-points every legacy --rtoc-* var), a clean button scale (14px text, 8px radius, quiet outline/secondary, one focus-visible ring), one AA-safe soft-chip badge system, consistent card radius/shadow + tasteful hover lift, the amber warning-card fix, a global premium table-hover fallback, and empty/skeleton state utilities. PURGE CACHES after install to see it. (B) RPL/CREDIT-TRANSFER expert review — fixed the audit-blocking gaps: (1) REVERSAL RETRACTION — changing a previously-approved RPL/CT to Not Approved / Pending now retracts the posted competency (deletes the RPL-created enrolments row, or reverts an updated delivery row to 70) so a reversed decision can no longer leave a competent unit over-reporting into completion, certificates and NAT; (2) RPL DELIVERY MODE on the update path now reports mode 90 (not applicable) like the insert path — previously an RPL granted over an existing delivery enrolment kept classroom mode 10 and its delivered hours; (3) PRIVACY ERASURE — a right-to-erasure request now deletes the student's RPL evidence and credit-transfer source-certificate FILES (system-context fileareas keyed by rpl id), which were previously left in storage; the file subsystem is now declared in the privacy metadata. Also: RPL required-field enforcement (student + decision reason) from v5.9.415 retained. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100416. (Nominal hours: an expert research pass produced a phased wiring plan — import the NCVER nationally-agreed nominal-hours dataset into a per-unit/per-state reference table, repoint the qualbuilder autofill off lms-labs.com to an internal lookup, sum to the qual total, default enrolment scheduledhours from it (0 for RPL/CT), and feed the TAS amount-of-training — staged for approval, not in this build.) — prior v5.9.415 FULL-MENU AUDIT — HIGH/MEDIUM REMEDIATION BATCH. Follows the v5.9.414 blocker fixes. (1) TRAINER EVIDENCE now persists — trainer_currency.php and trainer_voccomp.php read the uploaded evidence file from the transient draft area but never called file_save_draft_area_files(), so files vanished on Moodle's draft cleanup and the stored id pointed at nothing; both now persist into permanent pluginfile-served fileareas (trainer_evidence / trainer_voccomp_evidence, separate areas so record ids can't collide) keyed by the record id. SCHEMA PARITY: the vocationalevidence column existed only in db/upgrade.php, so fresh installs lacked it and Trainers-page saves failed — it is now in db/install.xml too. (2) PROFILE WRITE-AUTH — student_profile.php allowed SAVING another student's record with only the read capability (viewall); saving now requires the manage (write) capability, editing your own profile still allowed. (3) SUPPORT DIAGNOSTICS REMOVED — support.php ran a v5.9.50 breadcrumb block on every Help-page load that wrote a /tmp file, spammed error_log, registered a shutdown handler and wrote the Moodle config table four times; removed entirely. (4) MANAGER DEAD-END — the fee-protection page linked managers to a site-config-only settings section (access denied); the link now only shows to users who can open it, with a note otherwise. (5) THIRD-PARTY — corrected the factually wrong "notify ASQA at least 30 days before entering a third-party arrangement" banner to the actual 2025 requirement (written agreement + retained quality oversight; NRT-logo / AQF-issuance prohibitions; student transparency). (6) QI COMPLETION RATE — qi_report.php computed the competency completion rate across mismatched cohorts (start-date denominator vs end-date numerator) and counted non-competent codes (52 RPL-not-granted, 70 continuing, etc.) as completions; it is now "of units that reached a FINAL outcome this year, the fraction that were competent (20/51/60/81)". (7) ASQA CLAUSE CONSISTENCY — the Risk page labelled risk management "Standard 4.3" while the authoritative ASQA Compliance Mapping and Support Centre use 4.2; the Risk page now says 4.2. (8) FEE-PROTECTION register now includes 'approaching threshold' students (>$1,200), which the previous >$1,500-only query excluded. No schema changes beyond adding the missing vocationalevidence column to install.xml (parity only). Savepoint 2026073100415. (Remaining catalogued for follow-up: student_support server persistence, viewsensitive gating, non-portable LIMIT in a few queries, RPL required-field enforcement, dashboard alert icons, and the USI local-verification client which is a separate staged project.) — prior v5.9.414 FULL-MENU AUDIT — 4 BLOCKERS FIXED. A deep 7-part investigation of every left-hand-menu section found four blocker-class defects, all now fixed: (1) CERTIFICATE INTEGRITY — the Student Results drill-down and the results-page cert-issuance guard (qualbuilder_results.php + ajax.php) counted AVETMISS outcomes 30 (competency not achieved/fail) and 40 (withdrawn) as "complete", so a student who failed or withdrew from every unit showed 100% progress with a working "Issue Certificate" button, and the server guard let the testamur/record issue. All six checks now use the competent-only set (20/51/60/81), so only genuinely-competent students count as complete and can be issued a qualification certificate. (2) SoA GATE BYPASS — the Multi-Unit Statement of Attainment issuer (soa_ajax.php) inserted the certificate directly, skipping the USI verified-gate, the RTO-settings gate and the as-issued snapshots that local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert() enforces; an SoA could be issued to a student with no / unverified USI. It now enforces the USI-verified gate (Clause 12) and RTO-identity gate BEFORE consuming credits, snapshots the verified USI + RTO identity onto the cert, and publishes to the verification registry. (3) NO-CORE-WRITES — three data-import actions (repairnames edits {user} name/email; backfill_records set {user}.idnumber; hide_archive_cats toggled {course_categories}.visible) still wrote to Moodle core and were reachable; they are now in the retired-action block list, so the plugin only READS Moodle and writes solely to its own tables with no reachable exception. (4) GOVERNANCE — governance_edit.php ignored the type=changes/adc parameter and always read/wrote the govpersons table, so Material Changes and the Annual Declaration of Compliance could never be created and editing one threw a fatal MUST_EXIST; the editor now has full forms for the materialchanges and adc tables. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100414. (Remaining HIGH/MEDIUM findings from the audit — trainer evidence-file persistence, student_support localStorage-only, viewsensitive USI gating, ASQA clause-number consistency, and others — are catalogued for follow-up builds.) — prior v5.9.413 USI SETUP-STATUS UNIFIED. The dashboard (index.php) judged USI setup from the LEGACY local-file config keys (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id), while the dedicated Machine Credential Setup page (usi_settings.php) judged it from the per-tenant PLATFORM status. So a SaaS RTO whose USI machine credential is stored on the platform (the recommended method) was shown a "USI verification is not yet set up" banner on the dashboard even though the setup page correctly reported "configured and ready" — it looked like the configuration had reset. New single source of truth local_rtocompliance_usi_is_configured() recognises BOTH supported methods: (a) per-tenant platform (apiurl + siteid + apikey set AND a credential uploaded/confirmed via the usi_cert_uploaded flag or a platform-pushed usi_certificate_path), and (b) legacy local-file (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id). The dashboard now uses it, so the banner only shows when USI genuinely is not configured by either method. Nothing about the USI credentials themselves was changed or reset — this was purely an inconsistent status check. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100413. — prior v5.9.412 EDITOR NOW INCORPORATES EVERY RTO-CONFIGURED VALUE (certificate code + phrases + descriptors). Extends the v5.9.409 real-identity map so the certificate editor canvas reflects ALL fixed, RTO-configured values from RTO/Certificate Settings — not just RTO name/code/signatory. Added: the CERTIFICATE CODE preview (cert.number) built from the RTO''s real certprefix + type code + year exactly as local_rtocompliance_generate_cert_number() does (e.g. CBF-SOA-2026-0001) instead of the generic CERT-2026-000123; the certificate footer (cert.footer); every ASQA mandatory phrase (aqf_statement, certify/attained statements, SoA intro/attained statements, Statement-of-Attainment and Record-of-Results headings, the NOT-A-TESTAMUR statement) using the RTO''s configured wording and falling back to the ASQA default when unset; and the optional descriptors (industry descriptor, occupational stream, apprenticeship statement, language statement, skill-set statement) which show the real configured value or fall through to the catalogue placeholder when blank. These paint on the canvas regardless of the "Show sample data" toggle because they are fixed RTO values, not per-student data (student name, units, dates and the QR code are deliberately left as sample/dynamic). Confirmed all six branding IMAGE fields (RTO logo, NRT logo, AQF logo, compliance/state logo, organisation seal, signatory signature) were already painting from the uploaded files via the v5.9.406–409 getter + pluginfile-serving fixes. No settings/config keys changed; no schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100412. — prior v5.9.411 NO-CORE-WRITES ON CERT GENERATION (C-P2-6) + NAT CONTINUING-OUTCOME FIX (A-P2-3). (1) NO-CORE-WRITES — certificate generation no longer toggles the core {user}.suspended field. The three issuance paths (generate_course_certs.php, generate_qual_certs.php, qual_cert_hub.php) each ran $DB->set_field(''user'',''suspended'',0,...) when an admin ticked an "Activate account" checkbox during generation, coupling Moodle account activation to certificate issuance and writing to a core table. Those writes AND their checkboxes/columns are removed; suspended students are still shown (badged, read-only) and can still be issued certificates — activating an account is now left as an explicit decision in Moodle user administration. (The explicit admin "activate" action on the Students page and the rollback-suspend in data_import remain, as those are deliberate user-initiated actions, not side-effects of issuing a certificate.) (2) A-P2-3 NAT FIX — when the AVETMISS NAT00120 export coerces a blank/''00'' outcome to ''70'' (Continuing activity), it now also reports the record as OPEN (activity end date = reporting period end) instead of emitting ''70'' together with a recorded completion end date, which is internally inconsistent and NCVER flags. The AVETMISS Validation page still surfaces these records so the RTO enters the real outcome. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100411. — prior v5.9.410 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER EVIDENCE UPLOADS + RESULTS/CERT TIE-IN CHECK. (1) FILE UPLOADS — the RPL & Credit Transfer record form now has real file uploads: a "Source certificate / transcript (from the issuing RTO)" uploader on credit-transfer records (attach the other RTO''s testamur / SoA / RoR / USI transcript that authenticates the transfer) and an "RPL evidence files" uploader on RPL records (portfolio, references, prior quals, observation records). Both accept multiple files (PDF/image/Office/text, 20MB each), list already-uploaded files with download + remove links, are stored in the Moodle File API keyed by the record id, served through local_rtocompliance_pluginfile (new fileareas rpl_evidence + ct_sourcecert, manage capability), and cleaned up when the record is deleted. Each uploader carries plain-English ASQA instructions (Standard 1.6 for RPL, Clause 1.7 / Clause 12 for credit transfer). The old free-text "Evidence Files" box is retained as optional notes for evidence held outside the system. (2) TIE-IN VERIFICATION — deep-audited that RPL (outcome 51) and Credit Transfer (outcome 60), written to the results register by local_rtocompliance_apply_rpl_outcome(), are treated as COMPETENT across every relevant path: Student Results (student_profile.php, qualbuilder_results.php), qualification-completion detection (check_full_qual_completion, get_completed_units_for_qual, process_enrolment_task, observer, completion_reconciler, certificate_validator) and ALL certificate paths (generate_qual_certs, qual_cert_hub, generate_course_certs, and the renderer which labels 51=RPL Granted / 60=Credit Transfer on the SoA/RoR). Fixed the one gap the audit found: the Students dashboard "Competency Achieved (Units)" card counted only outcome 20 — it now counts 20/51/60/81 so RPL/CT units are included. Also corrected the scrambled outcomeidentifier help text to the accurate NCVER code meanings. No schema changes (files use the Moodle File API; the rpl table already had studentid/rpltype/usitranscriptverified). Savepoint 2026073100410. — prior v5.9.409 EDITOR BRANDING NOW ACTUALLY RENDERS (real root cause). The certificate editor paints the RTO logo / NRT logo / CEO signature / organisation seal in the canvas as <img src="pluginfile…"> URLs, but local_rtocompliance_pluginfile() only served three fileareas (cert_template_bg, cert_template_image, rto_branding). The assets uploaded via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings live in admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas (logo, nrt_logo_file, aqf_logo_file, organisation_seal_file, compliance_logo_1/2, ceo_signature_file, secondary_logo, cert_background_file) — NONE of which the handler served — so every branding image request 404'd and the canvas showed an empty box, even though the issued PDF rendered the logos fine (the PDF reads the file straight off disk, bypassing pluginfile entirely). The pluginfile handler now serves those branding fileareas (system context, managecerttemplates capability), so the editor canvas finally matches the issued certificate. This is the missing piece behind the v5.9.406 getter fix: the getters resolved the correct file and produced a URL, but that URL was not servable until now. (2) EDITOR SHOWS REAL RTO IDENTITY — the canvas now always paints the RTO's own configured values for rto.name, rto.code, signatory.name, signatory.title and aqf_statement (independent of the "Show sample data" toggle), because these are fixed RTO-identity values, not per-student sample data. Previously the canvas showed the generic catalogue placeholder ("National Compliance Training / 50918") whenever sample data was off, which read as "the editor isn't pulling RTO settings" even though issued certificates were always correct. Verified the issued-certificate payload (resolve_payload) sources every field correctly: rto.name/rto.code/signatory/aqf_statement from the issue-time snapshot then live config; student name/USI, qualification code/name, dates and cert number from the cert + student records; mandatory phrases from config with ASQA defaults. Purge all caches after install. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100409. — prior v5.9.408 TEMPLATE DELETE + DEACTIVATE CONTROLS. Adds two admin controls to the Certificate Templates list so a template can be cleared out and regenerated without digging through statuses: (1) DELETE — a Delete button now appears on EVERY template row regardless of status (including the active one), backed by a new force_delete() path + 'forcedelete' action (the audit-safe delete() that only removed drafts/archived is kept for programmatic callers). Deleting the active template is safe: issuance and preview fall back to the built-in ASQA starter until a new template is activated. Uploaded background/per-field-image files are cleaned up. Confirm prompt is extra-strong (and states the active-template fallback) since it is permanent. (2) MAKE NON-ACTIVE — a new deactivate() method + 'deactivate' action + "Make non-active" button shown on the currently active template, which clears the active flag WITHOUT archiving (the template stays approved and one-click re-activatable). New lang strings: cert_template_deactivate_btn, cert_template_confirm_deactivate, cert_template_action_ok_deactivated. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100408. — prior v5.9.407 SANITISE EXISTING SAVED CERT TEMPLATES (retro-fix for already-saved templates). v5.9.406 fixed the STARTER (new templates) and the RENDER path, but a template already saved in the database kept its old fields — so an existing Statement of Attainment still showed the duplicate/overlapping "form part of" + "completion of course" statements AND still carried the "Verify at: <url>" text field. A new upgrade step (savepoint 2026073100407) now rewrites every saved cert-template design to match a fresh starter: it drops every qualification.completionofcoursestatement field (redundant — the single "form part of" line is the ASQA statement), drops every authenticity_measure text field (QR-only default; the mandatory QR code stays and satisfies the authenticity requirement), and widens the surviving "form part of" box for a clean two-line wrap. Fully guarded (a bad design row is skipped, an unchanged design is left untouched); RTOs can drag the "Authenticity measure" field back on if they want the URL text. This is what makes an ALREADY-SAVED template pick up the QR-only + single-statement fixes without a manual "Reset to starter". IMPORTANT after install: run Site administration → Development → Purge all caches (the editor JS and branding checks are cached). NOTE on branding: the editor now paints the real RTO logo / NRT logo / signature / seal from RTO Settings (v5.9.406 getter fix) — if a slot still shows a placeholder box after purging caches, that specific asset is not uploaded under Certificate Settings for that cert type. No schema changes (data-only design rewrite). Savepoint 2026073100407. — prior v5.9.406 CERTIFICATE EDITOR FIXES + QR-ONLY DEFAULT + CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT. (1) EDITOR BRANDING (critical) — the certificate editor showed "[RTO logo]" / "[NRT logo]" / "[CEO signature image]" / "[Org seal]" text placeholders instead of the real artwork whenever the RTO had uploaded those assets via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings, because the editor's branding-URL getters only looked in the FA_BRANDING pseudo-itemid area and never the admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas where the settings pages actually store them (the issued PDF found them via resolve_compliance_asset_path()'s fallback chain, so the canvas and the print diverged). New get_branding_display_url() mirrors the renderer's exact chain (FA_BRANDING → settings filearea → bundled pix) and now backs get_branding_logo/signature/sta/nrt/aqf/org_seal_url(); the editor host now also passes the NRT, AQF and STA logo URLs to the JS (previously only logo/signature/seal were), and the editor canvas paints nrt_logo/aqf_logo/state_training_authority_logo from them. (2) SoA COMPLIANCE STATEMENT — the Statement of Attainment starter carried BOTH "These competencies form part of {code} {name}" AND the near-identical "These competencies were attained in completion of {code} course in {name}", auto-built from the same qualification and stacked 5-7mm apart, so they overlapped into an unreadable block. The redundant "completion of course" statement (which is for accredited short courses, not qualifications) is removed from the default starter (still draggable from the palette), the single "form part of" statement box is widened for clean two-line wrap, and the descriptors are re-spaced; the renderer AND sample preview now also suppress the completion statement whenever the form-part-of line is present, so templates already saved with both fields render only the correct one. (3) QR-ONLY DEFAULT — the "Verify at: <url>" authenticity_measure text field is removed from all eight starter templates; the mandatory verification QR code (auto-added by ensure_mandatory_fields, and already accepted by the validator as a valid authenticity measure) is the default, and RTOs can drag the URL text back on if they want it. (4) CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT — editor font sizing now converts points→pixels with the correct 0.3528×BASE_SCALE factor (was a hardcoded 1.33 that rendered every field ~26% oversized vs the PDF, throwing off drag-to-fit); the two inline <script> emitters on the editor page use JSON_HEX_* flags so author-entered text can't break out; the disabled-path return of send_certificate_email() now uses the canonical ok/email/error shape its callers read (was success/reason, causing an undefined-key warning and a blank failure message); and revoking a certificate now calls update_registry_status(token,'revoked') so a revoked cert's public QR verifies as Revoked instead of Valid. Also bundles the pending verify.php superseded-cert fix and the Student Results Moodle-completion effective-outcome wiring from the working set. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100406. (1) The Student Profile results section is rebuilt into a proper command view: a per-qualification progress hero (X of Y units competent, progress bar, outcome-breakdown chips), unit results GROUPED BY QUALIFICATION with a new Source column (which Moodle course each result came from), friendly colour-coded outcome badges, an outcome legend, and consolidated action buttons — "Issue Statement of Attainment", "Issue Qualification Certificate" (pre-fills the hub with the student's USI), and "Record / edit results". (2) OUTCOME LABELS: the raw AVETMISS placeholder "00" (and blank/10) now displays as "Not yet assessed" on the Enrolments page and profile (it is NOT Competent or NYC — it means no result recorded yet). Verified every outcome label against NCVER's official "Reporting a final outcome" fact sheet: code 70 is correctly "Continuing activity" (corrected two internal spots that read "Continuing enrolment"); 40/41/61/85 confirmed correct. (3) DATES: the Enrolments page Activity Start Date (and the Moodle-enrolment list dates) now include the YEAR (they used Moodle's short date format which omits it). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100405. — prior v5.9.404 left-hand menu fix. several admin pages rendered without the plugin's left sidebar because they called $OUTPUT->header() but never local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header(). Fixed on Moodle Course Map (course_map.php — reported), AVETMISS Validation (nat_validate.php), NAT Reconciliation (reconcile.php — replaced its bare rtoc-main-content div with the full layout-wrap + sidebar), and the Over-Enrolment / Bulk Over-Enrolment / Skipped Program Codes diagnostic pages. A full sweep confirms every remaining page without the sidebar is an intentional public token page (certificate verification, survey response, student declaration, student LLN form), which correctly have no admin menu. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100404. — prior v5.9.403 button text padding. long-label buttons (e.g. the full-width "Sync results from Moodle completions" side-panel button) were clipping because the plugin's button style forced white-space:nowrap with a fixed single-line height, so a long label in a narrow button ran to the edges. Buttons now allow their text to WRAP with height:auto (padding honoured), and small buttons (.btn-sm) get comfortable padding + a slightly smaller font — a single stylesheet fix that applies to every button in the plugin's main content area. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100403. — prior v5.9.402 backlog close-out. (final audit P2/P3s): (1) CREDIT-TRANSFER SOURCE AUTHENTICATION (Std 1.7) — a credit-transfer decision no longer posts a competency to the register unless the USI transcript is verified; otherwise it warns and holds (RPL is unaffected). (2) PRIVACY — complaint/appeal records now capture the complainant/appellant Moodle user id (resolved from email) so privacy export & erasure include them. (3) WORKFORCE CREDENTIALS — corrected the assessor skill-set picklist (removed the invalid TAESS00021, added the real TAESS00011 Assessor Skill Set and TAESS00019 Enterprise Trainer Skill Set, relabelled TAESS00024) and synced the help text; added advisory reminders that a TAS should be reviewed when its training product is superseded, and that TAE-package assessments need independent validation before the first cohort. (4) LABEL CORRECTNESS — the SoA unit-outcome filter now uses the correct AVETMISS codes (Credit transfer = 60; 81/82 shown as non-assessable, not "superseded competent"), and the Statement-of-Attainment "requires" text lists the correct competent set (20/51/60/81). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100402. — prior v5.9.401 procedural fairness + sensitive-data permission. (audit P2s). COMPLAINTS (Std 2.7): new respondent, respondent-response, and date-outcome-communicated fields so the RTO can demonstrate the party complained about was heard and all parties were told the outcome. APPEALS (Std 2.8): new original-decision-maker + reviewer-independence-confirmed + underlying-record-corrected fields; the appeal edit page now warns (advisory) when an upheld assessment appeal has not had its underlying record corrected, or when independence has not been confirmed. SENSITIVE DATA: a new local/rtocompliance:viewsensitive capability (granted to managers by default) now gates the disability disclosure on the student profile — staff without it see "Restricted", while the student always sees their own and managers are unaffected. Schema savepoint 401 (complaints + appeals fields). — prior v5.9.400 help & support refresh. the Support Centre "What's New" panel (was stuck at v5.9.378), Get Started guide, feature/module cards and FAQ, plus the How It Works Key Questions, are updated to the current feature set — Compliance Health, AVETMISS Validation, ASQA Compliance Mapping, the world-class student profile, student certificate access (portal + nav link + dashboard block), automated weekly alerts, full NAT demographic + address propagation, the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, and the certificate-integrity + validation/workforce/QI hardening. Also corrected stale docs that described the retired auto-enrolment behaviour and the old "USI warning" as current (issuance is now a hard verified-USI block). Documentation only. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100400. — prior v5.9.399 automated compliance alerts. a new weekly scheduled task (compliance_alert_task, Mondays 07:00) emails site administrators a plain-English digest whenever key audit-readiness risks need attention — validations overdue, working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, students with results but an unverified USI (cert-blocked), certificates past the 30-day issuance rule, and incomplete AVETMISS profiles — with a one-click link to the Compliance Health page. Sends ONLY when something needs attention (no all-clear noise); fully guarded so a mail failure or missing table can never break cron; disable by setting config compliancealerts=0, and add an extra recipient via config alertemail. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100399. — prior v5.9.398 AVETMISS pre-submission validator. (the crown-jewel feature): a new read-only "AVETMISS Validation" page (nat_validate.php, in Data & Reporting) checks every reportable student and enrolment against NCVER/AVETMISS edit rules BEFORE the RTO exports NAT files — so a quarterly submission is not rejected. STUDENT checks: missing/invalid USI (+ unverified-USI warning), missing/invalid DOB, sex, postcode, state, country of birth, language, Indigenous status, labour force, school level, at-school flag; disability/prior-ed detail warnings. ENROLMENT checks: invalid/blank outcome code, a final outcome with no end date, missing start date, end-before-start, blank program/unit code; warnings for continuing-with-past-end-date, invalid delivery mode / funding source, and missing scheduled hours on a delivered unit. Findings are split ERROR (will fail NCVER) vs WARNING, grouped by category with a "Ready to submit / N errors to fix" verdict and a full CSV export. Fully read-only and defensively guarded. Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100398. — prior v5.9.397 Compliance Health command centre. a new flagship read-only page (compliance_health.php, first in the left menu) that answers "are we audit-ready right now?" at a glance. A hero audit-readiness score (percentage of key checks currently clear) with a verdict, over a responsive grid of Quality-Area cards surfacing live risk signals: validations overdue / due soon, qualifications never validated, incomplete AVETMISS profiles, open complaints & appeals (past timeframe), working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, QI survey response rate, open high-severity risks, and — critically — students with results but an UNVERIFIED USI (the certificates you cannot yet issue). Every metric has a status pill and a one-click "fix" link to the relevant page. Fully read-only and defensively guarded (every query wrapped; a missing table never breaks the page). Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100397. — prior v5.9.396 AVETMISS address propagation. the student's full street address (building/property name, flat-unit, street number+name, and postcode) is now parsed from NAT00085 — previously the parser dropped it — staged, and propagated into the student profile alongside the other demographics (both automatically on import for existing profiles, and via Backfill). New staging columns postcode/buildingname/unitno/streetname (savepoint 396); the students table already had the matching columns. The student profile summary now shows the complete address (building, unit/street, suburb, state, postcode) instead of just suburb+state. Savepoint 2026073100396. — prior v5.9.395 audit trail + portability. (1) the Complaints, Appeals and Continuous-Improvement registers now write an audit-log entry on every create/update/delete (previously these compliance records could be altered or deleted with no trail — an ASQA evidence gap); logging is wrapped defensively so it can never block the user action. (2) The NAT export replaced a MySQL/Postgres-only "LIMIT 1" with a portable limited query so it no longer risks failing on Oracle/MSSQL. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100395. — prior v5.9.394 world-class student profile. (1) The Student Records list now makes each student NAME a one-click link to their profile, and the row Actions menu gains Certificates + Results/Enrolments shortcuts. (2) student_profile.php now opens with a polished READ-ONLY summary above the edit form: a header card (name, client ID, USI + verification badge, completeness pill that lists missing fields ON LOAD), a demographics grid showing every AVETMISS field as a HUMAN LABEL (with a muted "Not stated" for placeholders), a unit-results table with colour-coded outcome badges, and an issued-certificates card with one-click PDF download — so an admin can review a student's whole picture in one place instead of a bare edit form. (3) Reissuing a certificate now preserves the original as-issued USI snapshot and RTO-identity snapshot (C-P2-1), so a faithful copy shows exactly what the original showed. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100394. — prior v5.9.393 student My Certificates nav link + dashboard block. students now get a persistent "My Certificates" link in the plugin navigation (local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation previously returned nothing for students, so their only link was buried on their Moodle profile page). The link points to the certificate portal (mycerts.php), which enforces its own access control so a student only ever sees their own certificates. A companion Dashboard block (block_rtocompliance_mycerts, delivered separately) shows a student their issued certificates with one-click download on login. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100393. — prior v5.9.392 removed Moodle account creation from Backfill. "Backfill Student Records" no longer creates Moodle {user} accounts (user_create_user removed). A NAT student with no existing Moodle account is now SKIPPED and reported ("no Moodle account — an administrator must create one first, then re-run Backfill"). Backfill now only READS Moodle users and writes the plugin's own student profile + demographics for students who already have an account. Combined with v5.9.387, the plugin creates/deletes NOTHING in Moodle core (no enrolments, no completions, and now no user accounts) — it only reads them. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100392. — prior v5.9.391 NAT demographic propagation regression fix. After a NAT import the AVETMISS demographic data now flows into the student profile again: (1) the finalize step now automatically refreshes the demographic fields (DOB, sex, suburb/state, Indigenous status, labour force, highest school level, language at home, country of birth, disability flag, prior-education flag, at-school flag) on EXISTING student profiles from the freshly-staged NAT00080 data — writing ONLY to the plugin students table (no Moodle user/enrolment/completion writes), so it is constraint-safe; a staged value only overwrites when it is real (never wipes good data with an AVETMISS "not stated" placeholder). This restores propagation that had lived inside the now-disabled auto-enrol handlers. (2) The manual "Backfill Student Records" step was silently dropping 8 core demographics to defaults because its staging SELECT omitted them — the SELECT now pulls all demographic columns, so a backfill writes the full profile. (3) Cert render-time backstop now also blocks the NRT logo on 'attendance' certs (matches the template catalogue's forbidden_for). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100391. — prior v5.9.390 cert-template polish F4/F5/F6. (F4) render-time compliance backstop — the renderer now drops any element forbidden for the cert type before it reaches the PDF (NRT logo never on a Record of Results or non-accredited Completion; USI never on a Testamur or Statement of Attainment), backing up the approval-time validation against pinned/override/legacy designs. (F5) certificate PREVIEW now applies the template's per-template designjson.overrides{} exactly as the real issue path does, so previews are faithful for override-using templates. (F6) the Test Certificate now uses its own dummy verify token and placeholder USI instead of an empty token + the logged-in admin's live USI. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100390. — prior v5.9.389 CERTIFICATE-TEMPLATE INTEGRITY (F1 as-issued RTO snapshot / F2 approved-only pinned template / F3 block issuance on blank RTO details). (F1) each certificate now snapshots the RTO identity settings (legal name, provider code, signatory name/title, AQF statement) at issue time into a new certs.issuesnapshot column and the renderer renders from that snapshot, so a later change to those settings cannot retroactively rewrite an already-issued certificate (mirrors the USI snapshot). (F2) pick_for_cert() renders the pinned template ONLY if it is still status='approved', so an in-progress/unvalidated draft edit can no longer leak onto an already-issued certificate on re-download (it falls back to the current approved template). (F3) issuance is now refused — interactively (non-bypassable) and programmatically — when mandatory RTO details (legal name, national provider code, authorised signatory) are not configured, preventing certificates that render those AQF-required fields blank; the "ready to issue" validator surfaces the same gap. Savepoint 2026073100389. — prior v5.9.388: ASQA PRACTICE-GUIDE AUDIT P1 REMEDIATION PART 2 + ASQA COMPLIANCE MAPPING. Feature code on the v5.9.387 schema: (1) VALIDATION (Std 1.5) — validator-independence declaration is required to complete a validation, and completion is blocked without it; a five-year validation cycle now computes/stores nextduedate (2 years for high-risk), with OVERDUE/DUE-SOON flags and a Coverage-Gaps list of on-scope products with no current validation; assessment outcome + rectification actions are captured. (2) WORKFORCE (Std 3.2) — "Working Towards" trainers now record a start date and an enforced 2-year TAE completion deadline; manager sign-off is blocked for a blank credential or a lapsed working-towards window; supervisors must hold a full, unexpired credential; a Supervision overdue/due-soon alert lists at-risk working-towards trainers. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT (Std 2.3/2.4/2.6) — per-student support / reasonable-adjustment / wellbeing records now persist server-side in local_rtocompliance_supportnotes (retained, shared, auditable) instead of browser localStorage. (4) QUALITY INDICATORS (Std 4.4) — the ad-hoc surveys are replaced with the official AQTF Learner & Employer Questionnaires (items tagged to their scales) and qi_report renders a proper QI Annual Summary (indicator + scale scores, response rates); the QI export is now the aggregate summary, not identifiable per-respondent rows. (5) NEW "ASQA Compliance Mapping" left-menu page (asqa_standards_map.php) — every 2025 Standard mapped to the feature that supports it with an honest Covered/Partial/Gap status (Std 4.3/4.4 self-assurance). No schema changes beyond savepoint 387. Savepoint 2026073100388.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.452'; // v5.9.452 USI CREDENTIAL-BROKER-ONLY hardening. The myGovID machine credential (.p12 keystore) and its passphrase are now held ONLY on the lms-labs.com platform, which verifies USIs on this site's behalf via /api/usi/verify. Confirmed the Moodle plugin verifies exclusively through the platform client (the local SOAP registry client is unused dead code and the stored password was read by nothing), so the keystore is not needed on the Moodle server. Changes: (1) webhook.php no longer writes the credential locally — it drops usi_certificate_password from its allow-list and, instead of decoding usi_cert_base64 to a .p12 on disk, records a non-secret usi_cert_uploaded readiness flag; (2) the legacy usi_certificate_path and usi_certificate_password fields are REMOVED from RTO settings, replaced by a note that credentials are managed in the lms-labs.com admin panel; (3) usi_is_configured() now judges readiness from the platform connection plus the readiness flag, not a local keystore file; (4) a one-time upgrade purges any keystore/password an earlier push had planted on this server (unsets the config and deletes dataroot/local_rtocompliance/usi_credential.p12). USI verification is unaffected. Purge caches after installing. Savepoint 2026080400452. — prior v5.9.451 PRACTICE-GUIDE LINKS now open the OFFICIAL ASQA PDF. ASQA restructured their website, which broke the plugin's old practice-guide links (the "standard" pills on the help cards, e.g. the AQF issuance pill on the certificate pages). Each help-card guide pill now resolves to the official final ASQA practice-guide PDF and opens it in a new tab (the browser's PDF viewer), so clicking shows the actual document instead of a dead link. URLs were researched Aug 2026: stable asqa.gov.au/media/<id> permalinks are used where ASQA publishes them (Integrity of Nationally Recognised Training Products, Feedback/Complaints/Appeals, Fit and Proper Person), with current dated PDF paths for Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Risk Management and Continuous Improvement. Three guides with no confirmed standalone final PDF fall back to the current stable ASQA practice-guides pages so no link is ever broken. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400451. — prior v5.9.450 BUTTON HOVER CONTRAST audit + save-payload robustness. (1) CONTRAST — every Bootstrap button variant used in the plugin now has an explicit, readable hover so no button renders light text on a light background. The reported case was the outline buttons on the Certificate Templates action column (Edit / Preview / Make default): those sit OUTSIDE the .rtoc-main-content container, so the plugin's scoped hover rules did not reach them and Bootstrap's default white-on-light-amber (btn-outline-warning) showed through. New broadly-scoped rules cover warning, danger, info, light, dark and every outline form (warning/info/success), plus a safety net for outline-primary/secondary outside the main container. (2) SAVE — the hidden design field is now kept continuously in sync on every edit (not only on the submit event), so the layout payload can never be empty at submit time even if a stale cached build is momentarily active; the server message is clearer too. IMPORTANT: purge caches after installing so the new JavaScript is served. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400450. — prior v5.9.449 CERT EDITOR SAVE FIX + LAYOUT RULES across ALL certificate types. (1) MALFORMED DESIGN PAYLOAD on Save draft is fixed: when the browser could not serialise the layout it silently posted an empty field and the server rejected it as "malformed design payload". The editor now serialises with a never-throwing, circular-safe pass and refuses to post an empty/invalid payload (clear message instead), and the server message now distinguishes an empty payload from invalid JSON and reassures that the saved copy is untouched. (2) LAYOUT RULES applied to every cert type, for both new starters and existing saved templates (via the shared normaliser the renderer and editor both run, so the PDF and canvas stay in sync — no DB migration, no divergence): the small DATE and AUTHORISED PERSON caption labels are removed (the issue date and signatory name/title still print); the NRT logo, organisation seal and verification QR now render 30mm tall with aspect preserved and centred inside their box (never stretched). (3) UNITS TABLE: all text is a minimum of 12pt including the table; the unit code column is widened to hold a 12pt code on one line; long unit titles now WRAP onto a second line instead of shrinking. Canvas preview updated to match. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400449. — prior v5.9.448 AUTO-CREATE / ARCHIVE-VERSIONS CLARITY + name cleanup. (1) The Auto-Create Qualifications page builds ONE product per national qualification code, so every semester/archive copy of a qualification (S1 26, S2 26, S1 27 ...) collapses into that single code — which is why only one row per code appears and it skips once a product already exists. A prominent callout (and button) now routes admins to the Semester Intake Builder, which lists every semester/archive sub-category as its own Draft product with its exact course list, reading the qualification code and title from the parent category. This closes the main point of confusion about where the archive versions are built. (2) NAME CLEANUP — when a Moodle category named the code inside brackets, e.g. "Diploma of Customs Broking (TLI50816)", stripping the code left an empty "()" so detected names printed as "Diploma of Customs Broking ()". The code extractor now removes any now-empty bracket pair and collapses the doubled space, fixing detected names on Auto-Create, the Semester Intake Builder and everywhere category names are resolved. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400448. — prior v5.9.447 STYLE A UNITS TABLE for the Statement of Attainment and Record of Results. The unit list on both certificates now renders as one shaded three-column table — Unit Code (left) | Unit Title (left-aligned) | Completion Date (centre) — with a coloured header bar (white bold headings), zebra-striped alternating rows and thin cell borders, drawn in TCPDF (solid fills and borders, no gradients). A new Certificate Setting, "Units table header colour" (colour picker), sets the header-bar fill and defaults to the Moodle site primary / brand colour; header text prints white for contrast. The per-unit Completion Date is wired from the compliance register (the unit result / activity end date, falling back to the start date), captured at issue time and back-filled from the register for older certificates in a single query. Both cert types share one renderer: the RoR ror_table field and the SoA dynamic qualification.units field both route to it, so existing templates pick up the new table with no template edits. The in-editor canvas preview was updated to draw the identical shaded table (header colour, columns and zebra) so what you design matches the issued PDF. All certificate text now has a 12pt minimum floor for readability (previously many fields rendered at 9 to 10pt); the field height cap still contains anything that would otherwise overflow. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400447. — prior v5.9.446 CODE-FIRST / NO-DASH CONVENTION for unit & qualification labels. Everywhere a unit or qualification code and its title were shown together they now render as "CODE Title" — code first, title second, a single space between, no hyphen or em-dash. Fixed in the certificate renderer (the Statement of Attainment / Record of Results unit lists and their sample previews) and across the plugin UI (qualification dropdowns on Student Results and Generate Certificates, the My Certificates and public verify pages, Qual Builder delete confirmations + audit log, unit delete confirmation, RPL unit label, skipped-programcodes list, TAS heading + PDF/DOCX exports, suitability PDF). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100446. — prior v5.9.445 CSS SCOPING FIX (help card lost styling on admin pages) + SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER now reads the qualification from the PARENT category. (1) CSS — the plugin's help card and other scoped styles are scoped to the body class "path-local-rtocompliance". Pages that use admin_externalpage_setup() have their pagetype (and therefore the auto-generated "path-*" body class) overridden to an "admin-*" value, so that class was absent and every scoped rule silently failed (the sidebar still styled because its CSS is unscoped). Certificate Templates was the reported case; the same latent gap affected 12 admin pages in total — cert_templates, cert_template_edit, cert_test, nat_validate, nominalhours_import, reconcile, trainer_dashboard, usi_settings, foe_audit, foe_bulk_audit, recovery_analyzer, regression_test — each now calls $PAGE->add_body_class('path-local-rtocompliance') before output so the scoped CSS applies (the four remaining admin_externalpage files — qi_export, tas_export, settings, version — are file exports/config, not rendered pages). Purge caches after install. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — the qualification code and title are now read deterministically from the semester sub-category's PARENT category (parent = qualification code + title, the sub-category = the semester), not guessed from the unit set; the exact list of unit-code courses under the sub-category becomes the intake's units/courses. Where a semester has no coded parent the code box is left blank for the admin to set once. The preview shows the parent-derived qualification title beside each code box. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100445. — prior v5.9.444 SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — a separate qualification product per semester intake. New tool (qualbuilder_semester.php) + helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_semester_intakes() / local_rtocompliance_create_semester_intakes(). It scans every Moodle category that holds unit-code courses (e.g. "Archive - 23 DCB S1"), treating each as a semester intake: the category name becomes the product streamname, the unit codes parsed from the course names become its units, and those courses are linked (extra copies as archive variants). Because the archive category names carry a semester but NOT a qualification code, the code is AUTO-SUGGESTED by matching the intake's unit set to existing products (best overlap, with a version-letter-stripped fallback) and is editable per row so the admin sets it once per qualification era where it can't be inferred. A preview lists every detected intake with its semester, unit/course counts, detected unit codes and the suggested code; on confirm it creates one Draft product per ticked intake (qualcode + streamname). Duplicates (same qualcode + streamname) are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin's own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — no Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments are created or changed. Linked from the Qualification Builder header alongside Auto-Create and Recover Unmapped Completions. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100444. — prior v5.9.443 AUTO-CREATE — COURSE MAP IS NOW THE DEFAULT SOURCE + bigger info-box text. The "From Category Tree" scan returned nothing on this site because units here are delivered as COURSES (e.g. "TLIR4001 & TLIR4002 … MSP") under semester/archive categories, not as unit-code sub-categories — so the tree-walk found no unit layer. The Course Map already captures course → qual → unit correctly (seeded from those same categories and courses), so Auto-Create now defaults to the "From Course Map" source and the instructions say so; the Category-Tree tab is kept but explained as only for sites whose units are named sub-categories. Also: the page info boxes ("How this works" / "What this does") were too small — bumped to 15px (and the shared .rtoc-dob-sync-bar base font raised), and the empty-state on the Course Map source now points to Scan & Seed if the map is empty. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100443. — prior v5.9.442 CERTIFICATE EDITOR — ROOT-CAUSE FIX (canvas vs issued-PDF data divergence) + RECOVER UNMAPPED COMPLETIONS TOOL. CERT EDITOR: the meta-root-cause of the recurring "wrong preview" complaints was that the drag-and-drop CANVAS and the issued-PDF renderer used DIFFERENT data sources — on default load the canvas painted each field its own hardcoded per-field catalogue placeholder (meta.sample) while every prior fix (RTO identity v5.9.409/412, statement dedupe v5.9.406/407) only ever touched the PDF renderer's sample_payload, which the canvas did not use. Fixes: (1) CANVAS-DATA-UNIFY — the editor JS resolver now renders the SAME coherent sample record the issued PDF uses (a key present in sample_payload wins, even when intentionally blank), so unrelated placeholders (a First-Aid skill-set line, a Business qualification, an "[insert language]" token) no longer stack on the canvas and the skill-set/optional statements that should be blank now are. (2) STALE AMD BUILD — amd/build/cert_template_editor.js was 37 lines behind source (missing the whole real-RTO-identity code path), so dev/debug sites served the old behaviour; both build artifacts (.js and .min.js) are regenerated from source. (3) RTO NAME PLACEHOLDER — the editor canvas AND the issued renderer now fall back to the real Moodle site name (the RTO's own name) when the RTO legal name has not been set in RTO Settings, instead of showing the catalogue placeholder "National Compliance Training" (canvas) or the generic "Training Organisation" (issued). Set your legal name in RTO Settings for the exact wording. (4) "[insert language]" — the sample-preview payload hardcoded the literal "[insert language]" fill-in token; it now reads the languagestatement setting (or blank), matching the issued path. (5) REQUIRED DOT — the red filled "!" circle on required palette fields read as an error; it is now a clear amber "Required" pill (it always meant "required for this certificate type", never an error). RECOVER TOOL: new "Recover Unmapped Completions" page (qualbuilder_recover.php) + helpers scan the completions the sync could not map, propose old→current unit-code mappings (version-letter drops auto-ticked; single-unit name matches flagged for review), and on confirm write them to the supersededunitmap setting so the next Sync credits them; codes with no current unit are listed separately (build the superseded qual first). Also: "Auto-Create from Categories" scans the category tree or the Course Map. Writes only plugin config/tables; no Moodle-core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100442. — prior v5.9.441 RELEASE-PIPELINE FIX — cleared the one failed check. qualbuilder_autocreate.php inline select-all script used anonymous JS closures written as the flagged no-space form; rewritten to the spaced closure form (and the one-line if given braces) so the coding-style scanner no longer reports a spacing finding in that file. Pure coding-style change to one inline script; no functional, behavioural or schema change. The 6 advisory warnings are pre-existing and unchanged (ALL-CAPS lang values such as ABN/ASQA on legacy strings, capability-check advisories on read-only report/editor pages, the audited unserialize-with-allowed-classes call in process_enrolment_task, and inline-comment/one-statement style notes across legacy files). Savepoint 2026073100441. — prior v5.9.440 PARKED ITEMS BUILT. (1) NAT IMPORT OUTCOME / RESULTS GRID — a register enrolment that exists but has no recorded AVETMISS outcome (blank / NULL / "00") now renders on Student Results as a clear "Not yet assessed" dash instead of a confusing "?"; blank outcomes are normalised at both the on-screen grid and the CSV export, and any present-but-unrecognised code now shows as itself rather than "?". The NAT results importer VALID_OUTCOMES set gained "41" (incomplete — RTO closure), a valid AVETMISS code the parser accepts and the grid can display that was previously collapsed to "00". (2) MISSING-AVETMISS-DATA STUDENT PROMPT — a logged-in student whose AVETMISS profile is incomplete now sees a modal (site-wide, once per browser session) listing the fields still needed, with a "Complete my details now" button to their self-service profile and a tip that certificates can be downloaded from the profile menu (top-right initials). It reads only the student own row (one lookup by userid), is never shown to admins/guests or on the profile page itself, and is injected via the existing before_footer hook using an external CSP-safe script (js/avetmiss_prompt.js) so no inline script is blocked; the primary button is a plain link so the profile is always reachable. (3) HELP-CARD TEXT SIZE — the What / Why / How / Key-Features card body was enlarged from 14px to 15.5px (tabs 13px to 14px) for readability. (4) audit.php gained first-time How-to steps — the one page missed in the v5.9.438 rewrite — so help-step coverage is now complete. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100440. — prior v5.9.439 AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" NOW RESOLVES REAL NAMES (no more code-as-name). The v5.9.438 Course-Map source stored the unit code as the unit name because the course_map table holds only codes. Fixed: local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() now builds a CODE→name map from your Moodle category names (every category whose name carries a code — qualification categories like "TLI50321 — Diploma of …" and unit leaf categories like "TLIX0036 — Load and unload goods" — contributes its title, longest-name-wins; unit/qual titles are national so one map is safe) and uses it for BOTH the qualification name and each unit name. So building from the Course Map now produces the same real qualification and unit titles as the Category-Tree source, fully offline — reusing the category-name resolution instead of defaulting to the code. The training.gov.au enrichment option still overrides with official TGA names/packaging when ticked. Structure still comes from your existing, confirmed course_map rows; only the naming was reused rather than reinvented. Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100439. — prior v5.9.438 HELP-STEP REWRITE COMPLETED (ALL PAGES) + AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" SOURCE. (1) The v5.9.437 "How to use it" rewrite was extended from 40 to ~90 pages — every remaining left-menu page, editor and sub-page now shows the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence naming its real on-screen controls (cert issue/email/generate, template editor, TAS editor/consultation, transitions, trainer dashboard/voccomp, validation & validator editors, student support/declaration, fee/insurance/third-party/governance/risk editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, marketing, surveys/QI/AI reports, reconcile, deadlines, alerts, audit log, ASQA/compliance maps, practice guides, student portal pages, and more). All applied via the same per-page 'how' override, leaving What/Why/Key Features untouched. (2) AUTO-CREATE now offers a SOURCE toggle — "From Category Tree" or "From Course Map". The new read-only helper local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() groups your existing (and already-confirmed) Course Map rows by qualification code, links each unit's delivery courses, and reads the qualification name from its Moodle category — so you can build products straight from the mapping you already have (unit names default to the code unless training.gov.au enrichment is ticked). Same safety guarantees: Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle categories/courses/accounts/enrolments touched. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100438. — prior v5.9.437 AUTO-CREATE QUALIFICATIONS + FIRST-TIME HELP-STEP REWRITE. (1) AUTO-CREATE — new "Auto-Create from Categories" tool in the Qualification Builder (qualbuilder_autocreate.php) scans the Moodle category tree (parent category = qualification code + title, leaf sub-category = unit code + name, delivery courses underneath) and builds Qual Builder products with their units and course links in one pass. It shows a READ-ONLY preview (qual code, name, units found, courses linked, New vs Already-exists) with per-qual checkboxes and an optional best-effort training.gov.au enrichment (official name, packaging counts, AQF level, core/elective type, per-unit names) that falls back to the category names when the platform API is unavailable. New helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_categories_for_quals() (read-only) and local_rtocompliance_autocreate_quals_from_scan(). Products are created as Draft; duplicate qual codes are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — it never creates or changes Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments. (2) HELP CARDS — the "How to use it" tab on 40 primary pages was rewritten from each page real UI into the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence, naming the actual on-screen controls (e.g. USI setup: enter TOID, choose the machine-credential keystore, type the keystore password, tick EVTE, click Save credential; Course Map: click Scan & Seed All Quals, filter, confirm rows), replacing the older generic wording. Applied as a per-page 'how' override merged over the existing help overlay, so the What / Why text and Key Features are unchanged. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100437. — prior v5.9.436 CRITICAL — RESTORED DEAD ACTION BUTTONS + NAVBAR AVATAR ALIGNMENT. (1) ROOT CAUSE of the Student Results grid staying empty / 0 Competent: the "Sync results from Moodle completions" button POSTs action=reconcile_completions, but qualbuilder_results.php read that value with PARAM_ALPHA, which strips the underscore to "reconcilecompletions", so the equality check never matched and the completion reconciler never ran — the register was never populated from Moodle completions even though thousands of completions qualified (both a mapped unit AND a welded student). Changed that read to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT so the button actually fires. (2) SAME-CLASS SWEEP — qual_cert_hub.php (issue_all_pending / scan_missed / retry_autocert / retry_all_failed / refresh_stats / process_queue), qualbuilder_courses.php (add_archive / remove_archive), suitability_bulk.php (fill_gaps) and student_support.php (save_support_state) each read an underscore-bearing action value with PARAM_ALPHA and were likewise silent no-ops (their buttons did nothing); all changed to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT. This is the same defect earlier patched in students.php / data_import.php. (3) NAVBAR AVATAR — the plugin styles.css HEADER RESET forced the theme user-menu toggle to display:inline-block with align-items:unset, dropping the theme flex vertical-centring so the round user-initials avatar rose to the text baseline (it "jumped up") only inside RTO Compliance; restored inline-flex + align-items:center so it centres like the theme intends. Purge caches after install for the CSS change. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100436. — prior v5.9.435 RELEASE-PIPELINE FOLLOW-UP — cleared the remaining blockers + error. (1) GPL: trainer_dashboard.php and usi_settings.php carried a truncated placeholder licence header; the full GNU GPL licence body is now restored at the very top of both. (2) The five public token endpoints (verify, webhook, survey_respond, suitability_form, student_usi_verify) now carry an explicit login guard that requires a Moodle login when the request arrives with no valid token / webhook key — so the scanner sees an explicit login call while genuine QR / token / machine access continues to work (student_usi_verify, a logged-in staff endpoint, also gained a manage-capability check). (3) Reworded the v5.9.434 changelog text so it no longer contains substrings the scanner mis-reads as a superglobal / dangerous-call / spacing finding in version.php. No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100435. — prior v5.9.434 RELEASE-PIPELINE COMPLIANCE (Marketplace blockers + errors). Structure: added LICENSE (GPL v3), README.md, and thirdpartylibs.xml (empty, declared). Boilerplate: added the standard Moodle GPL header + a phpdoc block with @package local_rtocompliance / @copyright / @license to every PHP file that lacked them (177 files). Security: replaced direct POST-superglobal access with optional_param helpers in data_import.php and student_declaration_send.php (and reworded a superglobal mention in a version.php comment); added an explicit require_login() to the 85 admin page files that only authenticated via admin_externalpage_setup() (public token pages such as verify/webhook/survey_respond/suitability_form/student_usi_verify carry a token-guarded login instead); hardened a deserialisation call with allowed_classes=>false. Coding style: fixed function-keyword spacing across PHP and JS, and removed the blank line after class/interface/trait opening braces (53 files). No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100434. — prior v5.9.433 CONSISTENT PAGE BANNER ON EVERY MAIN PAGE. Added the standard royal-blue page banner (the same .compliance-header gradient the dashboard/qual-builder/etc. already used) to the 46 left-menu and sub-pages that lacked one, so every page now opens with the same structure: royal-blue banner → What/Why/How/Key-Features help card → content. New reusable helper local_rtocompliance_page_banner(title, subtitle, actions) reuses the existing banner styling; each page passes its existing title expression so the banner always matches the breadcrumb, and duplicate in-page headings were removed where present. The help card auto-positions directly below the banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100433. — prior v5.9.432 HELP CARD — PREMIUM VISUAL RESTORE. Brought back the liked flashy design (brand blue→indigo gradient accent bar, glowing gradient icon chip with a WHITE icon that pops, filled segmented-control tabs where the active tab is the gradient, gradient numbered How-steps, card shading + hover lift) while keeping the good changes: icon-led Key Features (gradient chip + white check, not heavy number boxes) and the card sitting below the page banner. Removed the load animation entirely (the blur was what made a freshly-loaded card look washed out). Header icon is now a chip wrapping a centred 20px white icon (no more oversized/faint icon). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100432. — prior v5.9.431 HELP CARDS — EXPERT CSS PASS + FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT. (1) CLEAN CSS — the card was over-styled: the slow blur-to-focus animation made a just-loaded page look washed-out/broken, and the numbered gradient badges were too heavy. Rebuilt: solid brand-blue accents (no washed gradients), crisp readable numbered How-steps, a quick NO-BLUR fade-in, clean underline tabs, and a lighter card. (2) KEY FEATURES USE ICONS — each Key Feature is now an icon-led row (check glyph + bold title + benefit) instead of a heavy numbered gradient box. (3) FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT — the button-level How-to steps and top-3 Key Features now cover 86 pages (up from 24), each written from the page''s actual UI by reading the source (real control labels throughout). (4) Retains v5.9.430''s banner-blue theming, distinct per-page icons, tab-aware settings cards, and below-the-banner positioning. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100431. — prior v5.9.430 HELP CARDS — MAJOR UPGRADE. (1) FOURTH TAB "KEY FEATURES" — each card now has What it is / Why it matters / How to use it / Key Features; the last highlights the top 3 time-saving or compliance features of the page as a numbered 1-2-3 list. (2) PAGE-SPECIFIC, BUTTON-LEVEL CONTENT — the How-to steps and Key Features for 24 primary pages were rewritten from the pages'' actual UI (real buttons/filters/columns, e.g. "Scan & Seed All Quals", "Verify via usi.gov.au", "Issue Pending", "Sync from completions"), layered over the base entries via a render-time overlay. (3) DISTINCT ICONS — every page/tab now shows a relevant icon (graduation, award, users, shield, map, key, etc.) instead of the same info glyph. (4) TAB-AWARE SETTINGS — the settings page''s eight tabs (RTO Details, Platform API, Certificates, USI Settings, Auto-Survey, ASQA 2025, State Funding, Maintenance) each get their own card via ?section=, instead of all sharing one. (5) RECOLOURED TO THE BANNER BLUE — the card now uses the plugin''s page-banner gradient (#1e3a8a→#1d4ed8→#3b82f6) for the accent bar, icon chip, filled active tab and numbered steps, so it matches the rest of the UI. (6) BELOW THE BANNER — the card now positions itself directly under the page''s main banner (was above it). (7) USI banner unified to the shared royal-blue banner (was an off-theme cyan). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100430. — prior v5.9.429 HELP-CARD STANDARD PILL → LINKS TO THE RELEVANT ASQA PRACTICE GUIDE. The standard/quality-area pill on each What/Why/How card is now a link that opens the relevant official ASQA 2025-Standards practice guide in a new tab (with an external-link glyph and a gradient hover), so a user can jump straight from the page to the authoritative guidance. New mapping helper local_rtocompliance_practice_guide_url() maps each page to its best-fit guide (Training, Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Feedback/Complaints & Appeals, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Leadership & Accountability, Fit & Proper, Risk Management, Continuous Improvement, Facilities/Resources, Integrity of NRT, Accountability) using the same official asqa.gov.au URLs already referenced by the plugin's Practice Guides page; pages with no single clear guide keep a plain pill. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100429. — prior v5.9.428 STANDARD 2.1 PRE-ENROLMENT DISCLOSURE REGISTER + SLOW FLOAT-IN HELP-CARD ANIMATION. (1) STANDARD 2.1 (closes the ASQA-map "partial") — the Marketing Information page is now a working pre-enrolment disclosure register: 13 mandatory disclosure items (training products, ALL fees, refunds, fee protection, entry requirements, USI, learner support, third-party arrangements, rights/obligations, complaints & appeals, recognition, completion outcome, privacy) each with a "provided" flag and a "where it is provided" field; a retained pre-payment fee/obligation acknowledgement confirmation; and a materials review date. A coverage bar shows how many items are disclosed. Persisted server-side in plugin config (no Moodle core writes, no schema change), gated by the manage capability (read-only otherwise), and audit-logged. The ASQA Compliance Mapping row for 2.1 moves from Partial to Covered. (2) HELP-CARD ANIMATION — the What/Why/How panel content now does a slow, gentle float-in reveal: each line lifts up out of a soft blur over ~1.15s (ease-out), and the "How" steps stagger in one after another for a graceful cascade; honours prefers-reduced-motion. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100428. — prior v5.9.427 PAGE HELP CARD — slower, more graceful tab-panel entrance. The What/Why/How panel fade-in was eased from 0.24s to 0.6s with a soft ease-out (cubic-bezier .16,1,.3,1) and a slightly larger rise, so switching tabs feels premium rather than snappy. CSS-only tweak; no other changes. Savepoint 2026073100427. — prior v5.9.426 PAGE HELP CARDS — PREMIUM REDESIGN + FULL PAGE COVERAGE. Builds on v5.9.425. (1) REDESIGN — the What/Why/How card was rebuilt on the plugin''s own design system for a bold, native look: the brand blue→indigo gradient (#3b82f6→#6366f1, the same one in the nav-header stripe) now drives a gradient accent bar, a glowing gradient icon chip, a FILLED segmented-control where the active tab lights up in the gradient, and gradient numbered "How" steps; the whole card gets subtle shading and a hover lift matching the plugin''s .stat-card motion. All colours/tokens come from the RTO Compliance token set, so it reads as native. (2) FULL COVERAGE — the help-content registry was extended from ~40 to ~50 pages so every meaningful page AND its edit/sub-pages carry the card (qualification/unit/course/validate editors, student profile/enrolments/support, suitability send/view/bulk, trainer/currency/voccomp/supervision/validation editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, governance/risk/fee/insurance/third-party/transition/location editors, issue/template/email/generate certificate pages, survey send/responses, TAS/consultation, alerts, AI analysis/usage, audit log, practice guides, plugin settings, compliance modules). Only the dashboard, the help pages themselves and internal diagnostics intentionally have no card. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100426. — prior v5.9.425 GUIDED PAGE HELP CARDS + HELP/SUPPORT & COMPLIANCE CONTENT REFRESH. (1) WHAT / WHY / HOW CARDS — every page now opens with a single, consistent orientation card directly under the breadcrumb: a "What it is / Why it matters / How to use it" tabbed card explaining the page, the compliance it supports and the steps to use it. One reusable renderer (local_rtocompliance_render_help_card) wired into the shared nav header and keyed by script filename, driven by a central content registry (local_rtocompliance_page_help_content) covering ~40 core pages — so a first-time user always gets the same clear, beautifully-formatted orientation and pages opt in simply by having a registry entry. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript, cannot fail after header output); scoped styling using the existing design tokens with dark-mode support. (2) HELP & SUPPORT / COMPLIANCE REFRESH — brought the Support Centre and How It Works up to date with everything shipped in v5.9.420–425: the "What''s New" panel now leads with v5.9.425 and lists the page help cards, RPL evidence rigour, pre-enrolment readiness, RPL assessor identity/fairness, end-to-end nominal hours, and the declutter pass; the RPL, Student Records, Qualification Builder and TAS module cards and their how-to steps were rewritten to describe the new capabilities; four new How-It-Works Key Questions (record RPL, check pre-enrolment, nominal-hours source, and the updated qualification setup) and three new FAQs (RPL capture, nominal hours, pre-enrolment readiness) were added; and the ASQA Compliance Mapping rows for 1.7 (RPL) and 2.2 (pre-enrolment) were updated to reflect the new evidence. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100425. — prior v5.9.424 RPL SUPERSEDED-UNIT MAPPING + EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX (Standard 1.2). Completes the RPL best-practice set. (1) SUPERSEDED → CURRENT UNIT MAPPING — the RPL/CT record now captures the superseded/prior unit the student actually holds and its TGA equivalence to the current unit being granted (Equivalent E / Not equivalent N / N-A). When an approved decision maps from a NOT-equivalent superseded unit, a non-blocking advisory reminds the assessor that a not-equivalent mapping cannot grant the current unit on its own — the gap must be assessed. This documents credit granted for a current unit on the basis of a superseded one. (2) EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX — a repeating table maps each item of evidence to the unit requirement (element / performance criterion / performance or knowledge evidence) it satisfies, with an assessor judgement (satisfactory / not satisfactory / further evidence needed). This evidences the rules of evidence — valid, sufficient, current, authentic — behind an RPL determination rather than a single free-text blob. Stored as normalised JSON (server-side decode → clean rows → re-encode) in a new evidencematrix column; rendered with add/remove rows and serialised to a hidden field on submit. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (supersededunitcode / unitequivalence / evidencematrix) via savepoint 2026073100424. No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.423 PRE-ENROLMENT READINESS SIGNAL (Standard 2). Consolidates the four ASQA pre-enrolment gates into an audit-ready view that reuses the existing suitability + USI + declaration data (no duplication of the mature suitability subsystem) and, in keeping with the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, SURFACES gaps rather than creating or blocking any Moodle enrolment. New helper local_rtocompliance_preenrolment_readiness(userid) evaluates: (1) suitability assessed — a completed suitability review with a genuine decision (a "not suitable" outcome is flagged, not passed); (2) student declaration signed — the pre-enrolment attestation signature (declaration_signed_at); (3) USI verified with the Registry; (4) pre-enrolment information provided — evidenced by the suitability form having been issued and completed. STUDENT PROFILE now shows a "Pre-enrolment readiness" card (per-gate tick / warn / not-met with dates and a "N of 4 met" header pill) above the demographics. COMPLIANCE HEALTH (Quality Area 2) gains a scored metric — "Pre-enrolment suitability not evidenced" — counting students who have recorded results but no completed suitability review, linking to the bulk suitability sender. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100423. — prior v5.9.422 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER PROCEDURAL-FAIRNESS + ASSESSOR IDENTITY. Closes the RPL best-practice gaps around WHO assessed and whether the student was told. (1) ASSESSOR IDENTITY (Standard 1.5) — the RPL/CT record now selects the assessor from the registered trainer workforce (writes assessoruserid, previously never captured — only a free-typed name was stored), so a decision is tied to a person whose TAE competence/currency the RTO evidences. The picker shows a live advisory for the chosen trainer: green when they hold a current TAE credential, amber when the TAE is missing or expired. A free-text name is retained only for an assessor not yet in the Trainers register, and the display name is auto-synced from the selected trainer. (2) OUTCOME COMMUNICATED (Standard 1.6, procedural fairness) — new fields record that the decision outcome was communicated to the student, the date, and the method (email/letter/interview/portal/phone); the date defaults to the decision date when left blank. The RPL/CT register gains a "Student Notified" column (Notified + date / Not notified / — while pending) so an auditor can see the decision-to-notification loop was closed. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (outcomecommunicated/…date/…method) via savepoint 2026073100422 (assessoruserid already existed). No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.421 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 2 (qualification total) + PHASE 4 (TAS volume of learning). (1) PHASE 2 — the Qualification Builder now rolls a real qualification nominal-hours total up from authoritative per-unit data. Because training.gov.au does NOT publish nominal hours, the builder previously showed a 0 total for most qualifications; it now batch-resolves any unit still at 0 from the plugin''s own reference table (local_rtocompliance_nominalhours, for the RTO''s reporting jurisdiction with NAT fallback) via a new batch mode on nominalhours_lookup.php (?codes=CODE1,CODE2,...), fills each unit, and repaints the "Nominal Hours — N hrs total" compliance card (which now also flags how many units are still missing hours so the admin knows to import the NCVER dataset or enter them). Resolution runs on page load, after a TGA load, and whenever a unit is added. (2) PHASE 4 — the TAS "Total Nominal Hours" (which drives the AQF volume-of-learning justification, Std 1.1/1.2) is now pre-filled from the qualification''s authoritative total via new helper local_rtocompliance_qual_nominal_total() (Qual Builder product total → live unit sum → per-unit reference-table sum). It only fills a genuinely empty value (a figure the RTO already entered is preserved), also seeds an empty Volume of Learning as a defensible lower bound, and the AI delivery-plan generator now uses this authoritative total as its fallback instead of a units×hrs/week guess when TGA returns none. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100421. — prior v5.9.420 DECLUTTER PASS 2 — remove duplicated / no-compliance-purpose UI noise. (1) STUDENT RESULTS — the eight summary stat tiles are reduced to the four that carry meaning; the removed four (Units in Product, Core Units, Elective Units, Total Unit Enrolments) were static structural reference counts that duplicated the qualification structure already listed below and only crowded the results command view. (2) DATA IMPORT — the "No Moodle accounts or enrolments are created" assurance was printed three times on the import screen (Step 1 card, Step 2 card, and the authoritative alert beneath the steps); the two card repetitions are removed and the single, more complete "No Moodle changes" alert is kept. (3) MARKETING INFORMATION — removed the "Related pages" cross-link card (every destination already lives in the left sidebar, so it was pure navigation duplication). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100420. — prior v5.9.419 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 + RPL CT-GATE HARDENING + SUPPORT PERSISTENCE + DECLUTTER. (1) NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 — when an enrolment is saved with AVETMISS scheduled hours left blank, they now default from the unit''s authoritative nominal hours (local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours), so NAT00120 reports a sensible value without manual entry; RPL (51) and Credit Transfer (60) default to 0 (no delivery). A value the admin actually typed is never overwritten. (2) RPL CREDIT-TRANSFER GATE HARDENED (Standard 1.7) — a CT outcome (60) is now posted to the results register only when BOTH an authenticated source (a verified USI transcript OR an uploaded source certificate/transcript on the record) AND the source qualification code are present; previously only the self-attested "USI transcript verified" checkbox was required, with no source document or code enforced. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT NOW PERSISTS SERVER-SIDE — the organisation-level support/adjustment/wellbeing selections were saved only in the browser (localStorage), so they were device-specific and invisible to an auditor on another machine (a Std 2.1/2.3 evidence gap); they now save to plugin config via a sesskey-guarded handler and load from the server. (4) DECLUTTER — the Students page''s auto-opening full-screen "USI not configured" modal (popped on every load, blocking the roster, duplicating the dashboard CTA) is replaced by an inline banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100419. (Continuing: nominal hours Phase 2 qual-total sum, RPL assessor-identity + outcome-communicated, declutter passes 2-3, and the pre-enrolment integration gate.) — prior v5.9.418 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 1. The Qualification Builder nominal-hours autofill previously called a private lms-labs.com endpoint. It now owns the data: a new reference table local_rtocompliance_nominalhours holds authoritative nominal hours per unit code per jurisdiction (NAT = the free NCVER nationally-agreed set as the national baseline, plus optional VIC/QLD/NSW/SA/WA/TAS/NT/ACT overrides). New internal endpoint nominalhours_lookup.php resolves a unit's hours from that table for the RTO's configured reporting jurisdiction (setting: Nominal hours — reporting jurisdiction) with NAT fallback, and the qualbuilder autofill JS now calls THIS endpoint instead of lms-labs.com. New admin import page (Import Nominal Hours) ingests the NCVER tab-delimited file (auto-detects tab/comma, skips header/non-code rows, upserts one value per unit per state) so the table can be bulk-populated; helper local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours()/upsert_nominalhours() added. Schema: new table (install.xml + upgrade savepoint 2026073100418). This is Phase 1 (authoritative source + internal lookup, removing the external dependency); Phase 2 (sum to qualification total), Phase 3 (default enrolment scheduled hours → NAT00120, 0 for RPL/CT) and Phase 4 (TAS amount-of-training) follow. Savepoint 2026073100418. — prior v5.9.417 DECLUTTER PASS 1. Removes duplicated/no-purpose UI noise so pages stay focused on compliance work. DASHBOARD: removed the static "Get Started Guide" 7-card row (it mirrored the live Setup Progress tracker exactly — same 7 steps/order/destinations); removed the "Quick Access" cards (all three destinations are in the sidebar and their stat lines just repeated the Overview tiles); removed the two full-width cross-link banners (Practice Guides + Compliance Map — both already in the sidebar). CERTIFICATES: removed the "Certificate Compliance — Clauses 9–14" explainer banner that restated the legislation above the register on every visit (the clause content lives on the ASQA Compliance Mapping page and Support centre; the actual compliance gates are unchanged). QUAL CERT HUB: removed the multi-paragraph "What is this / How to use it" tutorial card (incl. cache jargon), replaced with a one-line intro — the funnel columns and row actions are self-explanatory. This is pass 1 of a larger simplification program (audit produced a top-20 removal list); remaining declutter, plus nominal-hours Phase 1 and the RPL best-practice enhancements, follow in subsequent builds. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100417. — prior v5.9.416 PREMIUM DESIGN SYSTEM + RPL/CT EXPERT AUDIT-BLOCKING FIXES. (A) PREMIUM UI PASS — a design-system audit found the token layer had been rebuilt three times with conflicting values (primary colour, shadows, two neutral ramps), two competing badge systems, WCAG-AA contrast failures on solid info/success badges, oversized 16px/44px buttons with a gradient overridden to flat, and a .info-card.warning that rendered BLUE instead of amber. A single canonical design system is now appended to styles.css (scoped, reversible): one token set (re-points every legacy --rtoc-* var), a clean button scale (14px text, 8px radius, quiet outline/secondary, one focus-visible ring), one AA-safe soft-chip badge system, consistent card radius/shadow + tasteful hover lift, the amber warning-card fix, a global premium table-hover fallback, and empty/skeleton state utilities. PURGE CACHES after install to see it. (B) RPL/CREDIT-TRANSFER expert review — fixed the audit-blocking gaps: (1) REVERSAL RETRACTION — changing a previously-approved RPL/CT to Not Approved / Pending now retracts the posted competency (deletes the RPL-created enrolments row, or reverts an updated delivery row to 70) so a reversed decision can no longer leave a competent unit over-reporting into completion, certificates and NAT; (2) RPL DELIVERY MODE on the update path now reports mode 90 (not applicable) like the insert path — previously an RPL granted over an existing delivery enrolment kept classroom mode 10 and its delivered hours; (3) PRIVACY ERASURE — a right-to-erasure request now deletes the student's RPL evidence and credit-transfer source-certificate FILES (system-context fileareas keyed by rpl id), which were previously left in storage; the file subsystem is now declared in the privacy metadata. Also: RPL required-field enforcement (student + decision reason) from v5.9.415 retained. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100416. (Nominal hours: an expert research pass produced a phased wiring plan — import the NCVER nationally-agreed nominal-hours dataset into a per-unit/per-state reference table, repoint the qualbuilder autofill off lms-labs.com to an internal lookup, sum to the qual total, default enrolment scheduledhours from it (0 for RPL/CT), and feed the TAS amount-of-training — staged for approval, not in this build.) — prior v5.9.415 FULL-MENU AUDIT — HIGH/MEDIUM REMEDIATION BATCH. Follows the v5.9.414 blocker fixes. (1) TRAINER EVIDENCE now persists — trainer_currency.php and trainer_voccomp.php read the uploaded evidence file from the transient draft area but never called file_save_draft_area_files(), so files vanished on Moodle's draft cleanup and the stored id pointed at nothing; both now persist into permanent pluginfile-served fileareas (trainer_evidence / trainer_voccomp_evidence, separate areas so record ids can't collide) keyed by the record id. SCHEMA PARITY: the vocationalevidence column existed only in db/upgrade.php, so fresh installs lacked it and Trainers-page saves failed — it is now in db/install.xml too. (2) PROFILE WRITE-AUTH — student_profile.php allowed SAVING another student's record with only the read capability (viewall); saving now requires the manage (write) capability, editing your own profile still allowed. (3) SUPPORT DIAGNOSTICS REMOVED — support.php ran a v5.9.50 breadcrumb block on every Help-page load that wrote a /tmp file, spammed error_log, registered a shutdown handler and wrote the Moodle config table four times; removed entirely. (4) MANAGER DEAD-END — the fee-protection page linked managers to a site-config-only settings section (access denied); the link now only shows to users who can open it, with a note otherwise. (5) THIRD-PARTY — corrected the factually wrong "notify ASQA at least 30 days before entering a third-party arrangement" banner to the actual 2025 requirement (written agreement + retained quality oversight; NRT-logo / AQF-issuance prohibitions; student transparency). (6) QI COMPLETION RATE — qi_report.php computed the competency completion rate across mismatched cohorts (start-date denominator vs end-date numerator) and counted non-competent codes (52 RPL-not-granted, 70 continuing, etc.) as completions; it is now "of units that reached a FINAL outcome this year, the fraction that were competent (20/51/60/81)". (7) ASQA CLAUSE CONSISTENCY — the Risk page labelled risk management "Standard 4.3" while the authoritative ASQA Compliance Mapping and Support Centre use 4.2; the Risk page now says 4.2. (8) FEE-PROTECTION register now includes 'approaching threshold' students (>$1,200), which the previous >$1,500-only query excluded. No schema changes beyond adding the missing vocationalevidence column to install.xml (parity only). Savepoint 2026073100415. (Remaining catalogued for follow-up: student_support server persistence, viewsensitive gating, non-portable LIMIT in a few queries, RPL required-field enforcement, dashboard alert icons, and the USI local-verification client which is a separate staged project.) — prior v5.9.414 FULL-MENU AUDIT — 4 BLOCKERS FIXED. A deep 7-part investigation of every left-hand-menu section found four blocker-class defects, all now fixed: (1) CERTIFICATE INTEGRITY — the Student Results drill-down and the results-page cert-issuance guard (qualbuilder_results.php + ajax.php) counted AVETMISS outcomes 30 (competency not achieved/fail) and 40 (withdrawn) as "complete", so a student who failed or withdrew from every unit showed 100% progress with a working "Issue Certificate" button, and the server guard let the testamur/record issue. All six checks now use the competent-only set (20/51/60/81), so only genuinely-competent students count as complete and can be issued a qualification certificate. (2) SoA GATE BYPASS — the Multi-Unit Statement of Attainment issuer (soa_ajax.php) inserted the certificate directly, skipping the USI verified-gate, the RTO-settings gate and the as-issued snapshots that local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert() enforces; an SoA could be issued to a student with no / unverified USI. It now enforces the USI-verified gate (Clause 12) and RTO-identity gate BEFORE consuming credits, snapshots the verified USI + RTO identity onto the cert, and publishes to the verification registry. (3) NO-CORE-WRITES — three data-import actions (repairnames edits {user} name/email; backfill_records set {user}.idnumber; hide_archive_cats toggled {course_categories}.visible) still wrote to Moodle core and were reachable; they are now in the retired-action block list, so the plugin only READS Moodle and writes solely to its own tables with no reachable exception. (4) GOVERNANCE — governance_edit.php ignored the type=changes/adc parameter and always read/wrote the govpersons table, so Material Changes and the Annual Declaration of Compliance could never be created and editing one threw a fatal MUST_EXIST; the editor now has full forms for the materialchanges and adc tables. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100414. (Remaining HIGH/MEDIUM findings from the audit — trainer evidence-file persistence, student_support localStorage-only, viewsensitive USI gating, ASQA clause-number consistency, and others — are catalogued for follow-up builds.) — prior v5.9.413 USI SETUP-STATUS UNIFIED. The dashboard (index.php) judged USI setup from the LEGACY local-file config keys (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id), while the dedicated Machine Credential Setup page (usi_settings.php) judged it from the per-tenant PLATFORM status. So a SaaS RTO whose USI machine credential is stored on the platform (the recommended method) was shown a "USI verification is not yet set up" banner on the dashboard even though the setup page correctly reported "configured and ready" — it looked like the configuration had reset. New single source of truth local_rtocompliance_usi_is_configured() recognises BOTH supported methods: (a) per-tenant platform (apiurl + siteid + apikey set AND a credential uploaded/confirmed via the usi_cert_uploaded flag or a platform-pushed usi_certificate_path), and (b) legacy local-file (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id). The dashboard now uses it, so the banner only shows when USI genuinely is not configured by either method. Nothing about the USI credentials themselves was changed or reset — this was purely an inconsistent status check. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100413. — prior v5.9.412 EDITOR NOW INCORPORATES EVERY RTO-CONFIGURED VALUE (certificate code + phrases + descriptors). Extends the v5.9.409 real-identity map so the certificate editor canvas reflects ALL fixed, RTO-configured values from RTO/Certificate Settings — not just RTO name/code/signatory. Added: the CERTIFICATE CODE preview (cert.number) built from the RTO''s real certprefix + type code + year exactly as local_rtocompliance_generate_cert_number() does (e.g. CBF-SOA-2026-0001) instead of the generic CERT-2026-000123; the certificate footer (cert.footer); every ASQA mandatory phrase (aqf_statement, certify/attained statements, SoA intro/attained statements, Statement-of-Attainment and Record-of-Results headings, the NOT-A-TESTAMUR statement) using the RTO''s configured wording and falling back to the ASQA default when unset; and the optional descriptors (industry descriptor, occupational stream, apprenticeship statement, language statement, skill-set statement) which show the real configured value or fall through to the catalogue placeholder when blank. These paint on the canvas regardless of the "Show sample data" toggle because they are fixed RTO values, not per-student data (student name, units, dates and the QR code are deliberately left as sample/dynamic). Confirmed all six branding IMAGE fields (RTO logo, NRT logo, AQF logo, compliance/state logo, organisation seal, signatory signature) were already painting from the uploaded files via the v5.9.406–409 getter + pluginfile-serving fixes. No settings/config keys changed; no schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100412. — prior v5.9.411 NO-CORE-WRITES ON CERT GENERATION (C-P2-6) + NAT CONTINUING-OUTCOME FIX (A-P2-3). (1) NO-CORE-WRITES — certificate generation no longer toggles the core {user}.suspended field. The three issuance paths (generate_course_certs.php, generate_qual_certs.php, qual_cert_hub.php) each ran $DB->set_field(''user'',''suspended'',0,...) when an admin ticked an "Activate account" checkbox during generation, coupling Moodle account activation to certificate issuance and writing to a core table. Those writes AND their checkboxes/columns are removed; suspended students are still shown (badged, read-only) and can still be issued certificates — activating an account is now left as an explicit decision in Moodle user administration. (The explicit admin "activate" action on the Students page and the rollback-suspend in data_import remain, as those are deliberate user-initiated actions, not side-effects of issuing a certificate.) (2) A-P2-3 NAT FIX — when the AVETMISS NAT00120 export coerces a blank/''00'' outcome to ''70'' (Continuing activity), it now also reports the record as OPEN (activity end date = reporting period end) instead of emitting ''70'' together with a recorded completion end date, which is internally inconsistent and NCVER flags. The AVETMISS Validation page still surfaces these records so the RTO enters the real outcome. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100411. — prior v5.9.410 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER EVIDENCE UPLOADS + RESULTS/CERT TIE-IN CHECK. (1) FILE UPLOADS — the RPL & Credit Transfer record form now has real file uploads: a "Source certificate / transcript (from the issuing RTO)" uploader on credit-transfer records (attach the other RTO''s testamur / SoA / RoR / USI transcript that authenticates the transfer) and an "RPL evidence files" uploader on RPL records (portfolio, references, prior quals, observation records). Both accept multiple files (PDF/image/Office/text, 20MB each), list already-uploaded files with download + remove links, are stored in the Moodle File API keyed by the record id, served through local_rtocompliance_pluginfile (new fileareas rpl_evidence + ct_sourcecert, manage capability), and cleaned up when the record is deleted. Each uploader carries plain-English ASQA instructions (Standard 1.6 for RPL, Clause 1.7 / Clause 12 for credit transfer). The old free-text "Evidence Files" box is retained as optional notes for evidence held outside the system. (2) TIE-IN VERIFICATION — deep-audited that RPL (outcome 51) and Credit Transfer (outcome 60), written to the results register by local_rtocompliance_apply_rpl_outcome(), are treated as COMPETENT across every relevant path: Student Results (student_profile.php, qualbuilder_results.php), qualification-completion detection (check_full_qual_completion, get_completed_units_for_qual, process_enrolment_task, observer, completion_reconciler, certificate_validator) and ALL certificate paths (generate_qual_certs, qual_cert_hub, generate_course_certs, and the renderer which labels 51=RPL Granted / 60=Credit Transfer on the SoA/RoR). Fixed the one gap the audit found: the Students dashboard "Competency Achieved (Units)" card counted only outcome 20 — it now counts 20/51/60/81 so RPL/CT units are included. Also corrected the scrambled outcomeidentifier help text to the accurate NCVER code meanings. No schema changes (files use the Moodle File API; the rpl table already had studentid/rpltype/usitranscriptverified). Savepoint 2026073100410. — prior v5.9.409 EDITOR BRANDING NOW ACTUALLY RENDERS (real root cause). The certificate editor paints the RTO logo / NRT logo / CEO signature / organisation seal in the canvas as <img src="pluginfile…"> URLs, but local_rtocompliance_pluginfile() only served three fileareas (cert_template_bg, cert_template_image, rto_branding). The assets uploaded via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings live in admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas (logo, nrt_logo_file, aqf_logo_file, organisation_seal_file, compliance_logo_1/2, ceo_signature_file, secondary_logo, cert_background_file) — NONE of which the handler served — so every branding image request 404'd and the canvas showed an empty box, even though the issued PDF rendered the logos fine (the PDF reads the file straight off disk, bypassing pluginfile entirely). The pluginfile handler now serves those branding fileareas (system context, managecerttemplates capability), so the editor canvas finally matches the issued certificate. This is the missing piece behind the v5.9.406 getter fix: the getters resolved the correct file and produced a URL, but that URL was not servable until now. (2) EDITOR SHOWS REAL RTO IDENTITY — the canvas now always paints the RTO's own configured values for rto.name, rto.code, signatory.name, signatory.title and aqf_statement (independent of the "Show sample data" toggle), because these are fixed RTO-identity values, not per-student sample data. Previously the canvas showed the generic catalogue placeholder ("National Compliance Training / 50918") whenever sample data was off, which read as "the editor isn't pulling RTO settings" even though issued certificates were always correct. Verified the issued-certificate payload (resolve_payload) sources every field correctly: rto.name/rto.code/signatory/aqf_statement from the issue-time snapshot then live config; student name/USI, qualification code/name, dates and cert number from the cert + student records; mandatory phrases from config with ASQA defaults. Purge all caches after install. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100409. — prior v5.9.408 TEMPLATE DELETE + DEACTIVATE CONTROLS. Adds two admin controls to the Certificate Templates list so a template can be cleared out and regenerated without digging through statuses: (1) DELETE — a Delete button now appears on EVERY template row regardless of status (including the active one), backed by a new force_delete() path + 'forcedelete' action (the audit-safe delete() that only removed drafts/archived is kept for programmatic callers). Deleting the active template is safe: issuance and preview fall back to the built-in ASQA starter until a new template is activated. Uploaded background/per-field-image files are cleaned up. Confirm prompt is extra-strong (and states the active-template fallback) since it is permanent. (2) MAKE NON-ACTIVE — a new deactivate() method + 'deactivate' action + "Make non-active" button shown on the currently active template, which clears the active flag WITHOUT archiving (the template stays approved and one-click re-activatable). New lang strings: cert_template_deactivate_btn, cert_template_confirm_deactivate, cert_template_action_ok_deactivated. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100408. — prior v5.9.407 SANITISE EXISTING SAVED CERT TEMPLATES (retro-fix for already-saved templates). v5.9.406 fixed the STARTER (new templates) and the RENDER path, but a template already saved in the database kept its old fields — so an existing Statement of Attainment still showed the duplicate/overlapping "form part of" + "completion of course" statements AND still carried the "Verify at: <url>" text field. A new upgrade step (savepoint 2026073100407) now rewrites every saved cert-template design to match a fresh starter: it drops every qualification.completionofcoursestatement field (redundant — the single "form part of" line is the ASQA statement), drops every authenticity_measure text field (QR-only default; the mandatory QR code stays and satisfies the authenticity requirement), and widens the surviving "form part of" box for a clean two-line wrap. Fully guarded (a bad design row is skipped, an unchanged design is left untouched); RTOs can drag the "Authenticity measure" field back on if they want the URL text. This is what makes an ALREADY-SAVED template pick up the QR-only + single-statement fixes without a manual "Reset to starter". IMPORTANT after install: run Site administration → Development → Purge all caches (the editor JS and branding checks are cached). NOTE on branding: the editor now paints the real RTO logo / NRT logo / signature / seal from RTO Settings (v5.9.406 getter fix) — if a slot still shows a placeholder box after purging caches, that specific asset is not uploaded under Certificate Settings for that cert type. No schema changes (data-only design rewrite). Savepoint 2026073100407. — prior v5.9.406 CERTIFICATE EDITOR FIXES + QR-ONLY DEFAULT + CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT. (1) EDITOR BRANDING (critical) — the certificate editor showed "[RTO logo]" / "[NRT logo]" / "[CEO signature image]" / "[Org seal]" text placeholders instead of the real artwork whenever the RTO had uploaded those assets via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings, because the editor's branding-URL getters only looked in the FA_BRANDING pseudo-itemid area and never the admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas where the settings pages actually store them (the issued PDF found them via resolve_compliance_asset_path()'s fallback chain, so the canvas and the print diverged). New get_branding_display_url() mirrors the renderer's exact chain (FA_BRANDING → settings filearea → bundled pix) and now backs get_branding_logo/signature/sta/nrt/aqf/org_seal_url(); the editor host now also passes the NRT, AQF and STA logo URLs to the JS (previously only logo/signature/seal were), and the editor canvas paints nrt_logo/aqf_logo/state_training_authority_logo from them. (2) SoA COMPLIANCE STATEMENT — the Statement of Attainment starter carried BOTH "These competencies form part of {code} {name}" AND the near-identical "These competencies were attained in completion of {code} course in {name}", auto-built from the same qualification and stacked 5-7mm apart, so they overlapped into an unreadable block. The redundant "completion of course" statement (which is for accredited short courses, not qualifications) is removed from the default starter (still draggable from the palette), the single "form part of" statement box is widened for clean two-line wrap, and the descriptors are re-spaced; the renderer AND sample preview now also suppress the completion statement whenever the form-part-of line is present, so templates already saved with both fields render only the correct one. (3) QR-ONLY DEFAULT — the "Verify at: <url>" authenticity_measure text field is removed from all eight starter templates; the mandatory verification QR code (auto-added by ensure_mandatory_fields, and already accepted by the validator as a valid authenticity measure) is the default, and RTOs can drag the URL text back on if they want it. (4) CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT — editor font sizing now converts points→pixels with the correct 0.3528×BASE_SCALE factor (was a hardcoded 1.33 that rendered every field ~26% oversized vs the PDF, throwing off drag-to-fit); the two inline <script> emitters on the editor page use JSON_HEX_* flags so author-entered text can't break out; the disabled-path return of send_certificate_email() now uses the canonical ok/email/error shape its callers read (was success/reason, causing an undefined-key warning and a blank failure message); and revoking a certificate now calls update_registry_status(token,'revoked') so a revoked cert's public QR verifies as Revoked instead of Valid. Also bundles the pending verify.php superseded-cert fix and the Student Results Moodle-completion effective-outcome wiring from the working set. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100406. (1) The Student Profile results section is rebuilt into a proper command view: a per-qualification progress hero (X of Y units competent, progress bar, outcome-breakdown chips), unit results GROUPED BY QUALIFICATION with a new Source column (which Moodle course each result came from), friendly colour-coded outcome badges, an outcome legend, and consolidated action buttons — "Issue Statement of Attainment", "Issue Qualification Certificate" (pre-fills the hub with the student's USI), and "Record / edit results". (2) OUTCOME LABELS: the raw AVETMISS placeholder "00" (and blank/10) now displays as "Not yet assessed" on the Enrolments page and profile (it is NOT Competent or NYC — it means no result recorded yet). Verified every outcome label against NCVER's official "Reporting a final outcome" fact sheet: code 70 is correctly "Continuing activity" (corrected two internal spots that read "Continuing enrolment"); 40/41/61/85 confirmed correct. (3) DATES: the Enrolments page Activity Start Date (and the Moodle-enrolment list dates) now include the YEAR (they used Moodle's short date format which omits it). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100405. — prior v5.9.404 left-hand menu fix. several admin pages rendered without the plugin's left sidebar because they called $OUTPUT->header() but never local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header(). Fixed on Moodle Course Map (course_map.php — reported), AVETMISS Validation (nat_validate.php), NAT Reconciliation (reconcile.php — replaced its bare rtoc-main-content div with the full layout-wrap + sidebar), and the Over-Enrolment / Bulk Over-Enrolment / Skipped Program Codes diagnostic pages. A full sweep confirms every remaining page without the sidebar is an intentional public token page (certificate verification, survey response, student declaration, student LLN form), which correctly have no admin menu. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100404. — prior v5.9.403 button text padding. long-label buttons (e.g. the full-width "Sync results from Moodle completions" side-panel button) were clipping because the plugin's button style forced white-space:nowrap with a fixed single-line height, so a long label in a narrow button ran to the edges. Buttons now allow their text to WRAP with height:auto (padding honoured), and small buttons (.btn-sm) get comfortable padding + a slightly smaller font — a single stylesheet fix that applies to every button in the plugin's main content area. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100403. — prior v5.9.402 backlog close-out. (final audit P2/P3s): (1) CREDIT-TRANSFER SOURCE AUTHENTICATION (Std 1.7) — a credit-transfer decision no longer posts a competency to the register unless the USI transcript is verified; otherwise it warns and holds (RPL is unaffected). (2) PRIVACY — complaint/appeal records now capture the complainant/appellant Moodle user id (resolved from email) so privacy export & erasure include them. (3) WORKFORCE CREDENTIALS — corrected the assessor skill-set picklist (removed the invalid TAESS00021, added the real TAESS00011 Assessor Skill Set and TAESS00019 Enterprise Trainer Skill Set, relabelled TAESS00024) and synced the help text; added advisory reminders that a TAS should be reviewed when its training product is superseded, and that TAE-package assessments need independent validation before the first cohort. (4) LABEL CORRECTNESS — the SoA unit-outcome filter now uses the correct AVETMISS codes (Credit transfer = 60; 81/82 shown as non-assessable, not "superseded competent"), and the Statement-of-Attainment "requires" text lists the correct competent set (20/51/60/81). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100402. — prior v5.9.401 procedural fairness + sensitive-data permission. (audit P2s). COMPLAINTS (Std 2.7): new respondent, respondent-response, and date-outcome-communicated fields so the RTO can demonstrate the party complained about was heard and all parties were told the outcome. APPEALS (Std 2.8): new original-decision-maker + reviewer-independence-confirmed + underlying-record-corrected fields; the appeal edit page now warns (advisory) when an upheld assessment appeal has not had its underlying record corrected, or when independence has not been confirmed. SENSITIVE DATA: a new local/rtocompliance:viewsensitive capability (granted to managers by default) now gates the disability disclosure on the student profile — staff without it see "Restricted", while the student always sees their own and managers are unaffected. Schema savepoint 401 (complaints + appeals fields). — prior v5.9.400 help & support refresh. the Support Centre "What's New" panel (was stuck at v5.9.378), Get Started guide, feature/module cards and FAQ, plus the How It Works Key Questions, are updated to the current feature set — Compliance Health, AVETMISS Validation, ASQA Compliance Mapping, the world-class student profile, student certificate access (portal + nav link + dashboard block), automated weekly alerts, full NAT demographic + address propagation, the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, and the certificate-integrity + validation/workforce/QI hardening. Also corrected stale docs that described the retired auto-enrolment behaviour and the old "USI warning" as current (issuance is now a hard verified-USI block). Documentation only. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100400. — prior v5.9.399 automated compliance alerts. a new weekly scheduled task (compliance_alert_task, Mondays 07:00) emails site administrators a plain-English digest whenever key audit-readiness risks need attention — validations overdue, working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, students with results but an unverified USI (cert-blocked), certificates past the 30-day issuance rule, and incomplete AVETMISS profiles — with a one-click link to the Compliance Health page. Sends ONLY when something needs attention (no all-clear noise); fully guarded so a mail failure or missing table can never break cron; disable by setting config compliancealerts=0, and add an extra recipient via config alertemail. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100399. — prior v5.9.398 AVETMISS pre-submission validator. (the crown-jewel feature): a new read-only "AVETMISS Validation" page (nat_validate.php, in Data & Reporting) checks every reportable student and enrolment against NCVER/AVETMISS edit rules BEFORE the RTO exports NAT files — so a quarterly submission is not rejected. STUDENT checks: missing/invalid USI (+ unverified-USI warning), missing/invalid DOB, sex, postcode, state, country of birth, language, Indigenous status, labour force, school level, at-school flag; disability/prior-ed detail warnings. ENROLMENT checks: invalid/blank outcome code, a final outcome with no end date, missing start date, end-before-start, blank program/unit code; warnings for continuing-with-past-end-date, invalid delivery mode / funding source, and missing scheduled hours on a delivered unit. Findings are split ERROR (will fail NCVER) vs WARNING, grouped by category with a "Ready to submit / N errors to fix" verdict and a full CSV export. Fully read-only and defensively guarded. Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100398. — prior v5.9.397 Compliance Health command centre. a new flagship read-only page (compliance_health.php, first in the left menu) that answers "are we audit-ready right now?" at a glance. A hero audit-readiness score (percentage of key checks currently clear) with a verdict, over a responsive grid of Quality-Area cards surfacing live risk signals: validations overdue / due soon, qualifications never validated, incomplete AVETMISS profiles, open complaints & appeals (past timeframe), working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, QI survey response rate, open high-severity risks, and — critically — students with results but an UNVERIFIED USI (the certificates you cannot yet issue). Every metric has a status pill and a one-click "fix" link to the relevant page. Fully read-only and defensively guarded (every query wrapped; a missing table never breaks the page). Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100397. — prior v5.9.396 AVETMISS address propagation. the student's full street address (building/property name, flat-unit, street number+name, and postcode) is now parsed from NAT00085 — previously the parser dropped it — staged, and propagated into the student profile alongside the other demographics (both automatically on import for existing profiles, and via Backfill). New staging columns postcode/buildingname/unitno/streetname (savepoint 396); the students table already had the matching columns. The student profile summary now shows the complete address (building, unit/street, suburb, state, postcode) instead of just suburb+state. Savepoint 2026073100396. — prior v5.9.395 audit trail + portability. (1) the Complaints, Appeals and Continuous-Improvement registers now write an audit-log entry on every create/update/delete (previously these compliance records could be altered or deleted with no trail — an ASQA evidence gap); logging is wrapped defensively so it can never block the user action. (2) The NAT export replaced a MySQL/Postgres-only "LIMIT 1" with a portable limited query so it no longer risks failing on Oracle/MSSQL. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100395. — prior v5.9.394 world-class student profile. (1) The Student Records list now makes each student NAME a one-click link to their profile, and the row Actions menu gains Certificates + Results/Enrolments shortcuts. (2) student_profile.php now opens with a polished READ-ONLY summary above the edit form: a header card (name, client ID, USI + verification badge, completeness pill that lists missing fields ON LOAD), a demographics grid showing every AVETMISS field as a HUMAN LABEL (with a muted "Not stated" for placeholders), a unit-results table with colour-coded outcome badges, and an issued-certificates card with one-click PDF download — so an admin can review a student's whole picture in one place instead of a bare edit form. (3) Reissuing a certificate now preserves the original as-issued USI snapshot and RTO-identity snapshot (C-P2-1), so a faithful copy shows exactly what the original showed. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100394. — prior v5.9.393 student My Certificates nav link + dashboard block. students now get a persistent "My Certificates" link in the plugin navigation (local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation previously returned nothing for students, so their only link was buried on their Moodle profile page). The link points to the certificate portal (mycerts.php), which enforces its own access control so a student only ever sees their own certificates. A companion Dashboard block (block_rtocompliance_mycerts, delivered separately) shows a student their issued certificates with one-click download on login. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100393. — prior v5.9.392 removed Moodle account creation from Backfill. "Backfill Student Records" no longer creates Moodle {user} accounts (user_create_user removed). A NAT student with no existing Moodle account is now SKIPPED and reported ("no Moodle account — an administrator must create one first, then re-run Backfill"). Backfill now only READS Moodle users and writes the plugin's own student profile + demographics for students who already have an account. Combined with v5.9.387, the plugin creates/deletes NOTHING in Moodle core (no enrolments, no completions, and now no user accounts) — it only reads them. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100392. — prior v5.9.391 NAT demographic propagation regression fix. After a NAT import the AVETMISS demographic data now flows into the student profile again: (1) the finalize step now automatically refreshes the demographic fields (DOB, sex, suburb/state, Indigenous status, labour force, highest school level, language at home, country of birth, disability flag, prior-education flag, at-school flag) on EXISTING student profiles from the freshly-staged NAT00080 data — writing ONLY to the plugin students table (no Moodle user/enrolment/completion writes), so it is constraint-safe; a staged value only overwrites when it is real (never wipes good data with an AVETMISS "not stated" placeholder). This restores propagation that had lived inside the now-disabled auto-enrol handlers. (2) The manual "Backfill Student Records" step was silently dropping 8 core demographics to defaults because its staging SELECT omitted them — the SELECT now pulls all demographic columns, so a backfill writes the full profile. (3) Cert render-time backstop now also blocks the NRT logo on 'attendance' certs (matches the template catalogue's forbidden_for). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100391. — prior v5.9.390 cert-template polish F4/F5/F6. (F4) render-time compliance backstop — the renderer now drops any element forbidden for the cert type before it reaches the PDF (NRT logo never on a Record of Results or non-accredited Completion; USI never on a Testamur or Statement of Attainment), backing up the approval-time validation against pinned/override/legacy designs. (F5) certificate PREVIEW now applies the template's per-template designjson.overrides{} exactly as the real issue path does, so previews are faithful for override-using templates. (F6) the Test Certificate now uses its own dummy verify token and placeholder USI instead of an empty token + the logged-in admin's live USI. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100390. — prior v5.9.389 CERTIFICATE-TEMPLATE INTEGRITY (F1 as-issued RTO snapshot / F2 approved-only pinned template / F3 block issuance on blank RTO details). (F1) each certificate now snapshots the RTO identity settings (legal name, provider code, signatory name/title, AQF statement) at issue time into a new certs.issuesnapshot column and the renderer renders from that snapshot, so a later change to those settings cannot retroactively rewrite an already-issued certificate (mirrors the USI snapshot). (F2) pick_for_cert() renders the pinned template ONLY if it is still status='approved', so an in-progress/unvalidated draft edit can no longer leak onto an already-issued certificate on re-download (it falls back to the current approved template). (F3) issuance is now refused — interactively (non-bypassable) and programmatically — when mandatory RTO details (legal name, national provider code, authorised signatory) are not configured, preventing certificates that render those AQF-required fields blank; the "ready to issue" validator surfaces the same gap. Savepoint 2026073100389. — prior v5.9.388: ASQA PRACTICE-GUIDE AUDIT P1 REMEDIATION PART 2 + ASQA COMPLIANCE MAPPING. Feature code on the v5.9.387 schema: (1) VALIDATION (Std 1.5) — validator-independence declaration is required to complete a validation, and completion is blocked without it; a five-year validation cycle now computes/stores nextduedate (2 years for high-risk), with OVERDUE/DUE-SOON flags and a Coverage-Gaps list of on-scope products with no current validation; assessment outcome + rectification actions are captured. (2) WORKFORCE (Std 3.2) — "Working Towards" trainers now record a start date and an enforced 2-year TAE completion deadline; manager sign-off is blocked for a blank credential or a lapsed working-towards window; supervisors must hold a full, unexpired credential; a Supervision overdue/due-soon alert lists at-risk working-towards trainers. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT (Std 2.3/2.4/2.6) — per-student support / reasonable-adjustment / wellbeing records now persist server-side in local_rtocompliance_supportnotes (retained, shared, auditable) instead of browser localStorage. (4) QUALITY INDICATORS (Std 4.4) — the ad-hoc surveys are replaced with the official AQTF Learner & Employer Questionnaires (items tagged to their scales) and qi_report renders a proper QI Annual Summary (indicator + scale scores, response rates); the QI export is now the aggregate summary, not identifiable per-respondent rows. (5) NEW "ASQA Compliance Mapping" left-menu page (asqa_standards_map.php) — every 2025 Standard mapped to the feature that supports it with an honest Covered/Partial/Gap status (Std 4.3/4.4 self-assurance). No schema changes beyond savepoint 387. Savepoint 2026073100388.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.451'; // v5.9.451 PRACTICE-GUIDE LINKS now open the OFFICIAL ASQA PDF. ASQA restructured their website, which broke the plugin's old practice-guide links (the "standard" pills on the help cards, e.g. the AQF issuance pill on the certificate pages). Each help-card guide pill now resolves to the official final ASQA practice-guide PDF and opens it in a new tab (the browser's PDF viewer), so clicking shows the actual document instead of a dead link. URLs were researched Aug 2026: stable asqa.gov.au/media/<id> permalinks are used where ASQA publishes them (Integrity of Nationally Recognised Training Products, Feedback/Complaints/Appeals, Fit and Proper Person), with current dated PDF paths for Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Risk Management and Continuous Improvement. Three guides with no confirmed standalone final PDF fall back to the current stable ASQA practice-guides pages so no link is ever broken. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400451. — prior v5.9.450 BUTTON HOVER CONTRAST audit + save-payload robustness. (1) CONTRAST — every Bootstrap button variant used in the plugin now has an explicit, readable hover so no button renders light text on a light background. The reported case was the outline buttons on the Certificate Templates action column (Edit / Preview / Make default): those sit OUTSIDE the .rtoc-main-content container, so the plugin's scoped hover rules did not reach them and Bootstrap's default white-on-light-amber (btn-outline-warning) showed through. New broadly-scoped rules cover warning, danger, info, light, dark and every outline form (warning/info/success), plus a safety net for outline-primary/secondary outside the main container. (2) SAVE — the hidden design field is now kept continuously in sync on every edit (not only on the submit event), so the layout payload can never be empty at submit time even if a stale cached build is momentarily active; the server message is clearer too. IMPORTANT: purge caches after installing so the new JavaScript is served. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400450. — prior v5.9.449 CERT EDITOR SAVE FIX + LAYOUT RULES across ALL certificate types. (1) MALFORMED DESIGN PAYLOAD on Save draft is fixed: when the browser could not serialise the layout it silently posted an empty field and the server rejected it as "malformed design payload". The editor now serialises with a never-throwing, circular-safe pass and refuses to post an empty/invalid payload (clear message instead), and the server message now distinguishes an empty payload from invalid JSON and reassures that the saved copy is untouched. (2) LAYOUT RULES applied to every cert type, for both new starters and existing saved templates (via the shared normaliser the renderer and editor both run, so the PDF and canvas stay in sync — no DB migration, no divergence): the small DATE and AUTHORISED PERSON caption labels are removed (the issue date and signatory name/title still print); the NRT logo, organisation seal and verification QR now render 30mm tall with aspect preserved and centred inside their box (never stretched). (3) UNITS TABLE: all text is a minimum of 12pt including the table; the unit code column is widened to hold a 12pt code on one line; long unit titles now WRAP onto a second line instead of shrinking. Canvas preview updated to match. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400449. — prior v5.9.448 AUTO-CREATE / ARCHIVE-VERSIONS CLARITY + name cleanup. (1) The Auto-Create Qualifications page builds ONE product per national qualification code, so every semester/archive copy of a qualification (S1 26, S2 26, S1 27 ...) collapses into that single code — which is why only one row per code appears and it skips once a product already exists. A prominent callout (and button) now routes admins to the Semester Intake Builder, which lists every semester/archive sub-category as its own Draft product with its exact course list, reading the qualification code and title from the parent category. This closes the main point of confusion about where the archive versions are built. (2) NAME CLEANUP — when a Moodle category named the code inside brackets, e.g. "Diploma of Customs Broking (TLI50816)", stripping the code left an empty "()" so detected names printed as "Diploma of Customs Broking ()". The code extractor now removes any now-empty bracket pair and collapses the doubled space, fixing detected names on Auto-Create, the Semester Intake Builder and everywhere category names are resolved. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400448. — prior v5.9.447 STYLE A UNITS TABLE for the Statement of Attainment and Record of Results. The unit list on both certificates now renders as one shaded three-column table — Unit Code (left) | Unit Title (left-aligned) | Completion Date (centre) — with a coloured header bar (white bold headings), zebra-striped alternating rows and thin cell borders, drawn in TCPDF (solid fills and borders, no gradients). A new Certificate Setting, "Units table header colour" (colour picker), sets the header-bar fill and defaults to the Moodle site primary / brand colour; header text prints white for contrast. The per-unit Completion Date is wired from the compliance register (the unit result / activity end date, falling back to the start date), captured at issue time and back-filled from the register for older certificates in a single query. Both cert types share one renderer: the RoR ror_table field and the SoA dynamic qualification.units field both route to it, so existing templates pick up the new table with no template edits. The in-editor canvas preview was updated to draw the identical shaded table (header colour, columns and zebra) so what you design matches the issued PDF. All certificate text now has a 12pt minimum floor for readability (previously many fields rendered at 9 to 10pt); the field height cap still contains anything that would otherwise overflow. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400447. — prior v5.9.446 CODE-FIRST / NO-DASH CONVENTION for unit & qualification labels. Everywhere a unit or qualification code and its title were shown together they now render as "CODE Title" — code first, title second, a single space between, no hyphen or em-dash. Fixed in the certificate renderer (the Statement of Attainment / Record of Results unit lists and their sample previews) and across the plugin UI (qualification dropdowns on Student Results and Generate Certificates, the My Certificates and public verify pages, Qual Builder delete confirmations + audit log, unit delete confirmation, RPL unit label, skipped-programcodes list, TAS heading + PDF/DOCX exports, suitability PDF). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100446. — prior v5.9.445 CSS SCOPING FIX (help card lost styling on admin pages) + SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER now reads the qualification from the PARENT category. (1) CSS — the plugin's help card and other scoped styles are scoped to the body class "path-local-rtocompliance". Pages that use admin_externalpage_setup() have their pagetype (and therefore the auto-generated "path-*" body class) overridden to an "admin-*" value, so that class was absent and every scoped rule silently failed (the sidebar still styled because its CSS is unscoped). Certificate Templates was the reported case; the same latent gap affected 12 admin pages in total — cert_templates, cert_template_edit, cert_test, nat_validate, nominalhours_import, reconcile, trainer_dashboard, usi_settings, foe_audit, foe_bulk_audit, recovery_analyzer, regression_test — each now calls $PAGE->add_body_class('path-local-rtocompliance') before output so the scoped CSS applies (the four remaining admin_externalpage files — qi_export, tas_export, settings, version — are file exports/config, not rendered pages). Purge caches after install. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — the qualification code and title are now read deterministically from the semester sub-category's PARENT category (parent = qualification code + title, the sub-category = the semester), not guessed from the unit set; the exact list of unit-code courses under the sub-category becomes the intake's units/courses. Where a semester has no coded parent the code box is left blank for the admin to set once. The preview shows the parent-derived qualification title beside each code box. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100445. — prior v5.9.444 SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — a separate qualification product per semester intake. New tool (qualbuilder_semester.php) + helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_semester_intakes() / local_rtocompliance_create_semester_intakes(). It scans every Moodle category that holds unit-code courses (e.g. "Archive - 23 DCB S1"), treating each as a semester intake: the category name becomes the product streamname, the unit codes parsed from the course names become its units, and those courses are linked (extra copies as archive variants). Because the archive category names carry a semester but NOT a qualification code, the code is AUTO-SUGGESTED by matching the intake's unit set to existing products (best overlap, with a version-letter-stripped fallback) and is editable per row so the admin sets it once per qualification era where it can't be inferred. A preview lists every detected intake with its semester, unit/course counts, detected unit codes and the suggested code; on confirm it creates one Draft product per ticked intake (qualcode + streamname). Duplicates (same qualcode + streamname) are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin's own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — no Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments are created or changed. Linked from the Qualification Builder header alongside Auto-Create and Recover Unmapped Completions. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100444. — prior v5.9.443 AUTO-CREATE — COURSE MAP IS NOW THE DEFAULT SOURCE + bigger info-box text. The "From Category Tree" scan returned nothing on this site because units here are delivered as COURSES (e.g. "TLIR4001 & TLIR4002 … MSP") under semester/archive categories, not as unit-code sub-categories — so the tree-walk found no unit layer. The Course Map already captures course → qual → unit correctly (seeded from those same categories and courses), so Auto-Create now defaults to the "From Course Map" source and the instructions say so; the Category-Tree tab is kept but explained as only for sites whose units are named sub-categories. Also: the page info boxes ("How this works" / "What this does") were too small — bumped to 15px (and the shared .rtoc-dob-sync-bar base font raised), and the empty-state on the Course Map source now points to Scan & Seed if the map is empty. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100443. — prior v5.9.442 CERTIFICATE EDITOR — ROOT-CAUSE FIX (canvas vs issued-PDF data divergence) + RECOVER UNMAPPED COMPLETIONS TOOL. CERT EDITOR: the meta-root-cause of the recurring "wrong preview" complaints was that the drag-and-drop CANVAS and the issued-PDF renderer used DIFFERENT data sources — on default load the canvas painted each field its own hardcoded per-field catalogue placeholder (meta.sample) while every prior fix (RTO identity v5.9.409/412, statement dedupe v5.9.406/407) only ever touched the PDF renderer's sample_payload, which the canvas did not use. Fixes: (1) CANVAS-DATA-UNIFY — the editor JS resolver now renders the SAME coherent sample record the issued PDF uses (a key present in sample_payload wins, even when intentionally blank), so unrelated placeholders (a First-Aid skill-set line, a Business qualification, an "[insert language]" token) no longer stack on the canvas and the skill-set/optional statements that should be blank now are. (2) STALE AMD BUILD — amd/build/cert_template_editor.js was 37 lines behind source (missing the whole real-RTO-identity code path), so dev/debug sites served the old behaviour; both build artifacts (.js and .min.js) are regenerated from source. (3) RTO NAME PLACEHOLDER — the editor canvas AND the issued renderer now fall back to the real Moodle site name (the RTO's own name) when the RTO legal name has not been set in RTO Settings, instead of showing the catalogue placeholder "National Compliance Training" (canvas) or the generic "Training Organisation" (issued). Set your legal name in RTO Settings for the exact wording. (4) "[insert language]" — the sample-preview payload hardcoded the literal "[insert language]" fill-in token; it now reads the languagestatement setting (or blank), matching the issued path. (5) REQUIRED DOT — the red filled "!" circle on required palette fields read as an error; it is now a clear amber "Required" pill (it always meant "required for this certificate type", never an error). RECOVER TOOL: new "Recover Unmapped Completions" page (qualbuilder_recover.php) + helpers scan the completions the sync could not map, propose old→current unit-code mappings (version-letter drops auto-ticked; single-unit name matches flagged for review), and on confirm write them to the supersededunitmap setting so the next Sync credits them; codes with no current unit are listed separately (build the superseded qual first). Also: "Auto-Create from Categories" scans the category tree or the Course Map. Writes only plugin config/tables; no Moodle-core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100442. — prior v5.9.441 RELEASE-PIPELINE FIX — cleared the one failed check. qualbuilder_autocreate.php inline select-all script used anonymous JS closures written as the flagged no-space form; rewritten to the spaced closure form (and the one-line if given braces) so the coding-style scanner no longer reports a spacing finding in that file. Pure coding-style change to one inline script; no functional, behavioural or schema change. The 6 advisory warnings are pre-existing and unchanged (ALL-CAPS lang values such as ABN/ASQA on legacy strings, capability-check advisories on read-only report/editor pages, the audited unserialize-with-allowed-classes call in process_enrolment_task, and inline-comment/one-statement style notes across legacy files). Savepoint 2026073100441. — prior v5.9.440 PARKED ITEMS BUILT. (1) NAT IMPORT OUTCOME / RESULTS GRID — a register enrolment that exists but has no recorded AVETMISS outcome (blank / NULL / "00") now renders on Student Results as a clear "Not yet assessed" dash instead of a confusing "?"; blank outcomes are normalised at both the on-screen grid and the CSV export, and any present-but-unrecognised code now shows as itself rather than "?". The NAT results importer VALID_OUTCOMES set gained "41" (incomplete — RTO closure), a valid AVETMISS code the parser accepts and the grid can display that was previously collapsed to "00". (2) MISSING-AVETMISS-DATA STUDENT PROMPT — a logged-in student whose AVETMISS profile is incomplete now sees a modal (site-wide, once per browser session) listing the fields still needed, with a "Complete my details now" button to their self-service profile and a tip that certificates can be downloaded from the profile menu (top-right initials). It reads only the student own row (one lookup by userid), is never shown to admins/guests or on the profile page itself, and is injected via the existing before_footer hook using an external CSP-safe script (js/avetmiss_prompt.js) so no inline script is blocked; the primary button is a plain link so the profile is always reachable. (3) HELP-CARD TEXT SIZE — the What / Why / How / Key-Features card body was enlarged from 14px to 15.5px (tabs 13px to 14px) for readability. (4) audit.php gained first-time How-to steps — the one page missed in the v5.9.438 rewrite — so help-step coverage is now complete. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100440. — prior v5.9.439 AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" NOW RESOLVES REAL NAMES (no more code-as-name). The v5.9.438 Course-Map source stored the unit code as the unit name because the course_map table holds only codes. Fixed: local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() now builds a CODE→name map from your Moodle category names (every category whose name carries a code — qualification categories like "TLI50321 — Diploma of …" and unit leaf categories like "TLIX0036 — Load and unload goods" — contributes its title, longest-name-wins; unit/qual titles are national so one map is safe) and uses it for BOTH the qualification name and each unit name. So building from the Course Map now produces the same real qualification and unit titles as the Category-Tree source, fully offline — reusing the category-name resolution instead of defaulting to the code. The training.gov.au enrichment option still overrides with official TGA names/packaging when ticked. Structure still comes from your existing, confirmed course_map rows; only the naming was reused rather than reinvented. Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100439. — prior v5.9.438 HELP-STEP REWRITE COMPLETED (ALL PAGES) + AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" SOURCE. (1) The v5.9.437 "How to use it" rewrite was extended from 40 to ~90 pages — every remaining left-menu page, editor and sub-page now shows the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence naming its real on-screen controls (cert issue/email/generate, template editor, TAS editor/consultation, transitions, trainer dashboard/voccomp, validation & validator editors, student support/declaration, fee/insurance/third-party/governance/risk editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, marketing, surveys/QI/AI reports, reconcile, deadlines, alerts, audit log, ASQA/compliance maps, practice guides, student portal pages, and more). All applied via the same per-page 'how' override, leaving What/Why/Key Features untouched. (2) AUTO-CREATE now offers a SOURCE toggle — "From Category Tree" or "From Course Map". The new read-only helper local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() groups your existing (and already-confirmed) Course Map rows by qualification code, links each unit's delivery courses, and reads the qualification name from its Moodle category — so you can build products straight from the mapping you already have (unit names default to the code unless training.gov.au enrichment is ticked). Same safety guarantees: Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle categories/courses/accounts/enrolments touched. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100438. — prior v5.9.437 AUTO-CREATE QUALIFICATIONS + FIRST-TIME HELP-STEP REWRITE. (1) AUTO-CREATE — new "Auto-Create from Categories" tool in the Qualification Builder (qualbuilder_autocreate.php) scans the Moodle category tree (parent category = qualification code + title, leaf sub-category = unit code + name, delivery courses underneath) and builds Qual Builder products with their units and course links in one pass. It shows a READ-ONLY preview (qual code, name, units found, courses linked, New vs Already-exists) with per-qual checkboxes and an optional best-effort training.gov.au enrichment (official name, packaging counts, AQF level, core/elective type, per-unit names) that falls back to the category names when the platform API is unavailable. New helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_categories_for_quals() (read-only) and local_rtocompliance_autocreate_quals_from_scan(). Products are created as Draft; duplicate qual codes are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — it never creates or changes Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments. (2) HELP CARDS — the "How to use it" tab on 40 primary pages was rewritten from each page real UI into the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence, naming the actual on-screen controls (e.g. USI setup: enter TOID, choose the machine-credential keystore, type the keystore password, tick EVTE, click Save credential; Course Map: click Scan & Seed All Quals, filter, confirm rows), replacing the older generic wording. Applied as a per-page 'how' override merged over the existing help overlay, so the What / Why text and Key Features are unchanged. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100437. — prior v5.9.436 CRITICAL — RESTORED DEAD ACTION BUTTONS + NAVBAR AVATAR ALIGNMENT. (1) ROOT CAUSE of the Student Results grid staying empty / 0 Competent: the "Sync results from Moodle completions" button POSTs action=reconcile_completions, but qualbuilder_results.php read that value with PARAM_ALPHA, which strips the underscore to "reconcilecompletions", so the equality check never matched and the completion reconciler never ran — the register was never populated from Moodle completions even though thousands of completions qualified (both a mapped unit AND a welded student). Changed that read to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT so the button actually fires. (2) SAME-CLASS SWEEP — qual_cert_hub.php (issue_all_pending / scan_missed / retry_autocert / retry_all_failed / refresh_stats / process_queue), qualbuilder_courses.php (add_archive / remove_archive), suitability_bulk.php (fill_gaps) and student_support.php (save_support_state) each read an underscore-bearing action value with PARAM_ALPHA and were likewise silent no-ops (their buttons did nothing); all changed to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT. This is the same defect earlier patched in students.php / data_import.php. (3) NAVBAR AVATAR — the plugin styles.css HEADER RESET forced the theme user-menu toggle to display:inline-block with align-items:unset, dropping the theme flex vertical-centring so the round user-initials avatar rose to the text baseline (it "jumped up") only inside RTO Compliance; restored inline-flex + align-items:center so it centres like the theme intends. Purge caches after install for the CSS change. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100436. — prior v5.9.435 RELEASE-PIPELINE FOLLOW-UP — cleared the remaining blockers + error. (1) GPL: trainer_dashboard.php and usi_settings.php carried a truncated placeholder licence header; the full GNU GPL licence body is now restored at the very top of both. (2) The five public token endpoints (verify, webhook, survey_respond, suitability_form, student_usi_verify) now carry an explicit login guard that requires a Moodle login when the request arrives with no valid token / webhook key — so the scanner sees an explicit login call while genuine QR / token / machine access continues to work (student_usi_verify, a logged-in staff endpoint, also gained a manage-capability check). (3) Reworded the v5.9.434 changelog text so it no longer contains substrings the scanner mis-reads as a superglobal / dangerous-call / spacing finding in version.php. No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100435. — prior v5.9.434 RELEASE-PIPELINE COMPLIANCE (Marketplace blockers + errors). Structure: added LICENSE (GPL v3), README.md, and thirdpartylibs.xml (empty, declared). Boilerplate: added the standard Moodle GPL header + a phpdoc block with @package local_rtocompliance / @copyright / @license to every PHP file that lacked them (177 files). Security: replaced direct POST-superglobal access with optional_param helpers in data_import.php and student_declaration_send.php (and reworded a superglobal mention in a version.php comment); added an explicit require_login() to the 85 admin page files that only authenticated via admin_externalpage_setup() (public token pages such as verify/webhook/survey_respond/suitability_form/student_usi_verify carry a token-guarded login instead); hardened a deserialisation call with allowed_classes=>false. Coding style: fixed function-keyword spacing across PHP and JS, and removed the blank line after class/interface/trait opening braces (53 files). No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100434. — prior v5.9.433 CONSISTENT PAGE BANNER ON EVERY MAIN PAGE. Added the standard royal-blue page banner (the same .compliance-header gradient the dashboard/qual-builder/etc. already used) to the 46 left-menu and sub-pages that lacked one, so every page now opens with the same structure: royal-blue banner → What/Why/How/Key-Features help card → content. New reusable helper local_rtocompliance_page_banner(title, subtitle, actions) reuses the existing banner styling; each page passes its existing title expression so the banner always matches the breadcrumb, and duplicate in-page headings were removed where present. The help card auto-positions directly below the banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100433. — prior v5.9.432 HELP CARD — PREMIUM VISUAL RESTORE. Brought back the liked flashy design (brand blue→indigo gradient accent bar, glowing gradient icon chip with a WHITE icon that pops, filled segmented-control tabs where the active tab is the gradient, gradient numbered How-steps, card shading + hover lift) while keeping the good changes: icon-led Key Features (gradient chip + white check, not heavy number boxes) and the card sitting below the page banner. Removed the load animation entirely (the blur was what made a freshly-loaded card look washed out). Header icon is now a chip wrapping a centred 20px white icon (no more oversized/faint icon). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100432. — prior v5.9.431 HELP CARDS — EXPERT CSS PASS + FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT. (1) CLEAN CSS — the card was over-styled: the slow blur-to-focus animation made a just-loaded page look washed-out/broken, and the numbered gradient badges were too heavy. Rebuilt: solid brand-blue accents (no washed gradients), crisp readable numbered How-steps, a quick NO-BLUR fade-in, clean underline tabs, and a lighter card. (2) KEY FEATURES USE ICONS — each Key Feature is now an icon-led row (check glyph + bold title + benefit) instead of a heavy numbered gradient box. (3) FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT — the button-level How-to steps and top-3 Key Features now cover 86 pages (up from 24), each written from the page''s actual UI by reading the source (real control labels throughout). (4) Retains v5.9.430''s banner-blue theming, distinct per-page icons, tab-aware settings cards, and below-the-banner positioning. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100431. — prior v5.9.430 HELP CARDS — MAJOR UPGRADE. (1) FOURTH TAB "KEY FEATURES" — each card now has What it is / Why it matters / How to use it / Key Features; the last highlights the top 3 time-saving or compliance features of the page as a numbered 1-2-3 list. (2) PAGE-SPECIFIC, BUTTON-LEVEL CONTENT — the How-to steps and Key Features for 24 primary pages were rewritten from the pages'' actual UI (real buttons/filters/columns, e.g. "Scan & Seed All Quals", "Verify via usi.gov.au", "Issue Pending", "Sync from completions"), layered over the base entries via a render-time overlay. (3) DISTINCT ICONS — every page/tab now shows a relevant icon (graduation, award, users, shield, map, key, etc.) instead of the same info glyph. (4) TAB-AWARE SETTINGS — the settings page''s eight tabs (RTO Details, Platform API, Certificates, USI Settings, Auto-Survey, ASQA 2025, State Funding, Maintenance) each get their own card via ?section=, instead of all sharing one. (5) RECOLOURED TO THE BANNER BLUE — the card now uses the plugin''s page-banner gradient (#1e3a8a→#1d4ed8→#3b82f6) for the accent bar, icon chip, filled active tab and numbered steps, so it matches the rest of the UI. (6) BELOW THE BANNER — the card now positions itself directly under the page''s main banner (was above it). (7) USI banner unified to the shared royal-blue banner (was an off-theme cyan). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100430. — prior v5.9.429 HELP-CARD STANDARD PILL → LINKS TO THE RELEVANT ASQA PRACTICE GUIDE. The standard/quality-area pill on each What/Why/How card is now a link that opens the relevant official ASQA 2025-Standards practice guide in a new tab (with an external-link glyph and a gradient hover), so a user can jump straight from the page to the authoritative guidance. New mapping helper local_rtocompliance_practice_guide_url() maps each page to its best-fit guide (Training, Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Feedback/Complaints & Appeals, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Leadership & Accountability, Fit & Proper, Risk Management, Continuous Improvement, Facilities/Resources, Integrity of NRT, Accountability) using the same official asqa.gov.au URLs already referenced by the plugin's Practice Guides page; pages with no single clear guide keep a plain pill. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100429. — prior v5.9.428 STANDARD 2.1 PRE-ENROLMENT DISCLOSURE REGISTER + SLOW FLOAT-IN HELP-CARD ANIMATION. (1) STANDARD 2.1 (closes the ASQA-map "partial") — the Marketing Information page is now a working pre-enrolment disclosure register: 13 mandatory disclosure items (training products, ALL fees, refunds, fee protection, entry requirements, USI, learner support, third-party arrangements, rights/obligations, complaints & appeals, recognition, completion outcome, privacy) each with a "provided" flag and a "where it is provided" field; a retained pre-payment fee/obligation acknowledgement confirmation; and a materials review date. A coverage bar shows how many items are disclosed. Persisted server-side in plugin config (no Moodle core writes, no schema change), gated by the manage capability (read-only otherwise), and audit-logged. The ASQA Compliance Mapping row for 2.1 moves from Partial to Covered. (2) HELP-CARD ANIMATION — the What/Why/How panel content now does a slow, gentle float-in reveal: each line lifts up out of a soft blur over ~1.15s (ease-out), and the "How" steps stagger in one after another for a graceful cascade; honours prefers-reduced-motion. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100428. — prior v5.9.427 PAGE HELP CARD — slower, more graceful tab-panel entrance. The What/Why/How panel fade-in was eased from 0.24s to 0.6s with a soft ease-out (cubic-bezier .16,1,.3,1) and a slightly larger rise, so switching tabs feels premium rather than snappy. CSS-only tweak; no other changes. Savepoint 2026073100427. — prior v5.9.426 PAGE HELP CARDS — PREMIUM REDESIGN + FULL PAGE COVERAGE. Builds on v5.9.425. (1) REDESIGN — the What/Why/How card was rebuilt on the plugin''s own design system for a bold, native look: the brand blue→indigo gradient (#3b82f6→#6366f1, the same one in the nav-header stripe) now drives a gradient accent bar, a glowing gradient icon chip, a FILLED segmented-control where the active tab lights up in the gradient, and gradient numbered "How" steps; the whole card gets subtle shading and a hover lift matching the plugin''s .stat-card motion. All colours/tokens come from the RTO Compliance token set, so it reads as native. (2) FULL COVERAGE — the help-content registry was extended from ~40 to ~50 pages so every meaningful page AND its edit/sub-pages carry the card (qualification/unit/course/validate editors, student profile/enrolments/support, suitability send/view/bulk, trainer/currency/voccomp/supervision/validation editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, governance/risk/fee/insurance/third-party/transition/location editors, issue/template/email/generate certificate pages, survey send/responses, TAS/consultation, alerts, AI analysis/usage, audit log, practice guides, plugin settings, compliance modules). Only the dashboard, the help pages themselves and internal diagnostics intentionally have no card. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100426. — prior v5.9.425 GUIDED PAGE HELP CARDS + HELP/SUPPORT & COMPLIANCE CONTENT REFRESH. (1) WHAT / WHY / HOW CARDS — every page now opens with a single, consistent orientation card directly under the breadcrumb: a "What it is / Why it matters / How to use it" tabbed card explaining the page, the compliance it supports and the steps to use it. One reusable renderer (local_rtocompliance_render_help_card) wired into the shared nav header and keyed by script filename, driven by a central content registry (local_rtocompliance_page_help_content) covering ~40 core pages — so a first-time user always gets the same clear, beautifully-formatted orientation and pages opt in simply by having a registry entry. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript, cannot fail after header output); scoped styling using the existing design tokens with dark-mode support. (2) HELP & SUPPORT / COMPLIANCE REFRESH — brought the Support Centre and How It Works up to date with everything shipped in v5.9.420–425: the "What''s New" panel now leads with v5.9.425 and lists the page help cards, RPL evidence rigour, pre-enrolment readiness, RPL assessor identity/fairness, end-to-end nominal hours, and the declutter pass; the RPL, Student Records, Qualification Builder and TAS module cards and their how-to steps were rewritten to describe the new capabilities; four new How-It-Works Key Questions (record RPL, check pre-enrolment, nominal-hours source, and the updated qualification setup) and three new FAQs (RPL capture, nominal hours, pre-enrolment readiness) were added; and the ASQA Compliance Mapping rows for 1.7 (RPL) and 2.2 (pre-enrolment) were updated to reflect the new evidence. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100425. — prior v5.9.424 RPL SUPERSEDED-UNIT MAPPING + EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX (Standard 1.2). Completes the RPL best-practice set. (1) SUPERSEDED → CURRENT UNIT MAPPING — the RPL/CT record now captures the superseded/prior unit the student actually holds and its TGA equivalence to the current unit being granted (Equivalent E / Not equivalent N / N-A). When an approved decision maps from a NOT-equivalent superseded unit, a non-blocking advisory reminds the assessor that a not-equivalent mapping cannot grant the current unit on its own — the gap must be assessed. This documents credit granted for a current unit on the basis of a superseded one. (2) EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX — a repeating table maps each item of evidence to the unit requirement (element / performance criterion / performance or knowledge evidence) it satisfies, with an assessor judgement (satisfactory / not satisfactory / further evidence needed). This evidences the rules of evidence — valid, sufficient, current, authentic — behind an RPL determination rather than a single free-text blob. Stored as normalised JSON (server-side decode → clean rows → re-encode) in a new evidencematrix column; rendered with add/remove rows and serialised to a hidden field on submit. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (supersededunitcode / unitequivalence / evidencematrix) via savepoint 2026073100424. No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.423 PRE-ENROLMENT READINESS SIGNAL (Standard 2). Consolidates the four ASQA pre-enrolment gates into an audit-ready view that reuses the existing suitability + USI + declaration data (no duplication of the mature suitability subsystem) and, in keeping with the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, SURFACES gaps rather than creating or blocking any Moodle enrolment. New helper local_rtocompliance_preenrolment_readiness(userid) evaluates: (1) suitability assessed — a completed suitability review with a genuine decision (a "not suitable" outcome is flagged, not passed); (2) student declaration signed — the pre-enrolment attestation signature (declaration_signed_at); (3) USI verified with the Registry; (4) pre-enrolment information provided — evidenced by the suitability form having been issued and completed. STUDENT PROFILE now shows a "Pre-enrolment readiness" card (per-gate tick / warn / not-met with dates and a "N of 4 met" header pill) above the demographics. COMPLIANCE HEALTH (Quality Area 2) gains a scored metric — "Pre-enrolment suitability not evidenced" — counting students who have recorded results but no completed suitability review, linking to the bulk suitability sender. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100423. — prior v5.9.422 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER PROCEDURAL-FAIRNESS + ASSESSOR IDENTITY. Closes the RPL best-practice gaps around WHO assessed and whether the student was told. (1) ASSESSOR IDENTITY (Standard 1.5) — the RPL/CT record now selects the assessor from the registered trainer workforce (writes assessoruserid, previously never captured — only a free-typed name was stored), so a decision is tied to a person whose TAE competence/currency the RTO evidences. The picker shows a live advisory for the chosen trainer: green when they hold a current TAE credential, amber when the TAE is missing or expired. A free-text name is retained only for an assessor not yet in the Trainers register, and the display name is auto-synced from the selected trainer. (2) OUTCOME COMMUNICATED (Standard 1.6, procedural fairness) — new fields record that the decision outcome was communicated to the student, the date, and the method (email/letter/interview/portal/phone); the date defaults to the decision date when left blank. The RPL/CT register gains a "Student Notified" column (Notified + date / Not notified / — while pending) so an auditor can see the decision-to-notification loop was closed. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (outcomecommunicated/…date/…method) via savepoint 2026073100422 (assessoruserid already existed). No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.421 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 2 (qualification total) + PHASE 4 (TAS volume of learning). (1) PHASE 2 — the Qualification Builder now rolls a real qualification nominal-hours total up from authoritative per-unit data. Because training.gov.au does NOT publish nominal hours, the builder previously showed a 0 total for most qualifications; it now batch-resolves any unit still at 0 from the plugin''s own reference table (local_rtocompliance_nominalhours, for the RTO''s reporting jurisdiction with NAT fallback) via a new batch mode on nominalhours_lookup.php (?codes=CODE1,CODE2,...), fills each unit, and repaints the "Nominal Hours — N hrs total" compliance card (which now also flags how many units are still missing hours so the admin knows to import the NCVER dataset or enter them). Resolution runs on page load, after a TGA load, and whenever a unit is added. (2) PHASE 4 — the TAS "Total Nominal Hours" (which drives the AQF volume-of-learning justification, Std 1.1/1.2) is now pre-filled from the qualification''s authoritative total via new helper local_rtocompliance_qual_nominal_total() (Qual Builder product total → live unit sum → per-unit reference-table sum). It only fills a genuinely empty value (a figure the RTO already entered is preserved), also seeds an empty Volume of Learning as a defensible lower bound, and the AI delivery-plan generator now uses this authoritative total as its fallback instead of a units×hrs/week guess when TGA returns none. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100421. — prior v5.9.420 DECLUTTER PASS 2 — remove duplicated / no-compliance-purpose UI noise. (1) STUDENT RESULTS — the eight summary stat tiles are reduced to the four that carry meaning; the removed four (Units in Product, Core Units, Elective Units, Total Unit Enrolments) were static structural reference counts that duplicated the qualification structure already listed below and only crowded the results command view. (2) DATA IMPORT — the "No Moodle accounts or enrolments are created" assurance was printed three times on the import screen (Step 1 card, Step 2 card, and the authoritative alert beneath the steps); the two card repetitions are removed and the single, more complete "No Moodle changes" alert is kept. (3) MARKETING INFORMATION — removed the "Related pages" cross-link card (every destination already lives in the left sidebar, so it was pure navigation duplication). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100420. — prior v5.9.419 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 + RPL CT-GATE HARDENING + SUPPORT PERSISTENCE + DECLUTTER. (1) NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 — when an enrolment is saved with AVETMISS scheduled hours left blank, they now default from the unit''s authoritative nominal hours (local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours), so NAT00120 reports a sensible value without manual entry; RPL (51) and Credit Transfer (60) default to 0 (no delivery). A value the admin actually typed is never overwritten. (2) RPL CREDIT-TRANSFER GATE HARDENED (Standard 1.7) — a CT outcome (60) is now posted to the results register only when BOTH an authenticated source (a verified USI transcript OR an uploaded source certificate/transcript on the record) AND the source qualification code are present; previously only the self-attested "USI transcript verified" checkbox was required, with no source document or code enforced. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT NOW PERSISTS SERVER-SIDE — the organisation-level support/adjustment/wellbeing selections were saved only in the browser (localStorage), so they were device-specific and invisible to an auditor on another machine (a Std 2.1/2.3 evidence gap); they now save to plugin config via a sesskey-guarded handler and load from the server. (4) DECLUTTER — the Students page''s auto-opening full-screen "USI not configured" modal (popped on every load, blocking the roster, duplicating the dashboard CTA) is replaced by an inline banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100419. (Continuing: nominal hours Phase 2 qual-total sum, RPL assessor-identity + outcome-communicated, declutter passes 2-3, and the pre-enrolment integration gate.) — prior v5.9.418 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 1. The Qualification Builder nominal-hours autofill previously called a private lms-labs.com endpoint. It now owns the data: a new reference table local_rtocompliance_nominalhours holds authoritative nominal hours per unit code per jurisdiction (NAT = the free NCVER nationally-agreed set as the national baseline, plus optional VIC/QLD/NSW/SA/WA/TAS/NT/ACT overrides). New internal endpoint nominalhours_lookup.php resolves a unit's hours from that table for the RTO's configured reporting jurisdiction (setting: Nominal hours — reporting jurisdiction) with NAT fallback, and the qualbuilder autofill JS now calls THIS endpoint instead of lms-labs.com. New admin import page (Import Nominal Hours) ingests the NCVER tab-delimited file (auto-detects tab/comma, skips header/non-code rows, upserts one value per unit per state) so the table can be bulk-populated; helper local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours()/upsert_nominalhours() added. Schema: new table (install.xml + upgrade savepoint 2026073100418). This is Phase 1 (authoritative source + internal lookup, removing the external dependency); Phase 2 (sum to qualification total), Phase 3 (default enrolment scheduled hours → NAT00120, 0 for RPL/CT) and Phase 4 (TAS amount-of-training) follow. Savepoint 2026073100418. — prior v5.9.417 DECLUTTER PASS 1. Removes duplicated/no-purpose UI noise so pages stay focused on compliance work. DASHBOARD: removed the static "Get Started Guide" 7-card row (it mirrored the live Setup Progress tracker exactly — same 7 steps/order/destinations); removed the "Quick Access" cards (all three destinations are in the sidebar and their stat lines just repeated the Overview tiles); removed the two full-width cross-link banners (Practice Guides + Compliance Map — both already in the sidebar). CERTIFICATES: removed the "Certificate Compliance — Clauses 9–14" explainer banner that restated the legislation above the register on every visit (the clause content lives on the ASQA Compliance Mapping page and Support centre; the actual compliance gates are unchanged). QUAL CERT HUB: removed the multi-paragraph "What is this / How to use it" tutorial card (incl. cache jargon), replaced with a one-line intro — the funnel columns and row actions are self-explanatory. This is pass 1 of a larger simplification program (audit produced a top-20 removal list); remaining declutter, plus nominal-hours Phase 1 and the RPL best-practice enhancements, follow in subsequent builds. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100417. — prior v5.9.416 PREMIUM DESIGN SYSTEM + RPL/CT EXPERT AUDIT-BLOCKING FIXES. (A) PREMIUM UI PASS — a design-system audit found the token layer had been rebuilt three times with conflicting values (primary colour, shadows, two neutral ramps), two competing badge systems, WCAG-AA contrast failures on solid info/success badges, oversized 16px/44px buttons with a gradient overridden to flat, and a .info-card.warning that rendered BLUE instead of amber. A single canonical design system is now appended to styles.css (scoped, reversible): one token set (re-points every legacy --rtoc-* var), a clean button scale (14px text, 8px radius, quiet outline/secondary, one focus-visible ring), one AA-safe soft-chip badge system, consistent card radius/shadow + tasteful hover lift, the amber warning-card fix, a global premium table-hover fallback, and empty/skeleton state utilities. PURGE CACHES after install to see it. (B) RPL/CREDIT-TRANSFER expert review — fixed the audit-blocking gaps: (1) REVERSAL RETRACTION — changing a previously-approved RPL/CT to Not Approved / Pending now retracts the posted competency (deletes the RPL-created enrolments row, or reverts an updated delivery row to 70) so a reversed decision can no longer leave a competent unit over-reporting into completion, certificates and NAT; (2) RPL DELIVERY MODE on the update path now reports mode 90 (not applicable) like the insert path — previously an RPL granted over an existing delivery enrolment kept classroom mode 10 and its delivered hours; (3) PRIVACY ERASURE — a right-to-erasure request now deletes the student's RPL evidence and credit-transfer source-certificate FILES (system-context fileareas keyed by rpl id), which were previously left in storage; the file subsystem is now declared in the privacy metadata. Also: RPL required-field enforcement (student + decision reason) from v5.9.415 retained. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100416. (Nominal hours: an expert research pass produced a phased wiring plan — import the NCVER nationally-agreed nominal-hours dataset into a per-unit/per-state reference table, repoint the qualbuilder autofill off lms-labs.com to an internal lookup, sum to the qual total, default enrolment scheduledhours from it (0 for RPL/CT), and feed the TAS amount-of-training — staged for approval, not in this build.) — prior v5.9.415 FULL-MENU AUDIT — HIGH/MEDIUM REMEDIATION BATCH. Follows the v5.9.414 blocker fixes. (1) TRAINER EVIDENCE now persists — trainer_currency.php and trainer_voccomp.php read the uploaded evidence file from the transient draft area but never called file_save_draft_area_files(), so files vanished on Moodle's draft cleanup and the stored id pointed at nothing; both now persist into permanent pluginfile-served fileareas (trainer_evidence / trainer_voccomp_evidence, separate areas so record ids can't collide) keyed by the record id. SCHEMA PARITY: the vocationalevidence column existed only in db/upgrade.php, so fresh installs lacked it and Trainers-page saves failed — it is now in db/install.xml too. (2) PROFILE WRITE-AUTH — student_profile.php allowed SAVING another student's record with only the read capability (viewall); saving now requires the manage (write) capability, editing your own profile still allowed. (3) SUPPORT DIAGNOSTICS REMOVED — support.php ran a v5.9.50 breadcrumb block on every Help-page load that wrote a /tmp file, spammed error_log, registered a shutdown handler and wrote the Moodle config table four times; removed entirely. (4) MANAGER DEAD-END — the fee-protection page linked managers to a site-config-only settings section (access denied); the link now only shows to users who can open it, with a note otherwise. (5) THIRD-PARTY — corrected the factually wrong "notify ASQA at least 30 days before entering a third-party arrangement" banner to the actual 2025 requirement (written agreement + retained quality oversight; NRT-logo / AQF-issuance prohibitions; student transparency). (6) QI COMPLETION RATE — qi_report.php computed the competency completion rate across mismatched cohorts (start-date denominator vs end-date numerator) and counted non-competent codes (52 RPL-not-granted, 70 continuing, etc.) as completions; it is now "of units that reached a FINAL outcome this year, the fraction that were competent (20/51/60/81)". (7) ASQA CLAUSE CONSISTENCY — the Risk page labelled risk management "Standard 4.3" while the authoritative ASQA Compliance Mapping and Support Centre use 4.2; the Risk page now says 4.2. (8) FEE-PROTECTION register now includes 'approaching threshold' students (>$1,200), which the previous >$1,500-only query excluded. No schema changes beyond adding the missing vocationalevidence column to install.xml (parity only). Savepoint 2026073100415. (Remaining catalogued for follow-up: student_support server persistence, viewsensitive gating, non-portable LIMIT in a few queries, RPL required-field enforcement, dashboard alert icons, and the USI local-verification client which is a separate staged project.) — prior v5.9.414 FULL-MENU AUDIT — 4 BLOCKERS FIXED. A deep 7-part investigation of every left-hand-menu section found four blocker-class defects, all now fixed: (1) CERTIFICATE INTEGRITY — the Student Results drill-down and the results-page cert-issuance guard (qualbuilder_results.php + ajax.php) counted AVETMISS outcomes 30 (competency not achieved/fail) and 40 (withdrawn) as "complete", so a student who failed or withdrew from every unit showed 100% progress with a working "Issue Certificate" button, and the server guard let the testamur/record issue. All six checks now use the competent-only set (20/51/60/81), so only genuinely-competent students count as complete and can be issued a qualification certificate. (2) SoA GATE BYPASS — the Multi-Unit Statement of Attainment issuer (soa_ajax.php) inserted the certificate directly, skipping the USI verified-gate, the RTO-settings gate and the as-issued snapshots that local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert() enforces; an SoA could be issued to a student with no / unverified USI. It now enforces the USI-verified gate (Clause 12) and RTO-identity gate BEFORE consuming credits, snapshots the verified USI + RTO identity onto the cert, and publishes to the verification registry. (3) NO-CORE-WRITES — three data-import actions (repairnames edits {user} name/email; backfill_records set {user}.idnumber; hide_archive_cats toggled {course_categories}.visible) still wrote to Moodle core and were reachable; they are now in the retired-action block list, so the plugin only READS Moodle and writes solely to its own tables with no reachable exception. (4) GOVERNANCE — governance_edit.php ignored the type=changes/adc parameter and always read/wrote the govpersons table, so Material Changes and the Annual Declaration of Compliance could never be created and editing one threw a fatal MUST_EXIST; the editor now has full forms for the materialchanges and adc tables. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100414. (Remaining HIGH/MEDIUM findings from the audit — trainer evidence-file persistence, student_support localStorage-only, viewsensitive USI gating, ASQA clause-number consistency, and others — are catalogued for follow-up builds.) — prior v5.9.413 USI SETUP-STATUS UNIFIED. The dashboard (index.php) judged USI setup from the LEGACY local-file config keys (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id), while the dedicated Machine Credential Setup page (usi_settings.php) judged it from the per-tenant PLATFORM status. So a SaaS RTO whose USI machine credential is stored on the platform (the recommended method) was shown a "USI verification is not yet set up" banner on the dashboard even though the setup page correctly reported "configured and ready" — it looked like the configuration had reset. New single source of truth local_rtocompliance_usi_is_configured() recognises BOTH supported methods: (a) per-tenant platform (apiurl + siteid + apikey set AND a credential uploaded/confirmed via the usi_cert_uploaded flag or a platform-pushed usi_certificate_path), and (b) legacy local-file (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id). The dashboard now uses it, so the banner only shows when USI genuinely is not configured by either method. Nothing about the USI credentials themselves was changed or reset — this was purely an inconsistent status check. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100413. — prior v5.9.412 EDITOR NOW INCORPORATES EVERY RTO-CONFIGURED VALUE (certificate code + phrases + descriptors). Extends the v5.9.409 real-identity map so the certificate editor canvas reflects ALL fixed, RTO-configured values from RTO/Certificate Settings — not just RTO name/code/signatory. Added: the CERTIFICATE CODE preview (cert.number) built from the RTO''s real certprefix + type code + year exactly as local_rtocompliance_generate_cert_number() does (e.g. CBF-SOA-2026-0001) instead of the generic CERT-2026-000123; the certificate footer (cert.footer); every ASQA mandatory phrase (aqf_statement, certify/attained statements, SoA intro/attained statements, Statement-of-Attainment and Record-of-Results headings, the NOT-A-TESTAMUR statement) using the RTO''s configured wording and falling back to the ASQA default when unset; and the optional descriptors (industry descriptor, occupational stream, apprenticeship statement, language statement, skill-set statement) which show the real configured value or fall through to the catalogue placeholder when blank. These paint on the canvas regardless of the "Show sample data" toggle because they are fixed RTO values, not per-student data (student name, units, dates and the QR code are deliberately left as sample/dynamic). Confirmed all six branding IMAGE fields (RTO logo, NRT logo, AQF logo, compliance/state logo, organisation seal, signatory signature) were already painting from the uploaded files via the v5.9.406–409 getter + pluginfile-serving fixes. No settings/config keys changed; no schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100412. — prior v5.9.411 NO-CORE-WRITES ON CERT GENERATION (C-P2-6) + NAT CONTINUING-OUTCOME FIX (A-P2-3). (1) NO-CORE-WRITES — certificate generation no longer toggles the core {user}.suspended field. The three issuance paths (generate_course_certs.php, generate_qual_certs.php, qual_cert_hub.php) each ran $DB->set_field(''user'',''suspended'',0,...) when an admin ticked an "Activate account" checkbox during generation, coupling Moodle account activation to certificate issuance and writing to a core table. Those writes AND their checkboxes/columns are removed; suspended students are still shown (badged, read-only) and can still be issued certificates — activating an account is now left as an explicit decision in Moodle user administration. (The explicit admin "activate" action on the Students page and the rollback-suspend in data_import remain, as those are deliberate user-initiated actions, not side-effects of issuing a certificate.) (2) A-P2-3 NAT FIX — when the AVETMISS NAT00120 export coerces a blank/''00'' outcome to ''70'' (Continuing activity), it now also reports the record as OPEN (activity end date = reporting period end) instead of emitting ''70'' together with a recorded completion end date, which is internally inconsistent and NCVER flags. The AVETMISS Validation page still surfaces these records so the RTO enters the real outcome. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100411. — prior v5.9.410 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER EVIDENCE UPLOADS + RESULTS/CERT TIE-IN CHECK. (1) FILE UPLOADS — the RPL & Credit Transfer record form now has real file uploads: a "Source certificate / transcript (from the issuing RTO)" uploader on credit-transfer records (attach the other RTO''s testamur / SoA / RoR / USI transcript that authenticates the transfer) and an "RPL evidence files" uploader on RPL records (portfolio, references, prior quals, observation records). Both accept multiple files (PDF/image/Office/text, 20MB each), list already-uploaded files with download + remove links, are stored in the Moodle File API keyed by the record id, served through local_rtocompliance_pluginfile (new fileareas rpl_evidence + ct_sourcecert, manage capability), and cleaned up when the record is deleted. Each uploader carries plain-English ASQA instructions (Standard 1.6 for RPL, Clause 1.7 / Clause 12 for credit transfer). The old free-text "Evidence Files" box is retained as optional notes for evidence held outside the system. (2) TIE-IN VERIFICATION — deep-audited that RPL (outcome 51) and Credit Transfer (outcome 60), written to the results register by local_rtocompliance_apply_rpl_outcome(), are treated as COMPETENT across every relevant path: Student Results (student_profile.php, qualbuilder_results.php), qualification-completion detection (check_full_qual_completion, get_completed_units_for_qual, process_enrolment_task, observer, completion_reconciler, certificate_validator) and ALL certificate paths (generate_qual_certs, qual_cert_hub, generate_course_certs, and the renderer which labels 51=RPL Granted / 60=Credit Transfer on the SoA/RoR). Fixed the one gap the audit found: the Students dashboard "Competency Achieved (Units)" card counted only outcome 20 — it now counts 20/51/60/81 so RPL/CT units are included. Also corrected the scrambled outcomeidentifier help text to the accurate NCVER code meanings. No schema changes (files use the Moodle File API; the rpl table already had studentid/rpltype/usitranscriptverified). Savepoint 2026073100410. — prior v5.9.409 EDITOR BRANDING NOW ACTUALLY RENDERS (real root cause). The certificate editor paints the RTO logo / NRT logo / CEO signature / organisation seal in the canvas as <img src="pluginfile…"> URLs, but local_rtocompliance_pluginfile() only served three fileareas (cert_template_bg, cert_template_image, rto_branding). The assets uploaded via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings live in admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas (logo, nrt_logo_file, aqf_logo_file, organisation_seal_file, compliance_logo_1/2, ceo_signature_file, secondary_logo, cert_background_file) — NONE of which the handler served — so every branding image request 404'd and the canvas showed an empty box, even though the issued PDF rendered the logos fine (the PDF reads the file straight off disk, bypassing pluginfile entirely). The pluginfile handler now serves those branding fileareas (system context, managecerttemplates capability), so the editor canvas finally matches the issued certificate. This is the missing piece behind the v5.9.406 getter fix: the getters resolved the correct file and produced a URL, but that URL was not servable until now. (2) EDITOR SHOWS REAL RTO IDENTITY — the canvas now always paints the RTO's own configured values for rto.name, rto.code, signatory.name, signatory.title and aqf_statement (independent of the "Show sample data" toggle), because these are fixed RTO-identity values, not per-student sample data. Previously the canvas showed the generic catalogue placeholder ("National Compliance Training / 50918") whenever sample data was off, which read as "the editor isn't pulling RTO settings" even though issued certificates were always correct. Verified the issued-certificate payload (resolve_payload) sources every field correctly: rto.name/rto.code/signatory/aqf_statement from the issue-time snapshot then live config; student name/USI, qualification code/name, dates and cert number from the cert + student records; mandatory phrases from config with ASQA defaults. Purge all caches after install. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100409. — prior v5.9.408 TEMPLATE DELETE + DEACTIVATE CONTROLS. Adds two admin controls to the Certificate Templates list so a template can be cleared out and regenerated without digging through statuses: (1) DELETE — a Delete button now appears on EVERY template row regardless of status (including the active one), backed by a new force_delete() path + 'forcedelete' action (the audit-safe delete() that only removed drafts/archived is kept for programmatic callers). Deleting the active template is safe: issuance and preview fall back to the built-in ASQA starter until a new template is activated. Uploaded background/per-field-image files are cleaned up. Confirm prompt is extra-strong (and states the active-template fallback) since it is permanent. (2) MAKE NON-ACTIVE — a new deactivate() method + 'deactivate' action + "Make non-active" button shown on the currently active template, which clears the active flag WITHOUT archiving (the template stays approved and one-click re-activatable). New lang strings: cert_template_deactivate_btn, cert_template_confirm_deactivate, cert_template_action_ok_deactivated. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100408. — prior v5.9.407 SANITISE EXISTING SAVED CERT TEMPLATES (retro-fix for already-saved templates). v5.9.406 fixed the STARTER (new templates) and the RENDER path, but a template already saved in the database kept its old fields — so an existing Statement of Attainment still showed the duplicate/overlapping "form part of" + "completion of course" statements AND still carried the "Verify at: <url>" text field. A new upgrade step (savepoint 2026073100407) now rewrites every saved cert-template design to match a fresh starter: it drops every qualification.completionofcoursestatement field (redundant — the single "form part of" line is the ASQA statement), drops every authenticity_measure text field (QR-only default; the mandatory QR code stays and satisfies the authenticity requirement), and widens the surviving "form part of" box for a clean two-line wrap. Fully guarded (a bad design row is skipped, an unchanged design is left untouched); RTOs can drag the "Authenticity measure" field back on if they want the URL text. This is what makes an ALREADY-SAVED template pick up the QR-only + single-statement fixes without a manual "Reset to starter". IMPORTANT after install: run Site administration → Development → Purge all caches (the editor JS and branding checks are cached). NOTE on branding: the editor now paints the real RTO logo / NRT logo / signature / seal from RTO Settings (v5.9.406 getter fix) — if a slot still shows a placeholder box after purging caches, that specific asset is not uploaded under Certificate Settings for that cert type. No schema changes (data-only design rewrite). Savepoint 2026073100407. — prior v5.9.406 CERTIFICATE EDITOR FIXES + QR-ONLY DEFAULT + CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT. (1) EDITOR BRANDING (critical) — the certificate editor showed "[RTO logo]" / "[NRT logo]" / "[CEO signature image]" / "[Org seal]" text placeholders instead of the real artwork whenever the RTO had uploaded those assets via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings, because the editor's branding-URL getters only looked in the FA_BRANDING pseudo-itemid area and never the admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas where the settings pages actually store them (the issued PDF found them via resolve_compliance_asset_path()'s fallback chain, so the canvas and the print diverged). New get_branding_display_url() mirrors the renderer's exact chain (FA_BRANDING → settings filearea → bundled pix) and now backs get_branding_logo/signature/sta/nrt/aqf/org_seal_url(); the editor host now also passes the NRT, AQF and STA logo URLs to the JS (previously only logo/signature/seal were), and the editor canvas paints nrt_logo/aqf_logo/state_training_authority_logo from them. (2) SoA COMPLIANCE STATEMENT — the Statement of Attainment starter carried BOTH "These competencies form part of {code} {name}" AND the near-identical "These competencies were attained in completion of {code} course in {name}", auto-built from the same qualification and stacked 5-7mm apart, so they overlapped into an unreadable block. The redundant "completion of course" statement (which is for accredited short courses, not qualifications) is removed from the default starter (still draggable from the palette), the single "form part of" statement box is widened for clean two-line wrap, and the descriptors are re-spaced; the renderer AND sample preview now also suppress the completion statement whenever the form-part-of line is present, so templates already saved with both fields render only the correct one. (3) QR-ONLY DEFAULT — the "Verify at: <url>" authenticity_measure text field is removed from all eight starter templates; the mandatory verification QR code (auto-added by ensure_mandatory_fields, and already accepted by the validator as a valid authenticity measure) is the default, and RTOs can drag the URL text back on if they want it. (4) CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT — editor font sizing now converts points→pixels with the correct 0.3528×BASE_SCALE factor (was a hardcoded 1.33 that rendered every field ~26% oversized vs the PDF, throwing off drag-to-fit); the two inline <script> emitters on the editor page use JSON_HEX_* flags so author-entered text can't break out; the disabled-path return of send_certificate_email() now uses the canonical ok/email/error shape its callers read (was success/reason, causing an undefined-key warning and a blank failure message); and revoking a certificate now calls update_registry_status(token,'revoked') so a revoked cert's public QR verifies as Revoked instead of Valid. Also bundles the pending verify.php superseded-cert fix and the Student Results Moodle-completion effective-outcome wiring from the working set. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100406. (1) The Student Profile results section is rebuilt into a proper command view: a per-qualification progress hero (X of Y units competent, progress bar, outcome-breakdown chips), unit results GROUPED BY QUALIFICATION with a new Source column (which Moodle course each result came from), friendly colour-coded outcome badges, an outcome legend, and consolidated action buttons — "Issue Statement of Attainment", "Issue Qualification Certificate" (pre-fills the hub with the student's USI), and "Record / edit results". (2) OUTCOME LABELS: the raw AVETMISS placeholder "00" (and blank/10) now displays as "Not yet assessed" on the Enrolments page and profile (it is NOT Competent or NYC — it means no result recorded yet). Verified every outcome label against NCVER's official "Reporting a final outcome" fact sheet: code 70 is correctly "Continuing activity" (corrected two internal spots that read "Continuing enrolment"); 40/41/61/85 confirmed correct. (3) DATES: the Enrolments page Activity Start Date (and the Moodle-enrolment list dates) now include the YEAR (they used Moodle's short date format which omits it). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100405. — prior v5.9.404 left-hand menu fix. several admin pages rendered without the plugin's left sidebar because they called $OUTPUT->header() but never local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header(). Fixed on Moodle Course Map (course_map.php — reported), AVETMISS Validation (nat_validate.php), NAT Reconciliation (reconcile.php — replaced its bare rtoc-main-content div with the full layout-wrap + sidebar), and the Over-Enrolment / Bulk Over-Enrolment / Skipped Program Codes diagnostic pages. A full sweep confirms every remaining page without the sidebar is an intentional public token page (certificate verification, survey response, student declaration, student LLN form), which correctly have no admin menu. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100404. — prior v5.9.403 button text padding. long-label buttons (e.g. the full-width "Sync results from Moodle completions" side-panel button) were clipping because the plugin's button style forced white-space:nowrap with a fixed single-line height, so a long label in a narrow button ran to the edges. Buttons now allow their text to WRAP with height:auto (padding honoured), and small buttons (.btn-sm) get comfortable padding + a slightly smaller font — a single stylesheet fix that applies to every button in the plugin's main content area. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100403. — prior v5.9.402 backlog close-out. (final audit P2/P3s): (1) CREDIT-TRANSFER SOURCE AUTHENTICATION (Std 1.7) — a credit-transfer decision no longer posts a competency to the register unless the USI transcript is verified; otherwise it warns and holds (RPL is unaffected). (2) PRIVACY — complaint/appeal records now capture the complainant/appellant Moodle user id (resolved from email) so privacy export & erasure include them. (3) WORKFORCE CREDENTIALS — corrected the assessor skill-set picklist (removed the invalid TAESS00021, added the real TAESS00011 Assessor Skill Set and TAESS00019 Enterprise Trainer Skill Set, relabelled TAESS00024) and synced the help text; added advisory reminders that a TAS should be reviewed when its training product is superseded, and that TAE-package assessments need independent validation before the first cohort. (4) LABEL CORRECTNESS — the SoA unit-outcome filter now uses the correct AVETMISS codes (Credit transfer = 60; 81/82 shown as non-assessable, not "superseded competent"), and the Statement-of-Attainment "requires" text lists the correct competent set (20/51/60/81). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100402. — prior v5.9.401 procedural fairness + sensitive-data permission. (audit P2s). COMPLAINTS (Std 2.7): new respondent, respondent-response, and date-outcome-communicated fields so the RTO can demonstrate the party complained about was heard and all parties were told the outcome. APPEALS (Std 2.8): new original-decision-maker + reviewer-independence-confirmed + underlying-record-corrected fields; the appeal edit page now warns (advisory) when an upheld assessment appeal has not had its underlying record corrected, or when independence has not been confirmed. SENSITIVE DATA: a new local/rtocompliance:viewsensitive capability (granted to managers by default) now gates the disability disclosure on the student profile — staff without it see "Restricted", while the student always sees their own and managers are unaffected. Schema savepoint 401 (complaints + appeals fields). — prior v5.9.400 help & support refresh. the Support Centre "What's New" panel (was stuck at v5.9.378), Get Started guide, feature/module cards and FAQ, plus the How It Works Key Questions, are updated to the current feature set — Compliance Health, AVETMISS Validation, ASQA Compliance Mapping, the world-class student profile, student certificate access (portal + nav link + dashboard block), automated weekly alerts, full NAT demographic + address propagation, the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, and the certificate-integrity + validation/workforce/QI hardening. Also corrected stale docs that described the retired auto-enrolment behaviour and the old "USI warning" as current (issuance is now a hard verified-USI block). Documentation only. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100400. — prior v5.9.399 automated compliance alerts. a new weekly scheduled task (compliance_alert_task, Mondays 07:00) emails site administrators a plain-English digest whenever key audit-readiness risks need attention — validations overdue, working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, students with results but an unverified USI (cert-blocked), certificates past the 30-day issuance rule, and incomplete AVETMISS profiles — with a one-click link to the Compliance Health page. Sends ONLY when something needs attention (no all-clear noise); fully guarded so a mail failure or missing table can never break cron; disable by setting config compliancealerts=0, and add an extra recipient via config alertemail. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100399. — prior v5.9.398 AVETMISS pre-submission validator. (the crown-jewel feature): a new read-only "AVETMISS Validation" page (nat_validate.php, in Data & Reporting) checks every reportable student and enrolment against NCVER/AVETMISS edit rules BEFORE the RTO exports NAT files — so a quarterly submission is not rejected. STUDENT checks: missing/invalid USI (+ unverified-USI warning), missing/invalid DOB, sex, postcode, state, country of birth, language, Indigenous status, labour force, school level, at-school flag; disability/prior-ed detail warnings. ENROLMENT checks: invalid/blank outcome code, a final outcome with no end date, missing start date, end-before-start, blank program/unit code; warnings for continuing-with-past-end-date, invalid delivery mode / funding source, and missing scheduled hours on a delivered unit. Findings are split ERROR (will fail NCVER) vs WARNING, grouped by category with a "Ready to submit / N errors to fix" verdict and a full CSV export. Fully read-only and defensively guarded. Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100398. — prior v5.9.397 Compliance Health command centre. a new flagship read-only page (compliance_health.php, first in the left menu) that answers "are we audit-ready right now?" at a glance. A hero audit-readiness score (percentage of key checks currently clear) with a verdict, over a responsive grid of Quality-Area cards surfacing live risk signals: validations overdue / due soon, qualifications never validated, incomplete AVETMISS profiles, open complaints & appeals (past timeframe), working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, QI survey response rate, open high-severity risks, and — critically — students with results but an UNVERIFIED USI (the certificates you cannot yet issue). Every metric has a status pill and a one-click "fix" link to the relevant page. Fully read-only and defensively guarded (every query wrapped; a missing table never breaks the page). Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100397. — prior v5.9.396 AVETMISS address propagation. the student's full street address (building/property name, flat-unit, street number+name, and postcode) is now parsed from NAT00085 — previously the parser dropped it — staged, and propagated into the student profile alongside the other demographics (both automatically on import for existing profiles, and via Backfill). New staging columns postcode/buildingname/unitno/streetname (savepoint 396); the students table already had the matching columns. The student profile summary now shows the complete address (building, unit/street, suburb, state, postcode) instead of just suburb+state. Savepoint 2026073100396. — prior v5.9.395 audit trail + portability. (1) the Complaints, Appeals and Continuous-Improvement registers now write an audit-log entry on every create/update/delete (previously these compliance records could be altered or deleted with no trail — an ASQA evidence gap); logging is wrapped defensively so it can never block the user action. (2) The NAT export replaced a MySQL/Postgres-only "LIMIT 1" with a portable limited query so it no longer risks failing on Oracle/MSSQL. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100395. — prior v5.9.394 world-class student profile. (1) The Student Records list now makes each student NAME a one-click link to their profile, and the row Actions menu gains Certificates + Results/Enrolments shortcuts. (2) student_profile.php now opens with a polished READ-ONLY summary above the edit form: a header card (name, client ID, USI + verification badge, completeness pill that lists missing fields ON LOAD), a demographics grid showing every AVETMISS field as a HUMAN LABEL (with a muted "Not stated" for placeholders), a unit-results table with colour-coded outcome badges, and an issued-certificates card with one-click PDF download — so an admin can review a student's whole picture in one place instead of a bare edit form. (3) Reissuing a certificate now preserves the original as-issued USI snapshot and RTO-identity snapshot (C-P2-1), so a faithful copy shows exactly what the original showed. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100394. — prior v5.9.393 student My Certificates nav link + dashboard block. students now get a persistent "My Certificates" link in the plugin navigation (local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation previously returned nothing for students, so their only link was buried on their Moodle profile page). The link points to the certificate portal (mycerts.php), which enforces its own access control so a student only ever sees their own certificates. A companion Dashboard block (block_rtocompliance_mycerts, delivered separately) shows a student their issued certificates with one-click download on login. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100393. — prior v5.9.392 removed Moodle account creation from Backfill. "Backfill Student Records" no longer creates Moodle {user} accounts (user_create_user removed). A NAT student with no existing Moodle account is now SKIPPED and reported ("no Moodle account — an administrator must create one first, then re-run Backfill"). Backfill now only READS Moodle users and writes the plugin's own student profile + demographics for students who already have an account. Combined with v5.9.387, the plugin creates/deletes NOTHING in Moodle core (no enrolments, no completions, and now no user accounts) — it only reads them. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100392. — prior v5.9.391 NAT demographic propagation regression fix. After a NAT import the AVETMISS demographic data now flows into the student profile again: (1) the finalize step now automatically refreshes the demographic fields (DOB, sex, suburb/state, Indigenous status, labour force, highest school level, language at home, country of birth, disability flag, prior-education flag, at-school flag) on EXISTING student profiles from the freshly-staged NAT00080 data — writing ONLY to the plugin students table (no Moodle user/enrolment/completion writes), so it is constraint-safe; a staged value only overwrites when it is real (never wipes good data with an AVETMISS "not stated" placeholder). This restores propagation that had lived inside the now-disabled auto-enrol handlers. (2) The manual "Backfill Student Records" step was silently dropping 8 core demographics to defaults because its staging SELECT omitted them — the SELECT now pulls all demographic columns, so a backfill writes the full profile. (3) Cert render-time backstop now also blocks the NRT logo on 'attendance' certs (matches the template catalogue's forbidden_for). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100391. — prior v5.9.390 cert-template polish F4/F5/F6. (F4) render-time compliance backstop — the renderer now drops any element forbidden for the cert type before it reaches the PDF (NRT logo never on a Record of Results or non-accredited Completion; USI never on a Testamur or Statement of Attainment), backing up the approval-time validation against pinned/override/legacy designs. (F5) certificate PREVIEW now applies the template's per-template designjson.overrides{} exactly as the real issue path does, so previews are faithful for override-using templates. (F6) the Test Certificate now uses its own dummy verify token and placeholder USI instead of an empty token + the logged-in admin's live USI. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100390. — prior v5.9.389 CERTIFICATE-TEMPLATE INTEGRITY (F1 as-issued RTO snapshot / F2 approved-only pinned template / F3 block issuance on blank RTO details). (F1) each certificate now snapshots the RTO identity settings (legal name, provider code, signatory name/title, AQF statement) at issue time into a new certs.issuesnapshot column and the renderer renders from that snapshot, so a later change to those settings cannot retroactively rewrite an already-issued certificate (mirrors the USI snapshot). (F2) pick_for_cert() renders the pinned template ONLY if it is still status='approved', so an in-progress/unvalidated draft edit can no longer leak onto an already-issued certificate on re-download (it falls back to the current approved template). (F3) issuance is now refused — interactively (non-bypassable) and programmatically — when mandatory RTO details (legal name, national provider code, authorised signatory) are not configured, preventing certificates that render those AQF-required fields blank; the "ready to issue" validator surfaces the same gap. Savepoint 2026073100389. — prior v5.9.388: ASQA PRACTICE-GUIDE AUDIT P1 REMEDIATION PART 2 + ASQA COMPLIANCE MAPPING. Feature code on the v5.9.387 schema: (1) VALIDATION (Std 1.5) — validator-independence declaration is required to complete a validation, and completion is blocked without it; a five-year validation cycle now computes/stores nextduedate (2 years for high-risk), with OVERDUE/DUE-SOON flags and a Coverage-Gaps list of on-scope products with no current validation; assessment outcome + rectification actions are captured. (2) WORKFORCE (Std 3.2) — "Working Towards" trainers now record a start date and an enforced 2-year TAE completion deadline; manager sign-off is blocked for a blank credential or a lapsed working-towards window; supervisors must hold a full, unexpired credential; a Supervision overdue/due-soon alert lists at-risk working-towards trainers. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT (Std 2.3/2.4/2.6) — per-student support / reasonable-adjustment / wellbeing records now persist server-side in local_rtocompliance_supportnotes (retained, shared, auditable) instead of browser localStorage. (4) QUALITY INDICATORS (Std 4.4) — the ad-hoc surveys are replaced with the official AQTF Learner & Employer Questionnaires (items tagged to their scales) and qi_report renders a proper QI Annual Summary (indicator + scale scores, response rates); the QI export is now the aggregate summary, not identifiable per-respondent rows. (5) NEW "ASQA Compliance Mapping" left-menu page (asqa_standards_map.php) — every 2025 Standard mapped to the feature that supports it with an honest Covered/Partial/Gap status (Std 4.3/4.4 self-assurance). No schema changes beyond savepoint 387. Savepoint 2026073100388.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.450'; // v5.9.450 BUTTON HOVER CONTRAST audit + save-payload robustness. (1) CONTRAST — every Bootstrap button variant used in the plugin now has an explicit, readable hover so no button renders light text on a light background. The reported case was the outline buttons on the Certificate Templates action column (Edit / Preview / Make default): those sit OUTSIDE the .rtoc-main-content container, so the plugin's scoped hover rules did not reach them and Bootstrap's default white-on-light-amber (btn-outline-warning) showed through. New broadly-scoped rules cover warning, danger, info, light, dark and every outline form (warning/info/success), plus a safety net for outline-primary/secondary outside the main container. (2) SAVE — the hidden design field is now kept continuously in sync on every edit (not only on the submit event), so the layout payload can never be empty at submit time even if a stale cached build is momentarily active; the server message is clearer too. IMPORTANT: purge caches after installing so the new JavaScript is served. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400450. — prior v5.9.449 CERT EDITOR SAVE FIX + LAYOUT RULES across ALL certificate types. (1) MALFORMED DESIGN PAYLOAD on Save draft is fixed: when the browser could not serialise the layout it silently posted an empty field and the server rejected it as "malformed design payload". The editor now serialises with a never-throwing, circular-safe pass and refuses to post an empty/invalid payload (clear message instead), and the server message now distinguishes an empty payload from invalid JSON and reassures that the saved copy is untouched. (2) LAYOUT RULES applied to every cert type, for both new starters and existing saved templates (via the shared normaliser the renderer and editor both run, so the PDF and canvas stay in sync — no DB migration, no divergence): the small DATE and AUTHORISED PERSON caption labels are removed (the issue date and signatory name/title still print); the NRT logo, organisation seal and verification QR now render 30mm tall with aspect preserved and centred inside their box (never stretched). (3) UNITS TABLE: all text is a minimum of 12pt including the table; the unit code column is widened to hold a 12pt code on one line; long unit titles now WRAP onto a second line instead of shrinking. Canvas preview updated to match. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400449. — prior v5.9.448 AUTO-CREATE / ARCHIVE-VERSIONS CLARITY + name cleanup. (1) The Auto-Create Qualifications page builds ONE product per national qualification code, so every semester/archive copy of a qualification (S1 26, S2 26, S1 27 ...) collapses into that single code — which is why only one row per code appears and it skips once a product already exists. A prominent callout (and button) now routes admins to the Semester Intake Builder, which lists every semester/archive sub-category as its own Draft product with its exact course list, reading the qualification code and title from the parent category. This closes the main point of confusion about where the archive versions are built. (2) NAME CLEANUP — when a Moodle category named the code inside brackets, e.g. "Diploma of Customs Broking (TLI50816)", stripping the code left an empty "()" so detected names printed as "Diploma of Customs Broking ()". The code extractor now removes any now-empty bracket pair and collapses the doubled space, fixing detected names on Auto-Create, the Semester Intake Builder and everywhere category names are resolved. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400448. — prior v5.9.447 STYLE A UNITS TABLE for the Statement of Attainment and Record of Results. The unit list on both certificates now renders as one shaded three-column table — Unit Code (left) | Unit Title (left-aligned) | Completion Date (centre) — with a coloured header bar (white bold headings), zebra-striped alternating rows and thin cell borders, drawn in TCPDF (solid fills and borders, no gradients). A new Certificate Setting, "Units table header colour" (colour picker), sets the header-bar fill and defaults to the Moodle site primary / brand colour; header text prints white for contrast. The per-unit Completion Date is wired from the compliance register (the unit result / activity end date, falling back to the start date), captured at issue time and back-filled from the register for older certificates in a single query. Both cert types share one renderer: the RoR ror_table field and the SoA dynamic qualification.units field both route to it, so existing templates pick up the new table with no template edits. The in-editor canvas preview was updated to draw the identical shaded table (header colour, columns and zebra) so what you design matches the issued PDF. All certificate text now has a 12pt minimum floor for readability (previously many fields rendered at 9 to 10pt); the field height cap still contains anything that would otherwise overflow. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400447. — prior v5.9.446 CODE-FIRST / NO-DASH CONVENTION for unit & qualification labels. Everywhere a unit or qualification code and its title were shown together they now render as "CODE Title" — code first, title second, a single space between, no hyphen or em-dash. Fixed in the certificate renderer (the Statement of Attainment / Record of Results unit lists and their sample previews) and across the plugin UI (qualification dropdowns on Student Results and Generate Certificates, the My Certificates and public verify pages, Qual Builder delete confirmations + audit log, unit delete confirmation, RPL unit label, skipped-programcodes list, TAS heading + PDF/DOCX exports, suitability PDF). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100446. — prior v5.9.445 CSS SCOPING FIX (help card lost styling on admin pages) + SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER now reads the qualification from the PARENT category. (1) CSS — the plugin's help card and other scoped styles are scoped to the body class "path-local-rtocompliance". Pages that use admin_externalpage_setup() have their pagetype (and therefore the auto-generated "path-*" body class) overridden to an "admin-*" value, so that class was absent and every scoped rule silently failed (the sidebar still styled because its CSS is unscoped). Certificate Templates was the reported case; the same latent gap affected 12 admin pages in total — cert_templates, cert_template_edit, cert_test, nat_validate, nominalhours_import, reconcile, trainer_dashboard, usi_settings, foe_audit, foe_bulk_audit, recovery_analyzer, regression_test — each now calls $PAGE->add_body_class('path-local-rtocompliance') before output so the scoped CSS applies (the four remaining admin_externalpage files — qi_export, tas_export, settings, version — are file exports/config, not rendered pages). Purge caches after install. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — the qualification code and title are now read deterministically from the semester sub-category's PARENT category (parent = qualification code + title, the sub-category = the semester), not guessed from the unit set; the exact list of unit-code courses under the sub-category becomes the intake's units/courses. Where a semester has no coded parent the code box is left blank for the admin to set once. The preview shows the parent-derived qualification title beside each code box. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100445. — prior v5.9.444 SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — a separate qualification product per semester intake. New tool (qualbuilder_semester.php) + helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_semester_intakes() / local_rtocompliance_create_semester_intakes(). It scans every Moodle category that holds unit-code courses (e.g. "Archive - 23 DCB S1"), treating each as a semester intake: the category name becomes the product streamname, the unit codes parsed from the course names become its units, and those courses are linked (extra copies as archive variants). Because the archive category names carry a semester but NOT a qualification code, the code is AUTO-SUGGESTED by matching the intake's unit set to existing products (best overlap, with a version-letter-stripped fallback) and is editable per row so the admin sets it once per qualification era where it can't be inferred. A preview lists every detected intake with its semester, unit/course counts, detected unit codes and the suggested code; on confirm it creates one Draft product per ticked intake (qualcode + streamname). Duplicates (same qualcode + streamname) are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin's own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — no Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments are created or changed. Linked from the Qualification Builder header alongside Auto-Create and Recover Unmapped Completions. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100444. — prior v5.9.443 AUTO-CREATE — COURSE MAP IS NOW THE DEFAULT SOURCE + bigger info-box text. The "From Category Tree" scan returned nothing on this site because units here are delivered as COURSES (e.g. "TLIR4001 & TLIR4002 … MSP") under semester/archive categories, not as unit-code sub-categories — so the tree-walk found no unit layer. The Course Map already captures course → qual → unit correctly (seeded from those same categories and courses), so Auto-Create now defaults to the "From Course Map" source and the instructions say so; the Category-Tree tab is kept but explained as only for sites whose units are named sub-categories. Also: the page info boxes ("How this works" / "What this does") were too small — bumped to 15px (and the shared .rtoc-dob-sync-bar base font raised), and the empty-state on the Course Map source now points to Scan & Seed if the map is empty. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100443. — prior v5.9.442 CERTIFICATE EDITOR — ROOT-CAUSE FIX (canvas vs issued-PDF data divergence) + RECOVER UNMAPPED COMPLETIONS TOOL. CERT EDITOR: the meta-root-cause of the recurring "wrong preview" complaints was that the drag-and-drop CANVAS and the issued-PDF renderer used DIFFERENT data sources — on default load the canvas painted each field its own hardcoded per-field catalogue placeholder (meta.sample) while every prior fix (RTO identity v5.9.409/412, statement dedupe v5.9.406/407) only ever touched the PDF renderer's sample_payload, which the canvas did not use. Fixes: (1) CANVAS-DATA-UNIFY — the editor JS resolver now renders the SAME coherent sample record the issued PDF uses (a key present in sample_payload wins, even when intentionally blank), so unrelated placeholders (a First-Aid skill-set line, a Business qualification, an "[insert language]" token) no longer stack on the canvas and the skill-set/optional statements that should be blank now are. (2) STALE AMD BUILD — amd/build/cert_template_editor.js was 37 lines behind source (missing the whole real-RTO-identity code path), so dev/debug sites served the old behaviour; both build artifacts (.js and .min.js) are regenerated from source. (3) RTO NAME PLACEHOLDER — the editor canvas AND the issued renderer now fall back to the real Moodle site name (the RTO's own name) when the RTO legal name has not been set in RTO Settings, instead of showing the catalogue placeholder "National Compliance Training" (canvas) or the generic "Training Organisation" (issued). Set your legal name in RTO Settings for the exact wording. (4) "[insert language]" — the sample-preview payload hardcoded the literal "[insert language]" fill-in token; it now reads the languagestatement setting (or blank), matching the issued path. (5) REQUIRED DOT — the red filled "!" circle on required palette fields read as an error; it is now a clear amber "Required" pill (it always meant "required for this certificate type", never an error). RECOVER TOOL: new "Recover Unmapped Completions" page (qualbuilder_recover.php) + helpers scan the completions the sync could not map, propose old→current unit-code mappings (version-letter drops auto-ticked; single-unit name matches flagged for review), and on confirm write them to the supersededunitmap setting so the next Sync credits them; codes with no current unit are listed separately (build the superseded qual first). Also: "Auto-Create from Categories" scans the category tree or the Course Map. Writes only plugin config/tables; no Moodle-core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100442. — prior v5.9.441 RELEASE-PIPELINE FIX — cleared the one failed check. qualbuilder_autocreate.php inline select-all script used anonymous JS closures written as the flagged no-space form; rewritten to the spaced closure form (and the one-line if given braces) so the coding-style scanner no longer reports a spacing finding in that file. Pure coding-style change to one inline script; no functional, behavioural or schema change. The 6 advisory warnings are pre-existing and unchanged (ALL-CAPS lang values such as ABN/ASQA on legacy strings, capability-check advisories on read-only report/editor pages, the audited unserialize-with-allowed-classes call in process_enrolment_task, and inline-comment/one-statement style notes across legacy files). Savepoint 2026073100441. — prior v5.9.440 PARKED ITEMS BUILT. (1) NAT IMPORT OUTCOME / RESULTS GRID — a register enrolment that exists but has no recorded AVETMISS outcome (blank / NULL / "00") now renders on Student Results as a clear "Not yet assessed" dash instead of a confusing "?"; blank outcomes are normalised at both the on-screen grid and the CSV export, and any present-but-unrecognised code now shows as itself rather than "?". The NAT results importer VALID_OUTCOMES set gained "41" (incomplete — RTO closure), a valid AVETMISS code the parser accepts and the grid can display that was previously collapsed to "00". (2) MISSING-AVETMISS-DATA STUDENT PROMPT — a logged-in student whose AVETMISS profile is incomplete now sees a modal (site-wide, once per browser session) listing the fields still needed, with a "Complete my details now" button to their self-service profile and a tip that certificates can be downloaded from the profile menu (top-right initials). It reads only the student own row (one lookup by userid), is never shown to admins/guests or on the profile page itself, and is injected via the existing before_footer hook using an external CSP-safe script (js/avetmiss_prompt.js) so no inline script is blocked; the primary button is a plain link so the profile is always reachable. (3) HELP-CARD TEXT SIZE — the What / Why / How / Key-Features card body was enlarged from 14px to 15.5px (tabs 13px to 14px) for readability. (4) audit.php gained first-time How-to steps — the one page missed in the v5.9.438 rewrite — so help-step coverage is now complete. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100440. — prior v5.9.439 AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" NOW RESOLVES REAL NAMES (no more code-as-name). The v5.9.438 Course-Map source stored the unit code as the unit name because the course_map table holds only codes. Fixed: local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() now builds a CODE→name map from your Moodle category names (every category whose name carries a code — qualification categories like "TLI50321 — Diploma of …" and unit leaf categories like "TLIX0036 — Load and unload goods" — contributes its title, longest-name-wins; unit/qual titles are national so one map is safe) and uses it for BOTH the qualification name and each unit name. So building from the Course Map now produces the same real qualification and unit titles as the Category-Tree source, fully offline — reusing the category-name resolution instead of defaulting to the code. The training.gov.au enrichment option still overrides with official TGA names/packaging when ticked. Structure still comes from your existing, confirmed course_map rows; only the naming was reused rather than reinvented. Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100439. — prior v5.9.438 HELP-STEP REWRITE COMPLETED (ALL PAGES) + AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" SOURCE. (1) The v5.9.437 "How to use it" rewrite was extended from 40 to ~90 pages — every remaining left-menu page, editor and sub-page now shows the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence naming its real on-screen controls (cert issue/email/generate, template editor, TAS editor/consultation, transitions, trainer dashboard/voccomp, validation & validator editors, student support/declaration, fee/insurance/third-party/governance/risk editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, marketing, surveys/QI/AI reports, reconcile, deadlines, alerts, audit log, ASQA/compliance maps, practice guides, student portal pages, and more). All applied via the same per-page 'how' override, leaving What/Why/Key Features untouched. (2) AUTO-CREATE now offers a SOURCE toggle — "From Category Tree" or "From Course Map". The new read-only helper local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() groups your existing (and already-confirmed) Course Map rows by qualification code, links each unit's delivery courses, and reads the qualification name from its Moodle category — so you can build products straight from the mapping you already have (unit names default to the code unless training.gov.au enrichment is ticked). Same safety guarantees: Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle categories/courses/accounts/enrolments touched. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100438. — prior v5.9.437 AUTO-CREATE QUALIFICATIONS + FIRST-TIME HELP-STEP REWRITE. (1) AUTO-CREATE — new "Auto-Create from Categories" tool in the Qualification Builder (qualbuilder_autocreate.php) scans the Moodle category tree (parent category = qualification code + title, leaf sub-category = unit code + name, delivery courses underneath) and builds Qual Builder products with their units and course links in one pass. It shows a READ-ONLY preview (qual code, name, units found, courses linked, New vs Already-exists) with per-qual checkboxes and an optional best-effort training.gov.au enrichment (official name, packaging counts, AQF level, core/elective type, per-unit names) that falls back to the category names when the platform API is unavailable. New helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_categories_for_quals() (read-only) and local_rtocompliance_autocreate_quals_from_scan(). Products are created as Draft; duplicate qual codes are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — it never creates or changes Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments. (2) HELP CARDS — the "How to use it" tab on 40 primary pages was rewritten from each page real UI into the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence, naming the actual on-screen controls (e.g. USI setup: enter TOID, choose the machine-credential keystore, type the keystore password, tick EVTE, click Save credential; Course Map: click Scan & Seed All Quals, filter, confirm rows), replacing the older generic wording. Applied as a per-page 'how' override merged over the existing help overlay, so the What / Why text and Key Features are unchanged. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100437. — prior v5.9.436 CRITICAL — RESTORED DEAD ACTION BUTTONS + NAVBAR AVATAR ALIGNMENT. (1) ROOT CAUSE of the Student Results grid staying empty / 0 Competent: the "Sync results from Moodle completions" button POSTs action=reconcile_completions, but qualbuilder_results.php read that value with PARAM_ALPHA, which strips the underscore to "reconcilecompletions", so the equality check never matched and the completion reconciler never ran — the register was never populated from Moodle completions even though thousands of completions qualified (both a mapped unit AND a welded student). Changed that read to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT so the button actually fires. (2) SAME-CLASS SWEEP — qual_cert_hub.php (issue_all_pending / scan_missed / retry_autocert / retry_all_failed / refresh_stats / process_queue), qualbuilder_courses.php (add_archive / remove_archive), suitability_bulk.php (fill_gaps) and student_support.php (save_support_state) each read an underscore-bearing action value with PARAM_ALPHA and were likewise silent no-ops (their buttons did nothing); all changed to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT. This is the same defect earlier patched in students.php / data_import.php. (3) NAVBAR AVATAR — the plugin styles.css HEADER RESET forced the theme user-menu toggle to display:inline-block with align-items:unset, dropping the theme flex vertical-centring so the round user-initials avatar rose to the text baseline (it "jumped up") only inside RTO Compliance; restored inline-flex + align-items:center so it centres like the theme intends. Purge caches after install for the CSS change. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100436. — prior v5.9.435 RELEASE-PIPELINE FOLLOW-UP — cleared the remaining blockers + error. (1) GPL: trainer_dashboard.php and usi_settings.php carried a truncated placeholder licence header; the full GNU GPL licence body is now restored at the very top of both. (2) The five public token endpoints (verify, webhook, survey_respond, suitability_form, student_usi_verify) now carry an explicit login guard that requires a Moodle login when the request arrives with no valid token / webhook key — so the scanner sees an explicit login call while genuine QR / token / machine access continues to work (student_usi_verify, a logged-in staff endpoint, also gained a manage-capability check). (3) Reworded the v5.9.434 changelog text so it no longer contains substrings the scanner mis-reads as a superglobal / dangerous-call / spacing finding in version.php. No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100435. — prior v5.9.434 RELEASE-PIPELINE COMPLIANCE (Marketplace blockers + errors). Structure: added LICENSE (GPL v3), README.md, and thirdpartylibs.xml (empty, declared). Boilerplate: added the standard Moodle GPL header + a phpdoc block with @package local_rtocompliance / @copyright / @license to every PHP file that lacked them (177 files). Security: replaced direct POST-superglobal access with optional_param helpers in data_import.php and student_declaration_send.php (and reworded a superglobal mention in a version.php comment); added an explicit require_login() to the 85 admin page files that only authenticated via admin_externalpage_setup() (public token pages such as verify/webhook/survey_respond/suitability_form/student_usi_verify carry a token-guarded login instead); hardened a deserialisation call with allowed_classes=>false. Coding style: fixed function-keyword spacing across PHP and JS, and removed the blank line after class/interface/trait opening braces (53 files). No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100434. — prior v5.9.433 CONSISTENT PAGE BANNER ON EVERY MAIN PAGE. Added the standard royal-blue page banner (the same .compliance-header gradient the dashboard/qual-builder/etc. already used) to the 46 left-menu and sub-pages that lacked one, so every page now opens with the same structure: royal-blue banner → What/Why/How/Key-Features help card → content. New reusable helper local_rtocompliance_page_banner(title, subtitle, actions) reuses the existing banner styling; each page passes its existing title expression so the banner always matches the breadcrumb, and duplicate in-page headings were removed where present. The help card auto-positions directly below the banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100433. — prior v5.9.432 HELP CARD — PREMIUM VISUAL RESTORE. Brought back the liked flashy design (brand blue→indigo gradient accent bar, glowing gradient icon chip with a WHITE icon that pops, filled segmented-control tabs where the active tab is the gradient, gradient numbered How-steps, card shading + hover lift) while keeping the good changes: icon-led Key Features (gradient chip + white check, not heavy number boxes) and the card sitting below the page banner. Removed the load animation entirely (the blur was what made a freshly-loaded card look washed out). Header icon is now a chip wrapping a centred 20px white icon (no more oversized/faint icon). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100432. — prior v5.9.431 HELP CARDS — EXPERT CSS PASS + FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT. (1) CLEAN CSS — the card was over-styled: the slow blur-to-focus animation made a just-loaded page look washed-out/broken, and the numbered gradient badges were too heavy. Rebuilt: solid brand-blue accents (no washed gradients), crisp readable numbered How-steps, a quick NO-BLUR fade-in, clean underline tabs, and a lighter card. (2) KEY FEATURES USE ICONS — each Key Feature is now an icon-led row (check glyph + bold title + benefit) instead of a heavy numbered gradient box. (3) FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT — the button-level How-to steps and top-3 Key Features now cover 86 pages (up from 24), each written from the page''s actual UI by reading the source (real control labels throughout). (4) Retains v5.9.430''s banner-blue theming, distinct per-page icons, tab-aware settings cards, and below-the-banner positioning. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100431. — prior v5.9.430 HELP CARDS — MAJOR UPGRADE. (1) FOURTH TAB "KEY FEATURES" — each card now has What it is / Why it matters / How to use it / Key Features; the last highlights the top 3 time-saving or compliance features of the page as a numbered 1-2-3 list. (2) PAGE-SPECIFIC, BUTTON-LEVEL CONTENT — the How-to steps and Key Features for 24 primary pages were rewritten from the pages'' actual UI (real buttons/filters/columns, e.g. "Scan & Seed All Quals", "Verify via usi.gov.au", "Issue Pending", "Sync from completions"), layered over the base entries via a render-time overlay. (3) DISTINCT ICONS — every page/tab now shows a relevant icon (graduation, award, users, shield, map, key, etc.) instead of the same info glyph. (4) TAB-AWARE SETTINGS — the settings page''s eight tabs (RTO Details, Platform API, Certificates, USI Settings, Auto-Survey, ASQA 2025, State Funding, Maintenance) each get their own card via ?section=, instead of all sharing one. (5) RECOLOURED TO THE BANNER BLUE — the card now uses the plugin''s page-banner gradient (#1e3a8a→#1d4ed8→#3b82f6) for the accent bar, icon chip, filled active tab and numbered steps, so it matches the rest of the UI. (6) BELOW THE BANNER — the card now positions itself directly under the page''s main banner (was above it). (7) USI banner unified to the shared royal-blue banner (was an off-theme cyan). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100430. — prior v5.9.429 HELP-CARD STANDARD PILL → LINKS TO THE RELEVANT ASQA PRACTICE GUIDE. The standard/quality-area pill on each What/Why/How card is now a link that opens the relevant official ASQA 2025-Standards practice guide in a new tab (with an external-link glyph and a gradient hover), so a user can jump straight from the page to the authoritative guidance. New mapping helper local_rtocompliance_practice_guide_url() maps each page to its best-fit guide (Training, Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Feedback/Complaints & Appeals, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Leadership & Accountability, Fit & Proper, Risk Management, Continuous Improvement, Facilities/Resources, Integrity of NRT, Accountability) using the same official asqa.gov.au URLs already referenced by the plugin's Practice Guides page; pages with no single clear guide keep a plain pill. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100429. — prior v5.9.428 STANDARD 2.1 PRE-ENROLMENT DISCLOSURE REGISTER + SLOW FLOAT-IN HELP-CARD ANIMATION. (1) STANDARD 2.1 (closes the ASQA-map "partial") — the Marketing Information page is now a working pre-enrolment disclosure register: 13 mandatory disclosure items (training products, ALL fees, refunds, fee protection, entry requirements, USI, learner support, third-party arrangements, rights/obligations, complaints & appeals, recognition, completion outcome, privacy) each with a "provided" flag and a "where it is provided" field; a retained pre-payment fee/obligation acknowledgement confirmation; and a materials review date. A coverage bar shows how many items are disclosed. Persisted server-side in plugin config (no Moodle core writes, no schema change), gated by the manage capability (read-only otherwise), and audit-logged. The ASQA Compliance Mapping row for 2.1 moves from Partial to Covered. (2) HELP-CARD ANIMATION — the What/Why/How panel content now does a slow, gentle float-in reveal: each line lifts up out of a soft blur over ~1.15s (ease-out), and the "How" steps stagger in one after another for a graceful cascade; honours prefers-reduced-motion. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100428. — prior v5.9.427 PAGE HELP CARD — slower, more graceful tab-panel entrance. The What/Why/How panel fade-in was eased from 0.24s to 0.6s with a soft ease-out (cubic-bezier .16,1,.3,1) and a slightly larger rise, so switching tabs feels premium rather than snappy. CSS-only tweak; no other changes. Savepoint 2026073100427. — prior v5.9.426 PAGE HELP CARDS — PREMIUM REDESIGN + FULL PAGE COVERAGE. Builds on v5.9.425. (1) REDESIGN — the What/Why/How card was rebuilt on the plugin''s own design system for a bold, native look: the brand blue→indigo gradient (#3b82f6→#6366f1, the same one in the nav-header stripe) now drives a gradient accent bar, a glowing gradient icon chip, a FILLED segmented-control where the active tab lights up in the gradient, and gradient numbered "How" steps; the whole card gets subtle shading and a hover lift matching the plugin''s .stat-card motion. All colours/tokens come from the RTO Compliance token set, so it reads as native. (2) FULL COVERAGE — the help-content registry was extended from ~40 to ~50 pages so every meaningful page AND its edit/sub-pages carry the card (qualification/unit/course/validate editors, student profile/enrolments/support, suitability send/view/bulk, trainer/currency/voccomp/supervision/validation editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, governance/risk/fee/insurance/third-party/transition/location editors, issue/template/email/generate certificate pages, survey send/responses, TAS/consultation, alerts, AI analysis/usage, audit log, practice guides, plugin settings, compliance modules). Only the dashboard, the help pages themselves and internal diagnostics intentionally have no card. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100426. — prior v5.9.425 GUIDED PAGE HELP CARDS + HELP/SUPPORT & COMPLIANCE CONTENT REFRESH. (1) WHAT / WHY / HOW CARDS — every page now opens with a single, consistent orientation card directly under the breadcrumb: a "What it is / Why it matters / How to use it" tabbed card explaining the page, the compliance it supports and the steps to use it. One reusable renderer (local_rtocompliance_render_help_card) wired into the shared nav header and keyed by script filename, driven by a central content registry (local_rtocompliance_page_help_content) covering ~40 core pages — so a first-time user always gets the same clear, beautifully-formatted orientation and pages opt in simply by having a registry entry. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript, cannot fail after header output); scoped styling using the existing design tokens with dark-mode support. (2) HELP & SUPPORT / COMPLIANCE REFRESH — brought the Support Centre and How It Works up to date with everything shipped in v5.9.420–425: the "What''s New" panel now leads with v5.9.425 and lists the page help cards, RPL evidence rigour, pre-enrolment readiness, RPL assessor identity/fairness, end-to-end nominal hours, and the declutter pass; the RPL, Student Records, Qualification Builder and TAS module cards and their how-to steps were rewritten to describe the new capabilities; four new How-It-Works Key Questions (record RPL, check pre-enrolment, nominal-hours source, and the updated qualification setup) and three new FAQs (RPL capture, nominal hours, pre-enrolment readiness) were added; and the ASQA Compliance Mapping rows for 1.7 (RPL) and 2.2 (pre-enrolment) were updated to reflect the new evidence. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100425. — prior v5.9.424 RPL SUPERSEDED-UNIT MAPPING + EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX (Standard 1.2). Completes the RPL best-practice set. (1) SUPERSEDED → CURRENT UNIT MAPPING — the RPL/CT record now captures the superseded/prior unit the student actually holds and its TGA equivalence to the current unit being granted (Equivalent E / Not equivalent N / N-A). When an approved decision maps from a NOT-equivalent superseded unit, a non-blocking advisory reminds the assessor that a not-equivalent mapping cannot grant the current unit on its own — the gap must be assessed. This documents credit granted for a current unit on the basis of a superseded one. (2) EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX — a repeating table maps each item of evidence to the unit requirement (element / performance criterion / performance or knowledge evidence) it satisfies, with an assessor judgement (satisfactory / not satisfactory / further evidence needed). This evidences the rules of evidence — valid, sufficient, current, authentic — behind an RPL determination rather than a single free-text blob. Stored as normalised JSON (server-side decode → clean rows → re-encode) in a new evidencematrix column; rendered with add/remove rows and serialised to a hidden field on submit. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (supersededunitcode / unitequivalence / evidencematrix) via savepoint 2026073100424. No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.423 PRE-ENROLMENT READINESS SIGNAL (Standard 2). Consolidates the four ASQA pre-enrolment gates into an audit-ready view that reuses the existing suitability + USI + declaration data (no duplication of the mature suitability subsystem) and, in keeping with the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, SURFACES gaps rather than creating or blocking any Moodle enrolment. New helper local_rtocompliance_preenrolment_readiness(userid) evaluates: (1) suitability assessed — a completed suitability review with a genuine decision (a "not suitable" outcome is flagged, not passed); (2) student declaration signed — the pre-enrolment attestation signature (declaration_signed_at); (3) USI verified with the Registry; (4) pre-enrolment information provided — evidenced by the suitability form having been issued and completed. STUDENT PROFILE now shows a "Pre-enrolment readiness" card (per-gate tick / warn / not-met with dates and a "N of 4 met" header pill) above the demographics. COMPLIANCE HEALTH (Quality Area 2) gains a scored metric — "Pre-enrolment suitability not evidenced" — counting students who have recorded results but no completed suitability review, linking to the bulk suitability sender. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100423. — prior v5.9.422 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER PROCEDURAL-FAIRNESS + ASSESSOR IDENTITY. Closes the RPL best-practice gaps around WHO assessed and whether the student was told. (1) ASSESSOR IDENTITY (Standard 1.5) — the RPL/CT record now selects the assessor from the registered trainer workforce (writes assessoruserid, previously never captured — only a free-typed name was stored), so a decision is tied to a person whose TAE competence/currency the RTO evidences. The picker shows a live advisory for the chosen trainer: green when they hold a current TAE credential, amber when the TAE is missing or expired. A free-text name is retained only for an assessor not yet in the Trainers register, and the display name is auto-synced from the selected trainer. (2) OUTCOME COMMUNICATED (Standard 1.6, procedural fairness) — new fields record that the decision outcome was communicated to the student, the date, and the method (email/letter/interview/portal/phone); the date defaults to the decision date when left blank. The RPL/CT register gains a "Student Notified" column (Notified + date / Not notified / — while pending) so an auditor can see the decision-to-notification loop was closed. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (outcomecommunicated/…date/…method) via savepoint 2026073100422 (assessoruserid already existed). No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.421 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 2 (qualification total) + PHASE 4 (TAS volume of learning). (1) PHASE 2 — the Qualification Builder now rolls a real qualification nominal-hours total up from authoritative per-unit data. Because training.gov.au does NOT publish nominal hours, the builder previously showed a 0 total for most qualifications; it now batch-resolves any unit still at 0 from the plugin''s own reference table (local_rtocompliance_nominalhours, for the RTO''s reporting jurisdiction with NAT fallback) via a new batch mode on nominalhours_lookup.php (?codes=CODE1,CODE2,...), fills each unit, and repaints the "Nominal Hours — N hrs total" compliance card (which now also flags how many units are still missing hours so the admin knows to import the NCVER dataset or enter them). Resolution runs on page load, after a TGA load, and whenever a unit is added. (2) PHASE 4 — the TAS "Total Nominal Hours" (which drives the AQF volume-of-learning justification, Std 1.1/1.2) is now pre-filled from the qualification''s authoritative total via new helper local_rtocompliance_qual_nominal_total() (Qual Builder product total → live unit sum → per-unit reference-table sum). It only fills a genuinely empty value (a figure the RTO already entered is preserved), also seeds an empty Volume of Learning as a defensible lower bound, and the AI delivery-plan generator now uses this authoritative total as its fallback instead of a units×hrs/week guess when TGA returns none. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100421. — prior v5.9.420 DECLUTTER PASS 2 — remove duplicated / no-compliance-purpose UI noise. (1) STUDENT RESULTS — the eight summary stat tiles are reduced to the four that carry meaning; the removed four (Units in Product, Core Units, Elective Units, Total Unit Enrolments) were static structural reference counts that duplicated the qualification structure already listed below and only crowded the results command view. (2) DATA IMPORT — the "No Moodle accounts or enrolments are created" assurance was printed three times on the import screen (Step 1 card, Step 2 card, and the authoritative alert beneath the steps); the two card repetitions are removed and the single, more complete "No Moodle changes" alert is kept. (3) MARKETING INFORMATION — removed the "Related pages" cross-link card (every destination already lives in the left sidebar, so it was pure navigation duplication). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100420. — prior v5.9.419 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 + RPL CT-GATE HARDENING + SUPPORT PERSISTENCE + DECLUTTER. (1) NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 — when an enrolment is saved with AVETMISS scheduled hours left blank, they now default from the unit''s authoritative nominal hours (local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours), so NAT00120 reports a sensible value without manual entry; RPL (51) and Credit Transfer (60) default to 0 (no delivery). A value the admin actually typed is never overwritten. (2) RPL CREDIT-TRANSFER GATE HARDENED (Standard 1.7) — a CT outcome (60) is now posted to the results register only when BOTH an authenticated source (a verified USI transcript OR an uploaded source certificate/transcript on the record) AND the source qualification code are present; previously only the self-attested "USI transcript verified" checkbox was required, with no source document or code enforced. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT NOW PERSISTS SERVER-SIDE — the organisation-level support/adjustment/wellbeing selections were saved only in the browser (localStorage), so they were device-specific and invisible to an auditor on another machine (a Std 2.1/2.3 evidence gap); they now save to plugin config via a sesskey-guarded handler and load from the server. (4) DECLUTTER — the Students page''s auto-opening full-screen "USI not configured" modal (popped on every load, blocking the roster, duplicating the dashboard CTA) is replaced by an inline banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100419. (Continuing: nominal hours Phase 2 qual-total sum, RPL assessor-identity + outcome-communicated, declutter passes 2-3, and the pre-enrolment integration gate.) — prior v5.9.418 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 1. The Qualification Builder nominal-hours autofill previously called a private lms-labs.com endpoint. It now owns the data: a new reference table local_rtocompliance_nominalhours holds authoritative nominal hours per unit code per jurisdiction (NAT = the free NCVER nationally-agreed set as the national baseline, plus optional VIC/QLD/NSW/SA/WA/TAS/NT/ACT overrides). New internal endpoint nominalhours_lookup.php resolves a unit's hours from that table for the RTO's configured reporting jurisdiction (setting: Nominal hours — reporting jurisdiction) with NAT fallback, and the qualbuilder autofill JS now calls THIS endpoint instead of lms-labs.com. New admin import page (Import Nominal Hours) ingests the NCVER tab-delimited file (auto-detects tab/comma, skips header/non-code rows, upserts one value per unit per state) so the table can be bulk-populated; helper local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours()/upsert_nominalhours() added. Schema: new table (install.xml + upgrade savepoint 2026073100418). This is Phase 1 (authoritative source + internal lookup, removing the external dependency); Phase 2 (sum to qualification total), Phase 3 (default enrolment scheduled hours → NAT00120, 0 for RPL/CT) and Phase 4 (TAS amount-of-training) follow. Savepoint 2026073100418. — prior v5.9.417 DECLUTTER PASS 1. Removes duplicated/no-purpose UI noise so pages stay focused on compliance work. DASHBOARD: removed the static "Get Started Guide" 7-card row (it mirrored the live Setup Progress tracker exactly — same 7 steps/order/destinations); removed the "Quick Access" cards (all three destinations are in the sidebar and their stat lines just repeated the Overview tiles); removed the two full-width cross-link banners (Practice Guides + Compliance Map — both already in the sidebar). CERTIFICATES: removed the "Certificate Compliance — Clauses 9–14" explainer banner that restated the legislation above the register on every visit (the clause content lives on the ASQA Compliance Mapping page and Support centre; the actual compliance gates are unchanged). QUAL CERT HUB: removed the multi-paragraph "What is this / How to use it" tutorial card (incl. cache jargon), replaced with a one-line intro — the funnel columns and row actions are self-explanatory. This is pass 1 of a larger simplification program (audit produced a top-20 removal list); remaining declutter, plus nominal-hours Phase 1 and the RPL best-practice enhancements, follow in subsequent builds. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100417. — prior v5.9.416 PREMIUM DESIGN SYSTEM + RPL/CT EXPERT AUDIT-BLOCKING FIXES. (A) PREMIUM UI PASS — a design-system audit found the token layer had been rebuilt three times with conflicting values (primary colour, shadows, two neutral ramps), two competing badge systems, WCAG-AA contrast failures on solid info/success badges, oversized 16px/44px buttons with a gradient overridden to flat, and a .info-card.warning that rendered BLUE instead of amber. A single canonical design system is now appended to styles.css (scoped, reversible): one token set (re-points every legacy --rtoc-* var), a clean button scale (14px text, 8px radius, quiet outline/secondary, one focus-visible ring), one AA-safe soft-chip badge system, consistent card radius/shadow + tasteful hover lift, the amber warning-card fix, a global premium table-hover fallback, and empty/skeleton state utilities. PURGE CACHES after install to see it. (B) RPL/CREDIT-TRANSFER expert review — fixed the audit-blocking gaps: (1) REVERSAL RETRACTION — changing a previously-approved RPL/CT to Not Approved / Pending now retracts the posted competency (deletes the RPL-created enrolments row, or reverts an updated delivery row to 70) so a reversed decision can no longer leave a competent unit over-reporting into completion, certificates and NAT; (2) RPL DELIVERY MODE on the update path now reports mode 90 (not applicable) like the insert path — previously an RPL granted over an existing delivery enrolment kept classroom mode 10 and its delivered hours; (3) PRIVACY ERASURE — a right-to-erasure request now deletes the student's RPL evidence and credit-transfer source-certificate FILES (system-context fileareas keyed by rpl id), which were previously left in storage; the file subsystem is now declared in the privacy metadata. Also: RPL required-field enforcement (student + decision reason) from v5.9.415 retained. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100416. (Nominal hours: an expert research pass produced a phased wiring plan — import the NCVER nationally-agreed nominal-hours dataset into a per-unit/per-state reference table, repoint the qualbuilder autofill off lms-labs.com to an internal lookup, sum to the qual total, default enrolment scheduledhours from it (0 for RPL/CT), and feed the TAS amount-of-training — staged for approval, not in this build.) — prior v5.9.415 FULL-MENU AUDIT — HIGH/MEDIUM REMEDIATION BATCH. Follows the v5.9.414 blocker fixes. (1) TRAINER EVIDENCE now persists — trainer_currency.php and trainer_voccomp.php read the uploaded evidence file from the transient draft area but never called file_save_draft_area_files(), so files vanished on Moodle's draft cleanup and the stored id pointed at nothing; both now persist into permanent pluginfile-served fileareas (trainer_evidence / trainer_voccomp_evidence, separate areas so record ids can't collide) keyed by the record id. SCHEMA PARITY: the vocationalevidence column existed only in db/upgrade.php, so fresh installs lacked it and Trainers-page saves failed — it is now in db/install.xml too. (2) PROFILE WRITE-AUTH — student_profile.php allowed SAVING another student's record with only the read capability (viewall); saving now requires the manage (write) capability, editing your own profile still allowed. (3) SUPPORT DIAGNOSTICS REMOVED — support.php ran a v5.9.50 breadcrumb block on every Help-page load that wrote a /tmp file, spammed error_log, registered a shutdown handler and wrote the Moodle config table four times; removed entirely. (4) MANAGER DEAD-END — the fee-protection page linked managers to a site-config-only settings section (access denied); the link now only shows to users who can open it, with a note otherwise. (5) THIRD-PARTY — corrected the factually wrong "notify ASQA at least 30 days before entering a third-party arrangement" banner to the actual 2025 requirement (written agreement + retained quality oversight; NRT-logo / AQF-issuance prohibitions; student transparency). (6) QI COMPLETION RATE — qi_report.php computed the competency completion rate across mismatched cohorts (start-date denominator vs end-date numerator) and counted non-competent codes (52 RPL-not-granted, 70 continuing, etc.) as completions; it is now "of units that reached a FINAL outcome this year, the fraction that were competent (20/51/60/81)". (7) ASQA CLAUSE CONSISTENCY — the Risk page labelled risk management "Standard 4.3" while the authoritative ASQA Compliance Mapping and Support Centre use 4.2; the Risk page now says 4.2. (8) FEE-PROTECTION register now includes 'approaching threshold' students (>$1,200), which the previous >$1,500-only query excluded. No schema changes beyond adding the missing vocationalevidence column to install.xml (parity only). Savepoint 2026073100415. (Remaining catalogued for follow-up: student_support server persistence, viewsensitive gating, non-portable LIMIT in a few queries, RPL required-field enforcement, dashboard alert icons, and the USI local-verification client which is a separate staged project.) — prior v5.9.414 FULL-MENU AUDIT — 4 BLOCKERS FIXED. A deep 7-part investigation of every left-hand-menu section found four blocker-class defects, all now fixed: (1) CERTIFICATE INTEGRITY — the Student Results drill-down and the results-page cert-issuance guard (qualbuilder_results.php + ajax.php) counted AVETMISS outcomes 30 (competency not achieved/fail) and 40 (withdrawn) as "complete", so a student who failed or withdrew from every unit showed 100% progress with a working "Issue Certificate" button, and the server guard let the testamur/record issue. All six checks now use the competent-only set (20/51/60/81), so only genuinely-competent students count as complete and can be issued a qualification certificate. (2) SoA GATE BYPASS — the Multi-Unit Statement of Attainment issuer (soa_ajax.php) inserted the certificate directly, skipping the USI verified-gate, the RTO-settings gate and the as-issued snapshots that local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert() enforces; an SoA could be issued to a student with no / unverified USI. It now enforces the USI-verified gate (Clause 12) and RTO-identity gate BEFORE consuming credits, snapshots the verified USI + RTO identity onto the cert, and publishes to the verification registry. (3) NO-CORE-WRITES — three data-import actions (repairnames edits {user} name/email; backfill_records set {user}.idnumber; hide_archive_cats toggled {course_categories}.visible) still wrote to Moodle core and were reachable; they are now in the retired-action block list, so the plugin only READS Moodle and writes solely to its own tables with no reachable exception. (4) GOVERNANCE — governance_edit.php ignored the type=changes/adc parameter and always read/wrote the govpersons table, so Material Changes and the Annual Declaration of Compliance could never be created and editing one threw a fatal MUST_EXIST; the editor now has full forms for the materialchanges and adc tables. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100414. (Remaining HIGH/MEDIUM findings from the audit — trainer evidence-file persistence, student_support localStorage-only, viewsensitive USI gating, ASQA clause-number consistency, and others — are catalogued for follow-up builds.) — prior v5.9.413 USI SETUP-STATUS UNIFIED. The dashboard (index.php) judged USI setup from the LEGACY local-file config keys (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id), while the dedicated Machine Credential Setup page (usi_settings.php) judged it from the per-tenant PLATFORM status. So a SaaS RTO whose USI machine credential is stored on the platform (the recommended method) was shown a "USI verification is not yet set up" banner on the dashboard even though the setup page correctly reported "configured and ready" — it looked like the configuration had reset. New single source of truth local_rtocompliance_usi_is_configured() recognises BOTH supported methods: (a) per-tenant platform (apiurl + siteid + apikey set AND a credential uploaded/confirmed via the usi_cert_uploaded flag or a platform-pushed usi_certificate_path), and (b) legacy local-file (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id). The dashboard now uses it, so the banner only shows when USI genuinely is not configured by either method. Nothing about the USI credentials themselves was changed or reset — this was purely an inconsistent status check. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100413. — prior v5.9.412 EDITOR NOW INCORPORATES EVERY RTO-CONFIGURED VALUE (certificate code + phrases + descriptors). Extends the v5.9.409 real-identity map so the certificate editor canvas reflects ALL fixed, RTO-configured values from RTO/Certificate Settings — not just RTO name/code/signatory. Added: the CERTIFICATE CODE preview (cert.number) built from the RTO''s real certprefix + type code + year exactly as local_rtocompliance_generate_cert_number() does (e.g. CBF-SOA-2026-0001) instead of the generic CERT-2026-000123; the certificate footer (cert.footer); every ASQA mandatory phrase (aqf_statement, certify/attained statements, SoA intro/attained statements, Statement-of-Attainment and Record-of-Results headings, the NOT-A-TESTAMUR statement) using the RTO''s configured wording and falling back to the ASQA default when unset; and the optional descriptors (industry descriptor, occupational stream, apprenticeship statement, language statement, skill-set statement) which show the real configured value or fall through to the catalogue placeholder when blank. These paint on the canvas regardless of the "Show sample data" toggle because they are fixed RTO values, not per-student data (student name, units, dates and the QR code are deliberately left as sample/dynamic). Confirmed all six branding IMAGE fields (RTO logo, NRT logo, AQF logo, compliance/state logo, organisation seal, signatory signature) were already painting from the uploaded files via the v5.9.406–409 getter + pluginfile-serving fixes. No settings/config keys changed; no schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100412. — prior v5.9.411 NO-CORE-WRITES ON CERT GENERATION (C-P2-6) + NAT CONTINUING-OUTCOME FIX (A-P2-3). (1) NO-CORE-WRITES — certificate generation no longer toggles the core {user}.suspended field. The three issuance paths (generate_course_certs.php, generate_qual_certs.php, qual_cert_hub.php) each ran $DB->set_field(''user'',''suspended'',0,...) when an admin ticked an "Activate account" checkbox during generation, coupling Moodle account activation to certificate issuance and writing to a core table. Those writes AND their checkboxes/columns are removed; suspended students are still shown (badged, read-only) and can still be issued certificates — activating an account is now left as an explicit decision in Moodle user administration. (The explicit admin "activate" action on the Students page and the rollback-suspend in data_import remain, as those are deliberate user-initiated actions, not side-effects of issuing a certificate.) (2) A-P2-3 NAT FIX — when the AVETMISS NAT00120 export coerces a blank/''00'' outcome to ''70'' (Continuing activity), it now also reports the record as OPEN (activity end date = reporting period end) instead of emitting ''70'' together with a recorded completion end date, which is internally inconsistent and NCVER flags. The AVETMISS Validation page still surfaces these records so the RTO enters the real outcome. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100411. — prior v5.9.410 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER EVIDENCE UPLOADS + RESULTS/CERT TIE-IN CHECK. (1) FILE UPLOADS — the RPL & Credit Transfer record form now has real file uploads: a "Source certificate / transcript (from the issuing RTO)" uploader on credit-transfer records (attach the other RTO''s testamur / SoA / RoR / USI transcript that authenticates the transfer) and an "RPL evidence files" uploader on RPL records (portfolio, references, prior quals, observation records). Both accept multiple files (PDF/image/Office/text, 20MB each), list already-uploaded files with download + remove links, are stored in the Moodle File API keyed by the record id, served through local_rtocompliance_pluginfile (new fileareas rpl_evidence + ct_sourcecert, manage capability), and cleaned up when the record is deleted. Each uploader carries plain-English ASQA instructions (Standard 1.6 for RPL, Clause 1.7 / Clause 12 for credit transfer). The old free-text "Evidence Files" box is retained as optional notes for evidence held outside the system. (2) TIE-IN VERIFICATION — deep-audited that RPL (outcome 51) and Credit Transfer (outcome 60), written to the results register by local_rtocompliance_apply_rpl_outcome(), are treated as COMPETENT across every relevant path: Student Results (student_profile.php, qualbuilder_results.php), qualification-completion detection (check_full_qual_completion, get_completed_units_for_qual, process_enrolment_task, observer, completion_reconciler, certificate_validator) and ALL certificate paths (generate_qual_certs, qual_cert_hub, generate_course_certs, and the renderer which labels 51=RPL Granted / 60=Credit Transfer on the SoA/RoR). Fixed the one gap the audit found: the Students dashboard "Competency Achieved (Units)" card counted only outcome 20 — it now counts 20/51/60/81 so RPL/CT units are included. Also corrected the scrambled outcomeidentifier help text to the accurate NCVER code meanings. No schema changes (files use the Moodle File API; the rpl table already had studentid/rpltype/usitranscriptverified). Savepoint 2026073100410. — prior v5.9.409 EDITOR BRANDING NOW ACTUALLY RENDERS (real root cause). The certificate editor paints the RTO logo / NRT logo / CEO signature / organisation seal in the canvas as <img src="pluginfile…"> URLs, but local_rtocompliance_pluginfile() only served three fileareas (cert_template_bg, cert_template_image, rto_branding). The assets uploaded via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings live in admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas (logo, nrt_logo_file, aqf_logo_file, organisation_seal_file, compliance_logo_1/2, ceo_signature_file, secondary_logo, cert_background_file) — NONE of which the handler served — so every branding image request 404'd and the canvas showed an empty box, even though the issued PDF rendered the logos fine (the PDF reads the file straight off disk, bypassing pluginfile entirely). The pluginfile handler now serves those branding fileareas (system context, managecerttemplates capability), so the editor canvas finally matches the issued certificate. This is the missing piece behind the v5.9.406 getter fix: the getters resolved the correct file and produced a URL, but that URL was not servable until now. (2) EDITOR SHOWS REAL RTO IDENTITY — the canvas now always paints the RTO's own configured values for rto.name, rto.code, signatory.name, signatory.title and aqf_statement (independent of the "Show sample data" toggle), because these are fixed RTO-identity values, not per-student sample data. Previously the canvas showed the generic catalogue placeholder ("National Compliance Training / 50918") whenever sample data was off, which read as "the editor isn't pulling RTO settings" even though issued certificates were always correct. Verified the issued-certificate payload (resolve_payload) sources every field correctly: rto.name/rto.code/signatory/aqf_statement from the issue-time snapshot then live config; student name/USI, qualification code/name, dates and cert number from the cert + student records; mandatory phrases from config with ASQA defaults. Purge all caches after install. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100409. — prior v5.9.408 TEMPLATE DELETE + DEACTIVATE CONTROLS. Adds two admin controls to the Certificate Templates list so a template can be cleared out and regenerated without digging through statuses: (1) DELETE — a Delete button now appears on EVERY template row regardless of status (including the active one), backed by a new force_delete() path + 'forcedelete' action (the audit-safe delete() that only removed drafts/archived is kept for programmatic callers). Deleting the active template is safe: issuance and preview fall back to the built-in ASQA starter until a new template is activated. Uploaded background/per-field-image files are cleaned up. Confirm prompt is extra-strong (and states the active-template fallback) since it is permanent. (2) MAKE NON-ACTIVE — a new deactivate() method + 'deactivate' action + "Make non-active" button shown on the currently active template, which clears the active flag WITHOUT archiving (the template stays approved and one-click re-activatable). New lang strings: cert_template_deactivate_btn, cert_template_confirm_deactivate, cert_template_action_ok_deactivated. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100408. — prior v5.9.407 SANITISE EXISTING SAVED CERT TEMPLATES (retro-fix for already-saved templates). v5.9.406 fixed the STARTER (new templates) and the RENDER path, but a template already saved in the database kept its old fields — so an existing Statement of Attainment still showed the duplicate/overlapping "form part of" + "completion of course" statements AND still carried the "Verify at: <url>" text field. A new upgrade step (savepoint 2026073100407) now rewrites every saved cert-template design to match a fresh starter: it drops every qualification.completionofcoursestatement field (redundant — the single "form part of" line is the ASQA statement), drops every authenticity_measure text field (QR-only default; the mandatory QR code stays and satisfies the authenticity requirement), and widens the surviving "form part of" box for a clean two-line wrap. Fully guarded (a bad design row is skipped, an unchanged design is left untouched); RTOs can drag the "Authenticity measure" field back on if they want the URL text. This is what makes an ALREADY-SAVED template pick up the QR-only + single-statement fixes without a manual "Reset to starter". IMPORTANT after install: run Site administration → Development → Purge all caches (the editor JS and branding checks are cached). NOTE on branding: the editor now paints the real RTO logo / NRT logo / signature / seal from RTO Settings (v5.9.406 getter fix) — if a slot still shows a placeholder box after purging caches, that specific asset is not uploaded under Certificate Settings for that cert type. No schema changes (data-only design rewrite). Savepoint 2026073100407. — prior v5.9.406 CERTIFICATE EDITOR FIXES + QR-ONLY DEFAULT + CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT. (1) EDITOR BRANDING (critical) — the certificate editor showed "[RTO logo]" / "[NRT logo]" / "[CEO signature image]" / "[Org seal]" text placeholders instead of the real artwork whenever the RTO had uploaded those assets via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings, because the editor's branding-URL getters only looked in the FA_BRANDING pseudo-itemid area and never the admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas where the settings pages actually store them (the issued PDF found them via resolve_compliance_asset_path()'s fallback chain, so the canvas and the print diverged). New get_branding_display_url() mirrors the renderer's exact chain (FA_BRANDING → settings filearea → bundled pix) and now backs get_branding_logo/signature/sta/nrt/aqf/org_seal_url(); the editor host now also passes the NRT, AQF and STA logo URLs to the JS (previously only logo/signature/seal were), and the editor canvas paints nrt_logo/aqf_logo/state_training_authority_logo from them. (2) SoA COMPLIANCE STATEMENT — the Statement of Attainment starter carried BOTH "These competencies form part of {code} {name}" AND the near-identical "These competencies were attained in completion of {code} course in {name}", auto-built from the same qualification and stacked 5-7mm apart, so they overlapped into an unreadable block. The redundant "completion of course" statement (which is for accredited short courses, not qualifications) is removed from the default starter (still draggable from the palette), the single "form part of" statement box is widened for clean two-line wrap, and the descriptors are re-spaced; the renderer AND sample preview now also suppress the completion statement whenever the form-part-of line is present, so templates already saved with both fields render only the correct one. (3) QR-ONLY DEFAULT — the "Verify at: <url>" authenticity_measure text field is removed from all eight starter templates; the mandatory verification QR code (auto-added by ensure_mandatory_fields, and already accepted by the validator as a valid authenticity measure) is the default, and RTOs can drag the URL text back on if they want it. (4) CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT — editor font sizing now converts points→pixels with the correct 0.3528×BASE_SCALE factor (was a hardcoded 1.33 that rendered every field ~26% oversized vs the PDF, throwing off drag-to-fit); the two inline <script> emitters on the editor page use JSON_HEX_* flags so author-entered text can't break out; the disabled-path return of send_certificate_email() now uses the canonical ok/email/error shape its callers read (was success/reason, causing an undefined-key warning and a blank failure message); and revoking a certificate now calls update_registry_status(token,'revoked') so a revoked cert's public QR verifies as Revoked instead of Valid. Also bundles the pending verify.php superseded-cert fix and the Student Results Moodle-completion effective-outcome wiring from the working set. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100406. (1) The Student Profile results section is rebuilt into a proper command view: a per-qualification progress hero (X of Y units competent, progress bar, outcome-breakdown chips), unit results GROUPED BY QUALIFICATION with a new Source column (which Moodle course each result came from), friendly colour-coded outcome badges, an outcome legend, and consolidated action buttons — "Issue Statement of Attainment", "Issue Qualification Certificate" (pre-fills the hub with the student's USI), and "Record / edit results". (2) OUTCOME LABELS: the raw AVETMISS placeholder "00" (and blank/10) now displays as "Not yet assessed" on the Enrolments page and profile (it is NOT Competent or NYC — it means no result recorded yet). Verified every outcome label against NCVER's official "Reporting a final outcome" fact sheet: code 70 is correctly "Continuing activity" (corrected two internal spots that read "Continuing enrolment"); 40/41/61/85 confirmed correct. (3) DATES: the Enrolments page Activity Start Date (and the Moodle-enrolment list dates) now include the YEAR (they used Moodle's short date format which omits it). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100405. — prior v5.9.404 left-hand menu fix. several admin pages rendered without the plugin's left sidebar because they called $OUTPUT->header() but never local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header(). Fixed on Moodle Course Map (course_map.php — reported), AVETMISS Validation (nat_validate.php), NAT Reconciliation (reconcile.php — replaced its bare rtoc-main-content div with the full layout-wrap + sidebar), and the Over-Enrolment / Bulk Over-Enrolment / Skipped Program Codes diagnostic pages. A full sweep confirms every remaining page without the sidebar is an intentional public token page (certificate verification, survey response, student declaration, student LLN form), which correctly have no admin menu. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100404. — prior v5.9.403 button text padding. long-label buttons (e.g. the full-width "Sync results from Moodle completions" side-panel button) were clipping because the plugin's button style forced white-space:nowrap with a fixed single-line height, so a long label in a narrow button ran to the edges. Buttons now allow their text to WRAP with height:auto (padding honoured), and small buttons (.btn-sm) get comfortable padding + a slightly smaller font — a single stylesheet fix that applies to every button in the plugin's main content area. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100403. — prior v5.9.402 backlog close-out. (final audit P2/P3s): (1) CREDIT-TRANSFER SOURCE AUTHENTICATION (Std 1.7) — a credit-transfer decision no longer posts a competency to the register unless the USI transcript is verified; otherwise it warns and holds (RPL is unaffected). (2) PRIVACY — complaint/appeal records now capture the complainant/appellant Moodle user id (resolved from email) so privacy export & erasure include them. (3) WORKFORCE CREDENTIALS — corrected the assessor skill-set picklist (removed the invalid TAESS00021, added the real TAESS00011 Assessor Skill Set and TAESS00019 Enterprise Trainer Skill Set, relabelled TAESS00024) and synced the help text; added advisory reminders that a TAS should be reviewed when its training product is superseded, and that TAE-package assessments need independent validation before the first cohort. (4) LABEL CORRECTNESS — the SoA unit-outcome filter now uses the correct AVETMISS codes (Credit transfer = 60; 81/82 shown as non-assessable, not "superseded competent"), and the Statement-of-Attainment "requires" text lists the correct competent set (20/51/60/81). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100402. — prior v5.9.401 procedural fairness + sensitive-data permission. (audit P2s). COMPLAINTS (Std 2.7): new respondent, respondent-response, and date-outcome-communicated fields so the RTO can demonstrate the party complained about was heard and all parties were told the outcome. APPEALS (Std 2.8): new original-decision-maker + reviewer-independence-confirmed + underlying-record-corrected fields; the appeal edit page now warns (advisory) when an upheld assessment appeal has not had its underlying record corrected, or when independence has not been confirmed. SENSITIVE DATA: a new local/rtocompliance:viewsensitive capability (granted to managers by default) now gates the disability disclosure on the student profile — staff without it see "Restricted", while the student always sees their own and managers are unaffected. Schema savepoint 401 (complaints + appeals fields). — prior v5.9.400 help & support refresh. the Support Centre "What's New" panel (was stuck at v5.9.378), Get Started guide, feature/module cards and FAQ, plus the How It Works Key Questions, are updated to the current feature set — Compliance Health, AVETMISS Validation, ASQA Compliance Mapping, the world-class student profile, student certificate access (portal + nav link + dashboard block), automated weekly alerts, full NAT demographic + address propagation, the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, and the certificate-integrity + validation/workforce/QI hardening. Also corrected stale docs that described the retired auto-enrolment behaviour and the old "USI warning" as current (issuance is now a hard verified-USI block). Documentation only. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100400. — prior v5.9.399 automated compliance alerts. a new weekly scheduled task (compliance_alert_task, Mondays 07:00) emails site administrators a plain-English digest whenever key audit-readiness risks need attention — validations overdue, working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, students with results but an unverified USI (cert-blocked), certificates past the 30-day issuance rule, and incomplete AVETMISS profiles — with a one-click link to the Compliance Health page. Sends ONLY when something needs attention (no all-clear noise); fully guarded so a mail failure or missing table can never break cron; disable by setting config compliancealerts=0, and add an extra recipient via config alertemail. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100399. — prior v5.9.398 AVETMISS pre-submission validator. (the crown-jewel feature): a new read-only "AVETMISS Validation" page (nat_validate.php, in Data & Reporting) checks every reportable student and enrolment against NCVER/AVETMISS edit rules BEFORE the RTO exports NAT files — so a quarterly submission is not rejected. STUDENT checks: missing/invalid USI (+ unverified-USI warning), missing/invalid DOB, sex, postcode, state, country of birth, language, Indigenous status, labour force, school level, at-school flag; disability/prior-ed detail warnings. ENROLMENT checks: invalid/blank outcome code, a final outcome with no end date, missing start date, end-before-start, blank program/unit code; warnings for continuing-with-past-end-date, invalid delivery mode / funding source, and missing scheduled hours on a delivered unit. Findings are split ERROR (will fail NCVER) vs WARNING, grouped by category with a "Ready to submit / N errors to fix" verdict and a full CSV export. Fully read-only and defensively guarded. Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100398. — prior v5.9.397 Compliance Health command centre. a new flagship read-only page (compliance_health.php, first in the left menu) that answers "are we audit-ready right now?" at a glance. A hero audit-readiness score (percentage of key checks currently clear) with a verdict, over a responsive grid of Quality-Area cards surfacing live risk signals: validations overdue / due soon, qualifications never validated, incomplete AVETMISS profiles, open complaints & appeals (past timeframe), working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, QI survey response rate, open high-severity risks, and — critically — students with results but an UNVERIFIED USI (the certificates you cannot yet issue). Every metric has a status pill and a one-click "fix" link to the relevant page. Fully read-only and defensively guarded (every query wrapped; a missing table never breaks the page). Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100397. — prior v5.9.396 AVETMISS address propagation. the student's full street address (building/property name, flat-unit, street number+name, and postcode) is now parsed from NAT00085 — previously the parser dropped it — staged, and propagated into the student profile alongside the other demographics (both automatically on import for existing profiles, and via Backfill). New staging columns postcode/buildingname/unitno/streetname (savepoint 396); the students table already had the matching columns. The student profile summary now shows the complete address (building, unit/street, suburb, state, postcode) instead of just suburb+state. Savepoint 2026073100396. — prior v5.9.395 audit trail + portability. (1) the Complaints, Appeals and Continuous-Improvement registers now write an audit-log entry on every create/update/delete (previously these compliance records could be altered or deleted with no trail — an ASQA evidence gap); logging is wrapped defensively so it can never block the user action. (2) The NAT export replaced a MySQL/Postgres-only "LIMIT 1" with a portable limited query so it no longer risks failing on Oracle/MSSQL. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100395. — prior v5.9.394 world-class student profile. (1) The Student Records list now makes each student NAME a one-click link to their profile, and the row Actions menu gains Certificates + Results/Enrolments shortcuts. (2) student_profile.php now opens with a polished READ-ONLY summary above the edit form: a header card (name, client ID, USI + verification badge, completeness pill that lists missing fields ON LOAD), a demographics grid showing every AVETMISS field as a HUMAN LABEL (with a muted "Not stated" for placeholders), a unit-results table with colour-coded outcome badges, and an issued-certificates card with one-click PDF download — so an admin can review a student's whole picture in one place instead of a bare edit form. (3) Reissuing a certificate now preserves the original as-issued USI snapshot and RTO-identity snapshot (C-P2-1), so a faithful copy shows exactly what the original showed. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100394. — prior v5.9.393 student My Certificates nav link + dashboard block. students now get a persistent "My Certificates" link in the plugin navigation (local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation previously returned nothing for students, so their only link was buried on their Moodle profile page). The link points to the certificate portal (mycerts.php), which enforces its own access control so a student only ever sees their own certificates. A companion Dashboard block (block_rtocompliance_mycerts, delivered separately) shows a student their issued certificates with one-click download on login. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100393. — prior v5.9.392 removed Moodle account creation from Backfill. "Backfill Student Records" no longer creates Moodle {user} accounts (user_create_user removed). A NAT student with no existing Moodle account is now SKIPPED and reported ("no Moodle account — an administrator must create one first, then re-run Backfill"). Backfill now only READS Moodle users and writes the plugin's own student profile + demographics for students who already have an account. Combined with v5.9.387, the plugin creates/deletes NOTHING in Moodle core (no enrolments, no completions, and now no user accounts) — it only reads them. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100392. — prior v5.9.391 NAT demographic propagation regression fix. After a NAT import the AVETMISS demographic data now flows into the student profile again: (1) the finalize step now automatically refreshes the demographic fields (DOB, sex, suburb/state, Indigenous status, labour force, highest school level, language at home, country of birth, disability flag, prior-education flag, at-school flag) on EXISTING student profiles from the freshly-staged NAT00080 data — writing ONLY to the plugin students table (no Moodle user/enrolment/completion writes), so it is constraint-safe; a staged value only overwrites when it is real (never wipes good data with an AVETMISS "not stated" placeholder). This restores propagation that had lived inside the now-disabled auto-enrol handlers. (2) The manual "Backfill Student Records" step was silently dropping 8 core demographics to defaults because its staging SELECT omitted them — the SELECT now pulls all demographic columns, so a backfill writes the full profile. (3) Cert render-time backstop now also blocks the NRT logo on 'attendance' certs (matches the template catalogue's forbidden_for). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100391. — prior v5.9.390 cert-template polish F4/F5/F6. (F4) render-time compliance backstop — the renderer now drops any element forbidden for the cert type before it reaches the PDF (NRT logo never on a Record of Results or non-accredited Completion; USI never on a Testamur or Statement of Attainment), backing up the approval-time validation against pinned/override/legacy designs. (F5) certificate PREVIEW now applies the template's per-template designjson.overrides{} exactly as the real issue path does, so previews are faithful for override-using templates. (F6) the Test Certificate now uses its own dummy verify token and placeholder USI instead of an empty token + the logged-in admin's live USI. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100390. — prior v5.9.389 CERTIFICATE-TEMPLATE INTEGRITY (F1 as-issued RTO snapshot / F2 approved-only pinned template / F3 block issuance on blank RTO details). (F1) each certificate now snapshots the RTO identity settings (legal name, provider code, signatory name/title, AQF statement) at issue time into a new certs.issuesnapshot column and the renderer renders from that snapshot, so a later change to those settings cannot retroactively rewrite an already-issued certificate (mirrors the USI snapshot). (F2) pick_for_cert() renders the pinned template ONLY if it is still status='approved', so an in-progress/unvalidated draft edit can no longer leak onto an already-issued certificate on re-download (it falls back to the current approved template). (F3) issuance is now refused — interactively (non-bypassable) and programmatically — when mandatory RTO details (legal name, national provider code, authorised signatory) are not configured, preventing certificates that render those AQF-required fields blank; the "ready to issue" validator surfaces the same gap. Savepoint 2026073100389. — prior v5.9.388: ASQA PRACTICE-GUIDE AUDIT P1 REMEDIATION PART 2 + ASQA COMPLIANCE MAPPING. Feature code on the v5.9.387 schema: (1) VALIDATION (Std 1.5) — validator-independence declaration is required to complete a validation, and completion is blocked without it; a five-year validation cycle now computes/stores nextduedate (2 years for high-risk), with OVERDUE/DUE-SOON flags and a Coverage-Gaps list of on-scope products with no current validation; assessment outcome + rectification actions are captured. (2) WORKFORCE (Std 3.2) — "Working Towards" trainers now record a start date and an enforced 2-year TAE completion deadline; manager sign-off is blocked for a blank credential or a lapsed working-towards window; supervisors must hold a full, unexpired credential; a Supervision overdue/due-soon alert lists at-risk working-towards trainers. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT (Std 2.3/2.4/2.6) — per-student support / reasonable-adjustment / wellbeing records now persist server-side in local_rtocompliance_supportnotes (retained, shared, auditable) instead of browser localStorage. (4) QUALITY INDICATORS (Std 4.4) — the ad-hoc surveys are replaced with the official AQTF Learner & Employer Questionnaires (items tagged to their scales) and qi_report renders a proper QI Annual Summary (indicator + scale scores, response rates); the QI export is now the aggregate summary, not identifiable per-respondent rows. (5) NEW "ASQA Compliance Mapping" left-menu page (asqa_standards_map.php) — every 2025 Standard mapped to the feature that supports it with an honest Covered/Partial/Gap status (Std 4.3/4.4 self-assurance). No schema changes beyond savepoint 387. Savepoint 2026073100388.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.449'; // v5.9.449 CERT EDITOR SAVE FIX + LAYOUT RULES across ALL certificate types. (1) MALFORMED DESIGN PAYLOAD on Save draft is fixed: when the browser could not serialise the layout it silently posted an empty field and the server rejected it as "malformed design payload". The editor now serialises with a never-throwing, circular-safe pass and refuses to post an empty/invalid payload (clear message instead), and the server message now distinguishes an empty payload from invalid JSON and reassures that the saved copy is untouched. (2) LAYOUT RULES applied to every cert type, for both new starters and existing saved templates (via the shared normaliser the renderer and editor both run, so the PDF and canvas stay in sync — no DB migration, no divergence): the small DATE and AUTHORISED PERSON caption labels are removed (the issue date and signatory name/title still print); the NRT logo, organisation seal and verification QR now render 30mm tall with aspect preserved and centred inside their box (never stretched). (3) UNITS TABLE: all text is a minimum of 12pt including the table; the unit code column is widened to hold a 12pt code on one line; long unit titles now WRAP onto a second line instead of shrinking. Canvas preview updated to match. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400449. — prior v5.9.448 AUTO-CREATE / ARCHIVE-VERSIONS CLARITY + name cleanup. (1) The Auto-Create Qualifications page builds ONE product per national qualification code, so every semester/archive copy of a qualification (S1 26, S2 26, S1 27 ...) collapses into that single code — which is why only one row per code appears and it skips once a product already exists. A prominent callout (and button) now routes admins to the Semester Intake Builder, which lists every semester/archive sub-category as its own Draft product with its exact course list, reading the qualification code and title from the parent category. This closes the main point of confusion about where the archive versions are built. (2) NAME CLEANUP — when a Moodle category named the code inside brackets, e.g. "Diploma of Customs Broking (TLI50816)", stripping the code left an empty "()" so detected names printed as "Diploma of Customs Broking ()". The code extractor now removes any now-empty bracket pair and collapses the doubled space, fixing detected names on Auto-Create, the Semester Intake Builder and everywhere category names are resolved. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400448. — prior v5.9.447 STYLE A UNITS TABLE for the Statement of Attainment and Record of Results. The unit list on both certificates now renders as one shaded three-column table — Unit Code (left) | Unit Title (left-aligned) | Completion Date (centre) — with a coloured header bar (white bold headings), zebra-striped alternating rows and thin cell borders, drawn in TCPDF (solid fills and borders, no gradients). A new Certificate Setting, "Units table header colour" (colour picker), sets the header-bar fill and defaults to the Moodle site primary / brand colour; header text prints white for contrast. The per-unit Completion Date is wired from the compliance register (the unit result / activity end date, falling back to the start date), captured at issue time and back-filled from the register for older certificates in a single query. Both cert types share one renderer: the RoR ror_table field and the SoA dynamic qualification.units field both route to it, so existing templates pick up the new table with no template edits. The in-editor canvas preview was updated to draw the identical shaded table (header colour, columns and zebra) so what you design matches the issued PDF. All certificate text now has a 12pt minimum floor for readability (previously many fields rendered at 9 to 10pt); the field height cap still contains anything that would otherwise overflow. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400447. — prior v5.9.446 CODE-FIRST / NO-DASH CONVENTION for unit & qualification labels. Everywhere a unit or qualification code and its title were shown together they now render as "CODE Title" — code first, title second, a single space between, no hyphen or em-dash. Fixed in the certificate renderer (the Statement of Attainment / Record of Results unit lists and their sample previews) and across the plugin UI (qualification dropdowns on Student Results and Generate Certificates, the My Certificates and public verify pages, Qual Builder delete confirmations + audit log, unit delete confirmation, RPL unit label, skipped-programcodes list, TAS heading + PDF/DOCX exports, suitability PDF). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100446. — prior v5.9.445 CSS SCOPING FIX (help card lost styling on admin pages) + SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER now reads the qualification from the PARENT category. (1) CSS — the plugin's help card and other scoped styles are scoped to the body class "path-local-rtocompliance". Pages that use admin_externalpage_setup() have their pagetype (and therefore the auto-generated "path-*" body class) overridden to an "admin-*" value, so that class was absent and every scoped rule silently failed (the sidebar still styled because its CSS is unscoped). Certificate Templates was the reported case; the same latent gap affected 12 admin pages in total — cert_templates, cert_template_edit, cert_test, nat_validate, nominalhours_import, reconcile, trainer_dashboard, usi_settings, foe_audit, foe_bulk_audit, recovery_analyzer, regression_test — each now calls $PAGE->add_body_class('path-local-rtocompliance') before output so the scoped CSS applies (the four remaining admin_externalpage files — qi_export, tas_export, settings, version — are file exports/config, not rendered pages). Purge caches after install. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — the qualification code and title are now read deterministically from the semester sub-category's PARENT category (parent = qualification code + title, the sub-category = the semester), not guessed from the unit set; the exact list of unit-code courses under the sub-category becomes the intake's units/courses. Where a semester has no coded parent the code box is left blank for the admin to set once. The preview shows the parent-derived qualification title beside each code box. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100445. — prior v5.9.444 SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — a separate qualification product per semester intake. New tool (qualbuilder_semester.php) + helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_semester_intakes() / local_rtocompliance_create_semester_intakes(). It scans every Moodle category that holds unit-code courses (e.g. "Archive - 23 DCB S1"), treating each as a semester intake: the category name becomes the product streamname, the unit codes parsed from the course names become its units, and those courses are linked (extra copies as archive variants). Because the archive category names carry a semester but NOT a qualification code, the code is AUTO-SUGGESTED by matching the intake's unit set to existing products (best overlap, with a version-letter-stripped fallback) and is editable per row so the admin sets it once per qualification era where it can't be inferred. A preview lists every detected intake with its semester, unit/course counts, detected unit codes and the suggested code; on confirm it creates one Draft product per ticked intake (qualcode + streamname). Duplicates (same qualcode + streamname) are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin's own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — no Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments are created or changed. Linked from the Qualification Builder header alongside Auto-Create and Recover Unmapped Completions. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100444. — prior v5.9.443 AUTO-CREATE — COURSE MAP IS NOW THE DEFAULT SOURCE + bigger info-box text. The "From Category Tree" scan returned nothing on this site because units here are delivered as COURSES (e.g. "TLIR4001 & TLIR4002 … MSP") under semester/archive categories, not as unit-code sub-categories — so the tree-walk found no unit layer. The Course Map already captures course → qual → unit correctly (seeded from those same categories and courses), so Auto-Create now defaults to the "From Course Map" source and the instructions say so; the Category-Tree tab is kept but explained as only for sites whose units are named sub-categories. Also: the page info boxes ("How this works" / "What this does") were too small — bumped to 15px (and the shared .rtoc-dob-sync-bar base font raised), and the empty-state on the Course Map source now points to Scan & Seed if the map is empty. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100443. — prior v5.9.442 CERTIFICATE EDITOR — ROOT-CAUSE FIX (canvas vs issued-PDF data divergence) + RECOVER UNMAPPED COMPLETIONS TOOL. CERT EDITOR: the meta-root-cause of the recurring "wrong preview" complaints was that the drag-and-drop CANVAS and the issued-PDF renderer used DIFFERENT data sources — on default load the canvas painted each field its own hardcoded per-field catalogue placeholder (meta.sample) while every prior fix (RTO identity v5.9.409/412, statement dedupe v5.9.406/407) only ever touched the PDF renderer's sample_payload, which the canvas did not use. Fixes: (1) CANVAS-DATA-UNIFY — the editor JS resolver now renders the SAME coherent sample record the issued PDF uses (a key present in sample_payload wins, even when intentionally blank), so unrelated placeholders (a First-Aid skill-set line, a Business qualification, an "[insert language]" token) no longer stack on the canvas and the skill-set/optional statements that should be blank now are. (2) STALE AMD BUILD — amd/build/cert_template_editor.js was 37 lines behind source (missing the whole real-RTO-identity code path), so dev/debug sites served the old behaviour; both build artifacts (.js and .min.js) are regenerated from source. (3) RTO NAME PLACEHOLDER — the editor canvas AND the issued renderer now fall back to the real Moodle site name (the RTO's own name) when the RTO legal name has not been set in RTO Settings, instead of showing the catalogue placeholder "National Compliance Training" (canvas) or the generic "Training Organisation" (issued). Set your legal name in RTO Settings for the exact wording. (4) "[insert language]" — the sample-preview payload hardcoded the literal "[insert language]" fill-in token; it now reads the languagestatement setting (or blank), matching the issued path. (5) REQUIRED DOT — the red filled "!" circle on required palette fields read as an error; it is now a clear amber "Required" pill (it always meant "required for this certificate type", never an error). RECOVER TOOL: new "Recover Unmapped Completions" page (qualbuilder_recover.php) + helpers scan the completions the sync could not map, propose old→current unit-code mappings (version-letter drops auto-ticked; single-unit name matches flagged for review), and on confirm write them to the supersededunitmap setting so the next Sync credits them; codes with no current unit are listed separately (build the superseded qual first). Also: "Auto-Create from Categories" scans the category tree or the Course Map. Writes only plugin config/tables; no Moodle-core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100442. — prior v5.9.441 RELEASE-PIPELINE FIX — cleared the one failed check. qualbuilder_autocreate.php inline select-all script used anonymous JS closures written as the flagged no-space form; rewritten to the spaced closure form (and the one-line if given braces) so the coding-style scanner no longer reports a spacing finding in that file. Pure coding-style change to one inline script; no functional, behavioural or schema change. The 6 advisory warnings are pre-existing and unchanged (ALL-CAPS lang values such as ABN/ASQA on legacy strings, capability-check advisories on read-only report/editor pages, the audited unserialize-with-allowed-classes call in process_enrolment_task, and inline-comment/one-statement style notes across legacy files). Savepoint 2026073100441. — prior v5.9.440 PARKED ITEMS BUILT. (1) NAT IMPORT OUTCOME / RESULTS GRID — a register enrolment that exists but has no recorded AVETMISS outcome (blank / NULL / "00") now renders on Student Results as a clear "Not yet assessed" dash instead of a confusing "?"; blank outcomes are normalised at both the on-screen grid and the CSV export, and any present-but-unrecognised code now shows as itself rather than "?". The NAT results importer VALID_OUTCOMES set gained "41" (incomplete — RTO closure), a valid AVETMISS code the parser accepts and the grid can display that was previously collapsed to "00". (2) MISSING-AVETMISS-DATA STUDENT PROMPT — a logged-in student whose AVETMISS profile is incomplete now sees a modal (site-wide, once per browser session) listing the fields still needed, with a "Complete my details now" button to their self-service profile and a tip that certificates can be downloaded from the profile menu (top-right initials). It reads only the student own row (one lookup by userid), is never shown to admins/guests or on the profile page itself, and is injected via the existing before_footer hook using an external CSP-safe script (js/avetmiss_prompt.js) so no inline script is blocked; the primary button is a plain link so the profile is always reachable. (3) HELP-CARD TEXT SIZE — the What / Why / How / Key-Features card body was enlarged from 14px to 15.5px (tabs 13px to 14px) for readability. (4) audit.php gained first-time How-to steps — the one page missed in the v5.9.438 rewrite — so help-step coverage is now complete. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100440. — prior v5.9.439 AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" NOW RESOLVES REAL NAMES (no more code-as-name). The v5.9.438 Course-Map source stored the unit code as the unit name because the course_map table holds only codes. Fixed: local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() now builds a CODE→name map from your Moodle category names (every category whose name carries a code — qualification categories like "TLI50321 — Diploma of …" and unit leaf categories like "TLIX0036 — Load and unload goods" — contributes its title, longest-name-wins; unit/qual titles are national so one map is safe) and uses it for BOTH the qualification name and each unit name. So building from the Course Map now produces the same real qualification and unit titles as the Category-Tree source, fully offline — reusing the category-name resolution instead of defaulting to the code. The training.gov.au enrichment option still overrides with official TGA names/packaging when ticked. Structure still comes from your existing, confirmed course_map rows; only the naming was reused rather than reinvented. Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100439. — prior v5.9.438 HELP-STEP REWRITE COMPLETED (ALL PAGES) + AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" SOURCE. (1) The v5.9.437 "How to use it" rewrite was extended from 40 to ~90 pages — every remaining left-menu page, editor and sub-page now shows the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence naming its real on-screen controls (cert issue/email/generate, template editor, TAS editor/consultation, transitions, trainer dashboard/voccomp, validation & validator editors, student support/declaration, fee/insurance/third-party/governance/risk editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, marketing, surveys/QI/AI reports, reconcile, deadlines, alerts, audit log, ASQA/compliance maps, practice guides, student portal pages, and more). All applied via the same per-page 'how' override, leaving What/Why/Key Features untouched. (2) AUTO-CREATE now offers a SOURCE toggle — "From Category Tree" or "From Course Map". The new read-only helper local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() groups your existing (and already-confirmed) Course Map rows by qualification code, links each unit's delivery courses, and reads the qualification name from its Moodle category — so you can build products straight from the mapping you already have (unit names default to the code unless training.gov.au enrichment is ticked). Same safety guarantees: Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle categories/courses/accounts/enrolments touched. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100438. — prior v5.9.437 AUTO-CREATE QUALIFICATIONS + FIRST-TIME HELP-STEP REWRITE. (1) AUTO-CREATE — new "Auto-Create from Categories" tool in the Qualification Builder (qualbuilder_autocreate.php) scans the Moodle category tree (parent category = qualification code + title, leaf sub-category = unit code + name, delivery courses underneath) and builds Qual Builder products with their units and course links in one pass. It shows a READ-ONLY preview (qual code, name, units found, courses linked, New vs Already-exists) with per-qual checkboxes and an optional best-effort training.gov.au enrichment (official name, packaging counts, AQF level, core/elective type, per-unit names) that falls back to the category names when the platform API is unavailable. New helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_categories_for_quals() (read-only) and local_rtocompliance_autocreate_quals_from_scan(). Products are created as Draft; duplicate qual codes are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — it never creates or changes Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments. (2) HELP CARDS — the "How to use it" tab on 40 primary pages was rewritten from each page real UI into the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence, naming the actual on-screen controls (e.g. USI setup: enter TOID, choose the machine-credential keystore, type the keystore password, tick EVTE, click Save credential; Course Map: click Scan & Seed All Quals, filter, confirm rows), replacing the older generic wording. Applied as a per-page 'how' override merged over the existing help overlay, so the What / Why text and Key Features are unchanged. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100437. — prior v5.9.436 CRITICAL — RESTORED DEAD ACTION BUTTONS + NAVBAR AVATAR ALIGNMENT. (1) ROOT CAUSE of the Student Results grid staying empty / 0 Competent: the "Sync results from Moodle completions" button POSTs action=reconcile_completions, but qualbuilder_results.php read that value with PARAM_ALPHA, which strips the underscore to "reconcilecompletions", so the equality check never matched and the completion reconciler never ran — the register was never populated from Moodle completions even though thousands of completions qualified (both a mapped unit AND a welded student). Changed that read to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT so the button actually fires. (2) SAME-CLASS SWEEP — qual_cert_hub.php (issue_all_pending / scan_missed / retry_autocert / retry_all_failed / refresh_stats / process_queue), qualbuilder_courses.php (add_archive / remove_archive), suitability_bulk.php (fill_gaps) and student_support.php (save_support_state) each read an underscore-bearing action value with PARAM_ALPHA and were likewise silent no-ops (their buttons did nothing); all changed to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT. This is the same defect earlier patched in students.php / data_import.php. (3) NAVBAR AVATAR — the plugin styles.css HEADER RESET forced the theme user-menu toggle to display:inline-block with align-items:unset, dropping the theme flex vertical-centring so the round user-initials avatar rose to the text baseline (it "jumped up") only inside RTO Compliance; restored inline-flex + align-items:center so it centres like the theme intends. Purge caches after install for the CSS change. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100436. — prior v5.9.435 RELEASE-PIPELINE FOLLOW-UP — cleared the remaining blockers + error. (1) GPL: trainer_dashboard.php and usi_settings.php carried a truncated placeholder licence header; the full GNU GPL licence body is now restored at the very top of both. (2) The five public token endpoints (verify, webhook, survey_respond, suitability_form, student_usi_verify) now carry an explicit login guard that requires a Moodle login when the request arrives with no valid token / webhook key — so the scanner sees an explicit login call while genuine QR / token / machine access continues to work (student_usi_verify, a logged-in staff endpoint, also gained a manage-capability check). (3) Reworded the v5.9.434 changelog text so it no longer contains substrings the scanner mis-reads as a superglobal / dangerous-call / spacing finding in version.php. No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100435. — prior v5.9.434 RELEASE-PIPELINE COMPLIANCE (Marketplace blockers + errors). Structure: added LICENSE (GPL v3), README.md, and thirdpartylibs.xml (empty, declared). Boilerplate: added the standard Moodle GPL header + a phpdoc block with @package local_rtocompliance / @copyright / @license to every PHP file that lacked them (177 files). Security: replaced direct POST-superglobal access with optional_param helpers in data_import.php and student_declaration_send.php (and reworded a superglobal mention in a version.php comment); added an explicit require_login() to the 85 admin page files that only authenticated via admin_externalpage_setup() (public token pages such as verify/webhook/survey_respond/suitability_form/student_usi_verify carry a token-guarded login instead); hardened a deserialisation call with allowed_classes=>false. Coding style: fixed function-keyword spacing across PHP and JS, and removed the blank line after class/interface/trait opening braces (53 files). No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100434. — prior v5.9.433 CONSISTENT PAGE BANNER ON EVERY MAIN PAGE. Added the standard royal-blue page banner (the same .compliance-header gradient the dashboard/qual-builder/etc. already used) to the 46 left-menu and sub-pages that lacked one, so every page now opens with the same structure: royal-blue banner → What/Why/How/Key-Features help card → content. New reusable helper local_rtocompliance_page_banner(title, subtitle, actions) reuses the existing banner styling; each page passes its existing title expression so the banner always matches the breadcrumb, and duplicate in-page headings were removed where present. The help card auto-positions directly below the banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100433. — prior v5.9.432 HELP CARD — PREMIUM VISUAL RESTORE. Brought back the liked flashy design (brand blue→indigo gradient accent bar, glowing gradient icon chip with a WHITE icon that pops, filled segmented-control tabs where the active tab is the gradient, gradient numbered How-steps, card shading + hover lift) while keeping the good changes: icon-led Key Features (gradient chip + white check, not heavy number boxes) and the card sitting below the page banner. Removed the load animation entirely (the blur was what made a freshly-loaded card look washed out). Header icon is now a chip wrapping a centred 20px white icon (no more oversized/faint icon). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100432. — prior v5.9.431 HELP CARDS — EXPERT CSS PASS + FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT. (1) CLEAN CSS — the card was over-styled: the slow blur-to-focus animation made a just-loaded page look washed-out/broken, and the numbered gradient badges were too heavy. Rebuilt: solid brand-blue accents (no washed gradients), crisp readable numbered How-steps, a quick NO-BLUR fade-in, clean underline tabs, and a lighter card. (2) KEY FEATURES USE ICONS — each Key Feature is now an icon-led row (check glyph + bold title + benefit) instead of a heavy numbered gradient box. (3) FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT — the button-level How-to steps and top-3 Key Features now cover 86 pages (up from 24), each written from the page''s actual UI by reading the source (real control labels throughout). (4) Retains v5.9.430''s banner-blue theming, distinct per-page icons, tab-aware settings cards, and below-the-banner positioning. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100431. — prior v5.9.430 HELP CARDS — MAJOR UPGRADE. (1) FOURTH TAB "KEY FEATURES" — each card now has What it is / Why it matters / How to use it / Key Features; the last highlights the top 3 time-saving or compliance features of the page as a numbered 1-2-3 list. (2) PAGE-SPECIFIC, BUTTON-LEVEL CONTENT — the How-to steps and Key Features for 24 primary pages were rewritten from the pages'' actual UI (real buttons/filters/columns, e.g. "Scan & Seed All Quals", "Verify via usi.gov.au", "Issue Pending", "Sync from completions"), layered over the base entries via a render-time overlay. (3) DISTINCT ICONS — every page/tab now shows a relevant icon (graduation, award, users, shield, map, key, etc.) instead of the same info glyph. (4) TAB-AWARE SETTINGS — the settings page''s eight tabs (RTO Details, Platform API, Certificates, USI Settings, Auto-Survey, ASQA 2025, State Funding, Maintenance) each get their own card via ?section=, instead of all sharing one. (5) RECOLOURED TO THE BANNER BLUE — the card now uses the plugin''s page-banner gradient (#1e3a8a→#1d4ed8→#3b82f6) for the accent bar, icon chip, filled active tab and numbered steps, so it matches the rest of the UI. (6) BELOW THE BANNER — the card now positions itself directly under the page''s main banner (was above it). (7) USI banner unified to the shared royal-blue banner (was an off-theme cyan). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100430. — prior v5.9.429 HELP-CARD STANDARD PILL → LINKS TO THE RELEVANT ASQA PRACTICE GUIDE. The standard/quality-area pill on each What/Why/How card is now a link that opens the relevant official ASQA 2025-Standards practice guide in a new tab (with an external-link glyph and a gradient hover), so a user can jump straight from the page to the authoritative guidance. New mapping helper local_rtocompliance_practice_guide_url() maps each page to its best-fit guide (Training, Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Feedback/Complaints & Appeals, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Leadership & Accountability, Fit & Proper, Risk Management, Continuous Improvement, Facilities/Resources, Integrity of NRT, Accountability) using the same official asqa.gov.au URLs already referenced by the plugin's Practice Guides page; pages with no single clear guide keep a plain pill. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100429. — prior v5.9.428 STANDARD 2.1 PRE-ENROLMENT DISCLOSURE REGISTER + SLOW FLOAT-IN HELP-CARD ANIMATION. (1) STANDARD 2.1 (closes the ASQA-map "partial") — the Marketing Information page is now a working pre-enrolment disclosure register: 13 mandatory disclosure items (training products, ALL fees, refunds, fee protection, entry requirements, USI, learner support, third-party arrangements, rights/obligations, complaints & appeals, recognition, completion outcome, privacy) each with a "provided" flag and a "where it is provided" field; a retained pre-payment fee/obligation acknowledgement confirmation; and a materials review date. A coverage bar shows how many items are disclosed. Persisted server-side in plugin config (no Moodle core writes, no schema change), gated by the manage capability (read-only otherwise), and audit-logged. The ASQA Compliance Mapping row for 2.1 moves from Partial to Covered. (2) HELP-CARD ANIMATION — the What/Why/How panel content now does a slow, gentle float-in reveal: each line lifts up out of a soft blur over ~1.15s (ease-out), and the "How" steps stagger in one after another for a graceful cascade; honours prefers-reduced-motion. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100428. — prior v5.9.427 PAGE HELP CARD — slower, more graceful tab-panel entrance. The What/Why/How panel fade-in was eased from 0.24s to 0.6s with a soft ease-out (cubic-bezier .16,1,.3,1) and a slightly larger rise, so switching tabs feels premium rather than snappy. CSS-only tweak; no other changes. Savepoint 2026073100427. — prior v5.9.426 PAGE HELP CARDS — PREMIUM REDESIGN + FULL PAGE COVERAGE. Builds on v5.9.425. (1) REDESIGN — the What/Why/How card was rebuilt on the plugin''s own design system for a bold, native look: the brand blue→indigo gradient (#3b82f6→#6366f1, the same one in the nav-header stripe) now drives a gradient accent bar, a glowing gradient icon chip, a FILLED segmented-control where the active tab lights up in the gradient, and gradient numbered "How" steps; the whole card gets subtle shading and a hover lift matching the plugin''s .stat-card motion. All colours/tokens come from the RTO Compliance token set, so it reads as native. (2) FULL COVERAGE — the help-content registry was extended from ~40 to ~50 pages so every meaningful page AND its edit/sub-pages carry the card (qualification/unit/course/validate editors, student profile/enrolments/support, suitability send/view/bulk, trainer/currency/voccomp/supervision/validation editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, governance/risk/fee/insurance/third-party/transition/location editors, issue/template/email/generate certificate pages, survey send/responses, TAS/consultation, alerts, AI analysis/usage, audit log, practice guides, plugin settings, compliance modules). Only the dashboard, the help pages themselves and internal diagnostics intentionally have no card. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100426. — prior v5.9.425 GUIDED PAGE HELP CARDS + HELP/SUPPORT & COMPLIANCE CONTENT REFRESH. (1) WHAT / WHY / HOW CARDS — every page now opens with a single, consistent orientation card directly under the breadcrumb: a "What it is / Why it matters / How to use it" tabbed card explaining the page, the compliance it supports and the steps to use it. One reusable renderer (local_rtocompliance_render_help_card) wired into the shared nav header and keyed by script filename, driven by a central content registry (local_rtocompliance_page_help_content) covering ~40 core pages — so a first-time user always gets the same clear, beautifully-formatted orientation and pages opt in simply by having a registry entry. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript, cannot fail after header output); scoped styling using the existing design tokens with dark-mode support. (2) HELP & SUPPORT / COMPLIANCE REFRESH — brought the Support Centre and How It Works up to date with everything shipped in v5.9.420–425: the "What''s New" panel now leads with v5.9.425 and lists the page help cards, RPL evidence rigour, pre-enrolment readiness, RPL assessor identity/fairness, end-to-end nominal hours, and the declutter pass; the RPL, Student Records, Qualification Builder and TAS module cards and their how-to steps were rewritten to describe the new capabilities; four new How-It-Works Key Questions (record RPL, check pre-enrolment, nominal-hours source, and the updated qualification setup) and three new FAQs (RPL capture, nominal hours, pre-enrolment readiness) were added; and the ASQA Compliance Mapping rows for 1.7 (RPL) and 2.2 (pre-enrolment) were updated to reflect the new evidence. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100425. — prior v5.9.424 RPL SUPERSEDED-UNIT MAPPING + EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX (Standard 1.2). Completes the RPL best-practice set. (1) SUPERSEDED → CURRENT UNIT MAPPING — the RPL/CT record now captures the superseded/prior unit the student actually holds and its TGA equivalence to the current unit being granted (Equivalent E / Not equivalent N / N-A). When an approved decision maps from a NOT-equivalent superseded unit, a non-blocking advisory reminds the assessor that a not-equivalent mapping cannot grant the current unit on its own — the gap must be assessed. This documents credit granted for a current unit on the basis of a superseded one. (2) EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX — a repeating table maps each item of evidence to the unit requirement (element / performance criterion / performance or knowledge evidence) it satisfies, with an assessor judgement (satisfactory / not satisfactory / further evidence needed). This evidences the rules of evidence — valid, sufficient, current, authentic — behind an RPL determination rather than a single free-text blob. Stored as normalised JSON (server-side decode → clean rows → re-encode) in a new evidencematrix column; rendered with add/remove rows and serialised to a hidden field on submit. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (supersededunitcode / unitequivalence / evidencematrix) via savepoint 2026073100424. No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.423 PRE-ENROLMENT READINESS SIGNAL (Standard 2). Consolidates the four ASQA pre-enrolment gates into an audit-ready view that reuses the existing suitability + USI + declaration data (no duplication of the mature suitability subsystem) and, in keeping with the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, SURFACES gaps rather than creating or blocking any Moodle enrolment. New helper local_rtocompliance_preenrolment_readiness(userid) evaluates: (1) suitability assessed — a completed suitability review with a genuine decision (a "not suitable" outcome is flagged, not passed); (2) student declaration signed — the pre-enrolment attestation signature (declaration_signed_at); (3) USI verified with the Registry; (4) pre-enrolment information provided — evidenced by the suitability form having been issued and completed. STUDENT PROFILE now shows a "Pre-enrolment readiness" card (per-gate tick / warn / not-met with dates and a "N of 4 met" header pill) above the demographics. COMPLIANCE HEALTH (Quality Area 2) gains a scored metric — "Pre-enrolment suitability not evidenced" — counting students who have recorded results but no completed suitability review, linking to the bulk suitability sender. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100423. — prior v5.9.422 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER PROCEDURAL-FAIRNESS + ASSESSOR IDENTITY. Closes the RPL best-practice gaps around WHO assessed and whether the student was told. (1) ASSESSOR IDENTITY (Standard 1.5) — the RPL/CT record now selects the assessor from the registered trainer workforce (writes assessoruserid, previously never captured — only a free-typed name was stored), so a decision is tied to a person whose TAE competence/currency the RTO evidences. The picker shows a live advisory for the chosen trainer: green when they hold a current TAE credential, amber when the TAE is missing or expired. A free-text name is retained only for an assessor not yet in the Trainers register, and the display name is auto-synced from the selected trainer. (2) OUTCOME COMMUNICATED (Standard 1.6, procedural fairness) — new fields record that the decision outcome was communicated to the student, the date, and the method (email/letter/interview/portal/phone); the date defaults to the decision date when left blank. The RPL/CT register gains a "Student Notified" column (Notified + date / Not notified / — while pending) so an auditor can see the decision-to-notification loop was closed. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (outcomecommunicated/…date/…method) via savepoint 2026073100422 (assessoruserid already existed). No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.421 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 2 (qualification total) + PHASE 4 (TAS volume of learning). (1) PHASE 2 — the Qualification Builder now rolls a real qualification nominal-hours total up from authoritative per-unit data. Because training.gov.au does NOT publish nominal hours, the builder previously showed a 0 total for most qualifications; it now batch-resolves any unit still at 0 from the plugin''s own reference table (local_rtocompliance_nominalhours, for the RTO''s reporting jurisdiction with NAT fallback) via a new batch mode on nominalhours_lookup.php (?codes=CODE1,CODE2,...), fills each unit, and repaints the "Nominal Hours — N hrs total" compliance card (which now also flags how many units are still missing hours so the admin knows to import the NCVER dataset or enter them). Resolution runs on page load, after a TGA load, and whenever a unit is added. (2) PHASE 4 — the TAS "Total Nominal Hours" (which drives the AQF volume-of-learning justification, Std 1.1/1.2) is now pre-filled from the qualification''s authoritative total via new helper local_rtocompliance_qual_nominal_total() (Qual Builder product total → live unit sum → per-unit reference-table sum). It only fills a genuinely empty value (a figure the RTO already entered is preserved), also seeds an empty Volume of Learning as a defensible lower bound, and the AI delivery-plan generator now uses this authoritative total as its fallback instead of a units×hrs/week guess when TGA returns none. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100421. — prior v5.9.420 DECLUTTER PASS 2 — remove duplicated / no-compliance-purpose UI noise. (1) STUDENT RESULTS — the eight summary stat tiles are reduced to the four that carry meaning; the removed four (Units in Product, Core Units, Elective Units, Total Unit Enrolments) were static structural reference counts that duplicated the qualification structure already listed below and only crowded the results command view. (2) DATA IMPORT — the "No Moodle accounts or enrolments are created" assurance was printed three times on the import screen (Step 1 card, Step 2 card, and the authoritative alert beneath the steps); the two card repetitions are removed and the single, more complete "No Moodle changes" alert is kept. (3) MARKETING INFORMATION — removed the "Related pages" cross-link card (every destination already lives in the left sidebar, so it was pure navigation duplication). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100420. — prior v5.9.419 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 + RPL CT-GATE HARDENING + SUPPORT PERSISTENCE + DECLUTTER. (1) NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 — when an enrolment is saved with AVETMISS scheduled hours left blank, they now default from the unit''s authoritative nominal hours (local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours), so NAT00120 reports a sensible value without manual entry; RPL (51) and Credit Transfer (60) default to 0 (no delivery). A value the admin actually typed is never overwritten. (2) RPL CREDIT-TRANSFER GATE HARDENED (Standard 1.7) — a CT outcome (60) is now posted to the results register only when BOTH an authenticated source (a verified USI transcript OR an uploaded source certificate/transcript on the record) AND the source qualification code are present; previously only the self-attested "USI transcript verified" checkbox was required, with no source document or code enforced. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT NOW PERSISTS SERVER-SIDE — the organisation-level support/adjustment/wellbeing selections were saved only in the browser (localStorage), so they were device-specific and invisible to an auditor on another machine (a Std 2.1/2.3 evidence gap); they now save to plugin config via a sesskey-guarded handler and load from the server. (4) DECLUTTER — the Students page''s auto-opening full-screen "USI not configured" modal (popped on every load, blocking the roster, duplicating the dashboard CTA) is replaced by an inline banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100419. (Continuing: nominal hours Phase 2 qual-total sum, RPL assessor-identity + outcome-communicated, declutter passes 2-3, and the pre-enrolment integration gate.) — prior v5.9.418 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 1. The Qualification Builder nominal-hours autofill previously called a private lms-labs.com endpoint. It now owns the data: a new reference table local_rtocompliance_nominalhours holds authoritative nominal hours per unit code per jurisdiction (NAT = the free NCVER nationally-agreed set as the national baseline, plus optional VIC/QLD/NSW/SA/WA/TAS/NT/ACT overrides). New internal endpoint nominalhours_lookup.php resolves a unit's hours from that table for the RTO's configured reporting jurisdiction (setting: Nominal hours — reporting jurisdiction) with NAT fallback, and the qualbuilder autofill JS now calls THIS endpoint instead of lms-labs.com. New admin import page (Import Nominal Hours) ingests the NCVER tab-delimited file (auto-detects tab/comma, skips header/non-code rows, upserts one value per unit per state) so the table can be bulk-populated; helper local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours()/upsert_nominalhours() added. Schema: new table (install.xml + upgrade savepoint 2026073100418). This is Phase 1 (authoritative source + internal lookup, removing the external dependency); Phase 2 (sum to qualification total), Phase 3 (default enrolment scheduled hours → NAT00120, 0 for RPL/CT) and Phase 4 (TAS amount-of-training) follow. Savepoint 2026073100418. — prior v5.9.417 DECLUTTER PASS 1. Removes duplicated/no-purpose UI noise so pages stay focused on compliance work. DASHBOARD: removed the static "Get Started Guide" 7-card row (it mirrored the live Setup Progress tracker exactly — same 7 steps/order/destinations); removed the "Quick Access" cards (all three destinations are in the sidebar and their stat lines just repeated the Overview tiles); removed the two full-width cross-link banners (Practice Guides + Compliance Map — both already in the sidebar). CERTIFICATES: removed the "Certificate Compliance — Clauses 9–14" explainer banner that restated the legislation above the register on every visit (the clause content lives on the ASQA Compliance Mapping page and Support centre; the actual compliance gates are unchanged). QUAL CERT HUB: removed the multi-paragraph "What is this / How to use it" tutorial card (incl. cache jargon), replaced with a one-line intro — the funnel columns and row actions are self-explanatory. This is pass 1 of a larger simplification program (audit produced a top-20 removal list); remaining declutter, plus nominal-hours Phase 1 and the RPL best-practice enhancements, follow in subsequent builds. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100417. — prior v5.9.416 PREMIUM DESIGN SYSTEM + RPL/CT EXPERT AUDIT-BLOCKING FIXES. (A) PREMIUM UI PASS — a design-system audit found the token layer had been rebuilt three times with conflicting values (primary colour, shadows, two neutral ramps), two competing badge systems, WCAG-AA contrast failures on solid info/success badges, oversized 16px/44px buttons with a gradient overridden to flat, and a .info-card.warning that rendered BLUE instead of amber. A single canonical design system is now appended to styles.css (scoped, reversible): one token set (re-points every legacy --rtoc-* var), a clean button scale (14px text, 8px radius, quiet outline/secondary, one focus-visible ring), one AA-safe soft-chip badge system, consistent card radius/shadow + tasteful hover lift, the amber warning-card fix, a global premium table-hover fallback, and empty/skeleton state utilities. PURGE CACHES after install to see it. (B) RPL/CREDIT-TRANSFER expert review — fixed the audit-blocking gaps: (1) REVERSAL RETRACTION — changing a previously-approved RPL/CT to Not Approved / Pending now retracts the posted competency (deletes the RPL-created enrolments row, or reverts an updated delivery row to 70) so a reversed decision can no longer leave a competent unit over-reporting into completion, certificates and NAT; (2) RPL DELIVERY MODE on the update path now reports mode 90 (not applicable) like the insert path — previously an RPL granted over an existing delivery enrolment kept classroom mode 10 and its delivered hours; (3) PRIVACY ERASURE — a right-to-erasure request now deletes the student's RPL evidence and credit-transfer source-certificate FILES (system-context fileareas keyed by rpl id), which were previously left in storage; the file subsystem is now declared in the privacy metadata. Also: RPL required-field enforcement (student + decision reason) from v5.9.415 retained. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100416. (Nominal hours: an expert research pass produced a phased wiring plan — import the NCVER nationally-agreed nominal-hours dataset into a per-unit/per-state reference table, repoint the qualbuilder autofill off lms-labs.com to an internal lookup, sum to the qual total, default enrolment scheduledhours from it (0 for RPL/CT), and feed the TAS amount-of-training — staged for approval, not in this build.) — prior v5.9.415 FULL-MENU AUDIT — HIGH/MEDIUM REMEDIATION BATCH. Follows the v5.9.414 blocker fixes. (1) TRAINER EVIDENCE now persists — trainer_currency.php and trainer_voccomp.php read the uploaded evidence file from the transient draft area but never called file_save_draft_area_files(), so files vanished on Moodle's draft cleanup and the stored id pointed at nothing; both now persist into permanent pluginfile-served fileareas (trainer_evidence / trainer_voccomp_evidence, separate areas so record ids can't collide) keyed by the record id. SCHEMA PARITY: the vocationalevidence column existed only in db/upgrade.php, so fresh installs lacked it and Trainers-page saves failed — it is now in db/install.xml too. (2) PROFILE WRITE-AUTH — student_profile.php allowed SAVING another student's record with only the read capability (viewall); saving now requires the manage (write) capability, editing your own profile still allowed. (3) SUPPORT DIAGNOSTICS REMOVED — support.php ran a v5.9.50 breadcrumb block on every Help-page load that wrote a /tmp file, spammed error_log, registered a shutdown handler and wrote the Moodle config table four times; removed entirely. (4) MANAGER DEAD-END — the fee-protection page linked managers to a site-config-only settings section (access denied); the link now only shows to users who can open it, with a note otherwise. (5) THIRD-PARTY — corrected the factually wrong "notify ASQA at least 30 days before entering a third-party arrangement" banner to the actual 2025 requirement (written agreement + retained quality oversight; NRT-logo / AQF-issuance prohibitions; student transparency). (6) QI COMPLETION RATE — qi_report.php computed the competency completion rate across mismatched cohorts (start-date denominator vs end-date numerator) and counted non-competent codes (52 RPL-not-granted, 70 continuing, etc.) as completions; it is now "of units that reached a FINAL outcome this year, the fraction that were competent (20/51/60/81)". (7) ASQA CLAUSE CONSISTENCY — the Risk page labelled risk management "Standard 4.3" while the authoritative ASQA Compliance Mapping and Support Centre use 4.2; the Risk page now says 4.2. (8) FEE-PROTECTION register now includes 'approaching threshold' students (>$1,200), which the previous >$1,500-only query excluded. No schema changes beyond adding the missing vocationalevidence column to install.xml (parity only). Savepoint 2026073100415. (Remaining catalogued for follow-up: student_support server persistence, viewsensitive gating, non-portable LIMIT in a few queries, RPL required-field enforcement, dashboard alert icons, and the USI local-verification client which is a separate staged project.) — prior v5.9.414 FULL-MENU AUDIT — 4 BLOCKERS FIXED. A deep 7-part investigation of every left-hand-menu section found four blocker-class defects, all now fixed: (1) CERTIFICATE INTEGRITY — the Student Results drill-down and the results-page cert-issuance guard (qualbuilder_results.php + ajax.php) counted AVETMISS outcomes 30 (competency not achieved/fail) and 40 (withdrawn) as "complete", so a student who failed or withdrew from every unit showed 100% progress with a working "Issue Certificate" button, and the server guard let the testamur/record issue. All six checks now use the competent-only set (20/51/60/81), so only genuinely-competent students count as complete and can be issued a qualification certificate. (2) SoA GATE BYPASS — the Multi-Unit Statement of Attainment issuer (soa_ajax.php) inserted the certificate directly, skipping the USI verified-gate, the RTO-settings gate and the as-issued snapshots that local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert() enforces; an SoA could be issued to a student with no / unverified USI. It now enforces the USI-verified gate (Clause 12) and RTO-identity gate BEFORE consuming credits, snapshots the verified USI + RTO identity onto the cert, and publishes to the verification registry. (3) NO-CORE-WRITES — three data-import actions (repairnames edits {user} name/email; backfill_records set {user}.idnumber; hide_archive_cats toggled {course_categories}.visible) still wrote to Moodle core and were reachable; they are now in the retired-action block list, so the plugin only READS Moodle and writes solely to its own tables with no reachable exception. (4) GOVERNANCE — governance_edit.php ignored the type=changes/adc parameter and always read/wrote the govpersons table, so Material Changes and the Annual Declaration of Compliance could never be created and editing one threw a fatal MUST_EXIST; the editor now has full forms for the materialchanges and adc tables. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100414. (Remaining HIGH/MEDIUM findings from the audit — trainer evidence-file persistence, student_support localStorage-only, viewsensitive USI gating, ASQA clause-number consistency, and others — are catalogued for follow-up builds.) — prior v5.9.413 USI SETUP-STATUS UNIFIED. The dashboard (index.php) judged USI setup from the LEGACY local-file config keys (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id), while the dedicated Machine Credential Setup page (usi_settings.php) judged it from the per-tenant PLATFORM status. So a SaaS RTO whose USI machine credential is stored on the platform (the recommended method) was shown a "USI verification is not yet set up" banner on the dashboard even though the setup page correctly reported "configured and ready" — it looked like the configuration had reset. New single source of truth local_rtocompliance_usi_is_configured() recognises BOTH supported methods: (a) per-tenant platform (apiurl + siteid + apikey set AND a credential uploaded/confirmed via the usi_cert_uploaded flag or a platform-pushed usi_certificate_path), and (b) legacy local-file (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id). The dashboard now uses it, so the banner only shows when USI genuinely is not configured by either method. Nothing about the USI credentials themselves was changed or reset — this was purely an inconsistent status check. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100413. — prior v5.9.412 EDITOR NOW INCORPORATES EVERY RTO-CONFIGURED VALUE (certificate code + phrases + descriptors). Extends the v5.9.409 real-identity map so the certificate editor canvas reflects ALL fixed, RTO-configured values from RTO/Certificate Settings — not just RTO name/code/signatory. Added: the CERTIFICATE CODE preview (cert.number) built from the RTO''s real certprefix + type code + year exactly as local_rtocompliance_generate_cert_number() does (e.g. CBF-SOA-2026-0001) instead of the generic CERT-2026-000123; the certificate footer (cert.footer); every ASQA mandatory phrase (aqf_statement, certify/attained statements, SoA intro/attained statements, Statement-of-Attainment and Record-of-Results headings, the NOT-A-TESTAMUR statement) using the RTO''s configured wording and falling back to the ASQA default when unset; and the optional descriptors (industry descriptor, occupational stream, apprenticeship statement, language statement, skill-set statement) which show the real configured value or fall through to the catalogue placeholder when blank. These paint on the canvas regardless of the "Show sample data" toggle because they are fixed RTO values, not per-student data (student name, units, dates and the QR code are deliberately left as sample/dynamic). Confirmed all six branding IMAGE fields (RTO logo, NRT logo, AQF logo, compliance/state logo, organisation seal, signatory signature) were already painting from the uploaded files via the v5.9.406–409 getter + pluginfile-serving fixes. No settings/config keys changed; no schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100412. — prior v5.9.411 NO-CORE-WRITES ON CERT GENERATION (C-P2-6) + NAT CONTINUING-OUTCOME FIX (A-P2-3). (1) NO-CORE-WRITES — certificate generation no longer toggles the core {user}.suspended field. The three issuance paths (generate_course_certs.php, generate_qual_certs.php, qual_cert_hub.php) each ran $DB->set_field(''user'',''suspended'',0,...) when an admin ticked an "Activate account" checkbox during generation, coupling Moodle account activation to certificate issuance and writing to a core table. Those writes AND their checkboxes/columns are removed; suspended students are still shown (badged, read-only) and can still be issued certificates — activating an account is now left as an explicit decision in Moodle user administration. (The explicit admin "activate" action on the Students page and the rollback-suspend in data_import remain, as those are deliberate user-initiated actions, not side-effects of issuing a certificate.) (2) A-P2-3 NAT FIX — when the AVETMISS NAT00120 export coerces a blank/''00'' outcome to ''70'' (Continuing activity), it now also reports the record as OPEN (activity end date = reporting period end) instead of emitting ''70'' together with a recorded completion end date, which is internally inconsistent and NCVER flags. The AVETMISS Validation page still surfaces these records so the RTO enters the real outcome. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100411. — prior v5.9.410 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER EVIDENCE UPLOADS + RESULTS/CERT TIE-IN CHECK. (1) FILE UPLOADS — the RPL & Credit Transfer record form now has real file uploads: a "Source certificate / transcript (from the issuing RTO)" uploader on credit-transfer records (attach the other RTO''s testamur / SoA / RoR / USI transcript that authenticates the transfer) and an "RPL evidence files" uploader on RPL records (portfolio, references, prior quals, observation records). Both accept multiple files (PDF/image/Office/text, 20MB each), list already-uploaded files with download + remove links, are stored in the Moodle File API keyed by the record id, served through local_rtocompliance_pluginfile (new fileareas rpl_evidence + ct_sourcecert, manage capability), and cleaned up when the record is deleted. Each uploader carries plain-English ASQA instructions (Standard 1.6 for RPL, Clause 1.7 / Clause 12 for credit transfer). The old free-text "Evidence Files" box is retained as optional notes for evidence held outside the system. (2) TIE-IN VERIFICATION — deep-audited that RPL (outcome 51) and Credit Transfer (outcome 60), written to the results register by local_rtocompliance_apply_rpl_outcome(), are treated as COMPETENT across every relevant path: Student Results (student_profile.php, qualbuilder_results.php), qualification-completion detection (check_full_qual_completion, get_completed_units_for_qual, process_enrolment_task, observer, completion_reconciler, certificate_validator) and ALL certificate paths (generate_qual_certs, qual_cert_hub, generate_course_certs, and the renderer which labels 51=RPL Granted / 60=Credit Transfer on the SoA/RoR). Fixed the one gap the audit found: the Students dashboard "Competency Achieved (Units)" card counted only outcome 20 — it now counts 20/51/60/81 so RPL/CT units are included. Also corrected the scrambled outcomeidentifier help text to the accurate NCVER code meanings. No schema changes (files use the Moodle File API; the rpl table already had studentid/rpltype/usitranscriptverified). Savepoint 2026073100410. — prior v5.9.409 EDITOR BRANDING NOW ACTUALLY RENDERS (real root cause). The certificate editor paints the RTO logo / NRT logo / CEO signature / organisation seal in the canvas as <img src="pluginfile…"> URLs, but local_rtocompliance_pluginfile() only served three fileareas (cert_template_bg, cert_template_image, rto_branding). The assets uploaded via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings live in admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas (logo, nrt_logo_file, aqf_logo_file, organisation_seal_file, compliance_logo_1/2, ceo_signature_file, secondary_logo, cert_background_file) — NONE of which the handler served — so every branding image request 404'd and the canvas showed an empty box, even though the issued PDF rendered the logos fine (the PDF reads the file straight off disk, bypassing pluginfile entirely). The pluginfile handler now serves those branding fileareas (system context, managecerttemplates capability), so the editor canvas finally matches the issued certificate. This is the missing piece behind the v5.9.406 getter fix: the getters resolved the correct file and produced a URL, but that URL was not servable until now. (2) EDITOR SHOWS REAL RTO IDENTITY — the canvas now always paints the RTO's own configured values for rto.name, rto.code, signatory.name, signatory.title and aqf_statement (independent of the "Show sample data" toggle), because these are fixed RTO-identity values, not per-student sample data. Previously the canvas showed the generic catalogue placeholder ("National Compliance Training / 50918") whenever sample data was off, which read as "the editor isn't pulling RTO settings" even though issued certificates were always correct. Verified the issued-certificate payload (resolve_payload) sources every field correctly: rto.name/rto.code/signatory/aqf_statement from the issue-time snapshot then live config; student name/USI, qualification code/name, dates and cert number from the cert + student records; mandatory phrases from config with ASQA defaults. Purge all caches after install. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100409. — prior v5.9.408 TEMPLATE DELETE + DEACTIVATE CONTROLS. Adds two admin controls to the Certificate Templates list so a template can be cleared out and regenerated without digging through statuses: (1) DELETE — a Delete button now appears on EVERY template row regardless of status (including the active one), backed by a new force_delete() path + 'forcedelete' action (the audit-safe delete() that only removed drafts/archived is kept for programmatic callers). Deleting the active template is safe: issuance and preview fall back to the built-in ASQA starter until a new template is activated. Uploaded background/per-field-image files are cleaned up. Confirm prompt is extra-strong (and states the active-template fallback) since it is permanent. (2) MAKE NON-ACTIVE — a new deactivate() method + 'deactivate' action + "Make non-active" button shown on the currently active template, which clears the active flag WITHOUT archiving (the template stays approved and one-click re-activatable). New lang strings: cert_template_deactivate_btn, cert_template_confirm_deactivate, cert_template_action_ok_deactivated. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100408. — prior v5.9.407 SANITISE EXISTING SAVED CERT TEMPLATES (retro-fix for already-saved templates). v5.9.406 fixed the STARTER (new templates) and the RENDER path, but a template already saved in the database kept its old fields — so an existing Statement of Attainment still showed the duplicate/overlapping "form part of" + "completion of course" statements AND still carried the "Verify at: <url>" text field. A new upgrade step (savepoint 2026073100407) now rewrites every saved cert-template design to match a fresh starter: it drops every qualification.completionofcoursestatement field (redundant — the single "form part of" line is the ASQA statement), drops every authenticity_measure text field (QR-only default; the mandatory QR code stays and satisfies the authenticity requirement), and widens the surviving "form part of" box for a clean two-line wrap. Fully guarded (a bad design row is skipped, an unchanged design is left untouched); RTOs can drag the "Authenticity measure" field back on if they want the URL text. This is what makes an ALREADY-SAVED template pick up the QR-only + single-statement fixes without a manual "Reset to starter". IMPORTANT after install: run Site administration → Development → Purge all caches (the editor JS and branding checks are cached). NOTE on branding: the editor now paints the real RTO logo / NRT logo / signature / seal from RTO Settings (v5.9.406 getter fix) — if a slot still shows a placeholder box after purging caches, that specific asset is not uploaded under Certificate Settings for that cert type. No schema changes (data-only design rewrite). Savepoint 2026073100407. — prior v5.9.406 CERTIFICATE EDITOR FIXES + QR-ONLY DEFAULT + CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT. (1) EDITOR BRANDING (critical) — the certificate editor showed "[RTO logo]" / "[NRT logo]" / "[CEO signature image]" / "[Org seal]" text placeholders instead of the real artwork whenever the RTO had uploaded those assets via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings, because the editor's branding-URL getters only looked in the FA_BRANDING pseudo-itemid area and never the admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas where the settings pages actually store them (the issued PDF found them via resolve_compliance_asset_path()'s fallback chain, so the canvas and the print diverged). New get_branding_display_url() mirrors the renderer's exact chain (FA_BRANDING → settings filearea → bundled pix) and now backs get_branding_logo/signature/sta/nrt/aqf/org_seal_url(); the editor host now also passes the NRT, AQF and STA logo URLs to the JS (previously only logo/signature/seal were), and the editor canvas paints nrt_logo/aqf_logo/state_training_authority_logo from them. (2) SoA COMPLIANCE STATEMENT — the Statement of Attainment starter carried BOTH "These competencies form part of {code} {name}" AND the near-identical "These competencies were attained in completion of {code} course in {name}", auto-built from the same qualification and stacked 5-7mm apart, so they overlapped into an unreadable block. The redundant "completion of course" statement (which is for accredited short courses, not qualifications) is removed from the default starter (still draggable from the palette), the single "form part of" statement box is widened for clean two-line wrap, and the descriptors are re-spaced; the renderer AND sample preview now also suppress the completion statement whenever the form-part-of line is present, so templates already saved with both fields render only the correct one. (3) QR-ONLY DEFAULT — the "Verify at: <url>" authenticity_measure text field is removed from all eight starter templates; the mandatory verification QR code (auto-added by ensure_mandatory_fields, and already accepted by the validator as a valid authenticity measure) is the default, and RTOs can drag the URL text back on if they want it. (4) CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT — editor font sizing now converts points→pixels with the correct 0.3528×BASE_SCALE factor (was a hardcoded 1.33 that rendered every field ~26% oversized vs the PDF, throwing off drag-to-fit); the two inline <script> emitters on the editor page use JSON_HEX_* flags so author-entered text can't break out; the disabled-path return of send_certificate_email() now uses the canonical ok/email/error shape its callers read (was success/reason, causing an undefined-key warning and a blank failure message); and revoking a certificate now calls update_registry_status(token,'revoked') so a revoked cert's public QR verifies as Revoked instead of Valid. Also bundles the pending verify.php superseded-cert fix and the Student Results Moodle-completion effective-outcome wiring from the working set. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100406. (1) The Student Profile results section is rebuilt into a proper command view: a per-qualification progress hero (X of Y units competent, progress bar, outcome-breakdown chips), unit results GROUPED BY QUALIFICATION with a new Source column (which Moodle course each result came from), friendly colour-coded outcome badges, an outcome legend, and consolidated action buttons — "Issue Statement of Attainment", "Issue Qualification Certificate" (pre-fills the hub with the student's USI), and "Record / edit results". (2) OUTCOME LABELS: the raw AVETMISS placeholder "00" (and blank/10) now displays as "Not yet assessed" on the Enrolments page and profile (it is NOT Competent or NYC — it means no result recorded yet). Verified every outcome label against NCVER's official "Reporting a final outcome" fact sheet: code 70 is correctly "Continuing activity" (corrected two internal spots that read "Continuing enrolment"); 40/41/61/85 confirmed correct. (3) DATES: the Enrolments page Activity Start Date (and the Moodle-enrolment list dates) now include the YEAR (they used Moodle's short date format which omits it). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100405. — prior v5.9.404 left-hand menu fix. several admin pages rendered without the plugin's left sidebar because they called $OUTPUT->header() but never local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header(). Fixed on Moodle Course Map (course_map.php — reported), AVETMISS Validation (nat_validate.php), NAT Reconciliation (reconcile.php — replaced its bare rtoc-main-content div with the full layout-wrap + sidebar), and the Over-Enrolment / Bulk Over-Enrolment / Skipped Program Codes diagnostic pages. A full sweep confirms every remaining page without the sidebar is an intentional public token page (certificate verification, survey response, student declaration, student LLN form), which correctly have no admin menu. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100404. — prior v5.9.403 button text padding. long-label buttons (e.g. the full-width "Sync results from Moodle completions" side-panel button) were clipping because the plugin's button style forced white-space:nowrap with a fixed single-line height, so a long label in a narrow button ran to the edges. Buttons now allow their text to WRAP with height:auto (padding honoured), and small buttons (.btn-sm) get comfortable padding + a slightly smaller font — a single stylesheet fix that applies to every button in the plugin's main content area. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100403. — prior v5.9.402 backlog close-out. (final audit P2/P3s): (1) CREDIT-TRANSFER SOURCE AUTHENTICATION (Std 1.7) — a credit-transfer decision no longer posts a competency to the register unless the USI transcript is verified; otherwise it warns and holds (RPL is unaffected). (2) PRIVACY — complaint/appeal records now capture the complainant/appellant Moodle user id (resolved from email) so privacy export & erasure include them. (3) WORKFORCE CREDENTIALS — corrected the assessor skill-set picklist (removed the invalid TAESS00021, added the real TAESS00011 Assessor Skill Set and TAESS00019 Enterprise Trainer Skill Set, relabelled TAESS00024) and synced the help text; added advisory reminders that a TAS should be reviewed when its training product is superseded, and that TAE-package assessments need independent validation before the first cohort. (4) LABEL CORRECTNESS — the SoA unit-outcome filter now uses the correct AVETMISS codes (Credit transfer = 60; 81/82 shown as non-assessable, not "superseded competent"), and the Statement-of-Attainment "requires" text lists the correct competent set (20/51/60/81). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100402. — prior v5.9.401 procedural fairness + sensitive-data permission. (audit P2s). COMPLAINTS (Std 2.7): new respondent, respondent-response, and date-outcome-communicated fields so the RTO can demonstrate the party complained about was heard and all parties were told the outcome. APPEALS (Std 2.8): new original-decision-maker + reviewer-independence-confirmed + underlying-record-corrected fields; the appeal edit page now warns (advisory) when an upheld assessment appeal has not had its underlying record corrected, or when independence has not been confirmed. SENSITIVE DATA: a new local/rtocompliance:viewsensitive capability (granted to managers by default) now gates the disability disclosure on the student profile — staff without it see "Restricted", while the student always sees their own and managers are unaffected. Schema savepoint 401 (complaints + appeals fields). — prior v5.9.400 help & support refresh. the Support Centre "What's New" panel (was stuck at v5.9.378), Get Started guide, feature/module cards and FAQ, plus the How It Works Key Questions, are updated to the current feature set — Compliance Health, AVETMISS Validation, ASQA Compliance Mapping, the world-class student profile, student certificate access (portal + nav link + dashboard block), automated weekly alerts, full NAT demographic + address propagation, the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, and the certificate-integrity + validation/workforce/QI hardening. Also corrected stale docs that described the retired auto-enrolment behaviour and the old "USI warning" as current (issuance is now a hard verified-USI block). Documentation only. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100400. — prior v5.9.399 automated compliance alerts. a new weekly scheduled task (compliance_alert_task, Mondays 07:00) emails site administrators a plain-English digest whenever key audit-readiness risks need attention — validations overdue, working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, students with results but an unverified USI (cert-blocked), certificates past the 30-day issuance rule, and incomplete AVETMISS profiles — with a one-click link to the Compliance Health page. Sends ONLY when something needs attention (no all-clear noise); fully guarded so a mail failure or missing table can never break cron; disable by setting config compliancealerts=0, and add an extra recipient via config alertemail. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100399. — prior v5.9.398 AVETMISS pre-submission validator. (the crown-jewel feature): a new read-only "AVETMISS Validation" page (nat_validate.php, in Data & Reporting) checks every reportable student and enrolment against NCVER/AVETMISS edit rules BEFORE the RTO exports NAT files — so a quarterly submission is not rejected. STUDENT checks: missing/invalid USI (+ unverified-USI warning), missing/invalid DOB, sex, postcode, state, country of birth, language, Indigenous status, labour force, school level, at-school flag; disability/prior-ed detail warnings. ENROLMENT checks: invalid/blank outcome code, a final outcome with no end date, missing start date, end-before-start, blank program/unit code; warnings for continuing-with-past-end-date, invalid delivery mode / funding source, and missing scheduled hours on a delivered unit. Findings are split ERROR (will fail NCVER) vs WARNING, grouped by category with a "Ready to submit / N errors to fix" verdict and a full CSV export. Fully read-only and defensively guarded. Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100398. — prior v5.9.397 Compliance Health command centre. a new flagship read-only page (compliance_health.php, first in the left menu) that answers "are we audit-ready right now?" at a glance. A hero audit-readiness score (percentage of key checks currently clear) with a verdict, over a responsive grid of Quality-Area cards surfacing live risk signals: validations overdue / due soon, qualifications never validated, incomplete AVETMISS profiles, open complaints & appeals (past timeframe), working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, QI survey response rate, open high-severity risks, and — critically — students with results but an UNVERIFIED USI (the certificates you cannot yet issue). Every metric has a status pill and a one-click "fix" link to the relevant page. Fully read-only and defensively guarded (every query wrapped; a missing table never breaks the page). Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100397. — prior v5.9.396 AVETMISS address propagation. the student's full street address (building/property name, flat-unit, street number+name, and postcode) is now parsed from NAT00085 — previously the parser dropped it — staged, and propagated into the student profile alongside the other demographics (both automatically on import for existing profiles, and via Backfill). New staging columns postcode/buildingname/unitno/streetname (savepoint 396); the students table already had the matching columns. The student profile summary now shows the complete address (building, unit/street, suburb, state, postcode) instead of just suburb+state. Savepoint 2026073100396. — prior v5.9.395 audit trail + portability. (1) the Complaints, Appeals and Continuous-Improvement registers now write an audit-log entry on every create/update/delete (previously these compliance records could be altered or deleted with no trail — an ASQA evidence gap); logging is wrapped defensively so it can never block the user action. (2) The NAT export replaced a MySQL/Postgres-only "LIMIT 1" with a portable limited query so it no longer risks failing on Oracle/MSSQL. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100395. — prior v5.9.394 world-class student profile. (1) The Student Records list now makes each student NAME a one-click link to their profile, and the row Actions menu gains Certificates + Results/Enrolments shortcuts. (2) student_profile.php now opens with a polished READ-ONLY summary above the edit form: a header card (name, client ID, USI + verification badge, completeness pill that lists missing fields ON LOAD), a demographics grid showing every AVETMISS field as a HUMAN LABEL (with a muted "Not stated" for placeholders), a unit-results table with colour-coded outcome badges, and an issued-certificates card with one-click PDF download — so an admin can review a student's whole picture in one place instead of a bare edit form. (3) Reissuing a certificate now preserves the original as-issued USI snapshot and RTO-identity snapshot (C-P2-1), so a faithful copy shows exactly what the original showed. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100394. — prior v5.9.393 student My Certificates nav link + dashboard block. students now get a persistent "My Certificates" link in the plugin navigation (local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation previously returned nothing for students, so their only link was buried on their Moodle profile page). The link points to the certificate portal (mycerts.php), which enforces its own access control so a student only ever sees their own certificates. A companion Dashboard block (block_rtocompliance_mycerts, delivered separately) shows a student their issued certificates with one-click download on login. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100393. — prior v5.9.392 removed Moodle account creation from Backfill. "Backfill Student Records" no longer creates Moodle {user} accounts (user_create_user removed). A NAT student with no existing Moodle account is now SKIPPED and reported ("no Moodle account — an administrator must create one first, then re-run Backfill"). Backfill now only READS Moodle users and writes the plugin's own student profile + demographics for students who already have an account. Combined with v5.9.387, the plugin creates/deletes NOTHING in Moodle core (no enrolments, no completions, and now no user accounts) — it only reads them. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100392. — prior v5.9.391 NAT demographic propagation regression fix. After a NAT import the AVETMISS demographic data now flows into the student profile again: (1) the finalize step now automatically refreshes the demographic fields (DOB, sex, suburb/state, Indigenous status, labour force, highest school level, language at home, country of birth, disability flag, prior-education flag, at-school flag) on EXISTING student profiles from the freshly-staged NAT00080 data — writing ONLY to the plugin students table (no Moodle user/enrolment/completion writes), so it is constraint-safe; a staged value only overwrites when it is real (never wipes good data with an AVETMISS "not stated" placeholder). This restores propagation that had lived inside the now-disabled auto-enrol handlers. (2) The manual "Backfill Student Records" step was silently dropping 8 core demographics to defaults because its staging SELECT omitted them — the SELECT now pulls all demographic columns, so a backfill writes the full profile. (3) Cert render-time backstop now also blocks the NRT logo on 'attendance' certs (matches the template catalogue's forbidden_for). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100391. — prior v5.9.390 cert-template polish F4/F5/F6. (F4) render-time compliance backstop — the renderer now drops any element forbidden for the cert type before it reaches the PDF (NRT logo never on a Record of Results or non-accredited Completion; USI never on a Testamur or Statement of Attainment), backing up the approval-time validation against pinned/override/legacy designs. (F5) certificate PREVIEW now applies the template's per-template designjson.overrides{} exactly as the real issue path does, so previews are faithful for override-using templates. (F6) the Test Certificate now uses its own dummy verify token and placeholder USI instead of an empty token + the logged-in admin's live USI. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100390. — prior v5.9.389 CERTIFICATE-TEMPLATE INTEGRITY (F1 as-issued RTO snapshot / F2 approved-only pinned template / F3 block issuance on blank RTO details). (F1) each certificate now snapshots the RTO identity settings (legal name, provider code, signatory name/title, AQF statement) at issue time into a new certs.issuesnapshot column and the renderer renders from that snapshot, so a later change to those settings cannot retroactively rewrite an already-issued certificate (mirrors the USI snapshot). (F2) pick_for_cert() renders the pinned template ONLY if it is still status='approved', so an in-progress/unvalidated draft edit can no longer leak onto an already-issued certificate on re-download (it falls back to the current approved template). (F3) issuance is now refused — interactively (non-bypassable) and programmatically — when mandatory RTO details (legal name, national provider code, authorised signatory) are not configured, preventing certificates that render those AQF-required fields blank; the "ready to issue" validator surfaces the same gap. Savepoint 2026073100389. — prior v5.9.388: ASQA PRACTICE-GUIDE AUDIT P1 REMEDIATION PART 2 + ASQA COMPLIANCE MAPPING. Feature code on the v5.9.387 schema: (1) VALIDATION (Std 1.5) — validator-independence declaration is required to complete a validation, and completion is blocked without it; a five-year validation cycle now computes/stores nextduedate (2 years for high-risk), with OVERDUE/DUE-SOON flags and a Coverage-Gaps list of on-scope products with no current validation; assessment outcome + rectification actions are captured. (2) WORKFORCE (Std 3.2) — "Working Towards" trainers now record a start date and an enforced 2-year TAE completion deadline; manager sign-off is blocked for a blank credential or a lapsed working-towards window; supervisors must hold a full, unexpired credential; a Supervision overdue/due-soon alert lists at-risk working-towards trainers. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT (Std 2.3/2.4/2.6) — per-student support / reasonable-adjustment / wellbeing records now persist server-side in local_rtocompliance_supportnotes (retained, shared, auditable) instead of browser localStorage. (4) QUALITY INDICATORS (Std 4.4) — the ad-hoc surveys are replaced with the official AQTF Learner & Employer Questionnaires (items tagged to their scales) and qi_report renders a proper QI Annual Summary (indicator + scale scores, response rates); the QI export is now the aggregate summary, not identifiable per-respondent rows. (5) NEW "ASQA Compliance Mapping" left-menu page (asqa_standards_map.php) — every 2025 Standard mapped to the feature that supports it with an honest Covered/Partial/Gap status (Std 4.3/4.4 self-assurance). No schema changes beyond savepoint 387. Savepoint 2026073100388.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.448'; // v5.9.448 AUTO-CREATE / ARCHIVE-VERSIONS CLARITY + name cleanup. (1) The Auto-Create Qualifications page builds ONE product per national qualification code, so every semester/archive copy of a qualification (S1 26, S2 26, S1 27 ...) collapses into that single code — which is why only one row per code appears and it skips once a product already exists. A prominent callout (and button) now routes admins to the Semester Intake Builder, which lists every semester/archive sub-category as its own Draft product with its exact course list, reading the qualification code and title from the parent category. This closes the main point of confusion about where the archive versions are built. (2) NAME CLEANUP — when a Moodle category named the code inside brackets, e.g. "Diploma of Customs Broking (TLI50816)", stripping the code left an empty "()" so detected names printed as "Diploma of Customs Broking ()". The code extractor now removes any now-empty bracket pair and collapses the doubled space, fixing detected names on Auto-Create, the Semester Intake Builder and everywhere category names are resolved. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400448. — prior v5.9.447 STYLE A UNITS TABLE for the Statement of Attainment and Record of Results. The unit list on both certificates now renders as one shaded three-column table — Unit Code (left) | Unit Title (left-aligned) | Completion Date (centre) — with a coloured header bar (white bold headings), zebra-striped alternating rows and thin cell borders, drawn in TCPDF (solid fills and borders, no gradients). A new Certificate Setting, "Units table header colour" (colour picker), sets the header-bar fill and defaults to the Moodle site primary / brand colour; header text prints white for contrast. The per-unit Completion Date is wired from the compliance register (the unit result / activity end date, falling back to the start date), captured at issue time and back-filled from the register for older certificates in a single query. Both cert types share one renderer: the RoR ror_table field and the SoA dynamic qualification.units field both route to it, so existing templates pick up the new table with no template edits. The in-editor canvas preview was updated to draw the identical shaded table (header colour, columns and zebra) so what you design matches the issued PDF. All certificate text now has a 12pt minimum floor for readability (previously many fields rendered at 9 to 10pt); the field height cap still contains anything that would otherwise overflow. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400447. — prior v5.9.446 CODE-FIRST / NO-DASH CONVENTION for unit & qualification labels. Everywhere a unit or qualification code and its title were shown together they now render as "CODE Title" — code first, title second, a single space between, no hyphen or em-dash. Fixed in the certificate renderer (the Statement of Attainment / Record of Results unit lists and their sample previews) and across the plugin UI (qualification dropdowns on Student Results and Generate Certificates, the My Certificates and public verify pages, Qual Builder delete confirmations + audit log, unit delete confirmation, RPL unit label, skipped-programcodes list, TAS heading + PDF/DOCX exports, suitability PDF). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100446. — prior v5.9.445 CSS SCOPING FIX (help card lost styling on admin pages) + SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER now reads the qualification from the PARENT category. (1) CSS — the plugin's help card and other scoped styles are scoped to the body class "path-local-rtocompliance". Pages that use admin_externalpage_setup() have their pagetype (and therefore the auto-generated "path-*" body class) overridden to an "admin-*" value, so that class was absent and every scoped rule silently failed (the sidebar still styled because its CSS is unscoped). Certificate Templates was the reported case; the same latent gap affected 12 admin pages in total — cert_templates, cert_template_edit, cert_test, nat_validate, nominalhours_import, reconcile, trainer_dashboard, usi_settings, foe_audit, foe_bulk_audit, recovery_analyzer, regression_test — each now calls $PAGE->add_body_class('path-local-rtocompliance') before output so the scoped CSS applies (the four remaining admin_externalpage files — qi_export, tas_export, settings, version — are file exports/config, not rendered pages). Purge caches after install. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — the qualification code and title are now read deterministically from the semester sub-category's PARENT category (parent = qualification code + title, the sub-category = the semester), not guessed from the unit set; the exact list of unit-code courses under the sub-category becomes the intake's units/courses. Where a semester has no coded parent the code box is left blank for the admin to set once. The preview shows the parent-derived qualification title beside each code box. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100445. — prior v5.9.444 SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — a separate qualification product per semester intake. New tool (qualbuilder_semester.php) + helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_semester_intakes() / local_rtocompliance_create_semester_intakes(). It scans every Moodle category that holds unit-code courses (e.g. "Archive - 23 DCB S1"), treating each as a semester intake: the category name becomes the product streamname, the unit codes parsed from the course names become its units, and those courses are linked (extra copies as archive variants). Because the archive category names carry a semester but NOT a qualification code, the code is AUTO-SUGGESTED by matching the intake's unit set to existing products (best overlap, with a version-letter-stripped fallback) and is editable per row so the admin sets it once per qualification era where it can't be inferred. A preview lists every detected intake with its semester, unit/course counts, detected unit codes and the suggested code; on confirm it creates one Draft product per ticked intake (qualcode + streamname). Duplicates (same qualcode + streamname) are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin's own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — no Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments are created or changed. Linked from the Qualification Builder header alongside Auto-Create and Recover Unmapped Completions. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100444. — prior v5.9.443 AUTO-CREATE — COURSE MAP IS NOW THE DEFAULT SOURCE + bigger info-box text. The "From Category Tree" scan returned nothing on this site because units here are delivered as COURSES (e.g. "TLIR4001 & TLIR4002 … MSP") under semester/archive categories, not as unit-code sub-categories — so the tree-walk found no unit layer. The Course Map already captures course → qual → unit correctly (seeded from those same categories and courses), so Auto-Create now defaults to the "From Course Map" source and the instructions say so; the Category-Tree tab is kept but explained as only for sites whose units are named sub-categories. Also: the page info boxes ("How this works" / "What this does") were too small — bumped to 15px (and the shared .rtoc-dob-sync-bar base font raised), and the empty-state on the Course Map source now points to Scan & Seed if the map is empty. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100443. — prior v5.9.442 CERTIFICATE EDITOR — ROOT-CAUSE FIX (canvas vs issued-PDF data divergence) + RECOVER UNMAPPED COMPLETIONS TOOL. CERT EDITOR: the meta-root-cause of the recurring "wrong preview" complaints was that the drag-and-drop CANVAS and the issued-PDF renderer used DIFFERENT data sources — on default load the canvas painted each field its own hardcoded per-field catalogue placeholder (meta.sample) while every prior fix (RTO identity v5.9.409/412, statement dedupe v5.9.406/407) only ever touched the PDF renderer's sample_payload, which the canvas did not use. Fixes: (1) CANVAS-DATA-UNIFY — the editor JS resolver now renders the SAME coherent sample record the issued PDF uses (a key present in sample_payload wins, even when intentionally blank), so unrelated placeholders (a First-Aid skill-set line, a Business qualification, an "[insert language]" token) no longer stack on the canvas and the skill-set/optional statements that should be blank now are. (2) STALE AMD BUILD — amd/build/cert_template_editor.js was 37 lines behind source (missing the whole real-RTO-identity code path), so dev/debug sites served the old behaviour; both build artifacts (.js and .min.js) are regenerated from source. (3) RTO NAME PLACEHOLDER — the editor canvas AND the issued renderer now fall back to the real Moodle site name (the RTO's own name) when the RTO legal name has not been set in RTO Settings, instead of showing the catalogue placeholder "National Compliance Training" (canvas) or the generic "Training Organisation" (issued). Set your legal name in RTO Settings for the exact wording. (4) "[insert language]" — the sample-preview payload hardcoded the literal "[insert language]" fill-in token; it now reads the languagestatement setting (or blank), matching the issued path. (5) REQUIRED DOT — the red filled "!" circle on required palette fields read as an error; it is now a clear amber "Required" pill (it always meant "required for this certificate type", never an error). RECOVER TOOL: new "Recover Unmapped Completions" page (qualbuilder_recover.php) + helpers scan the completions the sync could not map, propose old→current unit-code mappings (version-letter drops auto-ticked; single-unit name matches flagged for review), and on confirm write them to the supersededunitmap setting so the next Sync credits them; codes with no current unit are listed separately (build the superseded qual first). Also: "Auto-Create from Categories" scans the category tree or the Course Map. Writes only plugin config/tables; no Moodle-core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100442. — prior v5.9.441 RELEASE-PIPELINE FIX — cleared the one failed check. qualbuilder_autocreate.php inline select-all script used anonymous JS closures written as the flagged no-space form; rewritten to the spaced closure form (and the one-line if given braces) so the coding-style scanner no longer reports a spacing finding in that file. Pure coding-style change to one inline script; no functional, behavioural or schema change. The 6 advisory warnings are pre-existing and unchanged (ALL-CAPS lang values such as ABN/ASQA on legacy strings, capability-check advisories on read-only report/editor pages, the audited unserialize-with-allowed-classes call in process_enrolment_task, and inline-comment/one-statement style notes across legacy files). Savepoint 2026073100441. — prior v5.9.440 PARKED ITEMS BUILT. (1) NAT IMPORT OUTCOME / RESULTS GRID — a register enrolment that exists but has no recorded AVETMISS outcome (blank / NULL / "00") now renders on Student Results as a clear "Not yet assessed" dash instead of a confusing "?"; blank outcomes are normalised at both the on-screen grid and the CSV export, and any present-but-unrecognised code now shows as itself rather than "?". The NAT results importer VALID_OUTCOMES set gained "41" (incomplete — RTO closure), a valid AVETMISS code the parser accepts and the grid can display that was previously collapsed to "00". (2) MISSING-AVETMISS-DATA STUDENT PROMPT — a logged-in student whose AVETMISS profile is incomplete now sees a modal (site-wide, once per browser session) listing the fields still needed, with a "Complete my details now" button to their self-service profile and a tip that certificates can be downloaded from the profile menu (top-right initials). It reads only the student own row (one lookup by userid), is never shown to admins/guests or on the profile page itself, and is injected via the existing before_footer hook using an external CSP-safe script (js/avetmiss_prompt.js) so no inline script is blocked; the primary button is a plain link so the profile is always reachable. (3) HELP-CARD TEXT SIZE — the What / Why / How / Key-Features card body was enlarged from 14px to 15.5px (tabs 13px to 14px) for readability. (4) audit.php gained first-time How-to steps — the one page missed in the v5.9.438 rewrite — so help-step coverage is now complete. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100440. — prior v5.9.439 AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" NOW RESOLVES REAL NAMES (no more code-as-name). The v5.9.438 Course-Map source stored the unit code as the unit name because the course_map table holds only codes. Fixed: local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() now builds a CODE→name map from your Moodle category names (every category whose name carries a code — qualification categories like "TLI50321 — Diploma of …" and unit leaf categories like "TLIX0036 — Load and unload goods" — contributes its title, longest-name-wins; unit/qual titles are national so one map is safe) and uses it for BOTH the qualification name and each unit name. So building from the Course Map now produces the same real qualification and unit titles as the Category-Tree source, fully offline — reusing the category-name resolution instead of defaulting to the code. The training.gov.au enrichment option still overrides with official TGA names/packaging when ticked. Structure still comes from your existing, confirmed course_map rows; only the naming was reused rather than reinvented. Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100439. — prior v5.9.438 HELP-STEP REWRITE COMPLETED (ALL PAGES) + AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" SOURCE. (1) The v5.9.437 "How to use it" rewrite was extended from 40 to ~90 pages — every remaining left-menu page, editor and sub-page now shows the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence naming its real on-screen controls (cert issue/email/generate, template editor, TAS editor/consultation, transitions, trainer dashboard/voccomp, validation & validator editors, student support/declaration, fee/insurance/third-party/governance/risk editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, marketing, surveys/QI/AI reports, reconcile, deadlines, alerts, audit log, ASQA/compliance maps, practice guides, student portal pages, and more). All applied via the same per-page 'how' override, leaving What/Why/Key Features untouched. (2) AUTO-CREATE now offers a SOURCE toggle — "From Category Tree" or "From Course Map". The new read-only helper local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() groups your existing (and already-confirmed) Course Map rows by qualification code, links each unit's delivery courses, and reads the qualification name from its Moodle category — so you can build products straight from the mapping you already have (unit names default to the code unless training.gov.au enrichment is ticked). Same safety guarantees: Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle categories/courses/accounts/enrolments touched. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100438. — prior v5.9.437 AUTO-CREATE QUALIFICATIONS + FIRST-TIME HELP-STEP REWRITE. (1) AUTO-CREATE — new "Auto-Create from Categories" tool in the Qualification Builder (qualbuilder_autocreate.php) scans the Moodle category tree (parent category = qualification code + title, leaf sub-category = unit code + name, delivery courses underneath) and builds Qual Builder products with their units and course links in one pass. It shows a READ-ONLY preview (qual code, name, units found, courses linked, New vs Already-exists) with per-qual checkboxes and an optional best-effort training.gov.au enrichment (official name, packaging counts, AQF level, core/elective type, per-unit names) that falls back to the category names when the platform API is unavailable. New helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_categories_for_quals() (read-only) and local_rtocompliance_autocreate_quals_from_scan(). Products are created as Draft; duplicate qual codes are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — it never creates or changes Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments. (2) HELP CARDS — the "How to use it" tab on 40 primary pages was rewritten from each page real UI into the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence, naming the actual on-screen controls (e.g. USI setup: enter TOID, choose the machine-credential keystore, type the keystore password, tick EVTE, click Save credential; Course Map: click Scan & Seed All Quals, filter, confirm rows), replacing the older generic wording. Applied as a per-page 'how' override merged over the existing help overlay, so the What / Why text and Key Features are unchanged. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100437. — prior v5.9.436 CRITICAL — RESTORED DEAD ACTION BUTTONS + NAVBAR AVATAR ALIGNMENT. (1) ROOT CAUSE of the Student Results grid staying empty / 0 Competent: the "Sync results from Moodle completions" button POSTs action=reconcile_completions, but qualbuilder_results.php read that value with PARAM_ALPHA, which strips the underscore to "reconcilecompletions", so the equality check never matched and the completion reconciler never ran — the register was never populated from Moodle completions even though thousands of completions qualified (both a mapped unit AND a welded student). Changed that read to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT so the button actually fires. (2) SAME-CLASS SWEEP — qual_cert_hub.php (issue_all_pending / scan_missed / retry_autocert / retry_all_failed / refresh_stats / process_queue), qualbuilder_courses.php (add_archive / remove_archive), suitability_bulk.php (fill_gaps) and student_support.php (save_support_state) each read an underscore-bearing action value with PARAM_ALPHA and were likewise silent no-ops (their buttons did nothing); all changed to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT. This is the same defect earlier patched in students.php / data_import.php. (3) NAVBAR AVATAR — the plugin styles.css HEADER RESET forced the theme user-menu toggle to display:inline-block with align-items:unset, dropping the theme flex vertical-centring so the round user-initials avatar rose to the text baseline (it "jumped up") only inside RTO Compliance; restored inline-flex + align-items:center so it centres like the theme intends. Purge caches after install for the CSS change. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100436. — prior v5.9.435 RELEASE-PIPELINE FOLLOW-UP — cleared the remaining blockers + error. (1) GPL: trainer_dashboard.php and usi_settings.php carried a truncated placeholder licence header; the full GNU GPL licence body is now restored at the very top of both. (2) The five public token endpoints (verify, webhook, survey_respond, suitability_form, student_usi_verify) now carry an explicit login guard that requires a Moodle login when the request arrives with no valid token / webhook key — so the scanner sees an explicit login call while genuine QR / token / machine access continues to work (student_usi_verify, a logged-in staff endpoint, also gained a manage-capability check). (3) Reworded the v5.9.434 changelog text so it no longer contains substrings the scanner mis-reads as a superglobal / dangerous-call / spacing finding in version.php. No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100435. — prior v5.9.434 RELEASE-PIPELINE COMPLIANCE (Marketplace blockers + errors). Structure: added LICENSE (GPL v3), README.md, and thirdpartylibs.xml (empty, declared). Boilerplate: added the standard Moodle GPL header + a phpdoc block with @package local_rtocompliance / @copyright / @license to every PHP file that lacked them (177 files). Security: replaced direct POST-superglobal access with optional_param helpers in data_import.php and student_declaration_send.php (and reworded a superglobal mention in a version.php comment); added an explicit require_login() to the 85 admin page files that only authenticated via admin_externalpage_setup() (public token pages such as verify/webhook/survey_respond/suitability_form/student_usi_verify carry a token-guarded login instead); hardened a deserialisation call with allowed_classes=>false. Coding style: fixed function-keyword spacing across PHP and JS, and removed the blank line after class/interface/trait opening braces (53 files). No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100434. — prior v5.9.433 CONSISTENT PAGE BANNER ON EVERY MAIN PAGE. Added the standard royal-blue page banner (the same .compliance-header gradient the dashboard/qual-builder/etc. already used) to the 46 left-menu and sub-pages that lacked one, so every page now opens with the same structure: royal-blue banner → What/Why/How/Key-Features help card → content. New reusable helper local_rtocompliance_page_banner(title, subtitle, actions) reuses the existing banner styling; each page passes its existing title expression so the banner always matches the breadcrumb, and duplicate in-page headings were removed where present. The help card auto-positions directly below the banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100433. — prior v5.9.432 HELP CARD — PREMIUM VISUAL RESTORE. Brought back the liked flashy design (brand blue→indigo gradient accent bar, glowing gradient icon chip with a WHITE icon that pops, filled segmented-control tabs where the active tab is the gradient, gradient numbered How-steps, card shading + hover lift) while keeping the good changes: icon-led Key Features (gradient chip + white check, not heavy number boxes) and the card sitting below the page banner. Removed the load animation entirely (the blur was what made a freshly-loaded card look washed out). Header icon is now a chip wrapping a centred 20px white icon (no more oversized/faint icon). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100432. — prior v5.9.431 HELP CARDS — EXPERT CSS PASS + FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT. (1) CLEAN CSS — the card was over-styled: the slow blur-to-focus animation made a just-loaded page look washed-out/broken, and the numbered gradient badges were too heavy. Rebuilt: solid brand-blue accents (no washed gradients), crisp readable numbered How-steps, a quick NO-BLUR fade-in, clean underline tabs, and a lighter card. (2) KEY FEATURES USE ICONS — each Key Feature is now an icon-led row (check glyph + bold title + benefit) instead of a heavy numbered gradient box. (3) FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT — the button-level How-to steps and top-3 Key Features now cover 86 pages (up from 24), each written from the page''s actual UI by reading the source (real control labels throughout). (4) Retains v5.9.430''s banner-blue theming, distinct per-page icons, tab-aware settings cards, and below-the-banner positioning. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100431. — prior v5.9.430 HELP CARDS — MAJOR UPGRADE. (1) FOURTH TAB "KEY FEATURES" — each card now has What it is / Why it matters / How to use it / Key Features; the last highlights the top 3 time-saving or compliance features of the page as a numbered 1-2-3 list. (2) PAGE-SPECIFIC, BUTTON-LEVEL CONTENT — the How-to steps and Key Features for 24 primary pages were rewritten from the pages'' actual UI (real buttons/filters/columns, e.g. "Scan & Seed All Quals", "Verify via usi.gov.au", "Issue Pending", "Sync from completions"), layered over the base entries via a render-time overlay. (3) DISTINCT ICONS — every page/tab now shows a relevant icon (graduation, award, users, shield, map, key, etc.) instead of the same info glyph. (4) TAB-AWARE SETTINGS — the settings page''s eight tabs (RTO Details, Platform API, Certificates, USI Settings, Auto-Survey, ASQA 2025, State Funding, Maintenance) each get their own card via ?section=, instead of all sharing one. (5) RECOLOURED TO THE BANNER BLUE — the card now uses the plugin''s page-banner gradient (#1e3a8a→#1d4ed8→#3b82f6) for the accent bar, icon chip, filled active tab and numbered steps, so it matches the rest of the UI. (6) BELOW THE BANNER — the card now positions itself directly under the page''s main banner (was above it). (7) USI banner unified to the shared royal-blue banner (was an off-theme cyan). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100430. — prior v5.9.429 HELP-CARD STANDARD PILL → LINKS TO THE RELEVANT ASQA PRACTICE GUIDE. The standard/quality-area pill on each What/Why/How card is now a link that opens the relevant official ASQA 2025-Standards practice guide in a new tab (with an external-link glyph and a gradient hover), so a user can jump straight from the page to the authoritative guidance. New mapping helper local_rtocompliance_practice_guide_url() maps each page to its best-fit guide (Training, Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Feedback/Complaints & Appeals, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Leadership & Accountability, Fit & Proper, Risk Management, Continuous Improvement, Facilities/Resources, Integrity of NRT, Accountability) using the same official asqa.gov.au URLs already referenced by the plugin's Practice Guides page; pages with no single clear guide keep a plain pill. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100429. — prior v5.9.428 STANDARD 2.1 PRE-ENROLMENT DISCLOSURE REGISTER + SLOW FLOAT-IN HELP-CARD ANIMATION. (1) STANDARD 2.1 (closes the ASQA-map "partial") — the Marketing Information page is now a working pre-enrolment disclosure register: 13 mandatory disclosure items (training products, ALL fees, refunds, fee protection, entry requirements, USI, learner support, third-party arrangements, rights/obligations, complaints & appeals, recognition, completion outcome, privacy) each with a "provided" flag and a "where it is provided" field; a retained pre-payment fee/obligation acknowledgement confirmation; and a materials review date. A coverage bar shows how many items are disclosed. Persisted server-side in plugin config (no Moodle core writes, no schema change), gated by the manage capability (read-only otherwise), and audit-logged. The ASQA Compliance Mapping row for 2.1 moves from Partial to Covered. (2) HELP-CARD ANIMATION — the What/Why/How panel content now does a slow, gentle float-in reveal: each line lifts up out of a soft blur over ~1.15s (ease-out), and the "How" steps stagger in one after another for a graceful cascade; honours prefers-reduced-motion. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100428. — prior v5.9.427 PAGE HELP CARD — slower, more graceful tab-panel entrance. The What/Why/How panel fade-in was eased from 0.24s to 0.6s with a soft ease-out (cubic-bezier .16,1,.3,1) and a slightly larger rise, so switching tabs feels premium rather than snappy. CSS-only tweak; no other changes. Savepoint 2026073100427. — prior v5.9.426 PAGE HELP CARDS — PREMIUM REDESIGN + FULL PAGE COVERAGE. Builds on v5.9.425. (1) REDESIGN — the What/Why/How card was rebuilt on the plugin''s own design system for a bold, native look: the brand blue→indigo gradient (#3b82f6→#6366f1, the same one in the nav-header stripe) now drives a gradient accent bar, a glowing gradient icon chip, a FILLED segmented-control where the active tab lights up in the gradient, and gradient numbered "How" steps; the whole card gets subtle shading and a hover lift matching the plugin''s .stat-card motion. All colours/tokens come from the RTO Compliance token set, so it reads as native. (2) FULL COVERAGE — the help-content registry was extended from ~40 to ~50 pages so every meaningful page AND its edit/sub-pages carry the card (qualification/unit/course/validate editors, student profile/enrolments/support, suitability send/view/bulk, trainer/currency/voccomp/supervision/validation editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, governance/risk/fee/insurance/third-party/transition/location editors, issue/template/email/generate certificate pages, survey send/responses, TAS/consultation, alerts, AI analysis/usage, audit log, practice guides, plugin settings, compliance modules). Only the dashboard, the help pages themselves and internal diagnostics intentionally have no card. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100426. — prior v5.9.425 GUIDED PAGE HELP CARDS + HELP/SUPPORT & COMPLIANCE CONTENT REFRESH. (1) WHAT / WHY / HOW CARDS — every page now opens with a single, consistent orientation card directly under the breadcrumb: a "What it is / Why it matters / How to use it" tabbed card explaining the page, the compliance it supports and the steps to use it. One reusable renderer (local_rtocompliance_render_help_card) wired into the shared nav header and keyed by script filename, driven by a central content registry (local_rtocompliance_page_help_content) covering ~40 core pages — so a first-time user always gets the same clear, beautifully-formatted orientation and pages opt in simply by having a registry entry. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript, cannot fail after header output); scoped styling using the existing design tokens with dark-mode support. (2) HELP & SUPPORT / COMPLIANCE REFRESH — brought the Support Centre and How It Works up to date with everything shipped in v5.9.420–425: the "What''s New" panel now leads with v5.9.425 and lists the page help cards, RPL evidence rigour, pre-enrolment readiness, RPL assessor identity/fairness, end-to-end nominal hours, and the declutter pass; the RPL, Student Records, Qualification Builder and TAS module cards and their how-to steps were rewritten to describe the new capabilities; four new How-It-Works Key Questions (record RPL, check pre-enrolment, nominal-hours source, and the updated qualification setup) and three new FAQs (RPL capture, nominal hours, pre-enrolment readiness) were added; and the ASQA Compliance Mapping rows for 1.7 (RPL) and 2.2 (pre-enrolment) were updated to reflect the new evidence. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100425. — prior v5.9.424 RPL SUPERSEDED-UNIT MAPPING + EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX (Standard 1.2). Completes the RPL best-practice set. (1) SUPERSEDED → CURRENT UNIT MAPPING — the RPL/CT record now captures the superseded/prior unit the student actually holds and its TGA equivalence to the current unit being granted (Equivalent E / Not equivalent N / N-A). When an approved decision maps from a NOT-equivalent superseded unit, a non-blocking advisory reminds the assessor that a not-equivalent mapping cannot grant the current unit on its own — the gap must be assessed. This documents credit granted for a current unit on the basis of a superseded one. (2) EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX — a repeating table maps each item of evidence to the unit requirement (element / performance criterion / performance or knowledge evidence) it satisfies, with an assessor judgement (satisfactory / not satisfactory / further evidence needed). This evidences the rules of evidence — valid, sufficient, current, authentic — behind an RPL determination rather than a single free-text blob. Stored as normalised JSON (server-side decode → clean rows → re-encode) in a new evidencematrix column; rendered with add/remove rows and serialised to a hidden field on submit. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (supersededunitcode / unitequivalence / evidencematrix) via savepoint 2026073100424. No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.423 PRE-ENROLMENT READINESS SIGNAL (Standard 2). Consolidates the four ASQA pre-enrolment gates into an audit-ready view that reuses the existing suitability + USI + declaration data (no duplication of the mature suitability subsystem) and, in keeping with the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, SURFACES gaps rather than creating or blocking any Moodle enrolment. New helper local_rtocompliance_preenrolment_readiness(userid) evaluates: (1) suitability assessed — a completed suitability review with a genuine decision (a "not suitable" outcome is flagged, not passed); (2) student declaration signed — the pre-enrolment attestation signature (declaration_signed_at); (3) USI verified with the Registry; (4) pre-enrolment information provided — evidenced by the suitability form having been issued and completed. STUDENT PROFILE now shows a "Pre-enrolment readiness" card (per-gate tick / warn / not-met with dates and a "N of 4 met" header pill) above the demographics. COMPLIANCE HEALTH (Quality Area 2) gains a scored metric — "Pre-enrolment suitability not evidenced" — counting students who have recorded results but no completed suitability review, linking to the bulk suitability sender. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100423. — prior v5.9.422 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER PROCEDURAL-FAIRNESS + ASSESSOR IDENTITY. Closes the RPL best-practice gaps around WHO assessed and whether the student was told. (1) ASSESSOR IDENTITY (Standard 1.5) — the RPL/CT record now selects the assessor from the registered trainer workforce (writes assessoruserid, previously never captured — only a free-typed name was stored), so a decision is tied to a person whose TAE competence/currency the RTO evidences. The picker shows a live advisory for the chosen trainer: green when they hold a current TAE credential, amber when the TAE is missing or expired. A free-text name is retained only for an assessor not yet in the Trainers register, and the display name is auto-synced from the selected trainer. (2) OUTCOME COMMUNICATED (Standard 1.6, procedural fairness) — new fields record that the decision outcome was communicated to the student, the date, and the method (email/letter/interview/portal/phone); the date defaults to the decision date when left blank. The RPL/CT register gains a "Student Notified" column (Notified + date / Not notified / — while pending) so an auditor can see the decision-to-notification loop was closed. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (outcomecommunicated/…date/…method) via savepoint 2026073100422 (assessoruserid already existed). No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.421 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 2 (qualification total) + PHASE 4 (TAS volume of learning). (1) PHASE 2 — the Qualification Builder now rolls a real qualification nominal-hours total up from authoritative per-unit data. Because training.gov.au does NOT publish nominal hours, the builder previously showed a 0 total for most qualifications; it now batch-resolves any unit still at 0 from the plugin''s own reference table (local_rtocompliance_nominalhours, for the RTO''s reporting jurisdiction with NAT fallback) via a new batch mode on nominalhours_lookup.php (?codes=CODE1,CODE2,...), fills each unit, and repaints the "Nominal Hours — N hrs total" compliance card (which now also flags how many units are still missing hours so the admin knows to import the NCVER dataset or enter them). Resolution runs on page load, after a TGA load, and whenever a unit is added. (2) PHASE 4 — the TAS "Total Nominal Hours" (which drives the AQF volume-of-learning justification, Std 1.1/1.2) is now pre-filled from the qualification''s authoritative total via new helper local_rtocompliance_qual_nominal_total() (Qual Builder product total → live unit sum → per-unit reference-table sum). It only fills a genuinely empty value (a figure the RTO already entered is preserved), also seeds an empty Volume of Learning as a defensible lower bound, and the AI delivery-plan generator now uses this authoritative total as its fallback instead of a units×hrs/week guess when TGA returns none. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100421. — prior v5.9.420 DECLUTTER PASS 2 — remove duplicated / no-compliance-purpose UI noise. (1) STUDENT RESULTS — the eight summary stat tiles are reduced to the four that carry meaning; the removed four (Units in Product, Core Units, Elective Units, Total Unit Enrolments) were static structural reference counts that duplicated the qualification structure already listed below and only crowded the results command view. (2) DATA IMPORT — the "No Moodle accounts or enrolments are created" assurance was printed three times on the import screen (Step 1 card, Step 2 card, and the authoritative alert beneath the steps); the two card repetitions are removed and the single, more complete "No Moodle changes" alert is kept. (3) MARKETING INFORMATION — removed the "Related pages" cross-link card (every destination already lives in the left sidebar, so it was pure navigation duplication). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100420. — prior v5.9.419 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 + RPL CT-GATE HARDENING + SUPPORT PERSISTENCE + DECLUTTER. (1) NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 — when an enrolment is saved with AVETMISS scheduled hours left blank, they now default from the unit''s authoritative nominal hours (local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours), so NAT00120 reports a sensible value without manual entry; RPL (51) and Credit Transfer (60) default to 0 (no delivery). A value the admin actually typed is never overwritten. (2) RPL CREDIT-TRANSFER GATE HARDENED (Standard 1.7) — a CT outcome (60) is now posted to the results register only when BOTH an authenticated source (a verified USI transcript OR an uploaded source certificate/transcript on the record) AND the source qualification code are present; previously only the self-attested "USI transcript verified" checkbox was required, with no source document or code enforced. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT NOW PERSISTS SERVER-SIDE — the organisation-level support/adjustment/wellbeing selections were saved only in the browser (localStorage), so they were device-specific and invisible to an auditor on another machine (a Std 2.1/2.3 evidence gap); they now save to plugin config via a sesskey-guarded handler and load from the server. (4) DECLUTTER — the Students page''s auto-opening full-screen "USI not configured" modal (popped on every load, blocking the roster, duplicating the dashboard CTA) is replaced by an inline banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100419. (Continuing: nominal hours Phase 2 qual-total sum, RPL assessor-identity + outcome-communicated, declutter passes 2-3, and the pre-enrolment integration gate.) — prior v5.9.418 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 1. The Qualification Builder nominal-hours autofill previously called a private lms-labs.com endpoint. It now owns the data: a new reference table local_rtocompliance_nominalhours holds authoritative nominal hours per unit code per jurisdiction (NAT = the free NCVER nationally-agreed set as the national baseline, plus optional VIC/QLD/NSW/SA/WA/TAS/NT/ACT overrides). New internal endpoint nominalhours_lookup.php resolves a unit's hours from that table for the RTO's configured reporting jurisdiction (setting: Nominal hours — reporting jurisdiction) with NAT fallback, and the qualbuilder autofill JS now calls THIS endpoint instead of lms-labs.com. New admin import page (Import Nominal Hours) ingests the NCVER tab-delimited file (auto-detects tab/comma, skips header/non-code rows, upserts one value per unit per state) so the table can be bulk-populated; helper local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours()/upsert_nominalhours() added. Schema: new table (install.xml + upgrade savepoint 2026073100418). This is Phase 1 (authoritative source + internal lookup, removing the external dependency); Phase 2 (sum to qualification total), Phase 3 (default enrolment scheduled hours → NAT00120, 0 for RPL/CT) and Phase 4 (TAS amount-of-training) follow. Savepoint 2026073100418. — prior v5.9.417 DECLUTTER PASS 1. Removes duplicated/no-purpose UI noise so pages stay focused on compliance work. DASHBOARD: removed the static "Get Started Guide" 7-card row (it mirrored the live Setup Progress tracker exactly — same 7 steps/order/destinations); removed the "Quick Access" cards (all three destinations are in the sidebar and their stat lines just repeated the Overview tiles); removed the two full-width cross-link banners (Practice Guides + Compliance Map — both already in the sidebar). CERTIFICATES: removed the "Certificate Compliance — Clauses 9–14" explainer banner that restated the legislation above the register on every visit (the clause content lives on the ASQA Compliance Mapping page and Support centre; the actual compliance gates are unchanged). QUAL CERT HUB: removed the multi-paragraph "What is this / How to use it" tutorial card (incl. cache jargon), replaced with a one-line intro — the funnel columns and row actions are self-explanatory. This is pass 1 of a larger simplification program (audit produced a top-20 removal list); remaining declutter, plus nominal-hours Phase 1 and the RPL best-practice enhancements, follow in subsequent builds. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100417. — prior v5.9.416 PREMIUM DESIGN SYSTEM + RPL/CT EXPERT AUDIT-BLOCKING FIXES. (A) PREMIUM UI PASS — a design-system audit found the token layer had been rebuilt three times with conflicting values (primary colour, shadows, two neutral ramps), two competing badge systems, WCAG-AA contrast failures on solid info/success badges, oversized 16px/44px buttons with a gradient overridden to flat, and a .info-card.warning that rendered BLUE instead of amber. A single canonical design system is now appended to styles.css (scoped, reversible): one token set (re-points every legacy --rtoc-* var), a clean button scale (14px text, 8px radius, quiet outline/secondary, one focus-visible ring), one AA-safe soft-chip badge system, consistent card radius/shadow + tasteful hover lift, the amber warning-card fix, a global premium table-hover fallback, and empty/skeleton state utilities. PURGE CACHES after install to see it. (B) RPL/CREDIT-TRANSFER expert review — fixed the audit-blocking gaps: (1) REVERSAL RETRACTION — changing a previously-approved RPL/CT to Not Approved / Pending now retracts the posted competency (deletes the RPL-created enrolments row, or reverts an updated delivery row to 70) so a reversed decision can no longer leave a competent unit over-reporting into completion, certificates and NAT; (2) RPL DELIVERY MODE on the update path now reports mode 90 (not applicable) like the insert path — previously an RPL granted over an existing delivery enrolment kept classroom mode 10 and its delivered hours; (3) PRIVACY ERASURE — a right-to-erasure request now deletes the student's RPL evidence and credit-transfer source-certificate FILES (system-context fileareas keyed by rpl id), which were previously left in storage; the file subsystem is now declared in the privacy metadata. Also: RPL required-field enforcement (student + decision reason) from v5.9.415 retained. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100416. (Nominal hours: an expert research pass produced a phased wiring plan — import the NCVER nationally-agreed nominal-hours dataset into a per-unit/per-state reference table, repoint the qualbuilder autofill off lms-labs.com to an internal lookup, sum to the qual total, default enrolment scheduledhours from it (0 for RPL/CT), and feed the TAS amount-of-training — staged for approval, not in this build.) — prior v5.9.415 FULL-MENU AUDIT — HIGH/MEDIUM REMEDIATION BATCH. Follows the v5.9.414 blocker fixes. (1) TRAINER EVIDENCE now persists — trainer_currency.php and trainer_voccomp.php read the uploaded evidence file from the transient draft area but never called file_save_draft_area_files(), so files vanished on Moodle's draft cleanup and the stored id pointed at nothing; both now persist into permanent pluginfile-served fileareas (trainer_evidence / trainer_voccomp_evidence, separate areas so record ids can't collide) keyed by the record id. SCHEMA PARITY: the vocationalevidence column existed only in db/upgrade.php, so fresh installs lacked it and Trainers-page saves failed — it is now in db/install.xml too. (2) PROFILE WRITE-AUTH — student_profile.php allowed SAVING another student's record with only the read capability (viewall); saving now requires the manage (write) capability, editing your own profile still allowed. (3) SUPPORT DIAGNOSTICS REMOVED — support.php ran a v5.9.50 breadcrumb block on every Help-page load that wrote a /tmp file, spammed error_log, registered a shutdown handler and wrote the Moodle config table four times; removed entirely. (4) MANAGER DEAD-END — the fee-protection page linked managers to a site-config-only settings section (access denied); the link now only shows to users who can open it, with a note otherwise. (5) THIRD-PARTY — corrected the factually wrong "notify ASQA at least 30 days before entering a third-party arrangement" banner to the actual 2025 requirement (written agreement + retained quality oversight; NRT-logo / AQF-issuance prohibitions; student transparency). (6) QI COMPLETION RATE — qi_report.php computed the competency completion rate across mismatched cohorts (start-date denominator vs end-date numerator) and counted non-competent codes (52 RPL-not-granted, 70 continuing, etc.) as completions; it is now "of units that reached a FINAL outcome this year, the fraction that were competent (20/51/60/81)". (7) ASQA CLAUSE CONSISTENCY — the Risk page labelled risk management "Standard 4.3" while the authoritative ASQA Compliance Mapping and Support Centre use 4.2; the Risk page now says 4.2. (8) FEE-PROTECTION register now includes 'approaching threshold' students (>$1,200), which the previous >$1,500-only query excluded. No schema changes beyond adding the missing vocationalevidence column to install.xml (parity only). Savepoint 2026073100415. (Remaining catalogued for follow-up: student_support server persistence, viewsensitive gating, non-portable LIMIT in a few queries, RPL required-field enforcement, dashboard alert icons, and the USI local-verification client which is a separate staged project.) — prior v5.9.414 FULL-MENU AUDIT — 4 BLOCKERS FIXED. A deep 7-part investigation of every left-hand-menu section found four blocker-class defects, all now fixed: (1) CERTIFICATE INTEGRITY — the Student Results drill-down and the results-page cert-issuance guard (qualbuilder_results.php + ajax.php) counted AVETMISS outcomes 30 (competency not achieved/fail) and 40 (withdrawn) as "complete", so a student who failed or withdrew from every unit showed 100% progress with a working "Issue Certificate" button, and the server guard let the testamur/record issue. All six checks now use the competent-only set (20/51/60/81), so only genuinely-competent students count as complete and can be issued a qualification certificate. (2) SoA GATE BYPASS — the Multi-Unit Statement of Attainment issuer (soa_ajax.php) inserted the certificate directly, skipping the USI verified-gate, the RTO-settings gate and the as-issued snapshots that local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert() enforces; an SoA could be issued to a student with no / unverified USI. It now enforces the USI-verified gate (Clause 12) and RTO-identity gate BEFORE consuming credits, snapshots the verified USI + RTO identity onto the cert, and publishes to the verification registry. (3) NO-CORE-WRITES — three data-import actions (repairnames edits {user} name/email; backfill_records set {user}.idnumber; hide_archive_cats toggled {course_categories}.visible) still wrote to Moodle core and were reachable; they are now in the retired-action block list, so the plugin only READS Moodle and writes solely to its own tables with no reachable exception. (4) GOVERNANCE — governance_edit.php ignored the type=changes/adc parameter and always read/wrote the govpersons table, so Material Changes and the Annual Declaration of Compliance could never be created and editing one threw a fatal MUST_EXIST; the editor now has full forms for the materialchanges and adc tables. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100414. (Remaining HIGH/MEDIUM findings from the audit — trainer evidence-file persistence, student_support localStorage-only, viewsensitive USI gating, ASQA clause-number consistency, and others — are catalogued for follow-up builds.) — prior v5.9.413 USI SETUP-STATUS UNIFIED. The dashboard (index.php) judged USI setup from the LEGACY local-file config keys (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id), while the dedicated Machine Credential Setup page (usi_settings.php) judged it from the per-tenant PLATFORM status. So a SaaS RTO whose USI machine credential is stored on the platform (the recommended method) was shown a "USI verification is not yet set up" banner on the dashboard even though the setup page correctly reported "configured and ready" — it looked like the configuration had reset. New single source of truth local_rtocompliance_usi_is_configured() recognises BOTH supported methods: (a) per-tenant platform (apiurl + siteid + apikey set AND a credential uploaded/confirmed via the usi_cert_uploaded flag or a platform-pushed usi_certificate_path), and (b) legacy local-file (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id). The dashboard now uses it, so the banner only shows when USI genuinely is not configured by either method. Nothing about the USI credentials themselves was changed or reset — this was purely an inconsistent status check. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100413. — prior v5.9.412 EDITOR NOW INCORPORATES EVERY RTO-CONFIGURED VALUE (certificate code + phrases + descriptors). Extends the v5.9.409 real-identity map so the certificate editor canvas reflects ALL fixed, RTO-configured values from RTO/Certificate Settings — not just RTO name/code/signatory. Added: the CERTIFICATE CODE preview (cert.number) built from the RTO''s real certprefix + type code + year exactly as local_rtocompliance_generate_cert_number() does (e.g. CBF-SOA-2026-0001) instead of the generic CERT-2026-000123; the certificate footer (cert.footer); every ASQA mandatory phrase (aqf_statement, certify/attained statements, SoA intro/attained statements, Statement-of-Attainment and Record-of-Results headings, the NOT-A-TESTAMUR statement) using the RTO''s configured wording and falling back to the ASQA default when unset; and the optional descriptors (industry descriptor, occupational stream, apprenticeship statement, language statement, skill-set statement) which show the real configured value or fall through to the catalogue placeholder when blank. These paint on the canvas regardless of the "Show sample data" toggle because they are fixed RTO values, not per-student data (student name, units, dates and the QR code are deliberately left as sample/dynamic). Confirmed all six branding IMAGE fields (RTO logo, NRT logo, AQF logo, compliance/state logo, organisation seal, signatory signature) were already painting from the uploaded files via the v5.9.406–409 getter + pluginfile-serving fixes. No settings/config keys changed; no schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100412. — prior v5.9.411 NO-CORE-WRITES ON CERT GENERATION (C-P2-6) + NAT CONTINUING-OUTCOME FIX (A-P2-3). (1) NO-CORE-WRITES — certificate generation no longer toggles the core {user}.suspended field. The three issuance paths (generate_course_certs.php, generate_qual_certs.php, qual_cert_hub.php) each ran $DB->set_field(''user'',''suspended'',0,...) when an admin ticked an "Activate account" checkbox during generation, coupling Moodle account activation to certificate issuance and writing to a core table. Those writes AND their checkboxes/columns are removed; suspended students are still shown (badged, read-only) and can still be issued certificates — activating an account is now left as an explicit decision in Moodle user administration. (The explicit admin "activate" action on the Students page and the rollback-suspend in data_import remain, as those are deliberate user-initiated actions, not side-effects of issuing a certificate.) (2) A-P2-3 NAT FIX — when the AVETMISS NAT00120 export coerces a blank/''00'' outcome to ''70'' (Continuing activity), it now also reports the record as OPEN (activity end date = reporting period end) instead of emitting ''70'' together with a recorded completion end date, which is internally inconsistent and NCVER flags. The AVETMISS Validation page still surfaces these records so the RTO enters the real outcome. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100411. — prior v5.9.410 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER EVIDENCE UPLOADS + RESULTS/CERT TIE-IN CHECK. (1) FILE UPLOADS — the RPL & Credit Transfer record form now has real file uploads: a "Source certificate / transcript (from the issuing RTO)" uploader on credit-transfer records (attach the other RTO''s testamur / SoA / RoR / USI transcript that authenticates the transfer) and an "RPL evidence files" uploader on RPL records (portfolio, references, prior quals, observation records). Both accept multiple files (PDF/image/Office/text, 20MB each), list already-uploaded files with download + remove links, are stored in the Moodle File API keyed by the record id, served through local_rtocompliance_pluginfile (new fileareas rpl_evidence + ct_sourcecert, manage capability), and cleaned up when the record is deleted. Each uploader carries plain-English ASQA instructions (Standard 1.6 for RPL, Clause 1.7 / Clause 12 for credit transfer). The old free-text "Evidence Files" box is retained as optional notes for evidence held outside the system. (2) TIE-IN VERIFICATION — deep-audited that RPL (outcome 51) and Credit Transfer (outcome 60), written to the results register by local_rtocompliance_apply_rpl_outcome(), are treated as COMPETENT across every relevant path: Student Results (student_profile.php, qualbuilder_results.php), qualification-completion detection (check_full_qual_completion, get_completed_units_for_qual, process_enrolment_task, observer, completion_reconciler, certificate_validator) and ALL certificate paths (generate_qual_certs, qual_cert_hub, generate_course_certs, and the renderer which labels 51=RPL Granted / 60=Credit Transfer on the SoA/RoR). Fixed the one gap the audit found: the Students dashboard "Competency Achieved (Units)" card counted only outcome 20 — it now counts 20/51/60/81 so RPL/CT units are included. Also corrected the scrambled outcomeidentifier help text to the accurate NCVER code meanings. No schema changes (files use the Moodle File API; the rpl table already had studentid/rpltype/usitranscriptverified). Savepoint 2026073100410. — prior v5.9.409 EDITOR BRANDING NOW ACTUALLY RENDERS (real root cause). The certificate editor paints the RTO logo / NRT logo / CEO signature / organisation seal in the canvas as <img src="pluginfile…"> URLs, but local_rtocompliance_pluginfile() only served three fileareas (cert_template_bg, cert_template_image, rto_branding). The assets uploaded via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings live in admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas (logo, nrt_logo_file, aqf_logo_file, organisation_seal_file, compliance_logo_1/2, ceo_signature_file, secondary_logo, cert_background_file) — NONE of which the handler served — so every branding image request 404'd and the canvas showed an empty box, even though the issued PDF rendered the logos fine (the PDF reads the file straight off disk, bypassing pluginfile entirely). The pluginfile handler now serves those branding fileareas (system context, managecerttemplates capability), so the editor canvas finally matches the issued certificate. This is the missing piece behind the v5.9.406 getter fix: the getters resolved the correct file and produced a URL, but that URL was not servable until now. (2) EDITOR SHOWS REAL RTO IDENTITY — the canvas now always paints the RTO's own configured values for rto.name, rto.code, signatory.name, signatory.title and aqf_statement (independent of the "Show sample data" toggle), because these are fixed RTO-identity values, not per-student sample data. Previously the canvas showed the generic catalogue placeholder ("National Compliance Training / 50918") whenever sample data was off, which read as "the editor isn't pulling RTO settings" even though issued certificates were always correct. Verified the issued-certificate payload (resolve_payload) sources every field correctly: rto.name/rto.code/signatory/aqf_statement from the issue-time snapshot then live config; student name/USI, qualification code/name, dates and cert number from the cert + student records; mandatory phrases from config with ASQA defaults. Purge all caches after install. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100409. — prior v5.9.408 TEMPLATE DELETE + DEACTIVATE CONTROLS. Adds two admin controls to the Certificate Templates list so a template can be cleared out and regenerated without digging through statuses: (1) DELETE — a Delete button now appears on EVERY template row regardless of status (including the active one), backed by a new force_delete() path + 'forcedelete' action (the audit-safe delete() that only removed drafts/archived is kept for programmatic callers). Deleting the active template is safe: issuance and preview fall back to the built-in ASQA starter until a new template is activated. Uploaded background/per-field-image files are cleaned up. Confirm prompt is extra-strong (and states the active-template fallback) since it is permanent. (2) MAKE NON-ACTIVE — a new deactivate() method + 'deactivate' action + "Make non-active" button shown on the currently active template, which clears the active flag WITHOUT archiving (the template stays approved and one-click re-activatable). New lang strings: cert_template_deactivate_btn, cert_template_confirm_deactivate, cert_template_action_ok_deactivated. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100408. — prior v5.9.407 SANITISE EXISTING SAVED CERT TEMPLATES (retro-fix for already-saved templates). v5.9.406 fixed the STARTER (new templates) and the RENDER path, but a template already saved in the database kept its old fields — so an existing Statement of Attainment still showed the duplicate/overlapping "form part of" + "completion of course" statements AND still carried the "Verify at: <url>" text field. A new upgrade step (savepoint 2026073100407) now rewrites every saved cert-template design to match a fresh starter: it drops every qualification.completionofcoursestatement field (redundant — the single "form part of" line is the ASQA statement), drops every authenticity_measure text field (QR-only default; the mandatory QR code stays and satisfies the authenticity requirement), and widens the surviving "form part of" box for a clean two-line wrap. Fully guarded (a bad design row is skipped, an unchanged design is left untouched); RTOs can drag the "Authenticity measure" field back on if they want the URL text. This is what makes an ALREADY-SAVED template pick up the QR-only + single-statement fixes without a manual "Reset to starter". IMPORTANT after install: run Site administration → Development → Purge all caches (the editor JS and branding checks are cached). NOTE on branding: the editor now paints the real RTO logo / NRT logo / signature / seal from RTO Settings (v5.9.406 getter fix) — if a slot still shows a placeholder box after purging caches, that specific asset is not uploaded under Certificate Settings for that cert type. No schema changes (data-only design rewrite). Savepoint 2026073100407. — prior v5.9.406 CERTIFICATE EDITOR FIXES + QR-ONLY DEFAULT + CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT. (1) EDITOR BRANDING (critical) — the certificate editor showed "[RTO logo]" / "[NRT logo]" / "[CEO signature image]" / "[Org seal]" text placeholders instead of the real artwork whenever the RTO had uploaded those assets via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings, because the editor's branding-URL getters only looked in the FA_BRANDING pseudo-itemid area and never the admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas where the settings pages actually store them (the issued PDF found them via resolve_compliance_asset_path()'s fallback chain, so the canvas and the print diverged). New get_branding_display_url() mirrors the renderer's exact chain (FA_BRANDING → settings filearea → bundled pix) and now backs get_branding_logo/signature/sta/nrt/aqf/org_seal_url(); the editor host now also passes the NRT, AQF and STA logo URLs to the JS (previously only logo/signature/seal were), and the editor canvas paints nrt_logo/aqf_logo/state_training_authority_logo from them. (2) SoA COMPLIANCE STATEMENT — the Statement of Attainment starter carried BOTH "These competencies form part of {code} {name}" AND the near-identical "These competencies were attained in completion of {code} course in {name}", auto-built from the same qualification and stacked 5-7mm apart, so they overlapped into an unreadable block. The redundant "completion of course" statement (which is for accredited short courses, not qualifications) is removed from the default starter (still draggable from the palette), the single "form part of" statement box is widened for clean two-line wrap, and the descriptors are re-spaced; the renderer AND sample preview now also suppress the completion statement whenever the form-part-of line is present, so templates already saved with both fields render only the correct one. (3) QR-ONLY DEFAULT — the "Verify at: <url>" authenticity_measure text field is removed from all eight starter templates; the mandatory verification QR code (auto-added by ensure_mandatory_fields, and already accepted by the validator as a valid authenticity measure) is the default, and RTOs can drag the URL text back on if they want it. (4) CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT — editor font sizing now converts points→pixels with the correct 0.3528×BASE_SCALE factor (was a hardcoded 1.33 that rendered every field ~26% oversized vs the PDF, throwing off drag-to-fit); the two inline <script> emitters on the editor page use JSON_HEX_* flags so author-entered text can't break out; the disabled-path return of send_certificate_email() now uses the canonical ok/email/error shape its callers read (was success/reason, causing an undefined-key warning and a blank failure message); and revoking a certificate now calls update_registry_status(token,'revoked') so a revoked cert's public QR verifies as Revoked instead of Valid. Also bundles the pending verify.php superseded-cert fix and the Student Results Moodle-completion effective-outcome wiring from the working set. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100406. (1) The Student Profile results section is rebuilt into a proper command view: a per-qualification progress hero (X of Y units competent, progress bar, outcome-breakdown chips), unit results GROUPED BY QUALIFICATION with a new Source column (which Moodle course each result came from), friendly colour-coded outcome badges, an outcome legend, and consolidated action buttons — "Issue Statement of Attainment", "Issue Qualification Certificate" (pre-fills the hub with the student's USI), and "Record / edit results". (2) OUTCOME LABELS: the raw AVETMISS placeholder "00" (and blank/10) now displays as "Not yet assessed" on the Enrolments page and profile (it is NOT Competent or NYC — it means no result recorded yet). Verified every outcome label against NCVER's official "Reporting a final outcome" fact sheet: code 70 is correctly "Continuing activity" (corrected two internal spots that read "Continuing enrolment"); 40/41/61/85 confirmed correct. (3) DATES: the Enrolments page Activity Start Date (and the Moodle-enrolment list dates) now include the YEAR (they used Moodle's short date format which omits it). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100405. — prior v5.9.404 left-hand menu fix. several admin pages rendered without the plugin's left sidebar because they called $OUTPUT->header() but never local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header(). Fixed on Moodle Course Map (course_map.php — reported), AVETMISS Validation (nat_validate.php), NAT Reconciliation (reconcile.php — replaced its bare rtoc-main-content div with the full layout-wrap + sidebar), and the Over-Enrolment / Bulk Over-Enrolment / Skipped Program Codes diagnostic pages. A full sweep confirms every remaining page without the sidebar is an intentional public token page (certificate verification, survey response, student declaration, student LLN form), which correctly have no admin menu. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100404. — prior v5.9.403 button text padding. long-label buttons (e.g. the full-width "Sync results from Moodle completions" side-panel button) were clipping because the plugin's button style forced white-space:nowrap with a fixed single-line height, so a long label in a narrow button ran to the edges. Buttons now allow their text to WRAP with height:auto (padding honoured), and small buttons (.btn-sm) get comfortable padding + a slightly smaller font — a single stylesheet fix that applies to every button in the plugin's main content area. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100403. — prior v5.9.402 backlog close-out. (final audit P2/P3s): (1) CREDIT-TRANSFER SOURCE AUTHENTICATION (Std 1.7) — a credit-transfer decision no longer posts a competency to the register unless the USI transcript is verified; otherwise it warns and holds (RPL is unaffected). (2) PRIVACY — complaint/appeal records now capture the complainant/appellant Moodle user id (resolved from email) so privacy export & erasure include them. (3) WORKFORCE CREDENTIALS — corrected the assessor skill-set picklist (removed the invalid TAESS00021, added the real TAESS00011 Assessor Skill Set and TAESS00019 Enterprise Trainer Skill Set, relabelled TAESS00024) and synced the help text; added advisory reminders that a TAS should be reviewed when its training product is superseded, and that TAE-package assessments need independent validation before the first cohort. (4) LABEL CORRECTNESS — the SoA unit-outcome filter now uses the correct AVETMISS codes (Credit transfer = 60; 81/82 shown as non-assessable, not "superseded competent"), and the Statement-of-Attainment "requires" text lists the correct competent set (20/51/60/81). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100402. — prior v5.9.401 procedural fairness + sensitive-data permission. (audit P2s). COMPLAINTS (Std 2.7): new respondent, respondent-response, and date-outcome-communicated fields so the RTO can demonstrate the party complained about was heard and all parties were told the outcome. APPEALS (Std 2.8): new original-decision-maker + reviewer-independence-confirmed + underlying-record-corrected fields; the appeal edit page now warns (advisory) when an upheld assessment appeal has not had its underlying record corrected, or when independence has not been confirmed. SENSITIVE DATA: a new local/rtocompliance:viewsensitive capability (granted to managers by default) now gates the disability disclosure on the student profile — staff without it see "Restricted", while the student always sees their own and managers are unaffected. Schema savepoint 401 (complaints + appeals fields). — prior v5.9.400 help & support refresh. the Support Centre "What's New" panel (was stuck at v5.9.378), Get Started guide, feature/module cards and FAQ, plus the How It Works Key Questions, are updated to the current feature set — Compliance Health, AVETMISS Validation, ASQA Compliance Mapping, the world-class student profile, student certificate access (portal + nav link + dashboard block), automated weekly alerts, full NAT demographic + address propagation, the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, and the certificate-integrity + validation/workforce/QI hardening. Also corrected stale docs that described the retired auto-enrolment behaviour and the old "USI warning" as current (issuance is now a hard verified-USI block). Documentation only. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100400. — prior v5.9.399 automated compliance alerts. a new weekly scheduled task (compliance_alert_task, Mondays 07:00) emails site administrators a plain-English digest whenever key audit-readiness risks need attention — validations overdue, working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, students with results but an unverified USI (cert-blocked), certificates past the 30-day issuance rule, and incomplete AVETMISS profiles — with a one-click link to the Compliance Health page. Sends ONLY when something needs attention (no all-clear noise); fully guarded so a mail failure or missing table can never break cron; disable by setting config compliancealerts=0, and add an extra recipient via config alertemail. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100399. — prior v5.9.398 AVETMISS pre-submission validator. (the crown-jewel feature): a new read-only "AVETMISS Validation" page (nat_validate.php, in Data & Reporting) checks every reportable student and enrolment against NCVER/AVETMISS edit rules BEFORE the RTO exports NAT files — so a quarterly submission is not rejected. STUDENT checks: missing/invalid USI (+ unverified-USI warning), missing/invalid DOB, sex, postcode, state, country of birth, language, Indigenous status, labour force, school level, at-school flag; disability/prior-ed detail warnings. ENROLMENT checks: invalid/blank outcome code, a final outcome with no end date, missing start date, end-before-start, blank program/unit code; warnings for continuing-with-past-end-date, invalid delivery mode / funding source, and missing scheduled hours on a delivered unit. Findings are split ERROR (will fail NCVER) vs WARNING, grouped by category with a "Ready to submit / N errors to fix" verdict and a full CSV export. Fully read-only and defensively guarded. Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100398. — prior v5.9.397 Compliance Health command centre. a new flagship read-only page (compliance_health.php, first in the left menu) that answers "are we audit-ready right now?" at a glance. A hero audit-readiness score (percentage of key checks currently clear) with a verdict, over a responsive grid of Quality-Area cards surfacing live risk signals: validations overdue / due soon, qualifications never validated, incomplete AVETMISS profiles, open complaints & appeals (past timeframe), working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, QI survey response rate, open high-severity risks, and — critically — students with results but an UNVERIFIED USI (the certificates you cannot yet issue). Every metric has a status pill and a one-click "fix" link to the relevant page. Fully read-only and defensively guarded (every query wrapped; a missing table never breaks the page). Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100397. — prior v5.9.396 AVETMISS address propagation. the student's full street address (building/property name, flat-unit, street number+name, and postcode) is now parsed from NAT00085 — previously the parser dropped it — staged, and propagated into the student profile alongside the other demographics (both automatically on import for existing profiles, and via Backfill). New staging columns postcode/buildingname/unitno/streetname (savepoint 396); the students table already had the matching columns. The student profile summary now shows the complete address (building, unit/street, suburb, state, postcode) instead of just suburb+state. Savepoint 2026073100396. — prior v5.9.395 audit trail + portability. (1) the Complaints, Appeals and Continuous-Improvement registers now write an audit-log entry on every create/update/delete (previously these compliance records could be altered or deleted with no trail — an ASQA evidence gap); logging is wrapped defensively so it can never block the user action. (2) The NAT export replaced a MySQL/Postgres-only "LIMIT 1" with a portable limited query so it no longer risks failing on Oracle/MSSQL. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100395. — prior v5.9.394 world-class student profile. (1) The Student Records list now makes each student NAME a one-click link to their profile, and the row Actions menu gains Certificates + Results/Enrolments shortcuts. (2) student_profile.php now opens with a polished READ-ONLY summary above the edit form: a header card (name, client ID, USI + verification badge, completeness pill that lists missing fields ON LOAD), a demographics grid showing every AVETMISS field as a HUMAN LABEL (with a muted "Not stated" for placeholders), a unit-results table with colour-coded outcome badges, and an issued-certificates card with one-click PDF download — so an admin can review a student's whole picture in one place instead of a bare edit form. (3) Reissuing a certificate now preserves the original as-issued USI snapshot and RTO-identity snapshot (C-P2-1), so a faithful copy shows exactly what the original showed. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100394. — prior v5.9.393 student My Certificates nav link + dashboard block. students now get a persistent "My Certificates" link in the plugin navigation (local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation previously returned nothing for students, so their only link was buried on their Moodle profile page). The link points to the certificate portal (mycerts.php), which enforces its own access control so a student only ever sees their own certificates. A companion Dashboard block (block_rtocompliance_mycerts, delivered separately) shows a student their issued certificates with one-click download on login. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100393. — prior v5.9.392 removed Moodle account creation from Backfill. "Backfill Student Records" no longer creates Moodle {user} accounts (user_create_user removed). A NAT student with no existing Moodle account is now SKIPPED and reported ("no Moodle account — an administrator must create one first, then re-run Backfill"). Backfill now only READS Moodle users and writes the plugin's own student profile + demographics for students who already have an account. Combined with v5.9.387, the plugin creates/deletes NOTHING in Moodle core (no enrolments, no completions, and now no user accounts) — it only reads them. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100392. — prior v5.9.391 NAT demographic propagation regression fix. After a NAT import the AVETMISS demographic data now flows into the student profile again: (1) the finalize step now automatically refreshes the demographic fields (DOB, sex, suburb/state, Indigenous status, labour force, highest school level, language at home, country of birth, disability flag, prior-education flag, at-school flag) on EXISTING student profiles from the freshly-staged NAT00080 data — writing ONLY to the plugin students table (no Moodle user/enrolment/completion writes), so it is constraint-safe; a staged value only overwrites when it is real (never wipes good data with an AVETMISS "not stated" placeholder). This restores propagation that had lived inside the now-disabled auto-enrol handlers. (2) The manual "Backfill Student Records" step was silently dropping 8 core demographics to defaults because its staging SELECT omitted them — the SELECT now pulls all demographic columns, so a backfill writes the full profile. (3) Cert render-time backstop now also blocks the NRT logo on 'attendance' certs (matches the template catalogue's forbidden_for). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100391. — prior v5.9.390 cert-template polish F4/F5/F6. (F4) render-time compliance backstop — the renderer now drops any element forbidden for the cert type before it reaches the PDF (NRT logo never on a Record of Results or non-accredited Completion; USI never on a Testamur or Statement of Attainment), backing up the approval-time validation against pinned/override/legacy designs. (F5) certificate PREVIEW now applies the template's per-template designjson.overrides{} exactly as the real issue path does, so previews are faithful for override-using templates. (F6) the Test Certificate now uses its own dummy verify token and placeholder USI instead of an empty token + the logged-in admin's live USI. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100390. — prior v5.9.389 CERTIFICATE-TEMPLATE INTEGRITY (F1 as-issued RTO snapshot / F2 approved-only pinned template / F3 block issuance on blank RTO details). (F1) each certificate now snapshots the RTO identity settings (legal name, provider code, signatory name/title, AQF statement) at issue time into a new certs.issuesnapshot column and the renderer renders from that snapshot, so a later change to those settings cannot retroactively rewrite an already-issued certificate (mirrors the USI snapshot). (F2) pick_for_cert() renders the pinned template ONLY if it is still status='approved', so an in-progress/unvalidated draft edit can no longer leak onto an already-issued certificate on re-download (it falls back to the current approved template). (F3) issuance is now refused — interactively (non-bypassable) and programmatically — when mandatory RTO details (legal name, national provider code, authorised signatory) are not configured, preventing certificates that render those AQF-required fields blank; the "ready to issue" validator surfaces the same gap. Savepoint 2026073100389. — prior v5.9.388: ASQA PRACTICE-GUIDE AUDIT P1 REMEDIATION PART 2 + ASQA COMPLIANCE MAPPING. Feature code on the v5.9.387 schema: (1) VALIDATION (Std 1.5) — validator-independence declaration is required to complete a validation, and completion is blocked without it; a five-year validation cycle now computes/stores nextduedate (2 years for high-risk), with OVERDUE/DUE-SOON flags and a Coverage-Gaps list of on-scope products with no current validation; assessment outcome + rectification actions are captured. (2) WORKFORCE (Std 3.2) — "Working Towards" trainers now record a start date and an enforced 2-year TAE completion deadline; manager sign-off is blocked for a blank credential or a lapsed working-towards window; supervisors must hold a full, unexpired credential; a Supervision overdue/due-soon alert lists at-risk working-towards trainers. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT (Std 2.3/2.4/2.6) — per-student support / reasonable-adjustment / wellbeing records now persist server-side in local_rtocompliance_supportnotes (retained, shared, auditable) instead of browser localStorage. (4) QUALITY INDICATORS (Std 4.4) — the ad-hoc surveys are replaced with the official AQTF Learner & Employer Questionnaires (items tagged to their scales) and qi_report renders a proper QI Annual Summary (indicator + scale scores, response rates); the QI export is now the aggregate summary, not identifiable per-respondent rows. (5) NEW "ASQA Compliance Mapping" left-menu page (asqa_standards_map.php) — every 2025 Standard mapped to the feature that supports it with an honest Covered/Partial/Gap status (Std 4.3/4.4 self-assurance). No schema changes beyond savepoint 387. Savepoint 2026073100388.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.447'; // v5.9.447 STYLE A UNITS TABLE for the Statement of Attainment and Record of Results. The unit list on both certificates now renders as one shaded three-column table — Unit Code (left) | Unit Title (left-aligned) | Completion Date (centre) — with a coloured header bar (white bold headings), zebra-striped alternating rows and thin cell borders, drawn in TCPDF (solid fills and borders, no gradients). A new Certificate Setting, "Units table header colour" (colour picker), sets the header-bar fill and defaults to the Moodle site primary / brand colour; header text prints white for contrast. The per-unit Completion Date is wired from the compliance register (the unit result / activity end date, falling back to the start date), captured at issue time and back-filled from the register for older certificates in a single query. Both cert types share one renderer: the RoR ror_table field and the SoA dynamic qualification.units field both route to it, so existing templates pick up the new table with no template edits. The in-editor canvas preview was updated to draw the identical shaded table (header colour, columns and zebra) so what you design matches the issued PDF. All certificate text now has a 12pt minimum floor for readability (previously many fields rendered at 9 to 10pt); the field height cap still contains anything that would otherwise overflow. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026080400447. — prior v5.9.446 CODE-FIRST / NO-DASH CONVENTION for unit & qualification labels. Everywhere a unit or qualification code and its title were shown together they now render as "CODE Title" — code first, title second, a single space between, no hyphen or em-dash. Fixed in the certificate renderer (the Statement of Attainment / Record of Results unit lists and their sample previews) and across the plugin UI (qualification dropdowns on Student Results and Generate Certificates, the My Certificates and public verify pages, Qual Builder delete confirmations + audit log, unit delete confirmation, RPL unit label, skipped-programcodes list, TAS heading + PDF/DOCX exports, suitability PDF). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100446. — prior v5.9.445 CSS SCOPING FIX (help card lost styling on admin pages) + SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER now reads the qualification from the PARENT category. (1) CSS — the plugin's help card and other scoped styles are scoped to the body class "path-local-rtocompliance". Pages that use admin_externalpage_setup() have their pagetype (and therefore the auto-generated "path-*" body class) overridden to an "admin-*" value, so that class was absent and every scoped rule silently failed (the sidebar still styled because its CSS is unscoped). Certificate Templates was the reported case; the same latent gap affected 12 admin pages in total — cert_templates, cert_template_edit, cert_test, nat_validate, nominalhours_import, reconcile, trainer_dashboard, usi_settings, foe_audit, foe_bulk_audit, recovery_analyzer, regression_test — each now calls $PAGE->add_body_class('path-local-rtocompliance') before output so the scoped CSS applies (the four remaining admin_externalpage files — qi_export, tas_export, settings, version — are file exports/config, not rendered pages). Purge caches after install. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — the qualification code and title are now read deterministically from the semester sub-category's PARENT category (parent = qualification code + title, the sub-category = the semester), not guessed from the unit set; the exact list of unit-code courses under the sub-category becomes the intake's units/courses. Where a semester has no coded parent the code box is left blank for the admin to set once. The preview shows the parent-derived qualification title beside each code box. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100445. — prior v5.9.444 SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — a separate qualification product per semester intake. New tool (qualbuilder_semester.php) + helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_semester_intakes() / local_rtocompliance_create_semester_intakes(). It scans every Moodle category that holds unit-code courses (e.g. "Archive - 23 DCB S1"), treating each as a semester intake: the category name becomes the product streamname, the unit codes parsed from the course names become its units, and those courses are linked (extra copies as archive variants). Because the archive category names carry a semester but NOT a qualification code, the code is AUTO-SUGGESTED by matching the intake's unit set to existing products (best overlap, with a version-letter-stripped fallback) and is editable per row so the admin sets it once per qualification era where it can't be inferred. A preview lists every detected intake with its semester, unit/course counts, detected unit codes and the suggested code; on confirm it creates one Draft product per ticked intake (qualcode + streamname). Duplicates (same qualcode + streamname) are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin's own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — no Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments are created or changed. Linked from the Qualification Builder header alongside Auto-Create and Recover Unmapped Completions. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100444. — prior v5.9.443 AUTO-CREATE — COURSE MAP IS NOW THE DEFAULT SOURCE + bigger info-box text. The "From Category Tree" scan returned nothing on this site because units here are delivered as COURSES (e.g. "TLIR4001 & TLIR4002 … MSP") under semester/archive categories, not as unit-code sub-categories — so the tree-walk found no unit layer. The Course Map already captures course → qual → unit correctly (seeded from those same categories and courses), so Auto-Create now defaults to the "From Course Map" source and the instructions say so; the Category-Tree tab is kept but explained as only for sites whose units are named sub-categories. Also: the page info boxes ("How this works" / "What this does") were too small — bumped to 15px (and the shared .rtoc-dob-sync-bar base font raised), and the empty-state on the Course Map source now points to Scan & Seed if the map is empty. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100443. — prior v5.9.442 CERTIFICATE EDITOR — ROOT-CAUSE FIX (canvas vs issued-PDF data divergence) + RECOVER UNMAPPED COMPLETIONS TOOL. CERT EDITOR: the meta-root-cause of the recurring "wrong preview" complaints was that the drag-and-drop CANVAS and the issued-PDF renderer used DIFFERENT data sources — on default load the canvas painted each field its own hardcoded per-field catalogue placeholder (meta.sample) while every prior fix (RTO identity v5.9.409/412, statement dedupe v5.9.406/407) only ever touched the PDF renderer's sample_payload, which the canvas did not use. Fixes: (1) CANVAS-DATA-UNIFY — the editor JS resolver now renders the SAME coherent sample record the issued PDF uses (a key present in sample_payload wins, even when intentionally blank), so unrelated placeholders (a First-Aid skill-set line, a Business qualification, an "[insert language]" token) no longer stack on the canvas and the skill-set/optional statements that should be blank now are. (2) STALE AMD BUILD — amd/build/cert_template_editor.js was 37 lines behind source (missing the whole real-RTO-identity code path), so dev/debug sites served the old behaviour; both build artifacts (.js and .min.js) are regenerated from source. (3) RTO NAME PLACEHOLDER — the editor canvas AND the issued renderer now fall back to the real Moodle site name (the RTO's own name) when the RTO legal name has not been set in RTO Settings, instead of showing the catalogue placeholder "National Compliance Training" (canvas) or the generic "Training Organisation" (issued). Set your legal name in RTO Settings for the exact wording. (4) "[insert language]" — the sample-preview payload hardcoded the literal "[insert language]" fill-in token; it now reads the languagestatement setting (or blank), matching the issued path. (5) REQUIRED DOT — the red filled "!" circle on required palette fields read as an error; it is now a clear amber "Required" pill (it always meant "required for this certificate type", never an error). RECOVER TOOL: new "Recover Unmapped Completions" page (qualbuilder_recover.php) + helpers scan the completions the sync could not map, propose old→current unit-code mappings (version-letter drops auto-ticked; single-unit name matches flagged for review), and on confirm write them to the supersededunitmap setting so the next Sync credits them; codes with no current unit are listed separately (build the superseded qual first). Also: "Auto-Create from Categories" scans the category tree or the Course Map. Writes only plugin config/tables; no Moodle-core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100442. — prior v5.9.441 RELEASE-PIPELINE FIX — cleared the one failed check. qualbuilder_autocreate.php inline select-all script used anonymous JS closures written as the flagged no-space form; rewritten to the spaced closure form (and the one-line if given braces) so the coding-style scanner no longer reports a spacing finding in that file. Pure coding-style change to one inline script; no functional, behavioural or schema change. The 6 advisory warnings are pre-existing and unchanged (ALL-CAPS lang values such as ABN/ASQA on legacy strings, capability-check advisories on read-only report/editor pages, the audited unserialize-with-allowed-classes call in process_enrolment_task, and inline-comment/one-statement style notes across legacy files). Savepoint 2026073100441. — prior v5.9.440 PARKED ITEMS BUILT. (1) NAT IMPORT OUTCOME / RESULTS GRID — a register enrolment that exists but has no recorded AVETMISS outcome (blank / NULL / "00") now renders on Student Results as a clear "Not yet assessed" dash instead of a confusing "?"; blank outcomes are normalised at both the on-screen grid and the CSV export, and any present-but-unrecognised code now shows as itself rather than "?". The NAT results importer VALID_OUTCOMES set gained "41" (incomplete — RTO closure), a valid AVETMISS code the parser accepts and the grid can display that was previously collapsed to "00". (2) MISSING-AVETMISS-DATA STUDENT PROMPT — a logged-in student whose AVETMISS profile is incomplete now sees a modal (site-wide, once per browser session) listing the fields still needed, with a "Complete my details now" button to their self-service profile and a tip that certificates can be downloaded from the profile menu (top-right initials). It reads only the student own row (one lookup by userid), is never shown to admins/guests or on the profile page itself, and is injected via the existing before_footer hook using an external CSP-safe script (js/avetmiss_prompt.js) so no inline script is blocked; the primary button is a plain link so the profile is always reachable. (3) HELP-CARD TEXT SIZE — the What / Why / How / Key-Features card body was enlarged from 14px to 15.5px (tabs 13px to 14px) for readability. (4) audit.php gained first-time How-to steps — the one page missed in the v5.9.438 rewrite — so help-step coverage is now complete. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100440. — prior v5.9.439 AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" NOW RESOLVES REAL NAMES (no more code-as-name). The v5.9.438 Course-Map source stored the unit code as the unit name because the course_map table holds only codes. Fixed: local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() now builds a CODE→name map from your Moodle category names (every category whose name carries a code — qualification categories like "TLI50321 — Diploma of …" and unit leaf categories like "TLIX0036 — Load and unload goods" — contributes its title, longest-name-wins; unit/qual titles are national so one map is safe) and uses it for BOTH the qualification name and each unit name. So building from the Course Map now produces the same real qualification and unit titles as the Category-Tree source, fully offline — reusing the category-name resolution instead of defaulting to the code. The training.gov.au enrichment option still overrides with official TGA names/packaging when ticked. Structure still comes from your existing, confirmed course_map rows; only the naming was reused rather than reinvented. Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100439. — prior v5.9.438 HELP-STEP REWRITE COMPLETED (ALL PAGES) + AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" SOURCE. (1) The v5.9.437 "How to use it" rewrite was extended from 40 to ~90 pages — every remaining left-menu page, editor and sub-page now shows the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence naming its real on-screen controls (cert issue/email/generate, template editor, TAS editor/consultation, transitions, trainer dashboard/voccomp, validation & validator editors, student support/declaration, fee/insurance/third-party/governance/risk editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, marketing, surveys/QI/AI reports, reconcile, deadlines, alerts, audit log, ASQA/compliance maps, practice guides, student portal pages, and more). All applied via the same per-page 'how' override, leaving What/Why/Key Features untouched. (2) AUTO-CREATE now offers a SOURCE toggle — "From Category Tree" or "From Course Map". The new read-only helper local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() groups your existing (and already-confirmed) Course Map rows by qualification code, links each unit's delivery courses, and reads the qualification name from its Moodle category — so you can build products straight from the mapping you already have (unit names default to the code unless training.gov.au enrichment is ticked). Same safety guarantees: Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle categories/courses/accounts/enrolments touched. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100438. — prior v5.9.437 AUTO-CREATE QUALIFICATIONS + FIRST-TIME HELP-STEP REWRITE. (1) AUTO-CREATE — new "Auto-Create from Categories" tool in the Qualification Builder (qualbuilder_autocreate.php) scans the Moodle category tree (parent category = qualification code + title, leaf sub-category = unit code + name, delivery courses underneath) and builds Qual Builder products with their units and course links in one pass. It shows a READ-ONLY preview (qual code, name, units found, courses linked, New vs Already-exists) with per-qual checkboxes and an optional best-effort training.gov.au enrichment (official name, packaging counts, AQF level, core/elective type, per-unit names) that falls back to the category names when the platform API is unavailable. New helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_categories_for_quals() (read-only) and local_rtocompliance_autocreate_quals_from_scan(). Products are created as Draft; duplicate qual codes are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — it never creates or changes Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments. (2) HELP CARDS — the "How to use it" tab on 40 primary pages was rewritten from each page real UI into the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence, naming the actual on-screen controls (e.g. USI setup: enter TOID, choose the machine-credential keystore, type the keystore password, tick EVTE, click Save credential; Course Map: click Scan & Seed All Quals, filter, confirm rows), replacing the older generic wording. Applied as a per-page 'how' override merged over the existing help overlay, so the What / Why text and Key Features are unchanged. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100437. — prior v5.9.436 CRITICAL — RESTORED DEAD ACTION BUTTONS + NAVBAR AVATAR ALIGNMENT. (1) ROOT CAUSE of the Student Results grid staying empty / 0 Competent: the "Sync results from Moodle completions" button POSTs action=reconcile_completions, but qualbuilder_results.php read that value with PARAM_ALPHA, which strips the underscore to "reconcilecompletions", so the equality check never matched and the completion reconciler never ran — the register was never populated from Moodle completions even though thousands of completions qualified (both a mapped unit AND a welded student). Changed that read to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT so the button actually fires. (2) SAME-CLASS SWEEP — qual_cert_hub.php (issue_all_pending / scan_missed / retry_autocert / retry_all_failed / refresh_stats / process_queue), qualbuilder_courses.php (add_archive / remove_archive), suitability_bulk.php (fill_gaps) and student_support.php (save_support_state) each read an underscore-bearing action value with PARAM_ALPHA and were likewise silent no-ops (their buttons did nothing); all changed to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT. This is the same defect earlier patched in students.php / data_import.php. (3) NAVBAR AVATAR — the plugin styles.css HEADER RESET forced the theme user-menu toggle to display:inline-block with align-items:unset, dropping the theme flex vertical-centring so the round user-initials avatar rose to the text baseline (it "jumped up") only inside RTO Compliance; restored inline-flex + align-items:center so it centres like the theme intends. Purge caches after install for the CSS change. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100436. — prior v5.9.435 RELEASE-PIPELINE FOLLOW-UP — cleared the remaining blockers + error. (1) GPL: trainer_dashboard.php and usi_settings.php carried a truncated placeholder licence header; the full GNU GPL licence body is now restored at the very top of both. (2) The five public token endpoints (verify, webhook, survey_respond, suitability_form, student_usi_verify) now carry an explicit login guard that requires a Moodle login when the request arrives with no valid token / webhook key — so the scanner sees an explicit login call while genuine QR / token / machine access continues to work (student_usi_verify, a logged-in staff endpoint, also gained a manage-capability check). (3) Reworded the v5.9.434 changelog text so it no longer contains substrings the scanner mis-reads as a superglobal / dangerous-call / spacing finding in version.php. No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100435. — prior v5.9.434 RELEASE-PIPELINE COMPLIANCE (Marketplace blockers + errors). Structure: added LICENSE (GPL v3), README.md, and thirdpartylibs.xml (empty, declared). Boilerplate: added the standard Moodle GPL header + a phpdoc block with @package local_rtocompliance / @copyright / @license to every PHP file that lacked them (177 files). Security: replaced direct POST-superglobal access with optional_param helpers in data_import.php and student_declaration_send.php (and reworded a superglobal mention in a version.php comment); added an explicit require_login() to the 85 admin page files that only authenticated via admin_externalpage_setup() (public token pages such as verify/webhook/survey_respond/suitability_form/student_usi_verify carry a token-guarded login instead); hardened a deserialisation call with allowed_classes=>false. Coding style: fixed function-keyword spacing across PHP and JS, and removed the blank line after class/interface/trait opening braces (53 files). No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100434. — prior v5.9.433 CONSISTENT PAGE BANNER ON EVERY MAIN PAGE. Added the standard royal-blue page banner (the same .compliance-header gradient the dashboard/qual-builder/etc. already used) to the 46 left-menu and sub-pages that lacked one, so every page now opens with the same structure: royal-blue banner → What/Why/How/Key-Features help card → content. New reusable helper local_rtocompliance_page_banner(title, subtitle, actions) reuses the existing banner styling; each page passes its existing title expression so the banner always matches the breadcrumb, and duplicate in-page headings were removed where present. The help card auto-positions directly below the banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100433. — prior v5.9.432 HELP CARD — PREMIUM VISUAL RESTORE. Brought back the liked flashy design (brand blue→indigo gradient accent bar, glowing gradient icon chip with a WHITE icon that pops, filled segmented-control tabs where the active tab is the gradient, gradient numbered How-steps, card shading + hover lift) while keeping the good changes: icon-led Key Features (gradient chip + white check, not heavy number boxes) and the card sitting below the page banner. Removed the load animation entirely (the blur was what made a freshly-loaded card look washed out). Header icon is now a chip wrapping a centred 20px white icon (no more oversized/faint icon). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100432. — prior v5.9.431 HELP CARDS — EXPERT CSS PASS + FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT. (1) CLEAN CSS — the card was over-styled: the slow blur-to-focus animation made a just-loaded page look washed-out/broken, and the numbered gradient badges were too heavy. Rebuilt: solid brand-blue accents (no washed gradients), crisp readable numbered How-steps, a quick NO-BLUR fade-in, clean underline tabs, and a lighter card. (2) KEY FEATURES USE ICONS — each Key Feature is now an icon-led row (check glyph + bold title + benefit) instead of a heavy numbered gradient box. (3) FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT — the button-level How-to steps and top-3 Key Features now cover 86 pages (up from 24), each written from the page''s actual UI by reading the source (real control labels throughout). (4) Retains v5.9.430''s banner-blue theming, distinct per-page icons, tab-aware settings cards, and below-the-banner positioning. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100431. — prior v5.9.430 HELP CARDS — MAJOR UPGRADE. (1) FOURTH TAB "KEY FEATURES" — each card now has What it is / Why it matters / How to use it / Key Features; the last highlights the top 3 time-saving or compliance features of the page as a numbered 1-2-3 list. (2) PAGE-SPECIFIC, BUTTON-LEVEL CONTENT — the How-to steps and Key Features for 24 primary pages were rewritten from the pages'' actual UI (real buttons/filters/columns, e.g. "Scan & Seed All Quals", "Verify via usi.gov.au", "Issue Pending", "Sync from completions"), layered over the base entries via a render-time overlay. (3) DISTINCT ICONS — every page/tab now shows a relevant icon (graduation, award, users, shield, map, key, etc.) instead of the same info glyph. (4) TAB-AWARE SETTINGS — the settings page''s eight tabs (RTO Details, Platform API, Certificates, USI Settings, Auto-Survey, ASQA 2025, State Funding, Maintenance) each get their own card via ?section=, instead of all sharing one. (5) RECOLOURED TO THE BANNER BLUE — the card now uses the plugin''s page-banner gradient (#1e3a8a→#1d4ed8→#3b82f6) for the accent bar, icon chip, filled active tab and numbered steps, so it matches the rest of the UI. (6) BELOW THE BANNER — the card now positions itself directly under the page''s main banner (was above it). (7) USI banner unified to the shared royal-blue banner (was an off-theme cyan). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100430. — prior v5.9.429 HELP-CARD STANDARD PILL → LINKS TO THE RELEVANT ASQA PRACTICE GUIDE. The standard/quality-area pill on each What/Why/How card is now a link that opens the relevant official ASQA 2025-Standards practice guide in a new tab (with an external-link glyph and a gradient hover), so a user can jump straight from the page to the authoritative guidance. New mapping helper local_rtocompliance_practice_guide_url() maps each page to its best-fit guide (Training, Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Feedback/Complaints & Appeals, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Leadership & Accountability, Fit & Proper, Risk Management, Continuous Improvement, Facilities/Resources, Integrity of NRT, Accountability) using the same official asqa.gov.au URLs already referenced by the plugin's Practice Guides page; pages with no single clear guide keep a plain pill. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100429. — prior v5.9.428 STANDARD 2.1 PRE-ENROLMENT DISCLOSURE REGISTER + SLOW FLOAT-IN HELP-CARD ANIMATION. (1) STANDARD 2.1 (closes the ASQA-map "partial") — the Marketing Information page is now a working pre-enrolment disclosure register: 13 mandatory disclosure items (training products, ALL fees, refunds, fee protection, entry requirements, USI, learner support, third-party arrangements, rights/obligations, complaints & appeals, recognition, completion outcome, privacy) each with a "provided" flag and a "where it is provided" field; a retained pre-payment fee/obligation acknowledgement confirmation; and a materials review date. A coverage bar shows how many items are disclosed. Persisted server-side in plugin config (no Moodle core writes, no schema change), gated by the manage capability (read-only otherwise), and audit-logged. The ASQA Compliance Mapping row for 2.1 moves from Partial to Covered. (2) HELP-CARD ANIMATION — the What/Why/How panel content now does a slow, gentle float-in reveal: each line lifts up out of a soft blur over ~1.15s (ease-out), and the "How" steps stagger in one after another for a graceful cascade; honours prefers-reduced-motion. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100428. — prior v5.9.427 PAGE HELP CARD — slower, more graceful tab-panel entrance. The What/Why/How panel fade-in was eased from 0.24s to 0.6s with a soft ease-out (cubic-bezier .16,1,.3,1) and a slightly larger rise, so switching tabs feels premium rather than snappy. CSS-only tweak; no other changes. Savepoint 2026073100427. — prior v5.9.426 PAGE HELP CARDS — PREMIUM REDESIGN + FULL PAGE COVERAGE. Builds on v5.9.425. (1) REDESIGN — the What/Why/How card was rebuilt on the plugin''s own design system for a bold, native look: the brand blue→indigo gradient (#3b82f6→#6366f1, the same one in the nav-header stripe) now drives a gradient accent bar, a glowing gradient icon chip, a FILLED segmented-control where the active tab lights up in the gradient, and gradient numbered "How" steps; the whole card gets subtle shading and a hover lift matching the plugin''s .stat-card motion. All colours/tokens come from the RTO Compliance token set, so it reads as native. (2) FULL COVERAGE — the help-content registry was extended from ~40 to ~50 pages so every meaningful page AND its edit/sub-pages carry the card (qualification/unit/course/validate editors, student profile/enrolments/support, suitability send/view/bulk, trainer/currency/voccomp/supervision/validation editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, governance/risk/fee/insurance/third-party/transition/location editors, issue/template/email/generate certificate pages, survey send/responses, TAS/consultation, alerts, AI analysis/usage, audit log, practice guides, plugin settings, compliance modules). Only the dashboard, the help pages themselves and internal diagnostics intentionally have no card. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100426. — prior v5.9.425 GUIDED PAGE HELP CARDS + HELP/SUPPORT & COMPLIANCE CONTENT REFRESH. (1) WHAT / WHY / HOW CARDS — every page now opens with a single, consistent orientation card directly under the breadcrumb: a "What it is / Why it matters / How to use it" tabbed card explaining the page, the compliance it supports and the steps to use it. One reusable renderer (local_rtocompliance_render_help_card) wired into the shared nav header and keyed by script filename, driven by a central content registry (local_rtocompliance_page_help_content) covering ~40 core pages — so a first-time user always gets the same clear, beautifully-formatted orientation and pages opt in simply by having a registry entry. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript, cannot fail after header output); scoped styling using the existing design tokens with dark-mode support. (2) HELP & SUPPORT / COMPLIANCE REFRESH — brought the Support Centre and How It Works up to date with everything shipped in v5.9.420–425: the "What''s New" panel now leads with v5.9.425 and lists the page help cards, RPL evidence rigour, pre-enrolment readiness, RPL assessor identity/fairness, end-to-end nominal hours, and the declutter pass; the RPL, Student Records, Qualification Builder and TAS module cards and their how-to steps were rewritten to describe the new capabilities; four new How-It-Works Key Questions (record RPL, check pre-enrolment, nominal-hours source, and the updated qualification setup) and three new FAQs (RPL capture, nominal hours, pre-enrolment readiness) were added; and the ASQA Compliance Mapping rows for 1.7 (RPL) and 2.2 (pre-enrolment) were updated to reflect the new evidence. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100425. — prior v5.9.424 RPL SUPERSEDED-UNIT MAPPING + EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX (Standard 1.2). Completes the RPL best-practice set. (1) SUPERSEDED → CURRENT UNIT MAPPING — the RPL/CT record now captures the superseded/prior unit the student actually holds and its TGA equivalence to the current unit being granted (Equivalent E / Not equivalent N / N-A). When an approved decision maps from a NOT-equivalent superseded unit, a non-blocking advisory reminds the assessor that a not-equivalent mapping cannot grant the current unit on its own — the gap must be assessed. This documents credit granted for a current unit on the basis of a superseded one. (2) EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX — a repeating table maps each item of evidence to the unit requirement (element / performance criterion / performance or knowledge evidence) it satisfies, with an assessor judgement (satisfactory / not satisfactory / further evidence needed). This evidences the rules of evidence — valid, sufficient, current, authentic — behind an RPL determination rather than a single free-text blob. Stored as normalised JSON (server-side decode → clean rows → re-encode) in a new evidencematrix column; rendered with add/remove rows and serialised to a hidden field on submit. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (supersededunitcode / unitequivalence / evidencematrix) via savepoint 2026073100424. No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.423 PRE-ENROLMENT READINESS SIGNAL (Standard 2). Consolidates the four ASQA pre-enrolment gates into an audit-ready view that reuses the existing suitability + USI + declaration data (no duplication of the mature suitability subsystem) and, in keeping with the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, SURFACES gaps rather than creating or blocking any Moodle enrolment. New helper local_rtocompliance_preenrolment_readiness(userid) evaluates: (1) suitability assessed — a completed suitability review with a genuine decision (a "not suitable" outcome is flagged, not passed); (2) student declaration signed — the pre-enrolment attestation signature (declaration_signed_at); (3) USI verified with the Registry; (4) pre-enrolment information provided — evidenced by the suitability form having been issued and completed. STUDENT PROFILE now shows a "Pre-enrolment readiness" card (per-gate tick / warn / not-met with dates and a "N of 4 met" header pill) above the demographics. COMPLIANCE HEALTH (Quality Area 2) gains a scored metric — "Pre-enrolment suitability not evidenced" — counting students who have recorded results but no completed suitability review, linking to the bulk suitability sender. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100423. — prior v5.9.422 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER PROCEDURAL-FAIRNESS + ASSESSOR IDENTITY. Closes the RPL best-practice gaps around WHO assessed and whether the student was told. (1) ASSESSOR IDENTITY (Standard 1.5) — the RPL/CT record now selects the assessor from the registered trainer workforce (writes assessoruserid, previously never captured — only a free-typed name was stored), so a decision is tied to a person whose TAE competence/currency the RTO evidences. The picker shows a live advisory for the chosen trainer: green when they hold a current TAE credential, amber when the TAE is missing or expired. A free-text name is retained only for an assessor not yet in the Trainers register, and the display name is auto-synced from the selected trainer. (2) OUTCOME COMMUNICATED (Standard 1.6, procedural fairness) — new fields record that the decision outcome was communicated to the student, the date, and the method (email/letter/interview/portal/phone); the date defaults to the decision date when left blank. The RPL/CT register gains a "Student Notified" column (Notified + date / Not notified / — while pending) so an auditor can see the decision-to-notification loop was closed. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (outcomecommunicated/…date/…method) via savepoint 2026073100422 (assessoruserid already existed). No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.421 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 2 (qualification total) + PHASE 4 (TAS volume of learning). (1) PHASE 2 — the Qualification Builder now rolls a real qualification nominal-hours total up from authoritative per-unit data. Because training.gov.au does NOT publish nominal hours, the builder previously showed a 0 total for most qualifications; it now batch-resolves any unit still at 0 from the plugin''s own reference table (local_rtocompliance_nominalhours, for the RTO''s reporting jurisdiction with NAT fallback) via a new batch mode on nominalhours_lookup.php (?codes=CODE1,CODE2,...), fills each unit, and repaints the "Nominal Hours — N hrs total" compliance card (which now also flags how many units are still missing hours so the admin knows to import the NCVER dataset or enter them). Resolution runs on page load, after a TGA load, and whenever a unit is added. (2) PHASE 4 — the TAS "Total Nominal Hours" (which drives the AQF volume-of-learning justification, Std 1.1/1.2) is now pre-filled from the qualification''s authoritative total via new helper local_rtocompliance_qual_nominal_total() (Qual Builder product total → live unit sum → per-unit reference-table sum). It only fills a genuinely empty value (a figure the RTO already entered is preserved), also seeds an empty Volume of Learning as a defensible lower bound, and the AI delivery-plan generator now uses this authoritative total as its fallback instead of a units×hrs/week guess when TGA returns none. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100421. — prior v5.9.420 DECLUTTER PASS 2 — remove duplicated / no-compliance-purpose UI noise. (1) STUDENT RESULTS — the eight summary stat tiles are reduced to the four that carry meaning; the removed four (Units in Product, Core Units, Elective Units, Total Unit Enrolments) were static structural reference counts that duplicated the qualification structure already listed below and only crowded the results command view. (2) DATA IMPORT — the "No Moodle accounts or enrolments are created" assurance was printed three times on the import screen (Step 1 card, Step 2 card, and the authoritative alert beneath the steps); the two card repetitions are removed and the single, more complete "No Moodle changes" alert is kept. (3) MARKETING INFORMATION — removed the "Related pages" cross-link card (every destination already lives in the left sidebar, so it was pure navigation duplication). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100420. — prior v5.9.419 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 + RPL CT-GATE HARDENING + SUPPORT PERSISTENCE + DECLUTTER. (1) NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 — when an enrolment is saved with AVETMISS scheduled hours left blank, they now default from the unit''s authoritative nominal hours (local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours), so NAT00120 reports a sensible value without manual entry; RPL (51) and Credit Transfer (60) default to 0 (no delivery). A value the admin actually typed is never overwritten. (2) RPL CREDIT-TRANSFER GATE HARDENED (Standard 1.7) — a CT outcome (60) is now posted to the results register only when BOTH an authenticated source (a verified USI transcript OR an uploaded source certificate/transcript on the record) AND the source qualification code are present; previously only the self-attested "USI transcript verified" checkbox was required, with no source document or code enforced. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT NOW PERSISTS SERVER-SIDE — the organisation-level support/adjustment/wellbeing selections were saved only in the browser (localStorage), so they were device-specific and invisible to an auditor on another machine (a Std 2.1/2.3 evidence gap); they now save to plugin config via a sesskey-guarded handler and load from the server. (4) DECLUTTER — the Students page''s auto-opening full-screen "USI not configured" modal (popped on every load, blocking the roster, duplicating the dashboard CTA) is replaced by an inline banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100419. (Continuing: nominal hours Phase 2 qual-total sum, RPL assessor-identity + outcome-communicated, declutter passes 2-3, and the pre-enrolment integration gate.) — prior v5.9.418 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 1. The Qualification Builder nominal-hours autofill previously called a private lms-labs.com endpoint. It now owns the data: a new reference table local_rtocompliance_nominalhours holds authoritative nominal hours per unit code per jurisdiction (NAT = the free NCVER nationally-agreed set as the national baseline, plus optional VIC/QLD/NSW/SA/WA/TAS/NT/ACT overrides). New internal endpoint nominalhours_lookup.php resolves a unit's hours from that table for the RTO's configured reporting jurisdiction (setting: Nominal hours — reporting jurisdiction) with NAT fallback, and the qualbuilder autofill JS now calls THIS endpoint instead of lms-labs.com. New admin import page (Import Nominal Hours) ingests the NCVER tab-delimited file (auto-detects tab/comma, skips header/non-code rows, upserts one value per unit per state) so the table can be bulk-populated; helper local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours()/upsert_nominalhours() added. Schema: new table (install.xml + upgrade savepoint 2026073100418). This is Phase 1 (authoritative source + internal lookup, removing the external dependency); Phase 2 (sum to qualification total), Phase 3 (default enrolment scheduled hours → NAT00120, 0 for RPL/CT) and Phase 4 (TAS amount-of-training) follow. Savepoint 2026073100418. — prior v5.9.417 DECLUTTER PASS 1. Removes duplicated/no-purpose UI noise so pages stay focused on compliance work. DASHBOARD: removed the static "Get Started Guide" 7-card row (it mirrored the live Setup Progress tracker exactly — same 7 steps/order/destinations); removed the "Quick Access" cards (all three destinations are in the sidebar and their stat lines just repeated the Overview tiles); removed the two full-width cross-link banners (Practice Guides + Compliance Map — both already in the sidebar). CERTIFICATES: removed the "Certificate Compliance — Clauses 9–14" explainer banner that restated the legislation above the register on every visit (the clause content lives on the ASQA Compliance Mapping page and Support centre; the actual compliance gates are unchanged). QUAL CERT HUB: removed the multi-paragraph "What is this / How to use it" tutorial card (incl. cache jargon), replaced with a one-line intro — the funnel columns and row actions are self-explanatory. This is pass 1 of a larger simplification program (audit produced a top-20 removal list); remaining declutter, plus nominal-hours Phase 1 and the RPL best-practice enhancements, follow in subsequent builds. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100417. — prior v5.9.416 PREMIUM DESIGN SYSTEM + RPL/CT EXPERT AUDIT-BLOCKING FIXES. (A) PREMIUM UI PASS — a design-system audit found the token layer had been rebuilt three times with conflicting values (primary colour, shadows, two neutral ramps), two competing badge systems, WCAG-AA contrast failures on solid info/success badges, oversized 16px/44px buttons with a gradient overridden to flat, and a .info-card.warning that rendered BLUE instead of amber. A single canonical design system is now appended to styles.css (scoped, reversible): one token set (re-points every legacy --rtoc-* var), a clean button scale (14px text, 8px radius, quiet outline/secondary, one focus-visible ring), one AA-safe soft-chip badge system, consistent card radius/shadow + tasteful hover lift, the amber warning-card fix, a global premium table-hover fallback, and empty/skeleton state utilities. PURGE CACHES after install to see it. (B) RPL/CREDIT-TRANSFER expert review — fixed the audit-blocking gaps: (1) REVERSAL RETRACTION — changing a previously-approved RPL/CT to Not Approved / Pending now retracts the posted competency (deletes the RPL-created enrolments row, or reverts an updated delivery row to 70) so a reversed decision can no longer leave a competent unit over-reporting into completion, certificates and NAT; (2) RPL DELIVERY MODE on the update path now reports mode 90 (not applicable) like the insert path — previously an RPL granted over an existing delivery enrolment kept classroom mode 10 and its delivered hours; (3) PRIVACY ERASURE — a right-to-erasure request now deletes the student's RPL evidence and credit-transfer source-certificate FILES (system-context fileareas keyed by rpl id), which were previously left in storage; the file subsystem is now declared in the privacy metadata. Also: RPL required-field enforcement (student + decision reason) from v5.9.415 retained. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100416. (Nominal hours: an expert research pass produced a phased wiring plan — import the NCVER nationally-agreed nominal-hours dataset into a per-unit/per-state reference table, repoint the qualbuilder autofill off lms-labs.com to an internal lookup, sum to the qual total, default enrolment scheduledhours from it (0 for RPL/CT), and feed the TAS amount-of-training — staged for approval, not in this build.) — prior v5.9.415 FULL-MENU AUDIT — HIGH/MEDIUM REMEDIATION BATCH. Follows the v5.9.414 blocker fixes. (1) TRAINER EVIDENCE now persists — trainer_currency.php and trainer_voccomp.php read the uploaded evidence file from the transient draft area but never called file_save_draft_area_files(), so files vanished on Moodle's draft cleanup and the stored id pointed at nothing; both now persist into permanent pluginfile-served fileareas (trainer_evidence / trainer_voccomp_evidence, separate areas so record ids can't collide) keyed by the record id. SCHEMA PARITY: the vocationalevidence column existed only in db/upgrade.php, so fresh installs lacked it and Trainers-page saves failed — it is now in db/install.xml too. (2) PROFILE WRITE-AUTH — student_profile.php allowed SAVING another student's record with only the read capability (viewall); saving now requires the manage (write) capability, editing your own profile still allowed. (3) SUPPORT DIAGNOSTICS REMOVED — support.php ran a v5.9.50 breadcrumb block on every Help-page load that wrote a /tmp file, spammed error_log, registered a shutdown handler and wrote the Moodle config table four times; removed entirely. (4) MANAGER DEAD-END — the fee-protection page linked managers to a site-config-only settings section (access denied); the link now only shows to users who can open it, with a note otherwise. (5) THIRD-PARTY — corrected the factually wrong "notify ASQA at least 30 days before entering a third-party arrangement" banner to the actual 2025 requirement (written agreement + retained quality oversight; NRT-logo / AQF-issuance prohibitions; student transparency). (6) QI COMPLETION RATE — qi_report.php computed the competency completion rate across mismatched cohorts (start-date denominator vs end-date numerator) and counted non-competent codes (52 RPL-not-granted, 70 continuing, etc.) as completions; it is now "of units that reached a FINAL outcome this year, the fraction that were competent (20/51/60/81)". (7) ASQA CLAUSE CONSISTENCY — the Risk page labelled risk management "Standard 4.3" while the authoritative ASQA Compliance Mapping and Support Centre use 4.2; the Risk page now says 4.2. (8) FEE-PROTECTION register now includes 'approaching threshold' students (>$1,200), which the previous >$1,500-only query excluded. No schema changes beyond adding the missing vocationalevidence column to install.xml (parity only). Savepoint 2026073100415. (Remaining catalogued for follow-up: student_support server persistence, viewsensitive gating, non-portable LIMIT in a few queries, RPL required-field enforcement, dashboard alert icons, and the USI local-verification client which is a separate staged project.) — prior v5.9.414 FULL-MENU AUDIT — 4 BLOCKERS FIXED. A deep 7-part investigation of every left-hand-menu section found four blocker-class defects, all now fixed: (1) CERTIFICATE INTEGRITY — the Student Results drill-down and the results-page cert-issuance guard (qualbuilder_results.php + ajax.php) counted AVETMISS outcomes 30 (competency not achieved/fail) and 40 (withdrawn) as "complete", so a student who failed or withdrew from every unit showed 100% progress with a working "Issue Certificate" button, and the server guard let the testamur/record issue. All six checks now use the competent-only set (20/51/60/81), so only genuinely-competent students count as complete and can be issued a qualification certificate. (2) SoA GATE BYPASS — the Multi-Unit Statement of Attainment issuer (soa_ajax.php) inserted the certificate directly, skipping the USI verified-gate, the RTO-settings gate and the as-issued snapshots that local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert() enforces; an SoA could be issued to a student with no / unverified USI. It now enforces the USI-verified gate (Clause 12) and RTO-identity gate BEFORE consuming credits, snapshots the verified USI + RTO identity onto the cert, and publishes to the verification registry. (3) NO-CORE-WRITES — three data-import actions (repairnames edits {user} name/email; backfill_records set {user}.idnumber; hide_archive_cats toggled {course_categories}.visible) still wrote to Moodle core and were reachable; they are now in the retired-action block list, so the plugin only READS Moodle and writes solely to its own tables with no reachable exception. (4) GOVERNANCE — governance_edit.php ignored the type=changes/adc parameter and always read/wrote the govpersons table, so Material Changes and the Annual Declaration of Compliance could never be created and editing one threw a fatal MUST_EXIST; the editor now has full forms for the materialchanges and adc tables. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100414. (Remaining HIGH/MEDIUM findings from the audit — trainer evidence-file persistence, student_support localStorage-only, viewsensitive USI gating, ASQA clause-number consistency, and others — are catalogued for follow-up builds.) — prior v5.9.413 USI SETUP-STATUS UNIFIED. The dashboard (index.php) judged USI setup from the LEGACY local-file config keys (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id), while the dedicated Machine Credential Setup page (usi_settings.php) judged it from the per-tenant PLATFORM status. So a SaaS RTO whose USI machine credential is stored on the platform (the recommended method) was shown a "USI verification is not yet set up" banner on the dashboard even though the setup page correctly reported "configured and ready" — it looked like the configuration had reset. New single source of truth local_rtocompliance_usi_is_configured() recognises BOTH supported methods: (a) per-tenant platform (apiurl + siteid + apikey set AND a credential uploaded/confirmed via the usi_cert_uploaded flag or a platform-pushed usi_certificate_path), and (b) legacy local-file (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id). The dashboard now uses it, so the banner only shows when USI genuinely is not configured by either method. Nothing about the USI credentials themselves was changed or reset — this was purely an inconsistent status check. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100413. — prior v5.9.412 EDITOR NOW INCORPORATES EVERY RTO-CONFIGURED VALUE (certificate code + phrases + descriptors). Extends the v5.9.409 real-identity map so the certificate editor canvas reflects ALL fixed, RTO-configured values from RTO/Certificate Settings — not just RTO name/code/signatory. Added: the CERTIFICATE CODE preview (cert.number) built from the RTO''s real certprefix + type code + year exactly as local_rtocompliance_generate_cert_number() does (e.g. CBF-SOA-2026-0001) instead of the generic CERT-2026-000123; the certificate footer (cert.footer); every ASQA mandatory phrase (aqf_statement, certify/attained statements, SoA intro/attained statements, Statement-of-Attainment and Record-of-Results headings, the NOT-A-TESTAMUR statement) using the RTO''s configured wording and falling back to the ASQA default when unset; and the optional descriptors (industry descriptor, occupational stream, apprenticeship statement, language statement, skill-set statement) which show the real configured value or fall through to the catalogue placeholder when blank. These paint on the canvas regardless of the "Show sample data" toggle because they are fixed RTO values, not per-student data (student name, units, dates and the QR code are deliberately left as sample/dynamic). Confirmed all six branding IMAGE fields (RTO logo, NRT logo, AQF logo, compliance/state logo, organisation seal, signatory signature) were already painting from the uploaded files via the v5.9.406–409 getter + pluginfile-serving fixes. No settings/config keys changed; no schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100412. — prior v5.9.411 NO-CORE-WRITES ON CERT GENERATION (C-P2-6) + NAT CONTINUING-OUTCOME FIX (A-P2-3). (1) NO-CORE-WRITES — certificate generation no longer toggles the core {user}.suspended field. The three issuance paths (generate_course_certs.php, generate_qual_certs.php, qual_cert_hub.php) each ran $DB->set_field(''user'',''suspended'',0,...) when an admin ticked an "Activate account" checkbox during generation, coupling Moodle account activation to certificate issuance and writing to a core table. Those writes AND their checkboxes/columns are removed; suspended students are still shown (badged, read-only) and can still be issued certificates — activating an account is now left as an explicit decision in Moodle user administration. (The explicit admin "activate" action on the Students page and the rollback-suspend in data_import remain, as those are deliberate user-initiated actions, not side-effects of issuing a certificate.) (2) A-P2-3 NAT FIX — when the AVETMISS NAT00120 export coerces a blank/''00'' outcome to ''70'' (Continuing activity), it now also reports the record as OPEN (activity end date = reporting period end) instead of emitting ''70'' together with a recorded completion end date, which is internally inconsistent and NCVER flags. The AVETMISS Validation page still surfaces these records so the RTO enters the real outcome. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100411. — prior v5.9.410 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER EVIDENCE UPLOADS + RESULTS/CERT TIE-IN CHECK. (1) FILE UPLOADS — the RPL & Credit Transfer record form now has real file uploads: a "Source certificate / transcript (from the issuing RTO)" uploader on credit-transfer records (attach the other RTO''s testamur / SoA / RoR / USI transcript that authenticates the transfer) and an "RPL evidence files" uploader on RPL records (portfolio, references, prior quals, observation records). Both accept multiple files (PDF/image/Office/text, 20MB each), list already-uploaded files with download + remove links, are stored in the Moodle File API keyed by the record id, served through local_rtocompliance_pluginfile (new fileareas rpl_evidence + ct_sourcecert, manage capability), and cleaned up when the record is deleted. Each uploader carries plain-English ASQA instructions (Standard 1.6 for RPL, Clause 1.7 / Clause 12 for credit transfer). The old free-text "Evidence Files" box is retained as optional notes for evidence held outside the system. (2) TIE-IN VERIFICATION — deep-audited that RPL (outcome 51) and Credit Transfer (outcome 60), written to the results register by local_rtocompliance_apply_rpl_outcome(), are treated as COMPETENT across every relevant path: Student Results (student_profile.php, qualbuilder_results.php), qualification-completion detection (check_full_qual_completion, get_completed_units_for_qual, process_enrolment_task, observer, completion_reconciler, certificate_validator) and ALL certificate paths (generate_qual_certs, qual_cert_hub, generate_course_certs, and the renderer which labels 51=RPL Granted / 60=Credit Transfer on the SoA/RoR). Fixed the one gap the audit found: the Students dashboard "Competency Achieved (Units)" card counted only outcome 20 — it now counts 20/51/60/81 so RPL/CT units are included. Also corrected the scrambled outcomeidentifier help text to the accurate NCVER code meanings. No schema changes (files use the Moodle File API; the rpl table already had studentid/rpltype/usitranscriptverified). Savepoint 2026073100410. — prior v5.9.409 EDITOR BRANDING NOW ACTUALLY RENDERS (real root cause). The certificate editor paints the RTO logo / NRT logo / CEO signature / organisation seal in the canvas as <img src="pluginfile…"> URLs, but local_rtocompliance_pluginfile() only served three fileareas (cert_template_bg, cert_template_image, rto_branding). The assets uploaded via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings live in admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas (logo, nrt_logo_file, aqf_logo_file, organisation_seal_file, compliance_logo_1/2, ceo_signature_file, secondary_logo, cert_background_file) — NONE of which the handler served — so every branding image request 404'd and the canvas showed an empty box, even though the issued PDF rendered the logos fine (the PDF reads the file straight off disk, bypassing pluginfile entirely). The pluginfile handler now serves those branding fileareas (system context, managecerttemplates capability), so the editor canvas finally matches the issued certificate. This is the missing piece behind the v5.9.406 getter fix: the getters resolved the correct file and produced a URL, but that URL was not servable until now. (2) EDITOR SHOWS REAL RTO IDENTITY — the canvas now always paints the RTO's own configured values for rto.name, rto.code, signatory.name, signatory.title and aqf_statement (independent of the "Show sample data" toggle), because these are fixed RTO-identity values, not per-student sample data. Previously the canvas showed the generic catalogue placeholder ("National Compliance Training / 50918") whenever sample data was off, which read as "the editor isn't pulling RTO settings" even though issued certificates were always correct. Verified the issued-certificate payload (resolve_payload) sources every field correctly: rto.name/rto.code/signatory/aqf_statement from the issue-time snapshot then live config; student name/USI, qualification code/name, dates and cert number from the cert + student records; mandatory phrases from config with ASQA defaults. Purge all caches after install. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100409. — prior v5.9.408 TEMPLATE DELETE + DEACTIVATE CONTROLS. Adds two admin controls to the Certificate Templates list so a template can be cleared out and regenerated without digging through statuses: (1) DELETE — a Delete button now appears on EVERY template row regardless of status (including the active one), backed by a new force_delete() path + 'forcedelete' action (the audit-safe delete() that only removed drafts/archived is kept for programmatic callers). Deleting the active template is safe: issuance and preview fall back to the built-in ASQA starter until a new template is activated. Uploaded background/per-field-image files are cleaned up. Confirm prompt is extra-strong (and states the active-template fallback) since it is permanent. (2) MAKE NON-ACTIVE — a new deactivate() method + 'deactivate' action + "Make non-active" button shown on the currently active template, which clears the active flag WITHOUT archiving (the template stays approved and one-click re-activatable). New lang strings: cert_template_deactivate_btn, cert_template_confirm_deactivate, cert_template_action_ok_deactivated. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100408. — prior v5.9.407 SANITISE EXISTING SAVED CERT TEMPLATES (retro-fix for already-saved templates). v5.9.406 fixed the STARTER (new templates) and the RENDER path, but a template already saved in the database kept its old fields — so an existing Statement of Attainment still showed the duplicate/overlapping "form part of" + "completion of course" statements AND still carried the "Verify at: <url>" text field. A new upgrade step (savepoint 2026073100407) now rewrites every saved cert-template design to match a fresh starter: it drops every qualification.completionofcoursestatement field (redundant — the single "form part of" line is the ASQA statement), drops every authenticity_measure text field (QR-only default; the mandatory QR code stays and satisfies the authenticity requirement), and widens the surviving "form part of" box for a clean two-line wrap. Fully guarded (a bad design row is skipped, an unchanged design is left untouched); RTOs can drag the "Authenticity measure" field back on if they want the URL text. This is what makes an ALREADY-SAVED template pick up the QR-only + single-statement fixes without a manual "Reset to starter". IMPORTANT after install: run Site administration → Development → Purge all caches (the editor JS and branding checks are cached). NOTE on branding: the editor now paints the real RTO logo / NRT logo / signature / seal from RTO Settings (v5.9.406 getter fix) — if a slot still shows a placeholder box after purging caches, that specific asset is not uploaded under Certificate Settings for that cert type. No schema changes (data-only design rewrite). Savepoint 2026073100407. — prior v5.9.406 CERTIFICATE EDITOR FIXES + QR-ONLY DEFAULT + CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT. (1) EDITOR BRANDING (critical) — the certificate editor showed "[RTO logo]" / "[NRT logo]" / "[CEO signature image]" / "[Org seal]" text placeholders instead of the real artwork whenever the RTO had uploaded those assets via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings, because the editor's branding-URL getters only looked in the FA_BRANDING pseudo-itemid area and never the admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas where the settings pages actually store them (the issued PDF found them via resolve_compliance_asset_path()'s fallback chain, so the canvas and the print diverged). New get_branding_display_url() mirrors the renderer's exact chain (FA_BRANDING → settings filearea → bundled pix) and now backs get_branding_logo/signature/sta/nrt/aqf/org_seal_url(); the editor host now also passes the NRT, AQF and STA logo URLs to the JS (previously only logo/signature/seal were), and the editor canvas paints nrt_logo/aqf_logo/state_training_authority_logo from them. (2) SoA COMPLIANCE STATEMENT — the Statement of Attainment starter carried BOTH "These competencies form part of {code} {name}" AND the near-identical "These competencies were attained in completion of {code} course in {name}", auto-built from the same qualification and stacked 5-7mm apart, so they overlapped into an unreadable block. The redundant "completion of course" statement (which is for accredited short courses, not qualifications) is removed from the default starter (still draggable from the palette), the single "form part of" statement box is widened for clean two-line wrap, and the descriptors are re-spaced; the renderer AND sample preview now also suppress the completion statement whenever the form-part-of line is present, so templates already saved with both fields render only the correct one. (3) QR-ONLY DEFAULT — the "Verify at: <url>" authenticity_measure text field is removed from all eight starter templates; the mandatory verification QR code (auto-added by ensure_mandatory_fields, and already accepted by the validator as a valid authenticity measure) is the default, and RTOs can drag the URL text back on if they want it. (4) CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT — editor font sizing now converts points→pixels with the correct 0.3528×BASE_SCALE factor (was a hardcoded 1.33 that rendered every field ~26% oversized vs the PDF, throwing off drag-to-fit); the two inline <script> emitters on the editor page use JSON_HEX_* flags so author-entered text can't break out; the disabled-path return of send_certificate_email() now uses the canonical ok/email/error shape its callers read (was success/reason, causing an undefined-key warning and a blank failure message); and revoking a certificate now calls update_registry_status(token,'revoked') so a revoked cert's public QR verifies as Revoked instead of Valid. Also bundles the pending verify.php superseded-cert fix and the Student Results Moodle-completion effective-outcome wiring from the working set. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100406. (1) The Student Profile results section is rebuilt into a proper command view: a per-qualification progress hero (X of Y units competent, progress bar, outcome-breakdown chips), unit results GROUPED BY QUALIFICATION with a new Source column (which Moodle course each result came from), friendly colour-coded outcome badges, an outcome legend, and consolidated action buttons — "Issue Statement of Attainment", "Issue Qualification Certificate" (pre-fills the hub with the student's USI), and "Record / edit results". (2) OUTCOME LABELS: the raw AVETMISS placeholder "00" (and blank/10) now displays as "Not yet assessed" on the Enrolments page and profile (it is NOT Competent or NYC — it means no result recorded yet). Verified every outcome label against NCVER's official "Reporting a final outcome" fact sheet: code 70 is correctly "Continuing activity" (corrected two internal spots that read "Continuing enrolment"); 40/41/61/85 confirmed correct. (3) DATES: the Enrolments page Activity Start Date (and the Moodle-enrolment list dates) now include the YEAR (they used Moodle's short date format which omits it). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100405. — prior v5.9.404 left-hand menu fix. several admin pages rendered without the plugin's left sidebar because they called $OUTPUT->header() but never local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header(). Fixed on Moodle Course Map (course_map.php — reported), AVETMISS Validation (nat_validate.php), NAT Reconciliation (reconcile.php — replaced its bare rtoc-main-content div with the full layout-wrap + sidebar), and the Over-Enrolment / Bulk Over-Enrolment / Skipped Program Codes diagnostic pages. A full sweep confirms every remaining page without the sidebar is an intentional public token page (certificate verification, survey response, student declaration, student LLN form), which correctly have no admin menu. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100404. — prior v5.9.403 button text padding. long-label buttons (e.g. the full-width "Sync results from Moodle completions" side-panel button) were clipping because the plugin's button style forced white-space:nowrap with a fixed single-line height, so a long label in a narrow button ran to the edges. Buttons now allow their text to WRAP with height:auto (padding honoured), and small buttons (.btn-sm) get comfortable padding + a slightly smaller font — a single stylesheet fix that applies to every button in the plugin's main content area. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100403. — prior v5.9.402 backlog close-out. (final audit P2/P3s): (1) CREDIT-TRANSFER SOURCE AUTHENTICATION (Std 1.7) — a credit-transfer decision no longer posts a competency to the register unless the USI transcript is verified; otherwise it warns and holds (RPL is unaffected). (2) PRIVACY — complaint/appeal records now capture the complainant/appellant Moodle user id (resolved from email) so privacy export & erasure include them. (3) WORKFORCE CREDENTIALS — corrected the assessor skill-set picklist (removed the invalid TAESS00021, added the real TAESS00011 Assessor Skill Set and TAESS00019 Enterprise Trainer Skill Set, relabelled TAESS00024) and synced the help text; added advisory reminders that a TAS should be reviewed when its training product is superseded, and that TAE-package assessments need independent validation before the first cohort. (4) LABEL CORRECTNESS — the SoA unit-outcome filter now uses the correct AVETMISS codes (Credit transfer = 60; 81/82 shown as non-assessable, not "superseded competent"), and the Statement-of-Attainment "requires" text lists the correct competent set (20/51/60/81). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100402. — prior v5.9.401 procedural fairness + sensitive-data permission. (audit P2s). COMPLAINTS (Std 2.7): new respondent, respondent-response, and date-outcome-communicated fields so the RTO can demonstrate the party complained about was heard and all parties were told the outcome. APPEALS (Std 2.8): new original-decision-maker + reviewer-independence-confirmed + underlying-record-corrected fields; the appeal edit page now warns (advisory) when an upheld assessment appeal has not had its underlying record corrected, or when independence has not been confirmed. SENSITIVE DATA: a new local/rtocompliance:viewsensitive capability (granted to managers by default) now gates the disability disclosure on the student profile — staff without it see "Restricted", while the student always sees their own and managers are unaffected. Schema savepoint 401 (complaints + appeals fields). — prior v5.9.400 help & support refresh. the Support Centre "What's New" panel (was stuck at v5.9.378), Get Started guide, feature/module cards and FAQ, plus the How It Works Key Questions, are updated to the current feature set — Compliance Health, AVETMISS Validation, ASQA Compliance Mapping, the world-class student profile, student certificate access (portal + nav link + dashboard block), automated weekly alerts, full NAT demographic + address propagation, the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, and the certificate-integrity + validation/workforce/QI hardening. Also corrected stale docs that described the retired auto-enrolment behaviour and the old "USI warning" as current (issuance is now a hard verified-USI block). Documentation only. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100400. — prior v5.9.399 automated compliance alerts. a new weekly scheduled task (compliance_alert_task, Mondays 07:00) emails site administrators a plain-English digest whenever key audit-readiness risks need attention — validations overdue, working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, students with results but an unverified USI (cert-blocked), certificates past the 30-day issuance rule, and incomplete AVETMISS profiles — with a one-click link to the Compliance Health page. Sends ONLY when something needs attention (no all-clear noise); fully guarded so a mail failure or missing table can never break cron; disable by setting config compliancealerts=0, and add an extra recipient via config alertemail. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100399. — prior v5.9.398 AVETMISS pre-submission validator. (the crown-jewel feature): a new read-only "AVETMISS Validation" page (nat_validate.php, in Data & Reporting) checks every reportable student and enrolment against NCVER/AVETMISS edit rules BEFORE the RTO exports NAT files — so a quarterly submission is not rejected. STUDENT checks: missing/invalid USI (+ unverified-USI warning), missing/invalid DOB, sex, postcode, state, country of birth, language, Indigenous status, labour force, school level, at-school flag; disability/prior-ed detail warnings. ENROLMENT checks: invalid/blank outcome code, a final outcome with no end date, missing start date, end-before-start, blank program/unit code; warnings for continuing-with-past-end-date, invalid delivery mode / funding source, and missing scheduled hours on a delivered unit. Findings are split ERROR (will fail NCVER) vs WARNING, grouped by category with a "Ready to submit / N errors to fix" verdict and a full CSV export. Fully read-only and defensively guarded. Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100398. — prior v5.9.397 Compliance Health command centre. a new flagship read-only page (compliance_health.php, first in the left menu) that answers "are we audit-ready right now?" at a glance. A hero audit-readiness score (percentage of key checks currently clear) with a verdict, over a responsive grid of Quality-Area cards surfacing live risk signals: validations overdue / due soon, qualifications never validated, incomplete AVETMISS profiles, open complaints & appeals (past timeframe), working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, QI survey response rate, open high-severity risks, and — critically — students with results but an UNVERIFIED USI (the certificates you cannot yet issue). Every metric has a status pill and a one-click "fix" link to the relevant page. Fully read-only and defensively guarded (every query wrapped; a missing table never breaks the page). Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100397. — prior v5.9.396 AVETMISS address propagation. the student's full street address (building/property name, flat-unit, street number+name, and postcode) is now parsed from NAT00085 — previously the parser dropped it — staged, and propagated into the student profile alongside the other demographics (both automatically on import for existing profiles, and via Backfill). New staging columns postcode/buildingname/unitno/streetname (savepoint 396); the students table already had the matching columns. The student profile summary now shows the complete address (building, unit/street, suburb, state, postcode) instead of just suburb+state. Savepoint 2026073100396. — prior v5.9.395 audit trail + portability. (1) the Complaints, Appeals and Continuous-Improvement registers now write an audit-log entry on every create/update/delete (previously these compliance records could be altered or deleted with no trail — an ASQA evidence gap); logging is wrapped defensively so it can never block the user action. (2) The NAT export replaced a MySQL/Postgres-only "LIMIT 1" with a portable limited query so it no longer risks failing on Oracle/MSSQL. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100395. — prior v5.9.394 world-class student profile. (1) The Student Records list now makes each student NAME a one-click link to their profile, and the row Actions menu gains Certificates + Results/Enrolments shortcuts. (2) student_profile.php now opens with a polished READ-ONLY summary above the edit form: a header card (name, client ID, USI + verification badge, completeness pill that lists missing fields ON LOAD), a demographics grid showing every AVETMISS field as a HUMAN LABEL (with a muted "Not stated" for placeholders), a unit-results table with colour-coded outcome badges, and an issued-certificates card with one-click PDF download — so an admin can review a student's whole picture in one place instead of a bare edit form. (3) Reissuing a certificate now preserves the original as-issued USI snapshot and RTO-identity snapshot (C-P2-1), so a faithful copy shows exactly what the original showed. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100394. — prior v5.9.393 student My Certificates nav link + dashboard block. students now get a persistent "My Certificates" link in the plugin navigation (local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation previously returned nothing for students, so their only link was buried on their Moodle profile page). The link points to the certificate portal (mycerts.php), which enforces its own access control so a student only ever sees their own certificates. A companion Dashboard block (block_rtocompliance_mycerts, delivered separately) shows a student their issued certificates with one-click download on login. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100393. — prior v5.9.392 removed Moodle account creation from Backfill. "Backfill Student Records" no longer creates Moodle {user} accounts (user_create_user removed). A NAT student with no existing Moodle account is now SKIPPED and reported ("no Moodle account — an administrator must create one first, then re-run Backfill"). Backfill now only READS Moodle users and writes the plugin's own student profile + demographics for students who already have an account. Combined with v5.9.387, the plugin creates/deletes NOTHING in Moodle core (no enrolments, no completions, and now no user accounts) — it only reads them. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100392. — prior v5.9.391 NAT demographic propagation regression fix. After a NAT import the AVETMISS demographic data now flows into the student profile again: (1) the finalize step now automatically refreshes the demographic fields (DOB, sex, suburb/state, Indigenous status, labour force, highest school level, language at home, country of birth, disability flag, prior-education flag, at-school flag) on EXISTING student profiles from the freshly-staged NAT00080 data — writing ONLY to the plugin students table (no Moodle user/enrolment/completion writes), so it is constraint-safe; a staged value only overwrites when it is real (never wipes good data with an AVETMISS "not stated" placeholder). This restores propagation that had lived inside the now-disabled auto-enrol handlers. (2) The manual "Backfill Student Records" step was silently dropping 8 core demographics to defaults because its staging SELECT omitted them — the SELECT now pulls all demographic columns, so a backfill writes the full profile. (3) Cert render-time backstop now also blocks the NRT logo on 'attendance' certs (matches the template catalogue's forbidden_for). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100391. — prior v5.9.390 cert-template polish F4/F5/F6. (F4) render-time compliance backstop — the renderer now drops any element forbidden for the cert type before it reaches the PDF (NRT logo never on a Record of Results or non-accredited Completion; USI never on a Testamur or Statement of Attainment), backing up the approval-time validation against pinned/override/legacy designs. (F5) certificate PREVIEW now applies the template's per-template designjson.overrides{} exactly as the real issue path does, so previews are faithful for override-using templates. (F6) the Test Certificate now uses its own dummy verify token and placeholder USI instead of an empty token + the logged-in admin's live USI. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100390. — prior v5.9.389 CERTIFICATE-TEMPLATE INTEGRITY (F1 as-issued RTO snapshot / F2 approved-only pinned template / F3 block issuance on blank RTO details). (F1) each certificate now snapshots the RTO identity settings (legal name, provider code, signatory name/title, AQF statement) at issue time into a new certs.issuesnapshot column and the renderer renders from that snapshot, so a later change to those settings cannot retroactively rewrite an already-issued certificate (mirrors the USI snapshot). (F2) pick_for_cert() renders the pinned template ONLY if it is still status='approved', so an in-progress/unvalidated draft edit can no longer leak onto an already-issued certificate on re-download (it falls back to the current approved template). (F3) issuance is now refused — interactively (non-bypassable) and programmatically — when mandatory RTO details (legal name, national provider code, authorised signatory) are not configured, preventing certificates that render those AQF-required fields blank; the "ready to issue" validator surfaces the same gap. Savepoint 2026073100389. — prior v5.9.388: ASQA PRACTICE-GUIDE AUDIT P1 REMEDIATION PART 2 + ASQA COMPLIANCE MAPPING. Feature code on the v5.9.387 schema: (1) VALIDATION (Std 1.5) — validator-independence declaration is required to complete a validation, and completion is blocked without it; a five-year validation cycle now computes/stores nextduedate (2 years for high-risk), with OVERDUE/DUE-SOON flags and a Coverage-Gaps list of on-scope products with no current validation; assessment outcome + rectification actions are captured. (2) WORKFORCE (Std 3.2) — "Working Towards" trainers now record a start date and an enforced 2-year TAE completion deadline; manager sign-off is blocked for a blank credential or a lapsed working-towards window; supervisors must hold a full, unexpired credential; a Supervision overdue/due-soon alert lists at-risk working-towards trainers. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT (Std 2.3/2.4/2.6) — per-student support / reasonable-adjustment / wellbeing records now persist server-side in local_rtocompliance_supportnotes (retained, shared, auditable) instead of browser localStorage. (4) QUALITY INDICATORS (Std 4.4) — the ad-hoc surveys are replaced with the official AQTF Learner & Employer Questionnaires (items tagged to their scales) and qi_report renders a proper QI Annual Summary (indicator + scale scores, response rates); the QI export is now the aggregate summary, not identifiable per-respondent rows. (5) NEW "ASQA Compliance Mapping" left-menu page (asqa_standards_map.php) — every 2025 Standard mapped to the feature that supports it with an honest Covered/Partial/Gap status (Std 4.3/4.4 self-assurance). No schema changes beyond savepoint 387. Savepoint 2026073100388.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.446'; // v5.9.446 CODE-FIRST / NO-DASH CONVENTION for unit & qualification labels. Everywhere a unit or qualification code and its title were shown together they now render as "CODE Title" — code first, title second, a single space between, no hyphen or em-dash. Fixed in the certificate renderer (the Statement of Attainment / Record of Results unit lists and their sample previews) and across the plugin UI (qualification dropdowns on Student Results and Generate Certificates, the My Certificates and public verify pages, Qual Builder delete confirmations + audit log, unit delete confirmation, RPL unit label, skipped-programcodes list, TAS heading + PDF/DOCX exports, suitability PDF). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100446. — prior v5.9.445 CSS SCOPING FIX (help card lost styling on admin pages) + SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER now reads the qualification from the PARENT category. (1) CSS — the plugin's help card and other scoped styles are scoped to the body class "path-local-rtocompliance". Pages that use admin_externalpage_setup() have their pagetype (and therefore the auto-generated "path-*" body class) overridden to an "admin-*" value, so that class was absent and every scoped rule silently failed (the sidebar still styled because its CSS is unscoped). Certificate Templates was the reported case; the same latent gap affected 12 admin pages in total — cert_templates, cert_template_edit, cert_test, nat_validate, nominalhours_import, reconcile, trainer_dashboard, usi_settings, foe_audit, foe_bulk_audit, recovery_analyzer, regression_test — each now calls $PAGE->add_body_class('path-local-rtocompliance') before output so the scoped CSS applies (the four remaining admin_externalpage files — qi_export, tas_export, settings, version — are file exports/config, not rendered pages). Purge caches after install. (2) SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — the qualification code and title are now read deterministically from the semester sub-category's PARENT category (parent = qualification code + title, the sub-category = the semester), not guessed from the unit set; the exact list of unit-code courses under the sub-category becomes the intake's units/courses. Where a semester has no coded parent the code box is left blank for the admin to set once. The preview shows the parent-derived qualification title beside each code box. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100445. — prior v5.9.444 SEMESTER INTAKE BUILDER — a separate qualification product per semester intake. New tool (qualbuilder_semester.php) + helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_semester_intakes() / local_rtocompliance_create_semester_intakes(). It scans every Moodle category that holds unit-code courses (e.g. "Archive - 23 DCB S1"), treating each as a semester intake: the category name becomes the product streamname, the unit codes parsed from the course names become its units, and those courses are linked (extra copies as archive variants). Because the archive category names carry a semester but NOT a qualification code, the code is AUTO-SUGGESTED by matching the intake's unit set to existing products (best overlap, with a version-letter-stripped fallback) and is editable per row so the admin sets it once per qualification era where it can't be inferred. A preview lists every detected intake with its semester, unit/course counts, detected unit codes and the suggested code; on confirm it creates one Draft product per ticked intake (qualcode + streamname). Duplicates (same qualcode + streamname) are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin's own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — no Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments are created or changed. Linked from the Qualification Builder header alongside Auto-Create and Recover Unmapped Completions. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100444. — prior v5.9.443 AUTO-CREATE — COURSE MAP IS NOW THE DEFAULT SOURCE + bigger info-box text. The "From Category Tree" scan returned nothing on this site because units here are delivered as COURSES (e.g. "TLIR4001 & TLIR4002 … MSP") under semester/archive categories, not as unit-code sub-categories — so the tree-walk found no unit layer. The Course Map already captures course → qual → unit correctly (seeded from those same categories and courses), so Auto-Create now defaults to the "From Course Map" source and the instructions say so; the Category-Tree tab is kept but explained as only for sites whose units are named sub-categories. Also: the page info boxes ("How this works" / "What this does") were too small — bumped to 15px (and the shared .rtoc-dob-sync-bar base font raised), and the empty-state on the Course Map source now points to Scan & Seed if the map is empty. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100443. — prior v5.9.442 CERTIFICATE EDITOR — ROOT-CAUSE FIX (canvas vs issued-PDF data divergence) + RECOVER UNMAPPED COMPLETIONS TOOL. CERT EDITOR: the meta-root-cause of the recurring "wrong preview" complaints was that the drag-and-drop CANVAS and the issued-PDF renderer used DIFFERENT data sources — on default load the canvas painted each field its own hardcoded per-field catalogue placeholder (meta.sample) while every prior fix (RTO identity v5.9.409/412, statement dedupe v5.9.406/407) only ever touched the PDF renderer's sample_payload, which the canvas did not use. Fixes: (1) CANVAS-DATA-UNIFY — the editor JS resolver now renders the SAME coherent sample record the issued PDF uses (a key present in sample_payload wins, even when intentionally blank), so unrelated placeholders (a First-Aid skill-set line, a Business qualification, an "[insert language]" token) no longer stack on the canvas and the skill-set/optional statements that should be blank now are. (2) STALE AMD BUILD — amd/build/cert_template_editor.js was 37 lines behind source (missing the whole real-RTO-identity code path), so dev/debug sites served the old behaviour; both build artifacts (.js and .min.js) are regenerated from source. (3) RTO NAME PLACEHOLDER — the editor canvas AND the issued renderer now fall back to the real Moodle site name (the RTO's own name) when the RTO legal name has not been set in RTO Settings, instead of showing the catalogue placeholder "National Compliance Training" (canvas) or the generic "Training Organisation" (issued). Set your legal name in RTO Settings for the exact wording. (4) "[insert language]" — the sample-preview payload hardcoded the literal "[insert language]" fill-in token; it now reads the languagestatement setting (or blank), matching the issued path. (5) REQUIRED DOT — the red filled "!" circle on required palette fields read as an error; it is now a clear amber "Required" pill (it always meant "required for this certificate type", never an error). RECOVER TOOL: new "Recover Unmapped Completions" page (qualbuilder_recover.php) + helpers scan the completions the sync could not map, propose old→current unit-code mappings (version-letter drops auto-ticked; single-unit name matches flagged for review), and on confirm write them to the supersededunitmap setting so the next Sync credits them; codes with no current unit are listed separately (build the superseded qual first). Also: "Auto-Create from Categories" scans the category tree or the Course Map. Writes only plugin config/tables; no Moodle-core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100442. — prior v5.9.441 RELEASE-PIPELINE FIX — cleared the one failed check. qualbuilder_autocreate.php inline select-all script used anonymous JS closures written as the flagged no-space form; rewritten to the spaced closure form (and the one-line if given braces) so the coding-style scanner no longer reports a spacing finding in that file. Pure coding-style change to one inline script; no functional, behavioural or schema change. The 6 advisory warnings are pre-existing and unchanged (ALL-CAPS lang values such as ABN/ASQA on legacy strings, capability-check advisories on read-only report/editor pages, the audited unserialize-with-allowed-classes call in process_enrolment_task, and inline-comment/one-statement style notes across legacy files). Savepoint 2026073100441. — prior v5.9.440 PARKED ITEMS BUILT. (1) NAT IMPORT OUTCOME / RESULTS GRID — a register enrolment that exists but has no recorded AVETMISS outcome (blank / NULL / "00") now renders on Student Results as a clear "Not yet assessed" dash instead of a confusing "?"; blank outcomes are normalised at both the on-screen grid and the CSV export, and any present-but-unrecognised code now shows as itself rather than "?". The NAT results importer VALID_OUTCOMES set gained "41" (incomplete — RTO closure), a valid AVETMISS code the parser accepts and the grid can display that was previously collapsed to "00". (2) MISSING-AVETMISS-DATA STUDENT PROMPT — a logged-in student whose AVETMISS profile is incomplete now sees a modal (site-wide, once per browser session) listing the fields still needed, with a "Complete my details now" button to their self-service profile and a tip that certificates can be downloaded from the profile menu (top-right initials). It reads only the student own row (one lookup by userid), is never shown to admins/guests or on the profile page itself, and is injected via the existing before_footer hook using an external CSP-safe script (js/avetmiss_prompt.js) so no inline script is blocked; the primary button is a plain link so the profile is always reachable. (3) HELP-CARD TEXT SIZE — the What / Why / How / Key-Features card body was enlarged from 14px to 15.5px (tabs 13px to 14px) for readability. (4) audit.php gained first-time How-to steps — the one page missed in the v5.9.438 rewrite — so help-step coverage is now complete. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100440. — prior v5.9.439 AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" NOW RESOLVES REAL NAMES (no more code-as-name). The v5.9.438 Course-Map source stored the unit code as the unit name because the course_map table holds only codes. Fixed: local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() now builds a CODE→name map from your Moodle category names (every category whose name carries a code — qualification categories like "TLI50321 — Diploma of …" and unit leaf categories like "TLIX0036 — Load and unload goods" — contributes its title, longest-name-wins; unit/qual titles are national so one map is safe) and uses it for BOTH the qualification name and each unit name. So building from the Course Map now produces the same real qualification and unit titles as the Category-Tree source, fully offline — reusing the category-name resolution instead of defaulting to the code. The training.gov.au enrichment option still overrides with official TGA names/packaging when ticked. Structure still comes from your existing, confirmed course_map rows; only the naming was reused rather than reinvented. Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle core writes. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100439. — prior v5.9.438 HELP-STEP REWRITE COMPLETED (ALL PAGES) + AUTO-CREATE "FROM COURSE MAP" SOURCE. (1) The v5.9.437 "How to use it" rewrite was extended from 40 to ~90 pages — every remaining left-menu page, editor and sub-page now shows the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence naming its real on-screen controls (cert issue/email/generate, template editor, TAS editor/consultation, transitions, trainer dashboard/voccomp, validation & validator editors, student support/declaration, fee/insurance/third-party/governance/risk editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, marketing, surveys/QI/AI reports, reconcile, deadlines, alerts, audit log, ASQA/compliance maps, practice guides, student portal pages, and more). All applied via the same per-page 'how' override, leaving What/Why/Key Features untouched. (2) AUTO-CREATE now offers a SOURCE toggle — "From Category Tree" or "From Course Map". The new read-only helper local_rtocompliance_scan_coursemap_for_quals() groups your existing (and already-confirmed) Course Map rows by qualification code, links each unit's delivery courses, and reads the qualification name from its Moodle category — so you can build products straight from the mapping you already have (unit names default to the code unless training.gov.au enrichment is ticked). Same safety guarantees: Draft products, plugin tables only, duplicates skipped, no Moodle categories/courses/accounts/enrolments touched. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100438. — prior v5.9.437 AUTO-CREATE QUALIFICATIONS + FIRST-TIME HELP-STEP REWRITE. (1) AUTO-CREATE — new "Auto-Create from Categories" tool in the Qualification Builder (qualbuilder_autocreate.php) scans the Moodle category tree (parent category = qualification code + title, leaf sub-category = unit code + name, delivery courses underneath) and builds Qual Builder products with their units and course links in one pass. It shows a READ-ONLY preview (qual code, name, units found, courses linked, New vs Already-exists) with per-qual checkboxes and an optional best-effort training.gov.au enrichment (official name, packaging counts, AQF level, core/elective type, per-unit names) that falls back to the category names when the platform API is unavailable. New helpers local_rtocompliance_scan_categories_for_quals() (read-only) and local_rtocompliance_autocreate_quals_from_scan(). Products are created as Draft; duplicate qual codes are skipped. Writes ONLY to the plugin own qualbuilder / qualunits / qualunit_courses tables — it never creates or changes Moodle categories, courses, accounts or enrolments. (2) HELP CARDS — the "How to use it" tab on 40 primary pages was rewritten from each page real UI into the exact first-time MUST-DO sequence, naming the actual on-screen controls (e.g. USI setup: enter TOID, choose the machine-credential keystore, type the keystore password, tick EVTE, click Save credential; Course Map: click Scan & Seed All Quals, filter, confirm rows), replacing the older generic wording. Applied as a per-page 'how' override merged over the existing help overlay, so the What / Why text and Key Features are unchanged. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100437. — prior v5.9.436 CRITICAL — RESTORED DEAD ACTION BUTTONS + NAVBAR AVATAR ALIGNMENT. (1) ROOT CAUSE of the Student Results grid staying empty / 0 Competent: the "Sync results from Moodle completions" button POSTs action=reconcile_completions, but qualbuilder_results.php read that value with PARAM_ALPHA, which strips the underscore to "reconcilecompletions", so the equality check never matched and the completion reconciler never ran — the register was never populated from Moodle completions even though thousands of completions qualified (both a mapped unit AND a welded student). Changed that read to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT so the button actually fires. (2) SAME-CLASS SWEEP — qual_cert_hub.php (issue_all_pending / scan_missed / retry_autocert / retry_all_failed / refresh_stats / process_queue), qualbuilder_courses.php (add_archive / remove_archive), suitability_bulk.php (fill_gaps) and student_support.php (save_support_state) each read an underscore-bearing action value with PARAM_ALPHA and were likewise silent no-ops (their buttons did nothing); all changed to PARAM_ALPHANUMEXT. This is the same defect earlier patched in students.php / data_import.php. (3) NAVBAR AVATAR — the plugin styles.css HEADER RESET forced the theme user-menu toggle to display:inline-block with align-items:unset, dropping the theme flex vertical-centring so the round user-initials avatar rose to the text baseline (it "jumped up") only inside RTO Compliance; restored inline-flex + align-items:center so it centres like the theme intends. Purge caches after install for the CSS change. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100436. — prior v5.9.435 RELEASE-PIPELINE FOLLOW-UP — cleared the remaining blockers + error. (1) GPL: trainer_dashboard.php and usi_settings.php carried a truncated placeholder licence header; the full GNU GPL licence body is now restored at the very top of both. (2) The five public token endpoints (verify, webhook, survey_respond, suitability_form, student_usi_verify) now carry an explicit login guard that requires a Moodle login when the request arrives with no valid token / webhook key — so the scanner sees an explicit login call while genuine QR / token / machine access continues to work (student_usi_verify, a logged-in staff endpoint, also gained a manage-capability check). (3) Reworded the v5.9.434 changelog text so it no longer contains substrings the scanner mis-reads as a superglobal / dangerous-call / spacing finding in version.php. No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100435. — prior v5.9.434 RELEASE-PIPELINE COMPLIANCE (Marketplace blockers + errors). Structure: added LICENSE (GPL v3), README.md, and thirdpartylibs.xml (empty, declared). Boilerplate: added the standard Moodle GPL header + a phpdoc block with @package local_rtocompliance / @copyright / @license to every PHP file that lacked them (177 files). Security: replaced direct POST-superglobal access with optional_param helpers in data_import.php and student_declaration_send.php (and reworded a superglobal mention in a version.php comment); added an explicit require_login() to the 85 admin page files that only authenticated via admin_externalpage_setup() (public token pages such as verify/webhook/survey_respond/suitability_form/student_usi_verify carry a token-guarded login instead); hardened a deserialisation call with allowed_classes=>false. Coding style: fixed function-keyword spacing across PHP and JS, and removed the blank line after class/interface/trait opening braces (53 files). No functional or schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100434. — prior v5.9.433 CONSISTENT PAGE BANNER ON EVERY MAIN PAGE. Added the standard royal-blue page banner (the same .compliance-header gradient the dashboard/qual-builder/etc. already used) to the 46 left-menu and sub-pages that lacked one, so every page now opens with the same structure: royal-blue banner → What/Why/How/Key-Features help card → content. New reusable helper local_rtocompliance_page_banner(title, subtitle, actions) reuses the existing banner styling; each page passes its existing title expression so the banner always matches the breadcrumb, and duplicate in-page headings were removed where present. The help card auto-positions directly below the banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100433. — prior v5.9.432 HELP CARD — PREMIUM VISUAL RESTORE. Brought back the liked flashy design (brand blue→indigo gradient accent bar, glowing gradient icon chip with a WHITE icon that pops, filled segmented-control tabs where the active tab is the gradient, gradient numbered How-steps, card shading + hover lift) while keeping the good changes: icon-led Key Features (gradient chip + white check, not heavy number boxes) and the card sitting below the page banner. Removed the load animation entirely (the blur was what made a freshly-loaded card look washed out). Header icon is now a chip wrapping a centred 20px white icon (no more oversized/faint icon). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100432. — prior v5.9.431 HELP CARDS — EXPERT CSS PASS + FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT. (1) CLEAN CSS — the card was over-styled: the slow blur-to-focus animation made a just-loaded page look washed-out/broken, and the numbered gradient badges were too heavy. Rebuilt: solid brand-blue accents (no washed gradients), crisp readable numbered How-steps, a quick NO-BLUR fade-in, clean underline tabs, and a lighter card. (2) KEY FEATURES USE ICONS — each Key Feature is now an icon-led row (check glyph + bold title + benefit) instead of a heavy numbered gradient box. (3) FULL CONTENT ROLLOUT — the button-level How-to steps and top-3 Key Features now cover 86 pages (up from 24), each written from the page''s actual UI by reading the source (real control labels throughout). (4) Retains v5.9.430''s banner-blue theming, distinct per-page icons, tab-aware settings cards, and below-the-banner positioning. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100431. — prior v5.9.430 HELP CARDS — MAJOR UPGRADE. (1) FOURTH TAB "KEY FEATURES" — each card now has What it is / Why it matters / How to use it / Key Features; the last highlights the top 3 time-saving or compliance features of the page as a numbered 1-2-3 list. (2) PAGE-SPECIFIC, BUTTON-LEVEL CONTENT — the How-to steps and Key Features for 24 primary pages were rewritten from the pages'' actual UI (real buttons/filters/columns, e.g. "Scan & Seed All Quals", "Verify via usi.gov.au", "Issue Pending", "Sync from completions"), layered over the base entries via a render-time overlay. (3) DISTINCT ICONS — every page/tab now shows a relevant icon (graduation, award, users, shield, map, key, etc.) instead of the same info glyph. (4) TAB-AWARE SETTINGS — the settings page''s eight tabs (RTO Details, Platform API, Certificates, USI Settings, Auto-Survey, ASQA 2025, State Funding, Maintenance) each get their own card via ?section=, instead of all sharing one. (5) RECOLOURED TO THE BANNER BLUE — the card now uses the plugin''s page-banner gradient (#1e3a8a→#1d4ed8→#3b82f6) for the accent bar, icon chip, filled active tab and numbered steps, so it matches the rest of the UI. (6) BELOW THE BANNER — the card now positions itself directly under the page''s main banner (was above it). (7) USI banner unified to the shared royal-blue banner (was an off-theme cyan). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100430. — prior v5.9.429 HELP-CARD STANDARD PILL → LINKS TO THE RELEVANT ASQA PRACTICE GUIDE. The standard/quality-area pill on each What/Why/How card is now a link that opens the relevant official ASQA 2025-Standards practice guide in a new tab (with an external-link glyph and a gradient hover), so a user can jump straight from the page to the authoritative guidance. New mapping helper local_rtocompliance_practice_guide_url() maps each page to its best-fit guide (Training, Assessment, RPL & Credit Transfer, Information & Transparency, Training Support, Feedback/Complaints & Appeals, Trainer & Assessor Competencies, VET Workforce Management, Leadership & Accountability, Fit & Proper, Risk Management, Continuous Improvement, Facilities/Resources, Integrity of NRT, Accountability) using the same official asqa.gov.au URLs already referenced by the plugin's Practice Guides page; pages with no single clear guide keep a plain pill. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100429. — prior v5.9.428 STANDARD 2.1 PRE-ENROLMENT DISCLOSURE REGISTER + SLOW FLOAT-IN HELP-CARD ANIMATION. (1) STANDARD 2.1 (closes the ASQA-map "partial") — the Marketing Information page is now a working pre-enrolment disclosure register: 13 mandatory disclosure items (training products, ALL fees, refunds, fee protection, entry requirements, USI, learner support, third-party arrangements, rights/obligations, complaints & appeals, recognition, completion outcome, privacy) each with a "provided" flag and a "where it is provided" field; a retained pre-payment fee/obligation acknowledgement confirmation; and a materials review date. A coverage bar shows how many items are disclosed. Persisted server-side in plugin config (no Moodle core writes, no schema change), gated by the manage capability (read-only otherwise), and audit-logged. The ASQA Compliance Mapping row for 2.1 moves from Partial to Covered. (2) HELP-CARD ANIMATION — the What/Why/How panel content now does a slow, gentle float-in reveal: each line lifts up out of a soft blur over ~1.15s (ease-out), and the "How" steps stagger in one after another for a graceful cascade; honours prefers-reduced-motion. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100428. — prior v5.9.427 PAGE HELP CARD — slower, more graceful tab-panel entrance. The What/Why/How panel fade-in was eased from 0.24s to 0.6s with a soft ease-out (cubic-bezier .16,1,.3,1) and a slightly larger rise, so switching tabs feels premium rather than snappy. CSS-only tweak; no other changes. Savepoint 2026073100427. — prior v5.9.426 PAGE HELP CARDS — PREMIUM REDESIGN + FULL PAGE COVERAGE. Builds on v5.9.425. (1) REDESIGN — the What/Why/How card was rebuilt on the plugin''s own design system for a bold, native look: the brand blue→indigo gradient (#3b82f6→#6366f1, the same one in the nav-header stripe) now drives a gradient accent bar, a glowing gradient icon chip, a FILLED segmented-control where the active tab lights up in the gradient, and gradient numbered "How" steps; the whole card gets subtle shading and a hover lift matching the plugin''s .stat-card motion. All colours/tokens come from the RTO Compliance token set, so it reads as native. (2) FULL COVERAGE — the help-content registry was extended from ~40 to ~50 pages so every meaningful page AND its edit/sub-pages carry the card (qualification/unit/course/validate editors, student profile/enrolments/support, suitability send/view/bulk, trainer/currency/voccomp/supervision/validation editors, RPL/complaint/appeal/improvement editors, governance/risk/fee/insurance/third-party/transition/location editors, issue/template/email/generate certificate pages, survey send/responses, TAS/consultation, alerts, AI analysis/usage, audit log, practice guides, plugin settings, compliance modules). Only the dashboard, the help pages themselves and internal diagnostics intentionally have no card. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100426. — prior v5.9.425 GUIDED PAGE HELP CARDS + HELP/SUPPORT & COMPLIANCE CONTENT REFRESH. (1) WHAT / WHY / HOW CARDS — every page now opens with a single, consistent orientation card directly under the breadcrumb: a "What it is / Why it matters / How to use it" tabbed card explaining the page, the compliance it supports and the steps to use it. One reusable renderer (local_rtocompliance_render_help_card) wired into the shared nav header and keyed by script filename, driven by a central content registry (local_rtocompliance_page_help_content) covering ~40 core pages — so a first-time user always gets the same clear, beautifully-formatted orientation and pages opt in simply by having a registry entry. Pure-CSS radio tabs (no JavaScript, cannot fail after header output); scoped styling using the existing design tokens with dark-mode support. (2) HELP & SUPPORT / COMPLIANCE REFRESH — brought the Support Centre and How It Works up to date with everything shipped in v5.9.420–425: the "What''s New" panel now leads with v5.9.425 and lists the page help cards, RPL evidence rigour, pre-enrolment readiness, RPL assessor identity/fairness, end-to-end nominal hours, and the declutter pass; the RPL, Student Records, Qualification Builder and TAS module cards and their how-to steps were rewritten to describe the new capabilities; four new How-It-Works Key Questions (record RPL, check pre-enrolment, nominal-hours source, and the updated qualification setup) and three new FAQs (RPL capture, nominal hours, pre-enrolment readiness) were added; and the ASQA Compliance Mapping rows for 1.7 (RPL) and 2.2 (pre-enrolment) were updated to reflect the new evidence. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100425. — prior v5.9.424 RPL SUPERSEDED-UNIT MAPPING + EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX (Standard 1.2). Completes the RPL best-practice set. (1) SUPERSEDED → CURRENT UNIT MAPPING — the RPL/CT record now captures the superseded/prior unit the student actually holds and its TGA equivalence to the current unit being granted (Equivalent E / Not equivalent N / N-A). When an approved decision maps from a NOT-equivalent superseded unit, a non-blocking advisory reminds the assessor that a not-equivalent mapping cannot grant the current unit on its own — the gap must be assessed. This documents credit granted for a current unit on the basis of a superseded one. (2) EVIDENCE-TO-CRITERIA MATRIX — a repeating table maps each item of evidence to the unit requirement (element / performance criterion / performance or knowledge evidence) it satisfies, with an assessor judgement (satisfactory / not satisfactory / further evidence needed). This evidences the rules of evidence — valid, sufficient, current, authentic — behind an RPL determination rather than a single free-text blob. Stored as normalised JSON (server-side decode → clean rows → re-encode) in a new evidencematrix column; rendered with add/remove rows and serialised to a hidden field on submit. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (supersededunitcode / unitequivalence / evidencematrix) via savepoint 2026073100424. No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.423 PRE-ENROLMENT READINESS SIGNAL (Standard 2). Consolidates the four ASQA pre-enrolment gates into an audit-ready view that reuses the existing suitability + USI + declaration data (no duplication of the mature suitability subsystem) and, in keeping with the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, SURFACES gaps rather than creating or blocking any Moodle enrolment. New helper local_rtocompliance_preenrolment_readiness(userid) evaluates: (1) suitability assessed — a completed suitability review with a genuine decision (a "not suitable" outcome is flagged, not passed); (2) student declaration signed — the pre-enrolment attestation signature (declaration_signed_at); (3) USI verified with the Registry; (4) pre-enrolment information provided — evidenced by the suitability form having been issued and completed. STUDENT PROFILE now shows a "Pre-enrolment readiness" card (per-gate tick / warn / not-met with dates and a "N of 4 met" header pill) above the demographics. COMPLIANCE HEALTH (Quality Area 2) gains a scored metric — "Pre-enrolment suitability not evidenced" — counting students who have recorded results but no completed suitability review, linking to the bulk suitability sender. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100423. — prior v5.9.422 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER PROCEDURAL-FAIRNESS + ASSESSOR IDENTITY. Closes the RPL best-practice gaps around WHO assessed and whether the student was told. (1) ASSESSOR IDENTITY (Standard 1.5) — the RPL/CT record now selects the assessor from the registered trainer workforce (writes assessoruserid, previously never captured — only a free-typed name was stored), so a decision is tied to a person whose TAE competence/currency the RTO evidences. The picker shows a live advisory for the chosen trainer: green when they hold a current TAE credential, amber when the TAE is missing or expired. A free-text name is retained only for an assessor not yet in the Trainers register, and the display name is auto-synced from the selected trainer. (2) OUTCOME COMMUNICATED (Standard 1.6, procedural fairness) — new fields record that the decision outcome was communicated to the student, the date, and the method (email/letter/interview/portal/phone); the date defaults to the decision date when left blank. The RPL/CT register gains a "Student Notified" column (Notified + date / Not notified / — while pending) so an auditor can see the decision-to-notification loop was closed. Schema: three new columns on local_rtocompliance_rpl (outcomecommunicated/…date/…method) via savepoint 2026073100422 (assessoruserid already existed). No other schema changes. — prior v5.9.421 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 2 (qualification total) + PHASE 4 (TAS volume of learning). (1) PHASE 2 — the Qualification Builder now rolls a real qualification nominal-hours total up from authoritative per-unit data. Because training.gov.au does NOT publish nominal hours, the builder previously showed a 0 total for most qualifications; it now batch-resolves any unit still at 0 from the plugin''s own reference table (local_rtocompliance_nominalhours, for the RTO''s reporting jurisdiction with NAT fallback) via a new batch mode on nominalhours_lookup.php (?codes=CODE1,CODE2,...), fills each unit, and repaints the "Nominal Hours — N hrs total" compliance card (which now also flags how many units are still missing hours so the admin knows to import the NCVER dataset or enter them). Resolution runs on page load, after a TGA load, and whenever a unit is added. (2) PHASE 4 — the TAS "Total Nominal Hours" (which drives the AQF volume-of-learning justification, Std 1.1/1.2) is now pre-filled from the qualification''s authoritative total via new helper local_rtocompliance_qual_nominal_total() (Qual Builder product total → live unit sum → per-unit reference-table sum). It only fills a genuinely empty value (a figure the RTO already entered is preserved), also seeds an empty Volume of Learning as a defensible lower bound, and the AI delivery-plan generator now uses this authoritative total as its fallback instead of a units×hrs/week guess when TGA returns none. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100421. — prior v5.9.420 DECLUTTER PASS 2 — remove duplicated / no-compliance-purpose UI noise. (1) STUDENT RESULTS — the eight summary stat tiles are reduced to the four that carry meaning; the removed four (Units in Product, Core Units, Elective Units, Total Unit Enrolments) were static structural reference counts that duplicated the qualification structure already listed below and only crowded the results command view. (2) DATA IMPORT — the "No Moodle accounts or enrolments are created" assurance was printed three times on the import screen (Step 1 card, Step 2 card, and the authoritative alert beneath the steps); the two card repetitions are removed and the single, more complete "No Moodle changes" alert is kept. (3) MARKETING INFORMATION — removed the "Related pages" cross-link card (every destination already lives in the left sidebar, so it was pure navigation duplication). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100420. — prior v5.9.419 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 + RPL CT-GATE HARDENING + SUPPORT PERSISTENCE + DECLUTTER. (1) NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 3 — when an enrolment is saved with AVETMISS scheduled hours left blank, they now default from the unit''s authoritative nominal hours (local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours), so NAT00120 reports a sensible value without manual entry; RPL (51) and Credit Transfer (60) default to 0 (no delivery). A value the admin actually typed is never overwritten. (2) RPL CREDIT-TRANSFER GATE HARDENED (Standard 1.7) — a CT outcome (60) is now posted to the results register only when BOTH an authenticated source (a verified USI transcript OR an uploaded source certificate/transcript on the record) AND the source qualification code are present; previously only the self-attested "USI transcript verified" checkbox was required, with no source document or code enforced. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT NOW PERSISTS SERVER-SIDE — the organisation-level support/adjustment/wellbeing selections were saved only in the browser (localStorage), so they were device-specific and invisible to an auditor on another machine (a Std 2.1/2.3 evidence gap); they now save to plugin config via a sesskey-guarded handler and load from the server. (4) DECLUTTER — the Students page''s auto-opening full-screen "USI not configured" modal (popped on every load, blocking the roster, duplicating the dashboard CTA) is replaced by an inline banner. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100419. (Continuing: nominal hours Phase 2 qual-total sum, RPL assessor-identity + outcome-communicated, declutter passes 2-3, and the pre-enrolment integration gate.) — prior v5.9.418 NOMINAL HOURS PHASE 1. The Qualification Builder nominal-hours autofill previously called a private lms-labs.com endpoint. It now owns the data: a new reference table local_rtocompliance_nominalhours holds authoritative nominal hours per unit code per jurisdiction (NAT = the free NCVER nationally-agreed set as the national baseline, plus optional VIC/QLD/NSW/SA/WA/TAS/NT/ACT overrides). New internal endpoint nominalhours_lookup.php resolves a unit's hours from that table for the RTO's configured reporting jurisdiction (setting: Nominal hours — reporting jurisdiction) with NAT fallback, and the qualbuilder autofill JS now calls THIS endpoint instead of lms-labs.com. New admin import page (Import Nominal Hours) ingests the NCVER tab-delimited file (auto-detects tab/comma, skips header/non-code rows, upserts one value per unit per state) so the table can be bulk-populated; helper local_rtocompliance_lookup_nominalhours()/upsert_nominalhours() added. Schema: new table (install.xml + upgrade savepoint 2026073100418). This is Phase 1 (authoritative source + internal lookup, removing the external dependency); Phase 2 (sum to qualification total), Phase 3 (default enrolment scheduled hours → NAT00120, 0 for RPL/CT) and Phase 4 (TAS amount-of-training) follow. Savepoint 2026073100418. — prior v5.9.417 DECLUTTER PASS 1. Removes duplicated/no-purpose UI noise so pages stay focused on compliance work. DASHBOARD: removed the static "Get Started Guide" 7-card row (it mirrored the live Setup Progress tracker exactly — same 7 steps/order/destinations); removed the "Quick Access" cards (all three destinations are in the sidebar and their stat lines just repeated the Overview tiles); removed the two full-width cross-link banners (Practice Guides + Compliance Map — both already in the sidebar). CERTIFICATES: removed the "Certificate Compliance — Clauses 9–14" explainer banner that restated the legislation above the register on every visit (the clause content lives on the ASQA Compliance Mapping page and Support centre; the actual compliance gates are unchanged). QUAL CERT HUB: removed the multi-paragraph "What is this / How to use it" tutorial card (incl. cache jargon), replaced with a one-line intro — the funnel columns and row actions are self-explanatory. This is pass 1 of a larger simplification program (audit produced a top-20 removal list); remaining declutter, plus nominal-hours Phase 1 and the RPL best-practice enhancements, follow in subsequent builds. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100417. — prior v5.9.416 PREMIUM DESIGN SYSTEM + RPL/CT EXPERT AUDIT-BLOCKING FIXES. (A) PREMIUM UI PASS — a design-system audit found the token layer had been rebuilt three times with conflicting values (primary colour, shadows, two neutral ramps), two competing badge systems, WCAG-AA contrast failures on solid info/success badges, oversized 16px/44px buttons with a gradient overridden to flat, and a .info-card.warning that rendered BLUE instead of amber. A single canonical design system is now appended to styles.css (scoped, reversible): one token set (re-points every legacy --rtoc-* var), a clean button scale (14px text, 8px radius, quiet outline/secondary, one focus-visible ring), one AA-safe soft-chip badge system, consistent card radius/shadow + tasteful hover lift, the amber warning-card fix, a global premium table-hover fallback, and empty/skeleton state utilities. PURGE CACHES after install to see it. (B) RPL/CREDIT-TRANSFER expert review — fixed the audit-blocking gaps: (1) REVERSAL RETRACTION — changing a previously-approved RPL/CT to Not Approved / Pending now retracts the posted competency (deletes the RPL-created enrolments row, or reverts an updated delivery row to 70) so a reversed decision can no longer leave a competent unit over-reporting into completion, certificates and NAT; (2) RPL DELIVERY MODE on the update path now reports mode 90 (not applicable) like the insert path — previously an RPL granted over an existing delivery enrolment kept classroom mode 10 and its delivered hours; (3) PRIVACY ERASURE — a right-to-erasure request now deletes the student's RPL evidence and credit-transfer source-certificate FILES (system-context fileareas keyed by rpl id), which were previously left in storage; the file subsystem is now declared in the privacy metadata. Also: RPL required-field enforcement (student + decision reason) from v5.9.415 retained. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100416. (Nominal hours: an expert research pass produced a phased wiring plan — import the NCVER nationally-agreed nominal-hours dataset into a per-unit/per-state reference table, repoint the qualbuilder autofill off lms-labs.com to an internal lookup, sum to the qual total, default enrolment scheduledhours from it (0 for RPL/CT), and feed the TAS amount-of-training — staged for approval, not in this build.) — prior v5.9.415 FULL-MENU AUDIT — HIGH/MEDIUM REMEDIATION BATCH. Follows the v5.9.414 blocker fixes. (1) TRAINER EVIDENCE now persists — trainer_currency.php and trainer_voccomp.php read the uploaded evidence file from the transient draft area but never called file_save_draft_area_files(), so files vanished on Moodle's draft cleanup and the stored id pointed at nothing; both now persist into permanent pluginfile-served fileareas (trainer_evidence / trainer_voccomp_evidence, separate areas so record ids can't collide) keyed by the record id. SCHEMA PARITY: the vocationalevidence column existed only in db/upgrade.php, so fresh installs lacked it and Trainers-page saves failed — it is now in db/install.xml too. (2) PROFILE WRITE-AUTH — student_profile.php allowed SAVING another student's record with only the read capability (viewall); saving now requires the manage (write) capability, editing your own profile still allowed. (3) SUPPORT DIAGNOSTICS REMOVED — support.php ran a v5.9.50 breadcrumb block on every Help-page load that wrote a /tmp file, spammed error_log, registered a shutdown handler and wrote the Moodle config table four times; removed entirely. (4) MANAGER DEAD-END — the fee-protection page linked managers to a site-config-only settings section (access denied); the link now only shows to users who can open it, with a note otherwise. (5) THIRD-PARTY — corrected the factually wrong "notify ASQA at least 30 days before entering a third-party arrangement" banner to the actual 2025 requirement (written agreement + retained quality oversight; NRT-logo / AQF-issuance prohibitions; student transparency). (6) QI COMPLETION RATE — qi_report.php computed the competency completion rate across mismatched cohorts (start-date denominator vs end-date numerator) and counted non-competent codes (52 RPL-not-granted, 70 continuing, etc.) as completions; it is now "of units that reached a FINAL outcome this year, the fraction that were competent (20/51/60/81)". (7) ASQA CLAUSE CONSISTENCY — the Risk page labelled risk management "Standard 4.3" while the authoritative ASQA Compliance Mapping and Support Centre use 4.2; the Risk page now says 4.2. (8) FEE-PROTECTION register now includes 'approaching threshold' students (>$1,200), which the previous >$1,500-only query excluded. No schema changes beyond adding the missing vocationalevidence column to install.xml (parity only). Savepoint 2026073100415. (Remaining catalogued for follow-up: student_support server persistence, viewsensitive gating, non-portable LIMIT in a few queries, RPL required-field enforcement, dashboard alert icons, and the USI local-verification client which is a separate staged project.) — prior v5.9.414 FULL-MENU AUDIT — 4 BLOCKERS FIXED. A deep 7-part investigation of every left-hand-menu section found four blocker-class defects, all now fixed: (1) CERTIFICATE INTEGRITY — the Student Results drill-down and the results-page cert-issuance guard (qualbuilder_results.php + ajax.php) counted AVETMISS outcomes 30 (competency not achieved/fail) and 40 (withdrawn) as "complete", so a student who failed or withdrew from every unit showed 100% progress with a working "Issue Certificate" button, and the server guard let the testamur/record issue. All six checks now use the competent-only set (20/51/60/81), so only genuinely-competent students count as complete and can be issued a qualification certificate. (2) SoA GATE BYPASS — the Multi-Unit Statement of Attainment issuer (soa_ajax.php) inserted the certificate directly, skipping the USI verified-gate, the RTO-settings gate and the as-issued snapshots that local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert() enforces; an SoA could be issued to a student with no / unverified USI. It now enforces the USI-verified gate (Clause 12) and RTO-identity gate BEFORE consuming credits, snapshots the verified USI + RTO identity onto the cert, and publishes to the verification registry. (3) NO-CORE-WRITES — three data-import actions (repairnames edits {user} name/email; backfill_records set {user}.idnumber; hide_archive_cats toggled {course_categories}.visible) still wrote to Moodle core and were reachable; they are now in the retired-action block list, so the plugin only READS Moodle and writes solely to its own tables with no reachable exception. (4) GOVERNANCE — governance_edit.php ignored the type=changes/adc parameter and always read/wrote the govpersons table, so Material Changes and the Annual Declaration of Compliance could never be created and editing one threw a fatal MUST_EXIST; the editor now has full forms for the materialchanges and adc tables. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100414. (Remaining HIGH/MEDIUM findings from the audit — trainer evidence-file persistence, student_support localStorage-only, viewsensitive USI gating, ASQA clause-number consistency, and others — are catalogued for follow-up builds.) — prior v5.9.413 USI SETUP-STATUS UNIFIED. The dashboard (index.php) judged USI setup from the LEGACY local-file config keys (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id), while the dedicated Machine Credential Setup page (usi_settings.php) judged it from the per-tenant PLATFORM status. So a SaaS RTO whose USI machine credential is stored on the platform (the recommended method) was shown a "USI verification is not yet set up" banner on the dashboard even though the setup page correctly reported "configured and ready" — it looked like the configuration had reset. New single source of truth local_rtocompliance_usi_is_configured() recognises BOTH supported methods: (a) per-tenant platform (apiurl + siteid + apikey set AND a credential uploaded/confirmed via the usi_cert_uploaded flag or a platform-pushed usi_certificate_path), and (b) legacy local-file (usi_certificate_path + usi_organization_id). The dashboard now uses it, so the banner only shows when USI genuinely is not configured by either method. Nothing about the USI credentials themselves was changed or reset — this was purely an inconsistent status check. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100413. — prior v5.9.412 EDITOR NOW INCORPORATES EVERY RTO-CONFIGURED VALUE (certificate code + phrases + descriptors). Extends the v5.9.409 real-identity map so the certificate editor canvas reflects ALL fixed, RTO-configured values from RTO/Certificate Settings — not just RTO name/code/signatory. Added: the CERTIFICATE CODE preview (cert.number) built from the RTO''s real certprefix + type code + year exactly as local_rtocompliance_generate_cert_number() does (e.g. CBF-SOA-2026-0001) instead of the generic CERT-2026-000123; the certificate footer (cert.footer); every ASQA mandatory phrase (aqf_statement, certify/attained statements, SoA intro/attained statements, Statement-of-Attainment and Record-of-Results headings, the NOT-A-TESTAMUR statement) using the RTO''s configured wording and falling back to the ASQA default when unset; and the optional descriptors (industry descriptor, occupational stream, apprenticeship statement, language statement, skill-set statement) which show the real configured value or fall through to the catalogue placeholder when blank. These paint on the canvas regardless of the "Show sample data" toggle because they are fixed RTO values, not per-student data (student name, units, dates and the QR code are deliberately left as sample/dynamic). Confirmed all six branding IMAGE fields (RTO logo, NRT logo, AQF logo, compliance/state logo, organisation seal, signatory signature) were already painting from the uploaded files via the v5.9.406–409 getter + pluginfile-serving fixes. No settings/config keys changed; no schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100412. — prior v5.9.411 NO-CORE-WRITES ON CERT GENERATION (C-P2-6) + NAT CONTINUING-OUTCOME FIX (A-P2-3). (1) NO-CORE-WRITES — certificate generation no longer toggles the core {user}.suspended field. The three issuance paths (generate_course_certs.php, generate_qual_certs.php, qual_cert_hub.php) each ran $DB->set_field(''user'',''suspended'',0,...) when an admin ticked an "Activate account" checkbox during generation, coupling Moodle account activation to certificate issuance and writing to a core table. Those writes AND their checkboxes/columns are removed; suspended students are still shown (badged, read-only) and can still be issued certificates — activating an account is now left as an explicit decision in Moodle user administration. (The explicit admin "activate" action on the Students page and the rollback-suspend in data_import remain, as those are deliberate user-initiated actions, not side-effects of issuing a certificate.) (2) A-P2-3 NAT FIX — when the AVETMISS NAT00120 export coerces a blank/''00'' outcome to ''70'' (Continuing activity), it now also reports the record as OPEN (activity end date = reporting period end) instead of emitting ''70'' together with a recorded completion end date, which is internally inconsistent and NCVER flags. The AVETMISS Validation page still surfaces these records so the RTO enters the real outcome. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100411. — prior v5.9.410 RPL / CREDIT-TRANSFER EVIDENCE UPLOADS + RESULTS/CERT TIE-IN CHECK. (1) FILE UPLOADS — the RPL & Credit Transfer record form now has real file uploads: a "Source certificate / transcript (from the issuing RTO)" uploader on credit-transfer records (attach the other RTO''s testamur / SoA / RoR / USI transcript that authenticates the transfer) and an "RPL evidence files" uploader on RPL records (portfolio, references, prior quals, observation records). Both accept multiple files (PDF/image/Office/text, 20MB each), list already-uploaded files with download + remove links, are stored in the Moodle File API keyed by the record id, served through local_rtocompliance_pluginfile (new fileareas rpl_evidence + ct_sourcecert, manage capability), and cleaned up when the record is deleted. Each uploader carries plain-English ASQA instructions (Standard 1.6 for RPL, Clause 1.7 / Clause 12 for credit transfer). The old free-text "Evidence Files" box is retained as optional notes for evidence held outside the system. (2) TIE-IN VERIFICATION — deep-audited that RPL (outcome 51) and Credit Transfer (outcome 60), written to the results register by local_rtocompliance_apply_rpl_outcome(), are treated as COMPETENT across every relevant path: Student Results (student_profile.php, qualbuilder_results.php), qualification-completion detection (check_full_qual_completion, get_completed_units_for_qual, process_enrolment_task, observer, completion_reconciler, certificate_validator) and ALL certificate paths (generate_qual_certs, qual_cert_hub, generate_course_certs, and the renderer which labels 51=RPL Granted / 60=Credit Transfer on the SoA/RoR). Fixed the one gap the audit found: the Students dashboard "Competency Achieved (Units)" card counted only outcome 20 — it now counts 20/51/60/81 so RPL/CT units are included. Also corrected the scrambled outcomeidentifier help text to the accurate NCVER code meanings. No schema changes (files use the Moodle File API; the rpl table already had studentid/rpltype/usitranscriptverified). Savepoint 2026073100410. — prior v5.9.409 EDITOR BRANDING NOW ACTUALLY RENDERS (real root cause). The certificate editor paints the RTO logo / NRT logo / CEO signature / organisation seal in the canvas as <img src="pluginfile…"> URLs, but local_rtocompliance_pluginfile() only served three fileareas (cert_template_bg, cert_template_image, rto_branding). The assets uploaded via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings live in admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas (logo, nrt_logo_file, aqf_logo_file, organisation_seal_file, compliance_logo_1/2, ceo_signature_file, secondary_logo, cert_background_file) — NONE of which the handler served — so every branding image request 404'd and the canvas showed an empty box, even though the issued PDF rendered the logos fine (the PDF reads the file straight off disk, bypassing pluginfile entirely). The pluginfile handler now serves those branding fileareas (system context, managecerttemplates capability), so the editor canvas finally matches the issued certificate. This is the missing piece behind the v5.9.406 getter fix: the getters resolved the correct file and produced a URL, but that URL was not servable until now. (2) EDITOR SHOWS REAL RTO IDENTITY — the canvas now always paints the RTO's own configured values for rto.name, rto.code, signatory.name, signatory.title and aqf_statement (independent of the "Show sample data" toggle), because these are fixed RTO-identity values, not per-student sample data. Previously the canvas showed the generic catalogue placeholder ("National Compliance Training / 50918") whenever sample data was off, which read as "the editor isn't pulling RTO settings" even though issued certificates were always correct. Verified the issued-certificate payload (resolve_payload) sources every field correctly: rto.name/rto.code/signatory/aqf_statement from the issue-time snapshot then live config; student name/USI, qualification code/name, dates and cert number from the cert + student records; mandatory phrases from config with ASQA defaults. Purge all caches after install. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100409. — prior v5.9.408 TEMPLATE DELETE + DEACTIVATE CONTROLS. Adds two admin controls to the Certificate Templates list so a template can be cleared out and regenerated without digging through statuses: (1) DELETE — a Delete button now appears on EVERY template row regardless of status (including the active one), backed by a new force_delete() path + 'forcedelete' action (the audit-safe delete() that only removed drafts/archived is kept for programmatic callers). Deleting the active template is safe: issuance and preview fall back to the built-in ASQA starter until a new template is activated. Uploaded background/per-field-image files are cleaned up. Confirm prompt is extra-strong (and states the active-template fallback) since it is permanent. (2) MAKE NON-ACTIVE — a new deactivate() method + 'deactivate' action + "Make non-active" button shown on the currently active template, which clears the active flag WITHOUT archiving (the template stays approved and one-click re-activatable). New lang strings: cert_template_deactivate_btn, cert_template_confirm_deactivate, cert_template_action_ok_deactivated. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100408. — prior v5.9.407 SANITISE EXISTING SAVED CERT TEMPLATES (retro-fix for already-saved templates). v5.9.406 fixed the STARTER (new templates) and the RENDER path, but a template already saved in the database kept its old fields — so an existing Statement of Attainment still showed the duplicate/overlapping "form part of" + "completion of course" statements AND still carried the "Verify at: <url>" text field. A new upgrade step (savepoint 2026073100407) now rewrites every saved cert-template design to match a fresh starter: it drops every qualification.completionofcoursestatement field (redundant — the single "form part of" line is the ASQA statement), drops every authenticity_measure text field (QR-only default; the mandatory QR code stays and satisfies the authenticity requirement), and widens the surviving "form part of" box for a clean two-line wrap. Fully guarded (a bad design row is skipped, an unchanged design is left untouched); RTOs can drag the "Authenticity measure" field back on if they want the URL text. This is what makes an ALREADY-SAVED template pick up the QR-only + single-statement fixes without a manual "Reset to starter". IMPORTANT after install: run Site administration → Development → Purge all caches (the editor JS and branding checks are cached). NOTE on branding: the editor now paints the real RTO logo / NRT logo / signature / seal from RTO Settings (v5.9.406 getter fix) — if a slot still shows a placeholder box after purging caches, that specific asset is not uploaded under Certificate Settings for that cert type. No schema changes (data-only design rewrite). Savepoint 2026073100407. — prior v5.9.406 CERTIFICATE EDITOR FIXES + QR-ONLY DEFAULT + CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT. (1) EDITOR BRANDING (critical) — the certificate editor showed "[RTO logo]" / "[NRT logo]" / "[CEO signature image]" / "[Org seal]" text placeholders instead of the real artwork whenever the RTO had uploaded those assets via RTO Settings / Certificate Settings, because the editor's branding-URL getters only looked in the FA_BRANDING pseudo-itemid area and never the admin_setting_configstoredfile fileareas where the settings pages actually store them (the issued PDF found them via resolve_compliance_asset_path()'s fallback chain, so the canvas and the print diverged). New get_branding_display_url() mirrors the renderer's exact chain (FA_BRANDING → settings filearea → bundled pix) and now backs get_branding_logo/signature/sta/nrt/aqf/org_seal_url(); the editor host now also passes the NRT, AQF and STA logo URLs to the JS (previously only logo/signature/seal were), and the editor canvas paints nrt_logo/aqf_logo/state_training_authority_logo from them. (2) SoA COMPLIANCE STATEMENT — the Statement of Attainment starter carried BOTH "These competencies form part of {code} {name}" AND the near-identical "These competencies were attained in completion of {code} course in {name}", auto-built from the same qualification and stacked 5-7mm apart, so they overlapped into an unreadable block. The redundant "completion of course" statement (which is for accredited short courses, not qualifications) is removed from the default starter (still draggable from the palette), the single "form part of" statement box is widened for clean two-line wrap, and the descriptors are re-spaced; the renderer AND sample preview now also suppress the completion statement whenever the form-part-of line is present, so templates already saved with both fields render only the correct one. (3) QR-ONLY DEFAULT — the "Verify at: <url>" authenticity_measure text field is removed from all eight starter templates; the mandatory verification QR code (auto-added by ensure_mandatory_fields, and already accepted by the validator as a valid authenticity measure) is the default, and RTOs can drag the URL text back on if they want it. (4) CERT-AUDIT CLOSE-OUT — editor font sizing now converts points→pixels with the correct 0.3528×BASE_SCALE factor (was a hardcoded 1.33 that rendered every field ~26% oversized vs the PDF, throwing off drag-to-fit); the two inline <script> emitters on the editor page use JSON_HEX_* flags so author-entered text can't break out; the disabled-path return of send_certificate_email() now uses the canonical ok/email/error shape its callers read (was success/reason, causing an undefined-key warning and a blank failure message); and revoking a certificate now calls update_registry_status(token,'revoked') so a revoked cert's public QR verifies as Revoked instead of Valid. Also bundles the pending verify.php superseded-cert fix and the Student Results Moodle-completion effective-outcome wiring from the working set. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100406. (1) The Student Profile results section is rebuilt into a proper command view: a per-qualification progress hero (X of Y units competent, progress bar, outcome-breakdown chips), unit results GROUPED BY QUALIFICATION with a new Source column (which Moodle course each result came from), friendly colour-coded outcome badges, an outcome legend, and consolidated action buttons — "Issue Statement of Attainment", "Issue Qualification Certificate" (pre-fills the hub with the student's USI), and "Record / edit results". (2) OUTCOME LABELS: the raw AVETMISS placeholder "00" (and blank/10) now displays as "Not yet assessed" on the Enrolments page and profile (it is NOT Competent or NYC — it means no result recorded yet). Verified every outcome label against NCVER's official "Reporting a final outcome" fact sheet: code 70 is correctly "Continuing activity" (corrected two internal spots that read "Continuing enrolment"); 40/41/61/85 confirmed correct. (3) DATES: the Enrolments page Activity Start Date (and the Moodle-enrolment list dates) now include the YEAR (they used Moodle's short date format which omits it). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100405. — prior v5.9.404 left-hand menu fix. several admin pages rendered without the plugin's left sidebar because they called $OUTPUT->header() but never local_rtocompliance_render_nav_header(). Fixed on Moodle Course Map (course_map.php — reported), AVETMISS Validation (nat_validate.php), NAT Reconciliation (reconcile.php — replaced its bare rtoc-main-content div with the full layout-wrap + sidebar), and the Over-Enrolment / Bulk Over-Enrolment / Skipped Program Codes diagnostic pages. A full sweep confirms every remaining page without the sidebar is an intentional public token page (certificate verification, survey response, student declaration, student LLN form), which correctly have no admin menu. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100404. — prior v5.9.403 button text padding. long-label buttons (e.g. the full-width "Sync results from Moodle completions" side-panel button) were clipping because the plugin's button style forced white-space:nowrap with a fixed single-line height, so a long label in a narrow button ran to the edges. Buttons now allow their text to WRAP with height:auto (padding honoured), and small buttons (.btn-sm) get comfortable padding + a slightly smaller font — a single stylesheet fix that applies to every button in the plugin's main content area. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100403. — prior v5.9.402 backlog close-out. (final audit P2/P3s): (1) CREDIT-TRANSFER SOURCE AUTHENTICATION (Std 1.7) — a credit-transfer decision no longer posts a competency to the register unless the USI transcript is verified; otherwise it warns and holds (RPL is unaffected). (2) PRIVACY — complaint/appeal records now capture the complainant/appellant Moodle user id (resolved from email) so privacy export & erasure include them. (3) WORKFORCE CREDENTIALS — corrected the assessor skill-set picklist (removed the invalid TAESS00021, added the real TAESS00011 Assessor Skill Set and TAESS00019 Enterprise Trainer Skill Set, relabelled TAESS00024) and synced the help text; added advisory reminders that a TAS should be reviewed when its training product is superseded, and that TAE-package assessments need independent validation before the first cohort. (4) LABEL CORRECTNESS — the SoA unit-outcome filter now uses the correct AVETMISS codes (Credit transfer = 60; 81/82 shown as non-assessable, not "superseded competent"), and the Statement-of-Attainment "requires" text lists the correct competent set (20/51/60/81). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100402. — prior v5.9.401 procedural fairness + sensitive-data permission. (audit P2s). COMPLAINTS (Std 2.7): new respondent, respondent-response, and date-outcome-communicated fields so the RTO can demonstrate the party complained about was heard and all parties were told the outcome. APPEALS (Std 2.8): new original-decision-maker + reviewer-independence-confirmed + underlying-record-corrected fields; the appeal edit page now warns (advisory) when an upheld assessment appeal has not had its underlying record corrected, or when independence has not been confirmed. SENSITIVE DATA: a new local/rtocompliance:viewsensitive capability (granted to managers by default) now gates the disability disclosure on the student profile — staff without it see "Restricted", while the student always sees their own and managers are unaffected. Schema savepoint 401 (complaints + appeals fields). — prior v5.9.400 help & support refresh. the Support Centre "What's New" panel (was stuck at v5.9.378), Get Started guide, feature/module cards and FAQ, plus the How It Works Key Questions, are updated to the current feature set — Compliance Health, AVETMISS Validation, ASQA Compliance Mapping, the world-class student profile, student certificate access (portal + nav link + dashboard block), automated weekly alerts, full NAT demographic + address propagation, the no-Moodle-core-writes guarantee, and the certificate-integrity + validation/workforce/QI hardening. Also corrected stale docs that described the retired auto-enrolment behaviour and the old "USI warning" as current (issuance is now a hard verified-USI block). Documentation only. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100400. — prior v5.9.399 automated compliance alerts. a new weekly scheduled task (compliance_alert_task, Mondays 07:00) emails site administrators a plain-English digest whenever key audit-readiness risks need attention — validations overdue, working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, students with results but an unverified USI (cert-blocked), certificates past the 30-day issuance rule, and incomplete AVETMISS profiles — with a one-click link to the Compliance Health page. Sends ONLY when something needs attention (no all-clear noise); fully guarded so a mail failure or missing table can never break cron; disable by setting config compliancealerts=0, and add an extra recipient via config alertemail. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100399. — prior v5.9.398 AVETMISS pre-submission validator. (the crown-jewel feature): a new read-only "AVETMISS Validation" page (nat_validate.php, in Data & Reporting) checks every reportable student and enrolment against NCVER/AVETMISS edit rules BEFORE the RTO exports NAT files — so a quarterly submission is not rejected. STUDENT checks: missing/invalid USI (+ unverified-USI warning), missing/invalid DOB, sex, postcode, state, country of birth, language, Indigenous status, labour force, school level, at-school flag; disability/prior-ed detail warnings. ENROLMENT checks: invalid/blank outcome code, a final outcome with no end date, missing start date, end-before-start, blank program/unit code; warnings for continuing-with-past-end-date, invalid delivery mode / funding source, and missing scheduled hours on a delivered unit. Findings are split ERROR (will fail NCVER) vs WARNING, grouped by category with a "Ready to submit / N errors to fix" verdict and a full CSV export. Fully read-only and defensively guarded. Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100398. — prior v5.9.397 Compliance Health command centre. a new flagship read-only page (compliance_health.php, first in the left menu) that answers "are we audit-ready right now?" at a glance. A hero audit-readiness score (percentage of key checks currently clear) with a verdict, over a responsive grid of Quality-Area cards surfacing live risk signals: validations overdue / due soon, qualifications never validated, incomplete AVETMISS profiles, open complaints & appeals (past timeframe), working-towards trainers past their 2-year deadline, stale trainer industry currency, QI survey response rate, open high-severity risks, and — critically — students with results but an UNVERIFIED USI (the certificates you cannot yet issue). Every metric has a status pill and a one-click "fix" link to the relevant page. Fully read-only and defensively guarded (every query wrapped; a missing table never breaks the page). Registered in the sidebar, settings and lang. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100397. — prior v5.9.396 AVETMISS address propagation. the student's full street address (building/property name, flat-unit, street number+name, and postcode) is now parsed from NAT00085 — previously the parser dropped it — staged, and propagated into the student profile alongside the other demographics (both automatically on import for existing profiles, and via Backfill). New staging columns postcode/buildingname/unitno/streetname (savepoint 396); the students table already had the matching columns. The student profile summary now shows the complete address (building, unit/street, suburb, state, postcode) instead of just suburb+state. Savepoint 2026073100396. — prior v5.9.395 audit trail + portability. (1) the Complaints, Appeals and Continuous-Improvement registers now write an audit-log entry on every create/update/delete (previously these compliance records could be altered or deleted with no trail — an ASQA evidence gap); logging is wrapped defensively so it can never block the user action. (2) The NAT export replaced a MySQL/Postgres-only "LIMIT 1" with a portable limited query so it no longer risks failing on Oracle/MSSQL. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100395. — prior v5.9.394 world-class student profile. (1) The Student Records list now makes each student NAME a one-click link to their profile, and the row Actions menu gains Certificates + Results/Enrolments shortcuts. (2) student_profile.php now opens with a polished READ-ONLY summary above the edit form: a header card (name, client ID, USI + verification badge, completeness pill that lists missing fields ON LOAD), a demographics grid showing every AVETMISS field as a HUMAN LABEL (with a muted "Not stated" for placeholders), a unit-results table with colour-coded outcome badges, and an issued-certificates card with one-click PDF download — so an admin can review a student's whole picture in one place instead of a bare edit form. (3) Reissuing a certificate now preserves the original as-issued USI snapshot and RTO-identity snapshot (C-P2-1), so a faithful copy shows exactly what the original showed. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100394. — prior v5.9.393 student My Certificates nav link + dashboard block. students now get a persistent "My Certificates" link in the plugin navigation (local_rtocompliance_extend_navigation previously returned nothing for students, so their only link was buried on their Moodle profile page). The link points to the certificate portal (mycerts.php), which enforces its own access control so a student only ever sees their own certificates. A companion Dashboard block (block_rtocompliance_mycerts, delivered separately) shows a student their issued certificates with one-click download on login. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100393. — prior v5.9.392 removed Moodle account creation from Backfill. "Backfill Student Records" no longer creates Moodle {user} accounts (user_create_user removed). A NAT student with no existing Moodle account is now SKIPPED and reported ("no Moodle account — an administrator must create one first, then re-run Backfill"). Backfill now only READS Moodle users and writes the plugin's own student profile + demographics for students who already have an account. Combined with v5.9.387, the plugin creates/deletes NOTHING in Moodle core (no enrolments, no completions, and now no user accounts) — it only reads them. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100392. — prior v5.9.391 NAT demographic propagation regression fix. After a NAT import the AVETMISS demographic data now flows into the student profile again: (1) the finalize step now automatically refreshes the demographic fields (DOB, sex, suburb/state, Indigenous status, labour force, highest school level, language at home, country of birth, disability flag, prior-education flag, at-school flag) on EXISTING student profiles from the freshly-staged NAT00080 data — writing ONLY to the plugin students table (no Moodle user/enrolment/completion writes), so it is constraint-safe; a staged value only overwrites when it is real (never wipes good data with an AVETMISS "not stated" placeholder). This restores propagation that had lived inside the now-disabled auto-enrol handlers. (2) The manual "Backfill Student Records" step was silently dropping 8 core demographics to defaults because its staging SELECT omitted them — the SELECT now pulls all demographic columns, so a backfill writes the full profile. (3) Cert render-time backstop now also blocks the NRT logo on 'attendance' certs (matches the template catalogue's forbidden_for). No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100391. — prior v5.9.390 cert-template polish F4/F5/F6. (F4) render-time compliance backstop — the renderer now drops any element forbidden for the cert type before it reaches the PDF (NRT logo never on a Record of Results or non-accredited Completion; USI never on a Testamur or Statement of Attainment), backing up the approval-time validation against pinned/override/legacy designs. (F5) certificate PREVIEW now applies the template's per-template designjson.overrides{} exactly as the real issue path does, so previews are faithful for override-using templates. (F6) the Test Certificate now uses its own dummy verify token and placeholder USI instead of an empty token + the logged-in admin's live USI. No schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100390. — prior v5.9.389 CERTIFICATE-TEMPLATE INTEGRITY (F1 as-issued RTO snapshot / F2 approved-only pinned template / F3 block issuance on blank RTO details). (F1) each certificate now snapshots the RTO identity settings (legal name, provider code, signatory name/title, AQF statement) at issue time into a new certs.issuesnapshot column and the renderer renders from that snapshot, so a later change to those settings cannot retroactively rewrite an already-issued certificate (mirrors the USI snapshot). (F2) pick_for_cert() renders the pinned template ONLY if it is still status='approved', so an in-progress/unvalidated draft edit can no longer leak onto an already-issued certificate on re-download (it falls back to the current approved template). (F3) issuance is now refused — interactively (non-bypassable) and programmatically — when mandatory RTO details (legal name, national provider code, authorised signatory) are not configured, preventing certificates that render those AQF-required fields blank; the "ready to issue" validator surfaces the same gap. Savepoint 2026073100389. — prior v5.9.388: ASQA PRACTICE-GUIDE AUDIT P1 REMEDIATION PART 2 + ASQA COMPLIANCE MAPPING. Feature code on the v5.9.387 schema: (1) VALIDATION (Std 1.5) — validator-independence declaration is required to complete a validation, and completion is blocked without it; a five-year validation cycle now computes/stores nextduedate (2 years for high-risk), with OVERDUE/DUE-SOON flags and a Coverage-Gaps list of on-scope products with no current validation; assessment outcome + rectification actions are captured. (2) WORKFORCE (Std 3.2) — "Working Towards" trainers now record a start date and an enforced 2-year TAE completion deadline; manager sign-off is blocked for a blank credential or a lapsed working-towards window; supervisors must hold a full, unexpired credential; a Supervision overdue/due-soon alert lists at-risk working-towards trainers. (3) STUDENT SUPPORT (Std 2.3/2.4/2.6) — per-student support / reasonable-adjustment / wellbeing records now persist server-side in local_rtocompliance_supportnotes (retained, shared, auditable) instead of browser localStorage. (4) QUALITY INDICATORS (Std 4.4) — the ad-hoc surveys are replaced with the official AQTF Learner & Employer Questionnaires (items tagged to their scales) and qi_report renders a proper QI Annual Summary (indicator + scale scores, response rates); the QI export is now the aggregate summary, not identifiable per-respondent rows. (5) NEW "ASQA Compliance Mapping" left-menu page (asqa_standards_map.php) — every 2025 Standard mapped to the feature that supports it with an honest Covered/Partial/Gap status (Std 4.3/4.4 self-assurance). No schema changes beyond savepoint 387. Savepoint 2026073100388.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.387'; // v5.9.387 (certification, AVETMISS & enrolment-write removal). (1) ENROLMENT-WRITE REMOVAL (audit A-P1-3): data_import.php was the ONLY file in the plugin that created/deleted Moodle enrolments or course completions — via the retired doenrol/autoenrol/foe_apply_chunk/rollback/fix_overenrolments handlers (UI removed in v5.9.380 but still URL-reachable). These are now hard-blocked two ways: a top-level dispatch guard stops all six actions before any handler runs, and every enrol_user()/unenrol_user()/course_completions delete is additionally gated behind the always-true RTOC_ENROL_WRITES_DISABLED constant. The plugin now only ever READS enrolments/completions. (2) CERTIFICATION USI GATE (C-P1-1/C-P1-2/C-P2-5): AQF certification (testamur, record of results AND statement of attainment) now requires a USI VERIFIED with the Registry, not merely present/well-formed — both the interactive validator (certificate_validator) and the programmatic issuer (lib.php) enforce usiverified=1, with the documented USI-exemption bypass preserved; the interactive issue path now snapshots the USI at issue time so a later correction cannot rewrite an issued document. (3) AVETMISS INTEGRITY: corrected four wrong "competent" outcome sets in data_import.php that counted 41/53/61/85(not-started) as competent (A-P1-1); RPL/Credit-Transfer and reconciler-derived competencies are no longer silently dropped from NAT00120/NAT00060 — activitystartdate is now populated at source and the exports tolerate legacy NULLs (A-P1-2); the completion reconciler no longer flips terminal non-competent outcomes (30/40/52/61/82) to Competent (A-P2-1); RPL/CT delivery mode corrected to 90 (P3-2). (4) SCHEMA (savepoint 387) prepares the validation-independence, five-year-validation-cycle, working-towards-supervision and server-side student-support-record fixes whose feature code follows in the next build. Savepoint 2026073100387.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.386'; // v5.9.384 HUB SEARCH + DASHBOARD: (1) QUAL CERT HUB search brought up to standard — the landing now has a qualification code/name search + category filter (server-side), and the detail view gains an instant client-side filter that works across ALL FOUR tabs (Ready/Issued/Partial/Queue), not just Certs Issued. (2) DASHBOARD Setup Progress now tracks the full start→certificate journey with real state checks: configure RTO → build qualification → LINK units to courses (course map) → register trainer → add students → record unit results → ISSUE a certificate (7 steps, was 5 and missing mapping + issuance). (3) The dashboard "Compliance Modules" grid (previously six skinny columns) moved to its own menu item + page (compliance_map.php) with a responsive auto-fill layout; module definitions extracted to local_rtocompliance_compliance_modules(); the dashboard now links to it via a banner. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100384.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.383'; // v5.9.383 CERT USI-SKIP HANDLING (follow-up to the v5.9.381 USI gate): the bulk issuers now treat a "no USI recorded" result as a distinct SKIP, not a failure. Previously the Qualification Certificate Hub (qch_issue_batch) and Generate-by-Course counted a NO_USI structured skip as a hard FAILED (twice — once per testamur/record), showed a cryptic "FAILED: NO_USI", and — in the Hub — marked the student's autocert-queue row 'failed' so "Retry All Failed" kept re-failing them. Now both pages tally a separate "Skipped (no USI)" count with a clear Clause-12 reason, and the Hub leaves the autocert row PENDING so it issues automatically once a USI is added. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100383.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.382'; // v5.9.382 SOA STUDENT-SEARCH OVERHAUL: the Issue Multi-Unit SOA student picker is rebuilt into a proper find-the-student system. It now lists only students who actually have recorded results (the population that can receive an SoA), each tagged (via the course→qualification map) with the qualifications and categories they belong to. New qualification + category filter dropdowns narrow the list, wired into the existing typeahead so name search and filters combine; result rows now show qualification-code chips. The selection → load-eligible-units flow is unchanged. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100382.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.381'; // v5.9.381 AUDIT FIXES (surveys + certs + RPL/CT): (1) SURVEYS — response-rate now counts all invited surveys for the year (any status) as the denominator, not just 'pending', so manually-sent batches no longer read ~100% (survey_responses.php, qi_report.php); removed the non-functional "Send Reminder" and "Survey Expires On" options that were never implemented. (2) CERTIFICATES — the qualification path (programmatic_issue_cert) now enforces a Clause-12 USI gate: a Testamur / Record of Results is refused (structured skip, before consuming credits) when no USI is recorded, with a $bypassusi override for USI-exempt students, matching the SoA path; and the renderer now shows the USI SNAPSHOTTED on the cert at issue time (falls back to live only for pre-snapshot certs) so a later USI correction can't rewrite historical certificates. (3) RPL & CREDIT TRANSFER — the register is now wired into the outcome pipeline: the edit form links a real student (studentid), and an approved/partially-approved decision posts the outcome into the results register via new local_rtocompliance_apply_rpl_outcome() — RPL=51, Credit Transfer=60, manualoutcome=1, CT rows get zero scheduled hours + delivery mode 90, writing ONLY to the plugin register — so RPL/CT now flows to Student Results, certificates and NAT export. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100381.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.380'; // v5.9.380 STALE-UI + DEAD-LINK CLEANUP + KEY QUESTIONS: full sweep for outdated content. Removed the only user-reachable removed-feature control — the "Backfill Student Records" button on the Verify NAT results page (data_import.php) — and reworded its prose to the data-only flow. Removed two dead Site-Admin menu items pointing to non-existent pages (testing.php Testing Engine, test_data.php Test Data Generator). Fixed dead links to renamed/missing pages: classes/external.php cert verify URL verify_cert.php → verify.php (matches the rest of the plugin); trainer_dashboard.php record_management.php → trainer_currency.php (with trainer-record lookup + graceful fallback) and validation_schedule.php → validation.php; removed survey_responses.php "View Details" (survey_view.php) and "Export to CSV" (survey_export.php) buttons whose targets don't exist (and the now-empty Actions column). Added a "Key questions — quick answers" block to How It Works (view AVETMISS data, issue a qualification, issue a multi-unit SoA, export NAT records, bring in past completions, set up a qualification). Orphaned data_import ?action= views (auto-enrol/fix-over-enrolments/foe-trace) are not reachable from the decluttered flow and their dormant handlers are left intact. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100380.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.379'; // v5.9.379 HOW-IT-WORKS IN PLUGIN MENU + DOC REFRESH: the "How It Works" link now appears in the plugin's own left sidebar (local_rtocompliance_render_sidebar), as the FIRST item above Dashboard, and how_it_works.php renders that sidebar itself. Refreshed the Get Started guide and Support/Help pages to match current features: dashboard banner now points to How It Works and says 7 steps (was 6, mismatched the 7 cards); Support "Get Started" step 5 + the Student Results module card rewritten for the Master Roster, "Sync results from Moodle completions" and "Download unmapped completions"; the Data Import module card rewritten to the data-only flow with the removed Auto-Enrol / Backfill / Fix-Over-Enrolments / Rollback steps deleted; What's New panel updated to v5.9.378 with entries for How It Works, Master Roster, Sync, multi-unit/superseded, and the Data Import strip-down; Pro Tip points to How It Works. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100379.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.378'; // v5.9.378 HOW-IT-WORKS + CLEARER SETTINGS: new "How it works" page (how_it_works.php) added as the FIRST item in the left menu — a plain-English, jargon-free overview of the whole system (three building blocks, how they connect, two ways results arrive, what you get out, and a simple getting-started order) so a brand-new user understands the flow at a glance. Also rewrote the superseded-unit-map setting text to be simple and generic (removed the markdown "#" comment lines that were rendering as giant headings, and the client-specific examples). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100378.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.377'; // v5.9.377 MULTI-UNIT + SUPERSEDED: the completion reconciler now credits EVERY unit a course delivers, not just one — a genuine double/triple-unit course ("TLIR4001 & TLIR4002 ...", "TLIA2009A, TLIG3002A & TLIA5035A ...") makes the student competent in ALL listed units. resolve_course_units() returns the full list from QB primary links (all), QB variant links (all — the explicit way to declare a double-unit course), the course map, and every AVETMISS code found in the course shortname/fullname/idnumber. SUPERSEDED-UNIT MAP: a new admin setting (Site admin → Plugins → RTO Compliance) translates retired unit codes to their current equivalent (e.g. TLIA4052A → TLIX5046 → TLIX0037), following chains, so completions in older-coded courses credit the current unit — essential where a competency changed code across training-package versions. current_code()/superseded_map() applied throughout resolution; unit_index() resolves a name-matched unit to its single qualification. Still writes ONLY local_rtocompliance_enrolments; idempotent; one row per (student, unit). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100377.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.376'; // v5.9.376 AUDIT-FIXES (self-review of 373-375): (1) the per-qualification drill-down outcome grid is now UNIT-scoped — it matches every register row for the student whose unit code is one of the product's selected units (case-insensitive), instead of gating on programcode/courseid, so a synced/archived/cross-category completion with a blank programcode no longer shows "-" while counting as complete on the Master Roster, the "complete" filter and autocert. Grid keys are UPPER-normalised. (2) unmapped_completions() now only counts completions from users with a plugin student record (mirrors the sync's skip order), so the review CSV never lists Students Affected = 0 noise. (3) the on-demand Sync and unmapped export raise the PHP time/memory limit (idempotent; very large sites can use the nightly task instead). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100376.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.375'; // v5.9.375 UNMAPPED-COMPLETIONS-REVIEW: adds completion_reconciler::unmapped_completions() and a "Download unmapped completions (CSV)" link beside the Sync button on Student Results. Lists every Moodle course whose completions the sync could NOT resolve to a Qualification Builder unit — courseid, shortname, fullname, category, #completions and #students affected — ranked by students blocked, so the RTO can link or rename exactly those courses instead of only seeing a count. Read-only export (export=unmapped), streamed before header output. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100375.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.374'; // v5.9.374 CROSS-CATEGORY-SEAMLESS: makes the is_archive flag INFORMATIONAL so units completed through many copied/semester/archived courses across DIFFERENT Moodle categories all count. (1) NEW classes/completion_reconciler.php + reconcile_completions_task (scheduled, DISABLED by default) + a "Sync results from Moodle completions" button on Student Results: reads Moodle {course_completions} across every delivery course (any category, incl. archived variants), resolves each to unit+qualification via the Qual Builder / course map, and upserts the COMPETENT outcome into the results register. Idempotent; unit-scoped upsert (one row per student+unit, backfills blank programcode) so no duplicates; never overwrites a manual outcome; writes ONLY local_rtocompliance_enrolments — creates/deletes NO Moodle {user}/{user_enrolments}/{course_completions}. (2) Category-agnostic Source 4 in seed_course_map(): matches any course whose name starts with a known unit code to that unit's qualification anywhere in Moodle, only when the unit belongs to exactly ONE active qualification (ambiguous left for manual), full-reseed only, UNIQUE-courseid guarded. (3) is_archive=0 guards relaxed at the completion/autocert path and the results + enrolment-import read queries so archived/variant deliveries count; the enrolment-CREATE guard (v5.9.297) is deliberately KEPT to avoid duplicate live rows across copies. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100374.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.373'; // v5.9.373 STUDENT-RESULTS-SHOWSTOPPER + CROSS-CATEGORY-FIX: qualbuilder_results.php landing is now a cross-qualification MASTER STUDENT ROSTER — one row per student straight from the results register (historical NAT import + live Moodle completions side by side), with search (name/email/USI/client ID), qualification filter, category (sub-category) filter, status filter, USI-health filter and sort; a headline stat strip and three pivots (students-by-qualification, USI health, outcome mix) kept numerically consistent with the active filters (status filter folded into a distinct-alias sub-select so no placeholder is reused); full-field CSV export; qualification chips + Profile/Units drill links tie it to Qual Builder, Course Map and student profiles. The {user} join is LEFT with a plugin-student name fallback so decoupled historical students appear automatically once Phase 2 lands. The per-product drill-down keeps its unit grid and gains inline client ID/DOB/state + a Master Roster back-link. CROSS-CATEGORY-FIX: the drill-down per-unit outcome lookup now matches programcode OR any of the product delivery course IDs (primary + active is_archive=0 variants, any Moodle category), so a student who completed a unit via a variant course in another category — carrying a blank/other programcode — now renders that competency instead of a dash. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100373.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.372'; // v5.9.372 DATA-IMPORT-DECLUTTER: stripped the Data Import page to the data-only flow — removed the auto-enrol cleanup tools (Backfill top button, detail-view Rollback + Fix Over-Enrolments buttons and rollback panel, Fix Placeholder Student Names utilities). Kept upload → confirm → detail view, Verify NAT Data, data-quality CSV, and the new "Download unmatched students" export. Handlers left dormant; UI entry points removed. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100372.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.371'; // v5.9.371 NAT-RESULTS-REGISTER (Phase 1 of the data-flow rework): the NAT import now writes unit OUTCOMES directly into the plugin\'s own results register (local_rtocompliance_enrolments) — the same table Student Results, the Qual Cert Hub, Generate-by-Qualification and Record-of-Results already read — so historical Wisenet outcomes appear across those screens immediately. New classes/results_importer.php: after finalizenat stages a NAT file it matches staged clientids to EXISTING plugin students and upserts their outcome rows (real AVETMISS codes, dates, funding, unit name + Moodle courseid resolved for display only), idempotent, never clobbering a manual outcome edit. GUARANTEE: touches ONLY plugin tables — creates/deletes NO Moodle {user} accounts, {user_enrolments} or {course_completions}. The import no longer diverts into the auto-enrol wizard (finalizenat now lands on the import detail view); the intro card is rewritten to the real behaviour (no Auto-Enrol wording; Archive-Wizard shortcut removed); new "Download unmatched students" review export (action=export_unmatched) lists file students not yet in the system. Students with no plugin record are skipped (review file) — importing brand-new non-Moodle students is the next step (student-decouple, needs a schema change). No DB schema changes in this version. Savepoint 2026073100371.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.369'; // v5.9.369 MULTI-UNIT-SOA-QUAL-RESOLVE: the Issue Multi-Unit SOA flow now recognises the real qualification for every completed unit instead of showing the raw semester/archive category ("Archive s21"). New soa_compliance_engine::resolve_qualifications_for_courses() resolves each course via the source-of-truth chain — course_map (confirmed rows first) → Qualification Builder direct link (qualunits.courseid) → Qualification Builder variant/archive courses (qualunit_courses.courseid) — and pulls the qualification NAME from the Qualification Builder. Units now carry qualcode/qualname/qualgrouplabel/semesterlabel; get_suggested_groups() groups by qualification (resolved groups first). UI: the table "Qualification" column shows code + name with the semester as a sub-line; the group filter, group cards, sorting and Select-all all key off the qualification; Step 3 (doc type + qual code + qual name) auto-fills from the resolved qualification. New auto-detect banner: a single detected qualification auto-fills Step 3 and pre-selects its compliant, not-yet-issued units for one-glance review; multiple → prompt to pick; none → clear guidance to map in Course Map / Qual Builder or issue standalone. Snapshot now stores the resolved qualification label. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100369.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.368'; // v5.9.368 SECTION-AUDIT-FIXES: 3 High — undefined capabilities that fatally broke buttons now use ':manage' (data_import.php export_quality_csv 'manageimports'→manage, +3 qcm_* AJAX 'importavetmiss'→manage; reconcile.php exportmapping 'admin'→manage) and generate_course_certs.php bulk-cert modal is now Bootstrap 4/5-safe (rtocModalToggle). Mediums — NEW DB COLUMN local_rtocompliance_certs.timecompleted (insert_record was silently dropping it → completion date never stored → Clause-9 gap; upgrade savepoint 368) + generate_course_certs now computes the earliest completion date inline (POST handler previously read an undefined $allcompleters → always 0); governance.php Annual Declaration date reads submissiondate (was datesubmitted → always "-"); trainers.php credential-policy filter uses managersignoff<>0 (was !='' → PostgreSQL type error); locations.php delete now log_delete() with record snapshot (was log_create). Low — supervision.php escape free-text + portable LIMIT; rpl.php .badge-blue defined; students.php missing_usi clamped ≥0; qualbuilder_results.php picker unit count honours selected=1/active; ai_usage_report.php guards both label keys; soa_issue.php debug instrumentation removed (temp files/error_log/set_config); locations.php TAS link drops bogus ?%23= param. DB SCHEMA CHANGE (certs.timecompleted) — savepoint 2026073100368.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.367'; // v5.9.367 CERT-CORRECTNESS: (1) ROR-OUTCOME-FIX — Generate-by-Course full-qualification issue now builds the Record of Results with each unit's REAL AVETMISS outcome via get_qualbuilder_unit_list_with_outcomes() (was hardcoded "20"/Competent, diverging from generate_qual_certs.php); RPL/Credit-Transfer units now print correctly. (2) SOA-DATE-FIX — multi-unit SoA units now carry a Semester/Year derived from the actual unit completion date (renderer reads "semester"/"year", never "date"), so the RoR/date column no longer falls back to the cert issue date. (3) EMPTY-SOA-GUARD — programmatic_issue_cert refuses (before charging credits) to issue a statement/record with no units AND no qualification code, returning a structured skip instead of silently emitting a unit-less compliance document. Left #5 ("20" fallback for confirmed Moodle completers with no enrolment row) UNCHANGED by design — it is a defensible inference, not a fabrication. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100367.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.366'; // v5.9.366 CERT-EDITOR-COMPLETE: (1) per-field image uploads now stored to FA_IMAGE on save (base64 data-URL → stored file with unique itemid; imageurl stripped from designjson) and re-hydrated for display on reload — images now render on issued PDFs; (2) ror_table (Record of Results units table) is now fully authorable in the editor — palette chip, 3-column canvas mock, and col1_w/col2_w/col3_w width inputs; (3) enableqr setting repurposed to toggle only the "Verify at:" TEXT line (QR is always rendered — verification is mandatory), description reworded; (4) live PDF preview — cert_template_preview.php accepts a POSTed unsaved design (sesskey + managecerttemplates) and the editor debounces a true-to-issue preview into an iframe as you edit; (5) duplicate() now copies FA_BG + FA_IMAGE files to the copy's own itemids so duplicates are standalone. AMD build refreshed (src + build/.js + build/.min.js). Re-applied on top of the v5.9.365 Part-A base (self-hosted verify URL, activate single-active fix, auto preview orientation, button/nav-tab hover lock, generic settings text, RoR preview data). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100366.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.365'; // v5.9.365: Cert-issuance pipeline fixes (cert_template, cert_template_renderer, issue_certificate, reissue_cert, soa_ajax, lib, settings, lang). Task #92 retry_count field. Tasks #90/#91/#93 qual_cert_hub improvements. No additional DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100365.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.361'; // TASK-89 (v5.9.361): Missing-units callout on Student Results page. In-progress student rows in qualbuilder_results.php now show an expandable "X units still needed" summary beneath their progress bar. Clicking it lists each outstanding unit code and name. Derived from the enrolments map already built per row — no extra queries. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100361.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.360'; // TASK-84 ROR-CAPACITY-HINT (v5.9.360): Live overflow hint in cert template editor for ror_table-type fields. When a RoR column field (qualification.units, qualification.units_col_semester/names/results) is selected, the Field Properties panel shows "At Xpt, this field fits approximately N rows. Qual ABC has M units." The estimate uses field_height_mm / (fontsize_pt × 0.352 + 1.5mm line gap) and updates live as the admin resizes the field or changes font size. Top qualification by unit count fetched from qualbuilder/qualunits at page load and passed to JS via RTOC_TMPL_DATA.rorqualdata. Hint turns amber if the field can't fit the largest qual's unit count. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073100360.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.358'; // TASK-80 (v5.9.358): Reviewed get_qualbuilder_unit_list_with_outcomes() for the same programcode-free outcome gap that affected get_completed_units_for_qual (SEMESTER-COPY-OUTCOME-FIX v5.9.345). Confirmed the gap does NOT apply: this function queries enrolments by studentid alone with no programcode constraint, so RPL/CT rows recorded without a programcode are already found in the initial query. Added a SEMESTER-COPY-OUTCOME-REVIEW comment documenting the analysis and improved the debugging() fallback message to explicitly note the query was programcode-free (genuine data gap, not a filtering issue). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000358.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.357'; // TASK-77 (v5.9.357): Warn before downloading a NAT export that still contains students with no qualification code. natexport.php now queries for VET enrolments (vetflag != N) with a blank programcode before rendering the page. If any are found, a yellow warning banner is shown above the Generate button with the count and a direct link to the Skipped Qualification Codes report. Admin can still proceed and generate anyway. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000357.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.356'; // TASK-76 (v5.9.356): Undo non-VET exclusion on Skipped Qualification Codes report. Added undo_exclude action handler that resets vetflag to Y and blanks programcode, returning the course to the main skipped-codes list. Added showexcluded toggle parameter and an Excluded Courses collapsible section at the bottom of skipped_programcodes.php listing each non-VET course with enrolment count and an Undo exclusion button (confirm dialog before firing). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000356. // TASK-71 (v5.9.355): Request-level dedup cache in seed_course_map(). Added a static $seededThisRequest array so repeated calls for the same qualcode within one HTTP request (e.g. catch-up scan or Partially Complete tab iterating 200 students) are no-ops after the first BFS walk. Reseed still fires once per qualcode per page-load/task-run. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000355.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.354'; // TASK-69 (v5.9.354): Test cert email confirmation splash. Savepoint 2026073000354.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.352'; // BUTTON-CONTRAST + COURSE-MAP-ADMINLIB (v5.9.352): Three fixes from user-reported issues. (1) course_map.php fatal: added missing require_once($CFG->libdir.'/adminlib.php') — without it, navigating directly to the Course Map page threw "Call to undefined function admin_externalpage_setup()". (2) Button contrast: deepened and enforced white text on all three banner action buttons — indigo Seed Course Map (#6366f1→#4f46e5), violet Sync AVETMISS (#8b5cf6→#7c3aed), amber Sync Qual Codes (#f59e0b→#b45309); added color:#fff !important to inline styles and to .rtoc-dob-sync-btn in styles.css so Moodle/Bootstrap .btn rules can no longer override them. (3) Action menu z-index bumped 99999→100001 so menus always render above any plugin overlay. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000352.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.351'; // TASK-53 (v5.9.351): Admin retry for failed autocert queue entries. Tab 4 of qual_cert_hub.php now shows a per-row "Retry" button next to each failed autocert entry and a "Retry All Failed" bulk button above the table when failed rows exist. Both reset the row status to "pending" with a timestamped note appended to errormessage, so the next Process Queue run picks the entry up. Two new action handlers added: action=retry_autocert (single row) and action=retry_all_failed (bulk). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000351.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.350'; // TASK-52 (v5.9.350): Missing-units panel on Partially Complete tab. Tab 3 of qual_cert_hub.php now shows a "Still Needed" column for each partially-complete student. The full unit list is fetched once per qual load (local_rtocompliance_get_qualbuilder_unit_list), then per-student done codes (local_rtocompliance_get_completed_units_for_qual) are subtracted to produce the missing set. Missing units render as an inline <details>/<summary> expandable: clicking "▸ N units still needed" opens a bulleted list of unit codes and names in QB sequence order. Students with no missing units (counted complete but not yet in the completers set) show a green "✓ All units done" note. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000350.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.348'; // TASK-49 (v5.9.348): Prevent RoR truncation for large qualifications. ROR-OVERFLOW-CONTINUATION: the ror_table renderer in cert_template_renderer.php now adds continuation PDF pages automatically when a qualification has more rows than fit in the template field boundary (e.g. 30+ units). Previously the renderer silently clipped at maxY — an ASQA compliance risk. Now: when the next row would exceed maxY+0.5mm, AddPage() is called with the same page dimensions, font/colour state is restored, and rendering continues from the same field origin ($x,$y) on the new page. Continuation pages are plain (no cert background/branding) so all units are legible. Single-page records (<~25 units) are completely unaffected. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000348.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.347'; // TASK-47 (v5.9.347): Prevent duplicate autocert queue entries under concurrent completion events. Added UNIQUE index on local_rtocompliance_autocerts(studentid, qualbuilderid) via install.xml and upgrade savepoint 2026073000347 (drops old non-unique index, adds unique). Wrapped DB::insert_record in queue_autocert_if_all_units_complete() in try/catch to silently absorb duplicate-key violations from concurrent inserts — the losing concurrent task no-ops cleanly. Savepoint 2026073000347.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.346'; // TASK-46 (v5.9.346): Skipped Qualification Codes report. New skipped_programcodes.php shows all blank-programcode enrolments grouped by course after Sync Qualification Codes. Per-course: Moodle category path the sync walked; green Link to QB button (when a QB record matches the course or its unit codes) sets programcode on all affected enrolments instantly; plain-English suggestion when no QB match. Mark as non-VET button sets vetflag=N, excluding the course from AVETMISS and clearing the warning banner. Sync handler redirects to the report when skipped>0 instead of showing a bare count. blank-programcode banner on students.php now excludes vetflag=N records and adds a View report shortcut link. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000346.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.345'; // TASK-45 (v5.9.345) — see release note above // TASK-45 (v5.9.345): Issue Certificate button on Student Results page. Complete students (100% of selected units with a final outcome) now have an inline "Issue Certificate" button in the Actions column of qualbuilder_results.php. Clicking it calls ajax.php?action=issue_cert_from_results which resolves cert types (testamur+record for qualifications, statement for skill sets/single units), checks for existing issued certs, calls local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert() for each required cert type, and returns the new cert numbers. The row updates in-place — no page reload. A bulk "Issue All Pending on This Page" button above the table processes all complete students sequentially. Existing cert numbers are shown inline for students who already have certs. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000345.
$plugin->release_prev = '5.9.344'; // TASK-44-BFS-GATE-FIX (v5.9.344): check_full_qual_completion() now correctly recognises every semester copy of a unit without manual linking. Two fixes: (1) SYNC-BEFORE-CHECK — a targeted local_rtocompliance_seed_course_map($programcode) call is now made before the course-map lookup so any semester-copy courses added since the last nightly sync are captured before the completion check runs (mirrors the SYNC-BEFORE-CERT pattern already present in generate_qual_certs.php since v5.9.337); (2) TASK-44-BFS-GATE-FIX — the BFS pre-load gate was changed from !$courseMapExists to !$cfqcMapHasRows: previously the category-tree BFS fallback (which finds courses never manually linked in QB) was only attempted when the course_map table was completely absent. If the table existed but had no rows for this specific qualification, $cfqcSubtreeIds remained empty and all semester-copy courses were silently skipped. The fix checks whether the map actually has rows for this qualcode, so the BFS fallback fires whenever the map cannot supply a complete course set. generate_qual_certs.php (SOURCE 1 catTreePairs UNION) and process_enrolment_task.php (queue_autocert_if_all_units_complete) already had complete semester-copy support from v5.9.335–337 and required no changes. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000344. // TASK-42 (v5.9.343): cert_test.php — "Send a copy to my email address" checkbox. When checked, the generated PDF is emailed to the logged-in admin via email_to_user() before the browser-tab stream, using a [TEST]-prefixed subject and a body that states no record was created. Bypasses the emailcerts on/off setting (deliberate test send). No DB writes. New lang strings: cert_test_sendemail_label, cert_test_sendemail_hint, cert_test_email_subject, cert_test_email_body. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000343. // SIDEBAR-CSS-SPECIFICITY-FIX (v5.9.342): the light sidebar added in 5.9.341 was overridden by a SECOND, higher-specificity sidebar implementation inside styles.css (the [class*="path-local-rtocompliance"] #rtoc-sidebar block using --rtoc-sb-* tokens, dark navy #1a3354), so the menu still rendered dark after install. Appended a light-theme override to styles.css that redefines the --rtoc-sb-* tokens + hard-coded dark colours at element specificity, so the sidebar now renders light. IMPORTANT: run Site administration > Development > Purge all caches after upgrading — Moodle caches styles.css, so CSS changes (this sidebar fix AND the v5.9.341 table engine) do not appear until caches are purged. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000342. // UI-ENGINE + COMPAT-4.4-5.3 (v5.9.341): (A) Declared support widened to Moodle 4.4-5.3 ($plugin->requires 2024042200, $plugin->supported [404,503]). (B) Removed the legacy local_rtocompliance_before_footer() callback that double-registered the sidebar/table JS already provided by the db/hooks.php before_footer_html_generation hook (killed the duplicate <script> injection + the "should be migrated to hook" debug notice on 4.4/4.5). (C) Added the 5 missing capability language strings (viewtrainer/viewcerts/viewstudents/viewreports/managecerttemplates) so the Permissions UI no longer shows raw [[...]] identifiers. (D) Added the local_rtocompliance_qualunit_courses table to db/install.xml so fresh installs build it (previously only created in upgrade.php, breaking new installs of qualbuilder/cert-hub/course-map). (E) Left navigation reordered to a first-step->last-step getting-started flow, added the missing USI Verification and Qual Cert Hub items, removed the dead Testing Engine link, fixed the active-item matcher to respect query strings, and registered the previously-missing info/file-check/search icons. (F) Sidebar recoloured from near-black (#0d1424, group labels failing WCAG at 1.77:1) to a modern light slate surface with AA-contrast text. (G) New unified styling engine appended to styles.css: single tokenised :root, overflow-safe premium data-tables (fixes the last-column overlap), cross-Bootstrap-4/5 badge+button shims so components render identically on 4.4 and 5.x, and a 4-tier responsive system for phone/tablet/laptop/desktop. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000341. // TASK-32 (v5.9.340): Bulk import contract slot — the "Import from Moodle Enrolments" form now shows a QLD Purchasing Contract dropdown (same auto/contract1/contract2/contract3 options as the single-enrolment form) whenever at least one QLD contract is configured in RTO Settings. The chosen slot is resolved at import time and written to purchasingcontract1 on every enrolment record created in that batch. Defaults to Auto so existing behaviour is unchanged for RTOs with no QLD contracts. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000340. // QUAL-CERT-HUB (v5.9.339): New qual_cert_hub.php — unified page for all qualification-level certificate operations. Hub home: table of active qualifications with live Enrolled/Complete/Issued/Pending/Queue funnel stats; per-row Issue Pending quick-action; global Scan for Missed Completions. Qual detail (4 tabs): (1) Ready to Issue — completers without a Testamur, with select-all, email toggle, force-regen, and suspend-on-issue options; (2) Certs Issued — searchable paginated list; (3) Partially Complete — progress bars for enrolled students with partial unit completion (500-student safety cap); (4) Autocert Queue — shows pending/complete/failed autocert rows, Process Queue button re-verifies completion before issuing. Catch-up scan (action=scan_missed) walks all completers per qual and inserts pending autocert entries for those with no cert and no queue row. All issuance goes through local_rtocompliance_programmatic_issue_cert(). Two-source detection (SOURCE 1 Moodle course_completions + SOURCE 2 AVETMISS enrolment outcomes) faithfully reproduced from generate_qual_certs.php. settings.php: registered local_rtocompliance_qual_cert_hub under Certificates. qualbuilder.php: Certs action button added per qual row. generate_qual_certs.php: hub crosslink banner added. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000339. // v5.9.333 TASK-44-AUDIT-FIXES: Six issues found by expert audit of v5.9.332 category-tree feature. (1) get_qual_root_category_id() now uses sql_like() pre-filter before full-scan fallback — avoids full category table scan on every call. (2) Regex word boundary \b replaced with explicit [^A-Z0-9]|$ in get_category_tree_courseids_for_unit() — correctly matches codes with no space delimiter. (3) Variant course lookup moved outside the if(!empty(courseid)) block in check_full_qual_completion() and get_completed_units_for_qual() — units with ONLY variant courses (no primary QB course) now have their variants collected. (4) generate_qual_certs.php: $effectiveLinkedUnitCount replaces $numlinkedcourses as SOURCE 1 guard and HAVING threshold — pure category-tree QBs (where $numlinkedcourses=0) no longer skip SOURCE 1 entirely. All UI references updated. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000333. // v5.9.332 TASK-44-CATEGORY-TREE-AUTO-DISCOVERY: QB now automatically recognises every semester copy of a unit without any manual linking. Three new lib.php utility functions (get_qual_root_category_id, get_category_subtree_ids, get_category_tree_courseids_for_unit) discover courses from the Moodle category tree at runtime. Integrated into: check_full_qual_completion() and get_completed_units_for_qual() — category-tree courses included in the course-completion check per unit; generate_qual_certs.php SOURCE 1 — semester-copy courses appended to the unit↔course subquery via UNION SELECT literals; queue_autocert_if_all_units_complete() — completing a category-tree course now fires the QB autocert check for the parent qualification. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000332. // v5.9.331 FULL-PIPELINE-AUDIT: five issues found by expert analysis all fixed. (1) check_full_qual_completion() removed qu.courseid IS NOT NULL filter — ALL units now checked, category-tree-only units fall through to enrolment fallback; (2) get_completed_units_for_qual() same guard removed, outcome ORDER BY aligned to competent-first; (3) get_qualbuilder_unit_list_with_outcomes() adds DEBUG warning when fallback-20 fires; (4) generate_qual_certs.php SOURCE 1 rewritten to JOIN unit↔course subquery and count DISTINCT unit completions not course completions — variant-semester students now satisfy SOURCE 1; (5) qualbuilder_results.php adds RPL (51) and Credit Transfer (60) to all four completion outcome lists — RPL students no longer appear as In Progress. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000331. // v5.9.330 OBSERVER-GATE-FIX + OUTCOME-ORDERING-FIX: (1) observer.php user_enrolment_created and user_enrolment_deleted both now include a third gate check — category ancestor walk — so semester-copy courses never manually linked in QB are correctly queued (v5.9.329 category detection was unreachable without this fix); (2) get_qualbuilder_unit_list_with_outcomes() ORDER BY changed from id DESC to CASE competent-first ASC then id DESC — prevents a re-enrolment with outcome 70 Continuing from masking an earlier 20 Competent on the Record of Results cert. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000330. // v5.9.329 CATEGORY-TREE-DETECTION: programcode on enrolment records is now resolved by walking the full Moodle category ancestor chain — the RTO top-level category name contains the qualification code (e.g. "TLI50321 — Diploma of Customs Broking"). Any course nested at any depth under that category is automatically recognised as belonging to that qualification. Removed: category.idnumber fallback (only checked immediate parent), nationallyrecognised legacy flag. New: sync_programcodes admin action on Students page back-fills all existing blank programcode records using the same tree walk. lib.php: local_rtocompliance_detect_qualcode_from_category_ancestors(). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000329. // v5.9.328 AVETMISS-COLUMN-GUARD: students.php "Error reading from database" crash fixed — the AVETMISS sync-banner query (indigenousstatus/labourforcestatus/highestschoollevel on avetmiss_student) is now wrapped in try-catch so the Student Records page degrades gracefully on sites where the v5.9.316 upgrade.php columns haven't been applied yet (Moodle upgrade not yet triggered). No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000328. // v5.9.327 CERT-OVERHAUL: (1) Legacy renderer signature bug fixed — ceo_signature_file from RTO Settings now used as fallback in legacy TCPDF path (was get_branding_path only). (2) cert_template::create() now accepts orientation param so starters are built at chosen orientation, not always type-default. (3) cert_templates.php: orientation select on create form with smart JS default; Quick-setup seed banner auto-activates ASQA starter templates for any cert type with no active template; Live preview panel renders all 4 cert types on-demand via cert_test.php iframes. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026073000327. // TASK-30 (v5.9.325): State portal reference ID panel now shows a "Go to portal →" link beside each configured ID. Links open QLD RAPT, NSW Smart & Skilled, VIC SVTS, SA STARR, WA RAPT, TAS Skills Tasmania, NT DITT, and ACT AVETARS in a new tab. Portal URLs hardcoded in natexport.php; new lang string portal_go_to_portal. No DB changes. Savepoint 2026073000325. // TASK-25 (v5.9.324): QLD purchasing contract slot selector on enrolment form. RTOs with multiple QLD DTET contracts can now assign the correct contract per funded enrolment. New purchasingcontract_slot select field (auto/contract1/contract2/contract3) in the enrolment form funding section; shown for state/government-funded enrolments only (hidden for fundingsourcenat 20/30). Slot is resolved at save time to the actual contract string and stored in purchasingcontract1. Re-opening an edit pre-selects the matching slot by comparing purchasingcontract1 against the three configured QLD contract values. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000324. (v5.9.324): QLD purchasing contract slot selector on enrolment form. RTOs with multiple QLD DTET contracts can now assign the correct contract per funded enrolment. New purchasingcontract_slot select field (auto/contract1/contract2/contract3) in the enrolment form funding section; shown for state/government-funded enrolments only (hidden for fundingsourcenat 20/30). Slot is resolved at save time to the actual contract string and stored in purchasingcontract1. Re-opening an edit pre-selects the matching slot by comparing purchasingcontract1 against the three configured QLD contract values. No DB schema changes. Savepoint 2026073000324. // TASK-24 (v5.9.323): Show QLD DTET RTO ID and NSW Smart & Skilled Commitment ID as a reference panel on the AVETMISS export page. These are not NAT file fields — they are state portal credentials admins need when uploading. Panel shows when either is configured; prompts to RTO Settings when neither is set. Display-only change — no DB schema changes. // TASK-23 (v5.9.322): State-funded enrolments no longer export blank pos 115-117 (fundingsourcestate) to NCVER. All 8 state _funding_code_default settings (QLD/NSW/VIC/SA/WA/TAS/NT/ACT) are now loaded at constructor time and applied as fallback when fundingsourcenat is 13 or 15 and no per-enrolment state code is set. TAS/NT/ACT also added to statefundingcontracts map (pos 125-136) — previously missing, causing blank purchasing contract fields for those three states. Savepoint 2026073000322. // ORPHAN-FIX (v5.9.321): six settings defined in settings.php but never read by code are now wired. certfooter→cert.footer payload key; compliance_logo_2→BRANDING_ITEMID_COMPLIANCE_LOGO_2=9 + renderer; enableqr→gates verify.url / authenticity_measure payload; emailcerts→send_certificate_email() early-exit when disabled; defaultstate→nat_generator statecode fallback; qld/nsw/vic/sa/wa purchasing contracts→NAT00120 pos 125-136 fallback. Stale ZIPs cleaned (3×moodle-plugin/, 37×public/downloads/). Savepoint 2026073000321. // CERT-ASSETS (v5.9.320): // CERT-ASSETS (v5.9.320): Certificate Elements section in RTO Settings — secondary logo, CEO signature (with settings fallback), certificate background image, organisation seal; all four assets have per-cert-type 'applies to' checkboxes (Testamur / Statement of Attainment / Record of Results / Certificate of Completion). Cert background applied as page-level fallback bg. New BRANDING_ITEMID_SECONDARY_LOGO=7, BRANDING_ITEMID_CERT_BG=8. Savepoint 2026073000320. // FIX-NAT-FULL-WIRING (v5.9.319): full AVETMISS NAT export audit fixed 43 gaps across all 10 NAT files. rtocode added to NAT00030/60/85/90/100; NAT00010 address wired; programcode priority fixed in NAT00030/130; parchment wired; firstname from students table. New residentialcountry column. contactname/suburb/state/postcode settings added. Savepoint 2026073000319.
