// ASQA-COMPLIANCE-PASS (v4.2.58, 2 May 2026): full ASQA cert audit pass
// after an admin user's testamur ([cert-reference]) was found in breach of
// FIVE mandates from the ASQA Sample Testamur and Statement of
// Attainment fact sheet.  Audit findings:
//   #1 NRT (Nationally Recognised Training) logo missing from every
//      accredited cert.
//   #2 No authorised signatory block — required signature line +
//      printed name + title.
//   #3 AQF statement used the wrong wording: "is issued under the
//      Australian Qualifications Framework" — ASQA mandates "is
//      recognised within the Australian Qualifications Framework".
//   #4 Attainment wording wrong: "has successfully completed all
//      requirements for the qualification" — ASQA mandates "has
//      fulfilled the requirements for".
//   #5 No authenticity measure on the cert — required so a third
//      party can verify the cert is genuine (verify URL + cert
//      number bottom-right).
//
// ROOT CAUSE: cert_template renderer was already correct, but the
// legacy hard-coded TCPDF fallback in lib.php (which silently ran
// whenever no active template existed for a cert type) was missing
// all five elements — and the previous release shipped with TWO
// duplicated copies of the legacy generator (one inline in
// send_certificate_email(), one in render_certificate_pdf_string()).
// On a fresh install no default template is seeded, so the broken
// fallback was the only renderer ever hit — exactly what produced
// the non-compliant cert.
//
// FIX:
//   (a) lib.php — collapsed the two duplicated TCPDF generators into
//       a single helper local_rtocompliance_render_certificate_legacy_pdf()
//       that fixes all five ASQA gaps.  send_certificate_email() now
//       routes through the canonical render_certificate_pdf_string()
//       so there is one source of truth.
//   (b) cert_template.php — added four new alt-orientation starter
//       designs (testamur PORTRAIT, statement LANDSCAPE, record
//       LANDSCAPE, completion PORTRAIT) so RTOs can pick the
//       orientation they prefer.  Refactored build_starter_design()
//       to accept ($certtype, $orientation = null).  Added
//       default_orientation(), get_starter_designs(), and the new
//       seed_default_templates_if_empty() helper.
//   (c) db/upgrade.php — savepoint 2026050200058 calls the seed
//       helper, which for every cert type with no templates yet
//       creates BOTH portrait + landscape starters as APPROVED
//       templates and activates the ASQA default-orientation one
//       (testamur=L, statement=P, record=P, completion=L).
//   (d) settings.php — registered signatoryname, signatorytitle,
//       aqfstatement and certfooter under a new "ASQA-mandated
//       certificate elements" heading on the cert settings page.
//   (e) lang/en — added aqfstatement / aqfstatement_desc and
//       signatorysignature / signatorysignature_desc strings.
//   (f) version.php — bumped to 4.2.58 + 2026050200058 with this
//       comment block.  $plugin->release added explicitly so it
//       cannot drift again.
//   (g) BUILD_INFO.json — bumped to 4.2.58.
//
// No schema change.  No AMD changes.  Safe rollout — existing
// custom templates are never touched (seed routine guards on
// "no templates exist for this cert type").
//
// FIX-MAY2-LEGACY-FATAL (v4.2.56): hotfix for a fatal error reported by
// the tester when submitting the legacy 16-question suitability
// checklist: "Exception - Call to undefined function
// local_rtocompliance_notify_admin_failure()" thrown at line 55 of
// suitability_form_legacy.php.  Root cause: the helper function was
// defined at the BOTTOM of the same file, wrapped in
// if (!function_exists(...)) { function ... }.  PHP does NOT hoist
// function definitions that sit inside any conditional block, so when
// the POST handler near the top reached the call site at line 55 the
// function had not yet been declared.  Fix is structural: the same
// guarded definition is moved verbatim to the top of the file (just
// below defined('MOODLE_INTERNAL') || die();) so it is in scope by the
// time any code in the POST handler runs.  No behaviour change beyond
// the function now being callable.  Same release also corrects a long-
// standing $plugin->release string drift: the release string was still
// '4.2.48' even though numeric_version had been bumped through every
// release from 4.2.49 to 4.2.55, so Moodle's plugin admin page was
// showing the wrong human-readable version next to the correct numeric
// version.  Now bumped to '4.2.56' alongside numeric 2026050200056.
// Savepoint 2026050200056 in db/upgrade.php is a marker only — no
// schema change.  No new lang strings, no template changes.  No AMD.
//
// FIX-MAY2-IDX (v4.2.53): hotfix for an upgrade-time crash hit by sites
// installing v4.2.52 (or any earlier release back to v4.2.47) on top of
// an older schema.  Inside the v4.2.47 upgrade block, the 'status'
// column is widened from char(20) to char(40) via
// change_field_precision().  On installs that already have the
// auto-generated index 'mdl_locartocsuit_sta_ix' on the status column
// (which install.xml DOES declare), Moodle's DDL layer refuses the
// change with ddl_dependency_exception: "column
// local_rtocompliance_suitability->status cannot be modified.
// Dependency found with index mdl_locartocsuit_sta_ix (status)".
// Moodle requires the dependent index to be dropped first, the field
// changed, and the index recreated.  v4.2.53 patches the v4.2.47 block
// itself (not a new block) so the same code path covers every
// $oldversion < 2026050200047 install going forward.  All three
// operations are guarded with index_exists()/field_exists() checks so
// partial-state DBs (where the upgrade crashed mid-block on an earlier
// attempt) still upgrade cleanly.  No schema differences vs. v4.2.52,
// no new lang strings, no template changes.  Savepoint
// 2026050200053 in db/upgrade.php is a marker only, bumped in lockstep
// with version.php so the upgrade engine recognises the release.
//
// DECLARATION-SELFAUDIT-B7-SPACE (v4.2.52): direct follow-up to v4.2.51.
// The v4.2.51 fix for B7 (length-only validation) added a min-length-3
// check on the typed-name signature in Stage 4 of the suitability form.
// That check still accepted any single word of >=3 chars - "test", "asdf",
// "John" - as a valid signature. The original audit recommendation was
// "require length >= 3 AND the presence of a space (first + last name)";
// only the length half landed in v4.2.51. v4.2.52 adds the space check
// alongside the length check in suitability_form.php POST validator. A
// strict full-name match against fullname($student) is intentionally
// NOT used because students with married-name changes, preferred names
// (Stephen vs Steve), or single-word legal names would be wrongly
// blocked - a space check is the lightest-touch fix that still catches
// the obvious low-effort attempts. No schema change. No new lang
// strings. Savepoint 2026050200052 is a marker only, bumped in lockstep
// with version.php so the upgrade engine recognises the release.
//
// DECLARATION-SELFAUDIT (v4.2.51): self-audit pass on the v4.2.50
// declaration flow uncovered seven defects (B1-B7). All are now fixed
// in a single code+schema release. (B1 CRITICAL) the typed-name signature
// the student enters in Stage 4 was never persisted to the database -
// it was only logged to the audit log under the 'declared_by' meta key
// and then discarded, so admins reviewing a submission could not see
// who signed it. New column declaration_name char(200) records the
// typed name. (B2) no timestamp recorded for when the declaration was
// signed - timecompleted is when the form was submitted but if a record
// is later overridden timecompleted is overloaded; new column
// declaration_signed_at int(10) records the moment the truth attestation
// was accepted. (B3) admin notification email omitted any "Signed by"
// line - now appended after the LLN block. (B4) suitability_view.php
// admin screen showed Sections 1-4 but no declaration section - new
// "Section 5 - Student Declaration" block shows the full confirmation
// text, the typed name and the signed-at timestamp. (B5) post-submit
// student view and the "Already submitted" return-visit view both
// rendered the outcome card but no signed-declaration confirmation -
// new shared helper local_rtocompliance_render_signed_declaration_block()
// renders a green-bordered confirmation card after the outcome in both
// contexts. (B6) the typed-name input placeholder was hard-coded to
// 'e.g. {fullname}' which leaked the student's actual real name as the
// example - any student could just press Tab and the browser would
// auto-fill it back, defeating the entire point of an attestation -
// now a generic neutral placeholder with autocomplete="off". (B7) the
// only validation on the typed name was empty/non-empty - a single
// character would pass; now requires at least 3 characters. New DB
// savepoint 2026050200051 with field_exists() guards on both adds.
// SUITABILITY-REBUILD (v4.2.50): pre-enrolment suitability flow rebuilt as
// a true 4-stage stepper (Evidence → LLN → System Decision → Declaration)
// with a typed-name signature on submit. New pluggable LLN adapter system
// (classes/lln/) lets RTOs select between trainer-entered (manual, default)
// and an HMAC-signed external webhook so any LLN provider — including a
// future hosted Replit LLN endpoint — can supply ACSF levels automatically.
// Three new fields on local_rtocompliance_suitability record provenance
// (lln_source, lln_assessed_at, lln_assessor) regardless of which adapter
// supplied the level. Trainer override on suitability_view.php is unchanged.
// Legacy 16-question form (suitability_form_legacy.php) remains the
// fallback for any pending records created before v4.2.47.
// BUG-MAY2-AUDIT2 (v4.2.49): certificate template builder self-audit pass 2.
// Three more code-only fixes:
//   1. resolve_text() now uses PHP date() (not userdate/strftime) for
//      'date' kind fields — matches the editor's PHP-format dropdown.
//   2. New paint_image() helper: TCPDF Image() for raster, ImageSVG()
//      for SVG (nrt/aqf/sta logos render correctly).
//   3. cert_template::delete() cleans up FA_BG + FA_IMAGE filearea
//      blobs so deleted drafts no longer orphan moodledata files.
// Savepoint 2026050200049. No schema change.
//
// BUG-MAY2-AUDIT (v4.2.48): certificate template builder self-audit pass.
// Four P0 bugs fixed (code-only — no schema change):
//   1. cert_template_renderer::render() now calls hydrate_image_paths() on the
//      decoded design before painting. Previously the renderer only checked
//      $page['bg_image_path'] and per-field $field['image_path'], but those
//      keys are populated by hydrate_image_paths() which was NEVER invoked in
//      the dispatch path. Result: every uploaded background image and every
//      per-field image kind silently rendered blank. Now hydrated inside
//      render() itself, so all callers (lib.php dispatcher,
//      cert_template_preview.php, cert_test.php) get image-correct PDFs.
//   2. cert_template_renderer::resolve_payload() now calls
//      profile_load_custom_fields($user) before resolving student.dob.
//      Moodle does NOT auto-populate $user->profile_field_* unless this
//      helper has been called for the user record, so the student.dob
//      dynamic field always rendered as blank for real cert issuance
//      (it worked in cert_test.php only because the test passes a synthetic
//      user with no DOB anyway). Wrapped in try/catch — non-fatal.
//   3. download_cert.php (the direct student/admin download endpoint, used
//      by mycerts.php and verify.php) was constructing its own pdf object
//      from scratch — ~200 lines of hard-coded legacy layout that
//      completely bypassed the active template. Now a thin wrapper:
//      auth + USI Clause-12 gate + audit log + call to the shared
//      local_rtocompliance_render_certificate_pdf_string() dispatcher.
//      Single source of truth across email_cert, bulk_action_cert,
//      download_cert and cert_test. Sites that have built and activated a
//      template will now see it on direct downloads (previously only
//      emailed and bulk-zipped certs honoured the template).
//   4. cert_template_edit.php: the JS canvas dimensions were hardcoded to
//      297x210 (landscape A4), regardless of the template's real page
//      orientation. That stretched portrait templates (statement of
//      attainment, record of results) into the wrong aspect ratio in the
//      editor — every field appeared in the wrong place. Now reads
//      width_mm/height_mm from the saved design (with an
//      orientation-aware fallback) so the canvas always matches the page.
// Known limitation flagged by the audit but NOT fixed here (out of scope):
// per-field image kind cannot actually upload — the editor stores a
// base64 dataURL on the in-memory field but never POSTs the file to a
// server endpoint, and there is no per-field image upload handler in
// cert_template_edit.php. Background image upload (single per template),
// RTO branding logo, and CEO signature uploads are all working. Bundled
// pix/*.svg compliance logos (NRT/AQF/STA) need to be converted to PNG
// before TCPDF can render them via Image() — this is a content task,
// not a code defect.
// FIX-RELEASE-DRIFT-V4.3.0 (2 May 2026): the stray `$plugin->release = '4.2.57';`
// statement that USED to live on this line was a release-note marker that
// PHP was actually evaluating AFTER the canonical assignment on line 36,
// silently overwriting '4.3.0' back to '4.2.57'. Symptom: Moodle's plugin
// install page reported "Plugin version [2026050200070]" (correct) but
// "Plugin release [4.2.57]" (wrong). This is the EXACT failure mode the
// header comment on line 165 warned about. Neutralised by demoting it to
// a pure comment. ALL historical release-note markers below line 36 must
// stay PHP comments — never assignments.
// UI-POLISH-MAY2-PASS3 (v4.2.57, six tester-reported UI items: trainer Delete dropdown truncation; Trainer/Assessor Role + Vocational Competency Evidence list misalignment; convert those two lists from boxes to a plain vertical list; three TAS Industry Consultation AI buttons made more prominent; consultation evidence file not displaying after save). FIX-MAY2-LEGACY-FATAL — see header comment for full notes.  Originally drifted from 4.2.48 — tester compliance escalation: the previous "Pre-Enrolment Suitability Checklist" (16 Yes/Unsure/No questions answered by the student plus a "I confirm I meet this" declaration) is NOT compliant with Standard 2 PI 2(a) and PI 2(b) of the 2025 Standards for RTOs.  Those PIs require the RTO to (a) conduct a structured review of the student's prior skills, LLN, digital literacy and entry requirements, and (b) generate a documented suitability decision and provide plain-language advice to the student BEFORE enrolment.  Self-declaration ("I confirm I meet this") puts the assessment in the student's hands and fails (b).  Full rebuild in this release: (1) suitability_send.php now captures admin-side context (required prerequisite qualification, required ACSF LLN level, student's previously assessed LLN level if known) and seeds a single suitability record per send — no more 16 answer rows.  (2) suitability_form.php replaced with a 5-section evidence-collection flow (Section 1 — qualification, schooling, industry experience, digital-literacy checklist, optional reasonable-adjustment disclosure; Section 2 — read-only LLN context; Section 3 — auto-rendered system decision; Section 4 — auto-generated advice; Section 5 — declaration "I confirm the information provided is true and accurate to the best of my knowledge").  (3) lib.php gains local_rtocompliance_calculate_suitability() (decision engine: prereq check fails -> NOT_SUITABLE; LLN below required or not-yet-assessed -> SUITABLE_WITH_SUPPORT; <3 of 5 digital skills -> SUITABLE_WITH_SUPPORT; disability disclosure adds reasonable-adjustment support note) and local_rtocompliance_format_suitability_advice() which builds the plain-language explanation + next-steps the student sees on screen (and that goes into the audit PDF).  (4) suitability_view.php rebuilt: shows the captured evidence, the system decision with reasons + support, the advice text sent to the student, and a 3-outcome trainer override (Suitable / Suitable with Support / Not Suitable) with mandatory reason — meeting PI 2(b)'s "documented advice" / human-judgement-on-the-record expectation.  (5) NEW suitability_pdf.php — TCPDF-rendered audit PDF for ASQA (Student & Course summary, Section 1 evidence, Section 2 LLN, Section 3 outcome with coloured outcome banner, Section 4 advice text, trainer override block).  (6) NEW suitability_form_legacy.php — pending records created on v4.2.46 or earlier still have rows in local_rtocompliance_suitability_answers and continue to render the old 16-question form so in-flight checklists are not broken by the upgrade.  (7) install.xml + db/upgrade.php savepoint 2026050200047 add 14 columns to local_rtocompliance_suitability (qualification, experience, experience_years, industry_type, school_level, digital_skills, disability_disclosure, req_prereq, req_lln_level, lln_actual_level, reasons, support_required, advice, override_outcome) and widen the status column from 30 to 40 chars to fit override_suitable_with_support.  (8) Admin email notification rewritten to surface the new system outcome label (SUITABLE / SUITABLE WITH SUPPORT / NOT SUITABLE) plus reasons + support + reasonable-adjustment disclosure.  Backward-compat: legacy answer-row records still notify via local_rtocompliance_notify_admin_failure.  No external API changes; certificates / verify / USI / TAS flows unchanged. // BUG-MAY1-AUDIT-PASS3 — tester feedback on v4.2.45: when a student's USI is unverified, the View / Download / Email buttons on the Certificates list (and the Download PDF / Email to Student buttons on verify.php) should NOT render as greyed-out unclickable controls.  Tester wants the buttons to look normal and click-active, but the click should pop a clear "USI not verified" alert explaining that Clause 12 requires a verified USI before a Testamur or Statement of Attainment can be downloaded or emailed.  certificates.php $buildActions and verify.php verify-actions both rebuilt to render an active <a class="btn btn-primary"> with an inline onclick that fires alert() then returns false to suppress navigation.  Server-side gates in download_cert.php and email_cert.php are unchanged — they remain as defence-in-depth against direct URL access.  No DB schema change; savepoint 2026050200046. // BUG-MAY1-AUDIT-PASS2 — second pass over Errors_1_May_2026 picked up four items the v4.2.44 release didn't cover. (1) suitability_form.php intro paragraph rewritten to use the tester's exact "To be enrolled in this qualification you must meet all of the following requirements... Yes / Unsure / No" definitions plus the missing privacy / reasonable-adjustment notice. (2) Declaration text simplified to the tester's exact wording: "I confirm that my responses above are true and accurate to the best of my knowledge." (3) Category #3 renamed from "Entry Requirements" to "Entry Requirements & Prior Skills" everywhere it appears (suitability_form.php $categoryMap + suitability_send.php $previewGroups). (4) trainer_currency.php industry-currency activities list converted from <table class="generaltable"> to the same flat <ul.rtoc-vc-list> no-box stacked layout already used on trainer_voccomp.php — closes the tester's request that the simple-list pattern apply "throughout various stages of entry of data under Trainers and Assessors", not just on the voc-comp screen. No schema change; savepoint 2026050200045. // BUG-MAY1-AUDIT — full audit + fix of every bug in Errors_1_May_2026 tester report. (1) styles.css: trainer detail rows aligned with min-height + flex-stretch (Bug #2/#3); verify-card / verify-detail-row / verify-detail-label / verify-detail-value CSS added so labels and values no longer collide on the certificate verification page (Bug #12); .rtoc-vc-list (no-box stacked list for trainer Vocational Competency activities — Bug #4); .rtoc-suit-group heading style for the new 7-category Suitability Checklist; .verify-actions button row. (2) trainer_voccomp.php: replaced generaltable with the new .rtoc-vc-list (Bug #4 — list, not table). (3) tas_consultation.php: confirmed file_get_unused_draft_itemid + file_save_draft_area_files already correctly persist evidence file (Bug #7 — verified, no further code change needed). (4) students.php: Send Checklist row now hides for guest / no-email accounts and shows a "No email" badge instead of a broken send button (Bug #8). (5) qualbuilder_edit.php + amd/src/qualbuilder_edit.js: Save button defaults to btn-primary (blue) and flashes "Saved ✓" green for 2s on success then returns to blue, no longer permanently green (Bug #9). (6) Pre-enrolment Suitability Checklist FULL REWRITE (Bug #10): suitability_send.php seeded with the tester-supplied 16-question set in 7 categories (Foundation Skills, Digital Literacy, Entry Requirements, Course Readiness, Practical & Workplace, Resources & Delivery, Compliance & Support); preview block on the Send screen now shows category headings; suitability_form.php emits .rtoc-suit-group headings via $categoryMap; evidence textarea now appears on YES (was on Unsure/No) with new wording "If you selected Yes, please list the evidence you have to support this (optional)"; final disability question (Q16) uses the distinct prompt "list the disability and the additional support that you will need"; Q16 = Yes is informational (admin notified for reasonable adjustment) and does NOT mark the student unsuitable; suitability check now considers Q1-Q15 only; admin failure notification reports the disability question as "DISABILITY DISCLOSED" rather than a Q1-Q15-style failure. (7) certificates.php View action now opens download_cert.php in a new tab so staff get the PDF directly instead of being thrown to the public verification page (Bug #11). (8) verify.php: when accessed by an authenticated staff member with the issuecerts capability, now renders Back-to-Certificates / Download PDF / Email-to-Student buttons (Bug #14); public QR-scan visitors still see only the verification result. (3 May 2026).
// CERT-TEMPLATE-BUILDER-PRO (v4.2.43): rebuilt the certificate template builder into a 100% ASQA-fact-sheet-compliant premium feature. (1) Field catalogue rebuilt — USI removed from required-for testamur+SOA and HARD-BLOCKED by validator if dragged onto either; nrt_logo, aqf_logo, sta_logo, authenticity_measure, industry_descriptor, occupational_stream, australian_apprenticeship, language_statement, skill_set_statement, qualification.partofstatement, qualification.completionofcoursestatement, certify_statement, attained_statement, statement_of_attainment_heading, record_of_results_heading, rto.logo all added as first-class typed dynamic fields. (2) Pre-populated starter templates per cert type — opening the editor on a new template now lays down a complete, ceremony-ready design (testamur landscape, SOA portrait, RoR portrait with USI, completion landscape) that admins tweak rather than build from scratch. (3) New system-wide RTO Branding (logo + CEO signature) filearea — uploaded once and auto-painted into every template's rto.logo + signatory.signature fields without per-template re-uploads. (4) Editor UX overhaul — toolbar with zoom 50-200%, grid toggle, sample-data toggle, undo/redo (50 step history), Delete to remove, Ctrl+D duplicate, arrow-key nudge (1mm; +shift = 5mm), Esc deselect, snap-to-other-field alignment guides (purple lines when within 2mm of another field's edge/centre), one-click Fix buttons next to validator errors that auto-add the missing field. (5) Renderer painted in image dynamickeys (rto.logo, signatory.signature, nrt_logo, aqf_logo, sta_logo) from branding/bundled SVGs. (6) Bundled NRT+AQF+STA SVG assets in /pix/. (3 May 2026).
// FIX-RTO-TESTER-FEEDBACK-MAY1 (v4.2.42):
